:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.bartleby.com/61/69/F0256900.html" ;
    :definitionText "ETYMOLOGY: Middle English, from Old French, from Medieval Latin forestis (silva), outside (forest), from Latin for s, outside. http://www.bartleby.com/61/69/F0256900.html. In several European languages, the root for(s) today still means outsider -(e.g. foreigner). http://www.europarl.eu.int/workingpapers/forest/eurfo124_en.htm. The word “forest” in Medieval England came to mean land outside cultivation and belonging by default to the Crown. There is no direct reference to trees or woodland. http" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :sourceRef "http://books.google.com/books?id=jhZsJc4z5RkC&pg=PA657&lpg=PA657&dq=hawaii+forestland&source=web&ots=YlCTj-qUZR&sig=PtkyXu4oaaWBg-3k45z2nub3mDs#PPA645" ;
    :definitionText "Manwood in Lawes of the Forest (1598) describes a forest as “a certain territory of woody grounds, fruitful pastures, privileged for wild beasts and fowls of forest, chase and warren, to rest and abide in the safe protection of the king, for his princely delight and pleasures.” (Encyclopedia Britannia 1910. p. 645. http://books.google.com/books?id=jhZsJc4z5RkC&pg=PA657&lpg=PA657&dq=hawaii+forestland&source=web&ots=YlCTj-qUZR&sig=PtkyXu4oaaWBg-3k45z2nub3mDs#PPA645,M1 ) A 'forest,' then, was origi" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :definitionText "Table 1 lists terms for forest, forestland and tree in a multitude of languages from around the world." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :sourceRef "http://forum.wordreference.com/showthread.php?t=186539" ;
    :definitionText "“A jungle is tropical and untrammeled. A forest is temperate and little touched by humans. Woods are forests that have been worked by humans.” http://forum.wordreference.com/showthread.php?t=186539" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_005
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.wrm.org.uy/bulletin/174/viewpoint.html" ;
    :definitionText "For Claudentina, a quilombola woman (descendant of escaped African slaves) in her 60s from the community of Angelim in Sapê do Norte, in the Brazilian state of Espíritu Santo, the forest is “a place where people used to go to find fruits and seeds, vines, wood, plants, roots; to hunt and fish. It was also a place to practice our faith.” http://www.wrm.org.uy/bulletin/174/viewpoint.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_006
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ncasi-nerc.org/projects/evmp/vcst/" ;
    :definitionText "We found over 1,700 definitions. Thresholds for tree cover vary from 0% to 80%. [Note: John Dwyer has done some work which shows that average forest cover in urban USA is about 33% (From: Smith_Brad/wo@fs.fed.us)]. A crosswalk of various forest classification systems may be found at http://www.ncasi-nerc.org/projects/evmp/vcst/. We can group forest definitions according to their source - those found in general dictionaries and glossaries, definitions from the International Community, National de" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_007
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :sourceRef "http://ruralsystemguide.com/Appendices/GlossF.html" ;
    :definitionText "Forest - (1) A community dominated by dense, extensive tree cover. (2) An area managed for producing timber and other products, or maintained under woody vegetation for such indirect benefits as protection of watersheds or recreation. (3) An area within an administrative boundary of a forest agency, whether having trees or not.(4) Land primarily devoted to trees. http://ruralsystemguide.com/Appendices/GlossF.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_008
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :sourceRef "https://howlingpixel.com/wiki/Outline_of_forestry" ;
    :definitionText "Forest – defined as either a geographic area or delineated by the general composition of individuals; https://howlingpixel.com/wiki/Outline_of_forestry" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_009
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "https://www.for.gov.bc.ca/hfd/library/documents/bib106996.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Treed: A vegetated polygon with 10% or more (by crown cover) of tree species of any size https://www.for.gov.bc.ca/hfd/library/documents/bib106996.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_010
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :definitionText "Definitions: forest, tree, forest summary, woodland, afforestation, deforestation, reforestation, other terms." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_011
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ceres.org/conference/notes/sustainable_forestry.htm" ;
    :definitionText "A certain territory of woody ground and fruitful pastures privileged for wild beasts and fowl of forest, chase and warren to rest and abide in, in the safe protection of the king for his pleasure. http://www.ceres.org/conference/notes/sustainable_forestry.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_012
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dictionary.com/cgi-bin/dict.pl?term=forest" ;
    :definitionText "A defined area of land formerly set aside in England as a royal hunting ground. http://www.dictionary.com/cgi-bin/dict.pl?term=forest" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_013
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://dspace.wbpublibnet.gov.in/dspace/bitstream/10689/10100/4/Chapter%201_1%20-%20125p.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "A forest is a certain territory of woody grounds, fruitful pastures, privileged for wild beast and fowls of forest chase, and warren, to nest and abide in, in the safe protection of the King, for his princely delight and pleasure, with territory of ground, so privilege is meered and bounded with unremovable marks, meers and boundaries either know by matter of record, or else by prescription. (Manwood. 1598. The Lawes of the Forest). http://dspace.wbpublibnet.gov.in/dspace/bitstream/10689/10100/4" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_014
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "A large extent or precinct of country, generally waste and woody, belonging to the sovereign, set apart for the keeping of game for his use, not inclosed, but distinguished by certain limits, and protected by certain laws, courts, and officers of its own. --Burrill. (Eng. Law) Source: Webster's Revised Unabridged Dictionary, © 1996, 1998 MICRA, Inc" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_015
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.biology-online.org/dictionary/Forest" ;
    :definitionText "A large extent or precinct of country, generally waste and woody, belonging to the sovereign, set apart for the keeping of game for his use, not inclosed, but distinguished by certain limits, and protected by certain laws, courts, and officers of its own. http://www.biology-online.org/dictionary/Forest" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_016
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.foresthistory.org/ASPNET/Publications/CCCforestry/contents.htm" ;
    :definitionText "A waste grounds belonging to the king (Blackstone) http://www.foresthistory.org/ASPNET/Publications/CCCforestry/contents.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_017
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "An area of land proclaimed to be forest under a Forest Act or Ordinance. Ford-Robertson 1971: 107, 298." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_018
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://dictionary.reverso.net/english-definition/forest%20reserve" ;
    :definitionText "An area of woodland, esp. one owned by the sovereign and set apart as a hunting ground with its own laws and officers. http://dictionary.reverso.net/english-definition/forest%20reserve" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_019
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://fwie.fw.vt.edu/rhgiles/appendices/glossf.htm" ;
    :definitionText "An area within an administrative boundary of a forest agency, whether having trees or not. http://fwie.fw.vt.edu/rhgiles/appendices/glossf.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_020
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.yourdictionary.com/forest" ;
    :definitionText "Any of certain tracts of woodland or wasteland, usually the property of the sovereign, preserved for gam http://www.yourdictionary.com/forest" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_021
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.alaska.net/~winter/bouvier1856_f_all.html" ;
    :definitionText "By the English law, a forest is a circuit of ground properly under the king's protection, for the peaceable living and abiding of beasts of hunting and the chase, and distinguished not only by having bounds and privileges, but also by having courts and Offices. 12 do. 22. http://www.alaska.net/~winter/bouvier1856_f_all.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_022
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.molluscsoftasmania.net/Portfolio/Grove_1998_NatureConservationSourcebookForForestryProfessionals.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Forest Reserve - A government land designation the purpose of which is to retain that land as forest or other natural vegetation, or to encourage its conversion to forest. http://www.molluscsoftasmania.net/Portfolio/Grove_1998_NatureConservationSourcebookForForestryProfessionals.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_023
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://ext.msstate.edu/pubs/pub1250.htm" ;
    :definitionText "From a management standpoint, a forest is a collection of stands administered as a unit. http://ext.msstate.edu/pubs/pub1250.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_024
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.tnw.org.uk/Note17.html" ;
    :definitionText "Historically, a prescribed but unenclosed area of land on which the sovereign had the exclusive right to hunt and make Forest Laws. More commonly, a large wooded area. http://www.tnw.org.uk/Note17.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_025
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://explanation-guide.info/meaning/Forest.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Historically, an area set aside for hunting. http://explanation-guide.info/meaning/Forest.htm and http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forest" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_026
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://info.sjc.ox.ac.uk/forests/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Hunting preserve of the king or lord-marcher, subject to forest law but not necessarily woodland (L 237); originally an area of land in which only the owner had the right to hunt deer and boar. http://info.sjc.ox.ac.uk/forests/glossary.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_027
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.deanverderers.org.uk/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "Its traditional definition is a territory, usually unenclosed, and not necessarily woodland but often covered with woods of varying density, but also included heathland, wood pasture, arable and even villages. It was designated by perambulation and used by the sovereign for his or her assigned, hunting, and subject to his will by forest law. The protection of deer and their habitat was paramount. In early centuries, forest virtually meant the King’s hunting ground. http://www.deanverderers.org.u" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_028
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.allwords.com/query.asp#AHD" ;
    :definitionText "National Forest - A large expanse of forest that is protected by a government and may be harvested or hunted in only under controlled conditions http://www.allwords.com/query.asp#AHD" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_029
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://fscus.org/html/standards_policies/us_regional_standards/archives/ozark_ouachita4.html" ;
    :definitionText "One or more stands managed together, under a single ownership or a single certificate http://fscus.org/html/standards_policies/us_regional_standards/archives/ozark_ouachita4.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_030
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dorsetcoppicegroup.co.uk/resources/Dorset_Coppice_Group_Glossary.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Originally a tract of heath, moor or woodland controlled by the Crown for the purpose of conserving deer and other woodland animals. http://www.dorsetcoppicegroup.co.uk/resources/Dorset_Coppice_Group_Glossary.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_031
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.bwf.org/laws/FSAO_15.html" ;
    :definitionText "The mass of land of the public domain comprising of the public forest, permanent/established forests or forest reserves and other forest reservations.http://www.bwf.org/laws/FSAO_15.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_032
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "65.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.birdlist.org/cam/themes/Volume_I_s.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Closed) forest – Formed by trees at least 5 m tall with their crowns interlocking, covering 65% of the sky or more. http://www.birdlist.org/cam/themes/Volume_I_s.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_033
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "40.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.geery.com/Norfork_MUC.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Closed) forest - Formed by trees at least 5 meters tall with their crowns interlocking. Total canopy cover is greater than 40%. http://www.geery.com/Norfork_MUC.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_034
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "https://www.uni-hohenheim.de/i490a/teaching/M4901-430/ws_03_04/reading_materials/New_Neef_Schwarzmeier_Studie.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Closed) Forest in which the stand density is greater than 20 percent of the area and tree crowns approach general contact with one another. https://www.uni-hohenheim.de/i490a/teaching/M4901-430/ws_03_04/reading_materials/New_Neef_Schwarzmeier_Studie.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Ecological_definition_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :appliesIn :Ecological_definition ;
    :definitionText "(Ecological definition) Forest is one of major types of vegetation, which comprises an aggregate of woody, srubs, herbaceous and other (mosses, liches) plants, including fauna and microorganismus; all these components are biologically interacted during their development, and impact both each other and environment. Ref. Forest Encyclopaedia, Vol 1, Soviet Encyclopaedia, Moscow, 1985, page 503" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_035
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.forestry.utoronto.ca/ac_staff/emeritus/My%20Webs/english.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Ecosystem) - An ecological system composed of interacting biotic and abiotic components of the environment in which trees are a major constituent, such that their canopies cover 20% or more of the area (Maini 1991) http://www.forestry.utoronto.ca/ac_staff/emeritus/My%20Webs/english.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_036
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.pbs.org/earthonedge/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Ecosystem) - Land areas dominated by trees where the tree canopy covers at least 10% of the ground area http://www.pbs.org/earthonedge/glossary.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_037
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "(Landscape) Forest is a natural and territorial complex of a different rank (from a facies to a geographical country) in which phytocoenoses are dominated by spontaneously developing tree vegetation. Ref. Kireev D.M. 1984. Ecological and Georaphical Terms in Forestry. Reference Glossary, Nauka, Novosibirsk, 1984, page 63" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_038
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nalms.org/glossary/lkword_f.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(NALMS) Land which is at least 10 percent occupied by forest trees of any size or formerly having had such tree cover and not currently developed for non-forest use. Lands developed for non-forest use include areas for crops, improved pasture, residential, or administrative areas, improved roads of any width, and adjoining road clearing and power line clearing of any width. http://www.nalms.org/glossary/lkword_f.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_039
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "https://www.uni-hohenheim.de/i490a/teaching/M4901-430/ws_03_04/reading_materials/New_Neef_Schwarzmeier_Studie.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Open) Forest in which the tree canopy layer is discontinuous but covers at least 10 percent of the area and in which the grass layer is continuous. https://www.uni-hohenheim.de/i490a/teaching/M4901-430/ws_03_04/reading_materials/New_Neef_Schwarzmeier_Studie.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Recommended_Definition_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :appliesIn :Recommended_Definition ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.forestcarbonportal.com/resource/critical-need-new-definitions-forest-and-forest-degradation-global-climate-change-agreement" ;
    :definitionText "(Recommended Definition) -While a definition of \"forest\" that is globally acceptable and appropriate for monitoring using standard remote sensing options will necessarily be based on a small set of easily measured parameters, there are dangers when simple definitions are applied locally. At the very least, we recommend that natural forest be differentiated from plantations and that for defining \"forest\" the lower height limit defining \"trees\" be set at more than 5 m tall with the minimum cover o" .

:def_Forest_Remote_sensing_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :appliesIn :Remote_sensing ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "7.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Remote sensing) Land with tree crown cover of more than 20 % of the area. Trees should be able to grow to a height of 7 m. Minimum area outside continuous forest: 0.5 ha. Minimum width outside continuous forest: 15 m. (minimum size stand; for instance 15 m x 333 m). (Köhl and Päivinen 1996)." .

:def_Forest_Riverine_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :appliesIn :Riverine ;
    :heightMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://icaci.org/files/documents/ICC_proceedings/ICC2013/_extendedAbstract/131_proceeding.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Riverine): 75-100% tree cover up to 20+ m. Shrub <10% if > 1m high http://icaci.org/files/documents/ICC_proceedings/ICC2013/_extendedAbstract/131_proceeding.pdf" .

:def_Forest_SAF_1958_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :appliesIn :SAF ;
    dcterms:date "1958"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://home.comcast.net/~gyde/5-agency_paper-2.doc" ;
    :definitionText "(SAF) (1958) (Forest) A plant association predominantly of trees and other woody vegetation. (SAF 1958) http://home.comcast.net/~gyde/5-agency_paper-2.doc" .

:def_Forest_SAF_1971_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :appliesIn :SAF ;
    dcterms:date "1971"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://home.comcast.net/~gyde/5-agency_paper-2.doc" ;
    :definitionText "(SAF) (1971) (Forest) Generally, an ecosystem characterized by a more or less dense and extensive tree cover. More particularly, a plant community predominantly of trees and other woody vegetation, growing more or less closely together. (FORD-ROBERTSON 1971) . (Society of American Foresters, 1971) http://home.comcast.net/~gyde/5-agency_paper-2.doc" .

:def_Forest_SAF_2001_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :appliesIn :SAF ;
    dcterms:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.safnet.org/aboutforestry/world.cfm" ;
    :definitionText "(SAF) (2001) A forest is considered an area with at least 10 per cent tree canopy cover. http://www.safnet.org/aboutforestry/world.cfm" .

:def_Forest_Science_ecology_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :appliesIn :Science_ecology ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.biology-online.org/dictionary/Forest" ;
    :definitionText "(Science: ecology) An extensive wood; a large tract of land covered with trees. http://www.biology-online.org/dictionary/Forest" .

:def_Forest_SRM_1980_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :appliesIn :SRM ;
    dcterms:date "1980"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "25.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://home.comcast.net/~gyde/5-agency_paper-2.doc" ;
    :definitionText "(SRM) (1980) Land on which the native vegetation (Climax or natural potential) is dominated by trees with at least 25 percent crown coverage at maturity of the trees. (SRM 1980) http://home.comcast.net/~gyde/5-agency_paper-2.doc" .

:def_Forest_Sub_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :appliesIn :Sub ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.forest.ru/eng/old-growth/eu-definition.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Sub) natural woodland vegetation comprising native species forming forests of tall trees, with typical undergrowth, and meeting the following criteria: rare or residual, and/or hosting species of Community interest (28). http://www.forest.ru/eng/old-growth/eu-definition.html" .

:def_Forest_Upland_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :appliesIn :Upland ;
    :canopyThreshold "66.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.1000friendsofflorida.org/PUBS/stmarksGreen/apend2.asp" ;
    :definitionText "(Upland) - An upland area with a tree canopy closure of greater than or equal to ten percent. Included in this category are pine, hardwood, and mixed forest and those areas where timber harvesting and subsequent regeneration are taking place. For a given forest stand to be classed as one particular species group, the polygon which contains the species must have a tree canopy comprised of 66 percent or more of the total canopy. Otherwise, the forest polygon will be classed as a mixed species. Cla" .

:def_Forest_woodlands_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :appliesIn :woodlands ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://content.alterra.wur.nl/Internet/webdocs/ilri-publicaties/publicaties/Pub36/Proceeding%20of%20the%20workshop%20leeg-h3.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(woodlands), almost exclusively of Aleppo Pine, with at least 20% ground cover by trees; http://content.alterra.wur.nl/Internet/webdocs/ilri-publicaties/publicaties/Pub36/Proceeding%20of%20the%20workshop%20leeg-h3.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_040
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.marinreleaf.org/" ;
    :definitionText "“Urban forest\" means those native or introduced trees and related vegetation in the urban and near-urban areas including, but not limited to, urban watersheds, soils and related habitats, street trees, park trees, residential trees, natural riparian habitats, and trees on other private and public properties http://www.marinreleaf.org/" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_041
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://europe.mtnforum.org/rs/econfreports/MountainPeopleForestsAndTrees.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "A \"tree dominated ecosystem,\" http://europe.mtnforum.org/rs/econfreports/MountainPeopleForestsAndTrees.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_042
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.landhelp.info/FramifyGlossary.php" ;
    :definitionText "A biological community dominated by trees and other woody plants. http://www.landhelp.info/FramifyGlossary.php" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_043
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.sfrc.ufl.edu/Extension/ssfor11.htm" ;
    :definitionText "A biological community of plants and animals which is dominated by trees and other woody plants. (Density greater than 20-30% understood) See Woodland. http://www.sfrc.ufl.edu/Extension/ssfor11.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_044
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/13035957/Christian_Gamborg.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "A broad definition of forest is: “An ecosystem characterised by a more or less dense and extensive tree cover, often consisting of stands varying in characteristics such as species composition, structure, age class, and associated processes, and commonly including meadows, streams, fish and wildlife” (Helms, 1998: 70). http://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/13035957/Christian_Gamborg.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_045
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://fwie.fw.vt.edu/rhgiles/appendices/glossf.htm" ;
    :definitionText "A community dominated by dense, extensive tree cover. http://fwie.fw.vt.edu/rhgiles/appendices/glossf.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_046
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.pauldonahue.net/for_InkaNatura_guides/environmental_glossary.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "A community dominated by dense, extensive tree cover….Plant community predominately of trees and other woody plants, growing more or less closely together.….Ecosystem characterized by more or less dense and extensive tree cover, i.e.,larger than what might be called a grove. http://www.pauldonahue.net/for_InkaNatura_guides/environmental_glossary.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_047
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://155.187.10.12/glossary/croft.html" ;
    :definitionText "A community dominated by trees with long trunks. http://155.187.10.12/glossary/croft.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_048
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.atlanticeurope.com/geography/GeographyGlossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "A community of trees and other plants, together with the animals that live in it. This natural community is called an ecosystem and it is self sustaining. Forests are most commonly found where there is enough water for their growth and so they are most common in moister rather than drier parts of the world. Geography Glossary - http://www.atlanticeurope.com/geography/GeographyGlossary.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_049
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.si.edu/crc/ep/forest/bin-pdf/Glossary.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "A community of trees, shrubs, herbs, and associated plants and organisms covering a considerable area; that use oxygen, water, and soil nutrients as the community attains maturity and reproduces itself. http://www.si.edu/crc/ep/forest/bin-pdf/Glossary.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_050
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "A community of trees, shrubs, herbs, microorganisms, and animals, the trees being the most obvious living structure. Academic American Encyclopedia" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_051
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "A community or society of living things, the most important of which is the tree. The forest is a unit or organized whole consisting of three distinct parts - the canopy, the floor, and the wood-mass. (Gifford 1902)" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_052
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.foresthistory.org/ASPNET/Publications/CCCforestry/contents.htm" ;
    :definitionText "A complex association of trees, shrubs, and other plants in which each individual plays some part in the life of the community\" (Graves and Guise). http://www.foresthistory.org/ASPNET/Publications/CCCforestry/contents.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_053
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.hww.ca/glossary.asp#letterR" ;
    :definitionText "A complex community of plants and animals in which trees are the most conspicuous members. A mixed forest includes both coniferous and deciduous trees. http://www.hww.ca/glossary.asp#letterR, http://www.minntrees.org/facts/ff17.htm and http://www.hww.ca/glossary.asp#letterF" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_054
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "A complex community with life of its own. It has a soil and atmosphere of its own, chemically and physically different from any other, with plants and shrubs as will as trees which are peculiar to it. It has resident population of insects and higher animals entirely distinct from that outside. (Pinchot 1914)" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_055
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://edugreen.teri.res.in/explore/forestry/what.htm" ;
    :definitionText "A complex ecosystem consisting mainly of trees that buffer the earth and support a myriad of life forms. http://edugreen.teri.res.in/explore/forestry/what.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_056
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.un.org/esa/socdev/unpfii/documents/6session_crp6.doc" ;
    :definitionText "A complex, self-regenerating system, encompassing soil, water, microclimate, energy, and a wide variety of plants and animals in a mutual relationship. Plantations, on the other hand, have one or a few species of trees/crops (often alien), planted in homogenous blocks of the same age. Plantation trees are much closer to industrial agricultural crops than to forests (as usually understood) or a traditional agricultural field. http://www.un.org/esa/socdev/unpfii/documents/6session_crp6.doc" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_057
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.kyagr.com/enviro_out/pesticide/pdf/302KAR28.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "A concentration of trees and related vegetation in nonurban areas characterized by natural terrain and drainage patterns. http://www.kyagr.com/enviro_out/pesticide/pdf/302KAR28.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_058
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :heightMin "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.bugwood.caes.uga.edu/glossary/" ;
    :definitionText "A continuous stand of trees > 10 m high, with interlocking crowns. There are many kinds of forests and ways to classify them, for example, by ecozone, vegetation type, climate, dominant species, conformation. http://www.bugwood.caes.uga.edu/glossary/ and http://www.worldagroforestrycentre.org/sea/AgroModels/DBases/af/" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_059
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.thealmightyguru.com/Pointless/NatureDefinitions.html" ;
    :definitionText "A dense grove of trees and underbrush covering a large tract. Grove - A small wood without underbrush. Wood - A dense grove of trees usually greater in extent than a grove and smaller than a forest. Thicket - A dense growth of shrubbery or small trees. http://www.thealmightyguru.com/Pointless/NatureDefinitions.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_060
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "A dense growth of trees and underbrush covering a large tract [Source: WWWebster Dictionary]" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_061
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.answers.com/topic/forest" ;
    :definitionText "A dense growth of trees, plants, and underbrush covering a large area. http://www.answers.com/topic/forest" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_062
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.bridgingthewatershed.org/glossary.html#d" ;
    :definitionText "A dense growth of trees, together with other plants, covering a large area. http://www.bridgingthewatershed.org/glossary.html#d" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_063
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dorsetcoppicegroup.co.uk/resources/Dorset_Coppice_Group_Glossary.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "A densely wooded area. http://www.dorsetcoppicegroup.co.uk/resources/Dorset_Coppice_Group_Glossary.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_064
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://mojavedesert.net/glossary/forest.html" ;
    :definitionText "A diverse community of plants and animals in which trees are the most conspicuous members. http://mojavedesert.net/glossary/forest.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_065
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://members.tripod.com/~nefpc/clearcut.htm" ;
    :definitionText "A diverse mix of trees and herbaceous plants, a home to wildlife, and a sanctuary for the spirit. http://members.tripod.com/~nefpc/clearcut.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_066
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "A forest (also called a wood, woodland, wold, weald, holt, frith, or firth) is an area with a high density of trees." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_067
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :heightMin "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.zamsoc.org/wp-content/uploads/2012/02/Dry-Forests-Report-Full-document.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "A forest has a canopy of trees whose crowns interlock at 10 m or higher, with variable lower layers; http://www.zamsoc.org/wp-content/uploads/2012/02/Dry-Forests-Report-Full-document.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_068
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "A forest is a dense growth of trees, together with other plants, covering a large area of land. The science concerned with the study, preservation, and management of forests is forestry." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_069
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.planetpals.com/habitats.html" ;
    :definitionText "A forest is an area with a high density of trees. Forests are also referred to as:a wood, woodland, wold, weald, holt, and firth. http://www.planetpals.com/habitats.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_070
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.pkarticleshub.com/2012/02/04/forests-–-an-imperative-resource/" ;
    :definitionText "A forest is an ecosystem-a community of plants and animals interacting with one another and with the physical environment. http://www.pkarticleshub.com/2012/02/04/forests-–-an-imperative-resource/ (26) http://www.genesisny.net/Commodity/Timber/Timberglos.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_071
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forest" ;
    :definitionText "A forest is usually an area filled with trees but any tall densely packed area of vegetation may be considered a forest, even underwater vegetation such as kelp forests, or non-vegetation such as fungi,[2] and bacteria http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forest" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_072
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.reference.com/browse/wiki/Forest" ;
    :definitionText "A forest is an area with a high density of trees. http://www.reference.com/browse/wiki/Forest" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_073
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://crosword911.com/forest.jsp?=aHR0cDovL2VuLndpa2lwZWRpYS5vcmcvd2lraS9Gb3Jlc3Q=" ;
    :definitionText "A forest, also referred to as a wood or the woods and less often as a ‘wold” (or ‘weald’), ‘holt’, or ‘firth” (or “firth”), is an area with a high density of trees. http://crosword911.com/forest.jsp?=aHR0cDovL2VuLndpa2lwZWRpYS5vcmcvd2lraS9Gb3Jlc3Q= and http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forest" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_074
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.chesco.com/~treeman/words/words-f.html" ;
    :definitionText "A highly ordered arrangement of living organisms living in, on and around (dead, dying & living) trees in such an highly ordered fashion it assures high quality survival for all. http://www.chesco.com/~treeman/words/words-f.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_075
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://figueresonline.com/csdafinal/English/publications/cdm/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "A land area with a minimum 10% tree crown coverage (or equivalent stocking level), or formerly having such tree cover and that is being naturally or artificially regenerated or is being afforested. http://figueresonline.com/csdafinal/English/publications/cdm/glossary.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_076
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.metla.fi/silvafennica/full/sf42/sf422247.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "A land spanning more than 0.5 ha with trees higher than 5 metres and a crown cover of more than 10%, or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ. For tree rows or shelterbelts, a minimum width of 20 m is required. It does not include land that is predominantly under agricultural or urban land use.” http://www.metla.fi/silvafennica/full/sf42/sf422247.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_077
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.foreignword.com/Tools/dictsrch_aff.asp?menu=Y&query=forest&src=BP&srcbox=18&go=Translate&trg=AG" ;
    :definitionText "A large area covered chiefly with trees and undergrowth or a large number or dense mass of vertical objects. http://www.foreignword.com/Tools/dictsrch_aff.asp?menu=Y&query=forest&src=BP&srcbox=18&go=Translate&trg=AG" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_078
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.cup.cam.ac.uk/esl/dictionary/default.asp?String=forest*1%2B0&ACT=SELECT" ;
    :definitionText "A large area full of trees, usually wild. http://www.cup.cam.ac.uk/esl/dictionary/default.asp?String=forest*1%2B0&ACT=SELECT" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_079
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.cup.cam.ac.uk/elt/dictionary/default.asp?String=forest*1%2B0&ACT=SELECT" ;
    :definitionText "A large area of land covered with trees and plants, usually larger than a wood, or the trees and plants themselves http://www.cup.cam.ac.uk/elt/dictionary/default.asp?String=forest*1%2B0&ACT=SELECT" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_080
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://machaut.uchicago.edu/cgi-bin/WEDT1.sh?word=forest&searchtype=default&constraint=1" ;
    :definitionText "A large area of land densely covered with trees and other plants http://machaut.uchicago.edu/cgi-bin/WEDT1.sh?word=forest&searchtype=default&constraint=1 and http://www.wordsmyth.net/cgi-bin/simplesearch.cgi?matchent=forest&matchtype=exact&matchid=-1&retall=1" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_081
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.europe.apnet.com/inscight/12031996/forest1.htm" ;
    :definitionText "A large area of land that is covered by trees and associated undergrowth, either growing wild or managed for the purpose of timber production. http://www.europe.apnet.com/inscight/12031996/forest1.htm and http://www.harcourt.com/dictionary/def/4/1/0/7/4107300.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_082
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://entomology.cornell.edu/cals/entomology/extension/outreach/upload/Daley_TeacherResource_Forest.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "A large area of trees clumped together is called a forest. http://entomology.cornell.edu/cals/entomology/extension/outreach/upload/Daley_TeacherResource_Forest.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_083
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.zmt-bremen.de/files/Downlods/marine_glossary.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "A large area thickly covered with trees. Forests grow in different conditions, although large stands of trees need temperatures above about 50 degrees F (10 degrees C) in the warmest months and an annual precipitation over 8 inches (20 cm). Forests are distinguished by their main species of trees and plants, density, and soil type. http://www.zmt-bremen.de/files/Downlods/marine_glossary.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_084
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.3datlas.com/list_gl.html" ;
    :definitionText "A large area thickly covered with trees. http://www.3datlas.com/list_gl.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_085
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.linguistics.ruhr-uni-bochum.de:8099/cgi-bin/search.sh?tmpl=tmpls&itmpl=tmpls&form=forest" ;
    :definitionText "A large area where trees grow close together. http://www.linguistics.ruhr-uni-bochum.de:8099/cgi-bin/search.sh?tmpl=tmpls&itmpl=tmpls&form=forest" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_086
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://nhd.heinle.com/nhd-bin/searchNHD.pl" ;
    :definitionText "A large area with many trees. http://nhd.heinle.com/nhd-bin/searchNHD.pl" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_087
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://scstsenvis.nic.in/envis/SDNPnewsletter.htm" ;
    :definitionText "A large tract of land covered with the different types of plant forms like shrubs, herbs and trees. http://scstsenvis.nic.in/envis/SDNPnewsletter.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_088
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.lpb.org/programs/forestseries/pforser_glossary.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "A large tract of land covered with trees and underbrush http://www.lpb.org/programs/forestseries/pforser_glossary.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_089
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "A large tract of land covered with trees: more exactly, a tract of land, more or less extensive, covered more or less densely with trees of useful character, viewed from the standpoint of economic use and development. SAF 1916 (Helms 2002)." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_090
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.mpl.ird.fr/crea/taller-colombia/FAO/AGLL/pdfdocs/landglos.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "A large tract of land with a fairly dense growth of trees. http://www.mpl.ird.fr/crea/taller-colombia/FAO/AGLL/pdfdocs/landglos.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_091
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.iapad.org/publications/ppgis/landglossary.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "A large tract of land with a fairly dense growth of trees. This differs in degree from woodland, which tends to refer more to open forests (Choudhury & Jansen 1998 and Timberlake & van der Poel 1979). http://www.iapad.org/publications/ppgis/landglossary.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_092
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://dictionary.reverso.net/english-definition/forest%20reserve" ;
    :definitionText "A large wooded area having a thick growth of trees and plants http://dictionary.reverso.net/english-definition/forest%20reserve" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_093
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.abanet.org/environ/committees/forest/Public%20Service%20Project%20UZ%20Forest.DOC" ;
    :definitionText "A living community of flora (plants) and fauna (animals) dominated by trees. http://www.abanet.org/environ/committees/forest/Public%20Service%20Project%20UZ%20Forest.DOC" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_094
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.lucs.lu.se/LUCS/020/LUCS.020.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "A natural place where trees grow http://www.lucs.lu.se/LUCS/020/LUCS.020.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_095
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.globalff.org/Feature_Articles/Previous_Articles/pre-defo.htm" ;
    :definitionText "A natural, self-sustaining community characterized by vertical structure created by the presence of trees. (http://www.globalff.org/Feature_Articles/Previous_Articles/pre-defo.htm and http://www.geocities.com/atlas/word/gff_deforest.html)" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_096
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://hassam.hubpages.com/hub/Types-Of-Forests" ;
    :definitionText "A piece of land that is thickly covered with trees is the general of definition of a forest. Forest is also known as woods, weald or woodlands. http://hassam.hubpages.com/hub/Types-Of-Forests" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_097
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://wings.ucdavis.edu/Book/Atmosphere/beginner/deforestation-01.html" ;
    :definitionText "A place with many trees and plants. http://wings.ucdavis.edu/Book/Atmosphere/beginner/deforestation-01.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_098
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.morcd.org/totorcd/Forestry%20Terms.htm" ;
    :definitionText "A plant and animal community dominated by trees. http://www.morcd.org/totorcd/Forestry%20Terms.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_099
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.inwoodlands.org" ;
    :definitionText "A plant association predominantly of trees and other woody vegetation. http://www.inwoodlands.org /, http://agebb.missouri.edu/mfgc/contest/glossary.htm, and http://www.fnr.purdue.edu/inwood/glossary.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_100
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "A plant association predominatly of trees and other woody vegetation occupying an extensive area of land. SF 1944, 1958. (Helms 2002)" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_101
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ag.iastate.edu/departments/forestry/ext/dictionary.html" ;
    :definitionText "A plant community dominated by trees and other wood plants. http://www.ag.iastate.edu/departments/forestry/ext/dictionary.html and http://muextension.missouri.edu/xplor/agguides/forestry/g05054.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_102
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.washingtonforests.com/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "A plant community dominated by trees and other woody plants. http://www.washingtonforests.com/glossary.html Washington Forest Protection Association, http://www.idahoforests.org/dict1.htm the Idaho Forest, and http://ext.msstate.edu/pubs/pub1250.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_103
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://msucares.com/pubs/pub1250.htm" ;
    :definitionText "A plant community dominated by trees and woody plants. From a management standpoint, a forest is a collection of stands administered as a unit. http://msucares.com/pubs/pub1250.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_104
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://research.yale.edu/gisf/assets/pdf/tfd/IFIR_report.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "A plant community of predominantly trees and other woody vegetation growing together, its land, flora and fauna, their interrelationships, and other resources and values attributed to it. http://research.yale.edu/gisf/assets/pdf/tfd/IFIR_report.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_105
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.cnr.vt.edu/for3364/ecolterms.htm#F" ;
    :definitionText "A plant community predominately of trees and other woody vegetation growing more closely together. http://www.cnr.vt.edu/for3364/ecolterms.htm#F, http://www.cofi.org/factbook98/seven/7-4.htm and SAF 1971 (Helms 2002)" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_106
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.chesco.com/~treeman/words/words-f.html" ;
    :definitionText "A system, where trees and their associates are so highly ordered in their connections that they all survive at a high quality state. http://www.chesco.com/~treeman/words/words-f.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_107
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.yourdictionary.com/forest" ;
    :definitionText "A thick growth of trees and underbrush covering an extensive tract of land; large woods: often used figuratively. http://www.yourdictionary.com/forest" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_108
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://pittsford.monroe.edu/jefferson/calfieri/maps&globes/Glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "A thick growth of trees in an area http://pittsford.monroe.edu/jefferson/calfieri/maps&globes/Glossary.html and http://www.mcwdn.org/MAPS&GLOBES/Glossary.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_109
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.wordsmyth.net/cgi-bin/simplesearch.cgi?matchent=forestland&matchtype=exact&matchid=-1&retall=1" ;
    :definitionText "A tract of land covered by a forest. http://www.wordsmyth.net/cgi-bin/simplesearch.cgi?matchent=forestland&matchtype=exact&matchid=-1&retall=1" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_110
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.planning.org/guidebookhtm/chapter_three.htm" ;
    :definitionText "A tract or tracts of contiguous trees or tree stands. http://www.planning.org/guidebookhtm/chapter_three.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_111
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://targetstudy.com/nature/habitats/forests/" ;
    :definitionText "A type of habitat or biome which has a high density of trees. http://targetstudy.com/nature/habitats/forests/" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_112
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "A type of vegetation dominated by trees and without narrow-leaved grasses in the herbaceous layer (Hamilton 1991)." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_113
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://oaspub.epa.gov/trs/trs_proc_qry.alphabet?p_term_nm=F" ;
    :definitionText "A vegetation community dominated by trees and other woody shrubs, growing close enough together that the tree tops touch or overlap, creating various degrees of shade on the forest floor. It may produce benefits such as timber, recreation, wildlife habitat, etc. European Environment Agency (EEA), European Topic Centre on Catalogue of Data Sources (ETC/CDS) : General Multilingual Environmental Thesaurus Term Detail http://oaspub.epa.gov/trs/trs_proc_qry.alphabet?p_term_nm=F." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_114
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://sedac.ciesin.org/guides/lu/glossary.jsp" ;
    :definitionText "All lands with a tree canopy density of more than 10%, though they may not be statutorily notified as forest. http://sedac.ciesin.org/guides/lu/glossary.jsp" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_115
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://envfor.nic.in/nfc/s-git.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "All lands, more than one hectare in area, with a tree canopy density of more than 10 percent. Such lands may not be statutorily notified as forest area. http://envfor.nic.in/nfc/s-git.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_116
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :heightMin "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "All vegetation comprising a continuous stand of trees at least 10m tall with interlocking crowns (White 1983)." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_117
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://sapiens.revues.org/734" ;
    :definitionText "An aggregate of trees, which grow near-by, affect each other and the surrounding space and, therefore, are changing their outside and inner structure Russian forestry scientist G.Morozov (1930) http://sapiens.revues.org/734" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_118
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.inhs.uiuc.edu/chf/pub/virtualbird/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "An area covered with many trees and plants. http://www.inhs.uiuc.edu/chf/pub/virtualbird/glossary.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_119
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.forestry.ubc.ca/concert/ashton.html#21" ;
    :definitionText "An area grown with trees. http://www.forestry.ubc.ca/concert/ashton.html#21" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_120
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.enchantedlearning.com/subjects/plants/glossary/indexf.shtml" ;
    :definitionText "An area in which trees are the dominant plant. http://www.enchantedlearning.com/subjects/plants/glossary/indexf.shtml" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_121
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.forestry.sa.gov.au/pdf/glossary.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "An area of land covered by trees; forests can be natural or planted. http://www.forestry.sa.gov.au/pdf/glossary.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_122
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://ohia.com/ohia/roadshows/sky/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "An area of land covered largely with trees. Forests are vital parts of our global ecosystem supplying oxygen, habitat for wildlife, timber and recreation areas. http://ohia.com/ohia/roadshows/sky/glossary.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_123
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "An area of tree-covered land typically consisting of hundreds or thousands (or more) of individual stands comprising trees of similar species composition, age-structure and management regime (Apps and Price 1996)." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_124
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://ehe.nmsu.edu/directory/esource/Powerpoint/HORT%20302-02a%20Definitions%20&%20Tools.ppt" ;
    :definitionText "An area supporting trees, ordinarily including multiple ages, species, and conditions. http://ehe.nmsu.edu/directory/esource/Powerpoint/HORT%20302-02a%20Definitions%20&%20Tools.ppt" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_125
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://dspace.wbpublibnet.gov.in/dspace/bitstream/10689/10100/4/Chapter%201_1%20-%20125p.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "An area which contain wild growing trees (19th century). http://dspace.wbpublibnet.gov.in/dspace/bitstream/10689/10100/4/Chapter%201_1%20-%20125p.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_126
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "An area whose principle crop is trees. A forest includes both the forest cover and the soil beneath it. (Moon and Courtlandt 1914)." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_127
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://explanation-guide.info/meaning/Forest.htm" ;
    :definitionText "An area with a high density of trees http://explanation-guide.info/meaning/Forest.htm and http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forest" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_128
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.mepred.eu/_docs/Triangel1.4.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "An area with a high density of trees. http://www.mepred.eu/_docs/Triangel1.4.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_129
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.sandiegozoo.org/wildideas/glossary_e-f.html" ;
    :definitionText "An area with many trees. http://www.sandiegozoo.org/wildideas/glossary_e-f.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_130
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.foresthistory.org/ASPNET/Publications/CCCforestry/contents.htm" ;
    :definitionText "An association of trees (as in large plantations with no undergrowth), or shrubs (as in the watersheds of the Southwest), or both (as in the hardwood and mixed forests), growing on a considerable area, upon which it is possible to practice forestry. http://www.foresthistory.org/ASPNET/Publications/CCCforestry/contents.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_131
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.evergreentheatre.com/forests.htm" ;
    :definitionText "An ecosystem characterised by more or less continuous tree cover. However, a forest is more than trees - a forest also includes shrubs, vines, herbs, mosses, microorganisms, insects and other animals, which interact among themselves and with their environment. The type of forest is defined by either geography or climate (e.g., tropical, boreal - another word for northern -or coastal) or for the predominant tree found in that forest (coniferous, deciduous or mixed). http://www.evergreentheatre.co" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_132
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "Alexander.Korotkov@unece.org" ;
    :definitionText "An ecosystem characterised by more or less dense and extensive tree cover. From: Alexander.Korotkov@unece.org. Date: Thu, 15 Oct 1998 17:09:40 +0200 and SAF 1971 (Helms 2002)" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_133
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://nfdp.ccfm.org/silviterm/silvi_e/silvitermetohe.htm#F" ;
    :definitionText "An ecosystem characterized by a more or less dense and extensive tree cover. More particularly, a plant community predominantly of trees and other woody vegetation, growing more or less closely together. http://nfdp.ccfm.org/silviterm/silvi_e/silvitermetohe.htm#F" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_134
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "An ecosystem characterized by more or less dense and extensive tree cover usually consisting of stands varying in characteristics such as species, structure, composition, age class, and commonly including streams, fish, and wildlife… SAF 1998 (Helms 2002)" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_135
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://figueresonline.com/csdafinal/English/publications/cdm/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "An ecosystem characterized by trees or a plant community in which trees predominate (from the Latin word meaning outside the door). http://figueresonline.com/csdafinal/English/publications/cdm/glossary.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_136
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://forestinfo.org/sust.htm" ;
    :definitionText "An ecosystem dominated by trees, with a unique combination of plants, animals, microbes, soil, and climate. http://forestinfo.org/sust.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_137
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.museum.state.il.us/muslink/forest/htmls/intro_def.html" ;
    :definitionText "An ecosystem or assemblage of ecosystems dominated by trees and other woody vegetation. http://www.museum.state.il.us/muslink/forest/htmls/intro_def.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_138
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fscus.org/html/about_fsc/who_we_are/glossary_of_terms.html" ;
    :definitionText "An ecosystem that, when intact, is characterized by tree cover usually consisting of stands varying in characteristics such as species, structure, composition, age-class, and commonly including streams, and wildlife. While forest ecosystems are not bound by property lines, for the purpose of this document, \"forest\" may be delimited by ownership or other qualifying characteristics. http://www.fscus.org/html/about_fsc/who_we_are/glossary_of_terms.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_139
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "An ecosystem with a minimum level of tree cover that is generally associated with wild flora, fauna and natural soil conditions, and not subject to agricultural practices (Gardner-Outlaw and Engelman 1998)" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_140
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.taxbar.com/tr/jaggers.htm" ;
    :definitionText "An extensive area of land covered with trees and undergrowth. Shorter Oxford English Dictionary http://www.taxbar.com/tr/jaggers.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_141
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.britell.com/lex.html" ;
    :definitionText "An extensive plant community in all stages of growth with a closed canopy, having the quality of self perpetuation and of potential development into an ecological climax. http://www.britell.com/lex.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_142
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.for.nau.edu/courses/for250/Definitions/Definitions.html" ;
    :definitionText "An extensive wood or tract of wooded country. http://www.for.nau.edu/courses/for250/Definitions/Definitions.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_143
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.christiantech.com/cgi-bin/webster.exe?search_for_cgi-bin_texts_web1828=forest" ;
    :definitionText "An extensive wood, or a large tract of land covered with trees. In America, the word is usually applied to a wood of native growth, or a tract of woodland which has never been cultivated. It differs from wood or woods chiefly in extent http://www.christiantech.com/cgi-bin/webster.exe?search_for_cgi-bin_texts_web1828=forest" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_144
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://machaut.uchicago.edu/cgi-bin/WEBSTER.sh?WORD=forest" ;
    :definitionText "An extensive wood; a large tract of land covered with trees; in the United States, a wood of native growth, or a tract of woodland which has never been cultivated. http://machaut.uchicago.edu/cgi-bin/WEBSTER.sh?WORD=forest and http://www.graylab.ac.uk/cgi-bin/omd?forest" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_145
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.forestcouncil.org/fv/fv103/article6.html" ;
    :definitionText "An interconnected web that focuses on sustaining the whole, not on producing any one part or commodity. Trees are critical structural members of the forest web, and also—from the human viewpoint—the most obvious component of a forest. However, trees are only a small portion of the whole that creates a fully functioning forest. A forest also consists of animals, plants, and microorganisms, arranged in infinite diversity across scales that range from soil bacteria to the continents of Earth. We ne" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_146
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.cbnrm.net/pdf/mutanga_e_001_forestmgmt.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "An open system with naturally occurring flora and fauna species which are interrelated and depends on one another for their survival. http://www.cbnrm.net/pdf/mutanga_e_001_forestmgmt.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_147
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.panda.org/forests4life/whatisforest.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Any area with over 40 per cent crown cover. This works well with broadleaf or mixed coniferous and broadleaf forests but less well with purely coniferous forests, where canopy cover is often less than 40 per cent. http://www.panda.org/forests4life/whatisforest.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_148
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.logos.it/pls/dictionary/new_dictionary.dic.main" ;
    :definitionText "Area of land covered by standing trees http://www.logos.it/pls/dictionary/new_dictionary.dic.main" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_149
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://crossword911.com/forest.html" ;
    :definitionText "Area thick with trees. http://crossword911.com/forest.html." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_150
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "25.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "6.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.maced.org/ardc/frm/about.htm#input" ;
    :definitionText "Areas characterized by tree cover (natural or semi-natural woody vegetation, generally greater than 6 meters tall); tree canopy accounts for 25-100 percent of the cover. http://www.maced.org/ardc/frm/about.htm#input and http://pubs.usgs.gov/wri/wri024301/pdf/wri02-4301.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_151
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "61.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.gap.uidaho.edu/handbook/LandCoverMapping/UNESCO/default.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Areas dominated by trees with a total canopy cover of 61 % or more, tree crowns usually interlocking. http://www.gap.uidaho.edu/handbook/LandCoverMapping/UNESCO/default.htm and http://www.cast.uark.edu/cast/projects/gap/landcover/foti.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_152
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :heightMin "6.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://home.comcast.net/~gyde/africover.html" ;
    :definitionText "Areas on which vegetation is dominated by woody perennial plants having 6 meters in height or greater. Examples are loblolly pine forests, black spruce swamps, live oak stands, pinyon-juniper, maple, hickory, larch, and birch. Includes areas on which vegetation is dominated by orchards or groves for fruit or nut production such as citrus, apples, peaches, pecans, filberts, trees grown primarily for Christmas trees, nurseries and arboretums. (http://home.comcast.net/~gyde/africover.html)" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_153
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "Areas where trees have grown naturally for centuries instead of being logged (about 150-200 years). Lindley and Moore 1998." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_154
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://sedac.ciesin.org/guides/lu/glossary.jsp" ;
    :definitionText "Areas with a? minimum of 10% crown cover of trees and/or bamboos, generally associated with wild flora and fauna and natural soil conditions, and are not subject to agricultural practices. Note that in some countries, some areas are statutorily defined as ?Forest Area? that contain no tree cover http://sedac.ciesin.org/guides/lu/glossary.jsp" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_155
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.millenniumassessment.org/documents/document.290.aspx.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Areas with substantially higher levels of canopy closure, for example 30–40%, depending on age, in Russia (FFSR 1995) and 60% in South Africa (Scholes 2004). http://www.millenniumassessment.org/documents/document.290.aspx.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_156
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "Assemblages of ecosystems comprised of trees, other vegetation, litter and soils, each having its own temporal dynamics, carbon storage patterns, and carbon release rates to the atmosphere. [Source: FCCC/SBSTA/1998/INF.1, 18 May 1998]" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_157
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "Bosque - Dentro de la categoriav”‘Formacion “ (anexo III.6). Vegetacion predominantemente arbborea, principalmente de zonas templadas a semifrias, en climas subhumedos a much humedos. Se caracterizan por tener especies arboreaas dominates con afinidad boreal. Incluye cuatro tipos de vegetacion: Bosque de conifereas, Gosque de conifereas y latifoliadas, Gosque de latfoliadas y Bosque mesofilo, y ocho comunidades: Bosquede tgascate, Bosque de oyamel (incluye ayarin yh cedro), Bosque de pino, Mator" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_158
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.allwords.com/query.asp#AHD" ;
    :definitionText "Bota plant community extending over a large area and dominated by trees, the crowns of which form an unbroken covering layer or canopy. http://www.allwords.com/query.asp#AHD" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_159
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "60.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.gisdevelopment.net/aars/acrs/1995/ts6/ts6003pf.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Canopy cover is > 60%. Tree height is exceeding 2 (3) meters. http://www.gisdevelopment.net/aars/acrs/1995/ts6/ts6003pf.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_160
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://ewg.gecp.virginia.edu/ewg_forest_us/general/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Combination of trees, scrub, grass, and other types of plants, as well as animals and microorganisms that are interrelated biologically in their growth and provide impact on each other and the environment. The term \"forest\" is used also to describe a landscape component, raw material, or an object of forestry management activities. Minimum Mapping Unit of 0.5 hectares. http://ewg.gecp.virginia.edu/ewg_forest_us/general/glossary.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_161
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fs.fed.us/ne/delaware/ilpin/ilpin.descript.txt" ;
    :definitionText "Community dominated by trees, 80% or better average canopy cover. Dr. Louis R. Iverson ILPIN http://www.fs.fed.us/ne/delaware/ilpin/ilpin.descript.txt" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_162
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.savannas.org.uk/savdef.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Complete tree canopy cover and three or more overlapping vegetation strata http://www.savannas.org.uk/savdef.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_163
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "Complex, ecological system in which trees are the dominant life form. Encyclopedia Britannia 1995" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_164
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :heightMin "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://hss.ulb.uni-bonn.de/2007/1280/1280.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Continuous stands of trees at least 10 meters tall, with interlocking crowns. Wass (1995 p. 1)http://hss.ulb.uni-bonn.de/2007/1280/1280.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_165
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "De manière analogue, parle d'une \"grande étendue de terrain couverte d'arbres, ensemble des grands arbres qui occupent et couvrent cette étendue. Le Larousse. Sandrine PETIT." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_166
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.enchantedlearning.com/subjects/butterfly/glossary/indexf.shtml" ;
    :definitionText "Dense concentrations of trees over a large area of land. http://www.enchantedlearning.com/subjects/butterfly/glossary/indexf.shtml and http://www.ZoomDinosaurs.com/subjects/rainforest/" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_167
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "Dense growth of trees and shrubs. Colliers Encyclopedia." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_168
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://crossword911.com/forest.html" ;
    :definitionText "Dense woodland – http://crossword911.com/forest.html. ." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_169
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.Colorado.Edu/INSTAAR/TEAML/atlas/chapters/definitions.html#Forest" ;
    :definitionText "Ecosystem characterized by more or less dense and extensive tree cover, i.e., larger than what might be called a grove. http://www.Colorado.Edu/INSTAAR/TEAML/atlas/chapters/definitions.html#Forest and http://www.arcticatlas.org/glossary/index" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_170
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.geog.ouc.bc.ca/conted/onlinecourses/enviroglos/f.html#anchor244824" ;
    :definitionText "Ecosystem dominated by trees. Major forest biomes include tropical evergreen forest, tropical savanna, deciduous forest, and boreal forest. http://www.geog.ouc.bc.ca/conted/onlinecourses/enviroglos/f.html#anchor244824 and http://www.physicalgeography.net/physgeoglos/f.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_171
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "Ecosystems dominated by trees usually having single stems, stand height exceeding 2m and with crown cover of overstorey strata about ≥ 20% (Australian National Forest Inventory). Ranges of crown cover used by the Australian National Forest Inventory are: open forest: 51-80% closed forest: 81-100%" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_172
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://info.sjc.ox.ac.uk/forests/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Extensive area of woodland (L 237) http://info.sjc.ox.ac.uk/forests/glossary.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_173
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.suzano.com.br/docs/recursos/maneucal/glossar.html" ;
    :definitionText "Floresta- Complexo vegetal primitivo ou implantado, com espécies nativas ou exóticas que possuam em sua porção dominante, porte arbóreo. http://www.suzano.com.br/docs/recursos/maneucal/glossar.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_174
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.suzano.com.br/docs/recursos/maneucal/glossar.html" ;
    :definitionText "Florestar - Promover a cobertura vegetal com espécies arbóreas em áreas onde esta tipologia florestal não era de ocorrência típica. http://www.suzano.com.br/docs/recursos/maneucal/glossar.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_175
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "26.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fish.washington.edu/naturemapping/wildlife/1cls9.html" ;
    :definitionText "Forest - 1- Open; 26-60% canopy closure. 2 - Closed; 60-100% canopy closure. Urban areas with a lot of large trees are not forests. http://www.fish.washington.edu/naturemapping/wildlife/1cls9.html." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_176
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nature.com/news/2009/090819/full/news.2009.842.html" ;
    :definitionText "Forest - Sasaki says that the minimum threshold for canopy cover should be raised to 40%, the minimum tree height should be 5 metres and that natural forests should be differentiated from plantations. http://www.nature.com/news/2009/090819/full/news.2009.842.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_177
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "70.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.cis.rit.edu/DocumentLibrary/admin/uploads/CIS000209.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Forest >70% cover - http://www.cis.rit.edu/DocumentLibrary/admin/uploads/CIS000209.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_178
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://icaci.org/files/documents/ICC_proceedings/ICC2013/_extendedAbstract/131_proceeding.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Forest: 76-100% Tree cover up to 20+ m. http://icaci.org/files/documents/ICC_proceedings/ICC2013/_extendedAbstract/131_proceeding.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_179
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "100.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://greenplanet.eolss.net/EolssLogn/mss/C12/E1-02/E1-02-15/E1-02-15-TXT.aspx#Glossary" ;
    :definitionText "Forest Cover - (Tree cover or canopy cover) The proportion of the land area which has foliage or canopy directly overhead. Thus a dense, closed forest would have 100 percent canopy cover while a woodland of scattered trees might have 5 percent or 10 percent cover. http://greenplanet.eolss.net/EolssLogn/mss/C12/E1-02/E1-02-15/E1-02-15-TXT.aspx#Glossary" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_180
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.cambridge.org/aus/catalogue/catalogue.asp?isbn=9780521834520&ss=exc" ;
    :definitionText "Forest cover in world regions, defined as including all natural forests and plantations. Taken from FAO (2005) http://www.cambridge.org/aus/catalogue/catalogue.asp?isbn=9780521834520&ss=exc" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_181
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fw.vt.edu/zedaker/3364/ecolterms.html" ;
    :definitionText "FOREST COVER: (1) All trees and other plants occupying the ground in a forest, i.e. including any ground cover. NOTE: Is the silviculturist's crop viewed from the ecologist's angle. (2) All woody growth occupying the ground in a forest, as distinct from the ground cover NOTE: Is the silviculturist's forest crop viewed from the ecologist's angle. (3) A category of forest site, including all the interchangeable phases of vegetation that it supports, defined mainly by the general nature of the grou" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_182
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.clayoquot.org/glossary.htm#F" ;
    :definitionText "Forest cover: forest stands or cover types consisting of a plant community made up of trees and other woody vegetation, growing more or less closely together http://www.clayoquot.org/glossary.htm#F" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_183
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.mckone.org/tfrrung.html" ;
    :definitionText "Forest includes woodland and other similar vegetation formations. http://www.mckone.org/tfrrung.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_184
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :areaMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://192.83.171.71/newcrons/navig/en/theme8/milieu/10fo/notmeth.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Forest land comprises the actual forests areas dominated by trees or shrubs capable of producing wood or other forest products. Minimum surface area is: 0,5 ha. Areas should be covered by forest trees for at least 20% measured as the vertical projection from the trees for a mature stand. Unstocked forest land includes areas which are not themselves productive but necessary for production. http://192.83.171.71/newcrons/navig/en/theme8/milieu/10fo/notmeth.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_185
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "Forest land currently stocked with trees. Encyclopedia Britannia 1970" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_186
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.geog.umd.edu/tropical/per80v141README" ;
    :definitionText "Forest refers to primarily closed canopy humid tropical forest, and includes cloud forest. http://www.geog.umd.edu/tropical/per80v141README" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_187
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://ma.caudillweb.com/proxy/Document.782.aspx" ;
    :definitionText "Forest systems: Systems in which trees are the predominant life forms. Statistics reported in this assessment are based on areas that are dominated by trees (perennial woody plants taller than five meters at maturity), where the tree crown cover exceeds 10%, and where the area is more than 0.5 hectares. ‘‘Open forests’’ have a canopy cover between 10% and 40%, and ‘‘closed forests’’ a canopy cover of more than 40%. ‘‘Fragmented forests’’ refer to mosaics of forest patches and non-forest land. ht" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_188
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "60.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.esd.ornl.gov/projects/qen/veg.html" ;
    :definitionText "FOREST VEGETATION; more than 60% canopy (leaf/branch) cover above a level 8m off the ground http://www.esd.ornl.gov/projects/qen/veg.html A suggestion for an improved vegetation scheme for local and global mapping and monitoring. Jonathan M. Adams Submitted to Environmental Management, January 1998." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_189
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.notredame.ac.jp/cgi-bin/wn?forest" ;
    :definitionText "Forest, woodland, timberland, timber -- (land that is covered with trees and shrubs) http://www.notredame.ac.jp/cgi-bin/wn?forest" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_190
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "60.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.museum.state.il.us/muslink/forest/htmls/intro_def.html" ;
    :definitionText "Forests (according to the U.S. National Vegetation Classification system) consist of trees with overlapping crowns forming 60% to 100% cover. Woodlands are more open, with 25% to 60% cover. http://www.museum.state.il.us/muslink/forest/htmls/intro_def.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_191
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.iea.org.uk/books/envindicators.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Forests (more accurately called woods) are areas covered in dense tree growth. http://www.iea.org.uk/books/envindicators.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_192
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.conservation.org/osiris/Documents/DNPI%20Green%20Review%20on%20REDD+.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Forests are described as non-annual plants reaching a height of minimum 5 m and with a crown cover of more than 30 percent of a defined area, normally one hectare. http://www.conservation.org/osiris/Documents/DNPI%20Green%20Review%20on%20REDD+.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_193
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fs.fed.us/research/publications/forest_production_for_tropical_america/appendix_d.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Forests differ from woodlands in that they have continuous canopies, gaps between the tree crowns and the ground, and juvenile trees http://www.fs.fed.us/research/publications/forest_production_for_tropical_america/appendix_d.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_194
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "70.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "8.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "Fôret Claire (woodland) - Woody plants > 8 m ht., 70-90% canopy cover. Yangambi Classification 1956. (Fournier 1991)." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_195
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.gap.uidaho.edu/handbook/LandCoverAssessment/Appendix5/default.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Generally 60% tree canopy with crowns interlocking. http://www.gap.uidaho.edu/handbook/LandCoverAssessment/Appendix5/default.htm and http://www.extension.iastate.edu/naturemapping/naturemapping_process/habitat_codes.html#forest" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_196
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.cnr.vt.edu/for3364/ecolterms.htm#F" ;
    :definitionText "Generally, an ecosystem characterized by a more or less dense and extensive tree cover. (2) More particularly, a plant community predominately of trees and other woody vegetation, growing more or less closely together. http://www.cnr.vt.edu/for3364/ecolterms.htm#F, http://www.fw.vt.edu/zedaker/3364/ecolterms.html and Ford-Robertson 1971: 107, 298 and http://www.fw.vt.edu/zedaker/3364/ecolterms.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_197
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://figueresonline.com/csdafinal/English/publications/cdm/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "Generally, that portion of the ecosystem characterized by tree cover; more particularly, a plant community predominantly of trees and other woody vegetation growing close together. http://figueresonline.com/csdafinal/English/publications/cdm/glossary.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_198
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.scopenvironment.org/downloadpubs/scope56/Chapter04.html" ;
    :definitionText "Have complete tree canopy cover and three or more overlapping vegetation strata; http://www.scopenvironment.org/downloadpubs/scope56/Chapter04.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_199
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "Having a closed canopy beneath which grasses do not grow. These are distinct form open-canopied woodlands that grow over a grass sward (IUCN and WCMC 1990)." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_200
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://ccel.wheaton.edu/pager.cgi?file=e/easton/ebd/ebd/T0001300.html&from=T0001374&up=e/easton/ebd/ebd.html" ;
    :definitionText "Heb. ya'ar, meaning a dense wood, from its luxuriance. http://ccel.wheaton.edu/pager.cgi?file=e/easton/ebd/ebd/T0001300.html&from=T0001374&up=e/easton/ebd/ebd.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_201
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.botany.uwc.ac.za/envfacts/facts/deforestation.htm" ;
    :definitionText "In a forest the crowns of individual trees touch to form a single canopy. In a woodland, trees grow far apart, so that the canopy is open. http://www.botany.uwc.ac.za/envfacts/facts/deforestation.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_202
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.globaled.org/issues/152/a.html" ;
    :definitionText "In a forest, the treetops touch each other to form a canopy, Woodlands, trees are spaced further apart. http://www.globaled.org/issues/152/a.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_203
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.wildlifetrust.org.uk/suffolk/redgrave/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "In England this means a wood with no coppiced trees, often conifer Plantations. Traditionally meant a hunting ground or 'chase' Nature Conservation Glossary http://www.wildlifetrust.org.uk/suffolk/redgrave/glossary.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_204
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.aces.edu/waterquality/glossary/glossary_results.php3?rowid=2008" ;
    :definitionText "In general, an area or biotic community dominated by trees of any size (usually, at least 10 percent of the area is covered by trees). If distinction is made to woodlands, forests are composed of taller, more closely-spaced trees. http://www.aces.edu/waterquality/glossary/glossary_results.php3?rowid=2008 and http://www.rmrs.nau.edu/publications/rm_gtr_295/glossary.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_205
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.arcticatlas.org/glossary/index" ;
    :definitionText "In the Preliminary Classification for Alaskan Vegetation, vegetation with at least a 10% crown cover by trees; i.e., single stemmed woody plants at least 5 m in height at maturity. http://www.arcticatlas.org/glossary/index." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_206
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.biology-online.org/dictionary/Forest" ;
    :definitionText "In the United States, a wood of native growth, or a tract of woodland which has never been cultivated. http://www.biology-online.org/dictionary/Forest" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_207
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.wilderness.org.au/projects/Forests/forbkgnd.html" ;
    :definitionText "Includes mangroves (which, along with rainforest, form 'closed forest'), and forest-forming mallees (which, along with schlerophyll forest, form 'open forest'). http://www.wilderness.org.au/projects/Forests/forbkgnd.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_208
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "50.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.wilderness.org.au/projects/Forests/forbkgnd.html" ;
    :definitionText "Includes sclerophyll forest ('hard-leaved' trees, mainly forests dominated by eucalypts, but also species like acacias and melaleucas) which has a canopy cover greater than 50%, and all rainforest. http://www.wilderness.org.au/projects/Forests/forbkgnd.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_209
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.wilderness.org.au/projects/Forests/forbkgnd.html" ;
    :definitionText "Includes woodlands and woodland-forming mallees (this is the definition now adopted by the Commonwealth Government - see NFI 1998, pp.10-11). http://www.wilderness.org.au/projects/Forests/forbkgnd.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_210
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://library.advanced.org/17456/main1.html" ;
    :definitionText "Interconnected communities of diverse organisms -- bacteria and fungi, gigantic trees, birds, shrubs, ants and beetles, fish, and mammals. http://library.advanced.org/17456/main1.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_211
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "La forêt est un formation végétale dans laquelle les arbres prédominent au point de modifier les conditions écologiques régnant au sol. Elle est dite dense ou fermée si les arbres (ou mieux la projection de leurs cimes sur le sol) sont jointifs ou occupent plus des 2/3 de la surface, claire et ouverte si les arbres couvrent de 2/3 à 1/4 de la surface. Les autres formations sont par définition exclues des forêts. l'Encyclopédia Universalis. Sandrine PETIT" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_212
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.pbs.org/earthonedge/ecosystems/forests1.html" ;
    :definitionText "Land areas \"dominated by trees where the tree canopy covers at least 10% of the ground area. http://www.pbs.org/earthonedge/ecosystems/forests1.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_213
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :heightMin "1.83"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.wvgazette.com/static/series/mining/reports/EIS/VIII.Glossary.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Land bearing a stand of trees of any stature, including seedlings, and of species attaining a minimum of 6 feet average height at maturity or land from which such a stand has been removed but on which no other use has been substituted. The term is commonly limited to land not in farms; forests on farms are commonly called woodland or farm forest. http://www.wvgazette.com/static/series/mining/reports/EIS/VIII.Glossary.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_214
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.uncg.edu/bio/ConBio105/info/glossary2.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Land bearing forest growth. http://www.uncg.edu/bio/ConBio105/info/glossary2.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_215
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :heightMin "7.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.usangu.org/reports/landres.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Land covered by a closed stand of trees of one or more storeys, with an interlaced upper canopy, rising to 7 - 40 m or more in height. The ground cover is dominated by herbs and shrubs, and lianes and epiphytes are characteristic. Dwarf forests are as defined but rise to less than 7 m in height. Sub-types are sub-alpine dwarf forest (2 500 - 3 500 m); lowland forest (<1 000 m); and groundwater forest. http://www.usangu.org/reports/landres.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_216
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://ag.arizona.edu/arec/pubs/rmg/2._Rangeland_Management_/4Terms.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Land on which the vegetation is dominated by trees. Lands shall be classified forestland if the trees now present will provide 25% or greater canopy cover at maturity. RANGELAND TERMINOLOGY http://ag.arizona.edu/arec/pubs/rmg/2._Rangeland_Management_/4Terms.pdf and http://www.agroselviter.unito.it/range/docs/4Terms.pdf and http://ag.arizona.edu/AREC/pubs/rmg/2._Rangeland_Management_/4Terms.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_217
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://dictionary.kids.net.au/word/forest" ;
    :definitionText "Land that is covered with trees and shrubs http://dictionary.kids.net.au/word/forest and http://www.scrabblefinder.com/word/forest/" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_218
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://src.doc.ic.ac.uk/packages/Project-Gutenberg/etext99/world97.txt" ;
    :definitionText "Land under dense stands of trees. Paraphrased from http://src.doc.ic.ac.uk/packages/Project-Gutenberg/etext99/world97.txt" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_219
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "25.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://rmmcweb.cr.usgs.gov/public/mrgb/mrgblulcdefs.html#vg4.11" ;
    :definitionText "Land where trees form at least 25% of the canopy cover http://rmmcweb.cr.usgs.gov/public/mrgb/mrgblulcdefs.html#vg4.11" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_220
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.cei-bois.org/files/FINAL_-_BoA_-_EN_-_2011_text_and_cover.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Land with tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 10% and area of more than 0.5 ha. The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of at least 5m at maturity in situ. http://www.cei-bois.org/files/FINAL_-_BoA_-_EN_-_2011_text_and_cover.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_221
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "7.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://books.google.com/books?id=zeTU8QauENcC&pg=PA192&lpg=PA192&dq=Germany+Forest+definition+define+%22forest+is%22+law+act+code&source=bl&ots=1jUsKaLHy4&sig=uRBHD83hyloLheFqPmfiDgK687o&hl=en&sa=X&ei" ;
    :definitionText "Land with tree crown cover (stand density) of more than about 20% of the area. Continuous forest with trees usually growing to more than 7 m in height and able to produce wood. This includes both closed forest formations where trees of various layers and undergrowth cover a high proportion of the ground and open forest formation with a continuous grass layer in which tree synusia cover at least 10 % of the ground.(1993). http://books.google.com/books?id=zeTU8QauENcC&pg=PA192&lpg=PA192&dq=Germany" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_222
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :heightMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://scholar.lib.vt.edu/theses/available/etd-61998-142359/unrestricted/part2_b.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Lands classified as “forest” are dominated by woody vegetation over 3 m tall. Tree basal area must be greater than 10 % of a pixel. http://scholar.lib.vt.edu/theses/available/etd-61998-142359/unrestricted/part2_b.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_223
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.geodan.nl/ec_lu/public/index.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Lands dominated by trees and shrubs. Pan-European Land Use and Land Cover Monitoring http://www.geodan.nl/ec_lu/public/index.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_224
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nrdc.org/sitings/fslook.html" ;
    :definitionText "Lands on which trees are the principal plant life, usually conducive to wide biodiversity. http://www.nrdc.org/sitings/fslook.html Natural Resources Defense Council. Environment Terms, http://www.nrdc.org/sitings/lookup/teraa.html and http://www.nrdc.org/reference/glossary/f.asp" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_225
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.panda.org/resources/factsheets/forests/frame.htm?31defor.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Lands where the crowns of individual trees touch to form a single canopy. In a woodland, trees grow far apart, so that the canopy is open.http://www.panda.org/resources/factsheets/forests/frame.htm?31defor.htm and http://abe.msstate.edu/csd-tc/p3-g2/intro.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_226
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.forestry.utoronto.ca/ac_staff/emeritus/My%20Webs/english.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Landscape dominated by trees and other woody vegetation with a canopy cover of 20% or more (Maini 1991). http://www.forestry.utoronto.ca/ac_staff/emeritus/My%20Webs/english.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_227
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "Large area covered with trees. World Book Encyclopedia 1998." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_228
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.newberry.org/k12maps/glossary/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "Large area of land that is covered by trees and undergrowth http://www.newberry.org/k12maps/glossary/index.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_229
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://crossword911.com/forest.html" ;
    :definitionText "Large area of trees and undergrowth – http://crossword911.com/forest.html." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_230
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.esd.ornl.gov/projects/qen/adams3.html" ;
    :definitionText "Leaf cover above a level 8m off ground, >60% http://www.esd.ornl.gov/projects/qen/adams3.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_231
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "50.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "More than 50% trees. Source: Amreican Forests via Fleishman, Sandra. 2003. Why were the trees cut down? The Washington Post. Section F1,8-9. 28 June." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_232
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :heightMin "6.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.rsgis.msu.edu/pdf/lclu/MIRIS_2_definitions.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Natural areas dominated by tree cover that is generally over 6 meters, or 20 feet, in height. http://www.rsgis.msu.edu/pdf/lclu/MIRIS_2_definitions.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_233
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.redd-monitor.org/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2009/09/2009-Putz-Conservation-Letters-on-REDD.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Natural forest be differentiated from plantations and that for defining “forest” the lower height limit defining “trees” be set at more than 5 m tall with the minimum cover of trees be set at more than 40%. Sasak, Nophea; Putz, Francis E. 2009. Critical need for new definitions of “forest” and “forest degradation” in global climate change agreements. Conservation Letters xx (2009) 1–7. http://www.redd-monitor.org/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2009/09/2009-Putz-Conservation-Letters-on-REDD.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_234
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "On désigne sous le nom de forêts les espaces couverts d'arbres c'est-à-dire de cette catégorie de végétaux que distinguent tout d'abord, la nature solide de leur tige, leurs énormes proportions et la longue durée de leur existence. [LE PLAY, 1847 ; p57]. Sandrine PETIT" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_235
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.Colorado.Edu/INSTAAR/TEAML/atlas/chapters/definitions.html#Forest" ;
    :definitionText "Plant community predominately of trees and other woody plants, growing more or less closely together. http://www.Colorado.Edu/INSTAAR/TEAML/atlas/chapters/definitions.html#Forest and http://www.arcticatlas.org/glossary/index" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_236
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fsc-uk.demon.co.uk/Appendices.html" ;
    :definitionText "Predominately tree covered land in large tracts - Paraphrased from http://www.fsc-uk.demon.co.uk/Appendices.html." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_237
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "Scholes & Hall (1996) define them as having complete tree canopy cover and three or more overlapping vegetation strata. The ground layer is NOT dominated by grasses but by other non-gramineceous herbs and shrubs. There are also open and closed forests, moist/rain and dry forests." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_238
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "50.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "Scholes & Hall (1996) use 50-100% tree canopy cover, and a graminaceous layer. There are also various types of woodlands." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_239
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "Selvas - Constituye parte de la categoria “Formacion (anexo III.6). Vegetacion preominanatementearborea en climas calido-humedos a calido-subhumedos. Se caracterizan por tener especies dominates arboraas de afinidad tropical. Incluye dos tipos de vegetaction: Selve perennifoia y subperennifolia y Selva caducifolia y subcaducifolia. A su vez abarca a ocho comunidades: Selva alta y mediana perennifoila, Selva baja perennikfolia, Selva alta y mediana subpoerennifolia, Selva baja subperennifolia, Se" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_240
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "Selvas - Vegetacion predominantemente arborea en climas calido-humedos a calido-subhumedos. Se caracterizan por tener especies arboreas de afinidad tropical (UNAM 2000)." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_241
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://dictionary.reverso.net/english-definition/forest%20reserve" ;
    :definitionText "Something resembling a large wooded area.esp. in density. http://dictionary.reverso.net/english-definition/forest%20reserve." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_242
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "That portion of the ecosystem characterized by tree cover; more particularly, a plant community predominately of trees and other woody vegetation growing close together (Maser 1991)." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_243
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://dictionary.kids.net.au/word/forest" ;
    :definitionText "The trees and other plants in a large densely wooded area http://dictionary.kids.net.au/word/forest and http://www.scrabblefinder.com/word/forest/" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_244
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.wordsmyth.net/cgi-bin/simplesearch.cgi?matchent=forest&matchtype=exact&matchid=-1&retall=1" ;
    :definitionText "The trees themselves: http://www.wordsmyth.net/cgi-bin/simplesearch.cgi?matchent=forest&matchtype=exact&matchid=-1&retall=1" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_245
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://ewg.gecp.virginia.edu/ewg_forest_us/general/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "This category includes productive forest land and open woodland with naturally and artificially grown forest (forest plantation), and shrubs. Minimum volume density is the main characteristic of these lands, it should be 0.4 and higher for young forest and shrubs, and 0.3 and higher - in all other stands. Minimum Mapping Unit of 0.5 ha. http://ewg.gecp.virginia.edu/ewg_forest_us/general/glossary.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_246
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://hermes.richmond.edu/urbanforests/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "Traditional forest - large, densely wooded areas that are found in remote areas with few people. http://hermes.richmond.edu/urbanforests/glossary.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_247
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :heightMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "Tree Cover, broadleaved, evergreen (LCCS >15% tree cover, tree height >3m ) www.gvm.sai.jrc.it/glc2000/march2002/GLC2000-LCCS_global-legend280502.doc" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_248
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "Ranil Senanayake <100232.3435@compuserve.com>" ;
    :definitionText "Tree dominated ecosystems displaying the seral dynamics of ecosystem maturity and possesses tree crown cover (stand density) of more than 20% of the area. Ranil Senanayake 100232.3435@compuserve.com" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_249
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.epa.gov/nerlesd1/land-sci/pdf/trend.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Tree-covered land where the tree cover density is greater than 10%. Note that cleared forest land (i.e., clearcuts) will be mapped according to current cover (e.g., disturbed or transitional, shrubland/grassland). http://www.epa.gov/nerlesd1/land-sci/pdf/trend.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_250
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://europe.mtnforum.org/rs/econfreports/MountainPeopleForestsAndTrees.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Tree-dominated ecosystems displaying the seral dynamics of ecosystem maturity, covering 20% of the area (Ranil Senanayake 1999). http://europe.mtnforum.org/rs/econfreports/MountainPeopleForestsAndTrees.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_251
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "Trees cover more than 10% of land (Nolte 2003)." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_252
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://web.uccs.edu/geogenvs/ges100-online/Chapt11.doc" ;
    :definitionText "Trees growing so closely their individual leaf canopies overlap. Shade precludes development of much undergrowth. Require considerable moisture except where inadequate moisture or short growing season. Forest are likely to become climax vegetation association in any area. http://web.uccs.edu/geogenvs/ges100-online/Chapt11.doc" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_253
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "60.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "6.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.greatplains.org/resource/biodiver/gpclass/IC2.HTM" ;
    :definitionText "Trees with their crowns interlocking (generally forming 60-100% cover). Forested Estuarine areas vegetated by woody plants 6 m tall or taller. http://www.greatplains.org/resource/biodiver/gpclass/IC2.HTM also http://www.cws-scf.ec.gc.ca/fff/GLOSS_E.HTM#Forest" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_254
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "60.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "Trees with their crowns overlapping (generally forming 60-100% cover) (Grossman, et al. 1998)." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_255
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/2014GL062777/full" ;
    :definitionText "Consistent with the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change [UNFCCC, 2002], United Nations Food and Agriculture Organization [UNFAO, 2002], and the International Geosphere-Biosphere Programme (IGBP) [Belward, 1996], we defined forest cover (as opposed to forest use [Belward, 1996; Hansen et al., 2010]) as parcels >1 ha in area and comprising pixels with >30% tree cover. Our definition corresponds with the definitions of IGBP classes for forest (>60% tree cover) and woody savannas (" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_256
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://eyesontheforest.or.id/index.php?option=com_docman&task=doc_download&gid=5" ;
    :definitionText "Unless otherwise indicated all references to “forest” in the report assume natural forest (regardless of its quality). Plantation forest areas are specified as such.(2005). http://eyesontheforest.or.id/index.php?option=com_docman&task=doc_download&gid=5" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_257
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "Usually understood to mean land covered with woody growth of economic importance. Zon 1910" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_258
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "Vaste étendue de terrain peuplée d'arbres; ensemble de ces arbres. Le Petit Robert. Sandrine PETIT" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_259
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ids.ac.uk/eldis/forests/forpap.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Vegetation dominated by trees, without a grassy or weedy under-storey, and which has not been recently farmed. Hall (1987) http://www.ids.ac.uk/eldis/forests/forpap.htm." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_260
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :heightMin "6.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://birds.cornell.edu/bfl/definitions.html" ;
    :definitionText "Vegetation with an average canopy height greater than 20 ft. (6m). http://birds.cornell.edu/bfl/definitions.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_261
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "Wood, Woods, area of land covered with trees. Babylon.com" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_262
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.notredame.ac.jp/cgi-bin/wn?forest" ;
    :definitionText "woods -- (the trees and other plants in a large densely wooded area) http://www.notredame.ac.jp/cgi-bin/wn?forest" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_263
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "35.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://gis.esri.com/library/userconf/proc02/pap0811/p0811.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Woody vegetation > 3 meters (10 ft) in height. Canopy closure must be >35% (<35% = Category 3). Also included in this category are areas commonly referenced as \"swamp\" or forested wetland http://gis.esri.com/library/userconf/proc02/pap0811/p0811.htm" .

:def_Forest_Agroforest_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :appliesIn :Agroforest ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.worldagroforestry.org/downloads/publications/PDFs/WP16263.PDF" ;
    :definitionText "(Agroforest) – Forest which is managed more or less intensively by small holders producing timber and non-timber products. (Zomer RJ, Trabucco A, Coe R and Place F. 2009. Trees on Farm: Analysis of Global Extent and Geographical Patterns of Agroforestry. ICRAF Working Paper no. 89. Nairobi, Kenya: World Agroforestry Centre. 63 p. http://www.worldagroforestry.org/downloads/publications/PDFs/WP16263.PDF)." .

:def_Forest_American_Legislative_Exchange_Council_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :appliesIn :American_Legislative_Exchange_Council ;
    :sourceRef "https://www.alec.org/model-policy/the-right-to-practice-forestry-act/" ;
    :definitionText "(American Legislative Exchange Council) “Forest” means a parcel of land in which at least 80% of the parcel is producing or is capable of producing at least 20 cubic feet of merchantable timber per acre per year {or as defined by state statute}. https://www.alec.org/model-policy/the-right-to-practice-forestry-act/" .

:def_Forest_SAF_1958_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :appliesIn :SAF ;
    dcterms:date "1958"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://home.comcast.net/~gyde/5-agency_paper-2.doc" ;
    :definitionText "(SAF 1958) Land bearing forest growth or land from which the forest has been removed but which shows evidence of past forestry occupancy and which is not now in other use. To qualify as forest, an area must: (1) be at least 100 feet wide; (2) be at least I acre in area; (3) have a sufficient number of trees to provide 10 percent crown coverage, be likely to remain in forest use. (SAF 1958) http://home.comcast.net/~gyde/5-agency_paper-2.doc" .

:def_Forest_SAF_1971_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :appliesIn :SAF ;
    dcterms:date "1971"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://home.comcast.net/~gyde/5-agency_paper-2.doc" ;
    :definitionText "(SAF 1971) Land carrying forest growth or, if totally lacking it, bearing evidence of former forest and not now in other use. Note: Such land formally qualifies as “forest” only if not less than I acre and not less than 100 feet wide, with trees providing not less than 10 percent crown cover, or, if less, if the lands likely to remain in forest use. (FORD-ROBERTSON 1971). http://home.comcast.net/~gyde/5-agency_paper-2.doc" .

:def_Forest_SAF_1998_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :appliesIn :SAF ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(SAF 1998) An ecosystem characterized by a more or less dense or extensive tree cover, often consisting of stands varying in characteristics such as species composition, structure, age class, and associated processes, and commonly including meadows streams, fish and wildlife. Note - forests include specialized kinds such as industrial forests, non-industrial private forests, plantations, public forests, production forests, and urban forests, as well as parks and wilderness (Helms 1998)." .

:def_Forest_Terre_forestiere_terreno_forestal_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :appliesIn :Terre_forestiere_terreno_forestal ;
    :definitionText "(Terre forestiere, terreno forestal) Land under natural or cultivated stands of trees intended for forest use, including land cleared of trees but which will be reforested. Permanent meadows and pastures with scattered trees and shrubs do not constitute forest (Miani 1991 - Forestry Chronicle 70(6):669 1994)." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_264
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://goatconnection.com/articles/publish/article_86.shtml" ;
    :definitionText "A classification of land use in the Natural Resources Inventory (NRI). It includes areas where trees cover at least 10% of the land and must be at least an acre in size. Forestland was found on 395 million acres, almost 30% of all private lands, in the 1992 NRI. http://goatconnection.com/articles/publish/article_86.shtml and http://www.pfb.com/resources/ag-information/glossary-of-ag-terms-F.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_265
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "A land area with a minimum 10 % tree crown coverage (or equivalent stocking level), or formerly having such tree cover and that is being naturally or artificially regenerated or that is being afforested (Päivinen et al. 1994)." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_266
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "A natural land that has not been subjected to human activities regarding change of use. Harrison (1992)" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_267
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dictionary.com/cgi-bin/dict.pl?term=forestland" ;
    :definitionText "A section of land covered with forest or set aside for the cultivation of forests.http://www.dictionary.com/cgi-bin/dict.pl?term=forestland" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_268
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.eresourcesystems.com/Help/Glossary/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "All land which is capable of supporting a merchantable stand of timber and is not actively being used in a use which is incompatible with timber growing. http://www.eresourcesystems.com/Help/Glossary/glossary.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_269
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.mrsc.org/mc/rcw/RCW%20%2076%20%20TITLE/RCW%20%2076%20.%2009%20%20CHAPTER/RCW%20%2076%20.%2009%20.020.htm" ;
    :definitionText "All land which is capable of supporting a merchantable stand of timber and is not being actively used for a use which is incompatible with timber growing. Forest land does not include agricultural land that is or was enrolled in the conservation reserve enhancement program by contract if such agricultural land was historically used for agricultural purposes and the landowner intends to continue to use the land for agricultural purposes in the future. As it applies to the operation of the road ma" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_270
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "All lands bearing vegetative associations dominated by trees of any size, exploited or not, capable of producing wood or other forest products, of exerting an influence on climate or on water regime, or providing shelter for livestock or wildlife. Includes lands which have been clearcut or burned but which will be reforested in the foreseeable future. Excludes orchards, shelterbelts, groups of trees along roads or city parks. Encyclopedia Britannia 1970" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_271
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "Alexander.Korotkov@unece.org" ;
    :definitionText "All lands bearing vegetative associations dominated by trees of any size, exploited or not, capable of producing wood or of exerting an influence on the local climate or on the water regime. Included are: lands from which forests have been recently clear cut or burned but which will be reforested in the near future; public and private forests of any size; tree nurseries; forest roads; mangrove forests, forests of low growth and of dwarfed or stunted forms. Excluded are: brush lands, groups of tr" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_272
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://fwie.fw.vt.edu/rhgiles/appendices/glossf.htm" ;
    :definitionText "An area managed for producing timber and other products, or maintained under woody vegetation for such indirect benefits as protection of watersheds or recreation. http://fwie.fw.vt.edu/rhgiles/appendices/glossf.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_273
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.genesisny.net/Commodity/Timber/Timberglos.html" ;
    :definitionText "An area managed for the production of timber and other forest products or maintained as wood vegetation for such indirect benefits as protection of catchment areas or recreation. http://www.genesisny.net/Commodity/Timber/Timberglos.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_274
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :definitionText "An area managed for the production of timber and other forest produce, or maintained under woody vegetation for such indirect benefits as protection of (water) catchment areas or recreation. SAF 1971 (Helms 2002)" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_275
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.safc.org/resources/glossary.htm#F" ;
    :definitionText "An area managed for the production of timber and other forest products, or maintained under woody vegetation for indirect benefits as protection of a watershed, recreation, or wildlife habitat. When used as a proper noun, it refers to the Chattahoochee or Oconee National Forest (both if plural). http://www.safc.org/resources/glossary.htm#F" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_276
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://nfdp.ccfm.org/silviterm/silvi_e/silvitermetohe.htm#F" ;
    :definitionText "An area managed for the production of timber and other forest produce, or maintained under woody vegetation for such indirect benefits as the protection of watersheds, the provision of recreation areas, or the preservation of natural habitat. http://nfdp.ccfm.org/silviterm/silvi_e/silvitermetohe.htm#F" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_277
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://books.google.com/books?id=jhZsJc4z5RkC&pg=PA657&lpg=PA657&dq=hawaii+forestland&source=web&ots=YlCTj-qUZR&sig=PtkyXu4oaaWBg-3k45z2nub3mDs#PPA645" ;
    :definitionText "An area which is for the most part set aside for the production of timber and other forest produce, or which is expected to exercise certain climatic effects, or to protect the locality against injurious influences. Encyclopedia Britannia 1910. p. 645. http://books.google.com/books?id=jhZsJc4z5RkC&pg=PA657&lpg=PA657&dq=hawaii+forestland&source=web&ots=YlCTj-qUZR&sig=PtkyXu4oaaWBg-3k45z2nub3mDs#PPA645,M1" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_278
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://dspace.wbpublibnet.gov.in/dspace/bitstream/10689/10100/4/Chapter%201_1%20-%20125p.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "An area, which has been set aside principally for the production of wood, and which, at any rate for the greater part, is covered with trees. (19th century) http://dspace.wbpublibnet.gov.in/dspace/bitstream/10689/10100/4/Chapter%201_1%20-%20125p.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_279
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.environmental-auditing.org/LinkClick.aspx?fileticket=fbx%2FbAIVeFU%3D&tabid=128&mid=568" ;
    :definitionText "An ecosystem characterized by more or less dense and extensive tree cover, often consisting of stands varying in characteristics such as species compositions, structure, age class and associated processes, and commonly including meadows, streams, fish, and wildlife. Thus forest could be defined as a set of land parcels that has or could have tree vegetation and is managed as a whole to achieve the objective of the owner. http://www.environmental-auditing.org/LinkClick.aspx?fileticket=fbx%2FbAIVe" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_280
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.bicusa.org/bicusa/issues/misc_resources/585.php" ;
    :definitionText "An ecosystem with a minimum of 10 percent crown cover of trees and/or bamboos, generally associated with wild flora, fauna and natural soil conditions and not subject to agriculture (Asian Development Bank 1995). http://www.bicusa.org/bicusa/issues/misc_resources/585.php" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_281
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "https://www.forestasyst.org/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "Any land with at least 10 percent coved by trees of any size, or having had such tree cover and not currently developed or under cultivation. https://www.forestasyst.org/glossary.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_282
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://rredc.nrel.gov/biomass/forest/tim_glossary/t_glossary.html#F" ;
    :definitionText "Area managed for the production of timber and other forest products or maintained as wood vegetation for such indirect benefits as protection of catchment areas or recreation (26). http://rredc.nrel.gov/biomass/forest/tim_glossary/t_glossary.html#F and Ford-Robertson 1971: 107, 298. Also Boundary Waters Compendium Glossary - http://www.rook.org/earl/bwca/lists/glossary/" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_283
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://sedac.ciesin.columbia.edu/tg/guide_frame.jsp?rd=LU&ds=1" ;
    :definitionText "Areas with a? minimum of 10% crown cover of trees and/or bamboos, generally associated with wild flora and fauna and natural soil conditions, and are not subject to agricultural practices. Note that in some countries, some areas are statutorily defined as ?Forest Area? that contain no tree cover. http://sedac.ciesin.columbia.edu/tg/guide_frame.jsp?rd=LU&ds=1" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_284
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "7.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.grida.no/baltic/related/balans_landcover_classification_methodology_ver2.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Forest is defined as >30% crown cover and the tree height shall be >7 m. Seedlings under forest are also included in this class. Areas occupied by forest and woodlands with a vegetation pattern composed of native or exotic coniferous trees, and which can be used for the production of timber or other forest products. The forest trees are under normal climatic conditions higher than 5 m with a canopy closure of 30% at least. http://www.grida.no/baltic/related/balans_landcover_classification_method" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_285
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.gcrio.org/CONSEQUENCES/spring95/Land.html" ;
    :definitionText "Forest land is characterized by a predominance of tree cover and is further divided by the U.S. Census into timberland and non-timberland. By definition, the former must be capable of producing 20 cubic feet of industrial wood per acre per year and remain legally open to timber production. http://www.gcrio.org/CONSEQUENCES/spring95/Land.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_286
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.mrsc.org/mc/rcw/RCW%20%2084%20%20TITLE/RCW%20%2084%20.%2033%20%20CHAPTER/RCW%20%2084%20.%2033%20.035.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Forest land is synonymous with \"designated forest land\" and means any parcel of land that is twenty or more acres or multiple parcels of land that are contiguous and total twenty or more acres that is or are devoted primarily to growing and harvesting timber. Designated forest land means the land only and does not include a residential homesite. The term includes land used for incidental uses that are compatible with the growing and harvesting of timber but no more than ten percent of the land m" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_287
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ancienttrees.org/fulltext.php" ;
    :definitionText "Forestland means land, other than land owned by the federal government, that was, as of the effective date of this section, available for and capable of growing a crop of trees of any commercial species used to produce lumber and other forest products, including Christmas trees. Commercial species are those species so designated by the board. http://www.ancienttrees.org/fulltext.php" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_288
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.reo.gov/general/definitions_n-z.htm#R" ;
    :definitionText "Land at least 10 percent stocked (based on crown cover) by forest trees of any size, or formerly having had such tree cover and not currently developed for nonforest use. http://www.reo.gov/general/definitions_n-z.htm#R 2003" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_289
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.idahoforests.org/dict1.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Land at least 10 percent stocked by tree stands of any size or that formerly had such tree cover and that will be regenerated with trees. http://www.idahoforests.org/dict1.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_290
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.4047"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ilea.org/birdsey/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "Land at least 10 percent stocked by trees of any size, including land that formerly had such tree cover and that will be naturally or artificially regenerated. Forest land includes transition zones, such as areas between heavily forested and nonforested lands that are at leas t 10 percent stocked with forest trees and forest areas adjacent to urban and built-up lands. Also included are pinyon-juniper and chaparral areas in the West and afforested areas. The minimum area for classification of for" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_291
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://maps.vcgi.org/indicators/metadata/cntyfrst.html" ;
    :definitionText "Land at least 10 percent stocked with trees of any size, or that formerly had tree cover and is not currently developed for a nonforest use. The minimum area for classification is one acre. http://maps.vcgi.org/indicators/metadata/cntyfrst.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_292
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://fwie.fw.vt.edu/rhgiles/appendices/glossf.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Land at least 10-percent occupied by forest trees of any size or formerly having had such tree cover and not currently developed for non-forest use. Lands developed for non-forest use include area for crops, improved pasture, residential or administrative areas, improved roads of any width, adjoining road clearing, and power-line clearing of any width. http://fwie.fw.vt.edu/rhgiles/appendices/glossf.htm and (36 CFR 219.3) http://www.safc.org/resources/glossary.htm#D" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_293
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "16.7"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.4047"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.pfmt.org/glossary/f.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Land at least 16.7 percent stocked by forest trees of any size, or formerly having had such tree cover, and not currently developed for nonforest use. (Note: Stocking is measured by comparing specified standards with basal area and /or number of trees, age or size, and spacing.) The minimum area for classification of forest land is 1 acre. Roadside, streamside, and shelterbelt strips of timber must have a crown width of at least 120 feet to qualify as forest land. Unimproved roads and trails, st" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_294
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :heightMin "1.83"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.wvgazette.com/static/series/mining/reports/EIS/VIII.Glossary.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Land bearing a stand of trees of any stature, including seedlings, and of species attaining a minimum of 6 feet average height at maturity or land from which such a stand has been removed but on which no other use has been substituted. The term is commonly limited to land not in farms; forests on farms are commonly called woodland or farm forests. http://www.wvgazette.com/static/series/mining/reports/EIS/VIII.Glossary.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_295
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.geocities.com/rboutilier000/wildlif1.html" ;
    :definitionText "Land bearing forest growth or land from which the forest has been removed but which shows surface evidence of past forest occupancy and is not now in other use; http://www.geocities.com/rboutilier000/wildlif1.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_296
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.lwvwa.org/forest/dynamic/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Land capable of supporting trees and not actively in a use which is incompatible with timber growing. Washington's Dynamic Forests - League of Women Voters of Washington Education Fund - http://www.lwvwa.org/forest/dynamic/glossary.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_297
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://eurodic.ip.lu/cgi-bin/edicbin/expert.pl" ;
    :definitionText "Land carrying forest growth or, if totally lacking it (non-stocked (USA), unstocked (Cw) forest land), bearing evidence of former forest and not now in other use Eurodicautom (http://eurodic.ip.lu/cgi-bin/edicbin/expert.pl)." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_298
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.m-w.com/cgi-bin/dictionary?book=Dictionary&va=forestland" ;
    :definitionText "Land covered with forest or reserved for the growth of forests http://www.m-w.com/cgi-bin/dictionary?book=Dictionary&va=forestland" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_299
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :areaMin "0.4047"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ciel.org/forestglossary.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Land currently growing forest trees of any size with a total stocking value of at least 16.7 (10 base 100) in the West), or lands formerly forested, currently capable of becoming forest land, and not currently developed for nonforest uses. These lands must be a minimum of 1 acre in area. Roadside, streamside, and shelterbelt strips of timber must have a crown width of at least 120 feet to qualify as forest land. Unimproved roads, trails, streams, and clearings within forest areas are classified " .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_300
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :areaMin "4.0469"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.forestmeister.com/highlights.html" ;
    :definitionText "Land must be at least 10 acres of contiguous forest not developed for non-forest use. http://www.forestmeister.com/highlights.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_301
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.planning.org/guidebookhtm/chapter_three.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Land on which the land use of forestry occurs. http://www.planning.org/guidebookhtm/chapter_three.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_302
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.forages.css.orst.edu/Topics/Pastures/Grazing/Terminology/grazterm_body.html#Vegetation" ;
    :definitionText "Land on which the vegetation is dominated by forest or, if trees are lacking, the land bears evidence of former forest and has not been converted to other vegetation. http://www.forages.css.orst.edu/Topics/Pastures/Grazing/Terminology/grazterm_body.html#Vegetation, http://www.agry.purdue.edu/ext/forages/rotational/glossary.html, http://www.crops.org/cropgloss/index.php, and http://www.ifad.org/lrkm/glossary.htm#f" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_303
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://fwie.fw.vt.edu/rhgiles/appendices/glossf.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Land primarily devoted to trees. http://fwie.fw.vt.edu/rhgiles/appendices/glossf.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_304
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.inac.gc.ca/building/forests/forest_j.html" ;
    :definitionText "Land primarily intended for growing, or currently supporting, forest. Includes land not now forested, i.e. clear-cut lands; northern lands that are forested but not intended for any use; and plantations. http://www.inac.gc.ca/building/forests/forest_j.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_305
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.pacificforest.org/about/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "Land that can support at least 10 percent native tree cover under natural conditions. Forestland may include areas of grassland, shrubland, wetland, or other land classes. http://www.pacificforest.org/about/glossary.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_306
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "Land that is at least 10 percent stocked by forest trees of any size, or land formerly having such tree cover, and is not currently developed for a nonforest use. The minimum area for classification as forest land is one acre. Roadside, stream-side, and shelterbelt strips of timber must have a crown width at least 120 feet wide to qualify as forest land. Unimproved roads and trails, streams and other bodies of water, or natural clearings in forested areas shall be classified as forest, if less t" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_307
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "16.7"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nationalaglawcenter.org/glossary/" ;
    :definitionText "Land that is at least 16.7 percent stocked by forest trees of any size, or land that formerly had such tree cover and is not currently being developed for nonforest uses. http://www.nationalaglawcenter.org/glossary/ and http://agglossary.uaex.edu/viewFGlossary1.asp#F" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_308
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.forestmeister.com/laws/ch61.html" ;
    :definitionText "Land that is at least sixteen and seven-tenths per cent stocked, that contains at least seven and five-tenths square feet of basal area per acre by forest trees of any size; or that formerly had such tree cover and is not currently developed for non-forest use; or that is a plantation containing at least five hundred trees per acre. http://www.forestmeister.com/laws/ch61.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_309
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.streamnet.org/pub-ed/ff/Glossary/glossaryforest.html" ;
    :definitionText "Land that is now, or is capable of becoming, at least 10 percent stocked with forest trees and that has not been developed for nontimber use. http://www.streamnet.org/pub-ed/ff/Glossary/glossaryforest.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_310
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://extension.usu.edu/forestry/UtahForests/Trees_ForestryTerms.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Land that supports tree species of commercial value (i.e., spruce-fir stands, ponderosa pine, etc.); also referred to as timberland. http://extension.usu.edu/forestry/UtahForests/Trees_ForestryTerms.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_311
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.forestry.utoronto.ca/ac_staff/emeritus/My%20Webs/english.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Land under natural or cultivated stands of trees intended for forest use, including land cleared of trees but which will be reforested. Permanent meadows and pastures with scattered trees and shrubs do not constitute forest land (Maini 1991) http://www.forestry.utoronto.ca/ac_staff/emeritus/My%20Webs/english.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_312
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "25.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.osmre.gov/pdf/022399a.txt" ;
    :definitionText "Land with at least 25 percent tree canopy or that has been stocked with at least 10 percent forest trees of any size, including land that formerly had such tree cover and that will be naturally or artificially reforested. http://www.osmre.gov/pdf/022399a.txt, http://www.wvgazette.com/static/series/mining/reports/EIS/VIII.Glossary.pdf 2001 and http://www.epa.gov/region3/mtntop/pdf/VIII.Glossary.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_313
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "Alexander.Korotkov@unece.org" ;
    :definitionText "Lands bearing vegetative associations dominated by trees of any size, capable of producing timber or other forest products or of exerting an influence on the climate or on the water regime. Also, lands from which forests have been recently clear cut or burned but which will be reforested in the near future. (World Forest Inventories 1947) From: Alexander.Korotkov@unece.org. Date: Thu, 15 Oct 1998 17:09:40 +0200" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_314
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.oneworld.org/cse/html/cmp/climate/ew/art20001124_5.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Lands that have, or will have because of continued growth, more than 10 per cent canopy cover http://www.oneworld.org/cse/html/cmp/climate/ew/art20001124_5.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_315
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.4"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "Lands that naturally have or can have at least 10 percent of the area covered by crowns of trees and are not currently developed for non-forest use. The minimum area for land classification is 0.4 ha. Unimproved roads, trails, streams, and stringers of vegetation are classed with surroundings if they are less than 36.6 meters in width. (Lund 1984)." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_316
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www4.gu.edu.au:8080/adt-root/uploads/approved/adt-QGU20060303.132137/public/03Main.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "The amount of land appropriated by the consumption of paper and timber products. http://www4.gu.edu.au:8080/adt-root/uploads/approved/adt-QGU20060303.132137/public/03Main.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_317
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.sustainableforests.net/C&I_workshops/Glossary%20as%20990101.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Total area of existing forest, Area of forest land, Net area of forest land available for timber production without risk of biodiversity loss. This can be composed of natural or plantation forests but should be listed separately. http://www.sustainableforests.net/C&I_workshops/Glossary%20as%20990101.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_318
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "25.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "4.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.statlab.iastate.edu/soils/nssh/622.htm#16" ;
    :definitionText "Tree Cover (>25% tree canopy cover) Vegetative cover recognized as woody plants which usually have one perennial stem, a definitely formed crown of foliage, and a mature height of at least 4 meters. This category contains all trees, even those planted for the purpose of producing food or ornamentals, including Christmas trees. It also includes those lands which have been harvested of trees, even those that have been clear cut, but will return to tree cover. http://www.statlab.iastate.edu/soils/n" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_319
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://media.lpb.org/images/pdf/CaseyTreesGlossary.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Urban forest: An urban forest includes all of the natural resources in an urban area: plants, soil, water, and animals (including all of us) [Urban Forestry]. http://media.lpb.org/images/pdf/CaseyTreesGlossary.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_320
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :canopyThreshold "60.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.wec.ufl.edu/coop/gap/moreinfo.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Vegetation dominated by trees with their crowns overlapping, generally forming 60 - 100% cover; includes reproductive stages or immature secondary growth stands that are temporarily less than 5 meters or 16.5 feet tall. http://www.wec.ufl.edu/coop/gap/moreinfo.htm" .

:def_Forest_Forestland_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :appliesIn :Forestland ;
    :sourceRef "http://ext.msstate.edu/pubs/pub1250.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Forestland) Land which is currently producing (or, in some cases, capable of producing) a forest. http://ext.msstate.edu/pubs/pub1250.htm and http://msucares.com/pubs/pub1250.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_321
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.oznet.ksu.edu/library/MISC2/SB661.PDF" ;
    :definitionText "A biome with enough precipitation to support various tree species. http://www.oznet.ksu.edu/library/MISC2/SB661.PDF" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_322
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://mff.dsisd.net/Environment/EcologyForests.htm" ;
    :definitionText "A collection of biological organisms and non-biological factors. From an ecological perspective, the definition of a forest includes all these things, from the trees to the bacteria, and the soil type to the microclimates http://mff.dsisd.net/Environment/EcologyForests.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_323
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.wrm.org.uy/english/bulletin/bull16.htm" ;
    :definitionText "A complex, self-regenerating system, encompassing soil, water, microclimate, energy, and a wide variety of plants and animals in mutual relation. A commercial plantation, on the other hand, is a cultivated area whose species and structure have been simplified dramatically to produce only a few goods, whether lumber, fuel, resin, oil, or fruit. http://www.wrm.org.uy/english/bulletin/bull16.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_324
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://forum.wordreference.com/showthread.php?t=186539" ;
    :definitionText "A forest is temperate and little touched by humans. A jungle is tropical and untrammeled. Woods are forests that have been worked by humans. http://forum.wordreference.com/showthread.php?t=186539" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_325
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.google.com/search?client=safari&rls=en&q=forest+facts&ie=UTF-8&oe=UTF-8" ;
    :definitionText "A forest, also referred to as a wood or the woods, is an area with a high amount of weed. People go to forests to get high. Wikipedia http://www.google.com/search?client=safari&rls=en&q=forest+facts&ie=UTF-8&oe=UTF-8" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_326
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.chesco.com/~treeman/words/words-t.html" ;
    :definitionText "A highly ordered arrangement of living organisms living in, on and around trees in such an highly ordered fashion it assures high quality survival for all. http://www.chesco.com/~treeman/words/words-t.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_327
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "Lorenzo Ciccarese <ciccarese@anpa.it>" ;
    :definitionText "A land comprehensive of vegetation, fauna and soil, providing wood and other goods, and values (protection, recreation, scenery, etc.). Lorenzo Ciccarese ciccarese@anpa.it" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_328
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://ewg.gecp.virginia.edu/ewg_forest_us/general/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "A landscape component, raw material, or an object of forestry management activities http://ewg.gecp.virginia.edu/ewg_forest_us/general/glossary.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_329
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://tropenbos.nl.php5.server34.firstfind.nl/tbi_publications/documents/Mirjam2.PDF" ;
    :definitionText "A natural ecosystem in which trees are a significant component http://tropenbos.nl.php5.server34.firstfind.nl/tbi_publications/documents/Mirjam2.PDF" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_330
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.battle1066.com/g118.html" ;
    :definitionText "A Norman law which gave the right to keep wild animals on land for the purpose of hunting. Penalties for infringements included mutilation and death. (Definition from some game). http://www.battle1066.com/g118.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_331
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://ext.nrs.wsu.edu/publications/pdf/wildlife/misc0198.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "A plant community dominated by woody plants, where the plnats interact with other living and nonliving components such as soil, water, air, animals, and microscopic orgnaisms (Forest ecosystem), http://ext.nrs.wsu.edu/publications/pdf/wildlife/misc0198.pdf." .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_332
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.chesco.com/~treeman/words/words-t.html" ;
    :definitionText "A system, where trees and their associates are so highly ordered in their connections that they all survive at a high quality state. http://www.chesco.com/~treeman/words/words-t.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_333
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.scribd.com/WorldBankPublications/d/16060052-Forest-Law-and-Sustainable-Development-Addressing-Contemporary-Challenges-Through-Legal-Reform" ;
    :definitionText "An ecosystem dominated by woody vegetation, potentially subject to the management or oversight of foresters. Christy, Lawrence C. et al. 2007. Forest law and sustainable development – Addressing contemporary Challenges through legal reform. Wolrd Bank, Law, Justice and Development Series. 228 p. http://www.scribd.com/WorldBankPublications/d/16060052-Forest-Law-and-Sustainable-Development-Addressing-Contemporary-Challenges-Through-Legal-Reform" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_334
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.britell.com/lex.html" ;
    :definitionText "An extensive area preserving some or all of its primitive wildness, usually having wild animals. http://www.britell.com/lex.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_335
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.gsu.edu/~mstnrhx/ecogloss.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Biome with enough average annual precipitation (at least 76 centimeters, or 30 inches) to support growth of various species of trees and smaller forms of vegetation. http://www.gsu.edu/~mstnrhx/ecogloss.htm" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_336
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.reservenaturelle.fr/upload/cahier74bis.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Forest - Synonymous with wilderness. It covers vast areas, is seldom visited, and forms the ultimate refuge for numerous large mammals and predators. http://www.reservenaturelle.fr/upload/cahier74bis.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_337
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.americanforests.org/discover-forests/forest-facts/" ;
    :definitionText "Forests are complex ecosystems in which plants and animals coexist with one another http://www.americanforests.org/discover-forests/forest-facts/" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_338
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.planetpals.com/habitats.html" ;
    :definitionText "Forests are small biomes. They represent a third of the Earth's land. http://www.planetpals.com/habitats.html" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_339
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://home.alltel.net/bsundquist1/se2.html#Dg" ;
    :definitionText "Forests generally occur only where precipitation exceeds 60 cm/ year (24\"/ year) (Ref.64 of DF91M1). http://home.alltel.net/bsundquist1/se2.html#Dg" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_340
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.kaieteurnewsonline.com/2011/02/01/real-or-imaginary-rates-of-deforestation/" ;
    :definitionText "Intact forest landscape (IFL): a territory within today’s global extent of forest cover which contains forest and non-forest ecosystems minimally influenced by human economic activity, with an area of at least 500 km2 (50,000 ha) and a minimal width of 10 km (measured as the diameter of a circle that is entirely inscribed within the boundaries of the territory). http://www.kaieteurnewsonline.com/2011/02/01/real-or-imaginary-rates-of-deforestation/" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_341
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.tamu.edu/classes/rang/rknight/rlem102/lecture3/rangeland-definitions.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Land on which the native vegetation (climax or natural potential) is forest. http://www.tamu.edu/classes/rang/rknight/rlem102/lecture3/rangeland-definitions.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_342
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.zoology.wisc.edu/courses/220/readings/Hardin/Hardin_population.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Land that produces woody plants-bushes as well as trees-anything that can serve as fuel in the cooking of food. http://www.zoology.wisc.edu/courses/220/readings/Hardin/Hardin_population.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_343
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.v-c-s.org/docs/Program%20Definitions" ;
    :definitionText "Land with woody vegetation that meets an internationally accepted definition (e.g., UNFCCC, FAO or IPCC) of what constitutes a forest, which includes threshold parameters, such as minimum forest area, tree height and level of crown cover, and may include mature, secondary, degraded and wetland forests. http://www.v-c-s.org/docs/Program%20Definitions,%20Consultation%202011.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_344
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :General ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.asb.cgiar.org/pdfwebdocs/ASBPB13.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "The term ‘forest’ refers to woody vegetation, but it is also linked to specific institutions empowered to manage forests. http://www.asb.cgiar.org/pdfwebdocs/ASBPB13.pdf" .

:def_Forest_ADB_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :ADB ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://figueresonline.com/csdafinal/English/publications/cdm/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "(ADB 1997), An ecosystem with a minimum of 10 percent crown cover of trees and/or bamboos, generally associated with wild flora, fauna and natural soil conditions and not subject to agriculture. Asian Development Bank. http://figueresonline.com/csdafinal/English/publications/cdm/glossary.html" .

:def_Forest_CBFP_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :CBFP ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://carpe.umd.edu/resources/Documents/THE_FORESTS_OF_THE_CONGO_BASIN_State_of_the_Forest_2006.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(CBFP 2006) - Congo Basin Forest Partnership. Forests are habitats where trees are dominant, where tree crowns form a more or less continuous layer and where grasses are virtually absent in the under story. The few grasses which are found in forests have broad leaves and are very different from savannah species. Forests are sensitive to fire. http://carpe.umd.edu/resources/Documents/THE_FORESTS_OF_THE_CONGO_BASIN_State_of_the_Forest_2006.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Central_Europe_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :Central_Europe ;
    :canopyThreshold "75.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/ag/agl/agll/landuse/clsys/Europecenral.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Central Europe) Forestry - Compact forest complexes covering 75-80% of the area. http://www.fao.org/ag/agl/agll/landuse/clsys/Europecenral.htm" .

:def_Forest_Convention_on_International_Trade_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :Convention_on_International_Trade ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nationmaster.com/country/gr-greece/env-environment" ;
    :definitionText "(Convention on International Trade 2000) Forest area is land under natural or planted stands of trees, whether productive or not. Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species of Wild Fauna and Flora, Report on National Reports Required Under Article VIII, Paragraph 7(a), of the Convention, Eleventh Meeting of the Conference of the Parties, Gigiri, Kenya, April 2000 http://www.nationmaster.com/country/gr-greece/env-environment" .

:def_Forest_Dry_zone_African_countries_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :Dry_zone_African_countries ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "Omnia.Moussa@fao.org" ;
    :definitionText "(Dry-zone African countries) An ecosystem with a minimum of 10 percent crown cover of trees, and other wooded lands are those which are covered by trees, bushes or scattered shrubs, whether natural or planted by people, and which may be cultivated (as agro-forestry lands) or not and which are generally associated with wild flora and fauna. \"Moussa, Omnia (FAORNE)\"Omnia.Moussa@fao.org" .

:def_Forest_EarthSat_GeoCover_LC_2002_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :EarthSat_GeoCover_LC ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "35.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(EarthSat GeoCover LC 2002) - Trees > 3 m height, canopy closure > 35 % (Kalensky et al. 2002)" .

:def_Forest_East_Africa_1943_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :East_Africa ;
    dcterms:date "1943"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "50.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(East Africa 1943) Forest is a continuous stand of trees which may attain a height of 50 m or more, with crowns touching or intermingling and often interlaced with lianas. file:///C:/Users/Owner/Downloads/Friis_Forest_vegetation.pdf" .

:def_Forest_ESA_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :ESA ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "15.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.esa.int/esaEO/SEM5N3TRJHG_index_0.html" ;
    :definitionText "(ESA 2009). >15 % crown cover, >5 meters high. European Space Agency. http://www.esa.int/esaEO/SEM5N3TRJHG_index_0.html." .

:def_Forest_EU_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :EU ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "7.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://europa.eu.int/estatref/info/sdds/en/for/for_res.htm#toc" ;
    :definitionText "(EU 2000). Forest land is defined as land with tree crown cover (stand density) of more than about 20% of the area. Continuous forest with trees usually growing to more than about 7 m in height and able to produce wood. This includes both closed forest formations where trees of various storeys and undergrowth cover a high proportion of the ground, and open forest formations with a continuous grass layer in which tree synusiae cover at least 10% of the ground. http://europa.eu.int/estatref/info/s" .

:def_Forest_EU_2004_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :EU ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://epp.eurostat.cec.eu.int/cache/ITY_OFFPUB/KS-CD-04-001-8/EN/KS-CD-04-001-8-EN.PDF" ;
    :definitionText "(EU 2004). Land with tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 10 % and area of more than 0.5 ha. The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 m at maturity in situ. http://epp.eurostat.cec.eu.int/cache/ITY_OFFPUB/KS-CD-04-001-8/EN/KS-CD-04-001-8-EN.PDF" .

:def_Forest_EU_2010_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :EU ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://euobserver.com/9/29410" ;
    :definitionText "(EU 2010) Continuously forested areas are defined as areas where trees have reached, or can reach, at least heights of five metres, making up a crown cover of more than 30 percent….They would normally include forest, forest plantations and other tree plantations such as palm oil. Short rotation coppice [the practice of repeatedly cutting young tree stems down] may qualify if it fulfils the height and canopy cover criteria. Phillips, Leigh. 2010. Palm oil plantations are now 'forests,' says EU. E" .

:def_Forest_EU_2010_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :EU ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.tropenbos.org/file.php/4/forests-dec21-final-web.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(EU 2010). Continuously forested areas are defined as areas where trees have reached, or can reach, at least heights of 5 metres, making up a crown cover of more than 30%. They would normally include natural forest, forest plantations and other tree plantations such as oil palm. This means, for example, that a change from forest to oil palm plantation would not per se constitute a breach of the criterion (para 4.2.3, draft communication).” http://www.tropenbos.org/file.php/4/forests-dec21-final-" .

:def_Forest_EU_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :EU ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://ec.europa.eu/agriculture/analysis/external/supply-wood/full_text_en.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(EU) Areas spanning more than 0.5 to 1.0 hectares (depending on national definitions) with trees higher than 5 meters and a canopy cover of more than 10 percent, or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ. It does not include land that is predominantly under agricultural or urban land use. Land registry systems should specify the concerned areas in terms of land use as „forest“ http://ec.europa.eu/agriculture/analysis/external/supply-wood/full_text_en.pdf" .

:def_Forest_EU_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :EU ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "7.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://ec.europa.eu/agriculture/envir/report/en/lex_en/report_en.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(EU) Forest area is \"areas with crown cover (stand density) greater than around 20% of the area. Continuous forest with trees usually reaching a height of more than 7 metres and providing a source of wood. http://ec.europa.eu/agriculture/envir/report/en/lex_en/report_en.htm" .

:def_Forest_EU_JRC_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :EU_JRC ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www-tem.jrc.it/PDF_publis/2003/Stibig_EUR_2003_full.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(EU-JRC 2003) Forests … have a tree cover of more than 10-20% and tree heights of more than 3(-5) metres. Tree cover and forest regrowth below these thresholds were considered ‘Wood & shrubland’. http://www-tem.jrc.it/PDF_publis/2003/Stibig_EUR_2003_full.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Europe_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :Europe ;
    :areaMin "25.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://etc.satellus.se/the_data/Technical_Guide/part_one_text2.htm#The" ;
    :definitionText "(Europe) Vegetation formation composed principally of trees, including shrub and bush understories. The surface area of the smallest unit mapped in the project is 25 hectares. http://etc.satellus.se/the_data/Technical_Guide/part_one_text2.htm#The nomenclature" .

:def_Forest_European_Community_DGXIII_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :European_Community_DGXIII ;
    :sourceRef "http://europa.eu.int/comm/dg08/forests/en/en4_6.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(European Community -DGXIII) - Ecosystems with a minimum of 10 per cent crown cover of trees and/or bamboos. They usually contain wild flora, fauna and natural soil conditions, and are not subject to agricultural practices. Forests can be divided into two categories: natural and plantation forests http://europa.eu.int/comm/dg08/forests/en/en4_6.htm and http://europa.eu.int/comm/development/body/publications/forests/en/en4_6.htm" .

:def_Forest_European_Community_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :European_Community ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://europa.eu.int/eur-lex/en/lif/dat/1993/en_393R0926.html" ;
    :definitionText "(European Community) Forest (for inventory) - forest tree stands with at least 20 % canopy closure at rotation age (closed forests according to the Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations (FAO) definition). However, for certain types of woodland which are characteristic of the Mediterranean region (maquis and similar woodland, stands of Quercus suber and Quercus ilex, etc.), this canopy closure should be at least 10 %. The minimum size of the forests to be sampled be 0.5 hectare." .

:def_Forest_European_Environment_Agency_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :European_Environment_Agency ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.epa.gov/trs" ;
    :definitionText "(European Environment Agency) - A vegetation community dominated by trees and other woody shrubs, growing close enough together that the tree tops touch or overlap, creating various degrees of shade on the forest floor. It may produce benefits such as timber, recreation, wildlife habitat, etc.(Source: DUNSTE) European Environment Agency (EEA), European Topic Centre on Catalogue of Data Sources (ETC/CDS) : General Multilingual Environmental Thesaurus Term Detail. http://www.epa.gov/trs" .

:def_Forest_European_Environment_Agency_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :European_Environment_Agency ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://glossary.eea.eu.int/EEAGlossary/F/forest" ;
    :definitionText "(European Environment Agency) Land with a tree canopy cover of more than 10 % and an area of more than 0.5 ha. http://glossary.eea.eu.int/EEAGlossary/F/forest" .

:def_Forest_Forest_Focus_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :Forest_Focus ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/tr_18.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Forest Focus ) Forest has in mature state a crown cover of at least 10%, trees of height minimum 5 m, and an area of at least 0.5 ha with a width of at least 20 m. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/tr_18.pdf" .

:def_Forest_FSC_2011_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :FSC ;
    dcterms:date "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fsc.org/fileadmin/web-data/public/document_center/Current_consultations/Report_P_C_Review_Workshop_2011-06-25_26_Final.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(FSC 2011) Forest” is not defined, as the “natural forest” and “plantation” covers the scope of forest areas for purpose of the P&C . Plantation Definition: Areas with tree cover in which the trees are established by either planting, sowing or using intensive silvicultural treatments, which lack most of the principal characteristics and key elements of native ecosystems, and which are characterized by either few species used in the treatments, even spacing, and/or even-ages, or by significant us" .

:def_Forest_GLC2000_legend_2005_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :GLC2000_legend ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "15.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.glcn.org/downs/pub/ppts/FRA-GLCN_india/Antonio%20DiGregorio/Review%20of%20LCCS.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(GLC2000 legend 2005) : percent tree cover >15% / tree height >3m http://www.glcn.org/downs/pub/ppts/FRA-GLCN_india/Antonio%20DiGregorio/Review%20of%20LCCS.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Global_Forest_Coalition_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :Global_Forest_Coalition ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "yvetogo@hotmail.com" ;
    :definitionText "(Global Forest Coalition 2009) Forests are complex tree dominated ecosystems with particular structural biotic and abiotic components, assembled within temporal and spatial limits and with a self sustained successional dynamic determined by its own biodiversity, including the determining anthropogenic interfaces, particularly with Indigenous Peoples and peoples who adopted their knowledge. Source: yvetogo@hotmail.com, 30 April 2009." .

:def_Forest_Global_Forest_Watch_2014_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :Global_Forest_Watch ;
    dcterms:date "2014"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.globalforestwatch.org/howto#terminology" ;
    :definitionText "(Global Forest Watch 2014) - Various definitions exist for the term “forest,” and GFW does not aim to provide a consensus definition. Data sets hosted on GFW may define “forest” differently or pertain to different types of forest (primary, secondary, tree plantations, etc.). Through information found on the Data page, we aim to be transparent about the assumptions and definitions feeding into each data set. In our general writing, including the GFW blog, “forest” refers to a landscape with a hig" .

:def_Forest_GOFCGOLD_Land_and_Forest_Cover_Classification_Sche_2002_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :GOFCGOLD_Land_and_Forest_Cover_Classification_Sche ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(GOFC/GOLD Land and Forest Cover Classification Scheme 2002) – Canopy cover 10-25 %, Tree height <1 m - > 2m. (Kalensky et al. 2002)" .

:def_Forest_IADB_2013_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :IADB ;
    dcterms:date "2013"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "https://www.imf.org/external/np/seminars/eng/2013/caribbean/pdf/approach.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(IADB 2013). A vegetation type dominated by trees. Inter-American Development Bank. https://www.imf.org/external/np/seminars/eng/2013/caribbean/pdf/approach.pdf" .

:def_Forest_ICRAF_2017_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :ICRAF ;
    dcterms:date "2017"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://dx.doi.org/10.5716/WP16079.PDF" ;
    :definitionText "(ICRAF- 2017) Land with trees under specified management authority; common definitions combine biophysical aspects of tree cover (minimum spatial tree cover over defined percentage of time at defined measurement scale) with institutional aspects (excluding trees that are considered to be agricultural) http://dx.doi.org/10.5716/WP16079.PDF" .

:def_Forest_ICSU_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :ICSU ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.icsu-scope.org/downloadpubs/scope56/Chapter04.html" ;
    :definitionText "(ICSU) Forests have complete tree canopy cover and three or more overlapping vegetation strata; http://www.icsu-scope.org/downloadpubs/scope56/Chapter04.html" .

:def_Forest_IGBP_2013_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :IGBP ;
    dcterms:date "2013"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "60.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.eapap.unep.org/lc/cd/html/training/module1.html" ;
    :definitionText "(IGBP 2013) In IGBP classification system, percent crown cover should be more than 60% and tree height should be more than 2 meters to be classified as forest. http://www.eapap.unep.org/lc/cd/html/training/module1.html http://www.unep.org/dewa/Portals/67/pdf/Nile_Basin.pdf." .

:def_Forest_IIASA_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :IIASA ;
    :canopyThreshold "40.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "6.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.iiasa.ac.at/Research/LUC/lucgis/docs/wp-96-026.htm#Land-Cover" ;
    :definitionText "(IIASA) Forest, canopy coverage > 40%, trees > 6 m. http://www.iiasa.ac.at/Research/LUC/lucgis/docs/wp-96-026.htm#Land-Cover" .

:def_Forest_IndexMundi_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :IndexMundi ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.indexmundi.com/facts/greece/forest-area" ;
    :definitionText "(IndexMundi) Forest area is land under natural or planted stands of trees of at least 5 meters in situ, whether productive or not, and excludes tree stands in agricultural production systems (for example, in fruit plantations and agroforestry systems) and trees in urban parks and gardens.. http://www.indexmundi.com/facts/greece/forest-area" .

:def_Forest_IPCC_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :IPCC ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.grida.no/climate/ipcc/regional/327.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(IPCC 1997) An ecosystem in which the dominant plants are trees; woodlands are distinguished from forests by their lower density of trees http://www.grida.no/climate/ipcc/regional/327.htm" .

:def_Forest_IPCC_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :IPCC ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.unep.ch/ipcc/pub/syrgloss.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(IPCC 2003) A vegetation type dominated by trees. http://www.unep.ch/ipcc/pub/syrgloss.pdf Many definitions of the term forest are in use throughout the world, reflecting wide differences in bio-geophysical conditions, social structure, and economics. For a discussion of the term forest and related terms such as →afforestation, →reforestation, and →deforestation: see the IPCC Report on Land Use, Land-Use Change and Forestry (IPCC, 2000). See also the Report on Definitions and Methodological Opti" .

:def_Forest_IPCC_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :IPCC ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://bookshop.europa.eu/is-bin/INTERSHOP.enfinity/WFS/EU-Bookshop-Site/en_GB/-/EUR/ViewPDFFile-OpenPDFFile?FileName=LBNA24300ENC_002.pdf&SKU=LBNA24300ENC_PDF" ;
    :definitionText "(IPCC?) Forest land: includes all land with woody vegetation consistent with thresholds used to define forest land in the national GHG inventory, sub-divided into managed and unmanaged. It also includes systems with vegetation that currently fall below, but are expected to exceed, the threshold of the forest land category. Countries must also specify a forest definition under the Kyoto Protocol. This definition is based on area (0.05 – 1.0 ha); canopy closure (10% - 30%) and tree height (2 – 5 m" .

:def_Forest_ISO_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :ISO ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(ISO 2003) An area of land tree crown cover more than ten per cent with the potential to reach a minimum height of two meters at maturity in situ. ISO TC207/WG5 N70 ISO/WD 14064-1.1 Secretariat: DSM/CSA. January 13, 2003. Principles and requirements for measuring, monitoring and reporting entity- and project-level greenhouse gas emissions and/or removals. 30 p." .

:def_Forest_IUCN_and_WCMC_1990_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :IUCN_and_WCMC ;
    dcterms:date "1990"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://figueresonline.com/csdafinal/English/publications/cdm/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "(IUCN and WCMC 1990) ‘Forests’ have a closed canopy beneath which grasses do not grow. They are distinct from open-canopied woodlands that grow over a grass sward. http://figueresonline.com/csdafinal/English/publications/cdm/glossary.html" .

:def_Forest_IUCN_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :IUCN ;
    :sourceRef "http://cmsdata.iucn.org/downloads/forestcover.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(IUCN) IUCN defines forests as tree dominated landscapes. http://cmsdata.iucn.org/downloads/forestcover.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Millnnieum_Assessment_Organization_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :Millnnieum_Assessment_Organization ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.millenniumassessment.org/documents/document.774.aspx.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Millnnieum Assessment Organization). Forest systems: Systems in which trees are the predominant life forms. Statistics reported in this assessment are based on areas that are dominated by trees (perennial woody plants taller than five meters at maturity), where the tree crown cover exceeds 10%, and where the area is more than 0.5 hectares. ‘‘Open forests’’ have a canopy cover between 10% and 40%, and ‘‘closed forests’’ a canopy cover of more than 40%. ‘‘Fragmented forests’’ refer to mosaics of " .

:def_Forest_NationMaster_2005_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :NationMaster ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nationmaster.com/graph/env_for_are_of_lan_are-environment-forest-area-of-land" ;
    :definitionText "(NationMaster 2005). Land under natural or planted stands of trees, whether productive or not. http://www.nationmaster.com/graph/env_for_are_of_lan_are-environment-forest-area-of-land" .

:def_Forest_North_Africa_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :North_Africa ;
    :sourceRef "Omnia.Moussa@fao.org" ;
    :definitionText "(North Africa) - An ecosystem with a predominance of trees constituting a minimum of 10 percent relatively dense crown cover. \"Moussa, Omnia (FAORNE)\" Omnia.Moussa@fao.org" .

:def_Forest_OECD_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :OECD ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://stats.oecd.org/glossary/detail.asp?ID=6459" ;
    :definitionText "(OECD) Forested land - Land with tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 10 per cent and an area of more than 0.5 hectares. The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 metres at maturity in situ. http://stats.oecd.org/glossary/detail.asp?ID=6459" .

:def_Forest_RED_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :RED ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.tropenbos.org/file.php/4/forests-dec21-final-web.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(RED 2009) Continuously forested areas with a land spanning of more than one hectare with trees higher than five metres and a canopy cover of more than 30%, or trees able to reach those thresholds in situ. http://www.tropenbos.org/file.php/4/forests-dec21-final-web.pdf" .

:def_Forest_SADC_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :SADC ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "70.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(SADC 1997) - All wooded areas with greater than +/- 70% tree canopy cover, where the dominant canopy is greater than +/- 5m in thight (minimum height). Essentially indigenous tree species growing under natural or semi-natural conditions (although it may include some localised areas of self-seeded exotic species). Excludes planted forests (and woodlots). (Trevett 1997)" .

:def_Forest_Small_Islands_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :Small_Islands ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cfa.juice-e.co.uk/Example%20paper/Example%20paper.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Small Islands) Forest is defined as land with tree crown cover of more than 10 percent and area of more than 0.5 ha whose primary use is forestry. The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 metres at maturity in situ. http://cfa.juice-e.co.uk/Example%20paper/Example%20paper.htm" .

:def_Forest_TBFRA_1990_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :TBFRA ;
    dcterms:date "1990"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "7.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.metla.fi/eu/cost/e4/coste4.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(TBFRA 1990) TBFRA criteria for 1990 were even stricter: crown cover had to be 20 % or more and tree height at least 7 meters. http://www.metla.fi/eu/cost/e4/coste4.pdf" .

:def_Forest_TBFRA_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :TBFRA ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.metla.fi/eu/cost/e4/coste4.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(TBFRA 2000) TBFRA 2000 requires that the crown cover is greater than 10 % and tree height is greater than 5 meters. http://www.metla.fi/eu/cost/e4/coste4.pdf" .

:def_Forest_TBFRA_2000_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :TBFRA ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.mosus.net/documents/MOSUS_Forestry%20sector.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(TBFRA-2000) items are most relevant for the present study: • Forest land: Forest is defined as “land with tree crown cover of more than 10 percent and area more than 0.5 ha.” Trees on the site are considered to be higher than 5 m. http://www.mosus.net/documents/MOSUS_Forestry%20sector.pdf" .

:def_Forest_TREES_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :TREES ;
    :canopyThreshold "70.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.gvm.sai.jrc.it/Forest/statistics.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(TREES) Evergreen and Semi-Deciduous Forest - forest cover > 70% in each AVHRR pixel http://www.gvm.sai.jrc.it/Forest/statistics.htm" .

:def_Forest_UN_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.equitybd.org/documents/cts_eng.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN 2009) the UN defines a forest as any area larger than 500 square metres with crown cover of 10 per cent and trees capable of growing two metres high. The differences between native forests and monoculture industrial tree plantations cannot be identified by this definition (UN-REDD, 2009). http://www.equitybd.org/documents/cts_eng.pdf" .

:def_Forest_UN_CBD_2001_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_CBD ;
    dcterms:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.millenniumassessment.org/documents/document.290.aspx.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-CBD 2001) Ecosystems in which trees are the predominant life forms. Global Biodiversity Outlook (Secretariat of the Convention on Biological Diversity 2001) http://www.millenniumassessment.org/documents/document.290.aspx.pdf" .

:def_Forest_UN_CCD_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_CCD ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.unccd.int/actionprogrammes/asia/national/2000/yemen-eng.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-CCD 2000) Dense canopy with multi-layered structure including large trees in the upper storey; http://www.unccd.int/actionprogrammes/asia/national/2000/yemen-eng.pdf United Nations Convention to Combat Desertification" .

:def_Forest_UN_ECEEFAO_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_ECEEFAO ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://figueresonline.com/csdafinal/English/publications/cdm/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-ECEE/FAO 1997) Land with tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 10 percent and area of more than 0.5 ha. The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 m at maturity in situ. May consist either of closed forest formations where trees of various storeys and undergrowth cover a high portion of the ground; or of open forest formations where trees of various storeys and undergrowth cover a high portion of the ground; or of open forest formations with a continuous v" .

:def_Forest_UN_EP_2013_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_EP ;
    dcterms:date "2013"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "60.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.unep.org/dewa/Portals/67/pdf/Nile_Basin.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-EP 2013) Lands dominated by trees with a per cent canopy cover >60% and height exceeding 2 metres http://www.unep.org/dewa/Portals/67/pdf/Nile_Basin.pdf" .

:def_Forest_UN_EP_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_EP ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.eapap.unep.org/lc/cd/html/training/module1.html" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-EP) - Land covered by trees with the percent canopy cover greater than 10%. Trees are woody plants land cover with a single well defined stem and more than 3 meters in height. Forest with 10-40% canopy cover is classified as open forest and with 40% and above is classified as closed forest. http://www.eapap.unep.org/lc/cd/html/training/module1.html" .

:def_Forest_UN_EPCBD_2001_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_EPCBD ;
    dcterms:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(UN-EP/CBD 2001) - Forest is a land area of more than 0.5 ha, with a tree canopy cover of more than 10 percent, which is not primarily under agriculture or other specific non-forest land use. In the case of young forest or regions where tree growth is climatically suppressed, the trees should be capable of reaching a height of 5 m in situ, and of meeting the canopy cover requirement. ftp://ftp.fao.org/docrep/fao/009/j9345e/j9345e00.pdf" .

:def_Forest_UN_EPCBD_2002_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_EPCBD ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.environmental-auditing.org/LinkClick.aspx?fileticket=fbx%2FbAIVeFU%3D&tabid=128&mid=568" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-EP/CBD 2002), A land area of more than 0.5 ha, with a tree canopy cover of more than 10 percent, which is not primarily under agriculture or other specific non-forest land use. In the case of young forest or regions where tree growth is climatically suppressed, the trees should be capable of reaching a height of 5 m in situ, and of meeting the canopy cover requirement http://www.environmental-auditing.org/LinkClick.aspx?fileticket=fbx%2FbAIVeFU%3D&tabid=128&mid=568" .

:def_Forest_UN_EP_EAP_AP_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_EP_EAP_AP ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.rrcap.unep.org/lc/cd/html/16thacrs.html" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-EP-EAP-AP) - Land covered by trees with the percent canopy cover greater than 10%. Trees are woody plants with a single weft defined stem and more than 3 meters in height. Forest with 10-40% canopy cover is classified as open forest and with 40% and above is classified as closed forest. http://www.rrcap.unep.org/lc/cd/html/16thacrs.html" .

:def_Forest_UN_EP_GRID_2001_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_EP_GRID ;
    dcterms:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.grida.no/climate/ipcc_tar/wg2/689.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-EP-GRID 2001) A vegetation type dominated by trees. http://www.grida.no/climate/ipcc_tar/wg2/689.htm (2001)" .

:def_Forest_UN_EP_GRID_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_EP_GRID ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.grida.no/climate/ipcc/regional/327.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-EP-GRID) An ecosystem in which the dominant plants are trees; woodlands are distinguished from forests by their lower density of trees http://www.grida.no/climate/ipcc/regional/327.htm" .

:def_Forest_UN_ESCO_1973_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_ESCO ;
    dcterms:date "1973"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "40.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(UN-ESCO 1973) Closed Forest - trees =5m with crowns interlocking. Woodland - trees =5m tall with crowns not usually touching but with canopy cover =40% (UNESCO 1973)." .

:def_Forest_UN_ESCO_1973_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_ESCO ;
    dcterms:date "1973"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "25.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://pdf.usaid.gov/pdf_docs/PNADL906.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-ESCO 1973) The standard international definition of “forest” is an area with >25 percent canopy cover by trees (UNESCO 1973; “savannah” is usually considered to be a grass-dominated system with sparse trees [by the UNESCO definition, <25 percent cover]). http://pdf.usaid.gov/pdf_docs/PNADL906.pdf" .

:def_Forest_UN_ESCO_1993_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_ESCO ;
    dcterms:date "1993"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://home.comcast.net/~gyde/1993annex3iufro.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-ESCO 1993) Continuous stand of trees at least 10 m tall, their crowns interlocking; - Rain forest, without any significant dry season and with trees usually more than 30 m high; - Dry forest, with dry season of several weeks or months; - Semi-evergreen forest, where some species are deciduous but understory mostly evergreen Deciduous forest, where trees lose their leaves simultaneously for months - Undifferentiated forest, with very heterogeneous patterns; http://home.comcast.net/~gyde/1993a" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_1953_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "1953"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/docrep/015/an053e/an053e00.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 1953) Forest is defined as land bearing vegetative associations dominated by trees of any size http://www.fao.org/docrep/015/an053e/an053e00.pdf" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_1958_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "1958"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dse.de/zel/landinfo/pas/tk247_lup_eth/forest_inventory.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 1958) Forest may be defined as all lands bearing a vegetative association dominated by tree of any size, exploited or not, capable of producing wood or other products, for exerting an influence on climate or on the water regime, or providing shelter for live stock and wild life. http://www.dse.de/zel/landinfo/pas/tk247_lup_eth/forest_inventory.pdf" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_1987_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "1987"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/legal/legstud/frmdocrep/41_AK476E.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 1987) the forest is a plant formation in which trees predominate to the extent of modifying the ecology of the terrain. In order to form a specific community of this kind, the trees must occupy a sufficiently large area of land and at a minimum level of density. http://www.fao.org/legal/legstud/frmdocrep/41_AK476E.pdf" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_1990_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "1990"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/docrep/007/t0830e/T0830E04.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 1990) (Tropical countries) Ecosystems with a minimum of 10 percent crown cover of trees and/or bamboos, generally associated with wild flora, fauna and natural soil conditions, and not subject to agricultural practices. http://www.fao.org/docrep/007/t0830e/T0830E04.htm and http://figueresonline.com/csdafinal/English/publications/cdm/glossary.html" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_1993_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "1993"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "100.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ciesin.columbia.edu/docs/002-471/002-471.html" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 1993) Forests are ecological systems with minimum crown coverage of land surface (here assumed as 10 percent) and generally associated with wild flora, fauna and natural soil conditions; and not subject to agronomic practices. For the present assessments, a tree is defined as a woody perennial with a single main stem (except in coppice crops where multiple stems replace a single stem), a more or less definite crown and a minimum height of more than 5 meters on maturity. Only forest areas" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_1995_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "1995"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://figueresonline.com/csdafinal/English/publications/cdm/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 1995) Ecosystems with a minimum of 10% cover of trees and/or bamboos, generally associated with wild flora, fauna and natural soil conditions, and not subject to agricultural practices. The term forest is further subdivided, according to its origin, into two categories: (i) Natural forests: a subset of forest composed of tree species known to be indigenous to the area; and; (ii) Plantation forests: established artificially by afforestation on lands which previously did not carry forests " .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_1995_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "1995"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "7.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://figueresonline.com/csdafinal/English/publications/cdm/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 1995) Land with tree crown cover (stand density) of more than about 20 percent of the area. Continuous forest with trees usually growing to more than about 7 m in height and able to produce wood. This includes both closed forest formations where trees of various storeys and undergrowth cover a high proportion of the ground, and open forest formations with a continuous grass layer in which tree synusia cover at least 10 percent of the ground. Definition applies for developed countries. ht" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "7.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 1997) (developed countries) Land with tree crown cover (stand density) of more than about 20 per cent of the area. Continuous forest with trees usually growing to more than about 7 m in height and able to produce wood. This includes both closed forest formations where trees of various storeys and undergrowth cover a high proportion of the ground, and open forest formations with a continuous grass layer in which tree synusia cover at least 10 per cent of the ground (FAO 1997)." .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_1997_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://faov02.fao.org:70/0gopher_root%3a[fao.fra" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 1997) (developing countries) Ecological systems with a minimum of 10% crown coverage of trees and/or bamboos, generally associated with wild flora, fauna and natural soil conditions, and not subject to agricultural practices. [Source: from http://faov02.fao.org:70/0gopher_root%3a[fao.fra]def_uk.txt (concepts, definitions and methodology of the FAO Forest Resources Assessment 1990) via Bernhard Schlamadinger], (FAO 1997) and http://www.ids.ac.uk/eldis/forests/forpap.htm." .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_1999_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://europe.mtnforum.org/rs/econfreports/MountainPeopleForestsAndTrees.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 1999) Land with tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 10% and area of more than 0.5 hectares (ha). The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5m at maturity in situ.\" http://europe.mtnforum.org/rs/econfreports/MountainPeopleForestsAndTrees.pdf" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/docrep/field/385907.htm#P280_16342" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 2000) Land with tree a crown cover of more than 10 percent, and a tree height of at least five meters. An important distinction is made between closed (40% crown cover) and open (10 -40 % crown cover) forest. http://www.fao.org/docrep/field/385907.htm#P280_16342. Note: There is another definition forest for FRA 2000 based on land use." .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.cof.orst.edu/cof/teach/fe456/Class_Materials/State%20of%20Worlds%20Forests/SOTWF_2003.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 2003) Forest land is defined as having more than 10 percent crown cover and an area of more than 0.5 ha, and excludes land predominantly used for agriculture. http://www.cof.orst.edu/cof/teach/fe456/Class_Materials/State%20of%20Worlds%20Forests/SOTWF_2003.pdf" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_2005_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/es/ess/census/PROGwca2010/glossary_r7.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 2005) Forest: land with trees of height 5 metres or more with crown cover of more than 10% (paragraph 11.35). http://www.fao.org/es/ess/census/PROGwca2010/glossary_r7.pdf" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_2005_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/docrep/013/i1757e/i1757e13.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 2005) Land spanning more than 0.5 hectares with trees higher than 5 meters and a canopy cover of more than 10 percent, or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ. It does not include land that is predominantly under agricultural or urban land use. FRA 2005 and 2010. http://www.fao.org/docrep/013/i1757e/i1757e13.pdf" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_2005_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/es/ess/census/12ch5.asp" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 2005) Woodland or forest - This includes woodlot or timber tracts, natural or planted, constituting part of the holding which have or will have value as wood, timber, other forest products or for protection. Forest tree nurseries should be included in this category. Rows, belts and small clumps of trees, bamboo and other woody vegetation should be included in woodland and forest. http://www.fao.org/es/ess/census/12ch5.asp" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_2007_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://earthobservatory.nasa.gov/Features/Deforestation/printall.php" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 2007) any area larger than one hectare (0.01 square miles) with a minimum tree cover of 10 percent to be forested. http://earthobservatory.nasa.gov/Features/Deforestation/printall.php" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_2014_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "2014"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/uploads/media/glc-share-doc.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 2014) Tree covered areas -This class includes any geographic area dominated by natural tree plants with a cover of 10% or more. Other types of plants (shrubs and/or herbs) can be present, even with a density higher than trees. Areas planted with trees for afforestation purposes and forest plantations are included in this class. This class includes areas seasonally or permanently flooded with fresh water. It excludes coastal mangroves. http://www.fao.org/uploads/media/glc-share-doc.pdf" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_2015_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "2015"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/3/a-i4498e.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 2015) Forest cover - Total cover of the forest area delineated by vertical projection http://www.fao.org/3/a-i4498e.pdf" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    :sourceRef "http://ddp-ext.worldbank.org/ext/ddpreports/viewSourceNotes?DIMENSION_NAME=WDI_Series&HIERARCHY=Topic&cubeId=7" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO) Forest area is land under natural or planted stands of trees, whether productive or not. http://ddp-ext.worldbank.org/ext/ddpreports/viewSourceNotes?DIMENSION_NAME=WDI_Series&HIERARCHY=Topic&cubeId=7" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    :canopyThreshold "40.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "Graeme Wild <GraemeW@za.sappi.com>" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO) Land covered by trees with a cover of more than 40% From: Graeme Wild GraemeW@za.sappi.com" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://glossary.eea.europa.eu" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO) Land with a tree canopy cover of more than 10% and an area of more than 0.5 ha. http://glossary.eea.europa.eu" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_RAP_2010_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO_RAP ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/docrep/012/i1594e/i1594e00.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO-RAP 2010) Forest is defined as: land spanning more than 0.5 hectares, with trees higher than 5 metres and a canopy cover of more than 10 percent or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ. It does not include land that is predominantly agricultural or under urban use. http://www.fao.org/docrep/012/i1594e/i1594e00.pdf" .

:def_Forest_UN_FCCC_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FCCC ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FCCC )Forest land - As part of COP7 (Marrakech accords) it was decided that parties could select a single value of tree height, crown area and area to define forests, subject to certain ranges. The Designated National Authority in each country is responsible for forest definition (see http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA and http://www.snvworld.org/en/regions/asia/ourwork/Documents/SNV_UnderstandingREDD.pdf)" .

:def_Forest_UN_FCCC_2001_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FCCC ;
    dcterms:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.worldgrowth.org/assets/file/WG%20Forestry_Development_Final%20Report.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FCCC 2001) (from the Marrakesh Accords of the Kyoto Protocol): An area of land: that is at least 0.05 – 1.0 hectares in size; which has more than 10-30 per cent of tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking levels); and which has trees that have the potential to reach a minimum height at maturity in situ of 2-5 metres. It may consist either of closed forest formations or open forest. Closed forest formations involve to a high proportion of the ground being covered by trees of various storeys a" .

:def_Forest_UN_HCR_2005_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_HCR ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://postconflict.unep.ch/liberia/displacement/documents/UNHCR_IUCN_Forest_Management_Refugee_Returnee_Situations.pdf(UN-IPCC" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-HCR 2005) An ecosystem with a minimum of 10 per cent crown cover of trees. http://postconflict.unep.ch/liberia/displacement/documents/UNHCR_IUCN_Forest_Management_Refugee_Returnee_Situations.pdf(UN-IPCC 2001) A vegetation type dominated by trees http://www.ipcc.ch/pub/tar/wg1/518.htm and http://www.pnl.gov/aisu/pubs/eemw/papers/ipccreports/workinggroup2/689.htm." .

:def_Forest_UN_OECD_2005_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_OECD ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://stats.oecd.org/glossary/detail.asp?ID=6459" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-OECD 2005) - Land with tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 10 per cent and an area of more than 0.5 hectares. The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 metres at maturity in situ. http://stats.oecd.org/glossary/detail.asp?ID=6459" .

:def_Forest_UN_SD_2001_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_SD ;
    dcterms:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(UN-SD 2001) Forest and other wooded land - Land with tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 10 per cent and area of more than 0.5 hectares and land either with a crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of 5-10 per cent of trees able to reach a height of 5 metres at maturity in situ; or a crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 10 per cent of trees not able to reach a height of 5 metres at maturity in situ (e.g. dwarf or stunted trees); or with shrub or b" .

:def_Forest_UN_SD_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_SD ;
    :sourceRef "http://esa.un.org/unsd/envmnt/gesform.asp?getitem=539" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-SD) Forest Cover - All the trees and other woody plants (underbrush) covering the ground in a forest. It includes (a) trees and all shrubs, (b) herbs and shrubs growing thereunder or in openings in the forest or brush fields, (c) litter or fallen leaves, branches, fallen trees and other vegetable material on the forest floor and (d) the rich humus of partially decayed vegetable matter at the surface and top layer of the soil. http://esa.un.org/unsd/envmnt/gesform.asp?getitem=539 United Natio" .

:def_Forest_WAF_2004_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :WAF ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.worldagroforestry.org/sea/Publications/files/book/BK0073-04.PDF" ;
    :definitionText "(WAF 2004) -An ecosystem in which the dominant plants are trees covering a vast tract of land. http://www.worldagroforestry.org/sea/Publications/files/book/BK0073-04.PDF" .

:def_Forest_WCMC_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :WCMC ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.wcmc.org.uk/forest/data/cdrom2/text2.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(WCMC) - While not a definition per se, the WCMC uses a 30% tree canopy cover for the development its Global Current Forest Map - http://www.wcmc.org.uk/forest/data/cdrom2/text2.htm" .

:def_Forest_World_Bank_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :World_Bank ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.holz.uni-goettingen.de/ek/woodsat/pdf/worldbankforestry.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(World Bank 2000) Ecosystem with a minimum of 10 percent crown cover of trees and/or bamboo, generally associated with wild flora and fauna and natural soil conditions and not subject to agricultural practices. Forests are in two categories: • Natural forests: forests composed of tree species known to be indigenous to the area. • Plantation forests: established artificially by afforestation on lands previously non-forested within living memory, or established artificially by reforestation on lan" .

:def_Forest_World_Bank_2000_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :World_Bank ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.holz.uni-goettingen.de/ek/woodsat/pdf/worldbankforestry.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(World Bank 2000) Forest, Open: Forest in which the tree canopy layer is discontinuous but covers at least 10 percent of the area and in which the grass layer is continuous. http://www.holz.uni-goettingen.de/ek/woodsat/pdf/worldbankforestry.pdf" .

:def_Forest_World_Bank_2000_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :World_Bank ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.holz.uni-goettingen.de/ek/woodsat/pdf/worldbankforestry.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(World Bank 2000) Forest. Closed: Forest with a stand density greater than 20 percent of the area, and where tree crowns nearly contact one another. . http://www.holz.uni-goettingen.de/ek/woodsat/pdf/worldbankforestry.pdf" .

:def_Forest_World_Bank_2005_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :World_Bank ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://siteresources.worldbank.org/INTARD/Resources/devpol_final_text.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(World Bank 2005) Total Forest is defined as land with tree crown cover of more than 10 percent of the ground and area of more than 0.5 hectares. Tree height at maturity should exceed 5 meters. (source: Earthtrends, WRI) http://siteresources.worldbank.org/INTARD/Resources/devpol_final_text.pdf" .

:def_Forest_World_Bank_2007_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :World_Bank ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.sasi.group.shef.ac.uk/worldmapper/display.php?selected=106" ;
    :definitionText "(World Bank 2007) Land under natural or planted stands of trees. http://www.sasi.group.shef.ac.uk/worldmapper/display.php?selected=106" .

:def_Forest_World_Bank_2008_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :World_Bank ;
    dcterms:date "2008"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://siteresources.worldbank.org/EXTARD/Resources/336681-1215724937571/eBook.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(World Bank 2008). Forest – Minimum are of 1 ha of land with tree-crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 30 percent with trees able to reach the potential of a minimum height of 5 m at maturity in situ. Young plantations and lands used for forestry are included even though they may not meet the cover and height thresholds. http://siteresources.worldbank.org/EXTARD/Resources/336681-1215724937571/eBook.pdf" .

:def_Forest_World_Bank_2012_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :World_Bank ;
    dcterms:date "2012"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://data.worldbank.org/indicator/AG.LND.FRST.ZS" ;
    :definitionText "(World Bank 2012) Forest area is land under natural or planted stands of trees of at least 5 meters in situ, whether productive or not, and excludes tree stands in agricultural production systems (for example, in fruit plantations and agroforestry systems) and trees in urban parks and gardens. http://data.worldbank.org/indicator/AG.LND.FRST.ZS" .

:def_Forest_World_Bank_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :World_Bank ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.iucn.org/themes/fcp/activities/publications/worldbankdraftdefinitions.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(World Bank) - An area of land of not less than 1.0 hectare with tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 10 per cent with trees with the potential to reach a minimum height of 2 meters at maturity in situ. A forest may consist of either closed forest formations where trees of various stories and undergrowth cover a high proportion of the ground or open forest. Young natural stands and all plantations which have yet to reach a crown density of 10 per cent or tree height of 2 " .

:def_Forest_WRI_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :WRI ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "60.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://earthtrends.wri.org/pdf_library/country_profiles/for_cou_188.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(WRI 2003) include all areas dominated by evergreen or deciduous trees with a canopy cover of greater than 60% and a height exceeding 2 meters. Both broadleaf and needleleaf trees are included. http://earthtrends.wri.org/pdf_library/country_profiles/for_cou_188.pdf" .

:def_Forest_WRI_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :WRI ;
    :sourceRef "http://pdf.wri.org/indoforest_glossary.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(WRI) Land on which trees form the dominant vegetation type. http://pdf.wri.org/indoforest_glossary.pdf" .

:def_Forest_WRI_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :WRI ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://pdf.wri.org/page_forests.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(WRI) Terrestrial ecosystems dominated by trees, where the tree canopy covers at least 10 percent of the ground area. http://pdf.wri.org/page_forests.pdf" .

:def_Forest_WRI_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :WRI ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://earthtrends.wri.org/pdf_library/country_profiles/for_cou_188.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(WRI) Total forest area includes both natural forests and plantations. Total Forest is defined as land with tree crown cover of more than 10 percent of the ground and area of more than 0.5 hectares. Tree height at maturity should exceed 5 meters. These forest statistics are based primarily on forest inventory information provided by national governments. http://earthtrends.wri.org/pdf_library/country_profiles/for_cou_188.pdf" .

:def_Forest_AR_SSC_AR_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :AR_SSC_AR ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/Reference/Guidclarif/glos_CDM_v04.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(A/R - SSC A/R) - “Forest” is a minimum area of land of 0.05-1.0 hectares with tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 10-30 per cent with trees with the potential to reach a minimum height of 2-5 metres at maturity in situ. A forest may consist either of closed forest formations where trees of various storeys and undergrowth cover a high proportion of the ground or open forest. Young natural stands and all plantations which have yet to reach a crown density of 10-30 per cen" .

:def_Forest_EU_2013_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :EU ;
    dcterms:date "2013"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32013D0529" ;
    :definitionText "(EU 2013) ‘Forest’ means an area of land defined by the minimum values for area size, tree crown cover or an equivalent stocking level, and potential tree height at maturity at the place of growth of the trees, as specified for each Member State in Annex V. It includes areas with trees, including groups of growing young natural trees, or plantations that have yet to reach the minimum values for tree crown cover or equivalent stocking level or minimum tree height as specified in Annex V, includin" .

:def_Forest_EU_Copenicus_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :EU_Copenicus ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://land.copernicus.eu/pan-european/high-resolution-layers/forests" ;
    :definitionText "(EU Copenicus) The forest type product allows to get as close as possible to the FAO forest definition. In its original (20m) resolution it consists of two products: 1) a dominant leaf type product that has a MMU of 0.5 ha, as well as a 10% tree cover density threshold applied, and 2) a support layer that maps, based on the dominant leaf type product, trees under agricultural use and in urban context (derived from CLC and imperviousness 2009 data). For the final 100m product trees under agricult" .

:def_Forest_EUROSTAT_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :EUROSTAT ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://epp.eurostat.ec.europa.eu/cache/ITY_OFFPUB/KS-74-06-823/EN/KS-74-06-823-EN.PDF" ;
    :definitionText "(EUROSTAT) Land with tree crown cover of more than 10 percent and area of more than 0.5 ha. The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5m at maturity in situ. Young natural stands and all plantations established for forestry purposes which have yet to reach a crown density of 10 percent or tree height of 5m are included under forest, as are areas normally forming part of the forest area but which are temporarily unstocked as a result of human intervention or natural causes but which a" .

:def_Forest_IFAD_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :IFAD ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ifad.org/lrkm/glossary/glossary.htm#/" ;
    :definitionText "(IFAD) Land on which the vegetation is dominated by forest or, if trees are lacking, the land bears evidence of former forest and has not been converted to other vegetation. International Fund for Agricultural Development. http://www.ifad.org/lrkm/glossary/glossary.htm#/" .

:def_Forest_IPCC_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :IPCC ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(IPCC 2006)This category includes all land with woody vegetation consistent with thresholds used to define Forest Land in the national greenhouse gas inventory. It also includes systems with a vegetation structure that currently fall below, but in situ could potentially reach the threshold values used by a country to define the Forest Land category." .

:def_Forest_IPCC_Kyoto_Protocol_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :IPCC_Kyoto_Protocol ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.v-c-s.org/docs/AFOLU%20Guidance%20Document.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(IPCC -Kyoto Protocol) A minimum area of land of 0.05 – 1.0 hectares with tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 10 – 30 per cent with trees with the potential to reach a minimum height of 2 – 5 metres at maturity in situ. A forest may consist either of closed forest formations where trees of various storeys and undergrowth cover a high portion of the ground or open forest. Young natural stands and all plantations which have yet to reach a crown density of 10 – 30 per cent " .

:def_Forest_Islamic_Countries_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :Islamic_Countries ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.sesrtcic.org/SUBFILES/SUBJDEF.HTM" ;
    :definitionText "(Islamic Countries) Forest (and woodland) - Areas covered by natural or planted trees and areas that are cleared but planned to be reforested. Source:http://www.sesrtcic.org/SUBFILES/SUBJDEF.HTM - for 56 Islamic Countries" .

:def_Forest_ITTO_2005_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :ITTO ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.cde.unibe.ch/University/pdf/Feu_CP_Vol6(3" ;
    :definitionText "(ITTO 2005) Forests, Permanent. ITTO defines permanent forests as ‘certain categories of land, whether public or private, that are to be kept under permanent forest cover to secure their optimal contribution to national development’ (ITTO, 2006). http://www.cde.unibe.ch/University/pdf/Feu_CP_Vol6(3)_Foener_et_al_edited_00A.pdf" .

:def_Forest_IUFRO_2002_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :IUFRO ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/ir_06.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(IUFRO 2002) A land area with a minimum 10% tree crown coverage (or equivalent stocking level), or formerly having such tree cover and that is being naturally or artificially regenerated or that is being afforested. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/ir_06.pdf" .

:def_Forest_TBFRA_20010_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :TBFRA_20010 ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://epp.eurostat.ec.europa.eu/cache/ITY_OFFPUB/KS-BE-02-003/EN/KS-BE-02-003-EN.PDF" ;
    :definitionText "(TBFRA-20010), forest is defined as land with tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 10 per cent and area more than 0.5 ha. The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 m at maturity in situ. Included are: • young natural stands and all plantations established for forestry purposes which have yet to reach the crown density of 10 percent or tree height of 5 m. • areas normally forming part of the forest area which are temporarily unstocked as a result of human int" .

:def_Forest_UN_1996_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN ;
    dcterms:date "1996"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(UN 1996) Forests - whether natural, modified or planted - are biotic communities characterized by a predominance of woody vegetation. They are found in all climatic zones (boreal, temperate, tropical and mountainous) and may take the form of closed canopy forests or open canopy woodlands. They comprise all the components of forest ecosystems and their natural resources. Forest lands may be covered by forests or degraded - that is, currently devoid of trees or not maintained in a sustainable man" .

:def_Forest_UN_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.un.org/Pubs/CyberSchoolBus/infonation/e_terms.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(UN) Land under natural or planted stands of trees, including land from which forest has been cleared but that will be reforested in the foreseeable future, and including areas occupied by roads, small cleared tracts and other small open areas within the forest. http://www.un.org/Pubs/CyberSchoolBus/infonation/e_terms.htm" .

:def_Forest_UN_CBD_2010_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_CBD ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.google.com/url?sa=t&source=web&cd=51&ved=0CBgQFjAAODI&url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.iucnael.org%2Fen%2Fdocuments%2Fdoc_download%2F560-lesniewska-definition-of-forests-in-international-environmental-" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-CBD 2010) - Forest is a land area of more than 0.5 ha, with a tree canopy cover of more than 10%, which is not primarily under agriculture or other specific non-forest land use. In the case of young forest or regions where tree growth is climatically suppressed, the trees should be capable of reaching a height of 5m in situ, and of meeting the canopy cover requirement.’ Convention on Biological Diversity. http://www.google.com/url?sa=t&source=web&cd=51&ved=0CBgQFjAAODI&url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.i" .

:def_Forest_UN_DP_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_DP ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.undp.kz/infobase/glossary_sector.html?glos_id%5B%5D=42" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-DP) Refers to land under natural or planted stands of trees, whether productive or not, including land from which forest has been cleared but which will be reforested in the foreseeable future, and including areas occupied by roads, small cleared tracts and other small open areas within the forest that constitute an integral part of the forest. Includes land under coniferous and non-coniferous forest, land under mixed forest and other wooded land. http://www.undp.kz/infobase/glossary_sector." .

:def_Forest_UN_EP_2007_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_EP ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.unep.org/geo/geo4/report/Glossary.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-EP 2007) - Land spanning more than 0.5 hectares with trees higher than 5 metres and a canopy cover of more than 10 per cent, or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ. It does not include land that is predominantly under agricultural or urban land use. http://www.unep.org/geo/geo4/report/Glossary.pdf" .

:def_Forest_UN_EPCBD_2001_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_EPCBD ;
    dcterms:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.worldgrowth.org/assets/file/WG%20Forestry_Development_Final%20Report.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-EP/CBD 2001) An area of land: that is more than 0.5 hectares in size; which has a tree canopy cover of more than 10 per cent; and which is not primarily under agriculture or other specific non-forest land use. It includes young forest or regions in which tree growth is climatically suppressed, only if the trees have the potential to: reach a height of five metres in situ; and meet the requirement in respect of canopy cover. http://www.worldgrowth.org/assets/file/WG%20Forestry_Development_Fin" .

:def_Forest_UN_EP_GRID_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_EP_GRID ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "7.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(UN-EP-GRID) Forest is defined as >30% crown cover and the tree height shall be >7 m. Seedlings under forest are also included in this class. Areas occupied by forest and woodlands with a vegetation pattern composed of native or exotic coniferous trees, and which can be used for the production of timber or other forest products. The forest trees are under normal climatic conditions higher than 5 m with a canopy closure of 30% at least. www.grida.no/baltic/related/balans_landcover_classification_" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_1948_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "1948"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/docrep/x5345e/x5345e03.htm#some%20definitions" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 1948) Lands bearing vegetative associations dominated by trees of any size, capable of producing timber or other forest products or of exerting an influence on the climate or on the water regime. Also, lands from which forests have been recently clear cut or burned, but which will be reforested in the near future. http://www.fao.org/docrep/x5345e/x5345e03.htm#some%20definitions" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_1958_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "1958"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/documents/show_cdr.asp?url_file=/docrep/007/ad906t/AD906T05.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 1958) All lands bearing vegetative associations dominated by trees of any size, exploited or not, capable of producing wood or other forest products, of exerting an influence on the climate or on the water regime, or providing shelter for livestock and wild life. Includes: Lands from which forests have been clear-cut or burned, but which will be reforested in the foreseeable future; Public and private forest of any size; Forest of slow growth and of dwarfed or stunted forms — e.g., subal" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_1960_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "1960"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/3/a-ad906t.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 1960) All lands bearing vegetative associations dominated by trees of any size, exploited or not, capable of producing wood or other forest products, of exerting an influence on the climate or on the water regime, or providing shelter for livestock and wildlife. Includes: Lands from which forests have been clear-cut or burned, but which will be reforested in the foreseeable future; Public and private forest of any size; Forest of slow growth and of dwarfed or stunted forms e.g., subalpin" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_1963_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "1963"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/3/a-ad907t.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 1963) : All lands bearing vegetative associations dominated by trees of any size, exploited or not, capable of producing wood or other forest products, of exerting an influence on the climate or on the water regime, or providing shelter for livestock and wild life. Includes: (i) Lands from which forest has been clear-cut or burned, but which will be reforested in the foreseeable future ; Public and private forests of any size; Forest of slow growth and of dwarfed or stunted forms - e.g.," .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_1987_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "1987"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/legal/legstud/frmdocrep/41_AK476E.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 1987) forest stands by referring to them as “plant formations where the principal products consist of timber” 1/, to the exclusion of any other plants that are not otherwise agricultural products 2/. http://www.fao.org/legal/legstud/frmdocrep/41_AK476E.pdf" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_1988_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "1988"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.wcslc.edu/pers_pages/r-ford/LUCC/unit2/background2.html#Forests" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 1988) (and Woodland) Land under natural or planted stands of trees, whether productive or not, and includes land from which forests have been cleared but that will be reforested in the foreseeable future (FAO 1988a: 3). http://www.wcslc.edu/pers_pages/r-ford/LUCC/unit2/background2.html#Forests, and http://resweb.llu.edu/rford/docs/VGD/LUCC/background2.html" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_1992_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "1992"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.mmm.fi/english/minkonf/criteria.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 1992) Land under natural or planted stand of trees, whether productive or not. Included are shrub land, savannah etc., land from which forests have been cleared but that will be reforested in the foreseeable future, area occupied by forest roads, small cleared tracts and other small open areas within the forest and which constitute an integral part of the forest. [Sources: FAO yearbook Production. 1992. Vol. 46. FAO Statistics Series No. 112. 281 pp. http://www.mmm.fi/english/minkonf/cri" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_1995_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "1995"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 1995) (and woodland) - Includes woodlot or timber tracts, natural or planted, constituting part of the holding which have or will have value as wood, timber, or other forest products or for protection. Forest tree nurseries should be included in this category. Rows, belts and small clumps of trees, bamboo and other woody vegetation should be included.... Proposed definition for the World Census for Agriculture 2000. (FAO 1995)." .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_1995_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "1995"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.archive.org/stream/forestresourcesa034883mbp/forestresourcesa034883mbp_djvu.txt" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 1995) land under natural or planted stands of trees, whether productive or not, including land from which forest has been cleared but that will be reforested in the foreseeable future, and including areas occupied by roads, small cleared tracts and other small open areas within the forest which constitute an integral part of the forest http://www.archive.org/stream/forestresourcesa034883mbp/forestresourcesa034883mbp_djvu.txt" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_1997_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/waicent/faosat/agricult/landuse-e.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 1997) (and Woodland). Land under natural or planted stands of trees, whether productive or not. This category included land from which trees have been cleared but will be reforested in the foreseeable future, but it excludes woodland or forest used only for recreation purposes. Stands of permanent crops such as rubber, fruit trees, nut trees, are classed as permanent crops under agricultural lands. [Source: FAO Production Yearbook. 10.10.97. http://www.fao.org/waicent/faosat/agricult/lan" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_2001_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/docrep/003/y0900e/y0900e11.htm#P1_7" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 2001) Forest includes natural forests and forest plantations. The term is used to refer to land with a tree canopy cover of more than 10 percent and area of more than 0.5 ha. Forests are determined both by the presence of trees and the absence of other predominant land uses. The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 m. Young stands that have not yet reached, but are expected to reach, a crown density of 10 percent and tree height of 5 m are included under forest, as are tem" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_2001_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 2001) Forests are lands of more than 0.5 hectares, with a tree canopy cover of more than 10 per cent, which are not primarily under agricultural or urban land use. Explanatory note: Forests are determined both by the presence of trees and the absence of other predominant land uses. The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 meters in situ. Areas under reforestation which have yet to reach a crown density of 10 per cent or tree height of 5 m are included, as are temporarily u" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_2004_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/forestry/foris/webview/forestry2/index.jsp?siteId=4261&sitetreeId=13629&langId=1&geoId=0" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 2004) Land spanning more than 0.5 hectares with trees higher than 5 meters and a canopy cover of more than 10 percent, or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ. It does not include land that is predominantly under agricultural or urban land use. Explanatory notes: 1. Forest is determined both by the presence of trees and the absence of other predominant land uses. The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 meters in situ. Areas under reforestation that have not yet re" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_2005_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/es/ess/census/PROGwca2010/chapter11_r7.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 2005) Forest land is land not classified as mainly “agricultural land” and is land with crown cover of more than 10 percent of trees able to reach a mature height of 5 metres or more. It includes natural and plantation forests. Areas that are temporarily not under trees but are expected to revert to forest are included. Forest tree nurseries that form an integral part of the forest should be included. http://www.fao.org/es/ess/census/PROGwca2010/chapter11_r7.pdf" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.worldgrowth.org/assets/file/WG%20Forestry_Development_Final%20Report.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 2006) (from the Global Forest Resources Assessment 2005): An area of land: that is more than 0.5 hectares in size; which has trees that are more than five metres in height; and which has a canopy cover of more than 10 per cent. It includes an area of land which has trees that have the potential to meet these thresholds in situ. It also includes areas which are temporarily unstocked (due to human intervention or natural causes) which are expected to regenerate. It excludes land that is pr" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_2006_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 2006) Land spanning more than 0.5 hectares with trees higher than 5 metres and a canopy cover of more than 10 percent, or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ. It does not include land that is predominantly under agriculture or urban use. Explanatory note: Forest is determined both by the presence of trees and the absence of other predominant land uses. The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 m in situ. Areas under reforestation that have not yet reached but are e" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_2007_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://faostat.fao.org/site/379/default.aspx" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 2007) (and Woodlands) - Land under natural or planted stands of trees, whether productive or not. This category includes land from which forests have been cleared but that will be reforested in the foreseeable future, but it excludes woodland or forest used only for recreation purposes. http://faostat.fao.org/site/379/default.aspx" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_2010_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/forestry/foris/pdf/fra/2010/north-and-central-america/united-states-virgin-islands-2010-224.doc" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 2010) Forest Land spanning more than 0.5 hectares with trees higher than 5 meters and a canopy cover of more than 10 percent, or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ. It does not include land that is predominantly under agricultural or urban land use. Explanatory notes 1. Forest is determined both by the presence of trees and the absence of other predominant land uses. The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 meters in situ 2. Includes areas with young trees that h" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_Kotka_III_1996_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO_Kotka_III ;
    dcterms:date "1996"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO Kotka III 1996) Land under natural or planted stands of trees with tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 10 percent and area of more than 0.5 ha. whose primary use is forestry. The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 m at maturity in situ. Includes: closed forest formations where trees of various storeys and undergrowth cover a height portion of the ground and open forest formations with a continuous vegetation layer in with tree crown cover exceeds" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/DOCREP/005/Y4357E/y4357e20.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO) Forest land: land used mainly for wood production and other forest products, protection. http://www.fao.org/DOCREP/005/Y4357E/y4357e20.htm" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_nd_005
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO) Land presently in forest, or showing evidence of having been recently under forest cover - e.g. recently clear-cut or burned and not being used for other purposes - which is expected/intended to revert to forest in the near future, either naturally or by artificial reforestation. This is because of its suitability and desirability, in view of its functions as a sustainable source of timber, as watershed protector or local climate regulator, as a shelter for macro-fauna and as biodiversi" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_2013_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "2013"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/docrep/017/ap862e/ap862e00.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO-2013) Land spanning more than 0.5 hectares with trees higher than 5 meters and a canopy cover of more than 10 percent, or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ. It does not include land that is predominantly under agricultural or urban land use. (Note – there are 9 explanatory notes with the definition. See http://www.fao.org/docrep/017/ap862e/ap862e00.pdf" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_FRA_1958_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO_FRA ;
    dcterms:date "1958"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "Alexander.Korotkov@unece.org" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO-FRA 1958) - All lands bearing vegetative associations dominated by trees of any size, exploited or not, capable of producing wood or other forest products, of exerting an influence on the climate or on the water regime, or providing shelter for livestock and wild life. Includes: (i) Lands from which forests have been clear-cut or burned, but which will be reforested in the foreseeable future; (ii) Public and private forest of any size; (iii) Forest of slow growth and of dwarfed or stunte" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_FRA_1990_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO_FRA ;
    dcterms:date "1990"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "7.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO-FRA 1990) - (Developed Countries) Land with tree crown cover of more than 20 % of the area. Trees should be able to grow to a height of 7 m. Included are: 1. The area with young trees or coppice able to form forest in the future. 2. The area temporarily unstocked due to regeneration or damage. Minimum area outside continuous forest: 0.5 ha. Minimum width outside continuous forest: 15 m. The forest roads and firebreaks etc. narrower than minimum width of nurseries and storage less than 0." .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_FRA_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO_FRA ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO-FRA 2000 and UNSD) Land with tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 10 percent and area of more than 0.5 ha. The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 m at maturity in situ. May consist either of closed forest formations where trees of various storeys and undergrowth cover a high portion of the ground; or of open forest formations with a continuous vegetation cover in which tree cover exceeds 10 percent. Young natural stands and all plantations establi" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_FRA_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO_FRA ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO-FRA 2003) Land under forestry or no land use, spanning more than 0.5 hectares; with trees higher than 5 meters and a canopy cover of more than 10 percent, or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ. NOTE: Forests are determined both by the presence of trees and the absence of other predominant land uses. The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 meters in situ. Areas under reforestation which have yet to reach a crown density of 10 percent or tree height of 5 meters ar" .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_FRA_2010_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO_FRA ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO-FRA 2010 Proposed) Land with tree canopy cover of more than 10 percent and area of more than 0.5 hectares. Trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5m at maturity in situ. Source: Brad Smith, USFS. May 2002." .

:def_Forest_UN_FAO_FRA_draft_Tree_land_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO_FRA_draft_Tree_land ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO-FRA draft Tree land): All land with tree cover of more than 10 % (or equivalent stocking level), or formerly having such tree cover and that is being naturally or artificially regenerated or that is being afforested. Land used for agricultural purposes but with 10 % or more tree cover is included. It includes coniferous and non-coniferous trees, bamboos and palms. Linear formations and planting over about 20 metres wide are also included. (Kotka-II)" .

:def_Forest_UN_FCCC_1990_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FCCC ;
    dcterms:date "1990"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FCCC 1990) Non-Kyoto Forest - Or ‘pre-1990 forest’, refers to forests already in existence on 1 January 1990." .

:def_Forest_UN_FCCC_2001_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FCCC ;
    dcterms:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.unfccc.int/resource/docs/cop6secpart/l11r01.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FCCC 2001) “Forest” is a minimum area of land of 0.05-1.0 hectares with tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 10-30 per cent with trees with the potential to reach a minimum height of 2-5 metres at maturity in situ. A forest may consist either of closed forest formations where trees of various storeys and undergrowth cover a high proportion of the ground or open forest. Young natural stands and all plantations which have yet to reach a crown density of 10-30 per cent o" .

:def_Forest_UN_FCCC_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FCCC ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://epress.anu.edu.au/green_carbon/pdf/imp_carbon_policy.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FCCC) Forests are defined under the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change (UNFCCC) as woody vegetation of at least 2 m in height and 10 per cent canopy cover. http://epress.anu.edu.au/green_carbon/pdf/imp_carbon_policy.pdf" .

:def_Forest_UN_FCCC_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FCCC ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FCCC) Kyoto Forest - A forest planted since 1 January 1990 on land that was previously non-forest." .

:def_Forest_UN_FCCC_IPCC_GPG_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FCCC_IPCC_GPG ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ipcc-nggip.iges.or.jp/public/gpglulucf/gpglulucf_files/Chp2/Chp2_Land_Areas.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FCCC-IPCC-GPG) This category includes all land with woody vegetation consistent with thresholds used to define forest land in the national GHG inventory, sub-divided into managed and unmanaged, and also by ecosystem type as specified in the IPCC Guidelines*. It also includes systems with vegetation that currently fall below, but are expected to exceed, the threshold of the forest land category. http://www.ipcc-nggip.iges.or.jp/public/gpglulucf/gpglulucf_files/Chp2/Chp2_Land_Areas.pdf (See Ma" .

:def_Forest_UN_Millinneium_Ecosystem_Assessment_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :UN_Millinneium_Ecosystem_Assessment ;
    :canopyThreshold "40.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.millenniumassessment.org/en/Products.EHWB.aspx#downloads" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-Millinneium Ecosystem Assessment) A canopy cover of at least 40 percent by woody plants taller than 5 meters. The existence of many other definitions is acknowledged, and other limits (such as crown cover greater than 10 percent, as used by the Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations) will also be reported. Includes temporarily cut-over forests and plantations; excludes orchards and agroforests where the main products are food crops. http://www.millenniumassessment.org/en/Pro" .

:def_Forest_World_Bank_2010_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :World_Bank ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.tradingeconomics.com/greece/forest-area-percent-of-land-area-wb-data.html" ;
    :definitionText "(World Bank 2010), Forest area is land under natural or planted stands of trees of at least 5 meters in situ, whether productive or not, and excludes tree stands in agricultural production systems (for example, in fruit plantations and agroforestry systems) and trees in urban parks and gardens http://www.tradingeconomics.com/greece/forest-area-percent-of-land-area-wb-data.html" .

:def_Forest_AFF_2011_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :AFF ;
    dcterms:date "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.afforum.org/index.php?option=com_docman&task=doc_download&gid=43&Itemid=b" ;
    :definitionText "(AFF 2011) A forest ecosystem is defined as a dynamic complex of plant, animal and microorganism communities and the non-living environment acting as a functional unit within the forest environment. http://www.afforum.org/index.php?option=com_docman&task=doc_download&gid=43&Itemid=b" .

:def_Forest_Africa_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :Africa ;
    :sourceRef "http://lucy.ukc.ac.uk/sonja/rf/ukpr/Report134.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Africa) According to present African legislations, a forest is defined as a non-cultivated natural environment. http://lucy.ukc.ac.uk/sonja/rf/ukpr/Report134.htm" .

:def_Forest_ISO_1998_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :ISO ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://thuvienkhcnvl.dyndns.org/tailieukhcn/data/TieuChuantoanvan/ISO14000/ISO_TR_14061_1998.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(ISO 1998) Forest - generally considered to be a plant community of predominantly trees and other woody vegetation growing together, its land, flora and fauna, their interrelationships, and the resources and values attributed to it. International Organization for Standardization http://thuvienkhcnvl.dyndns.org/tailieukhcn/data/TieuChuantoanvan/ISO14000/ISO_TR_14061_1998.pdf" .

:def_Forest_OAS_1991_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :OAS ;
    dcterms:date "1991"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.oas.org/dsd/publications/unit/oea66e/ch01.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(OAS 1991) forest is an ecosystem that offers goods, including trees that provide lumber, fuel, and fruit. The forest may also provide services in the form of water storage and flood control, wildlife habitat, nutrient storage, and recreation. http://www.oas.org/dsd/publications/unit/oea66e/ch01.htm" .

:def_Forest_Scandinavia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :Scandinavia ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.metla.fi/eu/cost/e4/coste4.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Scandinavia) applied. In Scandinavia, the concept of forest is based on productivity as a result of conventional forest management objectives. The annual growth of timber must be greater than 1m3/ha if an area is to be described as productive forest. For forest land where the mean annual increment of growing stock is typically 0,1-1m3/ha, the term scrubland is used. Forest land where the increment is less than 0.1m3/ha is called wasteland. In layman’s language, the term forest implies productiv" .

:def_Forest_WWF_2007_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :International ;
    :appliesIn :WWF ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.wwf.gr/en/index.php?option=com_content&view=category&layout=blog&id=113&Itemid=131" ;
    :definitionText "(WWF 2007). A forest is a community of trees and bushes, which extend on a large area and maintain a close interrelationship in ways that their canopy, fauna, soil and climatic conditions create a special ecosystem. Forested lands have similar characteristics to forests, but vegetation is more sparse. They are however very important in maintaining biological balance. Most of these areas, if protected from human activity, will often grow into forests. http://www.wwf.gr/en/index.php?option=com_con" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_345
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ghgprotocol.org/sites/default/files/ghgp/standards_supporting/GHG%20Assessment%20Guideline%20Volume%20II%20Aboveground%20Biomass_0.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "According to (GOFC-GOLD, 2009) definitions of forest are myriad, however, common to most definitions are threshold parameters including minimum area, minimum height and minimum level of crown cover. In its forest resource assessment of 2005, the FAO uses a minimum cover of 10%, height of 5m and area of 0.5 ha stating also that forest use should be the predominant use. However, the FAO approach of single worldwide value excludes variability in ecological conditions and differing perception of for" .

:def_Forest_Unknown_nd_346
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :definitionText "Note, many nations may use several definitions of forest land such as one as given in their forestry laws, that which is used for reporting to the FAO for its periodic global forest resource assessment and that which is used for reporting under the Kyoto Protocol under UNFCCC." .

:def_Forest_Armenia_2005_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Armenia ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nature-ic.am/res/pdfs/legislation/general/Forest%20Code%20of%20RA.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Armenia 2005) Forest lands – forested lands and lands allocated or envisaged for flora and fauna protection, nature protection as well as non-forested lands allocated or envisaged for the running of forest economy. Forest Code of the Republic of Armenia. http://www.nature-ic.am/res/pdfs/legislation/general/Forest%20Code%20of%20RA.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Australia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Australia ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fire.uni-Freiburg.de/iffn/iffn_26/IFFN_26.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia) The definition of ‘forest’ used by forestry organisations, for fire-reporting purposes, has been the vegetation of the land under forestry jurisdiction. http://www.fire.uni-Freiburg.de/iffn/iffn_26/IFFN_26.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Bangladesh_1950_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Bangladesh ;
    dcterms:date "1950"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "iucnbd@citechco.net" ;
    :definitionText "(Bangladesh 1950) \"Forest\" includes any land recorded as forest in a record-or-rights prepared under Chapter IX of the Sylhet Tenancy Act, 1936 or under Chapter X of the Bengal Tenancy Act, 1885 or under Chapter IV of the East Bengal Estate Acquisition and Tenancy Act, 1950 or such other land containing tree growth as may by notification be declared as forest by the Provincial Government\"(Page-234). iucnbd@citechco.net" .

:def_Forest_Bangladesh_1959_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Bangladesh ;
    dcterms:date "1959"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ihmsaw.org/resourcefiles/1260066650.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Bangladesh 1959) The Private Forest Ordinance, 1959 defines forest as land recorded as forest under specific laws and such other land containing tree growth as may by notification be declared as forest by the Government. http://www.ihmsaw.org/resourcefiles/1260066650.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Bhutan_1969_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Bhutan ;
    dcterms:date "1969"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/docrep/007/ad103e/AD103E07.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Bhutan 1969) \"forest\" as \"any land under forests in which no person has acquired a permanent, hereditary and transferable right of use and occupancy\" http://www.fao.org/docrep/007/ad103e/AD103E07.htm" .

:def_Forest_Bhutan_1995_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Bhutan ;
    dcterms:date "1995"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nec.gov.bt/clearance/EA%20Guidelines/clearance-guideline_forestry.PDF" ;
    :definitionText "(Bhutan 1995) Any land and water body, whether or not under vegetation cover, in which no person has acquired a permanent and transferable right of use and occupancy, whether such land is located inside or outside the forest boundary pillars, and includes land registered in a person's name as Tsamgrog (grazing land) or Sokshing (woodlot for collection of leaf litter). LEX-FAOC007101. BHUTAN: Forest and Nature Conservation Act of Bhutan, 1995. An Act to provide for the protection and sustainable " .

:def_Forest_Botswana_1968_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Botswana ;
    dcterms:date "1968"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Botswana 1968) Forest reserve -any area hereafter declared as a Forest Reserve by the President in pursuance of the provision of this Act. LEX-FAOC002748. BOTSWANA: Forest Act. An Act to provide for better regulation and protection of forests and forest produce. 1968." .

:def_Forest_Bulgaria_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Bulgaria ;
    :sourceRef "Forest Research Institute <forestin@bulnet.bg>" ;
    :definitionText "(Bulgaria) Forest land - every territory outside the building boundaries of the settlements, determined by general or detailed building projects or by outside limiting polygons, planned mainly for forests and including tree stands, shrubs, lands for afforestation, non-productive lands, indicated in the United Cadastre. Forest Research Institute forestin@bulnet.bg" .

:def_Forest_Bulgaria_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Bulgaria ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Bulgaria) Forest land - Forest territories include all forests, and also rocks, lakes, and pastures situated within forests. http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Cambodia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Cambodia ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.itto.int/direct/topics/topics_pdf_download/topics_id=2648&no=1&disp=inline" ;
    :definitionText "(Cambodia) Conversion forestland’ is defined as “idle land, comprised mainly of secondary vegetation, not yet designated for use by any sector that shall be classified as permanent forest reserves until the Royal Government decide[s] to use and develop the land for another purpose” http://www.itto.int/direct/topics/topics_pdf_download/topics_id=2648&no=1&disp=inline" .

:def_Forest_Celyon_1895_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Celyon ;
    dcterms:date "1895"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://books.google.com/books?id=E1JHAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA369&lpg=PA369&dq=%22forest+means%22&source=bl&ots=Wyb5K9BgeN&sig=UxCBQwHldjZw0oJjFHmGDauElOU&hl=en&ei=1hFXS57SKsSXtgfwmvm9BA&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=r" ;
    :definitionText "(Celyon 1895)Forest means all land at the disposal of the crown. Ceylon. 1895. http://books.google.com/books?id=E1JHAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA369&lpg=PA369&dq=%22forest+means%22&source=bl&ots=Wyb5K9BgeN&sig=UxCBQwHldjZw0oJjFHmGDauElOU&hl=en&ei=1hFXS57SKsSXtgfwmvm9BA&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=18&ved=0CDUQ6AEwETi0AQ#v=onepage&q=%22forest%20means%22&f=false" .

:def_Forest_Central_Africa_Republic_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Central_Africa_Republic ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.riddac.org/document/pdf/rca-loiforets.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Central Africa Republic) Le domaine forestier de l'Etat comprend : - les réserves naturelles intégrales, - les parcs nationaux, - les réserves de faune, - les forêts récréatives, - les périmètres de protection, - les périmètres de reboisement et - les forêts de production. Loi Nº 90.003 Portant Code Forestier Centrafricain http://www.riddac.org/document/pdf/rca-loiforets.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Central_African_Republic_1990_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Central_African_Republic ;
    dcterms:date "1990"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/forestry/FON/FONS/outlook/Africa/ACP/Lamb/Lamb-39.htm#P6708_430877" ;
    :definitionText "(Central African Republic 1990) Selon la Loi 90.003 du 9 Juin 1990 portant Code Forestier Centrafricain, le domaine forestier comprend: le domaine forestier de l'Etat et le domaine forestier des collectivités et des particuliers. Le domaine forestier de l'Etat comprend: les réserves naturelles intégrales; les parcs nationaux; les réserves de faune; les forêts récréatives; les périmètres de reboisement; et les forêts de production. http://www.fao.org/forestry/FON/FONS/outlook/Africa/ACP/Lamb/Lamb" .

:def_Forest_Cyprus_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Cyprus ;
    :definitionText "(Cyprus) State Forest: State land declared as forest according to the Forest Law disregarding whether there is any vegetation on that land or not. A.K. Christou \"Forestry Department - Research and Publicity Sector\"" .

:def_Forest_Czech_Republic_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Czech_Republic ;
    :areaMin "0.01"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Czech Republic) Forest - Forest stand with its environment and land designated for the fulfilment of forest functions. Forest stand means tree and shrub which, in their environment, fulfil forest functions. No area limit, classification into forest and non-forest according to the cadastre; the limit of 0.01 ha applied in the guidelines for forest management planning. http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Denmark_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Denmark ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www2.dmu.dk/1_viden/2_publikationer/3_arbrapporter/rapporter/ar211.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Denmark) the basic definition of a forest is that the forest area must be minimum 0.5 ha. There is no specific guideline on the crown cover or the height of the trees http://www2.dmu.dk/1_viden/2_publikationer/3_arbrapporter/rapporter/ar211.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Dominica_1945_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Dominica ;
    dcterms:date "1945"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Dominica 1945) Forest reserves means any area declared by the Administrator in Council by notice in the Gazette to be a forest reserve. LEX-FAOC002895. DOMINICA: Forest Ordinance (Chapter 80). Date of original text: 31 December 1945. Date of consolidation/reprint: 06 August 1959." .

:def_Forest_Estonia_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Estonia ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "https://www.riigiteataja.ee/en/eli/504092017014/consolide" ;
    :definitionText "(Estonia 2006) ‘Forest land’ means land that meets at least one of the following requirements: [RT I, 06.07.2017, 1 – entry into force 01.09.2017] 1) is entered in the cadastral register as a forest land parcel; [RT I 2008, 56, 314 – entry into force 01.01.2009]  https://www.riigiteataja.ee/en/eli/504092017014/consolide" .

:def_Forest_Ethiopia_2007_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Ethiopia ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.pfmp-farmsos.org/Docs/forest%20proclamation_english.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Ethiopia 2007) \"forest land\" means a land that is demarcated for the purpose of forest development and conservation. http://www.pfmp-farmsos.org/Docs/forest%20proclamation_english.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Fiji_1992_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Fiji ;
    dcterms:date "1992"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Fiji 1992) Forest or nature reserves from the following classes of land: (a) unalienated State land; (b) land leased to the State; and (c) unalienated native land, with the prior consent of the owners of the land and of the Native Land Trust Board. LEX-FAOC002912. FIJI: Forest Decree 1992 (Decree No. 31). Date of text: 12 May 1992." .

:def_Forest_Gabon_2002_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Gabon ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/docrep/005/y2328e/y2328e03.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Gabon 2002) By law: In Gabon, Law n° 1/82 (forest and water guidelines) distinguishes two types of forest: protected forests and classified state forests. Protected forests, belonging to the private domain of the State, may be disposed of and are the preferred area for \"customary rights of usage\" The state forests include permanent production forests, reforestation plots, national parks for forest use, protection forests, recreational forests, botanical gardens, arboretums and sanctuaries for s" .

:def_Forest_Gabon_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Gabon ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/forestry/FON/FONS/outlook/Africa/ACP/Lamb/Lamb-33.htm#P4712_334869" ;
    :definitionText "(Gabon) La Loi No 1/82 (loi dite d'orientation en matière des eaux et forêts) distingue 2 catégories de forêts: les forêts protégées et les forêts domaniales classées. Les forêts protégées font parties du domaine privé de l'état. Elles peuvent être aliénées et sont principalement le lieu d'élection des \"droits d'usage coutumier\". Selon la Loi, les villageois conservent pour leur subsistance, le libre exercice de leurs droits coutumiers sur tout le domaine forestier à condition que ces droits soi" .

:def_Forest_Georgia_1999_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Georgia ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Georgia 1999) State Forest Fund (SFF): The integrity of state forest, land and other resources defined as SFF by the Georgian legislation (Forest Code of Georgia, 1999). Includes the land categories listed below: Forest: Part of geographic landscape, which includes the unity of trees (defined by the Georgian legislation as parts of forests), lands, bushes, grasses, animals and other objects, which are biologically inter-related and have an impact upon each other as well as environment. Forest l" .

:def_Forest_Guyana_1953_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Guyana ;
    dcterms:date "1953"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Guyana 1953) The Minister may, by Order, declare any area of State land to be a State forest, excluding all land owned by any person in such area (sec. 3). LEX-FAOC004339. GUYANA : Forests Act. An Act to consolidate and amend the law relating to forests. Date of original text: 02 May 1953." .

:def_Forest_Haiti_1926_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Haiti ;
    dcterms:date "1926"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Haiti 1926) Cette loi institue la classification comme \" Forêt Nationale Réservée\" de terrains appartenant au domaine national et indique le régime juridique leur afférent. LEX-FAOC002943. HAITI: Loi du 3 février 1926 sur les Forêts Nationales Réservées. Date of text: 03 February 1926" .

:def_Forest_India_1879_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    dcterms:date "1879"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://books.google.com/books?pg=RA6-PA56&lpg=RA6-PA56&dq=%22forest%20means%22&sig=0C-6Qq9owihmR0j54aj8YA7qI30&ei=aQhXS92fHJCXtgfdlpW0BA&ct=result&id=RiETAAAAYAAJ&ots=6GPnEMMlVl&output=text" ;
    :definitionText "(India 1879). \" Reserved Forest\" means waste land which has been declared as* reserved forest at settlement or by any subsequent order of competent authority. * \"'Village Forest\" means such waste land as has been set apart under section 8 or section 9. http://books.google.com/books?pg=RA6-PA56&lpg=RA6-PA56&dq=%22forest%20means%22&sig=0C-6Qq9owihmR0j54aj8YA7qI30&ei=aQhXS92fHJCXtgfdlpW0BA&ct=result&id=RiETAAAAYAAJ&ots=6GPnEMMlVl&output=text ." .

:def_Forest_India_1927_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    dcterms:date "1927"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(India 1927) “forest land” means a piece of land notified by the Government as the forest land to develop, protect and conserve forest and includes a rangeland and wasteland;" .

:def_Forest_India_1927_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    dcterms:date "1927"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.itto.int/direct/topics/topics_pdf_download/topics_id=39100000&no=1&disp=inline" ;
    :definitionText "(India 1927) Forest is defined as a tract of land that is legally proclaimed to be a forest under the forest laws (mainly 1865 and 1927) and is notified as forest in the government gazette. http://www.itto.int/direct/topics/topics_pdf_download/topics_id=39100000&no=1&disp=inline" .

:def_Forest_India_1947_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    dcterms:date "1947"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ielrc.org/content/e4701.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(India 1947) \"forest\" means any land which the State Government may, by notification, declare to be forest for the purposes of this Act and shall be deemed to include any land which is entered as forest or jungle or jungle- Jhori or described by any synonymous term in any record-of-rights finally published under any law for the time being in force unless it is proved that such entry in respect of the land is incorrect ; BIHAR PRIVATE Forest ACT 1947 [Act No IX of 1948] http://www.ielrc.org/conte" .

:def_Forest_India_1980_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    dcterms:date "1980"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "Varma <v.varma@landfood.unimelb.edu.au>" ;
    :definitionText "(India 1980) Any land recorded as forest in any of the land records is legally a forest land. This legal connotation provides a working definition of forest land to the forest managers in India for all the practical purposes. This definition disregards whether there is any vegetation on that land or not. [Source: Forest Conservation Act, 1980, From: \"Vivek K. Varma\" v.varma@landfood.unimelb.edu.au Date: Fri, 17 Jul 1998 02:28:29 -0400 (EDT)]." .

:def_Forest_India_1980_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    dcterms:date "1980"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://forestsclearance.nic.in/writereaddata/FormA/UserAgencydoc/711712712128TYIMCompendium_on_FCA.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(India 1980) ) The term “Forest land’ mentioned in Section 2 of the Act refers to reserved forest, protected forest or any area recorded as forest in the Government records. Lands which are notified under Section 4 of the Indian Forest Act would also come within the purview of the Act. (Supreme Court’s Judgment in NTPC’s case). It would also include “Forest” as understood in the dictionary sense. (Supreme Court order dated: 12.12.1996 in WP No. 202/1995 – Annexure-I)… The term “forest” shall not" .

:def_Forest_India_2005_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.thehindu.com/2009/05/12/stories/2009051252140500.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(India 2005) - ‘forest’ means ‘any land covered with trees and undergrowth and includes all statutorily recognised forests, whether designated as reserve, protected or otherwise, and any land recorded as forests in the government records irrespective of the owners.’ India 2005. http://www.thehindu.com/2009/05/12/stories/2009051252140500.htm" .

:def_Forest_India_2007_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://moef.nic.in/divisions/fp/April_May_meet.doc" ;
    :definitionText "(India 2007 proposed) ‘An area owned by Govt and notified as forest under any act or recorded as a forest in any Govt record functioning as ecological, biological, livelihood-support and/or social resource’ Explanation: such forests will include areas having trees, scrub, grasslands, wetlands, water bodies, deserts, glaciers, geomorphic features or any other area fulfilling the functions of a forest. http://moef.nic.in/divisions/fp/April_May_meet.doc" .

:def_Forest_India_2007_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.mtnforum.org/sites/default/files/pub/4946.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(India 2007 Proposed) MoEF has proposed a definition that says forest is “an area under Government control notified or recorded as forest under any Act, for conservation and management of ecological and biological resources.” http://www.mtnforum.org/sites/default/files/pub/4946.pdf" .

:def_Forest_India_2007_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://moef.nic.in/divisions/fp/April_May_meet.doc" ;
    :definitionText "(India 2007) “An area under Government control notified or recorded as forests under any Act for the conservation and management of ecological and biological resources.” Explanation: Such forests will include areas with trees, scrubland, grasslands, wetlands, water bodies, deserts, glaciers, geomorphic features or any other area that is necessary to maintain ecological security. http://moef.nic.in/divisions/fp/April_May_meet.doc" .

:def_Forest_India_2008_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    dcterms:date "2008"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://mospi.nic.in/mospi_new/upload/nad10_2008_karnataka_final.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(India 2008) In India, forest area is defined by using the legal connotation. An area of land recorded as forest in revenue records or proclaimed to be forest under a forest law or Act is described as forest”. In other words, ‘forest area’ is an area recorded as forest in the government records. This is ifferent from the ‘forest cover’ which is based on the capability of remote sensing satellite sensor and is completely independent of the legality of land use or land ownership. This data is prov" .

:def_Forest_India_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(India 2009) - Notified’ forest is forest for which a state government has issued a notification in the Official Gazette declaring that the land has been constituted as forest." .

:def_Forest_India_2014_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    dcterms:date "2014"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.newindianexpress.com/nation/MoEF-Asks-States-to-Identify-Deemed-Forest-Areas/2014/08/26/article2398873.ece" ;
    :definitionText "(India 2014). Deemed Forests - basically not recorded forest areas as per government records, http://www.newindianexpress.com/nation/MoEF-Asks-States-to-Identify-Deemed-Forest-Areas/2014/08/26/article2398873.ece" .

:def_Forest_India_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.krishiworld.com/html/land_utilisation6.html" ;
    :definitionText "(India) Forests include all lands classed as forest under any legal enactment dealing with forests or administered as forests, whether state owned or private, & whether wooded or maintained as potential forest land. The area of crops raised in the forests & grazing lands or the area open for grazing within the forests should remain included under the forest area. http://www.krishiworld.com/html/land_utilisation6.html" .

:def_Forest_India_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    :sourceRef "Singh <tpsingh@teri.res.in>" ;
    :definitionText "(India) In India, the Recorded Forest Area is defined as \"all lands statutorily notified as forest though they may not necessarily bear tree cover\". T P Singh tpsingh@teri.res.in" .

:def_Forest_Indonesia_1967_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Indonesia ;
    dcterms:date "1967"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.jica.go.jp/project/indonesia/0065045I0/activities/pdf/output1_2_1_fulltext.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Indonesia 1967) Forest under the BFL (Basic Forestry Law) is defined as any kind of land-cover area (with or without tress), which is stated by the government as forest. It may be in the form of forest area or area without trees which the government as forest has designated. http://www.jica.go.jp/project/indonesia/0065045I0/activities/pdf/output1_2_1_fulltext.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Indonesia_1998_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Indonesia ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Indonesia 1998) Hutan ialah suatu lapangan bertumbuhan pohon-pohon yang secara keseluruhan merupakan persekutuan hidup alam hayati beserta alam lingkungannya dan yang ditetapkan oleh Pemerintah sebagai hutan. (Translation: A forest is an area growing trees which as a whole forms a living natural community and natural living environment, which is designated by the government as being forest). Source: Decision of the Minister of Forestry and Plantations on social forest(ry) (Keputusan Menteri Keh" .

:def_Forest_Indonesia_1999_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Indonesia ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://insideindonesia.org/content/view/1245/47/" ;
    :definitionText "(Indonesia 1999) ‘forest area’ means a certain area designated or stipulated by the government to be retained as permanent forest, and ‘state forest’ means a forest located on ‘lands bearing no ownership rights’ (the Indonesian phrase is ‘tanah yang tidak dibebani hak atas tanah’). http://insideindonesia.org/content/view/1245/47/ and Moniaga, Sandra 2009. Fighting over the land and forest. Inside Indonesia. http://www.insideindonesia.org/edition-98/fighting-over-the-land-and-forest" .

:def_Forest_Indonesia_1999_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Indonesia ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.itto.int/direct/topics/topics_pdf_download/topics_id=2648&no=1&disp=inline" ;
    :definitionText "(Indonesia 1999) titled forest is a forest located on land on which the land title is registered. http://www.itto.int/direct/topics/topics_pdf_download/topics_id=2648&no=1&disp=inline" .

:def_Forest_Indonesia_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Indonesia ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fire.uni-freiburg.de/iffn/country/id/id_25.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Indonesia 2000) - Forest area means a certain area which is designated and/or stipulated by government to be retained as permanent forest.\" http://www.fire.uni-freiburg.de/iffn/country/id/id_25.htm" .

:def_Forest_Indonesia_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Indonesia ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "https://www.elaw.org/system/files/REDD_PERMENHUT_P-30-2009_BILINGUAL.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Indonesia 2009). Forest area means a certain area designated and or stipulated by the government to preserve its existence as a permanent forest. https://www.elaw.org/system/files/REDD_PERMENHUT_P-30-2009_BILINGUAL.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Israel_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Israel ;
    :sourceRef "GilS@kkl.org.il" ;
    :definitionText "(Israel) 2. Land which was declared as Forest Land by any legal or official program or 3. Land managed by the Israeli Forest Department. From: GilS@kkl.org.il" .

:def_Forest_Italy_1923_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Italy ;
    dcterms:date "1923"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "Lorenzo Ciccarese <ciccarese@anpa.it>" ;
    :definitionText "(Italy 1923) In Italy, forests are part of the areas submitted to restraints imposed by a 1923 Italian law (R.D.L. 1923). This law obliges local authorities to demarcate all areas (not only wooded) that can not be subjected to land-use change, since they are important for slope stability, for mass and superficial erosion prevention and for regulating water regime. Regio Decreto Legislativo 30 Dicembre 1923, n. 3267. Riordinamento e riforma della legislazione in materia di boschi e terreni montan" .

:def_Forest_Kenya_1964_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Kenya ;
    dcterms:date "1964"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://freeafrica.tripod.com/ogiekland/book/Chapter06.htm#ActForest" ;
    :definitionText "(Kenya 1964) Forest areas means an area of land declared under section 4 to be a forest area. Section 4(1) empowers the Minister from time to time, by notice in the Gazettee:- Declare any unalienated Government land to be a forest area:- Declare the boundaries of a forest and from time to time after those boundaries; Declare that a forest area shall cease to be a forest area;http://freeafrica.tripod.com/ogiekland/book/Chapter06.htm#ActForest" .

:def_Forest_Kenya_2005_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Kenya ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://environment.yale.edu/tfd/uploads/TFD_ILCF_Kenya_BackgroundPaper.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Kenya 2005) Gazetted (state/public) forests are forest reserves managed by the state agency, the Kenya Forest Service (KFS). http://environment.yale.edu/tfd/uploads/TFD_ILCF_Kenya_BackgroundPaper.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Kenya_2005_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Kenya ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://formin.finland.fi/public/download.aspx?ID=15959&GUID=%7B88EFD0B8-9F47-4528-A24F-66DDE0CFE370%7D" ;
    :definitionText "(Kenya 2005) Forest area means any land declared to be a forest land under this act. http://formin.finland.fi/public/download.aspx?ID=15959&GUID=%7B88EFD0B8-9F47-4528-A24F-66DDE0CFE370%7D and http://www.fankenya.org/downloads/ForestsAct2005.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Kenya_2015_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Kenya ;
    dcterms:date "2015"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.kenyaforestservice.org/documents/ForestConservationandManagementActNo34of2016.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Kenya 2015) “Forest\" means land which is declared or registered as a forest. http://www.kenyaforestservice.org/documents/ForestConservationandManagementActNo34of2016.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Kosovo_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Kosovo ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.gazetazyrtare.com/e-gov/index.php?option=com_content&task=view&id=244&Itemid=28&lang=en" ;
    :definitionText "(Kosovo 2003) \"Forest\" is land registered as such in the cadastral records. \"Forestland\" is land that is being managed for the production of wood or other forest products or whose best use, given its natural characteristics and economic conditions, involves the growing of trees. . \"Forestland\" does not include --Orchards; Lands within the inhabited bounds of cities, towns, or villages, including urban parks; Parks or other areas for the protection of natural resources excluded from the jurisdict" .

:def_Forest_Laos_1996_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Laos ;
    dcterms:date "1996"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Laos 1996) - All areas under the management of the Ministry of Agriculture and Forestry whether covered with forest or not, but not used for or defined as permanent agricultural land. www.iges.or.jp/fc/ir98-3-24.PDF" .

:def_Forest_Laos_1996_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Laos ;
    dcterms:date "1996"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Laos 1996) - Land with or without forest on it, which the state has determined as forest land. www.iges.or.jp/fc/ir98-3-24.PDF" .

:def_Forest_Laos_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Laos ;
    :definitionText "(Laos) Living natural resources \"necessary for the preservation of the environment, water sources, soil, wildlife and the livelihood of the pluri-ethnical population\". Forest lands are all areas under the management of the Ministry of Agriculture and Forestry, whether covered or not by forests, if not used or defined as permanent agricultural land. Source: LEX-FAOC004704. LAOS: Decree of the Prime Minister on the Management and Use of Forests and Forest Land (No. 169/PM)" .

:def_Forest_Lativa_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Lativa ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.iufro.org/download/file/5574/4510/61300-jundola01_pdf/" ;
    :definitionText "(Lativa 2000) The definition of the notion “forest land” is given in Paragraph 1 of Article 3 of the Forest Law: as the land carrying forest, the land under forest infrastructure facilities, as well as overflowing clearings, bogs and gaps in the forest and areas contiguous to it. http://www.iufro.org/download/file/5574/4510/61300-jundola01_pdf/" .

:def_Forest_Lesotho_1998_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Lesotho ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Lesotho 1998) - Forest reserve - any area which has been declared as such by the King or (now) the Minister responsible for forestry. Forestry Act 1998. Via David May ISTF CVP Lesotho." .

:def_Forest_Liberia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Liberia ;
    :sourceRef "http://darwin.defra.gov.uk/documents/13008/3153/13-008%20AR1%20Ann%201%20CF_Manual_LFRfinal.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Liberia) “Communal Forest” means an area set aside legally or temporarily by regulation for the sustainable use of non-timber forest products by local communities on a non-commercial basis. http://darwin.defra.gov.uk/documents/13008/3153/13-008%20AR1%20Ann%201%20CF_Manual_LFRfinal.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Liberia_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Liberia ;
    :sourceRef "http://darwin.defra.gov.uk/documents/13008/3153/13-008%20AR1%20Ann%201%20CF_Manual_LFRfinal.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Liberia) Law defines ‘communal forest’ as “A small described forest area immediately adjacent to one or more villages to be used exclusively by the local inhabitants and shall not be used for any commercial purposes.” http://darwin.defra.gov.uk/documents/13008/3153/13-008%20AR1%20Ann%201%20CF_Manual_LFRfinal.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Liberia_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Liberia ;
    :sourceRef "http://darwin.defra.gov.uk/documents/13008/3153/13-008%20AR1%20Ann%201%20CF_Manual_LFRfinal.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Liberia) The Act creating a Protected Forest Area System in Liberia defines communal forests as “areas set aside legally or temporarily by regulation for sustainable use of forest products by local communities on a non-commercial basis” http://darwin.defra.gov.uk/documents/13008/3153/13-008%20AR1%20Ann%201%20CF_Manual_LFRfinal.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Madagascar_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Madagascar ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/forestry/FON/FONS/outlook/Africa/ACP/Lamb/Lamb-37.htm#P5876_393136" ;
    :definitionText "(Madagascar) Les ressources forestières de Madagascar comprennent les forêts et les produits issus de ces forêts. Les forêts sont composées de Réserves Naturelles Intégrales (RNI), de Réserves Spéciales (RS), de Parcs Nationaux (PN), de Stations Forestières (SF), de Forêts Classées (FC), de Réserves Forestières (RF), de Périmètres de Reboisement et de Restauration (PRR) et de Mangroves. Tous produits ligneux ou non-ligneux d'origine végétale fournis par la forêt notamment les bois, le charbon, l" .

:def_Forest_Malaysia_1984_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Malaysia ;
    dcterms:date "1984"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.agc.gov.my/Akta/Vol.%207/Act%20313.pdf0" ;
    :definitionText "(Malaysia 1984)\"open forest\" means any permanent reserved forest or part thereof declared to be an open forest under section 45; \"closed forest\" means any permanent reserved forest or part thereof declared or deemed to be a closed forest under section 45;  http://www.agc.gov.my/Akta/Vol.%207/Act%20313.pdf0" .

:def_Forest_Montserrat_1956_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Montserrat ;
    dcterms:date "1956"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Montserrat 1956) Forest reserves and Protected Forests shall be demarcated in accordance with section 16. LEX-FAOC017877. MONTSERRAT: Forestry Ordinance. Date of original text: 1956.(" .

:def_Forest_Myanmar_1992_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Myanmar ;
    dcterms:date "1992"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.blc-burma.org/html/Myanmar%20Law/lr_e_ml92_08.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Myanmar 1992) Forest Land means land including reserved forest and protected public forest; The Forest Law http://www.blc-burma.org/html/Myanmar%20Law/lr_e_ml92_08.html" .

:def_Forest_Myanmar_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Myanmar ;
    :definitionText "(Myanmar) Land including reserved forest and protected public forest; Reserved Forest means land constituted as a reserved forest under this Law; Protected Public Forest means land declared to be protected public forest under this Law. Source: FOREST LAW State Law and Order" .

:def_Forest_Namibia_2001_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Namibia ;
    dcterms:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "https://laws.parliament.na/cms_documents/forest-f6867dc9d1.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Namibia 2001) “Classified forest” means a forest reserve, a community forest or a forest management area; https://laws.parliament.na/cms_documents/forest-f6867dc9d1.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Nepal_1993_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Nepal ;
    dcterms:date "1993"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "Gautam <khg13@student.canterbury.ac.nz>" ;
    :definitionText "(Nepal 1993) Forest land (national forests)= meant all forests, excluding private forests, within the kingdom of Nepal, whether marked or unmarked with forest boundary markers; the term includes waste or uncultivated lands or unregistered lands surrounded by or adjoining forests, as well as paths, ponds, lakes, rivers, or streams and reverine lands with forests.(Forest Act 1993) Krishna H Gautam <khg13@student.canterbury.ac.nz" .

:def_Forest_Pakistan_1911_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Pakistan ;
    dcterms:date "1911"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Pakistan 1911) Forest land - Any land which has been declared to be forest by notification under a Forest Act. Definition adopted from Glossary of Technical Terms for use in Indian Forestry - compiled by A.M.F. Caccia and revised by R.S. Troup, 1911. Source: Mumtaz Ahmad, Section Forest Officer, Pakistan Min. of Environment, Local Government, and Rural Development." .

:def_Forest_Pakistan_1927_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Pakistan ;
    dcterms:date "1927"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://nwfp.gov.pk/nwfpgov/Gov/Details.php?id=76" ;
    :definitionText "(Pakistan 1927) \"Reserved Forest\" means land which was, demaracted as such at the settlement, or which may be constituted as such under the provision of the Forest Act, 1927. http://nwfp.gov.pk/nwfpgov/Gov/Details.php?id=76" .

:def_Forest_Pakistan_1953_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Pakistan ;
    dcterms:date "1953"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Pakistan 1953) Forest - in a legal sense, an area of land proclaimed to be forest under a Forest Act or Ordinance. Definition adopted from the British Commonwealth Forest Terminology Part-I, 1953. Source: Mumtaz Ahmad, Section Forest Officer, Pakistan Min. of Environment, Local Government, and Rural Development." .

:def_Forest_Pakistan_1959_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Pakistan ;
    dcterms:date "1959"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://bdlaws.gov.bd/print_sections.php?id=289&vol=&sections_id=11690" ;
    :definitionText "(Pakistan 1959) “forest” includes any land recorded as forest in a record-of-rights prepared under Chapter IV of the State Acquisition and Tenancy Act, 1950 (E.B. Act XXVIII of 1951) or such other land containing tree growth as may by notification be declared as forest by the Government;] Pakistan. (East Pakistan Ordinance No.XXXIV OF 1959). http://bdlaws.gov.bd/print_sections.php?id=289&vol=&sections_id=11690" .

:def_Forest_Pakistan_1992_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Pakistan ;
    dcterms:date "1992"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.cda.gov.pk/cda-latest/documents/docs/ICT-Zoning-regulations-1992.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Pakistan 1992) “Forest\" means and includes all protected, reserved and designated forest, grass- land and range land;. http://www.cda.gov.pk/cda-latest/documents/docs/ICT-Zoning-regulations-1992.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Philippines_1975_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Philippines ;
    dcterms:date "1975"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://bim.aseanbiodiversity.org/elib/reference/download.php?refNo=00541&fileId=541" ;
    :definitionText "(Philippines 1975) Forest lands include the public forest, the permanent forest or forest reserves, and forest reservations. a. Public forest is the mass of lands of the public domain which has not been the subject of the present system of classification for the determination of which lands are needed for forest purposes and which are not. b. Permanent forest or forest reserves refers to those lands of the public domain which have been the subject of the present system of classification and decl" .

:def_Forest_Philippines_1975_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Philippines ;
    dcterms:date "1975"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.cifor.org/publications/pdf_files/Books/Bchokkalingam0605-02.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Philippines 1975) The term “forest land” refers to all property owned by the national government that is still in the public domain. It is a legal, not a botanical description. http://www.cifor.org/publications/pdf_files/Books/Bchokkalingam0605-02.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Philippines_1996_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Philippines ;
    dcterms:date "1996"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.napocor.gov.ph/WMD%20WEBPAGE/mandates/memorandum/mo%2096-27.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Philippines 1996) FOREST LAND – refers to the public forest, or permanent forest inside the watershed reservations. http://www.napocor.gov.ph/WMD%20WEBPAGE/mandates/memorandum/mo%2096-27.htm" .

:def_Forest_Philippines_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Philippines ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.apforgen.org/National%20status%20reports.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Philippines 2009) Forest reserves as forest land which has been reserved by the President of the Philippines for any specific purpose or purposes. http://www.apforgen.org/National%20status%20reports.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Poland_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Poland ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Poland) Forest land - Definition of „Forests“ in the Forest Act includes: * Forest Stands * Other areas designated for forest production, nature reserves or part of National Park or listed in the nature conservation register * Forest infrastructure, and installations, including those for tourism. http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Puerto_Rico_1975_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Puerto_Rico ;
    dcterms:date "1975"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Puerto Rico 1975) The Governor may declare public land as Commonwealth Forests under section 3. Such areas shall be of particular interest for forestry use including development and protection of watersheds. These forests shall be controlled by the Secretary of Natural Resources. LEX-FAOC017870. PUERTO RICO: Puerto Rico Forest Act (No. 133 of 1975). Date of text: 01 July 1975" .

:def_Forest_Romania_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Romania ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.metla.fi/eu/cost/e43/minutes/wg1-min-florence.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Romania) Forest - National definition in use: designated areas, no sampling on other areas but for these areas some old data exist http://www.metla.fi/eu/cost/e43/minutes/wg1-min-florence.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Russia_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Russia ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.iufro.org/download/file/5574/4510/61300-jundola01_pdf/" ;
    :definitionText "(Russia 1997) Pursuant to the Russian Forest Code of 1997, the forest estate is defined as including “all forests”, excluding only defence lands, urban settlements and municipal forests, and its boundaries are identified by demarcation (sec. 7). http://www.iufro.org/download/file/5574/4510/61300-jundola01_pdf/" .

:def_Forest_Sierra_Leone_1988_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Sierra_Leone ;
    dcterms:date "1988"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Sierra Leone 1988) Classified Forest – a national production forest, national protection forest or community forest. National production forest means a national forest of which the primary management objective is production of forest produce. National protection forest means a national forest of which the primary management objective is preservation of the forest environment and protection of soil, water, flora and fauna. Community forest means an area of land which is constituted as a communit" .

:def_Forest_Slovakia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Slovakia ;
    :areaMin "0.01"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Slovakia) Forest includes forest stands with its environment and other areas designated for the fulfillment of forest functions. Forest stand means tree and shrub species which, in their environment, fulfill forest functions. No area limit, classification into forest and non-forest according to the cadastre; limit of 0.01 ha in the Guidelines for forest managm. planning. http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Slovenia_1993_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Slovenia ;
    dcterms:date "1993"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.05"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Slovenia 1993) The term “forest” is defined also by the Law on Forests of Slovenia (Official Journal of the Republic of Slovenia, nr. 30/1993). Article two states: .... “A forest is an area of land, covered with forest trees in the form of stands or other forest growths which provide any of the functions of a forest. Forest, according to this law also includes overgrown plots of land which are defined as forest in the spatial part of the forest management plan. The forest infrastructure which i" .

:def_Forest_South_Sudan_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :South_Sudan ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.gurtong.net/Governance/ConstitutionLaws/LawsofSouthSudan/tabid/342/Default.aspx" ;
    :definitionText "(South Sudan 2003) “Forest Reserve” means any area set aside in accordance with the provisions of Section 16 of this Act, for the purpose of Conservation, Protection and management of natural forests, its habitat and Environment and in which tree cutting and certain other activities of forest or its habitat and Environment are prohibited or controlled in accordance with the provisions of Sections 17, and 20 of this Act. Wildlife Conservation Act of 2003. http://www.gurtong.net/Governance/Constit" .

:def_Forest_Sri_Lanka_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Sri_Lanka ;
    :canopyThreshold "75.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/ag/agl/agll/landuse/clsys/Srilanka.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Sri Lanka) Forest - Dense Forest - High growing, natural trees with more than approx. 75 % crown coverage. Open Forest(- Dense natural vegetation cover with between 45 and 75 % Forest Plantations - Man-made, mostly monocultural forests of teak, eucalyptus, pines and other species http://www.fao.org/ag/agl/agll/landuse/clsys/Srilanka.htm" .

:def_Forest_St_Lucia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :St_Lucia ;
    :sourceRef "chiefforest@maffe.org" ;
    :definitionText "(St. Lucia) An area of land, with or without trees, declared to be a forest reserve, protected forest, or prohibited area (Source: Michael Andrew, chiefforest@maffe.org)" .

:def_Forest_Sudan_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Sudan ;
    :definitionText "(Sudan) Government forest reserves managed by the forest department. It can be bare land intended to be planted with trees or shrubs in the future (K. H. Badi, Forest Deptartment, Sudan A. M.S. Bayoumi, Forest Department, Sudan)" .

:def_Forest_Switzerland_1992_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Switzerland ;
    dcterms:date "1992"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.burmalibrary.org/docs11/Forest-Law-1992.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Switzerland 1992) Forest Land means land including reserved forest and protected public forest. The Forest Law; http://www.burmalibrary.org/docs11/Forest-Law-1992.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Taiwan_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Taiwan ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://law.moj.gov.tw/PDAENG/NewsContent.aspx?msgid=2429" ;
    :definitionText "(Taiwan 2006) Forestland as used in Paragraph 1, Article 3 of this Act is defined as follows: 1. A land designated for forestry purpose under Article 3 of the Non-Urban Land Use and Control Rules and land subject to forestland control under Article 7 of the same Rules; 2. A land in a non-urban land area not subject to zoning, and land in an urban planning preservation, scenery and agricultural areas determined as forestland by the competent authorities of a province-level municipality or county/" .

:def_Forest_Taiwan_2008_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Taiwan ;
    dcterms:date "2008"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://chiayi.forest.gov.tw/ct.asp?xItem=34177&CtNode=3036&mp=341" ;
    :definitionText "(Taiwan 2008). state forest means a forest belonging to the nation and in the territory of the nation, but without an owner. 2. A public forest means a forest held by a direct municipality, county (city), town, village or legal public entity. 3. A private forest means the ownership of a forest acquired by a private citizen or private legal entity. Chiayi Forest District Office. 2008. http://chiayi.forest.gov.tw/ct.asp?xItem=34177&CtNode=3036&mp=341" .

:def_Forest_Tajikistan_1993_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Tajikistan ;
    dcterms:date "1993"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Tajikistan 1993) The composition of lands of the state forest reserve the following lands are allocated:" .

:def_Forest_Thailand_1941_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Thailand ;
    dcterms:date "1941"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.forest.go.th/act/forest/fr3_e.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Thailand 1941) forest\" means land which has not been taken up or acquired by any other means under the Land Law; http://www.forest.go.th/act/forest/fr3_e.htm" .

:def_Forest_Thailand_1941_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Thailand ;
    dcterms:date "1941"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://enviroscope.iges.or.jp/modules/envirolib/upload/1504/attach/ir98-3-12.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Thailand 1941) Forestry Act (1941): “Forest is a land without occupants in accordance with the land law” (Praraachabanyat Paamai Po. So. 2484, Matraa 4 (1) [Forestry Act of 1941, Article 4, Section 1]. http://enviroscope.iges.or.jp/modules/envirolib/upload/1504/attach/ir98-3-12.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Thailand_1941_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Thailand ;
    dcterms:date "1941"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "Songkram Thammincha <fforskt@ku.ac.th>" ;
    :definitionText "(Thailand 1941) Land not entitled under any Land Acts. Forest Law of 1941. Songkram Thammincha fforskt@ku.ac.th" .

:def_Forest_Thailand_1941_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Thailand ;
    dcterms:date "1941"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www9.ocn.ne.jp/~aslan/pgazpape.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Thailand 1941) The Forest Act B.E. 2484 (1941) defines \"forest\" as any land which is not yet occupied by anyone according to the law. Since agricultural land and land upon which houses and other buildings are standing has presumably become private property, almost all other land except wasteland will be forest. http://www9.ocn.ne.jp/~aslan/pgazpape.pdf , http://eprints.lse.ac.uk/4743/1/The_Political_Ecology_of_the_Ecosystem_Approach_for_Forests(LSERO).pdf and http://personal.lse.ac.uk/FORSYTHT/" .

:def_Forest_Thailand_1967_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Thailand ;
    dcterms:date "1967"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "Songkram Thammincha <fforskt@ku.ac.th>" ;
    :definitionText "(Thailand 1967) Land including mountain, stream, swamp, canal, river, lake, island, coastal areas not entitled under any Land Acts. Forest Reserve Act of 1967. Songkram Thammincha fforskt@ku.ac.th" .

:def_Forest_Thailand_1996_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Thailand ;
    dcterms:date "1996"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.farmersrights.org/pdf/asia/Thailand/Thailand-commforestdraft96.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Thailand 1996) A community forest can be any area the community wants to be designated a community forest whether it is within the limits of a conservation zone such as a national park, wildlife sanctuary, watershed area; or non-conservation zone such as a national forest or public use area. Thailand's Community Forest Act Draft http://www.farmersrights.org/pdf/asia/Thailand/Thailand-commforestdraft96.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Tonga_1961_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Tonga ;
    dcterms:date "1961"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "Via James Barton <jpbarton@xtra.co.nz>" ;
    :definitionText "(Tonga 1961) - \"Forest reserve\" means any demarcated forest or proclaimed forest reserve but shall not include a village forest reserve… \"Reserved area \" means any demarcated area of land or proclaimed area of land which may be under grass or scrub but which may be needed for afforestation in the future… The King in Council may declare any unalienated land to be a forest reserve or reserved area Forests Act 1961 (Chapter 126 of the 1988 Revised Edition of the Laws of Tonga). Via James Barton jpb" .

:def_Forest_Trinidad_and_Tobago_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Trinidad_and_Tobago ;
    :definitionText "(Trinidad and Tobago) Forest Reserve - means and includes a forest and every part of a forest declared to be a Forest Reserve under the Land Regulations for the time being in force – Forest Act: Chapter 66:01. Narine Lackhan, Director of Forestry." .

:def_Forest_Uganda_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Uganda ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.sawlog.ug/downloads/The%20Uganda%20Forestry%20policy.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Uganda ) Forests include all alpine, tropical high and medium altitude forests, woodlands, wetland and riparian forests, plantations and trees, whether on land held in trust by government (gazetted Forest Reserves, National Parks and Wildlife Reserves) or nongazetted land (mailo, leasehold, freehold or customary lands). The Uganda Forestry Policy. http://www.sawlog.ug/downloads/The%20Uganda%20Forestry%20policy.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Uganda_1947_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Uganda ;
    dcterms:date "1947"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Uganda 1947) forest reserve - An area declared to be a central forest reserve or a local forest reserve under the provision of section 4 of the FORESTS ACT, 1947. An Act To Consolidate the Law Relating to Forests and Forest Reserves." .

:def_Forest_Ukraine_2010_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Ukraine ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.envsec.org/publications/fact_finding_study_illegal_logging_eng_feb_11.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Ukraine 2010) Forest Code of Ukraine: • According to Article 8, state forests include all forests with the exception of municipal and private forests. http://www.envsec.org/publications/fact_finding_study_illegal_logging_eng_feb_11.pdf" .

:def_Forest_United_Kingdom_1598_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :United_Kingdom ;
    dcterms:date "1598"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "Kenneth Rosenbaum <kenro@igc.apc.org>" ;
    :definitionText "(United Kingdom 1598) A certen Territorie of wooddy grounds & fruitfull pastures, priviledged for wild beasts and foules of, Forrest, Chase, and Warren, to rest and abide in, in the safe protection of the King, for his princely delight and pleasure, ...\" (Kenneth Rosenbaum <kenro@igc.apc.org from Manwood (1598)." .

:def_Forest_United_Kingdom_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :United_Kingdom ;
    :sourceRef "http://machaut.uchicago.edu/cgi-bin/WEBSTER.sh?WORD=forest" ;
    :definitionText "(United Kingdom) (Eng. Law) Large extent or precinct of country, generally waste and woody, belonging to the sovereign, set apart for the keeping of game for his use, not inclosed, but distinguished by certain limits, and protected by certain laws, courts, and officers of its own. Burrill. http://machaut.uchicago.edu/cgi-bin/WEBSTER.sh?WORD=forest and http://www.graylab.ac.uk/cgi-bin/omd?forest" .

:def_Forest_United_Kingdom_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :United_Kingdom ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dictionary.com/cgi-bin/dict.pl?term=forest" ;
    :definitionText "(United Kingdom) A defined area of land formerly set aside in England as a royal hunting ground. http://www.dictionary.com/cgi-bin/dict.pl?term=forest" .

:def_Forest_United_Kingdom_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :United_Kingdom ;
    :definitionText "(United Kingdom) By the English law, a forest is a circuit of ground properly under the king's protection, for the peaceable living and abiding of beasts of hunting and the chase, and distinguished not only by having bounds and privileges, but also by having courts and offices. 12 do." .

:def_Forest_United_Kingdom_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :United_Kingdom ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.planning.detr.gov.uk/luc15/annex_b.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(United Kingdom) Forest/woodland - Areas marked with woodland annotations on the OS map including woodland on farm holdings and woodland used for recreation. http://www.planning.detr.gov.uk/luc15/annex_b.htm" .

:def_Forest_United_Kingdom_nd_005
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :United_Kingdom ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.christiantech.com/cgi-bin/webster.exe?search_for_cgi-bin_texts_web1828=forest" ;
    :definitionText "(United Kingdom) In law, in Great Britain, a certain territory of woody grounds and pastures, privileged for wild beasts and fowls of forest, chase and warren, to rest and abide in, under the protection of the king, for his pleasure. In this sense, the word has no application in America. http://www.christiantech.com/cgi-bin/webster.exe?search_for_cgi-bin_texts_web1828=forest" .

:def_Forest_USA_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA ;
    :sourceRef "https://definitions.uslegal.com/n/national-forest-lands/" ;
    :definitionText "(USA) Pursuant to 16 USCS § 460hhh (1), [Title 16. Conservation; Chapter 1. National Parks, Military Parks, Monuments, and Seashores; Spring Mountains National Recreation Area] the term National Forest lands means “lands included in the National Forest System (as defined in section 11(a) of the Forest and Rangeland Renewable Resources Planning Act. https://definitions.uslegal.com/n/national-forest-lands/" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_FS_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_FS ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fs.fed.us/database/lar/lardefn.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-FS) (National Forest) - A unit formally established and permanently set aside and reserved for National Forest purposes. http://www.fs.fed.us/database/lar/lardefn.htm and http://www.fs.fed.us/land/staff/lar/definitions_of_terms.htm" .

:def_Forest_Uzbekistan_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Uzbekistan ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.iufro.org/download/file/7408/5123/Uzekistan_pdf/" ;
    :definitionText "(Uzbekistan) The area of the State Forest Fund is termed forest land and includes land for afforestation, and non-forest land, where afforestation requires additional reclamational activities for site preparation. • Forest lands include such categories of lands as forest covered area, non-closed-up artificial (young) plantings, sparse crops, sparse forests, fire-sites, perished stands, cut sites, and glade abandoned sites. • Non-forest lands include arable land, hayfields, pastures, marshes, san" .

:def_Forest_Western_Samoa_1967_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Western_Samoa ;
    dcterms:date "1967"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.thecommonwealth.org/Shared_ASP_Files/UploadedFiles/42862479-BC6A-481C-ADEB-50432C31A072_ForestsAct1967.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Western Samoa 1967) \"Forest land\" means, - (a) State forest land; or (b) Public or customary land which is subject to a licence or lease to the Minister or any other person for any purpose of forestry; or (c) Freehold land which is subject to a licence or lease to the Minister or any other person for any purpose of forestry, or in respect of which the Minister is a trustee under Part IX of this Act: Forests Act 1967 Laws of Western Samoa. http://www.thecommonwealth.org/Shared_ASP_Files/Uploaded" .

:def_Forest_Zambia_1973_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Zambia ;
    dcterms:date "1973"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Zambia 1973) Local Forest – any area declared to be a Local Forest under section seventeen. LEX-FAOC003914. ZAMBIA: Forests Act 1973 (Act No. 39). An Act to repeal and replace the Forest Act and to provide for the establishment and management of national forests and local forests, the conservation and protection of forests and trees, the licensing and sale of forest produce and other matters." .

:def_Forest_Afghanistan_1999_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Afghanistan ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Afghanistan 1999) Open Forest (Between 20-60% Canopy Cover) - Mainly needleleaved, evergreen, open cover of trees, with less than 60% cover, occurring mainly in mountainous areas.; Closed Forest (More Than 60% Canopy Cover) - Mainly needleleaved, evergreen, closed cover of trees, with more than 60% cover, occurring mainly in mountainous areas. Source: FAO. 1999. Provincial Land Cover Atlas of Islamic State of Afghanistan. AFG/90/002 Utilization of Remote Sensing for the Inventory and Monitoring" .

:def_Forest_Albania_2004_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Albania ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Albania 2004) Forest is defined as an area covered at least 30% by dense trees on more than one tenth of a hectare [Law no. 9385 “On Forests and Forest Service]" .

:def_Forest_Albania_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Albania ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Albania 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.1 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 30 Min. Tree Height (m) = 3 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/bak/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Albania_2007_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Albania ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.environmental-auditing.org/LinkClick.aspx?fileticket=fbx%2FbAIVeFU%3D&tabid=128&mid=568" ;
    :definitionText "(Albania 2007 UNFCCC ) An area with 30% minimum tree crown cover, minimum 0.1 ha land area value, and 3m of tree potential height. (Fida, 2007) http://www.environmental-auditing.org/LinkClick.aspx?fileticket=fbx%2FbAIVeFU%3D&tabid=128&mid=568" .

:def_Forest_Albania_2008_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Albania ;
    dcterms:date "2008"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.profor.info/profor/sites/profor.info/files/Annex%208%20-%20SQA%20Albania_E.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Albania 2008). 2 Forest is defined as an area covered at least 30% by dense trees on more than one tenth of a hectare [Law no. 9385 “On Forests and Forest Service]. 3 Open forest or forest land is defined as an area covered by 5-30% by forest vegetation, unregistered in another land use cadastre. [Law no. 9385 “On Forests and Forest Service]. 4. Forest is defined as dense woodland with a density of trees and shrubs not less than 30%. 5. Forest land is defined an area with a density of trees and" .

:def_Forest_Albania_2011_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Albania ;
    dcterms:date "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Albania 2011) A forest is defined as land with tree crown cover of more than 10%, an area of more than 0.5 ha and an average width of more than 20 m. Trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 m at maturity in situ.FOREST EUROPE, UNECE AND FAO, 2011. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Albania_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Albania ;
    :areaMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://faolex.fao.org/faolex1/" ;
    :definitionText "(Albania) ‘Forest’ is defined as dense woodland with a surface larger than 1000 m2 with a density of forest trees and shrubs not less than 30 %, which produces wood material and has influence on the surrounding environment. ‘Land with forest vegetation’ is defined as forest wood area with a density of forest trees and shrubs from 5 to 30 % which are not registered in the cadastra as other land estates. Forest estate includes also open areas up to 2 ha. such as openings, rocks and sandbank which " .

:def_Forest_Albania_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Albania ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Albania) Forest - Lands with tree crown cover of more than 30% and area of more than 0.1 ha. The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 m in situ... Includes high forest, coppice and shrubs. http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Albania_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Albania ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Albania) Forest land - Besides the forests according to the FAO definition, also areas where trees should not be able to reach a minimum height of 5 m at maturity and bare/rocky terrain, eroded and abandoned/refused lands are classified as the forest land. http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" .

:def_Forest_American_Samoa_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :American_Samoa ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/forestry/fo/country/index.jsp?lang_id=1&geo_id=109" ;
    :definitionText "(American Samoa) Includes: upland forests, coastal forests, mangrove forests, dwarf forests, moss forests, secondary vegetations and agroforest areas (including ones with coconuts and bananas). http://www.fao.org/forestry/fo/country/index.jsp?lang_id=1&geo_id=109" .

:def_Forest_Argentina_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Argentina ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fs.fed.us/research/sustain/2003SustainabilityReport/documents/SustainableForests.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Argentina 2003) Minimum area = 0.5 ha, minimum tree crown cover = 10%, minimum tree height = 5 m. http://www.fs.fed.us/research/sustain/2003SustainabilityReport/documents/SustainableForests.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Argentina_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Argentina ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "22.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/bak/allCountriesARInfos.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Argentina 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 1 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 22.5 Min. Tree Height (m) = 3 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/bak/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Argentina_2007_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Argentina ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "7.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.greenspace.it/index.php?option=com_docman&task=doc_download&gid=16&Itemid=336&lang=it" ;
    :definitionText "(Argentina 2007) Forest Land Land with tree crown cover of more than 20 percent. The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 7 meters at maturity in situ. It may consist of closed forest formation where trees of various storey and undergrowth cover a high proportion of the ground. http://www.greenspace.it/index.php?option=com_docman&task=doc_download&gid=16&Itemid=336&lang=it" .

:def_Forest_Argentina_2007_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Argentina ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "https://www.researchgate.net/post/Which_conditions_are_used_to_define_an_ecosystem_as_a_woodland?ch=reg&cp=re221_b1m_p32&pli=1&loginT=TIy9Igbuj555qN69cnuPm4x7mnABAv97" ;
    :definitionText "(Argentina 2007) The National Law 26.331 defines a woodland as a \"natural forestry ecosystem integrated by mature native trees, with different species of plants and animals, associated to the topsoil, subsoil, atmosphere, climate and hydric resources, [...] under a condition of dynamic equilibrium...\". Its regulation also defines as prime conditions that the woodlands should have trees of at least 3 m high and should occupy a surface superior to 10 has. https://www.researchgate.net/post/Which_co" .

:def_Forest_Argentina_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Argentina ;
    :sourceRef "Mirta Rosa Larrieu <milarr@sagyp.mecon.ar>" ;
    :definitionText "(Argentina) Forest Land: Native forest or plantation. \"Mirta Rosa Larrieu\" milarr@sagyp.mecon.ar" .

:def_Forest_Argentina_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Argentina ;
    :sourceRef "Mirta Rosa Larrieu <milarr@sagyp.mecon.ar>" ;
    :definitionText "(Argentina) Forest: Plantation of trees. - Bosque nativo: Native forest, Natural forest; Bosque cultivado: Plantation. (\"Mirta Rosa Larrieu\" milarr@sagyp.mecon.ar .)" .

:def_Forest_Armenia_1994_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Armenia ;
    dcterms:date "1994"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "Nature Protection <FREC@FREENET.AM>" ;
    :definitionText "(Armenia 1994) The forest is one of the elements of the geographical landscape, and an entire whole of interconnected and interrelated trees, other plant species, soil, animals, microorganisms, and the components of the environment. Source: FOREST CODE OF ARMENIA (1994). Preamble. Karen Ter-Ghazaryan, Ministry of Nature Protection FREC@FREENET.AM" .

:def_Forest_Aruba_1998_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Aruba ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Aruba 1998) Forest: (thorny) woodlands, protected areas including mangrove areas, urban parks and trees for agricultural and commercial purposes are considered to fit the definition of forest as well. Even single trees are included in the definition if they form important esthetical elements in town or in the landscape. FAO Forestry paper 137/2, FORESTRY POLICIES IN THE CARIBEAN, volume 2: Reports of 28 selected countries and territories, FAO 1998. Facundo Franken, Department of Agriculture, An" .

:def_Forest_Australia_1970_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Australia ;
    dcterms:date "1970"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.myenvironment.net.au/index.php/me/content/download/5678/33263/file/Uniting%20Church%20report.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia 1970) An area dominated by trees greater than 5m in height with canopy cover of 30% or greater (Specht 1970). http://www.myenvironment.net.au/index.php/me/content/download/5678/33263/file/Uniting%20Church%20report.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Australia_1992_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Australia ;
    dcterms:date "1992"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.myenvironment.net.au/index.php/me/content/download/5678/33263/file/Uniting%20Church%20report.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia 1992) An area dominated by trees greater than 5m in height with canopy cover of 30% or greater, …including plantations (NFPS 1992). http://www.myenvironment.net.au/index.php/me/content/download/5678/33263/file/Uniting%20Church%20report.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Australia_1992_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Australia ;
    dcterms:date "1992"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.brs.gov.au/nfi/forestinfo/summary.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia 1992) An area, incorporating all living and non-living components, that is dominated by trees having usually a single stem and a mature or potentially mature stand height exceeding 2 metres, and with existing or potential projected crown cover of overstorey strata about equal to or greater than 20 percent. This definition includes both native and plantation regardless of age. (From: \"Ross Penny\"Ross.Penny@nre.vic.gov.au the definition of forest used by the National Forest Inventory (a" .

:def_Forest_Australia_1996_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Australia ;
    dcterms:date "1996"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.oecd.org/officialdocuments/publicdisplaydocumentpdf/?cote=OCDE/GD(96" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia 1996) Forest is defined as areas dominated by trees having usually a single stem and a mature or potentially mature stand height exceeding 5 metres, and with existing or potential projective cover of overstorey strata about equal to or greater than 30 per cent; while woodland is similarly defined but with a projective cover of overstorey strata of less than 30 per cent. http://www.oecd.org/officialdocuments/publicdisplaydocumentpdf/?cote=OCDE/GD(96)5&docLanguage=En" .

:def_Forest_Australia_1998_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Australia ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://adl.brs.gov.au/data/warehouse/pe_brs90000003841/sofr2008Full_11a.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia 1998) Forest - A land area, incorporating all living and non-living components, dominated by trees usually having a single stem and a mature or potentially mature stand height exceeding 2 metres, and with existing or potential crown cover of overstorey strata about equal to or greater than 20%. This definition includes native forests and plantations and areas of trees that are sometimes described as woodlands. http://adl.brs.gov.au/data/warehouse/pe_brs90000003841/sofr2008Full_11a.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Australia_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Australia ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fs.fed.us/research/sustain/2003SustainabilityReport/documents/SustainableForests.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia 2003) Minimum area = 0.5 ha, minimum tree crown cover = 20%, miniumum tree height – 2 m. http://www.fs.fed.us/research/sustain/2003SustainabilityReport/documents/SustainableForests.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Australia_2003_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Australia ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "50.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.myenvironment.net.au/index.php/me/content/download/5678/33263/file/Uniting%20Church%20report.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia 2003) Sclerophyll forest with canopy cover greater than 50% including all rainforest. Excludes mangroves and woodland mallee (TWS 2003a). http://www.myenvironment.net.au/index.php/me/content/download/5678/33263/file/Uniting%20Church%20report.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Australia_2003_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Australia ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.myenvironment.net.au/index.php/me/content/download/5678/33263/file/Uniting%20Church%20report.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia 2003). An area dominated by trees having usually a single stem, greater than 2m in height with canopy cover of 20% or greater… including plantations. (NFI 2003) Current definition. http://www.myenvironment.net.au/index.php/me/content/download/5678/33263/file/Uniting%20Church%20report.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Australia_2004_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Australia ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://adl.brs.gov.au/data/warehouse/brsShop/data/callitris.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia 2004) An area dominated by trees having usually a single stem and a mature or potentially mature stand height exceeding two meters, and with existing or potential projected cover of overstorey strata about equal to or greater than 20 percent. http://adl.brs.gov.au/data/warehouse/brsShop/data/callitris.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Australia_2005_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Australia ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://wwwdocs.fce.unsw.edu.au/fce/Research/ResearchMicrosites/CAER/WorkingPaperSeries/WPS0705.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia 2005) forest area (defined as land with actual or potential tree cover greater than 20% canopy cover and 2 m in height. http://wwwdocs.fce.unsw.edu.au/fce/Research/ResearchMicrosites/CAER/WorkingPaperSeries/WPS0705.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Australia_2008_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
