    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.2"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/kyoto_target_web.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia 2008 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.2 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 20 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/kyoto_target_web.pdf (2008)" .

:def_Forest_Australia_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Australia ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.daff.gov.au/rfa/glossary" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia 2009) Forest - A vegetation type dominated by woody vegetation having a mature or potential mature stand height exceeding 5 metres, with an overstorey canopy cover greater than 20%. http://www.daff.gov.au/rfa/glossary" .

:def_Forest_Australia_2009_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Australia ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://greensmps.org.au/webfm_send/266" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia 2009). Forest means a vegetation community dominated by trees with a projective foliage cover greater than 20%. http://greensmps.org.au/webfm_send/266" .

:def_Forest_Australia_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Australia ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.climatechange.gov.au/government/initiatives/unfccc/submissions/~/media/submissions/international/forest-management-unfccc-submission-feb11.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia KPl) A forest is defined as vegetation that has a height of 2 metres, crown canopy cover of 20% and a minimum forest area of 0.2. ha. http://www.climatechange.gov.au/government/initiatives/unfccc/submissions/~/media/submissions/international/forest-management-unfccc-submission-feb11.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Australia_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Australia ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.rfa.gov.au/documents/janis/janis011.html#E9E11" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia Old) A vegetation type dominated by woody vegetation having a mature or potential mature stand height exceeding 5 metres, with an overstorey canopy cover greater than 20%. http://www.rfa.gov.au/documents/janis/janis011.html#E9E11" .

:def_Forest_Australia_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Australia ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.rfa.gov.au/dfa/other_info/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia- Old) An area incorporating all living and non-living components that is dominated by trees usually with a single stem and a mature or potentially mature stand height exceeding five metres. The existing or projected foliage cover of overstorey strata should be equal to or greater than 30 per cent. http://www.rfa.gov.au/dfa/other_info/glossary.html and http://www.rfa.gov.au/rfa/national/dfa/other/glossary.html" .

:def_Forest_Australia_nd_005
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Australia ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.rfa.gov.au/rfa/vic/east/raa/esfm/gloss1.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia) - An area, incorporating all living and nonliving components, that is dominated by trees having usually a single stem and a mature or potentially mature stand height exceeding 5 metres, and with existing or potential projective cover of overstorey strata about equal to or greater than 30 per cent. This definition includes Australia's diverse native forests and plantations, regardless of age. It is also sufficiently broad to encompass areas of trees that are sometimes described as woo" .

:def_Forest_Australia1999_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Australia1999 ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nfn.org.au/kyoto/gp9.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia1999) An ecosystem characterised by a more or less dense and extensive tree cover. It means natural forest and does not include plantations or agroforests (National Forest Summit, Australia 1999). http://www.nfn.org.au/kyoto/gp9.html" .

:def_Forest_Austria_1996_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Austria ;
    dcterms:date "1996"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://books.google.com/books?id=zeTU8QauENcC&pg=PA192&lpg=PA192&dq=Germany+Forest+definition+define+%22forest+is%22+law+act+code&source=bl&ots=1jUsKaLHy4&sig=uRBHD83hyloLheFqPmfiDgK687o&hl=en&sa=X&ei" ;
    :definitionText "(Austria 1996) Forests are areas of min. 1000 m2 and cover percentage 30% with tree species. http://books.google.com/books?id=zeTU8QauENcC&pg=PA192&lpg=PA192&dq=Germany+Forest+definition+define+%22forest+is%22+law+act+code&source=bl&ots=1jUsKaLHy4&sig=uRBHD83hyloLheFqPmfiDgK687o&hl=en&sa=X&ei=OcY-T7PEOcX10gHzx8jzBw&ved=0CDgQ6AEwAw#v=onepage&q=Germany%20Forest%20definition%20define%20%22forest%20is%22%20law%20act%20code&f=false" .

:def_Forest_Austria_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Austria ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.metla.fi/eu/cost/e43/minutes/wg1-min-florence.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Austria 1997) All areas of the country covered by woody plants specified in the appendix of forest law 1975 are forest are if minimum area of 500 m2, width = 10 m of are covered by woody plants and minimum crown coverage of 30 % (ocular estimation) (European Communities 1997a - p 43). and http://www.metla.fi/eu/cost/e43/minutes/wg1-min-florence.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Austria_2001_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
