    :appliesIn :Cambodia ;
    :sourceRef "http://ekh.unep.org/files/SEF%20II%20Report%20-%20Cambodia.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Cambodia) Forest: is a combination of evergreen forest, semi-evergreen forest, deciduous forest, re-growth of secondary forest, forest plantation and bamboo. http://ekh.unep.org/files/SEF%20II%20Report%20-%20Cambodia.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Cameroon_1994_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Cameroon ;
    dcterms:date "1994"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.communitycarbonforestry.org/NewPublications/ESP%20article%20CAMERON.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Cameroon 1994) CDM Executive Board. Section 2 of the 1994 forestry law (No. 94-1 of 20 January 1994) defines a forest as, ‘‘any land covered by vegetation with a predominance of trees, shrubs and other species capable of providing products other than agricultural produce’’. http://www.communitycarbonforestry.org/NewPublications/ESP%20article%20CAMERON.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Cameroon_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Cameroon ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://ftp.geog.ucl.ac.be/TDARprojets/SSTCt310006/telsat/raster-t.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Cameroon) (Dense Forest) - Evergreen or moist deciduous forest zones, dominated by trees of at least 5 m high and with a forest-cover proportion of 30% or more. http://ftp.geog.ucl.ac.be/TDARprojets/SSTCt310006/telsat/raster-t.html" .

:def_Forest_Cameroon_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Cameroon ;
    :sourceRef "http://www2.worldbank.org/hm/hmlandpolicy/0248.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Cameroon) Forest means any land covered by vegetation, with predominance of trees, shrubs and other species capable of providing products other than agricultural products. http://www2.worldbank.org/hm/hmlandpolicy/0248.html" .

:def_Forest_Canada_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Canada ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fs.fed.us/research/sustain/2003SustainabilityReport/documents/SustainableForests.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada 2003) Minimum area = 0.5 ha, minimum tree crown cover = 20%, minimum tree height = 5 m. http://www.fs.fed.us/research/sustain/2003SustainabilityReport/documents/SustainableForests.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Canada_2007_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Canada ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "25.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/initial_report_of_canada.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada 2007 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 1 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 25 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/initial_report_of_canada.pdf (2007)" .

:def_Forest_Canada_2011_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Canada ;
    dcterms:date "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://nfdp.ccfm.org/glossary_e.php" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada 2011) Forest land—Areas of land where tree canopies cover more than 10 percent of the total area and the trees, when mature, can grow to a height of more than 5 metres. Does not include land that is predominantly urban or used for agricultural purposes. http://nfdp.ccfm.org/glossary_e.php." .

:def_Forest_Canada_2011_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Canada ;
    dcterms:date "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://nfdp.ccfm.org/terms/terms_e.php?letter=f" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada 2011) Generally, an ecosystem characterized by a more or less dense and extensive tree cover. More particularly, a plant community predominantly of trees and other woody vegetation, growing more or less closely together. http://nfdp.ccfm.org/terms/terms_e.php?letter=f" .

:def_Forest_Canada_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Canada ;
    :canopyThreshold "25.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://carbon.cfs.nrcan.gc.ca/definitions_e.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada) Forest - A vegetation type dominated by trees. Many definitions of the term forest are used throughout the world. For reporting on managed forest carbon stock changes, Canada uses the definitions of 1 ha minimum area, 25% canopy cover of trees that have the potential to reach 5 m height at maturity. http://carbon.cfs.nrcan.gc.ca/definitions_e.html" .

:def_Forest_Canada_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Canada ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.pfc.cfs.nrcan.gc.ca/landscape/inventory/terms/haddon/glossary.html#F" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada) forest: [forêt] A plant community predominantly of trees and other woody vegetation, growing more or less closely together. http://www.pfc.cfs.nrcan.gc.ca/landscape/inventory/terms/haddon/glossary.html#F" .

:def_Forest_Cape_Verde_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Cape_Verde ;
    :definitionText "(Cape Verde) Floresta - Todo o povoamento de árvores destinado a protecção e fertilização do solo, sem prejuízo da utilidade produtiva florestal; LEX-FAOC013213. CAPE VERDE: Forestry Act (No. 48/V/98)." .

:def_Forest_Cayman_Islands_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Cayman_Islands ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "25.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "4.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.seaturtle.org/mtrg/projects/cayman/Cayman_NBAP.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Cayman Islands 2009) Forest and woodland defined as a class of vegetation characterized by a closed tree canopy, with interlocking crowns generally providing 60-100% cover. “Woodland”, by comparison, is characterized by an open canopy, with tree crowns constituting just 25-60% cover. The canopy height of forest and woodland ranges from about 16m, down to about 4.5m in height, below which shrubland species dominate. Burton (2008b): http://www.seaturtle.org/mtrg/projects/cayman/Cayman_NBAP.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Chile_1979_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Chile ;
    dcterms:date "1979"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://derechoambiental.udp.cl/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/chile-case-cdm-ar-projects-as-published-by-iucn.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Chile 1979) “a piece of land with vegetable formations in which trees predominate and that extend for at least 5,000m2, with a minimum width of 40m, with a tree top greater than 10% in arid and semiarid areas, or greater than 25% in more favourable conditions”. http://derechoambiental.udp.cl/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/chile-case-cdm-ar-projects-as-published-by-iucn.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Chile_2002_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Chile ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/docrep/005/y2328e/y2328e03.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Chile 2002) By forest cover: In Chile, forest land is any area covered by plant formations with a predominance of trees, covering an area greater than 5 000 m2 and 40 m wide, with crown cover of more than 10 per cent (arid and semi-arid zones) or 25 percent in more favoured zones. http://www.fao.org/docrep/005/y2328e/y2328e03.htm" .

:def_Forest_Chile_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Chile ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "25.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fs.fed.us/research/sustain/2003SustainabilityReport/documents/SustainableForests.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Chile 2003) Minimum area = 0.5 ha, minimum tree crown cover = 25%, minimum tree height = 2 m. http://www.fs.fed.us/research/sustain/2003SustainabilityReport/documents/SustainableForests.pdf. (" .

:def_Forest_Chile_2008_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Chile ;
    dcterms:date "2008"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.conaf.cl/cms/editorweb/transparencia/potestades/Ley-20283_bn.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Chile 2008) Bosque: sitio poblado con formaciones vegetales en las que predominan árboles y que ocupa una superficie de por lo menos 5.000 metros cuadrados, con un ancho mínimo de 40 metros, con cobertura de copa arbórea que supere el 10% de dicha superficie total en condiciones áridas y semiáridas y el 25% en circunstancias más favorables. Forest Law 20.283 22 , enacted in 2008 - Forest: site populated with vegetation in which trees predominate occupying an area of at least 5,000 square meters" .

:def_Forest_Chile_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Chile ;
    :canopyThreshold "25.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/filestorage/R/1/J/R1JCI978BD2ENFKQLP34SXZ5YVH0OW/PDD%20SIF%20CHILE.pdf?t=TnV8bHo4cGE3fDBiE0-069vqmcR6RdUAKaoS" ;
    :definitionText "(Chile KP) The Chilean Designated National Authority (CONAMA) adopted the below definition as the forest thresholds for afforestation and reforestation Clean Development Mechanism project activities: - A single minimum tree crown cover of 25 % - A single minimum plantation area of 0.5 hectare - A single minimum tree height of 5 meters http://cdm.unfccc.int/filestorage/R/1/J/R1JCI978BD2ENFKQLP34SXZ5YVH0OW/PDD%20SIF%20CHILE.pdf?t=TnV8bHo4cGE3fDBiE0-069vqmcR6RdUAKaoS and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/" .

:def_Forest_Chile_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Chile ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "Patricio Gonzalez <pgonzale@infor.cl>" ;
    :definitionText "(Chile) Any place covered with plant formations (predominantly trees) over 5,000 m2 and 40 m width, and arboreal cover over 10% of the area (arid and semiarid zones) or 25% of the area in zones with more advantageous conditions. Patricio Gonzalez pgonzale@infor.cl." .

:def_Forest_China_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :China ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.067"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/forestry/fo/country/index.jsp?lang_id=1&geo_id=102" ;
    :definitionText "(China 2000) Min. area = 0.067 ha, Min. Crown Cover = 20 %, Min. Height = 5 m, Min. Strip Width = 10. Includes bamboo and trees. Updated by Zhang Xiaoquan – (23 Jan 02). Trees > 2 cm dia. http://www.fao.org/forestry/fo/country/index.jsp?lang_id=1&geo_id=102." .

:def_Forest_China_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :China ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.0667"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://books.google.com/books?id=iU6ctBak3-gC&pg=PA142&lpg=PA142&dq=%22For+management+purposes" ;
    :definitionText "(China 2003) Forest land of arbour species spanning more than 0.0667 ha with a crown cover of more than 20%. http://books.google.com/books?id=iU6ctBak3-gC&pg=PA142&lpg=PA142&dq=%22For+management+purposes,+State+Forests+are+divided%22&source=bl&ots=yvf2xSmFSt&sig=RmwVGV7UljL1nK9cjAb0NK8VVdY&hl=en&sa=X&ei=QsM6T-mOKaG90QG6zfHdCw&ved=0CCMQ6AEwAA#v=onepage&q=%22For%20management%20purposes%2C%20State%20Forests%20are%20divided%22&f=false" .

:def_Forest_China_2003_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :China ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fs.fed.us/research/sustain/2003SustainabilityReport/documents/SustainableForests.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(China 2003) Minimum area = 0.5 ha, minimum tree crown cover = 20%, minimum tree height = 2 m. http://www.fs.fed.us/research/sustain/2003SustainabilityReport/documents/SustainableForests.pdf" .

:def_Forest_China_2004_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :China ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.forest.gov.tw/ct.asp?xItem=21160&CtNode=1870&mp=3" ;
    :definitionText "(China 2004) ‘forest(s)’ means the land(s) and its collateral trees and bamboo, collectively. According to the delineation of ownership, forest(s) shall be distinguished as national forest(s), public forest(s), and private forest(s); forests principally belong to the nation. http://www.forest.gov.tw/ct.asp?xItem=21160&CtNode=1870&mp=3" .

:def_Forest_China_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :China ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.067"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(China 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.067 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 20 Min. Tree Height (m) = 2 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_China_2006_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :China ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.environmental-auditing.org/LinkClick.aspx?fileticket=fbx%2FbAIVeFU%3D&tabid=128&mid=568" ;
    :definitionText "(China 2006) The definition of forest in China was adjusted from a minimum of 30 percent to 20 percent of cover in 1994. In 2004, the definition of forest was modified again to include special purpose scrubs, which grow in area with annual rainfall below 400 mm or above; the tree line in a mountain with a minimum canopy cover of 30% and in which its primary function is environmental protection. (Zhang, et al, 2006) http://www.environmental-auditing.org/LinkClick.aspx?fileticket=fbx%2FbAIVeFU%3D&" .

:def_Forest_China_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :China ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.portalforestal.com/informacion/noticias/3965-la-cobertura-forestal-de-china-alcanza-el-2036-por-ciento-del-territorio.html" ;
    :definitionText "(China 2009) En China, se consideran zonas forestales aquellas con una superficie de más de 1 mu (0,667 hectáreas) de árboles con una densidad de copa del 20 por ciento o superior. 18 de Noviembre de 2009 http://www.portalforestal.com/informacion/noticias/3965-la-cobertura-forestal-de-china-alcanza-el-2036-por-ciento-del-territorio.html" .

:def_Forest_China_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :China ;
    :areaMin "0.2"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "Zhengyq@rif.forestry.ac.cn" ;
    :definitionText "(China) Area with forest cover equal to or greater than 0.2 ha. Yongqi Zheng Chinese Academy of Forestry. Zhengyq@rif.forestry.ac.cn.." .

:def_Forest_Colombia_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Colombia ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Colombia 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 1.0 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 30 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html - Sasaki & Putz 2009 and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Congo_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Congo ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/forestry/fo/country/index.jsp?lang_id=1&geo_id=12" ;
    :definitionText "(Congo 2000). Min. Crown Cover = 10%. http://www.fao.org/forestry/fo/country/index.jsp?lang_id=1&geo_id=12" .

:def_Forest_Congo_Republic_of_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Congo_Republic_of ;
    :definitionText "(Congo, Republic of) - Area generally occupied by natural forestry stands. (A. Moutanda, Conférence des Responsables de Recherche Agronomique Africains (CORAF), Pointe Noire, Congo)" .

:def_Forest_Congo_Republic_of_2014_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Congo_Republic_of ;
    dcterms:date "2014"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://redd.unfccc.int/files/2016_submission_frel_republicofcongo.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Congo, Republic of 2014) Dans le cadre du NERF de la République du Congo, la définition à prendre en compte est celle qui a été officiellement adoptée en Mars 2014 (rapport d’atelier sur la définition forêt, CN-REDD 2014b).Cette définition précise que « la forêt est un espace couvrant sur une superficie minimale de 0,5 hectare (0,50 ha), avec des arbres ayant une hauteur minimale de 3 mètres (3 m) et un taux minimal de couverture de houppier de 30%». http://redd.unfccc.int/files/2016_submission" .

:def_Forest_Costa_Rica_Forestal_o_Bosque_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Costa_Rica_Forestal_o_Bosque ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/forestry/fo/country/index.jsp?lang_id=1&geo_id=172" ;
    :definitionText "(Costa Rica - Forestal o Bosque) -Todo tipo de vegetación natural la cual puede estar en espacios abiertos como lo es el bosque secundario, o bosque cerrado como el bosque maduro. El bosque secundario es clasificado como tal en la zona seca: (1) si tiene una altura mayor de 6 metros, por que el comportamiento arbóreo en estas zonas, con vegetación de menos de esta altura es rala y aun se detecta pasto Jaraugua mezclado con la vegetación arbórea. Y (2) si densidad de la vegetación arbórea y arbus" .

:def_Forest_Costa_Rica_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Costa_Rica ;
    :sourceRef "http://wiki.awf.forst.uni-goettingen.de/wiki/index.php/Forest_Definition" ;
    :definitionText "(Costa Rica ) Central American country, “forest” is defined for fiscal etc. reasons in the national forest act (Act 3 Ley Forestal No. 7575) as a native ecosystem, with human interventions or not, regenerated through succession or other forest techniques, covering an area of 2 or more hectares, characterized by the presence of mature trees of different ages, species or aspects, with one or more layers covering more than 70% of the surface area and with more than 70 trees per hectare of dbh 15cm " .

:def_Forest_Costa_Rica_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Costa_Rica ;
    :sourceRef "http://web.idrc.ca/en/ev-43425-201-1-DO_TOPIC.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Costa Rica ) The Forestry Law considers as forest any extension of land of two ha or greater with at least 60 trees per hectare. http://web.idrc.ca/en/ev-43425-201-1-DO_TOPIC.html" .

:def_Forest_Costa_Rica_1996_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Costa_Rica ;
    dcterms:date "1996"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "Eva Muller <coseform@sol.racsa.co.cr>" ;
    :definitionText "(Costa Rica 1996 Bosque) - Ecosistema nativo o autoctono, intervenido o no, regenerado por sucesion natural u otras tecnicas forestales, que ocupa una superficie de dos o mas hectareas, caracterizada por la presencia de arboles maduros de diferentes edades, especies y porte variado, con uno o mas doseles que cubran mas del 70% de esa superficie y donde existan mas de sesenta arboles por hectarea de quince o mas centimetros de diametro medido a la altura del pecho (DAP). From the \"Ley Forestal 75" .

:def_Forest_Costa_Rica_1996_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Costa_Rica ;
    dcterms:date "1996"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "Eva Muller <coseform@sol.racsa.co.cr>" ;
    :definitionText "(Costa Rica 1996 Ecosistema boscoso) - Composicion de plantas y animales diversos, mayores y menores, que interaccionan: nacen, crecen, se reproducen y mueren, dependen unos de otros a lo largo de su vida. Despues de miles de anos, esta composicion ha alcanzado un equilibrio que, de no ser interrumpido, se mantendra indefinidamente y surfrira transformaciones muy lentamente. From the \"Ley Forestal 7575 de Costa Rica de 1996\" \"Eva Muller\" coseform@sol.racsa.co.cr" .

:def_Forest_Costa_Rica_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Costa_Rica ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://web.idrc.ca/en/ev-43425-201-1-DO_TOPIC.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Costa Rica 2003?) The Forestry Law defines a forest as an autochthonous native ecosystem, intervened or not, regenerated by natural succession or other forestry techniques, occupying a surface of two or more ha, characterized by the presence of mature trees of different ages, species and size, with one or more canopies covering over 70% of this surface and having more than 60 trees/ha of 15 cm or more in diameter (Art .3). http://web.idrc.ca/en/ev-43425-201-1-DO_TOPIC.html" .

:def_Forest_Costa_Rica_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Costa_Rica ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Costa Rica 2006 KP) Min. Area (ha) = 1.0, Min Crown Cover (%) = 30; Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html - Sasaki & Putz 2009 and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Costa_Rica_2012_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Costa_Rica ;
    dcterms:date "2012"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.un-redd.org/FRELPublication/tabid/794487/Default.aspx" ;
    :definitionText "(Costa Rica 2012) The definition submitted to the CDM (minimum canopy cover of 30%, minimum height of 5 meters, minimum size of 1 hectare) is used as a preliminary definition for its REDD+ program, but Costa Rica has also reserved the right to change the definition and revise its reference level once a final decision is made and adopted http://www.un-redd.org/FRELPublication/tabid/794487/Default.aspx" .

:def_Forest_Costa_Rica_2014_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Costa_Rica ;
    dcterms:date "2014"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://theredddesk.org/countries/costa-rica/legal-frameworks" ;
    :definitionText "(Costa Rica 2014) According to Costa Rica’s Emissions Reduction Project Idea Note (ER-PIN) for design purposes of the National Forest Inventory and the MRV for REDD+, Costa Rica has used the definition of forest that it uses for CDM projects: “Forest is an area of land with a minimum size of 1.0 ha, with a canopy cover over 30%, and presenting trees with the potential to reach a minimum height of 5 meters at maturity in situ. A forest may consist of tight formations where trees of various strata" .

:def_Forest_Cote_dIvoire_1965_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Cote_dIvoire ;
    dcterms:date "1965"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Cote d’Ivoire 1965) Sont considérées comme forêts les formations végétales dont les fruits exclusifs ou principaux sont les bois d'ébénisterie, d'industrie et de service, les bois de chauffage et à charbon et qui accessoirement peuvent produire d'autres matières telles que bambous, écorces, latex, résines, gommes, graines et fruits. TITRE I DEFINITIONS, Article 1. - LOI NO 65/425 DU 20 DEC 1965. portant Code Forestier" .

:def_Forest_Côte_dIvoire_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Côte_dIvoire ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Côte d'Ivoire 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.1 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 30 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns Excludes palms and bamboos. http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Croatia_1995_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Croatia ;
    dcterms:date "1995"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Croatia 1995) Land coherently stocked with trees, shrubs and ground vegetation, where wood mass is permanently produced, and benefits of general welfare are expressed by ecological (protective) and social forest functions\". (\"Sumarski List\", Hrvatsko Sumarsko Drustvo, Journal of the Forestry Society of Croatia. No 9-10, Godina CXIX, Zagreb, 1995)" .

:def_Forest_Croatia_2008_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Croatia ;
    dcterms:date "2008"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/meetings/ad_hoc_working_groups/kp/application/pdf/awgkp_croatia_2011.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Croatia 2008 KP) Min. Area (ha) = 0.1 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 10 Min. Tree Height (m) = 2 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://unfccc.int/files/meetings/ad_hoc_working_groups/kp/application/pdf/awgkp_croatia_2011.pdf and http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/27-08-08_initial_report_croatia.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Croatia_2010_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Croatia ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/docrep/013/al485E/al485e.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Croatia 2010) Forest is defined as the land covered by forest trees formed as forest stand over an area larger than 10 ars (1 ar = 100 square meters). Separate forest tree groups over an area up to 10 ars, forest nurseries, wind barrier belts, tree avenues, and parks in settlements are not considered forests. http://www.fao.org/docrep/013/al485E/al485e.pdf and Faculty of forestry University of Zagreb, Ministry for regional development of forestry and water management, 2010. http://www.efi.int/f" .

:def_Forest_Croatia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Croatia ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://books.google.com/books?id=iU6ctBak3-gC&pg=PA132&lpg=PA132&dq=Croatia++Forest++definition+define+%22forest+is%22+law&source=bl&ots=yvf2xQpJPr&sig=mQUVqbZLIEa6C88qGsh1mYS9UDY&hl=en&sa=X&ei=SoI6T_" ;
    :definitionText "(Croatia KP) forest is land spanning more than 0.1 hectares with trees higher than 2 meters and canopy cover more than 10 percent, or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ, http://books.google.com/books?id=iU6ctBak3-gC&pg=PA132&lpg=PA132&dq=Croatia++Forest++definition+define+%22forest+is%22+law&source=bl&ots=yvf2xQpJPr&sig=mQUVqbZLIEa6C88qGsh1mYS9UDY&hl=en&sa=X&ei=SoI6T_26K4Tg0QGAmoHFCw&ved=0CCMQ6AEwAA#v=onepage&q=Croatia%20%20Forest%20%20definition%20define%20%22forest%20is%22%20law&f=fa" .

:def_Forest_Croatia_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Croatia ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://books.google.com/books?id=iU6ctBak3-gC&pg=PA132&lpg=PA132&dq=Croatia++Forest++definition+define+%22forest+is%22+law&source=bl&ots=yvf2xQpJPr&sig=mQUVqbZLIEa6C88qGsh1mYS9UDY&hl=en&sa=X&ei=SoI6T_" ;
    :definitionText "(Croatia) Forest is defined by Croatian Forest law as land with tree cover occupying areas greater than 0.1 ha. http://books.google.com/books?id=iU6ctBak3-gC&pg=PA132&lpg=PA132&dq=Croatia++Forest++definition+define+%22forest+is%22+law&source=bl&ots=yvf2xQpJPr&sig=mQUVqbZLIEa6C88qGsh1mYS9UDY&hl=en&sa=X&ei=SoI6T_26K4Tg0QGAmoHFCw&ved=0CCMQ6AEwAA#v=onepage&q=Croatia%20%20Forest%20%20definition%20define%20%22forest%20is%22%20law&f=false" .

:def_Forest_Cuba_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Cuba ;
    :sourceRef "Nelida Puentes Alvarez <npuentes@eco.upr.edu.cu>" ;
    :definitionText "(Cuba) Bosque: formaciones naturales (bosques naturales) o artificiales (plantaciones) integradas por árboles, arbustos y otras especies de plantas y animales superiores e inferiores, que constituyen un ecosistema de relevancia económica y social por las funciones que desempeña. \"Nelida Puentes Alvarez\" npuentes@eco.upr.edu.cu" .

:def_Forest_Cyprus_1992_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Cyprus ;
    dcterms:date "1992"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "Publicity Sector <publicity@cytanet.com.cy>" ;
    :definitionText "(Cyprus 1992) - An area of at least 1 ha covered with forest tree vegetation and crown cover more than 10 percent. A.K. Christou \"Forestry Department - Research and Publicity Sector\" publicity@cytanet.com.cy. Cyprus (open woodland) Forest area with only few trees per ha (that is crown cover about 1-2 percent) (UN/ECE 1992 p. 125)." .

:def_Forest_Cyprus_2002_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Cyprus ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Cyprus 2002) Old definition: Forest Land with tree crown cover of more that 10 % and area of more than 1 ha. Cyprus Department of forests ministry of agriculture, natural resources and environment, 2006. Kyriacou K. 2002. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Cyprus_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Cyprus ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Cyprus 2006) It corresponds to FRA definition except the threshold value for minimum area, which is 1 ha, with trees higher than 5 m and a crown cover of more than 10%, or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ. Land predominantly under agricultural or urban use not included. Cyprus Department of forests ministry of agriculture, natural resources and environment, 2006. Kyriacou K. 2002. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Cyprus_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Cyprus ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://books.google.com/books?id=iU6ctBak3-gC&pg=PA142&lpg=PA142&dq=%22For+management+purposes" ;
    :definitionText "(Cyprus) Spanning more than 0.5 ha with trees higher than 5 m and a crown cover of more than 10%, or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ, Land predominantly under agricultural or urban use not included. http://books.google.com/books?id=iU6ctBak3-gC&pg=PA142&lpg=PA142&dq=%22For+management+purposes,+State+Forests+are+divided%22&source=bl&ots=yvf2xSmFSt&sig=RmwVGV7UljL1nK9cjAb0NK8VVdY&hl=en&sa=X&ei=QsM6T-mOKaG90QG6zfHdCw&ved=0CCMQ6AEwAA#v=onepage&q=%22For%20management%20purposes%2C%20State" .

:def_Forest_Czech_Republic_2004_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Czech_Republic ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.01"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Czech Republic 2004) - Forest land: land with forest stands and land after cutting ready for reforestation, forest line and soft roads of width less than 4 m. Forest roads, water surfaces, land above timber line and other land serving for forest management. Minimum area is 0.01 ha and with a minimum width of 20 m. NIL definition: Forest - areas (subplot), which are forest land as defined in the Forest Act No. 289/95 Coll. § 3, paragraph 1, letter a) and the Ministry of Agriculture Decree No. 84" .

