:def_Forest_Democratic_Republic_of_Congo_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Democratic_Republic_of_Congo ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.mappingforrights.org/files/Rights%20and%20mapping%20in%20DRC%20%20-%20FINAL.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Democratic Republic of Congo) Article 1 defines forest as any land with trees or bushes that can produce forest products, act as home to wildlife or have an effect on climate or soils, or any land that previously had such vegetation on it. http://www.mappingforrights.org/files/Rights%20and%20mapping%20in%20DRC%20%20-%20FINAL.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Denmark_2004_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Denmark ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://en.itst.dk/spectrum-equipment/Auctions-and-calls-for-tenders/800-mhz/filarkiv/800MHz%20consultation%20document.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Denmark 2004) A forest is a tree-grown area which is larger than ½ hectare and is more than 20 metres wide. The trees shall be able to grow to a highstemmed closed forest inside a reasonable timespan, cf. the Danish Nature Agency's guidelines of 1 October 2004 on the Forest Act. http://en.itst.dk/spectrum-equipment/Auctions-and-calls-for-tenders/800-mhz/filarkiv/800MHz%20consultation%20document.pdf" .

