:def_Forest_Ecuador_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Ecuador ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Ecuador 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 1.0 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 30 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html - Sasaki & Putz 2009 and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Ecuador_2013_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Ecuador ;
    dcterms:date "2013"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Ecuador 2013) A national forest definition was adopted (http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html) in the context of identifying forest land in Ecuador’s land-use maps. According to this definition all land units bearing “a single minimum tree crown cover value of 30%; a single minimum land area value of 1.00 hectare; and, a single minimum tree height value of 5.00 meters” are considered as forest. This definition is consistent with Ministerial Agreement Number 033 of April the 5th, 2013 (MAE, 2013b" .

:def_Forest_Egypt_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Egypt ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "60.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.egyptchm.org/chm/implementation/pdf/arid_lands.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Egypt 2003) Forests include all areas dominated by evergreen or deciduous trees with a canopy cover of greater than 60% and a height exceeding 2 meters. Both broadleaf and needleleaf trees are included. http://www.egyptchm.org/chm/implementation/pdf/arid_lands.pdf" .

:def_Forest_El_Salvador_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :El_Salvador ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(El Salvador 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.5 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 30 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html - Sasaki & Putz 2009 and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Eritrea_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Eritrea ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/forestry/fo/country/index.jsp?lang_id=1&geo_id=62" ;
    :definitionText "(Eritrea 2000) Forest and woodland 10 % canopy closure. Source: ECE-FAO Partnership Programme: Kenya Workshop on Forestry Statistics. Appendix 6 and http://www.fao.org/forestry/fo/country/index.jsp?lang_id=1&geo_id=62" .

:def_Forest_Estonia_1998_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Estonia ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "1.3"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.envir.ee/metsaamet/english/acts/forestact.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Estonia 1998) Forest [mets] - growing site of ligneous plants which area is at least 0.5 ha and which corresponds to the following conditions: 1) height of growing trees is at least 1.3 m and density of crowns is at least 30%; 2) it is managed for timber and other forest products or there are ligneous plants preserved for use in ways which are described in the Forestry Act. Forests can be divided into productive forests (producing at least 1 cubic metre of stem timber as an average for long per" .

:def_Forest_Estonia_1998_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Estonia ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.keskkonnainfo.ee/publications/16285_PDF.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Estonia 1998) Forest Act (FA) (1998) forest is defined as a site of woody vegetation with an area of at least 0,5 ha which meets at least one of the following criteria: 1) the height of the trees is at least 1,3 m and the canopy density at least 30 per cent; 2) it is managed for obtaining timber or other forest produce, or woody vegetation is maintained there for the use in the ways specified in this Act. http://www.keskkonnainfo.ee/publications/16285_PDF.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Estonia_2006_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Estonia ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "1.3"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/msword/aau_report_estonia_24_10_unfccc.doc" ;
    :definitionText "(Estonia 2006 KP) Min. Area (ha) = 0.5 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 30 Min. Tree Height (m) = 1.3 Min. Strip Width (m) = 20 http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/msword/aau_report_estonia_24_10_unfccc.doc. (2006)" .

:def_Forest_Estonia_2007_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Estonia ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "1.3"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://stud.epsilon.slu.se/1798/1/Link_M_100910.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Estonia 2007) According to the act, forest land is land listed in the land register as forest and or land of at least 0.1 hectares where woody plants with a height of at least 1.3 m and with crown closure of at least 30% grow (Forest Act, 2007). http://stud.epsilon.slu.se/1798/1/Link_M_100910.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Estonia_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Estonia ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://afoludata.jrc.ec.europa.eu/metaed/project_collection/JRC_54744_Mascaref_Full_Report_for_print.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Estonia 2009 NIR) Crown cover > 30%, tree height > 2m, area > 0.5 ha. http://afoludata.jrc.ec.europa.eu/metaed/project_collection/JRC_54744_Mascaref_Full_Report_for_print.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Estonia_2010_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Estonia ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Estonia 2010 NFI) Crown cover > 30%." .

:def_Forest_Estonia_2010_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Estonia ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Estonia 2010) Forest land (reference definition, applied parallel with National definition since 2005) Land with tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 10% and area of more than 0.5 ha. The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 m at maturity in situ (incl. temporarily unstocked areas). Pärt E., Adermann V., Merenäk M., 2010. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Estonia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Estonia ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "1.3"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.environmental-auditing.org/LinkClick.aspx?fileticket=fbx%2FbAIVeFU%3D&tabid=128&mid=568" ;
    :definitionText "(Estonia KP) A plot of land with an area of at least 0.1ha and woody plants with the height of at least 1.3m and with the canopy density of at least 30 percent grow there. http://www.environmental-auditing.org/LinkClick.aspx?fileticket=fbx%2FbAIVeFU%3D&tabid=128&mid=568" .

:def_Forest_Estonia_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Estonia ;
    :sourceRef "Sulev Svilponis <Sulev@ekm.envir.ee>" ;
    :definitionText "(Estonia) Collection of trees which density is at least 30% and growing stock is more than 30 cubic metres per hectare. Forest Survey Centre From: \"Sulev Svilponis\" Sulev@ekm.envir.ee . Definitions are unofficial translations." .

:def_Forest_Estonia_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Estonia ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Estonia) Forest - forest land with vegetation growing on it and with wildlife living in it. The lower area limit is 0.5 ha. http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Estonia_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Estonia ;
    :sourceRef "Sulev Svilponis <Sulev@ekm.envir.ee>" ;
    :definitionText "(Estonia) Forest [mets] - forest land with plant community. Trees, bushes and other plants are important part of forest. Forest fauna is part of forest ecosystem. Current Estonian Forestry Act (valid until 01/01/99) From: \"Sulev Svilponis\" Sulev@ekm.envir.ee. Definitions are unofficial translations." .

:def_Forest_Estonia_nd_005
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Estonia ;
    :sourceRef "Sulev Svilponis <Sulev@ekm.envir.ee>" ;
    :definitionText "(Estonia) Forest [mets] - Part of landscape and habitat which is formed when trees are growing together and where appear multifarious mutual influence and relations between trees and site conditions (relief, soil, microclimate). Collection of trees is called forest if the area, height and density are exceeding the limits when environmental conditions start to change qualitatively. Estonian Encyclopedia From: \"Sulev Svilponis\" Sulev@ekm.envir.ee . Definitions are unofficial translations" .

:def_Forest_Estonia_2013_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Estonia ;
    dcterms:date "2013"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32013D0529" ;
    :definitionText "(Estonia 2013) - Area (ha) 0.5; Tree crown cover (%) 30; Tree height (m) 2. http://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32013D0529" .

:def_Forest_Ethiopia_1994_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Ethiopia ;
    dcterms:date "1994"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/filestorage/L/4/Q/L4QB30W8C5RYZMT6UKOFX1PV9GNIHS/Annex%205%20Legal%20aspects.pdf?t=OXR8bHpqZnlvfDByMiF2MIecUaf9gjv8IjJT" ;
    :definitionText "(Ethiopia 1994) The Forestry Conservation, Development and Utilization Proclamation. was issued at the Federal level in 1994 (Proclamation No.94/1994). The term.forest. is defined as ..a community of plants either naturally grown or developed by planting and in many respects are trees and other plants having a woody character. (Art.2.3). Forests are thus defined into natural forests (e.g. naturally growing indigenous trees) and forests established by planting (e.g. afforestation or reforestation" .

:def_Forest_Ethiopia_1998_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Ethiopia ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "68.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "7.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/docrep/003/X6684E/X6684E10.htm#P2311_178011" ;
    :definitionText "(Ethiopia 1998) Natural high forest. Min. av. height 7 m. Canopy closure 68%. Source: ECE-FAO Partnership Programme: Kenya Workshop on Forestry Statistics. Appendix 6. http://www.fao.org/docrep/003/X6684E/X6684E10.htm#P2311_178011" .

:def_Forest_Ethiopia_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Ethiopia ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.05"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Ethiopia 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.05 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 20 Min. Tree Height (m) = 2 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html - Sasaki & Putz 2009 and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Ethiopia_2007_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Ethiopia ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.pfmp-farmsos.org/Docs/forest%20proclamation_english.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Ethiopia 2007) \"forest\" means a community of plants, either naturally grown or developed by planting and mainly consisting of trees and other plants having woody character; http://www.pfmp-farmsos.org/Docs/forest%20proclamation_english.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Ethiopia_2015_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Ethiopia ;
    dcterms:date "2015"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://redd.unfccc.int/files/2016_submission_frel_ethiopia.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Ethiopia 2015) In February 2015 Ethiopia adopted a new forest definition as follows: 'Land spanning at least 0.5 ha covered by trees and bamboo ), attaining a height of at least 2m and a canopy cover of at least 20% or trees with the potential to reach these thresholds in situ in due course’ (Minutes of Forest sector management, MEFCC, Feb. 2015 (UNFCCC-Ethiopia, 2016). http://redd.unfccc.int/files/2016_submission_frel_ethiopia.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Ethiopia_2017_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Ethiopia ;
    dcterms:date "2017"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://redd.unfccc.int/files/ethiopia_frel_3.2_final_modified_submission.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Ethiopia 2017) In February 2015 Ethiopia adopted a new forest definition (MEF 2015) as follows: 'Land spanning more than 0.5 ha covered by trees (including bamboo) (with a minimum width of 20m or not more than two‐thirds of its length) attaining a height of more than 2m and a canopy cover of more than 20% or trees with the potential to reach these thresholds in situ in due course (Minutes of Forest sector management, MEFCC, Feb. 2015). Ethiopia is in the process of approving this as its nationa" .

:def_Forest_Ethiopia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Ethiopia ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.05"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/filestorage/L/4/Q/L4QB30W8C5RYZMT6UKOFX1PV9GNIHS/Annex%205%20Legal%20aspects.pdf?t=OXR8bHpqZnlvfDByMiF2MIecUaf9gjv8IjJT" ;
    :definitionText "(Ethiopia KP) The Ethiopian Designate National Authority for CDM, EPA, has communicated to the UNFCCC CDM Executive Board the definition of forest used for CDM projects in Ethiopia, which is as follows: •A minimum area of 0.05 hectares; •A minimum tree crown cover of 20 per cent; •A minimum average tree height above 2 m. http://cdm.unfccc.int/filestorage/L/4/Q/L4QB30W8C5RYZMT6UKOFX1PV9GNIHS/Annex%205%20Legal%20aspects.pdf?t=OXR8bHpqZnlvfDByMiF2MIecUaf9gjv8IjJT and http://database.v-c-s.org/sites" .

:def_Forest_Ethiopia_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Ethiopia ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.05"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.climate-standards.org/projects/files/ethiopia/Ethiopia_Humbo_CCBA_PDD_June_6.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Ethiopia KP) The Ethiopian DNA has determined that within Ethiopia, a forest is defined as land with trees that has:  A minimum area of 0.05 hectares;  A minimum tree crown cover of 20 per cent;  A minimum average tree height above 2 m. http://www.climate-standards.org/projects/files/ethiopia/Ethiopia_Humbo_CCBA_PDD_June_6.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Fiji_1992_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Fiji ;
    dcterms:date "1992"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "4.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Fiji 1992) In the National Forest Inventory (1991-1992) on a scale of 1:50,000 the minimum forested area shows on the map is 4 ha. There is no legal definition of what a forest is, although it is classified into three: Dense forest - Crown density by trees and/or ferns 75-100% and grown coverage of grass, palm and /or bamboo 0-25%. Medium dense - Crown density by trees and/or ferns 45-80% and ground coverage by grass, palm and/or bamboo 20-55%. Scattered forest (including scattered coconut stan" .

:def_Forest_Fiji_2007_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Fiji ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "4.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://geodata.rrcap.unep.org/all_reports/PECCO_Draft_30dec2010.docx" ;
    :definitionText "(Fiji 2007) The re-defined threshold for forest is from 4 hectares in the 1991 NFI down to 0.5 hectares in the 2007 NFI. http://geodata.rrcap.unep.org/all_reports/PECCO_Draft_30dec2010.docx" .

:def_Forest_Fiji_2010_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Fiji ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.cbd.int/doc/world/fj/fj-nr-04-en.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Fiji 2010)Forest Densities: 1. dense forest: crown density by trees and/ or ferns 75-100% and round coverage by grass, palm and/ or bamboo 0-25% 2. medium dense forest: crown density by trees and/ or ferns 45-80% and ground coverage by grass, palm and/ or bamboo 20-55% 3. scattered forest: shrub forest (including scattered coconut stands), dense bushland (thickets) with single trees. Crown density by trees and/or ferns 15-50% and ground coverage by grass, palm and/ or bamboo 50-85% http://www.c" .

:def_Forest_Fiji_2015_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Fiji ;
    dcterms:date "2015"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.parliament.gov.fj/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/Bill-No-13-Forest.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Fiji 2015) “natural forest” means a forest composed of indigenous trees and not classified as forest plantation; http://www.parliament.gov.fj/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/Bill-No-13-Forest.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Finland_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Finland ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/x-zip-compressed/fin_ir_report_22dec.zip" ;
    :definitionText "(Finland 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.5 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 10 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = 20 http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/x-zip-compressed/fin_ir_report_22dec.zip Temporarily unstocked areas are included (forest regeneration areas)." .

:def_Forest_Finland_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Finland ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://afoludata.jrc.ec.europa.eu/metaed/project_collection/JRC_54744_Mascaref_Full_Report_for_print.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Finland 2009 NIR) Crown cover > 10%, tree height > 5m, > area > 0.5 ha, width > 20 m. http://afoludata.jrc.ec.europa.eu/metaed/project_collection/JRC_54744_Mascaref_Full_Report_for_print.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Former_USSR_1992_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Former_USSR ;
    dcterms:date "1992"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Former USSR 1992) - Land bearing stands of the main forest-forming species as well as forest plantations, nurseries, and the like. Forests do not include roads or other land not subject to afforestation. …Other wooded land includes scrub and plantation in which trees are rare. This category also conventionally includes clearings, burnt areas, and glades subject to stocking in the future…. (UN/ECE 1992 p. 275)." .

:def_Forest_France_1992_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :France ;
    dcterms:date "1992"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "4.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(France 1992) Forest greater than or equal to 4 ha. (UN/ECE 1992 p. 156)." .

:def_Forest_France_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :France ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(France 1997) Identified from aerial photos, from ocular estimates. Lands with either measured trees (diameter 7.5 cm) have a crown cover percentage reaching at least 10% (ground projection of crowns) - or there are more than 500 stems per ha that are viable trees (able to make a stand): seedlings, plants or shoots, vigorous, well shaped and regularly distributed. Cover at least 5 acres, the average width of canopy being at least 15 m. Rest of definition appears to include orchards. (European Co" .

:def_Forest_France_2005_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :France ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.05"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://icaci.org/documents/ICC_proceedings/ICC2011/Oral%20Presentations%20PDF/A3-Data%20integration/CO-028.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(France 2005) According to the national forest definition the minimum forest area is 0.05 ha, with the canopy cover of 10% , minimum height of tree 5-7 m and the minimum width of strip 25 m.(FRA,2005) http://icaci.org/documents/ICC_proceedings/ICC2011/Oral%20Presentations%20PDF/A3-Data%20integration/CO-028.pdf" .

:def_Forest_France_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :France ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/rapport_initial_de_la_france_kyoto_quantite_attribue_ccnuc..pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(France 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.5 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 10 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = 20 http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/rapport_initial_de_la_france_kyoto_quantite_attribue_ccnuc..pdf. (2006)" .

:def_Forest_France_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :France ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://afoludata.jrc.ec.europa.eu/metaed/project_collection/JRC_54744_Mascaref_Full_Report_for_print.pd" ;
    :definitionText "(France 2009 NIR) Crown cover > 10%, tree height > 5m, area > 0.5 ha, width > 20 m. http://afoludata.jrc.ec.europa.eu/metaed/project_collection/JRC_54744_Mascaref_Full_Report_for_print.pd" .

:def_Forest_France_2010_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :France ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "15.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://afoludata.jrc.ec.europa.eu/metaed/project_collection/JRC_54744_Mascaref_Full_Report_for_print.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(France 2010 NFI) Crown cover > 10%, area > 0.5 ha, width > 15 m. http://afoludata.jrc.ec.europa.eu/metaed/project_collection/JRC_54744_Mascaref_Full_Report_for_print.pdf" .

:def_Forest_France_2010_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :France ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(France 2010) - A forest is defined as land with tree crown cover of more than 10%, an area of more than 0.5 ha and an average width of more than 20 m. Trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 m at maturity in situ.Institute National de l’Information Geographique et Forestiere, 2010. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" .

:def_Forest_French_Polynesia_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :French_Polynesia ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/forestry/fo/country/index.jsp?lang_id=1&geo_id=112" ;
    :definitionText "(French Polynesia 2000) Forest - Includes natural forest and forest plantations but excluding cocco plantations. http://www.fao.org/forestry/fo/country/index.jsp?lang_id=1&geo_id=112" .

:def_Forest_Gabon_2001_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Gabon ;
    dcterms:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://books.google.com/books?id=KDcRI1Nj9n0C&pg=PA31&lpg=PA31&dq=Gabon+forest+definition+define+%22forest+is%22+law" ;
    :definitionText "(Gabon 2001) An area with a plant cover that provides wood and nonagricultural plant products and which shelters wildlife and directly or indirectly affects the soil, climate or water supply. http://books.google.com/books?id=KDcRI1Nj9n0C&pg=PA31&lpg=PA31&dq=Gabon+forest+definition+define+%22forest+is%22+law,+code,+act&source=bl&ots=KcKcJElGQp&sig=VXqWDovWVaNhzxlOslyQu7G0HME&hl=en&sa=X&ei=mbE-T-C9JYXu0gGrv83MCA&ved=0CCMQ6AEwAA#v=onepage&q=Gabon%20forest%20definition%20define%20%22forest%20is%22%2" .

:def_Forest_Gambia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Gambia ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "Forestry Department <forestry.dept@gamtel.gm>" ;
    :definitionText "(Gambia) - A land area with at least 10% tree cover, naturally grown or planted, and or 50% or more shrub and tree generation cover and includes government forest parks, community forests and protected forests irrespective of their tree and shrub cover;..... Source: Danso A. A. Forestry Department forestry.dept@gamtel.gm" .

:def_Forest_Gambia_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Gambia ;
    :sourceRef "http://books.google.com/books?id=dZh6-ekpSawC&pg=PA104&lpg=PA104&dq=Ethiopia+Forest+definition+define+%22forest+is%22+law+act&source=bl&ots=Wx8pSUKv7a&sig=I5dj10rusCk4zljYh9dOAZi5Vgw&hl=en&sa=X&ei=jC8" ;
    :definitionText "(Gambia) all lands at leas10 % tree cover and 50% vegetative cover http://books.google.com/books?id=dZh6-ekpSawC&pg=PA104&lpg=PA104&dq=Ethiopia+Forest+definition+define+%22forest+is%22+law+act&source=bl&ots=Wx8pSUKv7a&sig=I5dj10rusCk4zljYh9dOAZi5Vgw&hl=en&sa=X&ei=jC8-T9mtFqHz0gH49OCpBw&ved=0CCMQ6AEwAA#v=onepage&q=Ethiopia%20Forest%20definition%20define%20%22forest%20is%22%20law%20act&f=false" .

:def_Forest_Gambia1998_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Gambia1998 ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://extwprlegs1.fao.org/docs/pdf/gam19052.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Gambia1998) \"Forest\" means a land area with at least 10% tree cover, naturally grown or planted, and or 50% or more shrub and tree regeneration cover and includes Government forest parks, community forests and protected forests irrespective of their tree and shrub cover; provided that vegetation on fallow land is not a forest except as specified in section 5 of this Act http://extwprlegs1.fao.org/docs/pdf/gam19052.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Georgia_1999_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Georgia ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "kattimet@geo.net.ge" ;
    :definitionText "(Georgia 1999) A part of geographical landscape, comprising attributed to forest by Georgian legislation, land under these trees, as well as shrubs, grass, animals and other components biologically linked in the process of their development, affecting each other and the environment. Source: Forest Code (June, 1999) Kate Metreveli, Head of the WB Forestry, Project Preparation Unit. kattimet@geo.net.ge" .

:def_Forest_Georgia_1999_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Georgia ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Georgia 1999): The integrity of state forest, land and other resources defined as SFF by the Georgian legislation (Forest Code of Georgia, 1999). Includes the land categories listed below: Forest: Part of geographic landscape, which includes the unity of trees (defined by the Georgian legislation as parts of forests), lands, bushes, grasses, animals and other objects, which are biologically inter-related and have an impact upon each other as well as environment. Forest lands: Open plantations, " .

:def_Forest_Georgia_2008_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Georgia ;
    dcterms:date "2008"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.unece.org/fileadmin/DAM/env/pp/compliance/C2009-35/Communication/Annex_1_ACCCC200835_GeorgianForestCode.doc" ;
    :definitionText "(Georgia 2008) - Forest - a part of geographical landscape, comprising trees attributed to forest by Georgian legislation, land under these trees, as well as shrubs, grass, animals, and other components biologically linked in the process of their development, affecting each other and the environment. http://www.unece.org/fileadmin/DAM/env/pp/compliance/C2009-35/Communication/Annex_1_ACCCC200835_GeorgianForestCode.doc" .

:def_Forest_Georgia_2010_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Georgia ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Georgia 2010) A forest is defined as land with tree crown cover of more than 10%, an area of more than 0.5 ha and an average width of more than 20 m. Trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 m at maturity in situ. FAO, 2010. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Germany_1975_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Germany ;
    dcterms:date "1975"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/legal/legstud/ls88/ls88e.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Germany 1975) Forests are all tracts of land where forest trees grow, including functionally related parts (e.g. clearings and openings, forest roads). http://www.fao.org/legal/legstud/ls88/ls88e.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Germany_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Germany ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/ec_assigned_amount_report_en.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Germany 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.1 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 10 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/ec_assigned_amount_report_en.pdf." .

:def_Forest_Ghana_1999_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Ghana ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Ghana 1999) A large area of land thickly covered with trees, bushes, shrubs and thickets. (Osei Kofi, Forestry Dept.- Letter 7 May 99)" .

:def_Forest_Ghana_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Ghana ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "15.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nature.com/news/2009/090819/full/news.2009.842.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Ghana 2009 KP) defines a forest as an area of land greater than 0.1 hectare, with more than 15% canopy cover and a minimum tree height of 2 metres. http://www.nature.com/news/2009/090819/full/news.2009.842.html" .

:def_Forest_Ghana_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Ghana ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "15.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Ghana 2006?) Canopy = 15%; Area = 0.1 ha; Tree height = 5 m. https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Greece_1945_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Greece ;
    dcterms:date "1945"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "25.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://lambda.qsensei.com/content/b7spn" ;
    :definitionText "(Greece 1945) - All land which has been forest or areas of equal ecological value with forest vegetation (like areas with wild bushes and sporadic trees with a density of their canopy ground projection larger than 25% of the area), as of 1945, is characterized as “forest” and is protected by the Law. Potsiou, Chryssy A.; Dimitriadi, Katerina. 2008. Tools for Legal Integration and Regeneration of Informal Development in Greece: A Research Study in the Municipality of Keratea. Surveying and Land I" .

:def_Forest_Greece_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Greece ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Greece 2000) FRA 2000. Land with tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 10%and area of more than 0.5 ha. The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 meters (m) at maturity in situ. FOREST EUROPE, UNECE AND FAO, 2011." .

:def_Forest_Greece_2002_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Greece ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ymparisto.fi/download.asp?contentid=25582&lan=en" ;
    :definitionText "(Greece 2002). Greece’s national definition of forest (an area of at least 0.5 ha or a strip of land 30 m wide with at least 10% tree coverage and forest type vegetation). http://www.ymparisto.fi/download.asp?contentid=25582&lan=en" .

:def_Forest_Greece_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Greece ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "25.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://tempus.marstu.net/presentations/mouflis1(eng" ;
    :definitionText "(Greece 2003) Forest is defined as an area made up of wild trees species creating a canopy with a crown density >25%. Forestland is defined as an area made up of wild woody vegetation (scattered trees, shrubs, or open land within forests and open land above tree line) with > 25% vegetation. There is a controversy over the threshold percent cover to characterize as forest or forest land (protection afforded by law) as formerly 15 % was used. Law 86/1969: “Forest Code”. Law 998/1979, 3208/2003.. M" .

:def_Forest_Greece_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Greece ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "25.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.3"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/msword/greece_-_initial_report.doc" ;
    :definitionText "(Greece 2006 KP) Greece has identified the following single minimum values for tree crown cover, land area and tree height for use in accounting for its activities under Article 3, paragraphs 3 and 4 of the Kyoto Protocol: Tree crown cover: 25%; Land area: 0.3 Ha; Tree height: 2 m. Hellenic Ministry for the Environment, Physical Planning and Public Works’ 2006. Initial Report of Greece under the Kyoto Protocol. Climate Change. 45 p. http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_" .

:def_Forest_Greece_2006_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Greece ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "25.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ec-gis.org/Workshops/12ec-gis/presentations/Plenary%20room/THU_Nat_SDI_2/palaskas.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Greece 2006) Forest –forest area: (Greek Constitution )The organic group of wild plants with wooded stem which form (with in site living flora and fauna) a special biocommunityand environment. Forest area if wooded vegetation is sparse (recent quantitative criteria L.3208/03: 25% cover, height of vegetation, species). Palaskas, Dimitrios Sp; Stamou, Nikolaos I. 2006. Social and economic benefits from compiling the Forest Data Bank Project (Dasologio) in Greece. 12th EC GI & GIS Workshop -Innsbr" .

:def_Forest_Greece_2006_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Greece ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.isprs.org/proceedings/XXXVI/4-C42/Papers/13_Automated%20classification%20IC%20I%20-%20Forest/OBIA2006_Mallinis_et_al.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Greece 2006) Specifically in order for a patch to be characterized as “forest” or “woodland”, its size should exceed 0,3 hectares or unless so, it should be at least 30 meters wide or in close interdependence and interaction with other forest areas. Furthermore the forest canopy cover should exceed 30 percent. The distinction among the two categories is based on criteria relating to the existence of stratums of forest canopy and the canopy cover of each layer. In general woodlands correspond ma" .

:def_Forest_Greece_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Greece ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://afoludata.jrc.ec.europa.eu/metaed/project_collection/JRC_54744_Mascaref_Full_Report_for_print.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Greece 2009 NIR and NFI) Crown cover > 10%, area > 0.5 ha, width > 30 m. http://afoludata.jrc.ec.europa.eu/metaed/project_collection/JRC_54744_Mascaref_Full_Report_for_print.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Greece_2011_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Greece ;
    dcterms:date "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Greece 2011). Land with tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 10%and area of more than 0.5 ha. The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 meters (m) at maturity in situ. FOREST EUROPE, UNECE AND FAO, 2011." .

:def_Forest_Greece_2012_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Greece ;
    dcterms:date "2012"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "chryssyp@survey.ntua.gr" ;
    :definitionText "(Greece 2012) - A forest is an area where wild trees with wooden trunk exist and forest lands where wild plants with hard branches like bushes, low or tall, even rocky areas that are surrounded by areas with such vegetation. Any piece of land if not cultivated can become a forest land. Chryssy Potsiou . chryssyp@survey.ntua.gr 5 Feb. 2012." .

:def_Forest_Greece_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Greece ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "7.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.lasy.gov.pl/dokumenty/in_english/files/forest_and_forestry_in_eu-pdf/at_download/file" ;
    :definitionText "(Greece) Forest is defined as land with tree crown cover (stand density) of more than about 20% of the area, and with trees which usually grow to more than about 7 m in height and are able to produce wood. This includes both, closed forest formations where trees of various storeys and undergrowth cover a high proportion of the ground, and open forest formations with a continuous grass layer in which tree synusia cover at least 10% of the ground. http://www.lasy.gov.pl/dokumenty/in_english/files/" .

:def_Forest_Greece_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Greece ;
    :sourceRef "http://bookshop.europa.eu/is-bin/INTERSHOP.enfinity/WFS/EU-Bookshop-Site/en_GB/-/EUR/ViewPDFFile-OpenPDFFile?FileName=LBNA24300ENC_002.pdf&SKU=LBNA24300ENC_PDF" ;
    :definitionText "(Greece) Forests are characterised by forest trees (high and coppice forests) that produce or are able to produce at least 1 m3 of commercial timber per hectare per year. http://bookshop.europa.eu/is-bin/INTERSHOP.enfinity/WFS/EU-Bookshop-Site/en_GB/-/EUR/ViewPDFFile-OpenPDFFile?FileName=LBNA24300ENC_002.pdf&SKU=LBNA24300ENC_PDF" .

:def_Forest_Guatemala_1996_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Guatemala ;
    dcterms:date "1996"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Guatemala 1996) Native or autochthon ecosystem, intervened or not, regenerated through natural succession or other forestry mechanisms, that does occupy an area greater than 2 ha, characterized by the presence of mature trees of different ages, species and appearance, with one or more layers. \"Ecosistema en donde los árboles son las especies dominantes y permanentes\"(Ley Forestal, Decreto 101-96, capitulo II: Art. 4)." .

:def_Forest_Guatemala_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Guatemala ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Guatemala 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.5 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 30 Min. Tree Height (m) = 2 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" .

:def_Forest_Guatemla_2007_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Guatemla ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Guatemla - 2007?) Cover = 30%; Area = 0.5 ha; Tree height = 5 m. https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Guinea_Bissau_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Guinea_Bissau ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/forestry/fo/country/index.jsp?lang_id=1&geo_id=67" ;
    :definitionText "(Guinea Bissau 2000) Min. crown cover = 10 % http://www.fao.org/forestry/fo/country/index.jsp?lang_id=1&geo_id=67" .

:def_Forest_Guyana_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Guyana ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "https://www.forestry.gov.gy/wp-content/uploads/2016/07/Forests-Act-2009.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Guyana 2009) Forest means an ecosystem dominated by woody plants, consisting of closed forest formations, where trees of various stories sand undergrowth cover a high proportion of the ground; or open forest with continuous vegetation cover in which tree crown cover exceeds 10 percent and includes mangrove forest and any wetlands or open lands within a forest which form an integral part of the ecosystem; forest produce in the ecosystem; and biological, soil and water resources of the ecosystem " .

:def_Forest_Guyana_2011_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Guyana ;
    dcterms:date "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.forestry.gov.gy/Downloads/Guyana_MRVS_Interim_Measures_Report_16_March_2011.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Guyana 2011 KP) In accordance with the Marrakech Accords, Guyana has elected to classify land as forest if it meets the following criteria:  Tree cover of minimum 30%  At a minimum height of 5 m  Over a minimum area of 1 ha. http://www.forestry.gov.gy/Downloads/Guyana_MRVS_Interim_Measures_Report_16_March_2011.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Guyana_2015_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Guyana ;
    dcterms:date "2015"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://redd.unfccc.int/files/guyanas_proposal_for_reference_level_for_redd__-_final_sept_2015.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Guyana 2015) Guyana has elected to classify land as forest if it meets the following criteria: • Tree cover of minimum 30% • Minimum height of 5 m • Minimum area of 1 ha. .It was recommended that based on Guyana’s forest characteristics, where there is largely undisturbed primary forest and the remaining being sustainably managed forests, where trees are predominantly 5 m in height, the minimum threshold for this variable is recommended to be 5m. From a monitoring perspective. The use of the up" .

:def_Forest_Honduras_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Honduras ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Honduras 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 1.0 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 30 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html - Sasaki & Putz 2009 and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Honduras_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Honduras ;
    :definitionText "(Honduras) Terrenos que sostienen una asociación vegetal dominada por árboles o arbustos de cualquier tamaño ya sea que crezcan espontáneamente o que procedan de siembra o plantación, que fueren capaces de producir madera, leña u otros productos forestales, de ejercer influencia sobre el clima, suelos, sobre el régimen de aguas o sobre el medio ambiente en general, o de proveer refugio al ganado y la vida silvestre. (Reglamento General Forestal Titulo I, Capítulo I, Art. 1)" .

:def_Forest_Hungary_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Hungary ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/hungaryaareport_v4fin.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Hungary 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.5 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 30 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = 10 http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/hungaryaareport_v4fin.pdf (2006)" .

:def_Forest_Hungary_2006_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Hungary ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "50.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Hungary 2006) Definition: Forest should be consisted more than 50% of the tree species (listed in the Forest Act) and forest cover is more than 30%. Mezőgazdasági Szakigazgatási Hivatal (MGSZH), 2006. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Hungary_2006_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Hungary ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "50.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1000.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Hungary 2006) Forest land (1000 ha) - With defined tree species, minimum block size 0.5 ha, -Crown cover min. 50% (30% if protection function). Area: all forest where the forest block is at least 0.5 ha (all area which has “forest” cadastral status, plus all area where forest is found) Definition: Forest should be consisted more than 50% of the tree species (listed in the Forest Act) and forest cover is more than 30%. Mezőgazdasági Szakigazgatási Hivatal (MGSZH), 2006. http://www.efi.int/files/" .

:def_Forest_Hungary_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Hungary ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://afoludata.jrc.ec.europa.eu/metaed/project_collection/JRC_54744_Mascaref_Full_Report_for_print.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Hungary 2009 NRI) Crown cover > 30%, tree height > 5m, area > 0.5 ha.. http://afoludata.jrc.ec.europa.eu/metaed/project_collection/JRC_54744_Mascaref_Full_Report_for_print.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Hungary_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Hungary ;
    :areaMin "15.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/forestry/foris/webview/forestry2/index.jsp?siteId=5081&sitetreeId=18927&langId=1&geoId=0" ;
    :definitionText "(Hungary) -By law forest means area covered by woody vegetation with area bigger than 0,15 ha. Other wooded lands not included can be only row of trees, alleys, etc. having no adequate system (ortho-photos, software, etc.) its quantity can be only wrong estimated. http://www.fao.org/forestry/foris/webview/forestry2/index.jsp?siteId=5081&sitetreeId=18927&langId=1&geoId=0" .

:def_Forest_Hungary_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Hungary ;
    :canopyThreshold "15.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.metla.fi/eu/cost/e43/minutes/wg1-min-florence.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Hungary) Forest - National definition based on limited species list & canopy cover limit (15 %), information for other land uses available http://www.metla.fi/eu/cost/e43/minutes/wg1-min-florence.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Iceland_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Iceland ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/msword/initial_report_-_iceland.doc" ;
    :definitionText "(Iceland 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.5 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 10 Min. Tree Height (m) = 2 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/msword/initial_report_-_iceland.doc (2006)" .

:def_Forest_Iceland_2010_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Iceland ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://groa.rala.is/Kortavefsja/ICELAND_NIR_2010.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Iceland 2010 KP) In accordance to the GPG arising from the Kyoto Protocol a country-specific definition of forest has been adopted. The minimal crown cover of forest is 10%, the minimal height 2 m, minimal area 0.5 ha and minimal width 20 m. http://groa.rala.is/Kortavefsja/ICELAND_NIR_2010.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Iceland_2011_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Iceland ;
    dcterms:date "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Iceland 2011)- Forest area is a land with a minimum area of 0.5 ha, with a minimum 10% crown cover, and minimum height of trees of 5 m at maturity in situ. FOREST EUROPE, UNECE and FAO 2011. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Iceland_2011_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Iceland ;
    dcterms:date "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Iceland 2011) National definition: areas with trees higher than 2 m and 10% crown cover are defined as forests in Iceland. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Iceland_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Iceland ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "Eysteinsson <throstur@simnet.is>" ;
    :definitionText "(Iceland) Forest (skogur) - Ecosystems where the dominant organisms are trees. The term includes all organisms, processes and physical components of these ecosystems. Includes scrubland where the dominant \"trees\" (usually the native birch, Betula pubescens) may only reach 1-2 m in height. Source: Latest draft of a new forestry act : Þröstur Eysteinsson throstur@simnet.is" .

:def_Forest_India_1865_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    dcterms:date "1865"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.mtnforum.org/sites/default/files/pub/4946.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(India 1865) forest was first defined in the Indian Forest Act, 1865 as “land covered with trees, brushwood and jungle,” http://www.mtnforum.org/sites/default/files/pub/4946.pdf" .

:def_Forest_India_1996_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    dcterms:date "1996"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://iasc2008.glos.ac.uk/conference%20papers/papers/P/Patnaik_130901.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(India 1996) An extensive are covered by trees and bushes with no agriculture. http://iasc2008.glos.ac.uk/conference%20papers/papers/P/Patnaik_130901.pdf" .

:def_Forest_India_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "Singh <tpsingh@teri.res.in>" ;
    :definitionText "(India 1997) For forest cover assessments - all lands with a tree canopy density of more than 10 percent though they may not be statutorily notified as forest. Thus the forest cover assessments would leave out barren \"forest\" areas but include plantations done outside forest reserves. T P Singh tpsingh@teri.res.in and Forest Survey of India. 1997. The state of Forest Report (Ministry of Environment and Forests. Dehra Dun, India.)" .

:def_Forest_India_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.itto.int/direct/topics/topics_pdf_download/topics_id=39100000&no=1&disp=inline" ;
    :definitionText "(India 2003) The 2003 forest cover analysis by the Forest Survey of India using satellite data, including forests of a defined area of more than 1 ha and 10% of tree canopy cover, http://www.itto.int/direct/topics/topics_pdf_download/topics_id=39100000&no=1&disp=inline" .

:def_Forest_India_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "15.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.05"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(India 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.05 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 15 Min. Tree Height (m) = 2 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html - Sasaki & Putz 2009 and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_India_2006_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.mtnforum.org/sites/default/files/pub/4946.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(India 2006) The Act has defined forest land as land of any description falling within any forest area and includes most types of forests. The Scheduled Tribes and Other Traditional Forest Dwellers (Recognition of Forest Rights) Act, 2006 http://www.mtnforum.org/sites/default/files/pub/4946.pdf" .

:def_Forest_India_2008_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    dcterms:date "2008"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://mospi.nic.in/mospi_new/upload/nad10_2008_karnataka_final.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(India 2008) Forest cover consists of all lands having tree canopy density of more than 10 percent that can be interpreted from satellite data. The resolution and limitations of the sensor are crucial in estimation of area under forest cover. http://mospi.nic.in/mospi_new/upload/nad10_2008_karnataka_final.pdf" .

:def_Forest_India_2017_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    dcterms:date "2017"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "70.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "https://scroll.in/article/868606/hold-the-celebrations-marginal-increase-in-indias-forest-cover-is-masking-massive-deforestation" ;
    :definitionText "(India 2017) Forest cover- any area more than one hectare in size that has more than 10% green canopy. Apart from traditional or natural forests that meet the criteria, this definition also includes plantations like tea and coffee gardens as well as orchards. The report classifies forest cover into three categories on the basis of their density measured in terms of canopy cover – the percentage of green cover on land as seen from satellite images. Dense forests are those where the canopy cover i" .

:def_Forest_India_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://moef.gov.in/nfc/s-git.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(India) Forest cover - All lands, more than one hectare in area, with a tree canopy density of more than 10 percent. Such lands may not be statutorily notified as forest area. http://moef.gov.in/nfc/s-git.pdf" .

:def_Forest_India_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://sudiv.gov.in/PDFFiles%5CNSR%5CNational%20Status%20Report%20(ITTO" ;
    :definitionText "(India) Forest Cover is defined as an area more than 1 ha in extent and having tree canopy density of 10 percent and above. This definition is based on the resolution of digital satellite data (pixel size 23.5m X 23.5m), scale of interpretation (1:50,000) and the technique used for image processing. http://sudiv.gov.in/PDFFiles%5CNSR%5CNational%20Status%20Report%20(ITTO)%20-%2023.9.06%5CCompiled%20Report%5CCompiled%20report%20_F_.pdf" .

:def_Forest_India_nd_005
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.thestatesman.net/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=382252&catid=52" ;
    :definitionText "(India) Forest land is one with standing trees. http://www.thestatesman.net/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=382252&catid=52" .

:def_Forest_Indonesia_1998_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Indonesia ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://europe.mtnforum.org/rs/econfreports/MountainPeopleForestsAndTrees.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Indonesia 1998) an area growing trees which as a whole forms a living natural community and a natural living environment, which is designated by the government as being a forest\" (Nico Smith 1999). http://europe.mtnforum.org/rs/econfreports/MountainPeopleForestsAndTrees.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Indonesia_2002_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Indonesia ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.globalforestwatch.org/common/indonesia/sof.indonesia.english.low.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Indonesia 2002) Land on which trees form the dominant vegetation type. The Indonesian government uses a land use definition of forest in the various land use classes that comprise “Permanent Forest Status” (see below). However, up to 20 percent of Permanent Forest Status land has been deforested. http://www.globalforestwatch.org/common/indonesia/sof.indonesia.english.low.pdf and SaveForest. n.d..Definitions. http://www.freewebs.com/irwantoforester/definition2.html" .

:def_Forest_Indonesia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Indonesia ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.forestcarbonpartnership.org/fcp/sites/forestcarbonpartnership.org/files/Documents/PDF/IFCA_Consolidation_report_REDD_Indonesia_0.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Indonesia KP) - Forest area: 0.05 to 1 ha (Indonesia decided on 0.25 ha)  Potential to reach a minimum height at maturity in situ of 2-5 m (Indonesia decided on 5 m).  Tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level): 10 to 30 % (Indonesia decided on >30%) Under this definition a forest can contain anything from 10% to 100% tree cover; it is only when cover falls below the minimum crown cover that it designated as non-forest. However, if this is only a temporary change, such as for timber harves" .

:def_Forest_Indonesia_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Indonesia ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.environmental-auditing.org/LinkClick.aspx?fileticket=fbx%2FbAIVeFU%3D&tabid=128&mid=568" ;
    :definitionText "(Indonesia KP) An area dominated by a group of trees having height usually more than 5m, with a canopy density of more than 10 percent. http://www.environmental-auditing.org/LinkClick.aspx?fileticket=fbx%2FbAIVeFU%3D&tabid=128&mid=568" .

:def_Forest_Indonesia_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Indonesia ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.25"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.communitycarbonforestry.org/NewPublications/ESP%20article%20CAMERON.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Indonesia KP) The values for the definition of forest have also been given as, minimum land area of 0.25 ha; 30% crown cover and 5m tree height. http://www.communitycarbonforestry.org/NewPublications/ESP%20article%20CAMERON.pdf and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Indonesia_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Indonesia ;
    :sourceRef "http://www2.bonet.co.id/dephut/41-99-1.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Indonesia) A unit of ecosystem in the form of lands comprising biological resources, dominated by trees in their natural forms and environment, which can not be separated each other. http://www2.bonet.co.id/dephut/41-99-1.htm" .

:def_Forest_Indonesia_2004_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Indonesia ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.25"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://redd.unfccc.int/files/national_frel_for_redd__in_indonesia_2015.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Indonesia 2004) As a formal right, forest in this document is defined as “Land spanning more than 0.25 hectares with trees higher than 5 meters at maturity and a canopy cover of more than 30 percent, or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ”. This is the definition of forest stated in the Minister of Forestry Decree No 14/2004 on A/R CDM (MoFor, 2004). The definition of forest used in the MoFor decree was established to meet the requirement of climate change mitigation scheme under CDM a" .

:def_Forest_Indonesia_2015_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Indonesia ;
    dcterms:date "2015"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "6.25"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://redd.unfccc.int/files/national_frel_for_redd__in_indonesia_2015.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Indonesia 2015) In this document, the term “working definition” of forest was used to produce land-cover maps through visual interpretation of satellite images in a scale that minimum area for polygon delineation is 0.25 cm2 at 1: 50,000 of scale which equals to 6.25 ha. http://redd.unfccc.int/files/national_frel_for_redd__in_indonesia_2015.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Iran_1962_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Iran ;
    dcterms:date "1962"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "Zobeiri <zobeiri@nrf.ut.ac.ir>" ;
    :definitionText "(Iran 1962) FOREST LAND: It is an area which comply with one of the following; a-Lands in which the forest characteristries like seedlings or sprouts or stumps collectively or sparsely exist, provided before the Forest Nationalization (January 1962), they were not under fallow or cultivation of annuals. b-Lands in which natural trees and shrubs sparsely exist, and their crown cover is 1-5% \"M.Zobeiri\" zobeiri@nrf.ut.ac.ir" .

:def_Forest_Iran_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Iran ;
    :sourceRef "http://neda.net/faro/forestry1.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Iran) A vegetation cover where trees are its main elements. They are divided into various types according to superficial and inner situation, and dominated by especial ecological conditions in respect of flora, fauna, climatic and edaphic factors. http://neda.net/faro/forestry1.htm" .

:def_Forest_Iran_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Iran ;
    :sourceRef "Zobeiri <zobeiri@nrf.ut.ac.ir>" ;
    :definitionText "(Iran) FOREST: It is a land mainly covered by trees, shrubs and other woody plants. Forest density is classified as follow: 1 Very dense: crown cover of woody elements (trees, shrubs) more than 75%, 2 Dense - 50 -75%, 3 Middle dense - 25 -50%, 4 Sparse 5 -25%, 5 Very - 1 - 5% \"M.Zobeiri\" <zobeiri@nrf.ut.ac.ir" .

:def_Forest_Ireland_2002_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Ireland ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "50.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ymparisto.fi/download.asp?contentid=25582&lan=en" ;
    :definitionText "(Ireland 2002) There are no legal definitions for the terms forest and forestry in Ireland. A practical definition for forest is an area of at least 0.5 ha (sometimes, in the case of broadleaves, 0.2 ha) with a minimum width of 40 m over no more than two-thirds of its length, with at least 50% canopy cover by trees. http://www.ymparisto.fi/download.asp?contentid=25582&lan=en" .

:def_Forest_Ireland_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Ireland ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/x-zip-compressed/fin_ir_report_22dec.zip" ;
    :definitionText "(Ireland 2006 KP) Use Min. Area (ha) = 0.1 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 20 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/x-zip-compressed/fin_ir_report_22dec.zip. (2006).Young natural stands and all plantations that have yet to reach a crown density of 20 percent or a tree height of 5 metres are included under forest. Areas normally forming part of the forest area that are temporarily un-stocked as a res" .

:def_Forest_Ireland_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Ireland ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://afoludata.jrc.ec.europa.eu/metaed/project_collection/JRC_54744_Mascaref_Full_Report_for_print.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Ireland 2009 NIR and NFI) Crown cover > 20%, tree height > 5m, area > 0.1 ha, width > 20 m. http://afoludata.jrc.ec.europa.eu/metaed/project_collection/JRC_54744_Mascaref_Full_Report_for_print.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Ireland_2010_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Ireland ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Ireland 2010) To define area as a forest it has to pass these minimum requirements: - tree crown cover: 10%- land area: 0.5 ha - tree height: 2 m. Further IFI has added practical requirements that are in accordance to international definitions: - minimum width of forest: 20 m - maximum permanent gap in forest. 0.5 ha. Tomppo E., Gschwantner T., Lawrence M., 2010. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Isle_of_Man_1984_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Isle_of_Man ;
    dcterms:date "1984"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "daff@gov.im" ;
    :definitionText "(Isle of Man 1984) - The term \"forest\" only appears in the Forestry Act 1984, where it is not defined. The context of its usage means a large woodland. \"IOM Gov DAFF\" <daff@gov.im" .

:def_Forest_Israel_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Israel ;
    :sourceRef "GilS@kkl.org.il" ;
    :definitionText "(Israel) Forest Land: 1. Land covered with forest. From: GilS@kkl.org.il" .

:def_Forest_Israel_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Israel ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "GilS@kkl.org.il" ;
    :definitionText "(Israel) Forest: A vegetation formation in which trees have more than 10% crown cover. From: GilS@kkl.org.il" .

:def_Forest_Italy_1988_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Italy ;
    dcterms:date "1988"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "Lorenzo Ciccarese <ciccarese@anpa.it>" ;
    :definitionText "(Italy 1988) A wooded land with an area =0,2 Ha; with a canopy width =20m; with a cover closure =20% MAF, Ministero dell'Agricoltura e delle Foreste (1988). Inventario Forestale Nazionale 1985. Istituto Sperimentale per l'Assessamento forestale e per l'Alpicoltura. 2 vols. Rome. Lorenzo Ciccarese ciccarese@anpa.it" .

:def_Forest_Italy_1998_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Italy ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "Lorenzo Ciccarese <ciccarese@anpa.it>" ;
    :definitionText "(Italy 1998) An area (min. area: 2000 m2; min. cover: 20%; min. width: 20 m.) having one (or more) of these features: aimed to provide wooden products and non-wooden (commonly considered-forest) products, such as berries, mushrooms, resins, etc; covered with woods or shrubs, having direct and indirect functions in protecting human activities from disturbances; with tree and shrub crown cover, which preservation is needed for naturalistic, scenic and recreational purposes. MAF, Ministero dell'Agr" .

:def_Forest_Italy_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Italy ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/aa-report-notificato.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Italy 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.5 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 10 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/aa-report-notificato.pdf (2006)" .

:def_Forest_Italy_2007_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Italy ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Italy 2007) National definition: forest is a land covered by trees more than 2000 m2, 20% of canopy, with a minimun width of 20 m. Ministero Delle Politiche Agricole, Alimentari e Forestali Corpo Forestale Dello Stato. CRA (Istituto Sperimentale per l’Assestamento Forestale e per l’Alpicoltura), 2007. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Italy_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Italy ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://afoludata.jrc.ec.europa.eu/metaed/project_collection/JRC_54744_Mascaref_Full_Report_for_print.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Italy 2009 NIR and NFI) Crown cover > 10%, tree height > 5m, area > 0.5 ha. http://afoludata.jrc.ec.europa.eu/metaed/project_collection/JRC_54744_Mascaref_Full_Report_for_print.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Jamaica_1987_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Jamaica ;
    dcterms:date "1987"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/ag/agl/agll/landuse/clsys/Jamaica.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Jamaica 1987) Forest stands including both coniferous (softwood) and broad leaf evergreens. Crown closure must equal or exceed 75%. Source: Land use map 1983/1984, 1:500 000, Rural Physical planning division, Ministry of Agriculture, Hope Gardens, Kingston 6, Jamaica, 03/1987 http://www.fao.org/ag/agl/agll/landuse/clsys/Jamaica.htm" .

:def_Forest_Jamaica_1992_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Jamaica ;
    dcterms:date "1992"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "75.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "7.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "4.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "forestman@cwjamaica.com" ;
    :definitionText "(Jamaica 1992) Jamaica has several definitions depending on remote sensing source used. Using the largest scale definition, forest land appears to be areas covered with trees at least 5-7 m tall, with a crown closure of 75% and a minimum area of 4 ha. See: 1) Land use classification 1:100 000 scale (National level, Landsat TM) and 1:15 000 scale (Watershed level, aerial photographs 1:15 000 and biophysical inventory): STRATES100-15.CDR; 2) Definition of land use types 1:100 000 scale: STRATES100" .

:def_Forest_Japan_academic_definition_forest_land_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Japan_academic_definition_forest_land ;
    :sourceRef "Yukichi Konohira <Konohira@cc.tuat.ac.jp>" ;
    :definitionText "(Japan - academic definition - forest land) A place covered by a group of trees with more or less height, density, and extent. Yukichi Konohira <Konohira@cc.tuat.ac.jp" .

:def_Forest_Japan_academic_definition_forest_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Japan_academic_definition_forest ;
    :sourceRef "Yukichi Konohira <Konohira@cc.tuat.ac.jp>" ;
    :definitionText "(Japan - academic definition - forest) Both trees growing in a group and the land where they stand. Yukichi Konohira <Konohira@cc.tuat.ac.jp" .

:def_Forest_Japan_1951_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Japan ;
    dcterms:date "1951"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.iufro.org/download/file/5574/4510/61300-jundola01_pdf/" ;
    :definitionText "(Japan 1951) A forest is a group of living trees or bamboos and the land on which the group of trees or bamboos is growing. The exception is land with trees that are managed for agriculture, residence, or similar purposes. http://www.iufro.org/download/file/5574/4510/61300-jundola01_pdf/" .

:def_Forest_Japan_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Japan ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.3"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fs.fed.us/research/sustain/2003SustainabilityReport/documents/SustainableForests.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Japan 2003) Minimum area = 0.3 ha, minimum tree crown cover = 30%, minimum tree height = 5 m. http://www.fs.fed.us/research/sustain/2003SustainabilityReport/documents/SustainableForests.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Japan_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Japan ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "Masahiro Amano <masahiro@ss.ffpri.affrc.go.jp>" ;
    :definitionText "(Japan) Forest: In addition to Forest Row, forestland is with tree crown cover of more than 30 percent. Definition of Forest Resource Inventory Book, Forest Agency. From: Masahiro Amano <masahiro@ss.ffpri.affrc.go.jp." .

:def_Forest_Japan_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Japan ;
    :sourceRef "Yukichi Konohira <Konohira@cc.tuat.ac.jp>" ;
    :definitionText "(Japan) Socially common definition - forest / forest land : a land where trees are growing in a group or an area of a certain size with dense tree cover. Yukichi Konohira <Konohira@cc.tuat.ac.jp" .

:def_Forest_Kenya_1965_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Kenya ;
    dcterms:date "1965"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.kalro.org:8080/repository/bitstream/0/5057/1/REPRINT%20COLLECTION%2063%20Split%2035.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Kenya 1965?) A closed stand of trees of one or more storeys, with an interlaced upper canopy, rising to 7·5-40 m or more in height. The ground cover is dominated by herbs and shrubs, and lianes and epiphytes are characteristic. Dwarf forests are as defined but rise to less than 7·5 m in height. http://www.kalro.org:8080/repository/bitstream/0/5057/1/REPRINT%20COLLECTION%2063%20Split%2035.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Kenya_1995_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Kenya ;
    dcterms:date "1995"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "40.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cmsdata.iucn.org/downloads/forestcover.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Kenya 1995) Kenya’s woody vegetation includes forests, woodlands, bushland and wooded grasslands. Wass (1995) defines forests as continuous stands of trees at least 10 meters tall, with interlocking crowns; woodlands as open stands of trees, at least 8 meters tall, with a canopy cover of 40% or more with the field layer usually dominated by grasses; bushlands as open stands of bushes and climbers, usually between 3 and 7 meters tall with a canopy cover of 40% or more and wooded grasslands as la" .

:def_Forest_Kenya_2005_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Kenya ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fankenya.org/downloads/ForestsAct2005.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Kenya 2005) “forests” refers to any land containing a vegetation association dominated by trees of any size, whether exploitable or not, capable of producing wood or other products, potentially capable of influencing climate, exercising an influence on the soil, water regime, and providing habitat for wildlife, and includes woodlands; “forest area” means any land declared to be a forest land under this Act. http://www.fankenya.org/downloads/ForestsAct2005.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Kenya_2005_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Kenya ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://formin.finland.fi/public/download.aspx?ID=15959&GUID=%7B88EFD0B8-9F47-4528-A24F-66DDE0CFE370%7D" ;
    :definitionText "(Kenya 2005) Mini-forest refers to a crop of trees occupying less than 10 ha of land http://formin.finland.fi/public/download.aspx?ID=15959&GUID=%7B88EFD0B8-9F47-4528-A24F-66DDE0CFE370%7D" .

:def_Forest_Kenya_2015_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Kenya ;
    dcterms:date "2015"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.kenyaforestservice.org/documents/ForestConservationandManagementActNo34of2016.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Kenya 2015) woody vegetation growing in close proximity in an area of over 0.5 of a hectares including a forest in the process of establishment, woodlands, thickets; http://www.kenyaforestservice.org/documents/ForestConservationandManagementActNo34of2016.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Kenya_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Kenya ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Kenya 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.1 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 30 Min. Tree Height (m) = 2 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html - Sasaki & Putz 2009 and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Kenya_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Kenya ;
    :canopyThreshold "40.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Kenya) Min. av. height 2 m, 40% canopy cover. Note these figures vary by vegetation type. The most liberal thresholds are shown here. Source: ECE-FAO Partnership Programme: Kenya Workshop on Forestry Statistics. Appendix 6." .

:def_Forest_Kirbati_2010_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Kirbati ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.sprep.org/att/irc/ecopies/countries/kiribati/115.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Kirbati 2010) At the regional level forest is defined as; ‘trees that have a certain size of canopy, they are not agricultural and are not located in urban areas’. http://www.sprep.org/att/irc/ecopies/countries/kiribati/115.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Kiribati_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Kiribati ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/forestry/fo/country/index.jsp?lang_id=1&geo_id=114" ;
    :definitionText "(Kiribati) Forest and woody vegetation - Intensive agroforestry practices system based on coconut breadfruit, bananas, pandanus and native figs. The system tends to represent natural forest since the trees occur spontaneously. It includes coastal vegetation, inland forest and wetlands. http://www.fao.org/forestry/fo/country/index.jsp?lang_id=1&geo_id=114" .

:def_Forest_Korea_Republic_of_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Korea_Republic_of ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Korea- Republic of 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.5 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 10 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Kosovo_2010_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Kosovo ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Kosovo 2010) - Land with tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 10% and area of more than 0.5 ha. The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 m at maturity in situ. Gashi F., 2010. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Kyrgyzstan_New_National_Forest_Inventory_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Kyrgyzstan_New_National_Forest_Inventory ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "Irina Yunusova <irina@lesic.elcat.kg>" ;
    :definitionText "(Kyrgyzstan - New National Forest Inventory) Forest -- Vegetation existing of forest species with the objective of timber production and various protective and other functions. The horizontal forest area has a minimum crown cover density of 20%, a minimum width of 25 meters and a minimum height of 2.0 meters. Source: Irina Yunusova irina@lesic.elcat.kg" .

:def_Forest_Kyrgyzstan_1999_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Kyrgyzstan ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "Irina Yunusova <irina@lesic.elcat.kg>" ;
    :definitionText "(Kyrgyzstan 1999)- New Forest Code - One of the main types of vegetation on the Earth, comprising trees, shrubs, grassland and other plants, including animals and microorganisms, which are biologically interrelated in their evolution and exert influence on one another and the environment. Forest soil is an integral part of the forest whole. Forest is an integral and a very important component of biosphere and geographic landscape. It plays an important role in maintaining the hydrological regime" .

:def_Forest_Kyrgyzstan_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Kyrgyzstan ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://kirfor.ucentralasia.org/bitcache/833d526f022370574cea70a841a6474fef581009?vid=610&disposition=attachment&op=download" ;
    :definitionText "(Kyrgyzstan 2000) Forest in strict sense (conifer/broadleaf/mixed - see definitions at 3.3) is defined as vegetation consisting of forest species (according to the species list in annex 2) with the objective of timber production and various protection and other functions. The horizontal forest area has a minimum crown cover density of 20 % (see Figure 2-4, Figure 2-5 and Figure 2-6), a minimum width of 25 metres and a minimum height of 2.0 metres. In case of forest cultures no minimum height has" .

:def_Forest_Kyrgyzstan_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Kyrgyzstan ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Kyrgyzstan 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.5 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 20 Min. Tree Height (m) = 3 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Kyrgyzstan_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Kyrgyzstan ;
    :sourceRef "Irina Yunusova <irina@lesic.elcat.kg>" ;
    :definitionText "(Kyrgyzstan) - Forest -One of the main types of vegetation, comprised of the concomitance (?) of trees, shrub, grass and other plants, also including animals and microorganisms , biologically interrelated in their development and influencing each other and environment. At the same time forest is a very important part of the biosphere and an element of geographical landscape. Forest is a raw material source. Source: Irina Yunusova <irina@lesic.elcat.kg" .

:def_Forest_Lao_1992_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Lao ;
    dcterms:date "1992"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.forestcarbonpartnership.org/fcp/sites/forestcarbonpartnership.org/files/Documents/PDF/Sep2010/Final_R-PPdraft3-09-10_submission_with_annexes.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Lao 1992) Forests – areas suitable for forest production and having a tree cover with a crown density of at least 20%, and supporting trees with a dbh more than 10cm, covering at least 0.5 ha (LSFP 92). http://www.forestcarbonpartnership.org/fcp/sites/forestcarbonpartnership.org/files/Documents/PDF/Sep2010/Final_R-PPdraft3-09-10_submission_with_annexes.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Lao_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Lao ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/forestry/fo/country/index.jsp?lang_id=1&geo_id=39" ;
    :definitionText "(Lao 2000) Min. Cover = 20% http://www.fao.org/forestry/fo/country/index.jsp?lang_id=1&geo_id=39" .

:def_Forest_Lao_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Lao ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Lao 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.5 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 20 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns. Excludes palms and bamboos http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Lao_2011_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Lao ;
    dcterms:date "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.recoftc.org/site/uploads/content/pdf/ASFN%20v10%20-web%20version%20(compressed" ;
    :definitionText "(Lao 2011) Lao PDR uses a definition of forest cover of 20% canopy density, which is different from the definition used by FAO (personal communication, Mr. Khamseneas, Planning Division, Department of Forestry (DoF). February 2011). http://www.recoftc.org/site/uploads/content/pdf/ASFN%20v10%20-web%20version%20(compressed)_139.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Lao_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Lao ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dof.maf.gov.la/docs/Lao_FIP_Investment%20Plan%20Master_2nd%20draft-for-public%20review.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Lao KP) GOL has already submitted a forest definition to UNFCCC (minimum 20% forest cover, minimum area 0.5 ha, minimum tree height 5 m, and palm trees and bamboo considered as non-forest). http://www.dof.maf.gov.la/docs/Lao_FIP_Investment%20Plan%20Master_2nd%20draft-for-public%20review.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Lao_2015_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Lao ;
    dcterms:date "2015"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.uncclearn.org/sites/default/files/inventory/fao13102015_4.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Lao 2015) In Lao PDR forests are defined as areas of at least 0.5 ha in size, with crown cover above 20%; with trees that will reach higher than 5 meters when mature. Dense forests have crown cover greater than 70%, medium-stocked between 40% and 70% and degraded forests have crown cover between 20% and 40% http://www.uncclearn.org/sites/default/files/inventory/fao13102015_4.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Latvia_1937_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Latvia ;
    dcterms:date "1937"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.iufro.org/download/file/5574/4510/61300-jundola01_pdf/" ;
    :definitionText "(Latvia 1937 ) The Law on Forest Protection of Oct. 14, 1937 defined the forest by the following traits: i) land areas overgrown by forest ; ii) meadows, pastureland and other non-cultivated lands overgrown by forest, stocked to no less than a half of full density and encircled by forest; iii) felling coupes, irrespective of the situation with forest regeneration there; iv) all lands, irrespective of the tree age and density, where the owner has ceased other management activities to let the fore" .

:def_Forest_Latvia_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Latvia ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/docrep/article/WFC/XII/0504-C3.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Latvia 2000) According to the Forest Law of the Republic of Latvia adopted in 2000 (Item 2, Paragraph 3, Section 1) Item 1 states: \"The forest is an ecosystem in all its stages of development. Trees with the height of at least seven metre prevail, and the present or potential tree crown cover accounts for at least 20% of the forest stand area.\" http://www.fao.org/docrep/article/WFC/XII/0504-C3.htm" .

:def_Forest_Latvia_2000_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Latvia ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "7.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Latvia 2000) Forest (area>0.1 ha, potential height of trees>7 m, present or potential projection of crowns >20%). Latvijas Valsts mezi, 2000. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Latvia_2001_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Latvia ;
    dcterms:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.iufro.org/download/file/5574/4510/61300-jundola01_pdf/" ;
    :definitionText "(Latvia 2001) “forest” is defined as “an ecosystem in all its development stages, dominated by trees, the height of which in the particular forest site may reach at least seven metres, and the present or potential tree crown cover accounts for at least 20% of the stand area.” http://www.iufro.org/download/file/5574/4510/61300-jundola01_pdf/" .

:def_Forest_Latvia_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Latvia ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/latvia_aa_report__unfccc.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Latvia 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.1 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 20 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/latvia_aa_report__unfccc.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Latvia_2007_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Latvia ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://circa.europa.eu/Public/irc/dsis/pip/library?l=/environmental_expenditur/country_studies/projects_awarded_2005/lv_296_forestpdf/_EN_1.0_&a=d" ;
    :definitionText "(Latvia 2007) Forest is an ecosystem in all stages of its development, dominated by trees the height of which at the particular location may reach at least seven meters and the present or potential projection of the crown of which is at least 20 per cent of the area occupied by the forest stand. The following shall not be regarded as forest: Areas separate from forests, covered with trees, the size of which does not exceed 0.1 ha; Rows of trees of artificial or natural origin, the width of which" .

:def_Forest_Latvia_2007_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Latvia ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://circa.europa.eu/Public/irc/dsis/pip/library?l=/environmental_expenditur/country_studies/projects_awarded_2005/lv_296_forestpdf/_EN_1.0_&a=d" ;
    :definitionText "(Latvia 2007) Forestland is land covered by forest, land under forest infrastructure facilities, as well as adjacent overflowing clearings, marshes and glades. http://circa.europa.eu/Public/irc/dsis/pip/library?l=/environmental_expenditur/country_studies/projects_awarded_2005/lv_296_forestpdf/_EN_1.0_&a=d" .

