    :definitionText "(Lithuania 2013) - Area (ha) 0.1; Tree crown cover (%) 30; Tree height (m) 5. http://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32013D0529" .

:def_Forest_Lithuania_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Lithuania ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://sapiens.revues.org/734" ;
    :definitionText "(Lithuania) forest can also be defined as “at least 0.1 ha area grown-up with trees the height of which reaches 5 m or more under natural conditions, as well as thinned out or even having lost the vegetation naturally or because of human activities” (Forest act of Republic of Lithuania). http://sapiens.revues.org/734" .

:def_Forest_Luxembourg_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Luxembourg ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Luxembourg 2003) Land with tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 10% and area of more than 0.5 ha. The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 m at maturity in situ. Le gouvernement du Grand Duchè du Luxembourg, 2003. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" .

