    :sourceRef "http://afoludata.jrc.ec.europa.eu/metaed/project_collection/JRC_54744_Mascaref_Full_Report_for_print.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Luxembourg 2009 NIR and NFI) Crown cover > 10%, tree height > 5m, area > 0.5 ha. http://afoludata.jrc.ec.europa.eu/metaed/project_collection/JRC_54744_Mascaref_Full_Report_for_print.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Macedonia_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Macedonia ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.8094"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.foper.org/download/alumni/todorov_thesis.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Macedonia 1997) Forest, as defined in this law, is land with forest types of trees and bushes, forest moor lands and meadows, forest roads, forest nurseries and other areas closely related to forests. As defined in this Law, alleys, plantations with fast-growing types of trees, parks with populated areas, field protection belts, protective vegetation in the coastal belts of the water flows outside from the forests, isolated groups of forest trees on area of maximum 2 acres, and border trees bet" .

