:def_Forest_Montenegro_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Montenegro ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.05"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.unece.org/fileadmin/DAM/publications/timber/QL_SoEF_Montenegro_final.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Montenegro 2000) Forest land definition based on the 2000 Forest law: “A forest relates to any area larger than 0.05 ha, covered with forest trees, having a protective function, and intended for forest production or it has special purpose, no matter of tree cover and size (high forest, copice forests and other types of forest vegetation such as shrubs, shrubberies and maquis).” Also forest bare land is part of the forest land according to that definition. http://www.unece.org/fileadmin/DAM/publ" .

:def_Forest_Morocco_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Morocco ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "25.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Morocco 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 1.0 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 25 Min. Tree Height (m) = 2 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html - Sasaki & Putz 2009 and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Morocco_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Morocco ;
    :areaMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "m.ellatifi@ellatifi.8m.com" ;
    :definitionText "(Morocco) Forest (Arabic : Ghabah, French : Foret, Spanish : Bosque, Berber : ‘Ari) - Piece of land covered a vegetation in which trees(not only fruit trees) are predominant(over 50%), and with at least 3 ha of continuously forested area, and with a tree crown cover equal or superior to 20%. Mohammed Ellatifi, m.ellatifi@ellatifi.8m.com" .

:def_Forest_Mozambique_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Mozambique ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "25.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Mozambique 1997) - High forest 18 m, low forest < 18 m. Canopy cover 25 %. (Trevett 1997)" .

:def_Forest_Mozambique_2007_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Mozambique ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Mozambique 2007) Cover = 30%; Area = 1 ha; tree height = 5 m. https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Myanmar_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Myanmar ;
