    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Myanmar 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 1 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 20 Min. Tree Height (m) = 2 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html." .

:def_Forest_Myanmar_2007_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Myanmar ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Myanmar 2007?) Cover = 10%; Area = 0.1 ha; Tree height = 2 m. https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Namibia_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Namibia ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "chakanga@forestry.met.gov.na" ;
    :definitionText "(Namibia 1997) Forest = areas with tree height 5 m, Savanna/shrub = areas with tree height <5 m. Canopy cover 20%. Moses Chakanga. chakanga@forestry.met.gov.na and (Trevett 1997)" .

:def_Forest_Namibia_2011_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Namibia ;
    dcterms:date "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "15.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.mawf.gov.na/Documents/Forest%20Research%20Strategy.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Namibia 2011 KP) - a general definition of what constitutes a forest is a stand of a minimum size of 0.5 ha, a minimum height of 5 m and a crown cover of 15 % or more. http://www.mawf.gov.na/Documents/Forest%20Research%20Strategy.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Nepal_1964_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Nepal ;
    dcterms:date "1964"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "50.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://rmportal.net/tools/biodiversity-support-program/cbnfm/USAID-BDB-cd-2-data/pnabb308-nepal.pdf/attachment_download/file" ;
    :definitionText "(Nepal 1964 &1977) Crown cover greater than 50 percent. Wallace, Michael B. 1988. Forest degradation in Nepal: Institutional context and policy alternatives. Research Report Series No. 6. 46 p. http://rmportal.net/tools/biodiversity-support-program/cbnfm/USAID-BDB-cd-2-data/pnabb308-nepal.pdf/attachment_download/file" .

:def_Forest_Nepal_1993_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Nepal ;
    dcterms:date "1993"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.biodiv-nepal.gov.np/dofchapter.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Nepal 1993) An area fully or partly covered by trees (Forest Act 1993). Krishna H Gautam <khg13@student.canterbury.ac.nz and. http://www.biodiv-nepal.gov.np/dofchapter.html and http://www.recoftc.org/site/fileadmin/docs/Country_profile/forest_act_combined.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Nepal_1999_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Nepal ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://eprints.usq.edu.au/568/1/Livelihood_Paper-Final.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Nepal 1999) Forest is defined as the land with a forest cover, i.e. with trees whose crown cover more than 10 percent of the area and not used primarily for the purpose other than forestry and shrub is same as forest but well defined stem can not be found (MFSC, 1999) http://eprints.usq.edu.au/568/1/Livelihood_Paper-Final.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Nepal_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Nepal ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/forestry/fo/country/index.jsp?lang_id=1&geo_id=35" ;
    :definitionText "(Nepal 2000) Crown Cover 10%. http://www.fao.org/forestry/fo/country/index.jsp?lang_id=1&geo_id=35 . Wallace (1988) also indicates a 50% threshold for crown cover." .

:def_Forest_Netherlands_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Netherlands ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Netherlands 1997) Land areas of 0.5 ha and more with a width of at least 30 m that are covered with trees or brushes; with a at maturity, a crown closure of 20% and over, the crown closure may (temporary) be lower than this figure because of final fellings for example; the tree and brush species should be able to form forests. (European Communities 1997b - p. 727)." .

:def_Forest_Netherlands_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Netherlands ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Netherlands 2006) - Land with tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 10 % and area of more than 0.5 ha. The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 m at maturity in situ. Landbouw, natuur en Voedselkwaliteit, 2006. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Netherlands_2006_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Netherlands ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Netherlands 2006) National definition: Under forest is normally closed forests with a mean crown projection of less than 60%. There is no longer any old natural forest present in the Netherlands, and virtually all forest is planted. Only in some heaths and marshes is there any spontaneous natural regeneration. About 7% of forest area is such naturally regenerating young forest. Landbouw, natuur en Voedselkwaliteit, 2006. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical" .

:def_Forest_Netherlands_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Netherlands ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://afoludata.jrc.ec.europa.eu/metaed/project_collection/JRC_54744_Mascaref_Full_Report_for_print.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Netherlands 2009 NIR and NFI) Crown cover > 20%, tree height > 5m, area > 0.5 ha, width > 30 m. http://afoludata.jrc.ec.europa.eu/metaed/project_collection/JRC_54744_Mascaref_Full_Report_for_print.pdf" .

:def_Forest_New_Zealand_1998_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :New_Zealand ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "6.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(New Zealand 1998) - A tree-covered area greater than 5 hectares with an average canopy height of at least 6 metres and a minimum 20 percent tree crown coverage. In \"closed forests\" the trees occur in single or multiple stories with crowns interlocking.From: Indigenous Forest Policy (New Zealand Institute of Forestry, July 1998)" .

:def_Forest_New_Zealand_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :New_Zealand ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "6.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fs.fed.us/research/sustain/2003SustainabilityReport/documents/SustainableForests.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(New Zealand 2003) Minimum area = 0.5 ha, minimum tree crown cover =20%, minimum tree height = 6 m. http://www.fs.fed.us/research/sustain/2003SustainabilityReport/documents/SustainableForests.pdf" .

:def_Forest_New_Zealand_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :New_Zealand ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/application/pdf/new_zealands_initial_report_under_the_kyoto_protocol.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(New Zealand 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 1 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 30 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/application/pdf/new_zealands_initial_report_under_the_kyoto_protocol.pdf (2006)" .

:def_Forest_New_Zealand_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :New_Zealand ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.climatechange.govt.nz/glossary.html#f" ;
    :definitionText "(New Zealand KP) Under New Zealand’s definition, forest is a minimum area of land of 1.0 hectares with tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 30 per cent with trees with the potential to reach a minimum height of 5 metres at maturity in situ. Tree cover less than 30 metres wide is excluded. http://www.climatechange.govt.nz/glossary.html#f" .

:def_Forest_Nicaragua_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Nicaragua ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "4.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Nicaragua 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 1.0 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 20 Min. Tree Height (m) = 4 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html - Sasaki & Putz 2009 and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Nicaragua_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Nicaragua ;
    :sourceRef "Harrie <harnic@ibw.com.ni>" ;
    :definitionText "(Nicaragua) Bosque - Draft -Ecosistema con un mínimo de un 25% de copas de árboles y/o bambú y palmáceas, asociadas generalmente a una fauna silvestre y condiciones de suelos naturales. www.nicarao.org.ni/ja (see Borrador de la ley, CAPITULO II DEFINICIONES) Harrie harnic@ibw.com.ni" .

:def_Forest_Niger_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Niger ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "4.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Niger 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 1.0 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 30 Min. Tree Height (m) = 4 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html - Sasaki & Putz 2009 and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Niger_2011_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Niger ;
    dcterms:date "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "4.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "https://s3.amazonaws.com/CCBA/Projects/Niger_Acacia_Senegal_Plantation_Project/CDM_Niger_Acacia_Senegal_Plantation_Project_PDD.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Niger 2011 KP) The Nigerien Designated National Authority (DNA) fixed the following values for afforestation and reforestation activities in the framework of the CDM. Minimum tree crown cover: 30 percents Minimum land area: 1 hectare Minimum tree height at maturity: 4 meters. https://s3.amazonaws.com/CCBA/Projects/Niger_Acacia_Senegal_Plantation_Project/CDM_Niger_Acacia_Senegal_Plantation_Project_PDD.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Nigeria_2005_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Nigeria ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.redd-monitor.org/2009/09/08/redd-will-fail-with-the-current-definition-of-forest/" ;
    :definitionText "(Nigeria 2005) Forest in terms of its resources from a research conducted in the forest communities of Cross Rivers State of Nigeria in 2005 which was sponsored by United States Agency for International Development (USAID). “Forest” means a land area covered by trees and other plant species and inhabited by animal species in its natural state or which could be State Forest Reserve, Community Forest, Private Forest or Forest designated as World Heritage, managed or manageable or exploited by huma" .

:def_Forest_Northern_Mariana_Islands_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Northern_Mariana_Islands ;
    :sourceRef "Estanislao Villagomez <stanvill@gtepacifica.net>" ;
    :definitionText "(Northern Mariana Islands) Forest - Natural or man-made group of trees (diverse species) growing within a minimum area of 100 sq. ft. Source: Estanislao Villagomez stanvill@gtepacifica.net Division of Agriculture." .

:def_Forest_Northern_Mariana_Islands_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Northern_Mariana_Islands ;
    :sourceRef "Estanislao Villagomez <stanvill@gtepacifica.net>" ;
    :definitionText "(Northern Mariana Islands) Forestland - Natural or managed area covered with diverse tree species reserved for dual purposes benefiting mankind, wildlife and ecosystem as a whole. Source: Estanislao Villagomez stanvill@gtepacifica.net Division of Agriculture." .

:def_Forest_Norway_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Norway ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/x-zip-compressed/nor_ir_report_22dec.zip" ;
    :definitionText "(Norway 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.5 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 10 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/x-zip-compressed/nor_ir_report_22dec.zip (2006)" .

:def_Forest_Norway_2010_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Norway ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.klif.no/publikasjoner/2639/ta2639.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Norway 2010) Forest land is defined according to the Global Forest Resources Assessment (FRA) 2004.Forest land is land with tree crown cover of more than 10 per cent and area of more than 0.5 ha. The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 m at maturity in situ. No minimum width for Forest land is considered in the Norwegian inventory causing a small discrepancy according to the definition in FRA 2004. http://www.klif.no/publikasjoner/2639/ta2639.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Pakistan_1953_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Pakistan ;
    dcterms:date "1953"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Pakistan 1953) Forest - A plant community predominantly of trees and other woody vegetation, usually with a closed canopy. Definition adopted from the British Commonwealth Forest Terminology Part-I, 1953. Source: Mumtaz Ahmad, Section Forest Officer, Pakistan Min. of Environment, Local Government, and Rural Development" .

:def_Forest_Pakistan_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Pakistan ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.05"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Pakistan 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.05 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 30 Min. Tree Height (m) = 3 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" .

:def_Forest_Pakistan_2007_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Pakistan ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.05"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.intercooperation.org.pk/uploads/CDM-FINAL%20report.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Pakistan 2007) Pakistan is an area comprising not less than 0.05 ha with tree crown cover of more than 30% with trees with the potential to reach a minimum height of 3 meters. http://www.intercooperation.org.pk/uploads/CDM-FINAL%20report.pdf and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Panama_1992_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Panama ;
    dcterms:date "1992"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Panama 1992) \"Cobertura Boscosa\" se definieron dos dases, la piimera como: a) \"Cobertura Boscosa poco Intervenida\" la cual corresponds a una superficie densamente cubierta por copas de una gran cantidad de arboles, independientemente del tipo de bosque y/o especies forestales que pudieran encontrarse; y una segunda categoria definida como: b) \"Cobertura Boscosa Fuertemente Intervenida\", la cual corresponds a superfides boscosas en donde la cobertura de copas fluctúa entre 45% y 60% del terreno," .

:def_Forest_Panama_1992_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Panama ;
    dcterms:date "1992"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Panama 1992) bosque - Vegetacíon dominante compuesta de árboles leñosos, que se presentan como primarios y que ban alcanzado su máximo desarroho, sobre una localización particular. Source: Informe de Cobertura Boscosa 1992. Junio 1995. Republic of Panama, Instituto Nacional de Recursos Naturales Renovables, Direccion Nacional de Cuencsa Hidrograficas" .

:def_Forest_Panama_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Panama ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Panama 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 1.0 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 30 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html - Sasaki & Putz 2009 and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Papua_New_Guinea_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Papua_New_Guinea ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "100.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Papua New Guinea) Forest - Natural communities of flora (trees) and fauna (birds, animals) in a natural setting. Forest has a crown closure of 10% and above as opposed to non-forest and an area of more than 100 hectares as being the standard. Forest can imply both natural forest and plantations but more so the former (natural). Vitus Ambia, Papua New Guinea Forest Authority." .

:def_Forest_Papua_New_Guinea_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Papua_New_Guinea ;
    :canopyThreshold "80.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Papua New Guinea) Forest Land - Land that has forest growing on it, be it natural and or plantation forest and irrespective of its exploitative capability. In PNG over 80% of the land is customarily owned and the State can only plan and designate areas for forest exploitation and other use. The final decision as to whether or not the area is exploited rests with the customary land-owners. Vitus Ambia, Papua New Guinea Forest Authority." .

:def_Forest_Paraguay_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Paraguay ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "25.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Paraguay 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.5 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 25 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html - Sasaki & Putz 2009 and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Peru_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Peru ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Peru 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.5 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 30 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html - Sasaki & Putz 2009 and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Peru_2010_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Peru ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.asb.cgiar.org/PDFwebdocs/REALU%20I-Peru%20Report-.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Peru 2010 KP), a forest within the CDM context is defined as “Land with canopy cover of more than 30 per cent of the area and a minimum area of 0.5 ha. Trees must reach a minimum height of 5m at maturity in situ.” http://www.asb.cgiar.org/PDFwebdocs/REALU%20I-Peru%20Report-.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Peru_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Peru ;
    :definitionText "(Peru) - Comunidades vegetales naturales en las que predominan especies leñosas referidas a determinada superficie del suelo, así como las plantaciones forestales. (Ley Forestal y de Fauna Silvestre, Art. 8)" .

:def_Forest_Peru_2014_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Peru ;
    dcterms:date "2014"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.09"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://redd.unfccc.int/files/2015_submission_frel_peru_en.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Peru 2014 FREL) Activity data used for constructing the proposed FREL is based on the following definition of \"forest\" of the National Forest Inventory (MINAM and MINAGRI, 2014.a) taking the minimum area to the technological requirements of a methodology: • Minimum Mapping Unit: 1 Landsat pixel (0.09 hectares); • Minimum tree height at maturity in situ: 5.00 . The Ministry of the Environment chose the third definition for REDD+ reporting purposes taking into consideration the scale of land-use " .

:def_Forest_Peru_2015_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Peru ;
    dcterms:date "2015"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://redd.unfccc.int/files/2015_submission_frel_peru_en.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Peru 2015 – Amazon) Currently being implemented, the National Forest Inventory applies specific forest definitions for the three biomes Costa, Sierra, and the Amazon. In case of the Amazon, the following parameters are used: • Minimum area: 0.50 hectares; • Minimum width: 20.00 m • Minimum tree height at maturity in situ: 5.00 m; • Minimum crown cover: 10%. http://redd.unfccc.int/files/2015_submission_frel_peru_en.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Peru_2015_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Peru ;
    dcterms:date "2015"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://redd.unfccc.int/files/2015_submission_frel_peru_en.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Peru 2015 - CDM) The Peruvian Designated National Authority (DNA) of the Clean Development Mechanism (CDM) reported to the UNFCCC the following definition of “forest”, which is used in the context of afforestation and reforestation project activities under the CDM. • Minimum area: 0.50 hectares; • Minimum tree height at maturity in situ: 5.00 m; • Minimum crown cover: 30%. http://redd.unfccc.int/files/2015_submission_frel_peru_en.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Philippines_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Philippines ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nscb.gov.ph/glossary/AGRI.ASP" ;
    :definitionText "(Philippines 2000) – Refers to land with an area of more than 0.5 hectare and tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 10 percent. The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 meters at maturity in situ. It consists either of closed forest formations where trees of various storeys and undergrowth cover a high proportion of the ground or open forest formations with a continuous vegetation cover in which tree crown cover exceeds 10 percent. Young natural stands and a" .

:def_Forest_Philippines_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Philippines ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Philippines 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.5 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 10 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns Includes palms and bamboos. http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Philippines_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Philippines ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.indigenousclimate.org/index.php?option=com_docman&task=doc_download&gid=85&Itemid=&lang=en" ;
    :definitionText "(Philippines KP) Philippines has adopted the UNFCCC’s definition of forest as “an area of at least half a hectare (5,000 square meters) in size with a 10 per cent stocking level,” meaning, that at least 500 square meters of which should be shaded by trees with a minimum height of five meters. http://www.indigenousclimate.org/index.php?option=com_docman&task=doc_download&gid=85&Itemid=&lang=en" .

:def_Forest_Philippines_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Philippines ;
    :canopyThreshold "60.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.haribon.org.ph/attachments/article/425/Forest%20Resources%20Bill_HB3638%20with%20primer.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Philippines) A forest is best described as an ecosystem wherein trees are the dominant life form, as a community of plants and animals interacting with one another and its physical environment, and as consisting of trees with overlapping crown of 60-100% forest cover, as defined by the United States National Vegetation Classification system (Section 4). http://www.haribon.org.ph/attachments/article/425/Forest%20Resources%20Bill_HB3638%20with%20primer.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Philippines_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Philippines ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nscb.gov.ph/ru12/DEFINE/DEF-ENV.HTM" ;
    :definitionText "(Philippines) Forest - areas of one hectare or more which are at least 10 percent stocked with forest trees (including seedlings and saplings), with palm, bamboo, or brush. Narrow strips of land bearing forest must be at least 60 meters wide and one hectare in size to qualify as forest. Industrial plantations and tree farms, one hectare or more in sizes, are also included. http://www.nscb.gov.ph/ru12/DEFINE/DEF-ENV.HTM and (Forest Management Bureau) http://www.nscb.gov.ph/glossary/enr.htm" .

:def_Forest_Philippines_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Philippines ;
    :sourceRef "http://law.upd.edu.ph/plj/images/files/PLJ%20volume%2066/PLJ%20volume%2066%20first%20quarter%20-05-%20Antonio%20G.M.%20La%20Viña%20-%20Conservation%20and%20Democratization.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Philippines) Senate Bill No. 1404 defines \"forest cover\" as follows: \"forest cover includes pine forest, mossy forest, dipterocarp forest (closed and open canopy) and mangrove vegetation: http://law.upd.edu.ph/plj/images/files/PLJ%20volume%2066/PLJ%20volume%2066%20first%20quarter%20-05-%20Antonio%20G.M.%20La%20Viña%20-%20Conservation%20and%20Democratization.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Poland_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Poland ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://afoludata.jrc.ec.europa.eu/metaed/project_collection/JRC_54744_Mascaref_Full_Report_for_print.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Poland 2009 NIR) Tree height > 2m, area > 0.1 ha. http://afoludata.jrc.ec.europa.eu/metaed/project_collection/JRC_54744_Mascaref_Full_Report_for_print.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Poland_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Poland ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Poland) Forest - Continuous area of at least 0.1 ha covered by forest vegetation (forest stands) = trees and shrubs with herbaceous ground cover. http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Poland_1991_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Poland ;
    dcterms:date "1991"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://icaci.org/documents/ICC_proceedings/ICC2011/Oral%20Presentations%20PDF/A3-Data%20integration/CO-028.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Poland? 1991) Forest Act of 28 September 1991. (OJ 1991 No 101 item. 444) for the forest land is considered a homogeneous area of at least 0.10 ha, which is covered by forest vegetation (forest crop), i.e. trees, shrubs and forest undergrowth or temporarily deprived of that what is intended for forest production(…) (Forest Act, 1991). http://icaci.org/documents/ICC_proceedings/ICC2011/Oral%20Presentations%20PDF/A3-Data%20integration/CO-028.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Poland_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Poland ;
    :sourceRef "http://icaci.org/documents/ICC_proceedings/ICC2011/Oral%20Presentations%20PDF/A3-Data%20integration/CO-028.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Poland?) Forest and wooded lands class covers the area with dense plantings: forests, scrubs and others. The minimum width of a wooded area shall be 15 m and a minimum length of 40 m. Group of trees, small forest or scrub with the surface less than 1000 m2 represent the class Natural Object. In the area of double-storied stand scrubs are included into the forest when their surface is less than 2000 m2. http://icaci.org/documents/ICC_proceedings/ICC2011/Oral%20Presentations%20PDF/A3-Data%20integ" .

:def_Forest_Portuga_2010_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Portuga ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Portuga 2010) –l Extent of land with an area ≥ 5 000 m2 and a width ≥ 20 m, with a degree of covered (defined as the ratio between the area of horizontal projection of the crown and the total area of the plot) ≥ 10% which reveal the presence of trees that forest for their characteristics or form of exploitation has reached or will reach, arboreal (height than 5 m) regardless of the stage which is the time of observation. Autoridade Florestal National (AFN) and Ministerio da Agricoltura do Desen" .

:def_Forest_Portugal_1994_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Portugal ;
    dcterms:date "1994"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "15.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "Gerry Lawson <gjl@ite.ac.uk>" ;
    :definitionText "(Portugal 1994) - According to minimum tree densities which vary from species to species (as low as 90/ha for cork oak, up to 840 for most conifers) with conifer heights from 1.5-5m hand broadleaf heights from 2-5m; or where the projected area of crowns of trees more than 5m height covers more than 15% of the ground areas. This rather complicated definition is necessary to define when grant payments are applicable and is necessary because Portugal has a long agroforestry tradition. (decree 199/9" .

:def_Forest_Portugal_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Portugal ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/pt_initialreportkp.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Portugal 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 1 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 10 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = 20 http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/pt_initialreportkp.pdf (2006)" .

:def_Forest_Portugal_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Portugal ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://afoludata.jrc.ec.europa.eu/metaed/project_collection/JRC_54744_Mascaref_Full_Report_for_print.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Portugal 2009 NRI and NFI) Crown cover > 10%, tree height > 5m, area > 0.5 ha, width > 20 m. http://afoludata.jrc.ec.europa.eu/metaed/project_collection/JRC_54744_Mascaref_Full_Report_for_print.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Portugal_2010_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Portugal ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Portugal 2010) Extent of land with an area ≥ 5 000 m2 and a width ≥ 20 m, with a degree of covered (defined as the ratio between the area of horizontal projection of the crown and the total area of the plot) ≥ 10% which reveal the presence of trees that forest for their characteristics or form of exploitation has reached or will reach, arboreal (height than 5 m) regardless of the stage which is the time of observation. Autoridade Florestal National (AFN) and Ministerio da Agricoltura do Desenvo" .

:def_Forest_Romania_1996_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Romania ;
    dcterms:date "1996"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.25"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/docrep/w7170E/w7170e0f.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Romania 1996) - The total forest vegetation mentioned in the Forest Management Plans, both state-owned or private property, constitute the national forest area. Under the Forestry Code/1996 a forest area is defined as an area larger than 0.25 ha and covered with forest trees; the current forestry code refers to forest vegetation not included in the national forest area as forested pastures, forest windbreaks, forested low production areas, forests for watershed protection, community forest park" .

:def_Forest_Romania_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Romania ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.25"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Romania 2000) - Forest - land covered by forest vegetation with an area of more than 0.25 ha. For FRA 2000 - Source: UN/ECE 2000 p 85 and http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Romania_2011_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Romania ;
    dcterms:date "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Romania 2011) - Forest is a land covered 0.5 ha, 10% crown cover and 5 m height. SILVA RNP, 2011. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Romania_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Romania ;
    :areaMin "0.25"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.unece.org/fileadmin/DAM/timber/fra/pdf/chp1_tot.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Romania) According to the definition given in our “Forest Code”, forest is considered land covered by forest vegetation with an area of more than 0.25 ha. In order to approximate the TBFRA definition of the forest, the item “Forest” includes lands needed for culture (nurseries, orchards...), for production (game food...), for administration (forest roads, fire breaks...) and temporarily excluded from the “forest fund”. These are separately recorded in our statistics and in addition to forest ar" .

:def_Forest_Romania_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Romania ;
    :sourceRef "Sorin Sfirlogea <sorinsf@rosilva.ro>" ;
    :definitionText "(Romania) -Dense group of trees, interdependent one to another and to the other plants, animals and environmental conditions, creating a complex and unitary community, able to fulfill social and economic functions. Sorin Sfirlogea <sorinsf@rosilva.ro National Forests Administration." .

:def_Forest_Romania_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Romania ;
    :sourceRef "Sorin Sfirlogea <sorinsf@rosilva.ro>" ;
    :definitionText "(Romania) Forest land - Surface of forest covered by forest vegetation, destined to fulfill social and/or economic function. Sorin Sfirlogea <sorinsf@rosilva.ro National Forests Administration" .

:def_Forest_Romania_nd_005
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Romania ;
    :definitionText "(Romania) -This term includes not only surfaces covered by forest vegetation, but also nurseries, administrative surfaces (around the forest ranges offices, a.o.) glades (blanks) (M. Ilie, Bucuresti, Romania)" .

:def_Forest_Russian_Federation_1998_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Russian_Federation ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "Igor Yakovlev <yakovlev@mari-el.ru>" ;
    :definitionText "(Russian Federation 1998) A population of forest plants changed in the exterior form and an internal structure under influence of effect against each other, on occupied soil and atmosphere. (G.F. Morozov- archfounder of scientific forestry in Russia). In practice of forestry forest consider as tree stands with a polnota more than 0,3. If polnota less than 0,3 - stand calls as light forest or open woodland. Main difference of a forest from \"not forests \" - the existence of mutual influence betwee" .

:def_Forest_Russian_Federation_1998_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Russian_Federation ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "Igor Yakovlev <yakovlev@mari-el.ru>" ;
    :definitionText "(Russian Federation 1998) One of main types of vegetation consist of an aggregate of trees, shrub, grassy etc. plants (mosses, lichens), including animals and microorganisms biologically interconnected in the development and influencing against each other and an environment. [From: \" Russian Forest Encyclopedia\" \"Igor Yakovlev\" yakovlev@mari-el.ru Date: Sat, 6 Jun 1998 21:16:59 +0400]" .

:def_Forest_Russian_Federation_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Russian_Federation ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fs.fed.us/research/sustain/2003SustainabilityReport/documents/SustainableForests.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Russian Federation 2003) Minimum area = 0.5 ha, minimum tree crown cover =30%, minimum tree height = Varies http://www.fs.fed.us/research/sustain/2003SustainabilityReport/documents/SustainableForests.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Russian_Federation_2007_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Russian_Federation ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
