    :definitionText "(Russian Federation 2007 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.5 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 30 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/initial_report_russia.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Russian_Federation_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Russian_Federation ;
    :definitionText "(Russian Federation) An element of the geographical landscape composed of the totality (the aggregate) of arboreal (woody), bushy (shrubbery), herbaceous plants, animals and microorganisms, which are biologically interdependent in their developments and influencing each other, as well as external environment (GOST 18486-73, Russia)" .

:def_Forest_Rwanda_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Rwanda ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.05"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Rwanda 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.05 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 10 Min. Tree Height (m) = 3 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Rwanda_2006_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Rwanda ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "7.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.itc.nl/library/papers_2006/general/westinga_for.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Rwanda 2006) In the humid region forest are areas larger than 0.5 ha with tree cover more than 20 % and trees are > 7m. In the dry region (Akagera) this is > 5m. Young forest plantation and coppices are only found in the humid area. Young forest plantation have trees less than 7 m and cover from 10- 40 % or trees more than 7 meter and cover from 10- 20 %. Bush is found in the larger humid natural forest. Tree cover is by definition less than 20 % and in practice mostly less than 10% and shrub c" .

:def_Forest_Rwanda_2010_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Rwanda ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "7.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.agit.at/php_files/myagit/papers/2010/8163.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Rwanda 2010) A land with 0.5 ha or more covered with trees higher than 7 meters and a canopy cover of more than 10%, or tree stands which have the potential to reach these thresholds in situ. http://www.agit.at/php_files/myagit/papers/2010/8163.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Rwanda_2010_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Rwanda ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://rnra.rw/uploads/media/Forestry_Sector_Strategic_Plan.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Rwanda 2010) An ecosystem dominated by trees (defined as perennial woody plants taller than 5 meters at maturity), where the tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) exceeds 10% of the ground surface and the area is larger than 0.5ha. http://rnra.rw/uploads/media/Forestry_Sector_Strategic_Plan.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Rwanda_2012_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Rwanda ;
    dcterms:date "2012"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "7.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.25"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.gsdi.org/gsdiconf/gsdi14/papers/29.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Rwanda 2012) A group of trees higher than 7 m and a canopy cover of more than 10 %, or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ on a land of about 0.25 ha or more. http://www.gsdi.org/gsdiconf/gsdi14/papers/29.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Senegal_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Senegal ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Senegal 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.5 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 30 Min. Tree Height (m) = 2 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Slovak_Republic_2011_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Slovak_Republic ;
    dcterms:date "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Slovak Republic 2011) - A forest is defined as land with tree crown cover of more than 10%, an area of more than 0.5 ha and an average width of more than 20 m. Trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 m at maturity in situ. FOREST EUROPE, UNECE AND FAO, 2011. Ministry of Agriculture of the Slovak Republic, 2009. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Slovak_Republilc_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Slovak_Republilc ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.3"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Slovak Republilc 2009) National definition: Forest is land spanning more than 0.3 ha with trees taller than 5 m and a canopy cover of more than 20%, or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ. Ministry of Agriculture of the Slovak Republic, 2009. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Slovenia_1993_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Slovenia ;
    dcterms:date "1993"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.iufro.org/download/file/5574/4510/61300-jundola01_pdf/" ;
    :definitionText "(Slovenia 1993) - Under the 1993 Forest Act, a forest is an area of land covered with forest trees in the form of a stand or with other forest growth, which ensures any forest function (economic, ecological and social). http://www.iufro.org/download/file/5574/4510/61300-jundola01_pdf/" .

:def_Forest_Slovenia_1994_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Slovenia ;
    dcterms:date "1994"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.05"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/msword/initial_report-slovenia.docSlovenian" ;
    :definitionText "(Slovenia 1994) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.05 Min. Crown Cover (%) = Min. Tree Height (m) = Min. Strip Width (m) = ns Excludes individual trees- riverine and windbelt trees- plantations- etc. http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/msword/initial_report-slovenia.docSlovenian Forest act (1994) -Forest means land overgrown with forest trees in the form of stands or other forest plants which provides any of the functions of a forest. Forest accord" .

:def_Forest_Slovenia_1998_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Slovenia ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "milan.sinko@UNI-LJ.SI" ;
    :definitionText "(Slovenia 1998) A plot of land overgrown with forest trees in the form of stands or other forest growths which provide any of the functions of a forest. Forests according to this law also include overgrown plots of land defined as forest in the spatial element of the forest management plan. The following are not forest within the meaning of this law: individual forest trees, groups of forest trees up to an area of five hectares, non-autochthonous riverine and windbelt trees, avenues, parks, plan" .

:def_Forest_Slovenia_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Slovenia ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.05"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/msword/initial_report-slovenia.doc" ;
    :definitionText "(Slovenia 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.05 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 30 Min. Tree Height (m) = 2 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/msword/initial_report-slovenia.doc" .

:def_Forest_Slovenia_2007_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Slovenia ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.25"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://bookshop.europa.eu/is-bin/INTERSHOP.enfinity/WFS/EU-Bookshop-Site/en_GB/-/EUR/ViewPDFFile-OpenPDFFile?FileName=LBNA24300ENC_002.pdf&SKU=LBNA24300ENC_PDF" ;
    :definitionText "(Slovenia 2007) forest is land covered with forest trees in the form of stands with minimal tree height 5 m and with minimal area of 0.25 ha. http://bookshop.europa.eu/is-bin/INTERSHOP.enfinity/WFS/EU-Bookshop-Site/en_GB/-/EUR/ViewPDFFile-OpenPDFFile?FileName=LBNA24300ENC_002.pdf&SKU=LBNA24300ENC_PDF" .

:def_Forest_Slovenia_2008_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Slovenia ;
    dcterms:date "2008"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://afoludata.jrc.ec.europa.eu/metaed/project_collection/JRC_54744_Mascaref_Full_Report_for_print.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Slovenia 2008 NIR) Area > 0.5 ha. http://afoludata.jrc.ec.europa.eu/metaed/project_collection/JRC_54744_Mascaref_Full_Report_for_print.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Slovenia_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Slovenia ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "75.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.25"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Slovenia 2009) The national forest inventory defines forest as: (a) A plot of land overgrown with forest trees in the form of stands, which can reach a height of at least 5 m and sized to at least 0.25 ha (b) A plot of agricultural land in transition to forest land sized to at least 0.25 ha that has not been used for agriculture for the last 20 years and is overgrown with forest trees which can reach a height of at least 5 m and their crown cover should be at least 75% (c) Riverside forest corr" .

:def_Forest_Slovenia_2013_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Slovenia ;
    dcterms:date "2013"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32013D0529" ;
    :definitionText "(Slovenia 2013) - Area (ha) 0.25; Tree crown cover (%) 30; Tree height (m) 2 http://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32013D0529" .

:def_Forest_Slovenia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Slovenia ;
    :areaMin "0.05"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Slovenia) Forest - A land overgrown with forest trees - stands or other plants - which provides any of the functions of forests. Includes: land defined as forests in the forest management plan, and forest infrastructure not allocated into a separate lot. Excludes: individual trees and groups of forest trees smaller than 0.05 ha, non-native riverain and windbelt trees, avenues, parks, plantations of forest trees, pens for rearing game, pastures overgrown with forest trees. Definition applies als" .

:def_Forest_Solomon_Islands_1999_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Solomon_Islands ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Solomon Islands 1999) Any area of land predominantly covered by trees, and includes areas planted with trees except when such planting is carried out for agricultural purposes. [LEX-FAOC018884] SOLOMON ISLANDS: Forests Act (No. 3 of 1999). Date of text: 24 September 1999." .

:def_Forest_Somalia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Somalia ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Somalia) Min. av. height 5-10 m. Canopy closure 20%. Source: ECE-FAO Partnership Programme: Kenya Workshop on Forestry Statistics. Appendix 6." .

:def_Forest_South_Africa_1996_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :South_Africa ;
    dcterms:date "1996"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "70.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(South Africa 1996) Tree canopy cover >70%. A multi-strata community with interlocking canopies, composed of canopy, subcanopy, shrub and herb layers. Excludes planted forests. Thompson. 1996? www.sac.co.za/geoinfo/ field_guide.htm" .

:def_Forest_South_Africa_1998_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :South_Africa ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.oceandocs.net/bitstream/1834/560/1/case%20study.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(South Africa 1998) Forest is defined as more than two trees whose canopies touch. 1998 Forest Act. http://www.oceandocs.net/bitstream/1834/560/1/case%20study.pdf" .

:def_Forest_South_Africa_1998_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :South_Africa ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "6.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ext.grida.no/soesa/nsoer/resource/wetland/inventory_classif.htm#classes" ;
    :definitionText "(South Africa 1998) Forested (wetland) A class is characterised by woody vegetation that is taller than 6 m. These habitats normally possess an overstorey of trees, an understorey of young trees or shrubs, and a herbaceous layer. http://www.ext.grida.no/soesa/nsoer/resource/wetland/inventory_classif.htm#classes South African National Wetland Inventory . Proposed wetland classification system for South Africa . J. Dini, G. Cowan & P. Goodman. FIRST DRAFT. August 1998" .

:def_Forest_South_Africa_1999_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :South_Africa ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "75.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.environmental-auditing.org/LinkClick.aspx?fileticket=fbx%2FbAIVeFU%3D&tabid=128&mid=568" ;
    :definitionText "(South Africa 1999) Forest is a continuous stand of trees at least 10m tall, with their crowns interlocking. It is generally multi-layered vegetation unit dominated by trees (largely evergreen or semi-deciduous) whose combined strata have overlapping crowns (i.e. crown cover is > 75 percent). (Bailey, et.al., 1999) http://www.environmental-auditing.org/LinkClick.aspx?fileticket=fbx%2FbAIVeFU%3D&tabid=128&mid=568" .

:def_Forest_South_Africa_2002_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :South_Africa ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/docrep/005/y4001e/Y4001E06a.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(South Africa 2002) Indigenous forest is defined as \"a generally multilayered vegetation unit dominated by trees (largely evergreen or semi-deciduous) whose combined strata have overlapping crowns (i.e. the crown cover is greater than or equal to 75 percent), and where graminoids in the herbaceous stratum (if present) are generally rare\" http://www.fao.org/docrep/005/y4001e/Y4001E06a.htm" .

:def_Forest_South_Africa_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :South_Africa ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.05"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(South Africa 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.05 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 30 Min. Tree Height (m) = 2 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html - Sasaki & Putz 2009 and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_South_Africa_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :South_Africa ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.polity.org.za/govdocs/white_papers/forestry.html" ;
    :definitionText "(South Africa) - forests of all kinds - Government policy in South Africa is formulated to include \"forests of all kinds\", that is, the indigenous forests, where trees grow with their crowns virtually intertwined, natural woodlands, where tree cover may be as little as 10%, plantation, and community forests. http://www.polity.org.za/govdocs/white_papers/forestry.html" .

:def_Forest_South_Africa_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :South_Africa ;
    :definitionText "(South Africa) “Forest” means any ecosystem containing trees on forest land or any component of such an ecosystem, and includes land, water, air, woody vegetation and living organisms; www.dwaf.gov.za/Forestry/Forestry%20Policy/October%202001%20draft%20Protocol.doc" .

:def_Forest_South_Africa_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :South_Africa ;
    :heightMin "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.polity.org.za/govdocs/green_papers/forest1.html#t1.1" ;
    :definitionText "(South Africa) Closed canopy with three or more tree layers; many species and age classes; typically 5 to 20 m tall. Fires penetrate only rarely. http://www.polity.org.za/govdocs/green_papers/forest1.html#t1.1 Note: This definition of Forest appearst to exclude Plantations, Woodlands, and Wooded Grasslands." .

:def_Forest_South_Africa_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :South_Africa ;
    :sourceRef "Graeme Wild <GraemeW@za.sappi.com>" ;
    :definitionText "(South Africa) Multi-layered vegetation of trees with a cover of greater than 75%. Fire does not normally pass through forest. From: Graeme Wild <GraemeW@za.sappi.com" .

:def_Forest_South_Sudan_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :South_Sudan ;
    :canopyThreshold "15.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.globalforestwatch.org/map/7/6.84/30.48/ALL/grayscale/loss" ;
    :definitionText "(South Sudan) Global Forest Watch South Sudan Product using 15% canopy cover. http://www.globalforestwatch.org/map/7/6.84/30.48/ALL/grayscale/loss,forestgain?begin=2001-01-01&end=2014-12-31&threshold=15" .

:def_Forest_South_Sudan_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :South_Sudan ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(South Sudan 2009) “Forest” mean any land containing a vegetation association dominated by trees of any size, whether exploitable or not, capable of producing wood or other products, potentially capable of influencing climate, exercising an influence on the soil, water regime, and providing habitat for wildlife, and includes woodlands; (CAMP Task Team, 2013)" .

:def_Forest_Spain_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Spain ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Spain 1997) A territory or ecosystem predominately with tree species and a cover closure = 10 %, also includes open forest over cultivated or pasture land where the crown closure is = 20 %. (European Communities 1997b - p. 927)." .

:def_Forest_Spain_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Spain ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Spain 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 1 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 10 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns" .

:def_Forest_Spain_2008_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Spain ;
    dcterms:date "2008"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Spain 2008) - Forest surface is considered the land populated by forest tree species and whose dominant canopy cover (FCC) is more than 10%. It consists of: (i) woodland - land with trees whose FCC> = 20%; (ii) sparse woodland - 10% = <FCC <20%. It also includes land with scrub or grassland species dominant plant natural expression, but a FCC of between 10% and 20%. Ministerio de Medio Ambiente y Medio Rural y Marino, 2008. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_techni" .

