    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Thailand ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.16"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Thailand 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.16 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 30 Min. Tree Height (m) = 3 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html - Sasaki & Putz 2009 and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Thailand_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Thailand ;
    :sourceRef "Songkram Thammincha <fforskt@ku.ac.th>" ;
    :definitionText "(Thailand) Forest land - forest area derived from satellite imagery interpretation by the Royal Forest Department. Songkram Thammincha fforskt@ku.ac.th" .

:def_Forest_Togo_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Togo ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Togo 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.5 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 10 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns Includes palms and bamboo. http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Trinidad_Tobago_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Trinidad_Tobago ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.4"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Trinidad & Tobago 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.4 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 10 Min. Tree Height (m) = 3 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Trinidad_and_Tobago_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Trinidad_and_Tobago ;
    :definitionText "(Trinidad and Tobago) Forest Reserve - means and includes a forest and every part of a forest declared to be a Forest Reserve under the Land Regulations for the time being in force – Forest Act: Chapter 66:01. Narine Lackhan, Director of Forestry." .

:def_Forest_Tunisia_1988_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Tunisia ;
    dcterms:date "1988"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Tunisia 1988) On entend par forêt, toute formation végétale d'origine naturelle ou artificielle composée d'une ou plusieurs espèces forestières d'arbes, d'arbustes ou de broussailles à l'état put ou en mélange.LEX-FAOC002805. TUNISIA: Loi n&ordm; 20 portant Code Forestier. Date of text: 13 April 1988." .

:def_Forest_Turkey_1937_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Turkey ;
    dcterms:date "1937"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/forestry/16407-0c0665eddd86a68c9fbbe87cdde52501c.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Turkey 1937) The first Forest Code defined forests as “areas covered by a collection of trees and shrubs grown either naturally or cultivated by humans, and producing woody materials or any kind of forest yield”. This definition excluded steppes, city parks, thorny areas, and areas of less than 5 ha that were not adjacent to natural forest boundaries and were owned by private entities. http://www.fao.org/forestry/16407-0c0665eddd86a68c9fbbe87cdde52501c.pdf." .

:def_Forest_Turkey_1950_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Turkey ;
    dcterms:date "1950"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://turkeyforest.com/files/forest_report_18.02.2011_with_font_14_&_navigation_--property_rights_in_turkish_forests_-_final_version.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Turkey 1950) AMMENDMENT 5653 was passed in 1950 (see APPENDIX_2). This law changed clauses 1 and 3 (among others) of Forest law 3116 redefying Legal Forests as follows : \"A collection of trees or bushes occurring naturally or planted by people\" with the exception of the following : \" All types of prickly plants, Trees in parks and graveyards, Trees not found in natural Forests such as poplar, eucalyptus,willow and acasia,Clumps of trees and bushes covering less than 3 hectars on private land mo" .

:def_Forest_Turkey_1956_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Turkey ;
    dcterms:date "1956"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://web.ogm.gov.tr/languages/English/dokumanlar/dgf6831law.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Turkey 1956). The groups of trees and small trees and their fields are in the scope of forest. Bit” sedgies; the fields containing steppe plants; all kinkds of prickly plants; parks; trees and groups of trees in city backyards and places in the territory of counties and villages, the places existing I private areas and cultivated trees and small trees. http://web.ogm.gov.tr/languages/English/dokumanlar/dgf6831law.pdf." .

:def_Forest_Turkey_1987_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Turkey ;
    dcterms:date "1987"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.elo.org/UserFiles/File/GR_GIRAUD.doc" ;
    :definitionText "(Turkey 1987) - THE CURRENT FORESTRY LAW 6831 of 1956 (see APPENDIX_4). In 1956 the present Forestry law was introduced replacing law 3116 and offering its own (similar) Forest definitions and Forestry policies. Legal Forests were again redefined as \"naturally occurring or planted collections of trees or shrubs together with the land they occupy.\" Exceptions were again listed as follows: \" Reed beds; Steppes; Land containing all types of prickly plants; parks (amendment 2896 clause 1 of 23/9/198" .

:def_Forest_Turkey_1987_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Turkey ;
    dcterms:date "1987"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://faolex.fao.org/docs/texts/tur20346.doc" ;
    :definitionText "(Turkey 1987) Tree and woodland communities, which are grown by human efforts, are regarded as Forest, together with their lands; Privately owned lands containing trees and woodland species, which do not grow naturally in the neighbouring forest or any kind of trees or woodlands on privately owned land and smaller than three hectares are not considered as forest; http://faolex.fao.org/docs/texts/tur20346.doc" .

:def_Forest_Turkey_1988_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Turkey ;
    dcterms:date "1988"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://turkeyforest.com/files/forest_report_18.02.2011_with_font_14_&_navigation_--property_rights_in_turkish_forests_-_final_version.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Turkey 1988) Naturally occurring or planted collections of trees or shrubs together with the land they occupy shall be called forests. …The word forest …refers to both the forest cover and the underlying real estate. Giraud, Brian. 2011. Property rights in Turkish forests. 106 p. http://turkeyforest.com/files/forest_report_18.02.2011_with_font_14_&_navigation_--property_rights_in_turkish_forests_-_final_version.pdf or http://turkeyforest.com/" .

:def_Forest_Turkey_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Turkey ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Turkey 2000) - Forest - All tree and tree formations communities together with their land are forest. Except for land covered with steppe vegetation, marshes and wetlands covered with buses, city park areas, cemeteries, private lands with tree cover which is not grown in surrounding forests naturally, land out of forest borders with an area of less than 3 ha. UN/ECE 2000 p 89." .

:def_Forest_Turkey_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Turkey ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://turkeyforest.com/files/forest_report_18.02.2011_with_font_14_&_navigation_--property_rights_in_turkish_forests_-_final_version.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Turkey 2003) Naturally occurring or planted collection of trees or shrubs together with the land they occupy. Exceptions are listed as follows: Reedbeds; Steppes; Land containing all types of prickly plants; Parks; Tree and shrub covered areas in city cemeteries and in old cemeteries located inside municipality and village limits; Private land containing trees and shrubs which do not grow naturally in surrounding forests; Land with Title Deeds within or adjacent to Forest Boundaries or if outsi" .

:def_Forest_Turkey_2004_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Turkey ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.sayistay.gov.tr/english_tca/Performance/ProtectionOfForests.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Turkey 2004) “Groups of trees and small trees growing naturally or grown by people are considered forest together with the land where they stand” and also includes exceptions of this definition within the rest of the article. (Turkish Article 1 of the Forest Law no. 6831). Karabeyli, Levent et al. 2004. Protection of forests. Turkish Court of Accounts. Performance Audit Report. 78 p. http://www.sayistay.gov.tr/english_tca/Performance/ProtectionOfForests.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Turkey_2004_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Turkey ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.sayistay.gov.tr/english_tca/Performance/ProtectionOfForests.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Turkey 2004) Article 1 of the Forest Law no. 6831 defines the forests as “Groups of trees and small trees growing naturally or grown by people are considered forest together with the land where they stand” and also includes exceptions of this definition within the rest of the article. http://www.sayistay.gov.tr/english_tca/Performance/ProtectionOfForests.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Turkey_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Turkey ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "11.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://web.ogm.gov.tr/languages/English/dokumanlar/Publications/stateofforests.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Turkey 2009) A forest ecosystem is a natural unit consisting of all plants of which the main element is forest trees, animals and micro-organisms (biotic factors) in an area functioning together with all of the non-living physical (abiotic factors) factors of the environment. …The forest area in terms of crown density is classified into two main groups. Forest area with the crown density of 11-100 percent is defined as productive forest area constituting about 50 percent of the country’s forest" .

:def_Forest_Turkey_2010_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Turkey ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://web.ogm.gov.tr/diger/forestandclimate/Dokumanlar/reports/ProposalforTurkey’sPost-2012NegotiatiForestry.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Turkey 2010) Land spanning more than 0.5 hectares with trees higher than 5 meters and a canopy cover of more than 10 percent, or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ. It does not include land that is predominantly under agricultural or urban land use. FRA and LULUCF. http://web.ogm.gov.tr/diger/forestandclimate/Dokumanlar/reports/ProposalforTurkey’sPost-2012NegotiatiForestry.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Turkey_2010_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Turkey ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "11.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://scialert.net/qredirect.php?doi=ijar.2007.22.32&linkid=pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Turkey 2010) The forest area of Turkey is classified into two main groups on the basis of crown coverage. Forest area with a crown coverage of 11-100 % is defined as productive forest area and covers about 50 % of the country’s forest area. Forest area with crown coverage of 1-10 % is considered as degraded forest area which covers the remaining 50 % of Turkish forest lands. Tolunay, Ahmet et al. 2007. Definition and Classification of Traditional Agroforestry Practices in the West Mediterranean" .

:def_Forest_Turkey_2011_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Turkey ;
    dcterms:date "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Turkey 2011) - A forest is defined as land with tree crown cover of more than 10%, an area of more than 0.5 ha and an average width of more than 20 m. Trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 m at maturity in situ. FOREST EUROPE, UNECE AND FAO, 2011. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Turkey_2013_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Turkey ;
    dcterms:date "2013"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://web.ogm.gov.tr/Dkmanlar/istatistikler/Ormancilik-Istatistikleri_2011.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Turkey 2013) - The ecosystem with the forest trees which are able to reach a minimum height of 5 mt at maturity in suitalble sites. Forest land: The the area of land with forest trees by hectares. http://web.ogm.gov.tr/Dkmanlar/istatistikler/Ormancilik-Istatistikleri_2011.pdf." .

:def_Forest_Uganda_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Uganda ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nemaug.org/regulations/forestry_tree_planting_act.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Uganda 2003) \"forest\" means an area of land containing a vegetation association that is predominantly composed of trees of any size, and includes - (a) a forest classified under this Act; (b) a natural forest, woodland or plantation; (c) the forest produce in a forest; and (d) the forest ecosystem; \"forest ecosystem\" means any natural or semi-natural formation of vegetation whose dominant element is trees, with closed or partially closed canopy, together with the biotic and abiotic environment;" .

:def_Forest_Uganda_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Uganda ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Uganda 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 1.0 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 30 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html - Sasaki & Putz 2009 and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Uganda_2008_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Uganda ;
    dcterms:date "2008"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.envalert.org/docs/Inventoryofcriticalissuesinforestry.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Uganda 2008) An area of at least one hectare of land with a minimum tree canopy cover of 30% and a minimum tree potential height of 5 metres (Adapted from UNFCCC, 2001). http://www.envalert.org/docs/Inventoryofcriticalissuesinforestry.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Uganda_2017_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Uganda ;
    dcterms:date "2017"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "40.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "4.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/3/a-i7849e.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Uganda 2017) Woodland. “Wooded areas where trees and shrubs are predominant. There are wet and dry types. The wet type occurs as a zone along wetlands (riverine forest) and the dry type is found on grass-covered upland areas. To qualify as woodland the average height of the trees must exceed 4 m.” Woodland can be categorized as closed or open woodland according to its canopy cover. Closed woodland has a canopy cover > 40 percent and open woodland has a canopy cover of 10–40 percent. http://www." .

:def_Forest_Uganda_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Uganda ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.greenresources.no/Portals/0/Carbon/KFP%20CCBA%20PDD%20Version%204.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Uganda KP) Uganda has defined and communicated the national forest thresholds as land which has: • Minimum area of 1 hectare • Minimum tree crown cover of 30 %; and • A minimum height of 5 meters at maturity. http://www.greenresources.no/Portals/0/Carbon/KFP%20CCBA%20PDD%20Version%204.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Uganda_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Uganda ;
    :canopyThreshold "40.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Uganda) Tropical high forest. Min. canopy closure 40%. Source: ECE-FAO Partnership Programme: Kenya Workshop on Forestry Statistics. Appendix 6." .

:def_Forest_Ukraine_1994_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Ukraine ;
    dcterms:date "1994"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "Maksym Polyakov <mpoliak@pcomp.usau.kiev.ua>" ;
    :definitionText "(Ukraine 1994) Combination of land, vegetation dominated by trees and shrubs, animals, microorganisms and other natural components interconnected in their development and influencing each other and the environment.'' [From: ``The Forest Code of Ukraine'' Kiev, 1994, 56p. \"Maksym Polyakov\" mpoliak@pcomp.usau.kiev.ua Date: Thu, 11 Jun 1998 12:06:37 +0300 (MSD)]" .

:def_Forest_Ukraine_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Ukraine ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/ukraine_aa_report.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Ukraine 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.1 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 30 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = 20 http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/ukraine_aa_report.pdf (2006)" .

:def_Forest_Ukraine_2006_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Ukraine ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdfagricultural" ;
    :definitionText "(Ukraine 2006) - In Ukraine's forest are forest areas, including those protective plantings linear type, area of not less than 0.1 ha. In Ukraine the forest area does not include: green spaces within settlements (parks, gardens, squares, boulevards, etc.) that are not included in the prescribed manner to the forest; individual trees and groups of trees, shrubs on http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdfagricultural land, homestead, cottage an" .

:def_Forest_United_Kingdom_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :United_Kingdom ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.25"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(United Kingdom 2000) - Forest 20 % and 0.25 ha. For FRA 2000 - Source: UN/ECE 2000 p 90" .

:def_Forest_United_Kingdom_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :United_Kingdom ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/report_final.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(United Kingdom 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.1 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 20 Min. Tree Height (m) = 2 Min. Strip Width (m) = 20. http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/report_final.pdf (2006)" .

:def_Forest_United_Kingdom_2006_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :United_Kingdom ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "25.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.communities.gov.uk/documents/planningandbuilding/pdf/144275.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(United Kingdom 2006) Woodland is defined as an area of trees, where a tree is a woody species capable of achieving >5m in height and 25% canopy cover under favourable growing conditions. http://www.communities.gov.uk/documents/planningandbuilding/pdf/144275.pdf" .

:def_Forest_United_Kingdom_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :United_Kingdom ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://afoludata.jrc.ec.europa.eu/metaed/project_collection/JRC_54744_Mascaref_Full_Report_for_print.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(United Kingdom 2009 NIR and NFI) Crown cover > 20%, tree height > 2m, area > 0.1 ha, width > 20 m. http://afoludata.jrc.ec.europa.eu/metaed/project_collection/JRC_54744_Mascaref_Full_Report_for_print.pdf" .

:def_Forest_United_Kingdom_2009_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :United_Kingdom ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(United Kingdom 2009) For the National Forest Inventory (2009-2014), the definition of forest or woodland as an area of tree covered land greater than 0.5ha (about 1.25 acres) and at least 20 m wide whose “canopy cover” or “canopy closure” extends to 20% or more of the land area (or the potential to achieve this).In other words, if the site were viewed from the air, 20% or more of the ground would be obscured by the trees' foliage when the trees are mature. This definition of woodland is in keep" .

:def_Forest_United_Kingdom_2010_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :United_Kingdom ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "50.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(United Kingdom 2010) - For the National Inventory of Woodland, forest is defined as areas with a canopy cover of 20% or more (or the potential to achieve this) and over 50 m in width. The NIWT woodland map aimed to include all areas satisfying this definition and with a minimum area of 2.0 ha or over. Woodland area from 0.1 ha to 2.0 ha was derived from the Survey of Small Woods and Trees http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" .

:def_Forest_United_Kingdom_nd_006
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :United_Kingdom ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://jncc.defra.gov.uk/page-2433#1858" ;
    :definitionText "(United Kingdom) (Woodland) vegetation dominated by trees that are more than 5 m high when mature, which form a distinct, although sometimes open canopy which has a cover of greater than 20%. http://jncc.defra.gov.uk/page-2433#1858." .

:def_Forest_United_Kingdom_nd_007
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :United_Kingdom ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.forestresearch.gov.uk/fr/INFD-5V8E8R" ;
    :definitionText "(United Kingdom) A large area dominated by trees, both conifers and broad-leaved, either planted or natural. Usually taken to include a complex landscape comprising of woodland, open space, water and settlements. http://www.forestresearch.gov.uk/fr/INFD-5V8E8R" .

:def_Forest_United_Kingdom_nd_008
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :United_Kingdom ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.forestry.gov.uk/forestry/hcou-4ubj75" ;
    :definitionText "(United Kingdom) Forest (Wood) - Generally speaking, a forest is a large wood or a collection of woods although the two terms are often interchangeable http://www.forestry.gov.uk/forestry/hcou-4ubj75" .

:def_Forest_Uruguay_1988_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Uruguay ;
    dcterms:date "1988"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Uruguay 1988) A los efectos de la aplicación de esa Ley, se consideran bosques las asociaciones vegetales que tengan ciertas características y que ocupen una superficie mínima de 2 500 m&sup2;. Además, se designan como terrenos forestales ciertas zonas o grupos de suelos (costas arenosas, orillas de ríos, etc.) y se habilita al departamento competente para designar otras por razones de conveniencia pública y teniendo en cuenta la aptitud forestal de los suelos. Por otra parte, el presente Decre" .

:def_Forest_Uruguay_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Uruguay ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.25"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fs.fed.us/research/sustain/2003SustainabilityReport/documents/SustainableForests.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Uruguay 2003) Minimum area = 0.25 ha http://www.fs.fed.us/research/sustain/2003SustainabilityReport/documents/SustainableForests.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Uruguay_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Uruguay ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.25"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Uruguay 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.25 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 30 Min. Tree Height (m) = 3 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html - Sasaki & Putz 2009 and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fs.fed.us/research/sustain/2003SustainabilityReport/documents/SustainableForests.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA 2003) Minimum area = 0.5 ha, minimum tree crown cover =30%, minimum tree height = Varies http://www.fs.fed.us/research/sustain/2003SustainabilityReport/documents/SustainableForests.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA ;
    :sourceRef "Foster <borealis@mail.wellsgray.net>" ;
    :definitionText "(USA) A stand of trees where trees are no more than 60 feet apart. Based upon excavated roots of some mature trees and determined that a forest could not be a forest if the trees were more than about 20 meters apart. This definition assumed that the trees were mature. This was a definition for the USA. Source: \"J. Foster\" <borealis@mail.wellsgray.net from an article in Journal of Forestry." .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_5_agency1982_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_5_agency1982 ;
    :sourceRef "http://home.comcast.net/~gyde/5-agency_paper-2.doc" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-5-agency1982). Treeland. Areas on which vegetation is dominated by trees, provided these areas do not qualify as Built-up land or Cultivated cropland: Examples are areas consisting of such species as Douglas fir, Ponderosa pine, slash pine, oak, aspen, ash, and maple. http://home.comcast.net/~gyde/5-agency_paper-2.doc" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_Census_Bureau1870_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_Census_Bureau1870 ;
    :areaMin "16.1874"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://memory.loc.gov/cgi-bin/query/r?ammem/gmd:@field(NUMBER+@band(g3701gm+gct00008" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-Census Bureau1870) Woodland over 40 acres of forest per square mile. Distribution of woodland within the territory of the U.S. (1873) – See images 49-60 http://memory.loc.gov/cgi-bin/query/r?ammem/gmd:@field(NUMBER+@band(g3701gm+gct00008))" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_Census_Bureau1995_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_Census_Bureau1995 ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.gcrio.org/CONSEQUENCES/spring95/Land.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-Census Bureau1995) Forest land is characterized by a predominance of tree cover and is further divided by the U.S. Census into timberland and non-timberland. By definition, the former must be capable of producing 20 cubic feet of industrial wood per acre per year and remain legally open to timber production. http://www.gcrio.org/CONSEQUENCES/spring95/Land.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_Corps_of_Engineers_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_Corps_of_Engineers ;
    :sourceRef "http://delta.geol.uno.edu/coastal/research/bump/usace_method.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-Corps of Engineers) Any area dominated by trees, that is not normally subject to inundation during the growing season or is only periodically influenced by flooding. (Trees understood to be more than 20 feet tall). http://delta.geol.uno.edu/coastal/research/bump/usace_method.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_Bureau_of_Forestry_1905_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_Bureau_of_Forestry ;
    dcterms:date "1905"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://ir.library.oregonstate.edu/xmlui/bitstream/handle/1957/6265/terms%20used%20in%20forestry%20%5Bocr%5D.pdf?sequence=1" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA Bureau of Forestry 1905) An area whose principal crop is trees. A forest includes both the forest cover and the soil beneath it. A forest judged by the character of the stand may be timberland or woodland. These constitute the two great classes of forest, between which it is possible to draw a practical but not an absolute distinction. Timberland may be broadly defined as that class of forest which contains in commercial quantities trees of sufficient size and of the required kind to" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_FS_1998_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_FS ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fs.fed.us/psw/publications/documents/psw_gtr145/psw_gtr145.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-FS 1998) Forests, upland - forests where palms do not predominate and where the water table is too low to support mangrove or swamp forest species (MacLean and others 1988a). http://www.fs.fed.us/psw/publications/documents/psw_gtr145/psw_gtr145.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_NRCS_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_NRCS ;
    :sourceRef "http://nsscnt.nssc.nrcs.usda.gov/nfm/apxframe.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-NRCS) For the purpose of developing ecological site descriptions, a spatially defined site where the historic climax plant community was dominated by a 25% overstory canopy of trees, as determined by crown perimeter-vertical projection. http://nsscnt.nssc.nrcs.usda.gov/nfm/apxframe.htm and National Soil Survey Handbook http://www.statlab.iastate.edu/soils/nssh/622.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_SCS_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_SCS ;
    :canopyThreshold "25.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-SCS) Lands with at least 25 percent tree canopy cover or lands at least 16.7 stocked by forest trees of any size. Source: USDA- Soil Conserv. Serv. 1977. INTERA -FS/S'CS Agreement-Inventory, Appraisal, and Assessment Responsibilities. Memo dated 1/17/77. Note: this was an attempt to resolve differences in definitions between the USFS and the Soil Conservation Service - now NRCS. See also Lund, et. al. 1981." .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DC_NOAA_2007_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DC_NOAA ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.csc.noaa.gov/crs/lca/tech_cls.html#9" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DC-NOAA 2007?) Areas dominated by trees generally greater than 5 meters tall and greater than 20 percent of total vegetation cover. http://www.csc.noaa.gov/crs/lca/tech_cls.html#9 and www.csc.noaa.gov/crs/lca/ccap.html." .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DC_NOAA_Coastal_Services_Center_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DC_NOAA_Coastal_Services_Center ;
    :heightMin "6.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.csc.noaa.gov/crs/lca/oldscheme.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DC-NOAA-Coastal Services Center) Includes areas dominated by single-stemmed, woody vegetation unbranched 2 to 3 feet above the ground having a height greater than 6 meters (20 feet) http://www.csc.noaa.gov/crs/lca/oldscheme.html (2004)" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DI_BLM_2011_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DI_BLM ;
    dcterms:date "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.blm.gov/pgdata/etc/medialib/blm/co/programs/land_use_planning/rmp/white_river/documents/rmpa-2.Par.82091.File.dat/07_WRFO_RMPA-EIS_Chapter%206_Aug2012.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DI-BLM 2011). Forest. Contains tree species commonly harvested as a timber resource including ponderosa pine, lodgepole pine, Douglas-fir, spruce/fir mix, and aspen. http://www.blm.gov/pgdata/etc/medialib/blm/co/programs/land_use_planning/rmp/white_river/documents/rmpa-2.Par.82091.File.dat/07_WRFO_RMPA-EIS_Chapter%206_Aug2012.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DI_FWS_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DI_FWS ;
    :heightMin "6.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nwi.fws.gov/riparian.htm#DEFINITIONS" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DI-FWS) Woody vegetation greater than 6 meters in height. http://www.nwi.fws.gov/riparian.htm#DEFINITIONS" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DI_FWS_2004_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DI_FWS ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "https://www.fws.gov/northeast/planning/ESV/PDF/(18" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DI-FWS 2004) – Land dominated by trees. For the purposes of the impacts analysis in this document, all forested land was assumed to have the potential to be occasionally harvested, and forested land owned by timber companies was assumed to be harvested on a more intensive, regular schedule. https://www.fws.gov/northeast/planning/ESV/PDF/(18)%20%20%20GLOSSARY.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DI_GS_NLCD_1992_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DI_GS_NLCD ;
    dcterms:date "1992"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "25.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "6.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://landcover.usgs.gov/classes.php#upland" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DI-GS-NLCD 1992). Forested Upland - Areas characterized by tree cover (natural or semi-natural woody vegetation, generally greater than 6 meters tall); tree canopy accounts for 25-100 percent of the cover NLCD 92 http://landcover.usgs.gov/classes.php#upland" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DI_NBSNPS_1994_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DI_NBSNPS ;
    dcterms:date "1994"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "60.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DI-NBS/NPS 1994) Areas with tree 5 m in height or more and with crowns interlocking (60-100% crown cover). (TNC-NBS/NPS. 1994)." .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DI_NPS_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DI_NPS ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://science.nature.nps.gov/im/units/netn/inventory/docs/Inventory%20Reports/Land_Cover_Change_FINAL_20091203.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DI-NPS 2009) Areas dominated by trees. Wang, Y. Q.; Nugranad-Marzilli, J. 2009. Land cover change in Northeast Temperate Network parks 1973-2002. Natural Resource Technical Report NPS/NETN/NRTR — 2009/238. National Park Service, Fort Collins, Colorado. http://science.nature.nps.gov/im/units/netn/inventory/docs/Inventory%20Reports/Land_Cover_Change_FINAL_20091203.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DS_AID_2008_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DS_AID ;
    dcterms:date "2008"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "60.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.usaid.gov/locations/latin_america_caribbean/environment/docs/section_118/Jamaica_2008_FAA_118_and_119_FINAL.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DS-AID 2008) A forest is best defined as an ecosystem or assemblage of ecosystems dominated by trees and other woody vegetation. Forests (according to the U.S. National Vegetation Classification system) consist of trees with overlapping crowns forming 60% to 100% cover. Woodlands are more open, with 25% to 60% cover. http://www.usaid.gov/locations/latin_america_caribbean/environment/docs/section_118/Jamaica_2008_FAA_118_and_119_FINAL.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_EPA_2001_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_EPA ;
    dcterms:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://a257.g.akamaitech.net/7/257/2422/14mar20010800/edocket.access.gpo.gov/cfr_2002/julqtr/pdf/40cfr171.2.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-EPA 2001) The term forest means a concentration of trees and related vegetation in non-urban areas sparsely inhabited by and infrequently used by humans; characterized by natural terrain and drainage patterns. http://a257.g.akamaitech.net/7/257/2422/14mar20010800/edocket.access.gpo.gov/cfr_2002/julqtr/pdf/40cfr171.2.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_EPA_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_EPA ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.epa.gov/indicate/roe/html/roeAppDf.htm#f" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-EPA) - Lands at least 10 percent covered by trees of any size, at least one acre in extent. This includes areas in which trees are intermingled with other cover, such as chaparral and pinyon, juniper areas in the Southwest, and both naturally regenerating forests and areas planted for future harvest (plantations or tree farms). http://www.epa.gov/indicate/roe/html/roeAppDf.htm#f" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_EPA_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_EPA ;
    :canopyThreshold "25.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.epa.gov/mrlc/Implmnt_plan.htm#Def" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-EPA) (Natural) Forested - A class of vegetation dominated by trees generally forming 25% canopy cover. http://www.epa.gov/mrlc/Implmnt_plan.htm#Def MRLC" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_EPA_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_EPA ;
    :sourceRef "http://oaspub.epa.gov/trs/trs_proc_qry.alphabet?p_term_nm=F" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-EPA) Plant communities which exist along floodplains or on the eastern side of rivers where they were protected from fires. They are dominated by trees that are intolerant of fire and can grow in poorly drained soils, although bur oak trees can be a part of this community. In Northeastern Illinois, the word \"forest\" is often used interchangeably with \"woodland\" or \"woods,\" as in the \"Big Woods.\" EPA/Great Lakes National Program Office : Natural Landscaping for Public Officials: Glossary" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_EPA_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_EPA ;
    :heightMin "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.epa.gov/nerlesd1/land-sci/table1.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-EPA) Vegetative communities comprised principally of trees potentially over 10m in height and typically characterized by closed or multi-layered canopies. http://www.epa.gov/nerlesd1/land-sci/table1.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_FGDC_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_FGDC ;
    :canopyThreshold "60.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://biology.usgs.gov/fgdc.veg/standards/appendix3.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-FGDC) Closed Tree Canopy - trees with crowns interlocking with crowns forming 60-100% cover. Open Tree Canopy - trees with crowns not usually touching forming 10- or 25-60% cover [Source: http://biology.usgs.gov/fgdc.veg/standards/appendix3.htm]" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_FGDC_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_FGDC ;
    :canopyThreshold "25.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.forestguild.org/climate_change/Pinon-Juniper.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-FGDC) Mature (late successional) height of trees > 5 m (16.5 ft.) and canopy cover =/>25%. FGDC. http://www.forestguild.org/climate_change/Pinon-Juniper.pdf and http://www.fgdc.gov/fgdc.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_NASA_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_NASA ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dictionary.com/cgi-bin/dict.pl?term=forest" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-NASA) A dense growth of trees, plants, and underbrush covering a large area. http://www.dictionary.com/cgi-bin/dict.pl?term=forest and http://vathena.arc.nasa.gov/curric/land/wetland/gloss.html" .

:def_Forest_Vanatu_1933_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Vanatu ;
    dcterms:date "1933"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cn.china.cn/2011images/vanuatu/NFP_Comprehensive_June_2011.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Vanatu 1933) An area covered with trees with a canopy height greater than 10 m, crowns touching or overlapping, and no groundlayer visible on airphotos (GoV 1993: VANRIS); http://cn.china.cn/2011images/vanuatu/NFP_Comprehensive_June_2011.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Vanatu_1993_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Vanatu ;
    dcterms:date "1993"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cn.china.cn/2011images/vanuatu/NFP_Comprehensive_June_2011.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Vanatu 1993) Areas of natural vegetation with a predominant canopy height of over 10 meters (Baldwin & Mathias, 1993); http://cn.china.cn/2011images/vanuatu/NFP_Comprehensive_June_2011.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Vanatu_2001_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Vanatu ;
    dcterms:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://cn.china.cn/2011images/vanuatu/NFP_Comprehensive_June_2011.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Vanatu 2001) Any area of Vanuatu predominantly covered by trees, and includes areas planted with trees,except where such trees are for agricultural purposes (Forestry Act, 2001); http://cn.china.cn/2011images/vanuatu/NFP_Comprehensive_June_2011.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Vanuatu_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Vanuatu ;
    :heightMin "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Vanuatu) Forest - Tree canopy is greater than 10 m in height. Crowns are touching or overlapping. Ground layer not visible on airphotos. Source: Bellamy, J.A. Vanuatu Resource Information System. VANRIS Handbook. Via Adam Gerrand." .

:def_Forest_Venezuela_1977_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Venezuela ;
    dcterms:date "1977"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "Via <Profauna@marnr.gov.ve>" ;
    :definitionText "(Venezuela 1977) AREAS BOSCOSAS: son espacios naturales compuestos por uno o más ecosistemas forestales que por sus característicaas ecológicas y masa arbórea predominante densa, son aptas para la producción permanente de bienes forestales (maderables y no maderables) y de servicios ambientales y sociales, cuyo manejo sustentable permita mantener los ciclos ecológicos y, por ende, la cubierta forestal. Reglamento de la Ley Forestal de Suelos y Aguas (1977). Areas Naturales Protegidas de Venezuel" .

:def_Forest_Venezuela_1977_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Venezuela ;
    dcterms:date "1977"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "Via <Profauna@marnr.gov.ve>" ;
    :definitionText "(Venezuela 1977) BOSQUE: Comunidad vegetal dominada por elementos típicamente arbóreos, que forman por lo menos un estrato de copas (dosel)más o menos contínuo, generalmente de 5 m de altura (2); espacio natural conformado por árboles, arbustos, hierbas,bacterias, hongos, protozoarios, artrópodos, otros invertebrados de todos los tamaños, clases y descripciones, vertebrados, oxígeno, dióxido de carbono, agua, minerales y materia orgánica muerta, que en su totalidad constituyen el ecosistema fore" .

:def_Forest_Venezuela_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Venezuela ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/forestry/fo/country/index.jsp?lang_id=1&geo_id=214" ;
    :definitionText "(Venezuela) - Incluye bosques (formas arbóreas) de al menos 5 metros de altura. http://www.fao.org/forestry/fo/country/index.jsp?lang_id=1&geo_id=214" .

:def_Forest_Vietnam_1998_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Vietnam ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Vietnam 1998) - A biological community (including tree or bamboo dominant) which have a large area and a determine density so that relation between the biological community and the environment , and between the diverse composition of the biological community for having an forestry environment different with the outside environment. {Definition of barren-land: It is area of barren land without forest or actually not yet afforested, only bush or scattered trees , bamboo with a coverage < 0.3 .} S" .

:def_Forest_Vietnam_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Vietnam ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Vietnam 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.5 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 30 Min. Tree Height (m) = 3 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html - Sasaki & Putz 2009 and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Vietnam_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Vietnam ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.asb.cgiar.org/PDFwebdocs/REALU-Final%20Report%20-%20Vietnam.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Vietnam KP) forest is: (i) an area of at least 0.5 ha; with (ii) a minimum crown cover of 30%; and (iii) a minimum tree height at maturity of 3m. http://www.asb.cgiar.org/PDFwebdocs/REALU-Final%20Report%20-%20Vietnam.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Virgin_Islands_St_Thomas_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Virgin_Islands_St_Thomas ;
    :canopyThreshold "50.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://rps.uvi.edu/CES/vivegzon.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Virgin Islands – St. Thomas) Forest – closed tree canopy (> 50%) http://rps.uvi.edu/CES/vivegzon.htm" .

:def_Forest_Yemen_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Yemen ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Yemen 2006 KP) Cover Min. Area (ha) = 0.5 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 30 Min. Tree Height (m) = 3 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html and https://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/DNA/allCountriesARInfos.html" .

:def_Forest_Yemen_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Yemen ;
    :areaMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "m.ellatifi@ellatifi.8m.com" ;
    :definitionText "(Yemen) (Local Arabic term for Forests: Ghabat or Ahraj) - Piece of land covered a vegetation in which trees (not only fruit trees) are predominant(over 50%), and with at least 3 ha of continuously forested area, and with a tree crown cover equal or superior to 10%. Mohammed Ellatifi, m.ellatifi@ellatifi.8m.com" .

:def_Forest_Zimbabwe_2002_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Zimbabwe ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "80.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "15.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://ageconsearch.umn.edu/bitstream/18021/1/dp020002.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Zimbabwe 2002) Natural moist forest Tree height >15m, canopy cover >80% http://ageconsearch.umn.edu/bitstream/18021/1/dp020002.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Zimbabwe_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Zimbabwe ;
    :canopyThreshold "80.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "15.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "vegris@harare.iafrica.com" ;
    :definitionText "(Zimbabwe) Natural forest - This class which consists of moist evergreen or deciduous species can be defined as vegetation which shows a canopy cover greater than 80% and tree heights greater than 15 metres. This class usually occurs in high rainfall areas and as riverine vegetation along big rivers. Dominick Kwesha \"VegRIS\" vegris@harare.iafrica.com" .

:def_Forest_America_Samoa_1988_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :America_Samoa ;
    dcterms:date "1988"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.botany.hawaii.edu/basch/uhnpscesu/pdfs/sam/Cole1988AS.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(America Samoa 1988). Land at least 10 percent stocked by live trees or land formerly having such tree cover and not currently developed for nonforest use. USDA Forest Service Resour. Bull. PSW 25. 14 p. http://www.botany.hawaii.edu/basch/uhnpscesu/pdfs/sam/Cole1988AS.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Antigua_and_Barbuda_2012_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Antigua_and_Barbuda ;
    dcterms:date "2012"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.tradingeconomics.com/antigua-and-barbuda/forest-area-percent-of-land-area-wb-data.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Antigua and Barbuda 2012) Land under natural or planted stands of trees of at least 5 meters in situ, whether productive or not, and excludes tree stands in agricultural production systems (for example, in fruit plantations and agroforestry systems) and trees in urban parks and gardens. http://www.tradingeconomics.com/antigua-and-barbuda/forest-area-percent-of-land-area-wb-data.html." .

:def_Forest_Argentina_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Argentina ;
    :definitionText "(Argentina) - Terreno que mantiene unas existencias forestales o del que ha sido extraído el arbolado, pero que muestra de forma evidente haber estado cubierto por él anteriormente y que en la actualidad no está dedicado a otro aprovechamiento. (I. Conesa de Flores, Universidad Nacional del Nordeste, Resistencia, Argentina)" .

:def_Forest_Armenia_2005_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Armenia ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nature-ic.am/res/pdfs/legislation/general/Forest%20Code%20of%20RA.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Armenia 2005) Forest - interconnected and interacting integrity of biological diversity dominated by tree-bush vegetation and of components of natural environment on forest lands or other lands allocated for afforestation with the minimal area of 0,1 ha, minimal width of 10 m and with tree crowns covering at least 30% of the area, as well as non-forested areas of previously forested forest lands. Forest Code of Armenia: http://www.nature-ic.am/res/pdfs/legislation/general/Forest%20Code%20of%20R" .

:def_Forest_Australia_nd_006
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Australia ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.rfa.gov.au/nfps/gloss.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia -Old) An area, incorporating all living and non-living components, that is dominated by trees having usually a single stem and a mature or potentially mature stand height exceeding 5 metres, and with existing or potential projective cover of overstorey strata about equal to or greater than 30 per cent. This definition includes Australia's diverse native forests and plantations, regardless of age. It is also sufficiently broad to encompass areas of trees that are sometimes described as" .

:def_Forest_Austria_1977_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Austria ;
    dcterms:date "1977"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "Weiss Peter <weissp@ubavie.gv.at>" ;
    :definitionText "(Austria 1977) An area stocked by trees (a list of tree species in this context is given in an annex to the Austrian Forestry Act), if the stocking of trees represents an area of at least 1000 m2 and is of an average width of at least 10 m. Forest areas, which are unstocked due to forest management practices (for instance harvesting areas or areas used for timber storage, skidding tracks or forest roads), are still referred to as \"forest land.\" (Austrian Forestry Act (Federal Legal Gazette no. 4" .

:def_Forest_Barbados_2011_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Barbados ;
    dcterms:date "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.tradingeconomics.com/barbados/forest-area-sq-km-wb-data.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Barbados – 2011) Forest area is land under natural or planted stands of trees of at least 5 meters in situ, whether productive or not, and excludes tree stands in agricultural production systems (for example, in fruit plantations and agroforestry systems) and trees in urban parks and gardens. http://www.tradingeconomics.com/barbados/forest-area-sq-km-wb-data.html" .

:def_Forest_Belarus_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Belarus ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Belarus 2000) Forest includes land covered in trees (main and other forest-forming species), non-continuous forest growth, nurseries, and plantations. Not covered in trees - openings, slashes, dead stands, cuttings, clearings. (For FRA 2000 - Source: UN/ECE 2000 p .73)." .

:def_Forest_Belarus_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Belarus ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/initial_report_belarus_english_1.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Belarus 2006 KP) Use Min. Area (ha) = 0.1 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 30 Min. Tree Height (m) = Min. Strip Width (m) = ns National Forest Legislation defines forested lands as forested lands of the forest fund occupied by young forest of timber species with stand density of 0.4 and higher, and stands of other age groups with stand density of 0.3 and higher, as well as areas occupied by bushes, at which stands of timber species cannot be developed without special forest improvement.. 0.1 hectare is a" .

:def_Forest_Bhutan_1969_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Bhutan ;
    dcterms:date "1969"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://extwprlegs1.fao.org/docs/pdf/bhu2744.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Bhutan 1969) Forest means any land under forest which no person has acquired a permanent heritable and transferable right of use and occupancy. http://extwprlegs1.fao.org/docs/pdf/bhu2744.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Bolivia_2002_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Bolivia ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/docrep/005/y2328e/y2328e03.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Bolivia 2002) By principal land use: in Bolivia, forest land refers to areas covered with natural forest, cultivated, intended for various uses, and also treeless lands which may be reforested. Meadows and pasture, with scattered trees or shrubs, do not constitute forest lands. http://www.fao.org/docrep/005/y2328e/y2328e03.htm" .

:def_Forest_Bolivia_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Bolivia ;
    :sourceRef "Luis Castello <faopaf@caoba.entelnet.bo>" ;
    :definitionText "(Bolivia) TERRENO FORESTAL: Es superficie cubierta de bosque nativo, cultivado, destinado para diferentes usos; también son terrenos desprovistos de árboles, que que pueden ser reforestados. Las praderas y pastizales con árboles o arbustos dispersos, no constituye un terreno forestal. Aquel que utilizado técnica y científicamente, proporciona en forma permanente mayor utilidad económica, protectora y escénica, con cultivo forestal de bajo aprovechamiento agropecuario. Source: Luis Castello faopa" .

:def_Forest_Bosnia_FbiH_RS_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Bosnia_FbiH_RS ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Bosnia – FbiH – RS) Forest land is land on which forest is grown or land that is, because its natural characteristics, foreseen or used for this purpose. Forest land is land covered with forest or where it is more rational, due to natural characteristics, to have a forest or cultivate the land for forestry production. http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Bosnia_2001_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Bosnia ;
    dcterms:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.iufro.org/download/file/5574/4510/61300-jundola01_pdf/" ;
    :definitionText "(Bosnia 2001) Forest Law, land covered by forest trees in the form of stands on an area bigger than 0.1 hectare is considered forest. Separated groups of forest trees on an area smaller than 0,1 hectare, forest nurseries, windscreen zones and parks in populated areas are not considered forests. Land where forests are grown or which are, because of their natural features and management conditions, anticipated to be favorable for growing of forests are considered as forestlands. http://www.iufro.o" .

:def_Forest_Bosnia_and_Herzegovina_2013_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Bosnia_and_Herzegovina ;
    dcterms:date "2013"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.16"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Bosnia and Herzegovina 2013) - Forests (definitions) Including all areas covered with forest tree species, minimum (0.16 ha, minimum width 20 m) with minimum crown coverage 20%, whatever age, or origin of the tree. Growth more than 5 m in height. Forest including areas temporarily unstocked areas (with crown cover less than 20%) if higher coverage can be expected in the near future. Forest includes forest roads inside the forest area, less than 5 m in wide (could be covered with tree crowns) an" .

:def_Forest_Bulgaria_2007_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Bulgaria ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/msword/initial_report-bulgaria.doc" ;
    :definitionText "(Bulgaria 2007 KP) “Area over 0.1 ha, covered with forest tree species higher than 5 meters and tree crown cover over 10% or with trees which can reach these parameters in natural environment. Forests are also: 1. areas which are in a process of recovering and are still under the parameters, but it is expected to reach forest crown cover over 10% and tree height 5 meters; 2. areas, which as the result of anthropogenic factors of or natural reasons are temporary deforested, but will be reforested" .

:def_Forest_Burkina_Faso_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Burkina_Faso ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Burkina Faso 1997) Au sens du present Code, sont consideres comme forets les espaces occupes par des formations vegetales d'arbres et d'arbustes, a l'exclusion de celles resultant d'activites agricoles (all area but town and agricultural lands) Source: au BF d'apres le Code Forestier au Burkina Faso (ministere de l'environnement et de l'eau, 1997) Loi n[006/97/ADP du 31 janvier 1997, portant Code Forestier au Burkina FAso, Article 12. Via Daniel-Yyves Alexandre." .

:def_Forest_Burundi_1985_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Burundi ;
    dcterms:date "1985"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Burundi 1985) Aux termes du présent Code, on entend, d'une manière générale, par forêts ou boisements: 1. Les terrains recouverts d'une formation végétale à base d'arbres ou d'arbustes, que cette formation soit naturelle ou résultant de semis ou de plantations faits de main d'homme: a. capables de produite du bois ou des produits forestiers; b. ou exerçant un effet indirect sur le climat, le régime des eaux ou le sol. 2. les terrains qui étaient recouverts de forêts ou boisements récemment coup" .

:def_Forest_Cambodia_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Cambodia ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.cedc-info.org/English/qtzcfg/8c09d4969ce4d2be/" ;
    :definitionText "(Cambodia 2009) Forest, means a unit of natural or artificial forest ecosystem, in the form of wet, flooded or dry land, comprised of mixed vegetation, natural or planted, wildlife and other natural resources located therein, primarily utilized for timber and NTFPs production conservation and other forest services. Lands to which this law does not apply include all land designated by the State as permanent agricultural land including, chamcar, idle land to be designated for non timber agricultur" .

:def_Forest_Cameroon_1994_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Cameroon ;
    dcterms:date "1994"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://files.forestsnetwork.org/Chapter4.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Cameroon 1994) Cameroon is based on the 1994 Forest Code, in which community forests are defined as forest areas in the ‘non-Permanent Forest Domain’ (NPFD), a land use designation that permits timber extraction, agriculture, mining, and other utilisation activities. Each community forest must not exceed 5,000 hectares, and must be managed by village communities following a simplified management plan that excludes the use of heavy machinery. http://files.forestsnetwork.org/Chapter4.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Canada_Indian_and_Northern_Affairs_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_Indian_and_Northern_Affairs ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ainc-inac.gc.ca/pr/pub/bldg/frst/glss_e.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada – Indian and Northern Affairs) Land primarily intended for growing, or currently supporting, forest. Includes land not now forested, i.e. clear-cut lands; northern lands that are forested but not intended for any use; and plantations. http://www.ainc-inac.gc.ca/pr/pub/bldg/frst/glss_e.html" .

:def_Forest_Canada_2011_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Canada ;
    dcterms:date "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://nfdp.ccfm.org/terms/terms_e.php?letter=f" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada 2011) Silviculture/forest management: An area managed for the production of timber and other forest produce, or maintained under woody vegetation for such indirect benefits as the protection of watersheds, the provision of recreation areas, or the preservation of natural habitat http://nfdp.ccfm.org/terms/terms_e.php?letter=f" .

:def_Forest_Canada_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Canada ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.pfc.cfs.nrcan.gc.ca/landscape/inventory/terms/363_ch2.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada) Forest land - Land primarily intended for growing, or currently supporting forests. Includes temporarily nonforested lands such as clearcuts. http://www.pfc.cfs.nrcan.gc.ca/landscape/inventory/terms/363_ch2.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Canada_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Canada ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.pfc.cfs.nrcan.gc.ca/landscape/inventory/terms/haddon/glossary.html#F" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada) Forest land: [terrain forestier] - Land primarily intended for growing, or currently supporting, forest. Includes land not now forested, e.g., clearcuts; northern lands that are forested but not intended for any use; and plantations. http://www.pfc.cfs.nrcan.gc.ca/landscape/inventory/terms/haddon/glossary.html#F" .

:def_Forest_Canada_nd_005
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Canada ;
    :sourceRef "Brian <BHaddon@nrcan.gc.ca>" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada) Land primarily intended for growing, or currently supporting, forest. Includes land not now forested (e.g., clearcuts), and plantations. Source: \"Forest Inventory Terms in Canada.\" From: \"Haddon, Brian\" <BHaddon@nrcan.gc.ca" .

:def_Forest_Cape_Verde_1998_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Cape_Verde ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Cape Verde 1998) Zona florestal - O espaço territorial que for reservado no plano de ordenamento do território a usos florestais, nomeadamente para a criação, restauração, conservação e aproveitamento do coberto florestal; LEX-FAOC013213. CAPE VERDE: Forestry Act (No. 48/V/98)." .

:def_Forest_Chile_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Chile ;
    :sourceRef "Patricio Gonzalez <pgonzale@infor.cl>" ;
    :definitionText "(Chile) Terrenos de aptitud preferentemente forestal (Lands with forestry preferably aptitude) - Todos aquellos terrenos que por las condiciones de clima y suelo no deban ararse en forma permanente, estén cubiertos o no de vegetación, excluyendo los que sin sufrir degradación puedan ser utilizados en agricultura, fruticultura o ganadería intensiva. All terrain where climate and soils conditions do not allow permanent plowing, being or not covered with vegetation, excluding those that would not b" .

:def_Forest_Colombia_2014_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Colombia ;
    dcterms:date "2014"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://redd.unfccc.int/files/20.10.15col__frel_english_clean_numbers.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Colombia 2014) For the purposes of the National REDD + Strategy (ENREDD +), and in particular for the construction of this FREL, forest is defined as: Land mainly covered by trees which might contain shrubs, palms, guaduas, grass and vines, in which tree cover predominates with a minimum canopy density of 30%, a minimum canopy height (in situ) of 5 meters at the time of identification , and a minimum area of 1.0 ha. Commercial forest plantations, palm crops and planted trees for agricultural pr" .

:def_Forest_Comoros_1930_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Comoros ;
    dcterms:date "1930"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Comoros 1930) (Article premier) Par forêt, au sens de la présente loi, on entend toutes surfaces répondant aux qualifications ci-après : - les surfaces couvertes d'arbres ou de végétation ligneuse, autres que plantées à des fins exclusives de production fruitière, de production de fourrage ou d'ornementation; - les surfaces occupées par les arbres et les buissons situés sur les berges des cours d'eau et lacs et sur des terrains érodés ; - les terrains dont les fruits exclusifs ou principaux son" .

:def_Forest_Congo_Democratic_Republic_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Congo_Democratic_Republic ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nortonrose.com/files/forest-carbon-rights-in-redd-countries-a-snapshot-of-africa-pdf-994-kb-32479.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Congo, Democratic Republic) Article 1(a) Forestry Code: “land covered with plant formation based on trees or bushes suitable for providing forest products, sheltering wild fauna and exercising a direct orindirect effect on the soil, climate or water system” and land that could benefit from reforestation under Article 1(b) Forestry Code: “land which, having previously contained a tree or shrub plant covering, has been cut bare or burnt and for which natural regeneration or reforestation actions " .

:def_Forest_Croatia_2010_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Croatia ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Croatia 2010) National definition: Forest is defined as the land covered by forest trees formed as forest stand over an area larger than 10 ars (1 ar = 100 m2). Separate forest tree groups over an area up to 10 ars, forest nurseries, windbreaks, tree avenues, and parks in settlements are not considered forests. Faculty of forestry University of Zagreb, Ministry for regional development of forestry and water management, 2010. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_techn" .

:def_Forest_Cuba_1998_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Cuba ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "Nelida Puentes Alvarez <npuentes@eco.upr.edu.cu>" ;
    :definitionText "(Cuba 1998) Patrimonio forestal lo integran los bosques naturales y artificiales, los terrenos destinados a esta actividad,las áreas deforestadas con condiciones para la actividad forestal, así como los árboles de especies forestales que se desarrollen en forma aislada o en grupos, cualquiera que sea su ubicación y tenencia. También forman parte del patrimonio forestal las áreas inforestales... (Artículo 3) Area inforestal: área dentro del bosque y en terrenos destinados a la actividad forestal " .

:def_Forest_Cyprus_2002_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Cyprus ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Cyprus 2002) It corresponds to FRA definition except the threshold value for minimum area, which is 1 ha, with trees higher than 5 m and a crown cover of more than 10%, or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ. Land predominantly under agricultural or urban use not included. Old definition: Forest Land with tree crown cover of more that 10 % and area of more than 1 ha. Cyprus Department of forests ministry of agriculture, natural resources and environment, 2006. Kyriacou K. 2002. http://" .

:def_Forest_Czech_Republic_1995_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Czech_Republic ;
    dcterms:date "1995"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.uhul.cz/images/ke_stazeni/legislativa_jazyky/Lesni_zakon_en.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Czech Republic 1995) Forest stands with its environment and land designated for the fulfillment of forest functions. Forest functions shall mean benefits towards the general well-being of the society conditional on the existence of forests, which consist of wood-producing and non-wood-producing functions. Forest stands shall mean trees and shrubs of forest tree species which, in their particular environment, fulfil forest functions. [Source: Act on Forests and Amendments to Some Acts (the Fores" .

:def_Forest_Czech_Republic_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Czech_Republic ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.01"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Czech Republic 1997) Land destined to fulfill the forest functions, that is: (a) land with forest stands and land after clear cutting ready for reforestation, forest line and soft road of a width less than 4 m; (b) forest roads, water surfaces, land above timber line and other land serving for forest management. Minimum area is 0.01 ha with a minimum width of 20 m and with no definition on crown cover or stand density. (European Communities 1997b - p. 1225)." .

:def_Forest_Czech_Republic_2004_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Czech_Republic ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.01"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Czech Republic 2004) Forest land: land with forest stands and land after cutting ready for reforestation, forest line and soft roads of width less than 4 m. Forest roads, water surfaces, land above timber line and other land serving for forest management. Minimum area is 0.01 ha and with a minimum width of 20 m. NIL definition: Forest - areas (subplot), which are forest land as defined in the Forest Act No. 289/95 Coll. § 3, paragraph 1, letter a) and the Ministry of Agriculture Decree No. 84/1" .

:def_Forest_Czech_Republic_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Czech_Republic ;
    :areaMin "0.01"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://afoludata.jrc.it/carboinvent/cimd_eufoin_data.cfm#countrylist" ;
    :definitionText "(Czech Republic) definition of forest is given by law: \"Forest land is land destined to fulfil the forest functions that is: land with forest stands and land after clear cutting ready for reforestation, forest line and soft road of a width less than 4 m; forest roads, water surfaces, land above timber line and other land serving for forest management.\" The Czech forest management instructions give 0.01 ha as a minimum area of forest, with a minimum width of 20 m. (CarboInvent JRC: http://afoluda" .

:def_Forest_Czech_Republic_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Czech_Republic ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Czech Republic) Forest land - Land with forests stands & cleared areas under regeneration, unpaved forest roads with width <4m, paved forest roads, nurseries, plantations, small water areas, other areas & lands above the alpine limit of woody vegetation. http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Denmark_1998_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Denmark ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "6.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "PMP@sns.dk" ;
    :definitionText "(Denmark 1998) More than 0.5 ha, broader than 30 m, covered by tree-species which are or is able to be more that 6 m's in height. (From: PMP@sns.dk Date: Tue, 29 Sep 1998 09:31:59 +0100). Note: at first glance this appears to be a land cover description, but subsequent definitions of afforestation and reforestation for Denmark show that \"forest\" is really a land use term." .

:def_Forest_Denmark_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Denmark ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/aareporttounfccc-20dec2006.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Denmark 2006 KP) Use Min. Area (ha) = 0.5 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 10 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = 20 http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/aareporttounfccc-20dec2006.pdf, (2006) In addition, the forest area includes temporarily unstocked areas, smaller open areas in the forest needed for management purposes and fire breaks. Forests in national parks, reserves, or areas under special protection are included. Windbreaks" .

:def_Forest_Denmark_2011_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Denmark ;
    dcterms:date "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Denmark 2011) - Land with tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 10% and area of more than 0.5 ha. The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 m at maturity in situ. Areas with agricultural production and urban land are not included.FOREST EUROPE, UNECE AND FAO, 2011. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Denmark_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Denmark ;
    :canopyThreshold "50.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "6.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Denmark) Areas covered with species capable of producing wood that grow to a height of more than 6 m. Forest or plantation shall be more than 0.5 ha in size. Forest area should be wider than 20 m (no hedgerows) although narrow sections are allowed as part of a larger forest. The forest area has -- or is expected to have within a short period -- a crown density of at least 50 percent. Older stands of Christmas trees on arable land are considered forest, if at the time of inventory, they were in " .

:def_Forest_Estonia_1999_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Estonia ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "Sulev Svilponis <Sulev@ekm.envir.ee>" ;
    :definitionText "(Estonia 1999) Forest land [metsamaa] - Land that is assigned for growing ligneous plants (by land survey or by land cadastre). Other lands that have importance for forestry can also be assigned into forest land if these are not suitable for other category. Current Estonian Forestry Act (valid until 01/01/99) From: \"Sulev Svilponis\" Sulev@ekm.envir.ee. Definitions are unofficial translations." .

:def_Forest_Estonia_2002_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Estonia ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www-sydsvenskskogsvetenskap.slu.se/Grundutbildning/Masterk/2002/Estonia/forest.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Estonia 2002) By legal definition, \"forest\" means a site of woody vegetation with an area of at least 0,5 ha, and at least one of the following requirements: Trees with the height of at least 1,3 m and with the canopy coverage of at least 30 %. If the site is managed for obtaining timber or other forest products. http://www-sydsvenskskogsvetenskap.slu.se/Grundutbildning/Masterk/2002/Estonia/forest.html" .

:def_Forest_Estonia_2005_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Estonia ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "1.3"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Estonia 2005) Forest land (= productive forest land, National definition) Minimum area 0.1 ha and 30% crown cover, with height more than 1.3 m, with average annual productivity more than 1 m3/ha of stem wood (incl. temporarily unstocked areas). Pärt E., Adermann V., Merenäk M., 2010. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Estonia_2006_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Estonia ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "1.3"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "https://www.riigiteataja.ee/en/eli/504092017014/consolide" ;
    :definitionText "(Estonia 2006) a plot of land with an area of at least 0.1 hectares and woody plants with the height of at least 1.3 metres and with the canopy density of at least 30 per cent grow there. The land of yards, residential land, parks, cemeteries, green areas, berry gardens, orchards, forest nurseries, gardening centres, arboreta, and plantations of trees and shrubs is not deemed forest land for the purposes of this Act. [RT I, 06.07.2017, 1 – entry into force 01.09.2017]. https://www.riigiteataja.e" .

:def_Forest_Estonia_2010_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Estonia ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Estonia 2010) Forest land (reference definition, applied parallel with National definition since 2005) Land with tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 10% and area of more than 0.5 ha. The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 m at maturity in situ (incl. temporarily unstocked areas). Forest land (= productive forest land, National definition) Minimum area 0.1 ha and 30% crown cover, with height more than 1.3 m, with average annual productivity more than 1 m" .

:def_Forest_Estonia_nd_006
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Estonia ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "1.3"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Estonia) Forest land - Land which fulfils at least one of the following: 1) Trees are >1.3 m high, crown density is >30%; 2) Land is or it is intended to be managed to get timber and other forest products or where trees are conserved for use in other ways (nature conservation, environment protection, sanitary protection, recreation, hygiene and sport, research and studies, multiple use, hunting, state security); 3) Ability to produce timber in the long run of at least 1 m3 of bole timber per 1 " .

:def_Forest_Estonia_nd_007
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Estonia ;
    :sourceRef "Sulev Svilponis <Sulev@ekm.envir.ee>" ;
    :definitionText "(Estonia) Forest land [metsamaa] - Land which is used for forestry. Forest land can be divided: - land with forest (stands), - land without forest (not regenerated cut over areas, treeless, openings, burnt woodlands, perished stands) - young silvicultures which are not yet dense enough, - tree nurseries. Estonian Encyclopedia From: \"Sulev Svilponis\" Sulev@ekm.envir.ee. Definitions are unofficial translations." .

:def_Forest_FIJI_2016_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :FIJI ;
    dcterms:date "2016"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.parliament.gov.fj/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/Bill-No-13-Forest.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(FIJI 2016) “forest” includes but is not limited to— (a) land spanning more than 0.5 hectares with trees higher than 5 metres and a canopy cover of more than 10 percent, or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ; (b) areas with bamboo and forest palms provided that height and canopy cover criteria are met; forest road, fire breaks and other small open areas; (c) areas defined by both the presence of trees and the absence of other predominant land uses; and (d) excluding tree stands in agri" .

:def_Forest_Finland_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Finland ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Finland 1997) Land with the potential capacity to produce a mean annual increment of at least 1 m3/ha stemwood, over bark, given an optimum tree species mixture, growing stock volume and prescribed rotations. (European Communities 1997a - p. 186)." .

:def_Forest_Finland_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Finland ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Finland 2000) - Finland adopts two definitions of forests: one is the FRA FAO 2000 definition: “Forest is land spanning more than 0.5 ha with trees higher than 5 m and a canopy cover of more than 10%, or trees able to reach these 5 m thresholds in situ. It does not include land that is predominantly under agricultural or urban land use.” METLA (Finnish Forest Research Institute), 2009. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Finland_2009_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Finland ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Finland 2009) The second definition is the national definition of forest that in Finland is the same as in the two other Nordic countries, Sweden and Norway: forest is defined as a land capable of producing an annual increment of volume growing stock of at least 1 m3/ha per year over the rotation under the most favorable tree species composition, and not used for any other purpose than forestry or forestry related purposes. METLA (Finnish Forest Research Institute)," .

:def_Forest_France_2011_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :France ;
    dcterms:date "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "20.2343"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www6.nancy.inra.fr/lef_eng/LEF-Data-Group/Tools/Glossary/" ;
    :definitionText "(France 2011) Forest: Wooden area of 50 acres with trees able to reach a height greater than five meters at maturity in situ, a of more than 10% and a width of at least 20 meters. Areas temporarily cleared or regenerating forests are classified as though they covered less than 10% during the inventory. Note: poplar (rate of free covered poplar grown on more than 75%) are included in the definition of forest. In contrast, walnut groves and chestnut groves as well as truffle cultivation and orchar" .

:def_Forest_Gabon_1982_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Gabon ;
    dcterms:date "1982"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Gabon 1982) Sont qualifiés de forêts au sens de la présente loi, les périmètres comportant ou non une couverture végétale et capables: soit de foumir du bois ou des produits végétaux autres qu'agricoles; soit d'abriter la faune sauvage; soit d'exercer un effet direct ou indirect sur le sol, le climat ou le régime des eaux. Source: Loi no. 1/82/PR, 22 Juillet 1982, d'orientation en matière des Eaux et Forêts Title II, Article 9 (Jean-Pierre Profizi)" .

:def_Forest_Germany_1975_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Germany ;
    dcterms:date "1975"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.landconsult.de/markus/foram/home/forrev2.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Germany 1975) A forest (\"Wald\") in the meaning of the Federal Forest Act (Section 2) is \"(1)... every tract of land planted with forest plants. Also to be rated as forests are clear-cut or thinned out tracts of land, forest tracks and roads, forest marking-off-safety strips, gaps in the forest cover as well as clearings, forest meadows, game feeding points, timber storing points as well as other areas connected with forests and ancillary to them. (2) Smaller lots planted with individual cluster" .

:def_Forest_Germany_2001_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Germany ;
    dcterms:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "50.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Germany 2001) Forest within the meaning of the FFI (Federal Forest Inventory) is any area of ground covered by forest vegetation, irrespective of the information in the cadastal survey or similar records. The term forest also refers to cutover or thinned areas, forest tracks, firebreaks, openings and clearings, forest glades, feeding grounds for game, landings, rides located in the forest, further areas linked to and serving the forest including areas with recreation facilities, overgrown heath" .

:def_Forest_Germany_2002_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Germany ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "50.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Germany 2002) - The National Forest Inventory definition follows the definition of forest under the Federal Forest Act: Forest within the meaning of the NFI is any area of ground covered by forest vegetation, irrespective of the information in the cadastral survey or similar records. The term forest also refers to cutover or thinned areas, forest tracks, fire breaks, openings and clearings, forest glades, feeding grounds for game, landings, rides located in the forest, further areas linked to a" .

:def_Forest_Germany1997_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Germany1997 ;
    :canopyThreshold "50.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Germany1997) Any area stocked with woody plants. Forest include clear-felled areas, forest roads, forest meadows, game pastures, timber yards, pipe routes located in the forest, further recreation facilities connected with the forest, overgrown heathens and moors, overgrown former meadows, alpine areas and rough grazing as well as dwarf pine and green alder areas. Heathens, moors, meadows, alpine areas and rough grazing are considered overgrown when the natural stocking has an average age of 5 " .

:def_Forest_Ghana_2006_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Ghana ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "15.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Ghana 2006 KP) Use Min. Area (ha) = 0.1 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 15 Min. Tree Height (m) = 2 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA/index.html - Sasaki & Putz 2009" .

:def_Forest_Greece_1992_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Greece ;
    dcterms:date "1992"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://bookshop.europa.eu/is-bin/INTERSHOP.enfinity/WFS/EU-Bookshop-Site/en_GB/-/EUR/ViewPDFFile-OpenPDFFile?FileName=LBNA24300ENC_002.pdf&SKU=LBNA24300ENC_PDF" ;
    :definitionText "(Greece 1992) Forest Land includes: (a) areas larger than 0.5 ha or strips more than 30 m wide with tree crown cover (stand density) of more than 10% of the area, or areas with 250 trees of reproductive age per hectare, able to produce wood or other products or services and are not used for any other land-use (b) areas where trees are removed to below 10% of stand density and are not given for other landuse (c) reforested areas and (d) scrublands (areas covered by broadleaved evergreens). http:/" .

:def_Forest_Greece_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Greece ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Greece 1997) Areas with 0.5 ha or 30cm (30 m?) strips with a tree crown closure that covers 10% of the area, or areas with 250 trees of a regeneration size not used for other purposes, and which are able to produce forest products or/and other services. Includes areas where trees have been removed with a crown closure less than 10% and they have not been used for other purposes, areas with regeneration, brush lands (areas covered by evergreen broad-leaved trees) Includes other wooded lands. (Eu" .

:def_Forest_Greece_2001_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Greece ;
    dcterms:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Greece 2001) NATIONAL DEFINITIONS. Area with 0.5 ha or 30 m strips with a tree crown closure that covers 10% of the area, or areas with 250 trees of a regeneration size, not used for other purposes or/and other services. Area where trees have been removed with a crown closure less than 10% and they have not been used for other purposes. Area with regeneration. Brush lands (area covered by evergreen broadleaved trees http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_repo" .

:def_Forest_Greece_2002_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Greece ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.05"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/ir_06.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Greece 2002) 1) Areas with 0.05 ha or 30 cm (30 m?) strips with a tree crown closure that covers 10% of the area, or areas with 250 trees of regeneration size not used for other purposes or/ and other services. 2) Areas where trees have been removed with a crown closure less than 10% and that have not been used for other purposes. 3) Areas with regeneration. 4) Brush lands (areas covered by evergreen broad-leaved trees.) Schuck, Andreas et al. 2002. Compilation of forestry terms and definitions" .

:def_Forest_Greece_2008_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Greece ;
    dcterms:date "2008"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.rainforestcoalition.org/TinyMceFiles/2008-presentations/Grassi_Berlin%20March%2016-18%202008.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Greece 2008) Includes: (a) areas larger than 0.5 ha or strips more than 30 m wide with tree crown cover (stand density) of more than 10% of the area, or areas with 250 trees of reproductive age per hectare, able to produce wood or other products or services and are not used for any other land-use (b) areas where trees are removed to below 10% of stand density and are not given for other land-use (c) reforested areas and (d) scrublands (areas covered by broadleaved evergreens). Grassi, Giacomo. " .

:def_Forest_Greece_2013_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Greece ;
    dcterms:date "2013"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Greece 2013) NEW DEFINTION: Forest is a land with 10% crown cover with minimum height of trees of 5 m at maturity (in situ); areas of approximately 0.5 ha or strips with widths of 30 m (with tree canopy cover of 10%); areas not used for any purpose other than production of wood. Galatsidas S. 2001. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Grenada_1949_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Grenada ;
    dcterms:date "1949"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Grenada 1949) \"Timber lands\" means lands whereon trees are growing and which are not under permanent agricultural cultivation. LEX-FAOC005062. GRENADA: Forest, Soil and Water Conservation Ordinance. An ordinance to make provision for the conservation of forest, soil, water and other natural resources of the Colony. Date of original text: 01 August 1949" .

:def_Forest_Hungary_1996_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Hungary ;
    dcterms:date "1996"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Hungary 1996) Forest-land shall be: a) an area of one thousand five hundred square meters or more covered with wood-including also land with spontaneous afforestation and land temporarily utilized – together with the glades and fire strips located in it; b) an area of one thousand five hundred square meters or more on which forest plantation (seed sowing, planting of saplings, propagation) was performed; c) the area of a tree plantation of one thousand five hundred square meters or more covered" .

:def_Forest_Hungary_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Hungary ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Hungary 1997) A biocoenosis formed of arborescent plants of the species determined in an order by the Minister of Agriculture and of associated live beings (forest biocoenosis) together with its soil, irrespective of whether the growing stock or another components of the biocoenosis is temporarily missing. (Act No. LIV of 1996 on Forests and the Protection of Forests, Ministry of Agriculture, Republic of Hungary, Budapest, 1997)" .

:def_Forest_Hungary_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Hungary ;
    :areaMin "0.15"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Hungary) Forest - Biocenosis formed of arborescent plants and associated live beings (forest biocenosis) together with its soil, irrespective of whether the growing stock or other components of the biocenosis is temporarily missing, minimum size >0.15 ha for forest landhttp://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Hungary_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Hungary ;
    :areaMin "0.15"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Hungary) Forest land - Area of 0.15 ha or more covered with wood – including land with spontaneous afforestation, land temporarily utilized for other purposes - together with glades and fire strips located in it. Includes forest plantations (seed sowing, planting or coppice sprouting) of 0.15 ha or more. Includes: Forest lands smaller than the limit if surrounded by a real estate registered in a sector other than forestry; and Land directly serving forestry activities (listed explicitly in §9)." .

:def_Forest_Iceland_2010_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Iceland ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://groa.rala.is/Kortavefsja/ICELAND_NIR_2010.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Iceland 2010) Forest land: All land, not included under Settlements, presently covered with trees or woody vegetation more than 2 m high, crown cover of minimum 10% and at least 0.5 ha in continuous area and minimum width 20 m and also land which currently fall below these thresholds, but in situ expected to reach these thresholds at mature state. http://groa.rala.is/Kortavefsja/ICELAND_NIR_2010.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Iceland_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Iceland ;
    :sourceRef "Eysteinsson <throstur@simnet.is>" ;
    :definitionText "(Iceland) Forest land (skoglendi) - Land that is or will be, mostly or fully, covered by forest vegetation, natural or planted, forest or scrub*. *The Icelandic word \"kjarr\", which is translated as scrub, refers to low-growing and crooked birch and in some cases willows. Source: Latest draft of a new forestry act : Þröstur Eysteinsson <throstur@simnet.is" .

:def_Forest_India_2007_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "https://tribal.nic.in/FRA/data/FRARulesBook.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(India 2007) \"Forest land\" means land of any description falling within any forest area and includes unclassified forests, undermarcated forests, existing or deemed forests, protected forests, reserved forests, Sanctuaries and National Parks; https://tribal.nic.in/FRA/data/FRARulesBook.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Indonesia_1998_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Indonesia ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Indonesia 1998) Hutan adalah hamparan lahan yang berisi atau yang dikehendaki akan berisi pepohonan, unsur-unsur hayati lainnya, dan non-hayati yang secara keseluruhan merupakan satu kesatuan ekosistem. (Rancangan Undang-Undang Nomor .... Tahun 1998 tentang Kehutanan). (Translation: A forest is a spread out area filled with or planned to be filled with trees, other living (biological) and non-living elements which as a whole form a ecosystem unit. (Law on Forestry, Number ... Year 1998))Other t" .

:def_Forest_Indonesia_1998_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Indonesia ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://europe.mtnforum.org/rs/econfreports/MountainPeopleForestsAndTrees.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Indonesia 1998) the legal definition of forest in Indonesia is: \"a spread out area filled with or planned to be filled with trees, other living (biological) and non-living elements which as a whole form an ecosystem unit\" (Law on Forestry 1998, Tr. Nico Smith 1999). http://europe.mtnforum.org/rs/econfreports/MountainPeopleForestsAndTrees.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Ireland_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Ireland ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Ireland 1997) - Coillte estate - High forests- commercial forests and plantable bare land - capable of growing trees. (European Communities 1997a - p. 401)" .

:def_Forest_Ireland_2014_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Ireland ;
    dcterms:date "2014"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "https://www.agriculture.gov.ie/media/migration/forestry/forestrythelaw/ForestryAct2014240517.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Ireland 2014) “Forest” means land under trees with— (a) a minimum area of 0.1 hectare, and (b) tree crown cover of more than 20 per cent of the total area, or the potential to achieve this cover at maturity, and includes all species of trees; https://www.agriculture.gov.ie/media/migration/forestry/forestrythelaw/ForestryAct2014240517.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Italy_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Italy ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Italy 1997) A territory with one or more of the following characteristics: purpose to wood or non-wood productions currently regards as forested, contain tree or bush stands with direct or indirect function of protection, contain spontaneous tree or bush stands with naturalist, scenic or recreation function. Included also are areas temporarily without a stand because cutting or exceptional occurrence. Not included city parks, gardens, nurseries, orchards, etc. (European Communities 1997a - p. 4" .

:def_Forest_Italy_2007_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Italy ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Italy 2007) - Land with tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 10% and area of more than 0.5 ha. The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 m at maturity in situ. May consist either of closed forest formations where trees of various stories and undergrowth cover a high proportion of the ground; or open forest formations with a continuous vegetation cover in which tree crown cover exceeds 10%. Young natural stands and all plantations established for forestry pu" .

:def_Forest_Japan_legal_definition_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Japan_legal_definition ;
    :sourceRef "Yukichi Konohira <Konohira@cc.tuat.ac.jp>" ;
    :definitionText "(Japan - legal definition) - 1) Land aimed at growing a group of trees (includes a non-forested land at present) or 2) a mountainous area with tree cover registered as 'forest' on a land register. Note: House lots and shrine enclosures being not aimed at growing trees are not forests even if they are covered with trees. Yukichi Konohira Konohira@cc.tuat.ac.jp" .

:def_Forest_Japan_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Japan ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.3"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/aarepjpn_4.1e.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Japan 2006 KP) Use Min. Area (ha) = 0.3 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 30 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = 20 http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/aarepjpn_4.1e.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Japan_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Japan ;
    :sourceRef "Masahiro Amano <masahiro@ss.ffpri.affrc.go.jp>" ;
    :definitionText "(Japan) Forest: In this law, FOREST shall be defined as listed below. The definition, however, shall exclude lands used for agriculture, housing, or equivalent purposes and standing trees and bamboo upon those lands. (1) Lands with trees and bamboo in groups and standing tree and bamboo upon the lands. (2) Besides the lands mentioned in the paragraphs, lands that serve as habitats for trees and bamboo. Definition of Forest Law, Forest Agency. From: Masahiro Amano masahiro@ss.ffpri.affrc.go.jp" .

:def_Forest_Kenya_2005_005
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Kenya ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.donorplatform.org/load/5971" ;
    :definitionText "(Kenya 2005) Forests are often thought of as areas with continuous tree cover consisting either of naturally occurring (indigenous) tree species or plantations. However, this definition ignores the importance of open savannah or dry land forests in which individual trees are scattered over wide areas of grassland. It also fails to cover small groups of trees planted on farms and other cultivated land. It is these dry land forests and farm trees that provide important livelihood strategies for ma" .

:def_Forest_Kenya_2015_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Kenya ;
    dcterms:date "2015"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.kenyaforestservice.org/documents/ForestConservationandManagementActNo34of2016.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Kenya 2015) “Forestland\" means a tract of land, including its flora and fauna, that is devoted to growing trees for the production of timber, wood and other forest products; http://www.kenyaforestservice.org/documents/ForestConservationandManagementActNo34of2016.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Korea_Republic_of_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Korea_Republic_of ;
    :sourceRef "Duck Koo <koochangd@hotmail.com>" ;
    :definitionText "(Korea, Republic of) Forest is defined as one of followings: 1. collectively standing and growing trees and bamboos, and the land that have them. 2. the land that temporarily lost standing trees and bamboos. 3. the land that is used for collectively growing trees and bamboos. 4. forestry roads. 5. rockland and wetland within 1, 2 and 3. Forest does not include followings 1. Orchard 2. the land that have growing trees and bamboos within buildings 3. the road with growing street trees. 4. stream b" .

:def_Forest_Korea_Republic_of_2015_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Korea_Republic_of ;
    dcterms:date "2015"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/3/a-i5444e.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Korea, Republic of- 2015) The Republic of Korea defines forest as including not only stands of timber and bamboo and the land on which they are growing, but also land that has temporarily lost its stands of timber and bamboo. Source: KFS, 2015; agricultural land area from World Bank, 2015 http://www.fao.org/3/a-i5444e.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Kyrgyz_1999_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Kyrgyz ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.libertas-institut.com/de/Mittel-Osteuropa/Forest%20Code.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Kyrgyz 1999) Forest lands are lands of the Forest Fund both covered and uncovered by forest and intended for forest growing. Forest Code of the Kyrgyz Republic: http://www.libertas-institut.com/de/Mittel-Osteuropa/Forest%20Code.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Kyrgyzstan_1999_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Kyrgyzstan ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.libertas-institut.com/de/Mittel-Osteuropa/Forest%20Code.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Kyrgyzstan -1999) - Forest lands Lands of the Forest Fund both covered and uncovered by forest and intended for forest growing. Source: Irina Yunusova irina@lesic.elcat.kg and http://www.libertas-institut.com/de/Mittel-Osteuropa/Forest%20Code.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Kyrgyzstan_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Kyrgyzstan ;
    :sourceRef "Irina Yunusova <irina@lesic.elcat.kg>" ;
    :definitionText "(Kyrgyzstan) (forest?) areas - - Areas both covered and not covered with the forest territories included into the National Forest Fund (stock). The main use of such lands is forest planting and growing. Source: Irina Yunusova irina@lesic.elcat.kg" .

:def_Forest_Latvia_2000_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Latvia ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/docrep/article/WFC/XII/0504-C3.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Latvia 2000) According to the Forest Law of the Republic of Latvia adopted in 2000 (Item 2, Paragraph 3, Section 1) \"forestland is the land carrying the forest, the land under forest infrastructure facilities, as well as overflowing clearings, bogs and glades in the forest and in the territories contiguous to it\". http://www.fao.org/docrep/article/WFC/XII/0504-C3.htm" .

:def_Forest_Latvia_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Latvia ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Latvia) Forest land includes areas which constitute an integral part of the forest: forest roads, cleared tracts, firebreaks and other small open areas within the forest. http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Latvia_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Latvia ;
    :sourceRef "Maksym Polyakov <mpoliak@pcomp.nauu.kiev.ua>" ;
    :definitionText "(Latvia) Rural or urban land covered by forest or land which is not covered by forest but prescribed for forest growing in compliance with the State Land Cadastre. Source: \"Maksym Polyakov\" mpoliak@pcomp.nauu.kiev.ua" .

:def_Forest_Latvia_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Latvia ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "7.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Latvia) The forest definition is not included in Forest Act. State Land Service for land use inventory is applying the following definition of forest and forest land: Land with tree crown cover of more than 20% and area of more than 0.1 ha. The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 7m at maturity in situ. Young natural stands and artificially reforested areas of more than 0.1 ha, up to 20 years old with mean height >1m and number of trees 2000-3000/ha (depends on species). Includes " .

:def_Forest_Lebanon_2011_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Lebanon ;
    dcterms:date "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.tradingeconomics.com/lebanon/forest-area-percent-of-land-area-wb-data.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Lebanon- 2011) land under natural or planted stands of trees of at least 5 meters in situ, whether productive or not, and excludes tree stands in agricultural production systems (for example, in fruit plantations and agroforestry systems) and trees in urban parks and gardens. http://www.tradingeconomics.com/lebanon/forest-area-percent-of-land-area-wb-data.html" .

:def_Forest_Lesotho_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Lesotho ;
    :definitionText "(Lesotho) - Forest - Any existing area of land under section 11 and any areas of land used for forestry, or declared forestry use, under sections 12, 13, and 14 of this Act. Forestry Act 1998. Via David May ISTF CVP Lesotho." .

:def_Forest_Liberia_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Liberia ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/forestry/16151-05fd47b845599b5d3a594a9b0240dacff.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Liberia 2006) Forest Land: A tract of land, including its flora and fauna, capable of producing Forest Resources, not including land in urban areas, land in permanent settlements, and land that has been in long-term use for non-shifting cultivation of crops or livestock in a manner that precludes producing Forest Resources. An Act Adopting the National Forestry Reform Law of 2006. http://www.fao.org/forestry/16151-05fd47b845599b5d3a594a9b0240dacff.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Liberia_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Liberia ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.forestcarbonpartnership.org/fcp/sites/forestcarbonpartnership.org/files/Documents/PDF/May2011/Liberia%20R-PP%20revised%20draft%20for%20presubmission%2017-03-11.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Liberia KP) Liberia is proposing a forest definition that consists of a minimum canopy cover of 30%, trees greater than 5 meters, and a minimum mapping unit of 1 hectare. http://www.forestcarbonpartnership.org/fcp/sites/forestcarbonpartnership.org/files/Documents/PDF/May2011/Liberia%20R-PP%20revised%20draft%20for%20presubmission%2017-03-11.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Liechtenstein_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Liechtenstein ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.0625"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/initial-report-lie.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Liechtenstein 2006 KP) Use Min. Area (ha) = 0.0625- 0.25 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 20-60 Min. Tree Height (m) = 3 Min. Strip Width (m) = 25-50 http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/initial-report-lie.pdf (2006). The following forest areas are not subject to the criterion of minimum stand height: shrub forest consisting of dwarf pine (Pinus mugo prostrata) and alpine alder (Alnus viridis). The following forest areas are not subject of the " .

:def_Forest_Lithuania_2001_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Lithuania ;
    dcterms:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.seniejitrakai.lt/law-on-the-amendment" ;
    :definitionText "(Lithuania 2001) Forest –a land area not less than 0.1 hectare in size covered with trees, the height of which in a natural site in the maturity age is not less than 5 meters, other forest plants as well as thinned or vegetation-lost forest due to the acts of nature or human activities (cutting areas, burnt areas, clearings). Tree lines up to 10 meters of width in fields, at roadsides, water bodies, in living areas and cemeteries , single trees and bushes, parks planted and grown by man in urban" .

:def_Forest_Lithuania_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Lithuania ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/initial_report_lithuania.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Lithuania 2006 KP) Use Min. Area (ha) = 0.1 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 10 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = 10 http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/initial_report_lithuania.pdf (2006) Temporarily unstocked areas (forest regeneration areas) are included" .

:def_Forest_Lithuania_2010_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Lithuania ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Lithuania 2010) Forest land NFI is: a land area not less than 0.1 ha in size covered with trees, the height of which in a natural site in the maturity age is not less than 5 m, other forest plants as well as thinned or vegetation lost forest due to the acts of nature or human activities (cutting areas, burnt areas, clearings). Forest pitches, nursery areas, forest seed orchards, raw-material bushings and plantation, forest roads, forest block, technological and fire break lines, areas covered b" .

:def_Forest_Lithuania_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Lithuania ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Lithuania) Forest - A tract of land not less than 0.1 ha, covered with trees or other forest vegetation or temporarily without it (cleared or burned areas). Not considered a forest: Clusters of trees situated in fields, by roadsides, water bodies, within towns or rural settlements as well as cemeteries, narrow - up to 10 metres - tree lines, hedges, single trees, shrubs as well as parks planted by man within towns and rural settlements. http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEuro" .

:def_Forest_Lithuania_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Lithuania ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "Sekrtetore <sek@mp.is.lt>" ;
    :definitionText "(Lithuania) Forest - land area, no less than 0,1 ha, covered by trees and other forest plants or temporarily has lost them (clear-cut and burnt areas). Narrow belts up to 10 m, small groups and single trees in villages and towns, also artificially established parks are not forests. In forest inventory we use such a restriction: all forests must have site index - 11 m and more. Forests with less productivity, mainly growing on peatlands are inventoried as peatlands covered by woody plants (Other " .

:def_Forest_Lithuania_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Lithuania ;
    :sourceRef "Sekrtetore <sek@mp.is.lt>" ;
    :definitionText "(Lithuania) Forest land - areas of land, covered by forest (stands) and without forests (clear-cut, destructed areas, glades, nurseries, seed orchards, woody plants and special plantations for preparation of various raw materials). Forest land also includes forest roads, block lines, border lines, technological lines, antifire belts, timber yards, other areas for technological, recreational needs, game forage, also land nominated for afforestation. Source: A. Kuliesis, Director of Lithuanain For" .

:def_Forest_Lithuania_nd_005
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Lithuania ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Lithuania) Forest land is land covered by forest stands or not covered by forest (cleared areas, perished stands, forest meadows, nurseries, seed-plots, seed orchards and raw shrubbery and plantations). Includes forest roads and drain ditches, forest compartment lines, technological and fire-prevention strips, piling places and facilities related to forest, rest spots, game feeding points, swamps, sands, as well as land for afforestation. Forest land may be forestry or conservation designated. " .

:def_Forest_Luxembourg_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Luxembourg ;
    :areaMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Luxembourg) Terres représentant un couvert forestier (ou peuplement équivalent) de plus de 10 % et une superficie supérieure à 0,5 ha. Les arbres doivent pouvoir atteindre une hauteur abattable minimale de 5 mètres. Ces forêts peuvent comprendre soit des formations forestières denses dont les divers étages et le sous-bois couvrent une forte proportion du sol, soit des formations forestières claires avec une strate herbacée continue dans lesquelles les cimes couvrent plus de 10 % de la superfici" .

:def_Forest_Macedonia_1997_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Macedonia ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Macedonia 1997) Land covered with forest tree and shrub as well as forest bare lands and forest roads, forest nurseries and other areas that are closely connected to forests. (Law on forests, 1997g., article 3). Republic Of Macedonia, Ministry Of Agriculture, Forestry And Water Economy. National Forestry Strategyfor Sustainable Development, 2002. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Macedonia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Macedonia ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Macedonia) - Forest - Land covered with forest trees and shrubs, including forest bare lands and meadows, pastures, nurseries, and area closely related to the forest, no area limit. http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Macedonia_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Macedonia ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Macedonia) Forest Land includes forest trees and shrubs, forest-bare lands and meadows, forest pastures, nurseries and other areas closely related to the forest. http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Madagascar_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Madagascar ;
    :definitionText "(Madagascar) (Article premier) Par forêt, au sens de la présente loi, on entend toutes surfaces répondant aux qualifications ci-après : - les surfaces couvertes d'arbres ou de végétation ligneuse, autres que plantées à des fins exclusives de production fruitière, de production de fourrage ou d'ornementation; - les surfaces occupées par les arbres et les buissons situés sur les berges des cours d'eau et lacs et sur des terrains érodés ; - les terrains dont les fruits exclusifs ou principaux sont " .

:def_Forest_Mali_1986_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Mali ;
    dcterms:date "1986"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Mali 1986) - Article premier. - Une forêt est une association d'arbres biologiquement interdépendants au cours de leur évolution et exerçant une influence sur le milieu dans un territoire plus ou moins grand. Les produits exclusifs ou principaux des forêts sont le bois d'oeuvre, le bois de service, le bois de chauffage, les résines, la gomme, les fuits et tous autres sous-produits ligneux. Art. 2 - Les périmètres de reboisement sont les terrains plantés de mains d'homme en espèces végetales ne " .

:def_Forest_Malta_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Malta ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Malta 2003) - Forest area is land under natural or planted stands of trees of at least 5 m in situ, whether productive or not, and excludes tree stands in agricultural production systems (for example, in fruit plantations and agroforestry systems) and trees in urban parks and gardens. EarthTrends, 2003. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Mexico_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Mexico ;
    :sourceRef "Inventario <varelah@servidor.unam.mx>" ;
    :definitionText "(Mexico) (Forestal).- Todo aquello que se relaciona con los bosques. Esta definición es adecuada desde el punto de vista económico y social, ya que da idea de la relación entre las áreas arboladas y la población. Sin embargo es más ambigua por la desigualdad en cada país en la distribución de la población urbana y rural Source: Glosario de Términos de la Memoria del Inventario Nacional Forestal Periódico y del Reglamento de la Ley Forestal from Unidad del Inventario <varelah@servidor.unam.mx" .

:def_Forest_Mexico_2014_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Mexico ;
    dcterms:date "2014"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "4.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "50.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://redd.unfccc.int/files/frel_mexico_modified.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Mexico 2014) - In the LGDFS, the definition of “forest land” comprises all lands covered by “forest vegetation”, and “forest vegetation” is defined as \"the set of plants and fungi that grow and develop naturally, forming temperate forests, tropical forests, arid and semi-arid areas, and other ecosystems.\" According to the definition above, forest is defined as all \"Forest Lands” with a canopy cover of more than 10 percent, with trees of more than 4 meters in height −or trees able to reach this " .

:def_Forest_Morocco_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Morocco ;
    :sourceRef "m.ellatifi@ellatifi.8m.com" ;
    :definitionText "(Morocco) Forest land /Forest domain (Arabic : Ard ghabawyah/Milk ghabawee, French : Terrain forestier/Domaine forestier, Spanish : Terreno forestal) - Land covered with a forest, or land belonging to the State and put under the control of the forest Service, even if it does not any more trees on it (but did in the past). Mohammed Ellatifi, m.ellatifi@ellatifi.8m.com" .

:def_Forest_Nepal_2002_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Nepal ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.bioone.org/doi/pdf/10.1659/0276-4741(2002" ;
    :definitionText "(Nepal 2002) - Area where trees with well-defined stems are growing and crown coverage is more than 10 per cent. Area must not be used primarily for uses other than forestry (widely understood) and must be at least 100 m wide. Area can include treeless patches not wider than 25 m and not exceeding 1 hectare. http://www.bioone.org/doi/pdf/10.1659/0276-4741(2002)022 per cent5B0085:IONSFR per cent5D2.0.CO per cent3B2" .

:def_Forest_Nepal_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Nepal ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/forestry/fo/country/index.jsp?lang_id=1&geo_id=35" ;
    :definitionText "(Nepal) Forest is defined as all land with a forest cover, i.e. with trees whose crowns cover more than 10% of the area, and not used primarily for purposes other than forestry. Temporarily clear-cut area that will be planted is also forest area. http://www.fao.org/forestry/fo/country/index.jsp?lang_id=1&geo_id=35" .

:def_Forest_Netherlands_2006_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Netherlands ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/initial_report_final_191206.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Netherlands 2006 KP) Use Min. Area (ha) = 0.5 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 20 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = 30 May consist either of closed forest formations where trees of various storeys and undergrowth cover a high proportion of the ground; or of open forest formations with a continuous vegetation cover in which tree crown cover exceeds 20 per cent. Young natural stands and all plantations established for forestry purposes which have yet to reach a crown density of 20 per cent or" .

:def_Forest_New_Zealand_1949_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :New_Zealand ;
    dcterms:date "1949"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(New Zealand 1949) Forest land - Land on which forest is growing, land used for agroforestry, and land intended to be forested or used for agroforestry by the owner or occupier of the land. (from Forests Act 1949)." .

:def_Forest_New_Zealand_2006_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :New_Zealand ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.cbd.int/doc/world/us/us-nr-vfe-en.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(New Zealand 2006) Use Min. Area (ha) = 5 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 20 Min. Tree Height (m) = 6 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns \"Tree\" includes not only timber trees- but also all other kinds of trees- shrubs- and bushes- seedlings- saplings- cuttings- suckers- and shoots of every description. http://www.cbd.int/doc/world/us/us-nr-vfe-en.pdf lists the minimum area of 0.5 ha. (2003) and USFS 2004. “Forests planted in exotic tree species predominately grown for wood or wood fibre greater than 1 ha in exten" .

:def_Forest_New_Zealand_2011_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :New_Zealand ;
    dcterms:date "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.maf.govt.nz/portals/0/documents/forestry/forestry-ets/2011-ETS-look-up-tables-guide.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(New Zealand 2011) Forest land: (a) means an area of land of at least 1 hectare that has, or is likely to have, tree crown cover from forest species of more than 30 percent in each hectare; and (b) includes an area of land that temporarily does not meet the requirements specified in paragraph (a) because of human intervention or natural causes but that is likely to revert to land that meets the requirements specified in paragraph (a); (c) does not include: – a shelter belt of forest species, whe" .

:def_Forest_New_Zealand_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :New_Zealand ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.climatechange.govt.nz/glossary.html#f" ;
    :definitionText "(New Zealand) Forest land - A minimum area of land of one hectare with tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 30 per cent with trees with the potential to reach a minimum height of five metres at maturity in situ. This category includes all land with woody vegetation consistent with thresholds used to define forest land in the national GHG inventory, sub-divided at the national level into managed and unmanaged and also by ecosystem type as specified in the IPCC Guidelines.6" .

:def_Forest_New_Zealand_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :New_Zealand ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.environment.govt.nz/footprint/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "(New Zealand) Forest land - land used for the production of commercial forests - http://www.environment.govt.nz/footprint/glossary.html" .

:def_Forest_Niger_1974_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Niger ;
    dcterms:date "1974"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Niger 1974) Sont qualifiés forêts, les terrains dont les fruits exclusifs ou principaux sont les bois d'ébénisterie, les bois de service ou d'industrie, les bois de chauffage et à charbon, ou des produits accessoires tels que : les écorces et fruits à tanin, les écorces textiles et tinctoriales, le kapok, la glu, les gommes, les palmiers spontanés et tous autres végétaux ne constituant pas un produit agricole. Article 2: LEX-FAOC002294. NIGER: Loi n&ordm; 74-7 du 4 mars 1974 fixant le régime fo" .

:def_Forest_Norway_1992_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Norway ;
    dcterms:date "1992"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Norway 1992) - Forest is Land spanning more than 0.5 ha with trees higher than 5 m and a canopy cover of more than 10%, or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ. It does not include land that is predominantly under agricultural or urban land use. Productive forest area: Forest area that under favourable stand conditions has an annual yield capacity per hectare of at least 1 cubic metre of wood including bark. Noregs Offisielle Statistikk, 1992. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/public" .

:def_Forest_Norway_1993_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Norway ;
    dcterms:date "1993"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nijos.no/panorama/!skog.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Norway 1993) Land which produces forest or which on an overall farming- and forestry assessment is considered to be most suitable for forest production and is not being used for any other purpose. [Source: The Norwegian Forest and Forest Protection Act of May 21, 1965 with amendments, latest by the Act no. 96 of June 11, 1993. http://www.nijos.no/panorama/!skog.htm From: \"Maksym Polyakov\" <mpoliak@pcomp.usau.kiev.ua Date: Mon, 15 Jun 1998 19:27:19 +0300 (MSD)]" .

:def_Forest_Norway_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Norway ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Norway 1997) Productive forest land - Land with an average potential production equal to or higher than 1 m3 (including bark) per ha and year regardless of the current stocking (European Communities 1997b - p. 832)." .

:def_Forest_Norway_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Norway ;
    :sourceRef "http://odin.dep.no/ld/engelsk/dep/020001-200002/index-dok000-b-n-a.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Norway) For the purpose of this Act, «forest land» means land which produces forest 2) or which on an overall farming- and forestry assessment is considered to be most suitable for forest production and is not being used for any other purpose. http://odin.dep.no/ld/engelsk/dep/020001-200002/index-dok000-b-n-a.html" .

:def_Forest_Pakistan_1953_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Pakistan ;
    dcterms:date "1953"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Pakistan 1953) Forest - An area set aside for the production of timber and other forest produce, or maintained under woody vegetation for certain indirect benefits which it provides e.g. climatic or protective. Definition adopted from the British Commonwealth Forest Terminology Part-I, 1953. Source: Mumtaz Ahmad, Section Forest Officer, Pakistan Min. of Environment, Local Government, and Rural Development." .

:def_Forest_Paraguay_2015_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Paraguay ;
    dcterms:date "2015"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://redd.unfccc.int/files/2016_submission_frel_paraguay_es.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Paraguay 2015) Definición de bosque nativo - En Paraguay, a los efectos de REDD+ el bosque nativo es un ecosistema natural con diversidad biológica, intervenido o no, regenerado y/o restaurado por sucesión natural o técnicas forestales de enriquecimiento con especies nativas, que produce bienes, provee servicios ambientales y sociales, cuya superficie mínima es de 1 ha, con una altura de los árboles igual o mayor a 3 m en la Región Occidental e igual o mayor a 5 m en la Región Oriental, y que a" .

:def_Forest_Peru_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Peru ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.mef.gob.pe/DGCP/Documentacion/fondos/PERU_USA/convenio_dinat.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Peru) “Forest Land” means (i) that portion of SINANPE described in Exhibit A, which will be conserved, maintained and restored with funds provided pursuant to the Forest Conservation Agreement, and (ii) any other forest land in Perú approved for conservation, maintenance and restoration by a majority vote of the Oversight Committee in accordance with the terms of the Forest Conservation Agreement. http://www.mef.gob.pe/DGCP/Documentacion/fondos/PERU_USA/convenio_dinat.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Philippines_nd_005
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Philippines ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.chanrobles.com/pd705.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Philippines) - Forest lands include the public forest, the permanent forest or forest reserves, and forest reservations. Public forest is the mass of lands of the public domain which has not been the subject of the present system of classification for the determination of which lands are needed for forest purposes and which are not. b. Permanent forest or forest reserves refers to those lands of the public domain which have been the subject of the present system of classification and declared a" .

:def_Forest_Philippines1904_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Philippines1904 ;
    :sourceRef "https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/119973" ;
    :definitionText "(Philippines1904) Public forests and torest reserves shall include all unreserved public lands covered with trees of whatever age. https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/119973" .

:def_Forest_Poland_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Poland ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Poland 1997) A ground covered with a forest vegetation, of area above 0.1 ha; it includes forest grounds, temporarily deprived of forest vegetation, and grounds related to forestry (forest roads, nurseries, etc.). (European Communities 1997b - p. 1251). Forest roads, nurseries, etc. excluded. For FRA 2000 - Source: UN/ECE 2000 p 83" .

:def_Forest_Poland_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Poland ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/raport_aau_eng_22-12-06.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Poland 2006 KP) Use Min. Area (ha) = 0.1 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 10 Min. Tree Height (m) = 2 Min. Strip Width (m) = 10 http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/raport_aau_eng_22-12-06.pdf (2006)" .

:def_Forest_Poland_2010_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Poland ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Poland 2010) (1) Land covered with forest vegetation, of area above 0.1 ha; it includes forest grounds temporarily deprived of forest vegetation, and (2) Lands related to forestry (forest roads, nurseries etc.) (FAO 2010). http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Poland_2012_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Poland ;
    dcterms:date "2012"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.stat.gov.pl/gus/definicje_ENG_HTML.htm?id=ANG-3369.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Poland 2012) Land covered with forest plants or lacking such plants for a temporary period of time as well as land associate with forestry management. Land covered with forest crops, young woodland and older trees as well as plantations of poplar and other fast growing trees being maintained both on forest land as well as outside of forests is included in forest land surface area. Land that has been temporarily deprived of trees and which includes logged over forest, blanks, irregularly stocked" .

:def_Forest_Poland_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Poland ;
    :sourceRef "http://icaci.org/documents/ICC_proceedings/ICC2011/Oral%20Presentations%20PDF/A3-Data%20integration/CO-028.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Poland? ) In SLMN forest is defined as an area of land use categories Ls wooded, with trees older than 20 years. http://icaci.org/documents/ICC_proceedings/ICC2011/Oral%20Presentations%20PDF/A3-Data%20integration/CO-028.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Portugal_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Portugal ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Portugal 1997) Every portion of land with a greater than 2000 m2 and 15 m wide, is considered forest area. Forest area includes exploitable forests, recently harvested or burned areas, recent seedlings and plantations, and green zones (reserves, protection forests and recreation forests). (European Communities 1997b - p. 879)." .

:def_Forest_Romania_2007_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Romania ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/romanias_initial_report_under_the_kyoto_protocol.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Romania 2007 KP) Use Min. Area (ha) = 0.25 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 10 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = ns http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/romanias_initial_report_under_the_kyoto_protocol.pdf (2007) includes also: forest nurseries, trees genetic trials within the forest land, forest pathways and roads, meadows, glades and other forest gaps, forest ecosystems within the national and natural parks, natural protected ar" .

:def_Forest_Romania_nd_006
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Romania ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Romania) Forest land - Land belonging to the national forest estate, and that intended for afforested to serve silvicultural, production and/or other needs. http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Russia_European_Part_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Russia_European_Part ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Russia (European Part) 2003) - Forest Land (FL) = covered by forest + uncovered by forest, comprises land which is suitable and designated for forest growth. FL is divided into following categories: Forested Areas; Non-Stocked Planted Forests; Forest Plantations and Nurseries; Natural Sparse Forests; and Unforested Areas. .Forested Areas include: (1) lands, covered by young stands with the relative stocking 0.4 and more, and stands of other age groups with the relative stocking 0.3 and more; (2" .

:def_Forest_Russian_Federation_1965_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Russian_Federation ;
    dcterms:date "1965"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Russian Federation 1965) Professional of Forest Inventory - Forest (forested area) includes lands: covered by young stands of tree species with relative stocking 0.4 and more, and stands of other age groups with relative stocking 0.3 and more; harvested areas, burnt stands and other forest lands, which are in the process of natural regeneration, and on which amount and quality of young trees both naturally regenerated or conserved during harvest is not less than those required by manuals applay" .

:def_Forest_Russian_Federation_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Russian_Federation ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Russian Federation 2000) - Forest includes land -wooded land (main and other forest-forming tree species), non-continuous forest growth, nurseries and plantations, and unwooded land-openings, slashes, dead stands, cuttings, clearings. For FRA 2000 - Source: UN/ECE 2000 p 85" .

:def_Forest_Russian_Federation1995_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Russian_Federation1995 ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fire.uni-freiburg.de/iffn/iffn_24/iffn24.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Russian Federation1995) Forest lands include lands covered by forest vegetation or those not covered by it but intended for its restoration (cutovers, slashes, perished forest stands, open stands [comment: better-sparse forests], wastelands, glades [comment: better-grassy glades and barrens], areas occupied by nurseries, free-growing forest cultures [comment; i.e., forest plantations], and others. http://www.fire.uni-freiburg.de/iffn/iffn_24/iffn24.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Rwanda_2013_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Rwanda ;
    dcterms:date "2013"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www-wds.worldbank.org/external/default/WDSContentServer/WDSP/IB/2014/08/14/000470435_20140814100003/Rendered/INDEX/PAD10410PAD0GE040Box385296B00OUO090.txt" ;
    :definitionText "(Rwanda 2013) land covered with trees, shrubs and other plants or land which was covered with trees and is in the process of regeneration or under replantation or land that has not been covered with trees but is intended for forestry purposes or other activities related to forests http://www-wds.worldbank.org/external/default/WDSContentServer/WDSP/IB/2014/08/14/000470435_20140814100003/Rendered/INDEX/PAD10410PAD0GE040Box385296B00OUO090.txt" .

:def_Forest_Rwanda_2014_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Rwanda ;
    dcterms:date "2014"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://knoema.com/WBWDIGDF2015Feb/world-development-indicators-wdi-february-2015" ;
    :definitionText "(Rwanda 2014) Land under natural or planted stands of trees of at least 5 meters in situ, whether productive or not, and excludes tree stands in agricultural production systems (for example, in fruit plantations and agroforestry systems) and trees in urban parks and gardens. http://knoema.com/WBWDIGDF2015Feb/world-development-indicators-wdi-february-2015" .

:def_Forest_Serbia_Montenegro_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Serbia_Montenegro ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.unece.org/trade/timber/docs/dp/dp-40.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Serbia & Montenegro) A forest is a forest area exceeding 0.5 ha. Hedgerows, municipal parks, forest nurseries and groups of trees on areas smaller then 0.5 ha are not considered forests. Plantations are forests raised from selected plant sources with intensive high yield measures (short rotation). Unstocked forest land includes land which yields the best results if forests are growing on it. http://www.unece.org/trade/timber/docs/dp/dp-40.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Serbia_2010_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Serbia ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.01"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Serbia 2010) - The inventory uses the definition of FRA FAO. A national definition is given in the FRA 2010 country report: A forest is every area over 5 are covered with forest trees in the form of stands having a protective function but is used for production of forest assortments or has a special purpose. Tree line paths, parks in inhabited places, forest tree nurseries, and groups of forest trees on an area under 5 are not considered a forest. [1are=0.01 ha] http://www.efi.int/files/attachm" .

:def_Forest_Seychelles_2011_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Seychelles ;
    dcterms:date "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.tradingeconomics.com/seychelles/forest-area-sq-km-wb-data.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Seychelles 2011) Land under natural or planted stands of trees of at least 5 meters in situ, whether productive or not, and excludes tree stands in agricultural production systems (for example, in fruit plantations and agroforestry systems) and trees in urban parks and gardens http://www.tradingeconomics.com/seychelles/forest-area-sq-km-wb-data.html" .

:def_Forest_Slovakia_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Slovakia ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.3"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/svk-_aaus-initial-_report-october-2006.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Slovakia 2006 KP) Use Min. Area (ha) = 0.3 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 20 Min. Tree Height (m) = 5 Min. Strip Width (m) = 20 http://unfccc.int/files/national_reports/initial_reports_under_the_kyoto_protocol/application/pdf/svk-_aaus-initial-_report-october-2006.pdf (2006) Temporarily unstocked areas are included (forest regeneration areas)." .

:def_Forest_Slovakia_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Slovakia ;
    :definitionText "(Slovakia) - Land determined to permanently fulfil the functions of forests (forest stands, forest nurseries, seed plantations, plots to be afforested, cleared boundary lines, skidding roads, infertile forest land, alpine land with specific functions) (M. Jasenská, Faculty of Wood Technology, Technical University Zvolen, Slovak Republic)" .

:def_Forest_Slovakia_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Slovakia ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Slovakia) Forest land includes the area of forest stands, nurseries, plantations, temporary clearings where forest is under regeneration, forest roads, meadows and other areas. http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Slovakia_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Slovakia ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.3"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://bookshop.europa.eu/is-bin/INTERSHOP.enfinity/WFS/EU-Bookshop-Site/en_GB/-/EUR/ViewPDFFile-OpenPDFFile?FileName=LBNA24300ENC_002.pdf&SKU=LBNA24300ENC_PDF" ;
    :definitionText "(Slovakia) Forest Land includes: land with minimum tree crown cover of 20 % for trees capable to reach minimum height of 5 m in situ. The minimum area for forest is 0.3 ha. Temporarily unstocked areas are included (forest regeneration areas). For linear formations, a minimum width of 20 m is applied. http://bookshop.europa.eu/is-bin/INTERSHOP.enfinity/WFS/EU-Bookshop-Site/en_GB/-/EUR/ViewPDFFile-OpenPDFFile?FileName=LBNA24300ENC_002.pdf&SKU=LBNA24300ENC_PDF" .

:def_Forest_Slovenia_1993_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Slovenia ;
    dcterms:date "1993"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.05"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Slovenia 1993) The term “forest” is defined also by the Law on Forests of Slovenia (Official Journal of the Republic of Slovenia, nr. 30/1993). Article two states: .... “A forest is an area of land, covered with forest trees in the form of stands or other forest growths which provide any of the functions of a forest. Forest, according to this law also includes overgrown plots of land which are defined as forest in the spatial part of the forest management plan. The forest infrastructure which i" .

:def_Forest_Slovenia_2011_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Slovenia ;
    dcterms:date "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "75.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.25"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Slovenia 2011) - The national forest inventory defines forest as: (a) A plot of land overgrown with forest trees in the form of stands, which can reach a height of at least 5 m and sized to at least 0.25 ha (b) A plot of agricultural land in transition to forest land sized to at least 0.25 ha that has not been used for agriculture for the last 20 years and is overgrown with forest trees which can reach a height of at least 5 m and their crown cover should be at least 75% (c) Riverside forest co" .

:def_Forest_Slovenia_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Slovenia ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.metla.fi/eu/cost/e43/minutes/wg1-min-florence.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Slovenia) Forest - National definition is use, probably close to FAO but a specific problem may be when to regard abandoned agriculture land as forest http://www.metla.fi/eu/cost/e43/minutes/wg1-min-florence.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Slovenia_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Slovenia ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Slovenia) Forest land is a forest or forest plot matching with the definition of forest, and non-forest plots of land ecologically or functionally linked to forest, together guaranteeing the performance of the function of forest. http://www.fris.sk/Phare/Projects/ManagementOfForestInEurope/PDF/annex2.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Solomon_Islands_2004_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Solomon_Islands ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.parliament.gov.sb/files/legislation/Bills/2004/The%20Forests%20Bill%202004.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Solomon Islands 2004) Forested land means an area of land predominately covered by trees other than trees planted for agricultural purposes. http://www.parliament.gov.sb/files/legislation/Bills/2004/The%20Forests%20Bill%202004.pdf" .

:def_Forest_South_Africa_nd_005
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :South_Africa ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nda.agric.za/doaDev/sideMenu/ForestryWeb/webapp/ResourceCentre/Documents/Policy" ;
    :definitionText "(South Africa) - In terms of the National Forests Act, 1998, forests include all natural forests, woodlands and plantations as well as the forest produce produced in it. In keeping with this definition, reference in this paper to forestry development and forest activities includes the use of these three categories of forest resources, as well as the primary processing of all timber, nontimber and non-wood forest products derived from these sources. http://www.nda.agric.za/doaDev/sideMenu/Forestr" .

:def_Forest_South_Africa_nd_006
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :South_Africa ;
    :definitionText "(South Africa) “Forest land”means any land covered by trees or which is designated in any legislation, or national or sub-national forestry plan, or land-use plan as forest land or as land for afforestation or reforestation; www.dwaf.gov.za/Forestry/Forestry%20Policy/October%202001%20draft%20Protocol.doc" .

:def_Forest_South_Sudan_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :South_Sudan ;
    :sourceRef "http://country-facts.findthedata.com/l/241/South-Sudan" ;
    :definitionText "(South Sudan) Forest area is land under natural or planted stands of trees of at least 5 meters in situ, whether productive or not, and excludes tree stands in agricultural production systems (for example, in fruit plantations and agroforestry systems) and trees in urban parks and gardens. http://country-facts.findthedata.com/l/241/South-Sudan" .

:def_Forest_Spain_1998_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Spain ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "7.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.25"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Spain 1998) Forest-tree lands. All lands with a forest-tree cover, at maturity, \"in situ, of more than 5% of the area, which is able to reach a minimum height of 7 m and to produce wood. Minimum area is 0.25 ha. Excludes wood lots and isolated tree groups with areas under 0.25 ha. Forest lands are divided into forest 20 % cc, open forests 5-20% cc, unstocked areas and complementary areas - roads, buildings, etc. related to forestry activities. Source: Establecimiento de una tipología de usos ag" .

:def_Forest_Spain_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Spain ;
    :definitionText "(Spain) Montes - de tierra en que vegetan espeices arbóreas arbustiva, de matorral o herbáceas, sea espontáneamente o prodedan de siembra o plantación, siempre que no sean caracteristicas del cultivo agricola o fueran objecto de mismo (Art. 1.2 Ley de Montes) Montes 57:49. A este en añaden en la Ley de Montes, las terrenos que haya quedado adscritos a la finalidad de ser repoblados y transformados en forestales, ye se excluyen en cambio los prados, las praderas cantá bricas y los terrenos en una" .

:def_Forest_Sweden_1992_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Sweden ;
    dcterms:date "1992"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Sweden 1992) Land suitable for wood production and not primarily used for other purposes. Potential yield under ideal management conditions at least 1 m3sk per hectare per year. Includes abandoned agricultural land and land user for grazing not yet covered by forest. Includes forest land with density of tree crowns = 0%. (UN/ECE 1992 p. 249)" .

:def_Forest_Sweden_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Sweden ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.25"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Sweden 1997) Land suitable for forest production, not used for other purposes, and with an average production higher than (or equal to) 1 m3 per hectare and year during a period of 100 years. The minimum area is 0.25 ha. (European Communities 1997b - p. 983)" .

:def_Forest_Sweden_2009_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Sweden ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Sweden 2009) Types of land under the Forestry Act Determined for the traditional types of land in productive forest, bog, mountain pine forests and other land. Forest land: Land bearing forest or without measures to increase production has the potential to bear forest with a height of 5 m and with a crown cover of at least 10%. Sveriges Lantbruksuniversitet (SLU), 2009. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf (Sweden) Land that is suitable " .

:def_Forest_Sweden_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Sweden ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.svo.se/eng/englaw.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Sweden) Land which is suitable for wood production, and not used to a significant extent for other purposes; and land where tree cover is desirable in order to protect against sand or soil erosion, or to prevent a lowering of the tree line. [Source: Swedish Forest Act - http://www.svo.se/eng/englaw.htm]" .

:def_Forest_Switzerland_1991_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Switzerland ;
    dcterms:date "1991"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "https://www.admin.ch/opc/en/classified-compilation/19910255/index.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Switzerland 1991) Forest is defined as any area that is covered with forest trees or forest shrubs and can fulfil forest functions. Origin, type of use and land registry designation are not decisive. Also defined as forest are: a. grazing forests, wooded pastures and chestnut and walnut groves; b. unstocked or unproductive areas of a forest plot, such as clearings, forest roads and other forest structures and installations; c. plots subject to compulsory afforestation. Isolated groups of trees " .

:def_Forest_Switzerland_2006_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Switzerland ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.0625"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Switzerland 2006 KP) Use Min. Area (ha) = 0.0625-0.25 Min. Crown Cover (%) = 20-60 Min. Tree Height (m) = 3 Min. Strip Width (m) = 25-50 (2006). The following forest areas are not subject to the criterion of minimum stand height: shrub forest consisting of dwarf pine (Pinus mugo prostrata) and alpine alder (Alnus viridis). The following forest areas are not subject of the criteria of minimum stand height and minimum crown cover, but must have the potential to achieve it: afforested, regenerated" .

:def_Forest_Taiwan_ROC_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Taiwan_ROC ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "service@dns.forest.gov.tw" ;
    :definitionText "(Taiwan, ROC) Forest land - the land that is at least 0.5 hectare in size with at least 10% of the area covered with tree crowns or commercial bamboo, the forest belt beside road or river is at least 50 meters wide. The road, river, other water area or open lands in forest is less than 20 meters wide. The open land over than 0.5 hectare which is considered to reforestation or afforestation. Source: The Third Forest Resources and Land Use Inventory in Taiwan&uml; - \"&ordf;L&deg;È&sect;&frac12;ser" .

:def_Forest_Tajikistan_1993_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Tajikistan ;
    dcterms:date "1993"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://faolex.fao.org/docs/texts/taj19369.doc" ;
    :definitionText "(Tajikistan 1993) Forests lands - covered with forests, non-closed forest cultures, forest-nurseries, plantations, thinning, burning, felling and clearings; Non-forests - pashni, hay making, pastures, waters, gardens and vineyards, roads and through cuts, farmsteads, bogs, sands and glaciers. Forest Code of the Republic of Tajikistan. . http://faolex.fao.org/docs/texts/taj19369.doc" .

:def_Forest_Tanzania_2002_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Tanzania ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.parliament.go.tz/Polis/PAMS/Docs/14-2002.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Tanzania 2002) ''forest'' means an area of land with at leas 10% tree crown cover, naturally grown or planted and or 50% or more shrub and tree regeneration cover and includes all forest reserves of whatever kind declared or gazetted under this Act and all plantations; http://www.parliament.go.tz/Polis/PAMS/Docs/14-2002.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Tanzania_2016_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Tanzania ;
    dcterms:date "2016"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "2.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.environment.go.ke/wp-content/uploads/2016/07/Kenya-NFP-draft-doc-2016-07-12-small-v2-1.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Tanzania 2016). Forest in this NFP means a land area of more than 0.5 ha, crown cover of 10%, trees of at least 2.5 m height, which is not primarily under agricultural or other specific non-forest land use. In line with the Constitution, the NFP also operates with “tree cover”, e.g. trees on farms. http://www.environment.go.ke/wp-content/uploads/2016/07/Kenya-NFP-draft-doc-2016-07-12-small-v2-1.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Thailand_1941_005
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Thailand ;
    dcterms:date "1941"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "Wilailak Pangtawaong <wpangtaw@deqp.go.th>" ;
    :definitionText "(Thailand 1941) Land which has not been taken up or acquired by any other means under the Land Law. Forest Act, 1941, Royal Forestry Department, Ministry of Agriculture and Cooperatives. \"Wilailak Pangtawaong\" <wpangtaw@deqp.go.th" .

:def_Forest_Thailand_1964_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Thailand ;
    dcterms:date "1964"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://thailawonline.com/en/thai-laws/laws-of-thailand/211-national-reserved-forest-act-be-2507-1964" ;
    :definitionText "(Thailand. 1964) “Forest” means land including mountain, rivulet, marsh, canal, swamp, waterway, lagoon, island, and sea shore in which nobody acquired by law; “National Reserved Forest” means forest determined to be national reserved forest under the provisions of this Act; “ http://thailawonline.com/en/thai-laws/laws-of-thailand/211-national-reserved-forest-act-be-2507-1964" .

:def_Forest_Togo_1938_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Togo ;
    dcterms:date "1938"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Togo 1938) Sont qualifiés forêts, les terrains dont les fruits exclusifs ou principaux sont les bois d'ébénisterie, d'industrie, ou de service, les bois de chauffage et à charbon ou des produits accessoires tels que: les écorces et fruits à tanin, les écorces textiles et tinctoriales, le kapok, le caoutchouc, la glu, les résines, les gommes, les bambous, les palmiers spontanés et tous autres végétaux ne constituant pas un produit agricole. 1. Décret du 5 février 1938 portant organisation du rég" .

:def_Forest_Turkey_1956_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Turkey ;
    dcterms:date "1956"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "yilmazersin@hotmail.com" ;
    :definitionText "(Turkey 1956) According to the Turkey's Forest Law in force, the community of trees, and shrubs grown naturally or artificially, together with the area they occupy, are considered as forest. According to Paragraph 20 of the Regulations still in force: a) The trees are the plants of at least 8 m., or more height, have crowns and the wooden stems, at any age or diameter. b) Shrubs are the wood plants showing generally horizontal growth and when mature reaches less than 8 m. in height. c) Community" .

:def_Forest_Ukraine_2006_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Ukraine ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Ukraine 2006) In Ukraine's forest are forest areas, including those protective plantings linear type, area of not less than 0.1 ha. In Ukraine the forest area does not include: green spaces within settlements (parks, gardens, squares, boulevards, etc.) that are not included in the prescribed manner to the forest; individual trees and groups of trees, shrubs on agricultural land, homestead, cottage and garden areas. Supreme Council of Ukraine, 2006. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publicati" .

:def_Forest_United_Kingdom_2010_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :United_Kingdom ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://uk-air.defra.gov.uk/reports/cat07/1010151419_ukghgi-90-08_main_chapters_Issue3_r.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(United Kingdom 2010) The definition of woodland in United Kingdom forestry statistics and in National Inventory is land under stands of trees with a canopy cover of at least 20% (or having the potential to achieve this), including integral open space, and including felled areas that are awaiting restocking. There is no minimum size for a woodland. http://uk-air.defra.gov.uk/reports/cat07/1010151419_ukghgi-90-08_main_chapters_Issue3_r.pdf" .

:def_Forest_United_Kingdom_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :United_Kingdom ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(United Kingdom 1997) Woodlands minimum mappable area of 1 ha. In general the width for a woodland is 50 m. Areas of scattered trees with distinct crowns constitute woodland if the canopy covers more than 20 percent of the ground. Areas of young trees which have to potential to achieve a canopy cover more than 20% are also interpreted as woodland. Woodland also includes areas that may be temporarily without tree cover following forest operations such as felling. Orchards are excluded. (European " .

:def_Forest_United_Kingdom_2009_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :United_Kingdom ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://uk-air.defra.gov.uk/reports/cat07/1010151419_ukghgi-90-08_main_chapters_Issue3_r.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(United Kingdom 2009) The UK has chosen the following definition of forest and single minimum values (also in table NIR.1). A definition of „forest‟ as agreed with the Forestry Commission comprising:  a minimum area of 0.1 hectares;  a minimum width of 20 metres;  tree crown cover of at least 20 per cent, or the potential to achieve it;  a minimum height of 2 metres, or the potential to achieve it. This definition includes felled areas awaiting restocking and integral open space (open areas up t" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_5_Agency1982_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_5_Agency1982 ;
    :sourceRef "http://home.comcast.net/~gyde/5-agency_paper-2.doc" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-5-Agency1982) Land at least ten percent stocked by trees of any size or formerly having had such tree cover and not currently built-up or developed for agricultural use. Forest land may include Grassland, Shrubland, Treeland, Wetland and/or Barren land. Examples of forest land use arc grazing, recreation and timber production. (Note we are not recommending that “ten percent stocked” be used to determine dominance in the classification categories.) (Land Use and Land Cover Common Termino" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_Census_Bureau_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_Census_Bureau ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.4047"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.allcountries.org/uscensus/383_land_cover_use_by_state.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-Census Bureau 2006). A Land cover/use category that is at least 10 percent stocked by single-stemmed woody species of any size that will be at least 4 meters (13 feet) tall at maturity. Also included is land bearing evidence of natural regeneration of tree cover (cut over forest or abandoned farmland) and not currently developed for nonforest use. Ten percent stocked, when viewed from a vertical direction, equates to an areal canopy cover of leaves and branches of 25 percent or greater." .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_Congressional_Research_Service_and_House_o_1992_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_Congressional_Research_Service_and_House_o ;
    dcterms:date "1992"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.cnie.org/nle/AgGlossary/letter-f.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-Congressional Research Service and House of Representatives 1992) A classification of land use in the Natural Resources Inventory (NRI). It includes areas where trees cover at least 10% of the land and must be at least an acre in size. Forestland was found on 395 million acres, almost 30% of all private lands, in the 1992 NRI. http://www.cnie.org/nle/AgGlossary/letter-f.html Congressional Research Service Report for Congress Agriculture: A Glossary of Terms, Programs, and Laws and http:" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.cbd.int/doc/world/us/us-nr-vfe-en.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA 2003) Land with a specified minimum tree crown cover and generally more than the specified minimum area, including land that formerly had such tree cover and that will be naturally or artificially regenerated. The trees should generally be able to reach a minimum specified tree height at maturity in situ. It may consist either of closed forest formations in which trees of various stories and undergrowth cover a high proportion of the ground, or of open forest formations with a contin" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_ERS_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_ERS ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ers.usda.gov/data/majorlanduses/glossary.htm#grassland" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-ERS 2003) Forest land, as defined by the U.S. Forest Service, includes land at least 10 percent of which is stocked by trees of any size, or land formerly having had such tree cover that will be naturally or artificially regenerated. Forest land includes transition zones, such as areas between heavily forested and nonforested lands that are at least 10 percent stocked with forest trees and forest areas adjacent to urban and built-up lands. The total includes pinyon-juniper and chapar" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_ERS_2003_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_ERS ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-ERS 2003) Forest-use land (total forest land exclusive of forested areas in parks and other special uses), 642 million acres (ERS 2003)" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_FS_1972_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_FS ;
    dcterms:date "1972"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.4047"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://home.comcast.net/~gyde/5-agency_paper-2.doc" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-FS 1972) Land at least 10 percent stocked by forest trees of any size or formerly having had such tree cover, and not currently developed for nonforest use. (Note: Stocking is measured by comparison of basal area and/or number of trees, by age or size and spacing with specified standards. The minimum area for classification forest land is 1 acre. Roadside, streamside. and shelterbelt strips of timber must have a crown width of at least 120 feet wide to qualify as forest land. Unimpro" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_FS_1993_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_FS ;
    dcterms:date "1993"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.4047"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fs.fed.us/land/sustain_dev/sd/criter2.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-FS 1993) Land at least 10 percent stocked by forest trees of any size, including land that formerly had such tree cover and that will be naturally or artificially regenerated. Forest land includes transition zones, such as areas between heavily forested and nonforested lands that are at least 10 percent stocked with forest trees and forested areas adjacent to urban or built-up lands. Also included are pinyon juniper and chaparral areas in the West and afforested areas. The minimum ar" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_FS_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_FS ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.4047"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-FS 1997) Land at least 10 percent stocked with live trees, or land that had this minimum tree stocking in the past and is not currently developed for nonforest use. The minimum area recognized is 1 acre. (Waddell and Bassett 1997)." .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_FS_2001_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_FS ;
    dcterms:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-FS 2001) Land that is at least 10 percent stocked by forest trees of any size, or land formerly having such tree cover, and is not currently developed for a nonforest use. The minimum area for classification as forest land is one acre. Roadside, stream-side, and shelterbelt strips of timber must have a crown width at least 120 feet wide to qualify as forest land. Unimproved roads and trails, streams and other bodies of water, or natural clearings in forested areas shall be classified" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_FS_2004_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_FS ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.4"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-FS 2004) Forest land -\"(a) the condition is at least 10-percent stocked by trees . . . of any size or has been at least 10-percent stocked in the past. Additionally, the condition is not subject to nonforest use(s) that prevent normal tree regeneration and succession such as regular mowing, intensive pruning, or recreation activities; or \"(b) in several western woodland species . . . where stocking cannot be determined, and the condition has at least 5 percent crown cover by trees of" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_FS_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_FS ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://socrates.lv-hrc.nevada.edu/fia/ab/issues/pending/glossary/Glossary_5_30_06.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-FS 2006). Land that is at least 10 percent stocked by forest trees of any size, or land formerly having such tree cover, and not currently developed for a nonforest use. The minimum area for classification as forest land is one acre. Roadside, stream-side, and shelterbelt strips of timber must be at least 120 feet wide to qualify as forest land. Unimproved roads and trails, streams and other bodies of water, or natural clearings in forested areas are classified as forest, if less tha" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_FS_2007_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_FS ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.4047"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fs.fed.us/nrs/pubs/gtr/gtr_wo78.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-FS 2007) forest land—Land at least 120 feet wide and 1 acre in size with at least 10 percent cover (or equivalent stocking) by live trees of any size, including land that formerly had such tree cover and that will be naturally or artificially regenerated. Forest land includes transition zones, such as areas between forest and nonforest lands that have at least 10 percent cover (or equivalent stocking) with live trees and forest areas adjacent to urban and built-up lands. Roadside, st" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_FS_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_FS ;
    :areaMin "0.4047"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.srsfia.usfs.msstate.edu/scripts/ew.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-FS) Land currently growing forest trees of any size with a total stocking value of at least 16.7 (10 base 100 in the West), or lands formerly forested, currently capable of becoming forest land, and not currently developed for nonforest uses. These lands must be a minimum of 1 acre in area. Roadside, streamside, and shelterbelt strips of timber must have a crown width of at least 120 feet to qualify as forest land. Unimproved roads, trails, streams, and clearings within forest areas " .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_FSA_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_FSA ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fsa.usda.gov/dafp/cepd/epb/pdf/ECP_Final_PEIS_0303/15_Glossary.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-FSA 2003). A land cover/land use category that is at least 10 percent stocked by singlestemmed woody species of any size that will be at least 13 feet tall at maturity. Also included, for the NRI, is land bearing evidence of natural regeneration of tree cover and not currently developed for nonforest use. http://www.fsa.usda.gov/dafp/cepd/epb/pdf/ECP_Final_PEIS_0303/15_Glossary.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_NRCS_1992_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_NRCS ;
    dcterms:date "1992"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "25.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ftc.nrcs.usda.gov/doc/nri/72.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-NRCS 1992) A Land Cover/Use that is at least 10 percent stocked by single stemmed forest trees of any size which will be at least 4 meters (13 feet) tall at maturity. When viewed vertically, canopy cover is 25 percent or greater. Also included are areas bearing evidence of natural regeneration of tree cover (cutover forest or abandoned farmland) and not currently developed for nonforest use. For classification as forest land, an area must be at least one acre and 100 feet wide. [NRI-" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_NRCS_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_NRCS ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://soils.usda.gov/technical/handbook/contents/part622.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-NRCS 2000) A site type of “forestland” is assigned and described where a 25% overstory canopy of trees, as determined by crown perimeter-vertical projection, dominated this historic vegetation. http://soils.usda.gov/technical/handbook/contents/part622.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_NRCS_2002_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_NRCS ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.4"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-NRCS 2002 & 2004) A land cover/use category that is at least 10 percent stocked by single-stemmed woody species of any size that will be at least 4 meters (13 feet) tall at maturity. Also included is land bearing evidence of natural regeneration of tree cover (cutover forest or abandoned farmland) and not currently developed for non-forest use. Ten percent stocked, when viewed from a vertical direction is a canopy cover of leaves and branches of 25 percent or greater. The minirnum ar" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_NRCS_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_NRCS ;
    :areaMin "0.4047"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nh.nrcs.usda.gov/NRI/Publications/NRIglossary.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-NRCS) A Land cover/use category that is at least 10 percent stocked by single –stemmed woody species of any size that will be at least 4 meters (13 feet) tall at maturity. Also included is land bearing evidence of natural regeneration of tree cover (cut over forest or abandoned farmland) and not currently developed for nonforest use. Ten percent stocked, when viewed from a vertical direction, equates to an areal canopy cover of leaves and branches of 25 percent or greater. The minimu" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_NRCS_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_NRCS ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ftc.nrcs.usda.gov/doc/npph/glossary/56.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-NRCS) Land use designation for land on which the primary vegetation is forest (climax, natural, or introduced plant community) and use is primarily for production of wood products http://www.ftc.nrcs.usda.gov/doc/npph/glossary/56.html National Planning Procedures Handbook (NPPH) Glossary" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_SCS_1980_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_SCS ;
    dcterms:date "1980"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.4047"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://home.comcast.net/~gyde/5-agency_paper-2.doc" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-SCS 1980) Land at least 10 percent stocked by forest trees of any size, or formerly having had such tree cover, and not currently developed for nonforest use. The minimum area is 1 acre and must be at least 100 feet wide. (Ten percent tree canopy cover is used to separate forest land from rangeland in the transition vegetation types.) (SCS 1980) http://home.comcast.net/~gyde/5-agency_paper-2.doc" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_SCS_1982_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_SCS ;
    dcterms:date "1982"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://farm.fic.niu.edu/foe2/report/foeglos.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-SCS 1982) Land at least 10 percent stocked by forest trees of any size, or formerly having had such tree cover and not currently developed for non-forest use. The minimum area for classification of forestland is one acre and must be at least 100 feet wide. Forestland is distinguished from rangeland in transition vegetation types if the tree canopy cover exceeds 10 percent. Forestlands include cut over areas temporarily unstocked as well as young stands and plantations established for" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DD_AF_1994_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DD_AF ;
    dcterms:date "1994"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.afrpa.hq.af.mil/handbook/basis/guidance/afi/af327064.htm#Att1" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DD-AF 1994) Land on which forest trees of various sizes constitute at least 10 percent of the area. This category includes open land that is capable of supporting trees and is planned for forest regeneration and management http://www.afrpa.hq.af.mil/handbook/basis/guidance/afi/af327064.htm#Att1" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DI_BIA_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DI_BIA ;
    :sourceRef "http://thorpe.ou.edu/codes/grandronde/ch620.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DI-BIA) Land for which a primary use is the growing and harvesting of forest tree species. Source: THE CONFEDERATED TRIBES OF THE GRAND RONDE COMMUNITY OF OREGON FOREST PRACTICES ORDINANCE TRIBAL CODE &sect; 6.20 http://thorpe.ou.edu/codes/grandronde/ch620.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DI_BLM_1971_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DI_BLM ;
    dcterms:date "1971"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DI-BLM 1971) (Productive forest land) Any forested land capable of being both at least 16.7% stocked and capable of producing 20 cubic feet per acre per year of merchantable wood. (Lund 1974)." .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DI_BLM_1973_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DI_BLM ;
    dcterms:date "1973"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "16.7"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://home.comcast.net/~gyde/5-agency_paper-2.doc" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DI-BLM 1973) Land which is, or has been, at least 16.7 percent stocked by forest trees (10 percent of normal yield values), and not currently developed for nonforest use. This included land currently developed for nonforest use, such as urban or thickly settled residential or resort areas, city parks, orchards, improved roads, or pastureland improved by such measures as seeding or irrigation. (BLM 1973). http://home.comcast.net/~gyde/5-agency_paper-2.doc" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DI_BLM_1998_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DI_BLM ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.blm.gov/narsc/blmannual/annual98/stewardship.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DI-BLM 1998) Lands capable of growing trees for harvest, land at least ten percent stocked with trees of any species and size, or lands that were stocked, have been harvested, and will be replanted. Source: Stewardship Assets - http://www.blm.gov/narsc/blmannual/annual98/stewardship.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DI_BLM_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DI_BLM ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.pinedalermp.com/documents/PinedaleGlossaryJanuaryMSA.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DI-BLM 2003) Land that is now, or is capable of becoming, at least 10 percent stocked with forest trees, and that has been developed for nontimber use. Pinedale Resource Management Plan, http://www.pinedalermp.com/documents/PinedaleGlossaryJanuaryMSA.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DI_BLM_2003_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DI_BLM ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.blm.gov/nhp/efoia/wo/fy03/im2003-035attach1.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DI-BLM 2003) Those lands with 10 percent or greater stocking (or the potential to in tree species which are typically used in commercially processed wood products (lumber, plywood, paper, etc.), such as ponderosa pine, lodgepole pine, Douglas-fir, white spruce, white fir, grandfir, hemlock, and aspen. Stocking can be measure by either crown density, stem density, or basal area. Include land that formerly had such tree cover and that will be managed to be naturally or artificially regene" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DI_BLM_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DI_BLM ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.or.blm.gov/coosbay/rmp/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DI-BLM) Land that is now, or is capable of becoming, at least l0 percent stocked with forest trees and that has not been developed for nontimber use. Source: Coos Bay Record of Decision - http://www.or.blm.gov/coosbay/rmp/glossary.html, .(Streamnet online) http://www.streamnet.org/ff/Glossary/glossaryforest.html, http://web.ead.anl.gov/rmpweb/application/rmp_browse.cfm?rmpid=28&idref=27602 and Medford Record of Decision and Resource Management Plan http://www.or.blm.gov/Medford/medford/" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DI_GS_1952_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DI_GS ;
    dcterms:date "1952"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.4047"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DI-GS 1952) (Woods, Woodland). Areas 1 acre or greater containing tree cover or brush that is potential tree cover. The growth must be at least 6 feet tall and dense enough to impede foot travel or give cover for troops. Logged or burnt areas are classed as \"woods\" unless new growth is not going to be established. (USGS 1952)" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DI_GS_1976_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DI_GS ;
    dcterms:date "1976"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://home.comcast.net/~gyde/5-agency_paper-2.doc" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DI-GS 1976) Land which has a tree-crown areal- density (crown closure percentage) of 10 percent or more, is stocked with trees capable of producing timber or other wood products, and exerts an influence on the climate or water regime. Land from which trees have been removed to less than 10 percent crown closure but which has not been developed for other uses also is included. (Anderson, et. al., 1976) http://home.comcast.net/~gyde/5-agency_paper-2.doc http://mapping.usgs.gov/pub/ti/LULC" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DI_GS_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DI_GS ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.4"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.pwrc.usgs.gov/brd/DefLandTerms.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DI-GS) Land currently supporting forest or land with potential to support forest that formerly had such tree cover and that will be naturally or artificially regenerated – Note 1) forest land includes (a) transition zones, such as areas between forested and non-forested lands that are at least 10 percent stocked with forest trees, and forest areas adjacent to urban and built-up lands; note 2) the minimum area for classification of forest land is 1 acre (0.4 ha); roadside, streamside, an" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DI_OSM_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DI_OSM ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.osmre.gov/stateregs/wyregschap1.txt" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DI-OSM) Land used or managed for the long-term production of wood, wood fiber, or wood-derived products. http://www.osmre.gov/stateregs/wyregschap1.txt" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DI_OSM_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DI_OSM ;
    :canopyThreshold "25.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.osmre.gov/mountaintop.htm#74" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DI-OSM) Land with at least 25 percent tree canopy or that has been stocked with at least 10 percent forest trees of any size, including land that formerly had such tree cover and that will be naturally or artificially reforested. http://www.osmre.gov/mountaintop.htm#74 and http://www.wvgazette.com/static/series/mining/reports/EIS/VIII.Glossary.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DOE_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DOE ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.eren.doe.gov/biopower/glossary.html#F" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DOE) Any land that is capable of producing or has produced forest growth or, if lacking forest growth, has evidence of a former forest and is not now in other use. http://www.eren.doe.gov/biopower/glossary.html#F" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DOE_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DOE ;
    :canopyThreshold "16.7"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DOE) Land at least 16.7 percent stocked by forest trees of any size, or formerly having such tree cover, and not currently developed for nonforest use. Glossary of Terms used in Timber Harvesting and Forest Engineering. Biomass Resource Information Clearinghouse, Renewable Resource Data Center, US Dept. of Energy" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DOE_EIA_2007_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DOE_EIA ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.eia.doe.gov/oiaf/1605/pdf/EIA1605_Instructions_10-23-07.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DOE-EIA 2007) Land at least 10 percent stocked by forest trees of any size, or formerly having such tree cover, and not currently developed for non-forest uses. The minimum area considered for classification is one (1) acre. U.S. Department of Energy, Energy Information Administration. Form EIA-1605 (2007) http://www.eia.doe.gov/oiaf/1605/pdf/EIA1605_Instructions_10-23-07.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_EPA_nd_005
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_EPA ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.epa.gov/indicate/roe/html/roeAppDf.htm#f" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-EPA) - Land that is at least 10 percent stocked by forest trees of any size, including land that formerly had tree cover and that will be naturally or artificially regenerated. The minimum area for classification of forest land is one acre. http://www.epa.gov/indicate/roe/html/roeAppDf.htm#f" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_GPO_2010_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_GPO ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://ecfr.gpoaccess.gov/cgi/t/text/text-idx?c=ecfr" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-GPO 2010)-Forest means any operation engaged in the outdoor production of any agricultural plant to produce wood fiber or timber products. USA WORKER PROTECTION STANDARD http://ecfr.gpoaccess.gov/cgi/t/text/text-idx?c=ecfr;sid=d5c57af0e98338afc8fe525fef980c92;rgn=div5;view=text;node=40%3A23.0.1.1.20;idno=40;cc=ecfr#40:23.0.1.1.20.1.19.2" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_NASA_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_NASA ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.hq.nasa.gov/iwgsdi/Forest_Land.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-NASA) Those ecosystems that have a tree crown density (crown closure percentage) of 10% or more and are stocked with trees capable of producing timber or other wood products. This includes land from which trees have been removed to less than 10%, but which have not been developed for other uses. http://www.hq.nasa.gov/iwgsdi/Forest_Land.html, http://www.hq.nasa.gov/iwgsdi/Land_Ecosystems.html, and http://www.hq.nasa.gov/iwgsdi/FW_SDI_Env_Endow.html" .

:def_Forest_Vanatu_2011_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Vanatu ;
    dcterms:date "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cn.china.cn/2011images/vanuatu/NFP_Comprehensive_June_2011.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Vanatu 2011 Proposed Definition) Land spanning more than 0.5 hectares with trees higher than 5 meters and a canopy cover of more than 10 percent, or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ. It does not include land that is predominantly under agriculture or urban use. Forest is determined both by the presence of trees and the absence of other predominant land uses. Areas under reforestation that have not yet reached but are expected to reach a canopy cover of 10 percent and a tree height o" .

:def_Forest_Venezuela_1969_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Venezuela ;
    dcterms:date "1969"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Venezuela 1969) Terrenos forestales: a) los que deban permanecer cubiertos por vegetación forestal; b) el que carece de vegetación alguna, pero que por su declive y estructura necesita una cobertura vegetal permanente que asegure su conservación; el que por sus condiciones climáticas, topográficas y agrológicas sea impropio para las actividades agropecuarias productivas y permanentes. LEX-FAOC003046. VENEZUELA: Decreto N&ordm; 1.333 por el cual se edita el Reglamento de la Ley Forestal, de Suel" .

:def_Forest_Viet_Nam_1991_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Viet_Nam ;
    dcterms:date "1991"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Viet Nam 1991) - Natural and man-made forests established on forest land with all their resources such as vegetation, wildlife and other natural assets found therein. Forest land comprises: 1) Forested land and 2) Non forested land for which plans have been made for forest plantation , below referred to as forest plantation land . Source: Article 1. The National assembly of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam, legislature VIII session IX , held from July 27th to August 12th 1991." .

:def_Forest_Viet_Nam_1991_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Viet_Nam ;
    dcterms:date "1991"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://coombs.anu.edu.au/~vern/luat/english/Law-forest-protect.txt" ;
    :definitionText "(Viet Nam 1991) Forestry land includes: 1. Land of forest cover, 2. Land of no forest cover is planned for afforestation, hereinafter called afforestation land. http://coombs.anu.edu.au/~vern/luat/english/Law-forest-protect.txt ORDER NO. 58-LCT/HDNN8 DATED 19-8-1991" .

:def_Forest_Viet_Nam_1993_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Viet_Nam ;
    dcterms:date "1993"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://coombs.anu.edu.au/~vern/luat/english/Law-land-law.txt" ;
    :definitionText "(Viet Nam 1993) Forestry Land = DDa^'t la^m nghie^.p - Land designated primarily for use in silviculture production, including land with natural forest, land under afforestation, and land used for forestry purposes such as afforestation, forest nursery, protection for natural rehabilitation, forest enrichment and experimental research on silviculture. http://coombs.anu.edu.au/~vern/luat/english/Law-land-law.txt LAND LAW OF VIETNAM Article 43 1993" .

:def_Forest_Viet_Nam_2016_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Viet_Nam ;
    dcterms:date "2016"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://redd.unfccc.int/files/2016_submission_frel_viet_nam.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Viet Nam 2016) The definition of forests used for the construction of FREL/FRL for Vietnam, applies the definitions provided under Circular No. 34/2009/TT-BNNPTNT on criteria for forest identification and classification, defining forests as: minimum 10% tree cover, at a minimum height of 5 meters, over a minimum area of 0.5 ha or forest tree strips of at least 20 meters in width and of at least 3 tree lines. Agricultural and aqua-cultural ecosystems with scattered perennial trees, bamboos or pa" .

:def_Forest_Yugoslavia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Yugoslavia ;
    :sourceRef "bojos@ptt.yu" ;
    :definitionText "(Yugoslavia) Forestland - a section of land on which forest is cultivated. \"Srdjan BOJOVIC\" <bojos@ptt.yu" .

:def_Forest_Zambia_2015_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Zambia ;
    dcterms:date "2015"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://redd.unfccc.int/files/2016_submission_frel_zambia.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Zambia 2015) The Forest Act (Commencement) Order, 2015 provides a definition of forest as below: “forest” means any land with a tree canopy cover of more than ten percent and area of more than zero point five hectares and includes young stands that have not yet reached, but are expected to reach, a crown density of ten percent and tree height of five metres that are temporarily under stocked areas; In practice, the bolded part of the forest definition is used in measurement of forest cover and " .

:def_Forest_Zambia_2015_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Zambia ;
    dcterms:date "2015"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.parliament.gov.zm/sites/default/files/documents/acts/The%20Forest%20Act%202015.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Zambia 2015) “Forest area” means a National Forest, Local Forest, botanical reserve, plantation, private forest, community forest, joint forest management area and open areas; http://www.parliament.gov.zm/sites/default/files/documents/acts/The%20Forest%20Act%202015.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Azerbaijan_Republic_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Azerbaijan_Republic ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.enpi-fleg.org/fileadmin/ufs/04.%20Program%20Information/4.02%20Program%20Components/4.02.01%20General/4.02.01.Azerbaijan/4.02.01.Forest_Code_ENG.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Azerbaijan Republic) - Forest - from the biological point of view the unity of interconnected and mutually influencing at development, lands, waters, trees, bushes and grasses, animals, microorganisms and other components of environment; The Forest Code of Azerbaijan Republic http://www.enpi-fleg.org/fileadmin/ufs/04.%20Program%20Information/4.02%20Program%20Components/4.02.01%20General/4.02.01.Azerbaijan/4.02.01.Forest_Code_ENG.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Azerbaijan_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Azerbaijan ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.enpi-fleg.az/index/leg/Forest%20Code%20in%20English.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Azerbaijan) Forest - from the biological point of view the unity of interconnected and mutually influencing at development, lands, waters, trees, bushes and grasses, animals, microorganisms and other components of environment; Forest Code of Azerbaijan; http://www.enpi-fleg.az/index/leg/Forest%20Code%20in%20English.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Cambodia_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Cambodia ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Cambodia 2000) \"Forest\" means natural ecosystems, land, water, plants, and micro-organisms etc. which are dominated by woody plants or bamboo of more than ten (10%) percent and has a size of 0.5 hectare or more, including dryland and wetland forest formations and any non-treed wetlands covering most part of land or open land within a forest that form ten (10%) of that ecosystem. All stages of natural forest succession and planted trees for forestry purposes with a leaf density smaller than ten " .

:def_Forest_Cambodia_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Cambodia ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.wisc.edu/ltc/news82a1.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Cambodia) - A forest is anywhere there have ever been trees. http://www.wisc.edu/ltc/news82a1.html" .

:def_Forest_Cameroon_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Cameroon ;
    :sourceRef "http://befac.net/pdf/t127.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Cameroon) A forest is an ecosystem or a combination of ecosystems. http://befac.net/pdf/t127.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Chile_1931_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Chile ;
    dcterms:date "1931"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://derechoambiental.udp.cl/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/chile-case-cdm-ar-projects-as-published-by-iucn.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Chile 1931) “lands preferentially suitable for forestry”. These are defined as “all those grounds that due to climate and soil conditions should not be plowed permanently, independently of whether they are covered by vegetation or not, excluding those grounds that might be used for intensive agriculture, fruit growing, or cattle ranching without suffering degradation”. http://derechoambiental.udp.cl/wp-content/uploads/2009/08/chile-case-cdm-ar-projects-as-published-by-iucn.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Czech_Republic_1995_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Czech_Republic ;
    dcterms:date "1995"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.natura2000.gov.si/uploads/tx_library/Diaci_Virgin_forests_and_forest_reserves__Cost_E4_.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Czech Republic 1995) The new Forest Act No. 289/1995 Coll., in force since 1 January 1996, defines forests as national heritage which constitutes an irreplaceable part of the environment http://www.natura2000.gov.si/uploads/tx_library/Diaci_Virgin_forests_and_forest_reserves__Cost_E4_.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Estonia_nd_008
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Estonia ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.metla.fi/eu/cost/e43/minutes/wg1-min-florence.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Estonia) Forest - National definition in use, related to productivity, do not have data for swamps http://www.metla.fi/eu/cost/e43/minutes/wg1-min-florence.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Estonia_2006_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Estonia ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "https://www.riigiteataja.ee/en/eli/504092017014/consolide" ;
    :definitionText "(Estonia 2006) Forest and forest land (1) Forest is an ecosystem consisting of forest land and the flora and fauna thereof. https://www.riigiteataja.ee/en/eli/504092017014/consolide" .

:def_Forest_Finland_2009_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Finland ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Finland 2009) The second definition is the national definition of forest that in Finland is the same as in the two other Nordic countries, Sweden and Norway: forest is defined as a land capable of producing an annual increment of volume growing stock of at least 1 m3/ha per year over the rotation under the most favorable tree species composition, and not used for any other purpose than forestry or forestry related purposes. METLA (Finnish Forest Research Institute), 2009. http://www.efi.int/fil" .

:def_Forest_Greece_1979_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Greece ;
    dcterms:date "1979"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.oikotechnics.org/greek_legislation.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Greece 1979) Greek Constitution, article 24, “As forest or forest ecosystem is meant the organic whole of wild plants with ligneous trunk on the requisite land surface, which, together with the co-existing flora and fauna, form throughout their mutual interdependence and interactions, a certain biological community (forest biological community) and a certain natural environment (forest environment). Wooded tract exists when in the aforementioned whole the wild ligneous vegetation, high or bushy" .

:def_Forest_Greece_2005_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Greece ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.oikotechnics.org/greek_legislation.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Greece 2005) According to the existing Greek Constitution, article 24, “As forest or forest ecosystem is meant the organic whole of wild plants with ligneous trunk on the requisite land surface, which, together with the co-existing flora and fauna, form throughout their mutual interdependence and interactions, a certain biological community (forest biological community) and a certain natural environment (forest environment). Wooded tract exists when in the aforementioned whole the wild ligneous" .

:def_Forest_Grenada_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Grenada ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.unccd.int/cop/reports/lac/national/2000/grenada-eng.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Grenada) ‘Forest’ is understood to include all forest ecosystems (from coastal scrub and mangroves through to cloud forests) and non-agricultural trees, as well as the goods and services that they provide. (Grenada’ means ‘Grenada, Carriacou and Petit Martinique) http://www.unccd.int/cop/reports/lac/national/2000/grenada-eng.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Indonesia_2000_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Indonesia ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fire.uni-freiburg.de/iffn/country/id/id_25.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Indonesia 2000) \"Forest means a unit of ecosystem….comprising biological resources, dominated by trees in their natural forms and environment….\". Indonesia. http://www.fire.uni-freiburg.de/iffn/country/id/id_25.htm" .

:def_Forest_Indonesia_2009_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Indonesia ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "https://www.elaw.org/system/files/REDD_PERMENHUT_P-30-2009_BILINGUAL.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Indonesia 2009) Forest means a unity of ecosystem in the form of land consisting of biological resources dominated by trees in their natural form and environment, in which one and another are inseparable. https://www.elaw.org/system/files/REDD_PERMENHUT_P-30-2009_BILINGUAL.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Ireland_1998_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Ireland ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nwpg.gov.za/esds/links/Act84%20-%20National%20Forests%20.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Ireland 1998) \"forest\" includes-- a natural forest, a woodland and a plantation; the forest produce in it; and the ecosystems which it makes up; http://www.nwpg.gov.za/esds/links/Act84%20-%20National%20Forests%20.htm" .

:def_Forest_Kazakhatan_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Kazakhatan ;
    :sourceRef "http://faolex.fao.org/docs/texts/kaz41426E.doc" ;
    :definitionText "(Kazakhatan) \"forest\" means a natural complex formed on a certain territory based on the aggregate of trees and shrubs vegetations and other wildlife components interacting with environment and having environmental, economic and social importance; http://faolex.fao.org/docs/texts/kaz41426E.doc" .

:def_Forest_Kazakhstan_2002_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Kazakhstan ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Kazakhstan 2002) \"forest\" means a natural complex formed on a certain territory based on the aggregate of trees and shrubs vegetations and other wildlife components interacting with environment and having environmental, economic and social importance; Forest Code of the Republic of Kazakhstan: faolex.fao.org/docs/texts/kaz41426E.doc" .

:def_Forest_Kyrgyz_Republic_1999_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Kyrgyz_Republic ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.libertas-institut.com/de/Mittel-Osteuropa/Forest%20Code.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Kyrgyz Republic 1999) Forest is one of the main types of vegetation on the Earth, comprising trees, shrubs, grassland and other plants, including animals and microorganisms, which are biologically interrelated in their evolution and exert influence on one another and the environment. Forest Code of The Kyrgyz Republic. http://www.libertas-institut.com/de/Mittel-Osteuropa/Forest%20Code.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Latvia_nd_005
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Latvia ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.iufro.org/download/file/5574/4510/61300-jundola01_pdf/" ;
    :definitionText "(Latvia) The term “forest” is defined as “an ecosystem in all its development stages, dominated by trees, the height of which in the particular forest site may reach at least seven metres, and the present or potential tree crown cover accounts for at least 20% of the stand area.” ). http://www.iufro.org/download/file/5574/4510/61300-jundola01_pdf/" .

:def_Forest_Liberia_nd_005
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Liberia ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.sdiliberia.org/sites/default/files/documents/So%20Who%20Owns%20the%20Forest_full%20report.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Liberia ) forest, as being ‘a tract of land consisting of flora and fauna’ (s.1.3). http://www.sdiliberia.org/sites/default/files/documents/So%20Who%20Owns%20the%20Forest_full%20report.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Nigeria_2002_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Nigeria ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.onlinenigeria.com/links/adv.asp?blurb=70" ;
    :definitionText "(Nigeria 2002) Forests: Forests are vegetation types or plant formations in which trees are the dominant species http://www.onlinenigeria.com/links/adv.asp?blurb=70" .

:def_Forest_Paraguay_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Paraguay ;
    :sourceRef "cdcdpnvs@venus.pla.net.py" ;
    :definitionText "(Paraguay) Suelos de prioridad forestal: Cuando los estudios técnicos determinen que su aptitud productiva es preferentemente forestal. Bosque: Todo agrupamiento vegetal en el que predominan árboles, incluyendo además los suelos, las aguas y la vida silvestre asociada a ellos. Suelos de aptitud productiva preferentemente forestal: Aquellos en el que el sitio pueda sostener en forma indefinida el cultivo de árboles adecuados para la industrialización y destinados principalmente para fines maderab" .

:def_Forest_Philippines_1972_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Philippines ;
    dcterms:date "1972"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "250.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "tjohnson@swift-elap.com.ph" ;
    :definitionText "(Philippines 1972) - Any untitled lands having slope greater than 18% are \"forestland\" (regardless of whether there have been any trees on them in generations!). Source: Presidential Decree 705 issued in 1972(?) (Todd R. Johnson - tjohnson@swift-elap.com.ph) The following lands, even if they are below eighteen percent (18%) in slope, are needed for forest purposes, and may not, therefore, be classified as alienable and disposable land, to wit: 1.Areas less than 250 hectares which are far from, o" .

:def_Forest_Philippines_2004_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Philippines ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://books.google.com/books?id=h6nVjxfMKQIC&pg=PA123&lpg=PA123&dq=%22Forests+are+ecosystems" ;
    :definitionText "(Philippines 2004) Forests are ecosystems, which include all living organisms (flora and fauna), as well as nonliving components (litter, soils, water, etc.) http://books.google.com/books?id=h6nVjxfMKQIC&pg=PA123&lpg=PA123&dq=%22Forests+are+ecosystems,+which+include+all+living+organisms+(flora+and+fauna)%22,&source=bl&ots=M5CZriR-J-&sig=MjGu90sbVH5BhOYbeU1c-W0IYJg&hl=en&sa=X&ei=rNk4T8akJOnf0QGPzMWfAg&sqi=2&ved=0CCEQ6AEwAA#v=onepage&q=%22Forests%20are%20ecosystems%2C%20which%20include%20all%20liv" .

:def_Forest_Romania_nd_007
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Romania ;
    :sourceRef "http://bucharest.usembassy.gov/InfoA/new05.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Romania) Forestland is land that is undeveloped. http://bucharest.usembassy.gov/InfoA/new05.htm" .

:def_Forest_Russia_Khabarovsk_Krai_1999_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Russia_Khabarovsk_Krai ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://wenku.baidu.com/view/d74f09d349649b6648d747c8.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Russia Khabarovsk Krai 1999) Forest is defined as the totality of forest vegetation, land, wildlife, and other components’ of the environment having important ecological, economic and social significance. http://wenku.baidu.com/view/d74f09d349649b6648d747c8.html" .

:def_Forest_Russian_Federation_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Russian_Federation ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Russian Federation 1997 Ecological) - Forest is the aggregate of forest vegetation, land, fauna and other components of the natural environment that are of great ecological, economic and social importance. Ref. Forest Code of the Russian Federation, adopted by the State Duma of the Russian Federation 22 January 1997, page 3, Moscow, 1997" .

:def_Forest_Russian_Federation_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Russian_Federation ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fire.uni-freiburg.de/GlobalNetworks/BalticRegion/ForestCode-3rdReading-061108-eng.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Russian Federation 2006) Статья 5. Понятие леса - Использование, охрана, защита, воспроизводство лесов осуществляются исходя из понятия о лесе как об экологической системе или как о природном ресурсе. Article 5. Definition of forest Utilization, protection, conservation and reforestation are carried out based on understanding forests as an ecological system or a natural resource. From Yelena Gordeeva, 3 June 2015. yelena.gordeeva@uhasselt.be See also http://www.fire.uni-freiburg.de/GlobalNetwor" .

:def_Forest_South_Africa_nd_007
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :South_Africa ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/legal/prs-ol/lpo%2084.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(South Africa ) Under the Forest Act, not only does the definition of forest include all biological organisms, it also includes the desire to “do anything in a state forest for which a licence is required” (which could apply to hunting) (sec. 29). http://www.fao.org/legal/prs-ol/lpo%2084.pdf" .

:def_Forest_South_Africa_1998_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :South_Africa ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nwpg.gov.za/esds/links/Act84%20-%20National%20Forests%20.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(South Africa 1998) forest\" includes-- a natural forest, a woodland and a plantation; the forest produce in it; and the ecosystems which it makes up; National Forests Act No. 84 of 1998 http://www.nwpg.gov.za/esds/links/Act84%20-%20National%20Forests%20.htm" .

:def_Forest_South_Africa_1998_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :South_Africa ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.info.gov.za/view/DownloadFileAction?id=70636" ;
    :definitionText "(South Africa 1998) forest” includes— (a) a natural forest, a woodland and a plantation; (b) the forest produce in it; and (c) the ecosystems which it make it up; (http://www.info.gov.za/view/DownloadFileAction?id=70636" .

:def_Forest_Suriname_2008_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Suriname ;
    dcterms:date "2008"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.tropenbos.org/file.php/243/proceedings_cli-preparatory-workshop_final.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Suriname 2008) Forests are part of (the form and nature) of the landscape of Suriname. http://www.tropenbos.org/file.php/243/proceedings_cli-preparatory-workshop_final.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Thailand_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Thailand ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.terraper.org/English_part/hot_issues/comfor_bill-people_s.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Thailand) Forest means land that is not legally occupied or tilled by any person. http://www.terraper.org/English_part/hot_issues/comfor_bill-people_s.htm" .

:def_Forest_Tonga_2008_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Tonga ;
    dcterms:date "2008"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.tonga-energy.to/wp-content/uploads/2009/12/Draft-Tonga-Natl-Forest-Policy-5Aug2008.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Tonga 2008) National Forest Policy defines forestry as the economic, social and environmental interaction of forests, and trees outside of forests, with people. http://www.tonga-energy.to/wp-content/uploads/2009/12/Draft-Tonga-Natl-Forest-Policy-5Aug2008.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Trinidad_and_Tobago_2011_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Trinidad_and_Tobago ;
    dcterms:date "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "50.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.4"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://idbdocs.iadb.org/wsdocs/getdocument.aspx?docnum=36486064" ;
    :definitionText "(Trinidad and Tobago 2011) Forests: are ecosystems occurring on areas of land with existing or potential tree canopy of at least 50% that cover a minimum land area of 0.4 ha. National Forest Policy. http://idbdocs.iadb.org/wsdocs/getdocument.aspx?docnum=36486064" .

:def_Forest_Turkey_1987_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Turkey ;
    dcterms:date "1987"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://faolex.fao.org/docs/texts/tur20346.doc" ;
    :definitionText "(Turkey 1987) - Tree and woodland communities, which are grown by human efforts, are regarded as Forest, together with their lands; • Privately owned lands containing trees and woodland species, which do not grow naturally in the neighbouring forest or any kind of trees or woodlands on privately owned land and smaller than three hectares are not considered as forest; FOREST LAW No. 6831, ARTICLE 1 (AS AMENDED BY LAW NO. 3373, 1987): http://faolex.fao.org/docs/texts/tur20346.doc" .

:def_Forest_Turkey_2004_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Turkey ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.sayistay.gov.tr/english_tca/Performance/ProtectionOfForests.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Turkey 2004) A unity of life consisting of small systems made of various plants, animals, bacteria and microorganisms. Karabeyli, Levent et al. 2004. Protection of forests. Turkish Court of Accounts. Performance Audit Report. 78 p. http://www.sayistay.gov.tr/english_tca/Performance/ProtectionOfForests.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Turkey_2004_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Turkey ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.sayistay.gov.tr/english_tca/Performance/ProtectionOfForests.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Turkey 2004) forest is a unity of life consisting of small systems made of various plants, animals, bacteria and microorganisms. http://www.sayistay.gov.tr/english_tca/Performance/ProtectionOfForests.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Turkey_2009_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Turkey ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "11.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://web.ogm.gov.tr/languages/English/dokumanlar/Publications/stateofforests.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Turkey 2009) GDF. A forest ecosystem is a natural unit consisting of all plants of which the main element is forest trees, animals and micro-organisms (biotic factors) in an area functioning together with all of the non-living physical (abiotic factors) factors of the environment. …The forest area in terms of crown density is classified into two main groups. Forest area with the crown density of 11-100 percent is defined as productive forest area constituting about 50 percent of the country’s f" .

:def_Forest_Ukraine_2010_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Ukraine ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.envsec.org/publications/fact_finding_study_illegal_logging_eng_feb_11.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Ukraine 2010) A forest is a type of natural complex combining mostly tree and bush vegetation with corresponding soils, herbaceous vegetation, fauna, micro-organisms and other natural components, which are interrelated in their development and affect each other and the environment. http://www.envsec.org/publications/fact_finding_study_illegal_logging_eng_feb_11.pdf" .

:def_Forest_United_Kingdom_nd_009
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :United_Kingdom ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.woodlander.co.uk/cgi-bin/viewrecordsalpha.asp?letter=F" ;
    :definitionText "(United Kingdom) Historically in Britain a Forest, with a capital 'F', was a tract of land subject to special laws for hunting (as in \"Royal Forests\" and \"Chases\"). Some of these Forests contained little woodland. The modern usage of the word is far more general, relating to any extensive tract of tree-covered land. Large areas of more or less natural tree cover are always termed forest. In Britain, the word has recently been applied specifically to large conifer plantations, such as those in th" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_NASS_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_NASS ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "lhutton@nass.usda.gov" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-NASS 2003) – “We rely on respondent ‘self’ definition for the 5 year Census of Agriculture via mail out/mail back. Our June area survey, we rely on data collected from trained enumerators who usually represent the ‘local’ definition”. Linda Hutton. lhutton@nass.usda.gov.. 12 August 2003." .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_NRCS_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_NRCS ;
    :heightMin "4.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.statlab.iastate.edu/soils/nssh/622.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-NRCS) Forestland ecological sites are separated from rangeland ecological sites based on the historic climax plant community that occupied the site before the arrival of European settlers. An Ecological Site Type of \"Forestland\" is assigned and described where this historic vegetation was dominated by a 25% overstory canopy of trees, as determined by crown perimeter-vertical projection. A tree is defined as a woody-stemmed plant that can grow to 4 meters in height at maturity. http:/" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_NRCS_nd_005
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_NRCS ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-NRCS) Land on which the historic climax plant community is dominated by trees. www.plant-materials.nrcs.usda.gov/pubs/idpmctn280101.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DI_BIA_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DI_BIA ;
    :sourceRef "http://codes.lp.findlaw.com/uscode/25/33/3103" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DI-BIA) (2) \"forest\" means an ecosystem of at least one acre in size, including timberland and woodland, which - (A) is characterized by a more or less dense and extensive tree cover, (B) contains, or once contained, at least ten percent tree crown cover, and (C) is not developed or planned for exclusive nonforest use; http://codes.lp.findlaw.com/uscode/25/33/3103" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DI_BLM_1999_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DI_BLM ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.blm.gov/nstc/library/pdf/1734-7.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DI-BLM 1999) Land on which the potential natural community is dominated by trees. http://www.blm.gov/nstc/library/pdf/1734-7.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DI_BLM_1999_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DI_BLM ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.blm.gov/nstc/library/pdf/samplveg.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DI-BLM 1999) Land on which the vegetation is dominated by trees. Lands are classified forestland if the trees now (not?) present will provide 25 percent or greater canopy cover at maturity. Lands not presently forestland that were originally or could become forested through natural succession may be classified as potential natural forestland. http://www.blm.gov/nstc/library/pdf/samplveg.pdf and http://www.blm.gov/nstc/library/pdf/utilstudies.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_EPA_2002_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_EPA ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.epa.gov/globalwarming/publications/outreach/general/glossary.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-EPA 2002) Terrestrial ecosystem (biome) with enough annual precipitation (at least 76 centimeters or 30 inches) to support growth of various species of trees and smaller forms of vegetation. http://www.epa.gov/globalwarming/publications/outreach/general/glossary.pdf, http://www.gcrio.org/OnLnDoc/pdf/2002-inventory.pdf, and http://yosemite.epa.gov/oar/globalwarming.nsf/webprintview/Glossary.html#F" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_OOP_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_OOP ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.epa.gov/trs" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-OOP) -Terrestrial ecosystem (biome) with enough average annual precipitation (at least 76 centimeters or 30 inches) to support growth of various species of trees and smaller forms of vegetation. Office of Policy : Inventory of U.S. Greenhouse Gas Emissions and Sinks. Annex T: Glossary Term Detail. http://www.epa.gov/trs" .

:def_Forest_Vietnam_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Vietnam ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.asb.cgiar.org/PDFwebdocs/REALU-Final%20Report%20-%20Vietnam.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Vietnam) forest. According to Vietnam’s Forest Protection and Development Law 2004, “forest” is defined as ‘an ecosystem with trees, animals and biota, soil and other environmental factors, in which timber species, bamboo or other species provide a canopy cover of more than 10%. Plantation forest and natural forest are grouped into production forest, protection forest and special-use forest’. http://www.asb.cgiar.org/PDFwebdocs/REALU-Final%20Report%20-%20Vietnam.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Yugoslavia_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :National ;
    :appliesIn :Yugoslavia ;
    :sourceRef "bojos@ptt.yu" ;
    :definitionText "(Yugoslavia) Forest - the terrain on which forest trees grow. \"Srdjan BOJOVIC\" <bojos@ptt.yu" .

:def_Forest_Canada_BC_2010_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_BC ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.bclaws.ca/Recon/document/freeside/--%20f%20--/forest%20act%20%20rsbc%201996%20%20c.%20157/00_act/96157_01.xml" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada-BC 2010) \"Provincial forest\" means forest land designated under section 5; FOREST ACT [RSBC 1996] CHAPTER 157 (Current to 19 Jan 2010). http://www.bclaws.ca/Recon/document/freeside/--%20f%20--/forest%20act%20%20rsbc%201996%20%20c.%20157/00_act/96157_01.xml" .

:def_Forest_Canada_BC_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_BC ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.for.gov.bc.ca/RIC/Pubs/teVeg/VRI-PhotoInterp/photo-03.htm#P213_14404" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada-BC) = Treed - A polygon is considered Treed if at least 10% of the polygon area, by crown cover, consists of tree species of any size. http://www.for.gov.bc.ca/RIC/Pubs/teVeg/VRI-PhotoInterp/photo-03.htm#P213_14404" .

:def_Forest_Canada_BC_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_BC ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.babineefmpp.com/glossary/F.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada-BC) Forest: as defined by the Forest Practices Code of British Columbia Act includes all of the following - forest land, whether Crown land or private land; Crown range; Crown land or private land that is predominantly maintained in one or more successive stands of trees, successive crops of forage, or wilderness. http://www.babineefmpp.com/glossary/F.html" .

:def_Forest_Canada_BC_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_BC ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.for.gov.bc.ca/pab/publctns/westland/gloss.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada-BC) In British Columbia, provincial forests and other unalienated Crown lands for which the Ministry of Forests is responsible, including both forested lands and non-forested lands such as tundra, wetlands, rangelands, deserts, rock, and ice. http://www.for.gov.bc.ca/pab/publctns/westland/gloss.htm" .

:def_Forest_Canada_BC_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_BC ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.for.gov.bc.ca/hfp/Planning/RPGLOSS/F.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada-BC) Land classified under Section 4 of the Forest Act that the chief forester considers will provide the greatest contribution to the social and economic welfare of the Province if predominantly maintained in successive crops of trees or forage, or both, or maintained as wilderness. http://www.for.gov.bc.ca/hfp/Planning/RPGLOSS/F.htm" .

:def_Forest_Canada_Saskatchewan1996_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
