    :appliesIn :Canada_Saskatchewan1996 ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.qp.gov.sk.ca/documents/english/statutes/statutes/f19-1.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada–Saskatchewan1996) “Forest land” means: (i) any Crown resource land that is designated as a provincial forest pursuant to the regulations; (ii) any Crown land described in a forest management agreement, a term supply licence or a forest product permit; (iii) any Crown land administered by the Ministry of Agriculture or the Ministry of Environment that: (A) in the opinion of the minister, has a forest ecosystem as the predominant ecosystem; or (B) is prescribed as forest fringe timber supp" .

:def_Forest_India_Maharashtra_and_Anr2010_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
