    :sourceRef "http://thelawofnature.ph/downloadables/legal-arsenal/CHAPTER_2-_LAND.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Philippine Palawan 1992) Forest land includes the public forest, the permanent forest or forest reserves, and forest reservations. Public forest is the mass of lands of the public domain which has not been subject to the present system of classification for the determination of which lands are needed for forest purposes and which are not. Permanent forest or forest reserves refers to those lands of the public domain which have been the subject of the present system of classification and declare" .

