:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Wisconsin_1912_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Wisconsin ;
    dcterms:date "1912"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://folio.legis.state.wi.us/cgi-bin/om_isapi.dll?clientID=171211&advquery=forest&headingswithhits=on&infobase=stats.nfo&record={D}&recordswithhits=on&zz=" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Wisconsin 1912) State forests lands include all lands granted to the state by an act of congress entitled, \"An act granting lands to the state of Wisconsin for forestry purposes,\" approved June 27, 1906; all lands donated to the state by the Nebagamon Lumber Company for forestry purposes; all lands acquired pursuant to chapter 450, laws of 1903, chapter 264, laws of 1905, chapter 638, laws of 1911, and chapter 639, laws of 1911, or under ss. 1494-41 to 1494-62, 1915 stats., and all la" .

:def_Forest_Australia_NSW_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Australia_NSW ;
    :sourceRef "http://155.187.10.12/glossary/fl-nsw.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia-NSW) - A plant community dominated by long-boled trees in close proximity. cf. woodland. Flora of New South Wales http://155.187.10.12/glossary/fl-nsw.html" .

:def_Forest_Australia_NSW_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Australia_NSW ;
    :canopyThreshold "80.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dlwc.nsw.gov.au/care/veg/pdfs/clearing_vegtypes_mar02.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia–NSW) - Closed Forest vegetation where trees cover more than 80% of the area under application. Open Forest vegetation where the trees cover more than 50% of the area under application. http://www.dlwc.nsw.gov.au/care/veg/pdfs/clearing_vegtypes_mar02.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Australia_Queensland_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Australia_Queensland ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nrm.qld.gov.au/slats/final9799.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia-Queensland) There are many definitions of what constitutes a forest or woody vegetation. A common definition used by foresters is 20 per cent crown cover which equates to approximately 12 per cent foliage projective cover (FPC) (NFI, 1998) http://www.nrm.qld.gov.au/slats/final9799.html" .

:def_Forest_Australia_South_Australia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Australia_South_Australia ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.atlas.sa.gov.au/atlas1986/2ENVIRONMENT_RESOURCES/5VEGETATION.cfm" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia-South Australia) - Forest is mapped where trees form the tallest stratum and their projective foliage covers more than 30% of the ground. http://www.atlas.sa.gov.au/atlas1986/2ENVIRONMENT_RESOURCES/5VEGETATION.cfm" .

:def_Forest_Australia_Tasmania_1985_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Australia_Tasmania ;
    dcterms:date "1985"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.austlii.edu.au/au/legis/tas/consol_act/fpa1985183/s3.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia-Tasmania 1985) \"forest\" means an area containing trees; Forest Practices Act 1985 - Sect 3. http://www.austlii.edu.au/au/legis/tas/consol_act/fpa1985183/s3.html" .

:def_Forest_Australia_Tasmania_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Australia_Tasmania ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.delm.tas.gov.au/pluc/glossy.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia-Tasmania) - An area, incorporating all living and non-living components, that is dominated by trees having usually a single stem and a mature or potentially mature stand height exceeding 5 metres, and with existing or potential projective cover of overstorey strata about equal to or greater than 30 per cent. http://www.delm.tas.gov.au/pluc/glossy.html" .

:def_Forest_Australia_Tasmania_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Australia_Tasmania ;
    :canopyThreshold "50.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dpiw.tas.gov.au/inter.nsf/Attachments/LJEM-6K32GF/$FILE/Glossary" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia-Tasmania) - Vegetation with trees more than 5 m high and more than 50% solid canopy cover. http://www.dpiw.tas.gov.au/inter.nsf/Attachments/LJEM-6K32GF/$FILE/Glossary,%20Appendices,%20Index.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Australia_Tasmania_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Australia_Tasmania ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.workplacetransformations.com/Forestry%20Scam%20Erica%206-426.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia-Tasmania) \"Forest\" or \"forest\" means an area of land carrying a Forest Community, or a plantation of one or more tree species established for timber production; http://www.workplacetransformations.com/Forestry%20Scam%20Erica%206-426.htm" .

:def_Forest_Australia_Tasmania_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Australia_Tasmania ;
    :heightMin "8.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.rfa.gov.au/rfa/tas/raa/envher/volumes1-4/gloss.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia-Tasmania) forest in the context of this regional forest agreement, is an area, incorporating all living and non-living components, that is dominated by trees having usually a single stem and a mature or potential mature stand height exceeding 8 metres, and with existing or potential projective cover of overstorey strata about equal to or greater than 5 per cent. http://www.rfa.gov.au/rfa/tas/raa/envher/volumes1-4/gloss.html" .

:def_Forest_Belgium_Wallonie_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Belgium_Wallonie ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://mrw.wallonie.be/cgi/dgrne/sibw/eunis.glo.pl?WORD=forest" ;
    :definitionText "(Belgium-Wallonie) A continuous tract over a large area where the dominant organisms are trees. Trees are of height >5m, tree crown cover of >10%, area >0.5ha and width >20m. http://mrw.wallonie.be/cgi/dgrne/sibw/eunis.glo.pl?WORD=forest" .

:def_Forest_Belgium_Walloon_Region_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Belgium_Walloon_Region ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "100.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Belgium-Walloon Region 1997) - Wooded areas 100 ha. (European Communities 1997a - p 94)." .

:def_Forest_Belgium_Walloon_Region_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Belgium_Walloon_Region ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "100.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "H.Lecomte@mrw.wallonie.be" ;
    :definitionText "(Belgium-Walloon Region 2000) Voici notre définition de la forêt. On se rattache en fait à la Définition de la FAO utilisée pour les statistiques internationales sauf pour l'étendue minimale qui est de 10 ares (surface pouvant contenir notre grande placette) et la largeur minimale du peuplement qui est de 9m. Terrains avec un couvert forestier de plus de 10%, que ce soit des formations forestières denses ou claires, avec des arbres dont la hauteur abattable minimale est de 5m; -terrains avec jeu" .

:def_Forest_Canada_BC_nd_005
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_BC ;
    :sourceRef "http://books.google.com/books?id=zeTU8QauENcC&pg=PA192&lpg=PA192&dq=Germany+Forest+definition+define+%22forest+is%22+law+act+code&source=bl&ots=1jUsKaLHy4&sig=uRBHD83hyloLheFqPmfiDgK687o&hl=en&sa=X&ei" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada- BC) Crown land or private land that is predominantly maintained in one or more successive stands of trees, successive crops fo forage or wilderness. http://books.google.com/books?id=zeTU8QauENcC&pg=PA192&lpg=PA192&dq=Germany+Forest+definition+define+%22forest+is%22+law+act+code&source=bl&ots=1jUsKaLHy4&sig=uRBHD83hyloLheFqPmfiDgK687o&hl=en&sa=X&ei=OcY-T7PEOcX10gHzx8jzBw&ved=0CDgQ6AEwAw#v=onepage&q=Germany%20Forest%20definition%20define%20%22forest%20is%22%20law%20act%20code&f=false" .

:def_Forest_Canada_Alberta_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_Alberta ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www3.gov.ab.ca/srd/forests/fmd/directives/fa.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada-Alberta 2000) Forest land means public land intermittently covered with forest growth. http://www3.gov.ab.ca/srd/forests/fmd/directives/fa.html and http://www.qp.alberta.ca/1266.cfm?page=F22.cfm&leg_type=Acts&isbncln=9780779784318" .

:def_Forest_Canada_BC_2008_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_BC ;
    dcterms:date "2008"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.for.gov.bc.ca/hfd/library/documents/glossary/Glossary.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada-BC 2008) “A complex community of plants and animals in which trees are the most conspicuous members and where the tree crown density—the amount of compactness of foliage in the tree tops—is greater than 10 percent” (64):Section F quote BC 2008 http://www.for.gov.bc.ca/hfd/library/documents/glossary/Glossary.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Canada_Newfoundland_and_Labrador_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_Newfoundland_and_Labrador ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.gov.nl.ca/hoa/statutes/f23.htm#2" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada-Newfoundland and Labrador) \"Forest land\" means land upon which are growing or standing trees or shrubs and includes dry marsh, bogland and land commonly known as \"barrens\"; http://www.gov.nl.ca/hoa/statutes/f23.htm#2" .

:def_Forest_Canada_Nova_Scotia_1989_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_Nova_Scotia ;
    dcterms:date "1989"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.gov.ns.ca/just/regulations/regs/for8297.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada-Nova Scotia 1989) “Forest\" means a plant association consisting predominately of trees. http://www.gov.ns.ca/just/regulations/regs/for8297.htm,  http://www.gov.ns.ca/just/regulations/regs/fofire.htm and https://nslegislature.ca/sites/default/files/legc/statutes/forests.htm" .

:def_Forest_Canada_Ontario_1998_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_Ontario ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "34.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ontarionature.org/pdf/Significant_Woodlands_Guidelines(Draft%20Aug%202004" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada-Ontario 1998) Forest (including woodland) - A treed community with at least 34% tree cover. (Ecological Land Classification for southern Ontario, O.M.N.R., 1998). http://www.ontarionature.org/pdf/Significant_Woodlands_Guidelines(Draft%20Aug%202004).pdf" .

:def_Forest_Canada_Ontario_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_Ontario ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.mnr.gov.on.ca/stdprodconsume/groups/lr/@mnr/@forests/documents/document/mnr_e000254.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada-Ontario 2003) (Ecology) A plant community predominantly of trees and other woody vegetation, growing more or less closely together. http://www.mnr.gov.on.ca/stdprodconsume/groups/lr/@mnr/@forests/documents/document/mnr_e000254.pdf." .

:def_Forest_Canada_Ontario_2003_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_Ontario ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.mnr.gov.on.ca/stdprodconsume/groups/lr/@mnr/@forests/documents/document/mnr_e000254.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada-Ontario 2003) (Forest Diversity) An aggregate of stands. http://www.mnr.gov.on.ca/stdprodconsume/groups/lr/@mnr/@forests/documents/document/mnr_e000254.pdf." .

:def_Forest_Canada_Ontario_2008_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_Ontario ;
    dcterms:date "2008"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.mnr.gov.on.ca/stdprodconsume/groups@mnr/@forests/documents/document/stdprod_0899387.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada-Ontario 2008) (woodland) – Synonymous with forest, any land covered with trees and shrubs. http://www.mnr.gov.on.ca/stdprodconsume/groups@mnr/@forests/documents/document/stdprod_0899387.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Canada_Ontario_Halton_Region_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_Ontario_Halton_Region ;
    :areaMin "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.region.halton.on.ca/ppw/OfficialPlan/definitions/cont1.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada-Ontario-Halton Region) Forest means woodlands as defined by The Woodlands Improvement Act, covering a ground area of 10ha or more. http://www.region.halton.on.ca/ppw/OfficialPlan/definitions/cont1.htm" .

:def_Forest_Canada_Saskatchewan_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_Saskatchewan ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.qp.gov.sk.ca/documents/English/Statutes/Statutes/P22-1.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada-Saskatchewan) “Forest land” means any uncultivated land in Saskatchewan on which trees or shrubs are growing or standing or any barren, dry marsh or bog, and includes any highway over any such lands; http://www.qp.gov.sk.ca/documents/English/Statutes/Statutes/P22-1.pdf ." .

:def_Forest_Ethiopia_Kafa_Biosphere_Reserve_2012_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Ethiopia_Kafa_Biosphere_Reserve ;
    dcterms:date "2012"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "https://www.nabu.de/imperia/md/content/nabude/international/131118-nabu-forest_status_report_kafa_biosphere_reserve.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Ethiopia-Kafa Biosphere Reserve 2012?) The forest definition of the Ethiopian government complies with the UNFCCC definition of a forest and can be used for the purposes of the Kyoto Protocol. 5 The UNFCCC defines a forest as an area of land 0.05–1 hectare in size, of which more than 10–30% is covered by tree canopy. Trees must also have the potential to reach a minimum height of 2-5 meters. The satellite image interpretation of the SPOT5 sensor (2011) is based on that forest definition. It res" .

:def_Forest_India_Harda_District_Madhya_Pradesh_2005_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :India_Harda_District_Madhya_Pradesh ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.geog.cam.ac.uk/research/projects/harda/reports/B4-ELDFReport.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(India- Harda District, Madhya Pradesh 2005). All lands with a tree canopy density of more than 10 per cent, though they may not be statutorily notified as forest. .http://www.geog.cam.ac.uk/research/projects/harda/reports/B4-ELDFReport.pdf" .

:def_Forest_India_Madhya_Pradesh_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :India_Madhya_Pradesh ;
    :areaMin "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "Narendra Kumar <nkumar@bom6.vsnl.net.in>" ;
    :definitionText "(India -Madhya Pradesh) Forest (in context of private forest) as area of 10 hectare or more having at least 200 trees per hectare. Source: Narendra Kumar nkumar@bom6.vsnl.net.in." .

:def_Forest_India_United_Khasi_and_Jaintia_Hills_Autonomous_Di_1960_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :India_United_Khasi_and_Jaintia_Hills_Autonomous_Di ;
    dcterms:date "1960"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.thestatesman.net/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=382252&catid=52" ;
    :definitionText "(India -United Khasi and Jaintia Hills Autonomous District 1960) The Management & Control of Forests), Act 1958, amended in 1960,“Forest is and shall be deemed to be a forest if in the area there are reasonable number of trees, say not less than 25 trees per acre, reserved or any other forest produce growing on such area, which have been or are capable of being exploited for purposes of business or trade.” http://www.thestatesman.net/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=382252&catid=52" .

:def_Forest_Russia_Federation_Tundra_Boundary_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Russia_Federation_Tundra_Boundary ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.resgeom.slu.se/swe/Publikationer/VisaPub.cfm?1080" ;
    :definitionText "(Russia Federation Tundra Boundary) In the Russian studies, the northern forest boundary was drawn based on medium resolution (Resurs MSU-SK) winter images, using data from sites with known characteristics as reference. The criteria set for boundary delineation of forest from tundra: · Minimum tree canopy cover of forest: 20 percent · Minimum width of forest: 20 kilometres. More narrow strips of forest (e.g., along river valleys), as well as directly adjacent treeless areas (alpine areas and bog" .

:def_Forest_UK_Great_Britain_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :UK_Great_Britain ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.metla.fi/eu/cost/e43/minutes/wg1-min-florence.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UK-Great Britain) Forest - 20 % crown cover http://www.metla.fi/eu/cost/e43/minutes/wg1-min-florence.pdf" .

:def_Forest_UK_Halton_Borough_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :UK_Halton_Borough ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.cartoplus.co.uk/halton/text/app_5_glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(UK-Halton Borough) Community Forest- A large area of wooded landscape in and around towns containing a mixture of woodlands and other land uses including farmland, villages, leisure enterprises, nature areas and public open space. http://www.cartoplus.co.uk/halton/text/app_5_glossary.htm" .

:def_Forest_UK_Scotland_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :UK_Scotland ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.forestry.gov.uk/forestry/HCOU-4X2K5J" ;
    :definitionText "(UK-Scotland) - An area of woodland, often used to describe large areas with coniferous or deciduous trees or a mixture of both http://www.forestry.gov.uk/forestry/HCOU-4X2K5J" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_FS_R8_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_FS_R8 ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "100.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-FS-R8 1997) An area of trees with overlapping crowns (generally forming a 60 to 100 percent cover) USDA" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_FS_SRS_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_FS_SRS ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.srs.fs.fed.us/sustain/report/appendix/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-FS-SRS) An assemblage of woody vegetation typically attaining positions in a plant community at the tallest level; attains height and diameter growth of canopy-layer trees within established averages for the species. http://www.srs.fs.fed.us/sustain/report/appendix/glossary.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_EPA_Yosemite_2007_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_EPA_Yosemite ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://yosemite.epa.gov/r10/water.nsf/NPDES+Permits/Sewage+S825/$FILE/503-032007.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-EPA-Yosemite 2007) Forest is a tract of land thick with trees and underbrush. http://yosemite.epa.gov/r10/water.nsf/NPDES+Permits/Sewage+S825/$FILE/503-032007.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Arizona_Santa_Cruz_Country_2008_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Arizona_Santa_Cruz_Country ;
    dcterms:date "2008"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "60.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "https://sonoraninstitute.org/files/pdf/santa-cruz-river-riparian-vegetation-map-final-report-10162008.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Arizona-Santa Cruz Country 2008) Forest = over 60% tree cover.  https://sonoraninstitute.org/files/pdf/santa-cruz-river-riparian-vegetation-map-final-report-10162008.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Arkansas_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Arkansas ;
    :sourceRef "Baker Jim Grant <jim.grant@mail.state.ar.us>" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Arkansas) Forest - a large area of land primarily covered with trees as well as the other organisms, soil, water and air associated with them. Source: Principles of Silviculture, Frederick F. Baker Jim Grant jim.grant@mail.state.ar.us no official definitions in Arkansas law." .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_California_2002_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_California ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fire.ca.gov/CDFBOFDB/pdfs/Role%20of%20RPF_2002%20ygeditfinal_.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-California 2002) A forest is a complex interrelationship of soil, air, water, climate, trees, plants, fish, wildlife, grazing animals, and people, together with their machines and structures. http://www.fire.ca.gov/CDFBOFDB/pdfs/Role%20of%20RPF_2002%20ygeditfinal_.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Connecticut_2004_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Connecticut ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://farm.fic.niu.edu/fic/laws/state/ct12107.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Connecticut 2004) - The term \"forest land\" means any tract or tracts of land aggregating twenty-five acres or more in area bearing tree growth in such quantity and so spaced as to constitute in the opinion of the State Forester a forest area and maintained in the opinion of the State Forester in a state of proper forest condition and such land consists of (1) one tract of land of twenty-five or more contiguous acres, which acres may be in contiguous municipalities, (2) two or more tra" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Connecticut_2011_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Connecticut ;
    dcterms:date "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.cga.ct.gov/2011/pub/chap451a.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Connecticut 2011) \"Forest land\" means that portion of a parcel of land which constitutes a total of at least one contiguous acre on which there is no structure, maintained landscape area, accessway or other improvement and which is (A) occupied in random distribution by trees having a minimum diameter of three inches as measured from a point on the trunk which is four and one-half feet above the ground such trees comprising at least seven and one-half square feet of basal area and the" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Delaware_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Delaware ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Delaware) \"Forest\" means a biological community dominated by trees covering a contiguous area of land and includes any definition thereof developed by the Department of Agriculture Forest Service. A \"forest\" may be identified by the diversity of the tree species composing it or by its type. A \"forest type\" is a forest composed of associations of tree species that have similar ecological requirements." .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Delaware_Wilmington_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Delaware_Wilmington ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.wilmingtonnc.gov/Portals/0/documents/Development%20Services/Plans%20and%20Documents/LDC/Art%2015%20-%20Definitions.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Delaware-Wilmington) Forested area(s): A forest is defined as any area on a site with greater than or equal to one hundred (100) trees per acre. http://www.wilmingtonnc.gov/Portals/0/documents/Development%20Services/Plans%20and%20Documents/LDC/Art%2015%20-%20Definitions.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Florida_1999_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Florida ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dot.state.fl.us/surveyingandmapping/Manuals/fluccmanual.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Florida 1999). Upland Forest -This category of land cover is reserved for those upland areas which support a tree canopy closure of ten (10) percent or more. http://www.dot.state.fl.us/surveyingandmapping/Manuals/fluccmanual.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Florida_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Florida ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://edis.ifas.ufl.edu/fr063" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Florida 2009) A biological community of plants and animals that is dominated by trees and other woody plants. http://edis.ifas.ufl.edu/fr063 Florida 2009" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Hawaii_1993_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Hawaii ;
    dcterms:date "1993"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.state.hi.us/dlnr/dofaw/rules/Chap106.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Hawaii 1993) “Forest” means forest land occupied by forest trees and associated wildlife species, and timber thereon. http://www.state.hi.us/dlnr/dofaw/rules/Chap106.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Hawaii_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Hawaii ;
    :canopyThreshold "60.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fs.fed.us/psw/publications/documents/psw_gtr076/psw_gtr076.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Hawaii) Closed forest--Generally, a unit of vegetation with overstory trees whose crowns are mostly touching. Plant communities with trees having a crown cover of 60 percent or more are considered closed forests. http://www.fs.fed.us/psw/publications/documents/psw_gtr076/psw_gtr076.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Hawaii_Kauai_County_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Hawaii_Kauai_County ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.kauaigov.org/finance/RPA/tfde.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Hawaii-Kauai County) \"Forest\" means forestland occupied by forest trees and associated wildlife species, and timber thereon. http://www.kauaigov.org/finance/RPA/tfde.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Idaho_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Idaho ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Idaho) Forest land means any land which has enough forest growth, standing or down, to constitute, in the judgement of the Department, an insect or disease infestation breeding ground of a nature to constitute a menace, injurious and dangerous to the forest resources in the district or zone of infestation. www.fs.fed.us/im/directives/field/r1/fsm/3400/3400_zero_code.rtf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Illinois_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Illinois ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.agr.state.il.us/gis/stats/landcover/mainpages/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Illinois) - Includes areas that are predominantly covered with trees and woody vegetation. http://www.agr.state.il.us/gis/stats/landcover/mainpages/glossary.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Illinois_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Illinois ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.gurnee.il.us/municipal_code/pdf_chapters/chapter45.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Illinois) Forest means a dense growth of trees and underbrush covering a large tract of land, or a significant portion of a large tract of land. http://www.gurnee.il.us/municipal_code/pdf_chapters/chapter45.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Illinois_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Illinois ;
    :canopyThreshold "16.7"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://dnr.state.il.us/orep/inrin/ctap/sumrepo/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Illinois) Generally, land with trees on it. Foresters define as forestland any land stocked with trees of any size that cover 16.7% of the land area. http://dnr.state.il.us/orep/inrin/ctap/sumrepo/glossary.htm The Changing Illinois Environment: Critical Trends." .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Iowa_1999_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Iowa ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.legis.state.ia.us/IACODE/1999SUPPLEMENT/161A/42.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Iowa 1999) \"Forest\" means stands of native or introduced trees containing at least two hundred trees per acre and located on privately owned land. However, a stand of fruit trees is not a forest. http://www.legis.state.ia.us/IACODE/1999SUPPLEMENT/161A/42.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Iowa_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Iowa ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.legis.state.ia.us/Rules/2003/iac/027iac/2710/2710.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Iowa 2003) “Forest land” means land with stands of native or introduced trees containing at least 200 trees per acre. Stands of fruit trees shall not be considered as forest land. http://www.legis.state.ia.us/Rules/2003/iac/027iac/2710/2710.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Iowa_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Iowa ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.legis.state.ia.us/GA/77GA/Legislation/HF/02300/HF02351/Current.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Iowa) \"Forestland\" means stands of native or introduced forest plantation of at least three acres, including trees located on privately owned land. However, a stand of fruit trees or Christmas trees is not forestland. http://www.legis.state.ia.us/GA/77GA/Legislation/HF/02300/HF02351/Current.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Kansas_1971_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Kansas ;
    dcterms:date "1971"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "Atchison <ratchiso@oznet.ksu.edu>" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Kansas 1971) Forest - Generally an ecosystem characterized by a more or less dense and extensive tree cover. More particularly, a plant community predominantly of trees and other woody vegetation, growing more or less closely together. \"Terminology of Forest Science, Technology, Practice & Products\" SAF, 1971. Robert L. Atchison ratchiso@oznet.ksu.edu" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Kentucky_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Kentucky ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.surfacemining.ky.gov/Publications/NonCoalRegs/405KAR5_001_Definitions_091203.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) \"Forest land\" means lands dominated by canopy forming trees, or from a postmining land use standpoint, areas planted throughout with trees. http://www.surfacemining.ky.gov/Publications/NonCoalRegs/405KAR5_001_Definitions_091203.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Kentucky_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Kentucky ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.lrc.state.ky.us/kar/302/028/010.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) \"Forest\" means a concentration of trees and related vegetation in nonurban areas characterized by natural terrain and drainage patterns. http://www.lrc.state.ky.us/kar/302/028/010.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Kentucky_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Kentucky ;
    :sourceRef "Steve.Kull@mail.state.ky.us" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) Forest - an ecosystem characterized by a more or less dense and extensive tree cover, often consisting of composition, structure, age class, and associated processes, and commonly including meadows, streams, fish, and wildlife. The State of Kentucky does not have the terms Forest, Forestland, or Tree officially defined in State Statute or Regulation. The Division of Forestry utilizes the Society of American Forester's definitions for these terms as listed in John A. Helms' T" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Louisiana_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Louisiana ;
    :sourceRef "http://text.lsuagcenter.com/en/environment/forestry/commercial_forestry/Glossary+of+Forestry+Terms.htm#F" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Louisiana) Forest - A large area of land primarily covered with trees as well as the other organisms, soil, water and air associated with them. http://text.lsuagcenter.com/en/environment/forestry/commercial_forestry/Glossary+of+Forestry+Terms.htm#F." .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Louisiana_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Louisiana ;
    :sourceRef "http://text.lsuagcenter.com/en/environment/forestry/commercial_forestry/Glossary+of+Forestry+Terms.htm#F" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Louisiana) Forestland - Tract of land with trees and woody plants generally covering the landscape. http://text.lsuagcenter.com/en/environment/forestry/commercial_forestry/Glossary+of+Forestry+Terms.htm#F." .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Maine_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Maine ;
    :areaMin "2.0234"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.memun.org/resources/public/html/TAXDATA/PropertyTaxBull/bulletin4.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Maine) - Land 5 acres or greater dominated by the growth of forest trees and other woody vegetation. http://www.memun.org/resources/public/html/TAXDATA/PropertyTaxBull/bulletin4.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Maine_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Maine ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.maine.gov/doc/mfs/woodswise/glossary.html#F" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Maine) A biological community dominated by trees and other woody plants. (http://www.maine.gov/doc/mfs/woodswise/glossary.html#F" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Maryland_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Maryland ;
    :areaMin "0.4047"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dnr.state.md.us/download/reforest.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Maryland) “Forest” means:(i) a biological community dominated by trees or other woody plants covering a land area of 1 acre or more, or (ii) an area that has been cut but not cleared of trees or other woody plants. http://www.dnr.state.md.us/download/reforest.pdf and http://www.sha.state.md.us/businesswithsha/bizStdsSpecs/oed/reforestationLawSum/reforestlaw.asp" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Maryland_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Maryland ;
    :canopyThreshold "50.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://pilot.wash.lib.md.us/washco/forestcn.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Maryland) A biological community dominated by trees and other woody plants covering a land area of at least 10,000 square feet as long as there are at least 100 live trees per acre with at least 50 percent of those trees having a 2-inch or greater diameter at 4.5 feet above the ground. Areas that have been cut but not cleared of stumps or the root mat may also be included. \"Forest\" does not include orchards. http://pilot.wash.lib.md.us/washco/forestcn.html and http://www.dnr.state.md." .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Maryland_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Maryland ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dnr.state.md.us/Forests/Education/gloss.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Maryland) A biological community dominated by trees and other woody plants. http://www.dnr.state.md.us/Forests/Education/gloss.html, http://www.pfmt.org/glossary/f.htm or http://www.dnr.state.md.us/forests/gloss.html#f" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Maryland_Rockville_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Maryland_Rockville ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.rockvillemd.gov/zoning/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Maryland-Rockville) A dense growth of trees, together with other plants, covering a large area. According to the Forest and Tree Preservation Ordinance of the City of Rockville, a forest must cover a land area of 10,000 square feet or greater. http://www.rockvillemd.gov/zoning/glossary.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Michigan_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Michigan ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Michigan) “Forest” means a tract of land that is thick with trees and underbrush. www.deq.state.mi.us/documents/deq-swq-biosolids-Part%2024.doc" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Michigan_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Michigan ;
    :heightMin "6.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.rsgis.msu.edu/pdf/lclu/MIRIS_2_definitions.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Michigan) Upland Forest - Natural areas dominated by tree cover that is generally over 6 meters, or 20 feet, in height. The forest cover must occur in an upland setting with an understory of natural plant material or ground cover. If the understory has been altered to accommodate an agricultural or urban land use activity, such as a pasture or park, the area would be assigned to the appropriate land use type. Forest cover occurring in wetland environments would be assigned to the fore" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Michigan_Alpena_County_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Michigan_Alpena_County ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.alpenalib.org/Alpena%20Library/Chapter6_Land-Use.PDF" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Michigan-Alpena County) Forestland use areas are generally at least ten percent stocked by trees of any size. http://www.alpenalib.org/Alpena%20Library/Chapter6_Land-Use.PDF" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Minnesota_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Minnesota ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.revisor.leg.state.mn.us/stats/88/01.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Minnesota 2009) \"Forest\" means a plant association predominantly of trees and other woody vegetation occupying an extensive area of land. http://www.revisor.leg.state.mn.us/stats/88/01.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Minnesota_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Minnesota ;
    :sourceRef "http://deli.dnr.state.mn.us/metadata/tables/lusatra3_tab.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Minnesota) Forest Includes areas with at least two-thirds or more of the total canopy cover composed of predominantly woody deciduous or coniferous species. http://deli.dnr.state.mn.us/metadata/tables/lusatra3_tab.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Minnesota_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Minnesota ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.lmic.state.mn.us/projects/aboutlanduse.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Minnesota) Forested: Areas where two-thirds or more of the total canopy cover is composed of predominantly woody deciduous and coniferous species and areas of regenerated or young forest where commercial timber has been completely or partially removed by logging, other management activities or natural events; includes woodlots, shelterbelts and plantation. http://www.lmic.state.mn.us/projects/aboutlanduse.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_MississippI_2008_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_MississippI ;
    dcterms:date "2008"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://msucares.com/pubs/publications/p1250.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-MississippI 2008) Forest -- A plant community dominated by trees and woody plants. http://msucares.com/pubs/publications/p1250.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Missouri_1998_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Missouri ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "Mike Hoffmann <hoffmm@mail.conservation.state.mo.us>" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Missouri 1998) Although we do not have \"official\" definitions, we commonly use the accepted SAF definitions for these terms. See Dictionary of Forestry; John A. Helms, editor; published 1998 by the Sociecy of American Foresters. \"Mike Hoffmann\" hoffmm@mail.conservation.state.mo.us" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Missouri_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Missouri ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://mdc4.mdc.mo.gov/Documents/13183.doc" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Missouri 2003) An area dominated by trees forming a closed canopy and interspersed with multilayer shade tolerant sub-canopy trees, shrubs, vines, ferns and herbs. Trees attain a height of 60 to over 100 feet. The ground-flora is rich in spring ephemerals. http://mdc4.mdc.mo.gov/Documents/13183.doc" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_MissourI_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_MissourI ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://mdc4.mdc.mo.gov/Documents/13183.doc" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-MissourI 2003) An ecosystem characterized by a more or less dense and extensive tree cover, often consisting of stands varying in characteristics such as species or composition, structure, age class, and associated processes, and commonly including meadows, streams, fish, and wildlife – note: forests include special kinds such as industrial forests, non-industrial private forests, plantations, public forests, protection forests, and urban forests, as well as parks and wilderness. http" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Montana_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Montana ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.deq.state.mt.us/dir/Legal/Chapters/CH50-08.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Montana) \"Forest\" means a tract of land with trees and underbrush. http://www.deq.state.mt.us/dir/Legal/Chapters/CH50-08.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Montana_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Montana ;
    :sourceRef "http://data.opi.state.mt.us/bills/mca/15/44/15-44-102.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Montana) \"Forest\" means forest land and the timber on the land. http://data.opi.state.mt.us/bills/mca/15/44/15-44-102.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_New_Jersey_2002_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_New_Jersey ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.state.nj.us/dep/gis/digidownload/metadata/lulc02/anderson2002.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-New Jersey 2002)This Level I category contains any lands covered by woody vegetation other than wetlands. These areas are capable of producing timber and other wood products, and of supporting many kinds of outdoor recreation. Forestland is an important category environmentally, because it affects air quality, water quality, wildlife habitat, climate, and many other aspects of the ecology of an area. The Level II categories under Forestland are Deciduous; Coniferous; Mixed Deciduous-C" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_New_Jersey_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_New_Jersey ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.state.nj.us/dep/parksandforests/fire/docs/conservation_and_development.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-New Jersey) “Forest” means and includes any forest, bushland, grassland, salt marsh, and any combination thereof. http://www.state.nj.us/dep/parksandforests/fire/docs/conservation_and_development.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_New_Jersey_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_New_Jersey ;
    :heightMin "6.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.state.nj.us/dep/landuse/mglossary.html#f" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-New Jersey) Forested - that tree species with an average height greater than 20 feet are the predominant vegetation present. http://www.state.nj.us/dep/landuse/mglossary.html#f" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_New_Mexico_2007_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_New_Mexico ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.emnrd.state.nm.us/FD/documents/19204_Amended_6-14-07.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-New Mexico 2007) “Forest” means an area of at least one acre with at least 10 percent tree crown cover. New Mexico. http://www.emnrd.state.nm.us/FD/documents/19204_Amended_6-14-07.pdf and http://www.conwaygreene.com/lpbin21/lpext.dll/Test/NMACRaw/1/51fd0/571dd/572c0/572d3?fn=document-frame.htm&f=templates" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_North_Carolina_1971_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_North_Carolina ;
    dcterms:date "1971"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "Brown <David.R.Brown@ncmail.net>" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-North Carolina 1971) Forest - A plant community predominantly of trees and other woody vegetation, growing more or less closely together. Source: Terminology of Forest Science, Technology Practice and Products. Edited by F.C. Ford-Robertson. Society of American Foresters, Washington, D.C., 1971. David R. Brown David.R.Brown@ncmail.net" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_North_Carolina_1994_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_North_Carolina ;
    dcterms:date "1994"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://cgia.cgia.state.nc.us/gicc/standards/nclulc.html#P3" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-North Carolina 1994) Forest lands are covered with deciduous or coniferous woody vegetation about 3 meters or more in height. Forest lands exhibit a tree-crown area density of at least 10 percent. Lands from which trees have been removed to less than 10 percent crown density should be included in Category 3 (Herbaceous Cover and Shrubland) or another land cover category if appropriate. This category includes upland forests and forest land on seasonally or permanently wet or inundated " .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_North_Dakota_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_North_Dakota ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.state.nd.us/lr//cencode/T57C57.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-North Dakota) \"Forest\" means an area of land normally supporting a growth of planted tree cover, woodlands, or windbreaks. http://www.state.nd.us/lr//cencode/T57C57.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Ohio_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Ohio ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dnr.state.oh.us/odnr/relm/remsen/landuse/class4.html#no4" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Ohio) Forest Lands have a tree-crown areal density (crown closure percentage) of 10 percent or more, are stocked with trees capable of producing timber or other wood products, and exert an influence on the climate or water regime. http://www.dnr.state.oh.us/odnr/relm/remsen/landuse/class4.html#no4" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Oregon_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Oregon ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.leg.state.or.us/ors/477.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Oregon) \"Forestland\" means any woodland, brushland, timberland, grazing land or clearing that, during any time of the year, contains enough forest growth, slashing or vegetation to constitute, in the judgment of the forester, a fire hazard, regardless of how the land is zoned or taxed. As used in this subsection, \"clearing\" means any grassland, improved area, lake, meadow, mechanically or manually cleared area, road, rocky area, stream or other similar forestland opening that is surro" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Oregon_Portland_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Oregon_Portland ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.portlandonline.com/shared/cfm/image.cfm?id=106047" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Oregon-Portland) Trees with their crowns overlapping (generally forming 60-100% of cover. Natural Resource Inventory vegetation mapping project City of Portland Bureau of Planning. 18 p. http://www.portlandonline.com/shared/cfm/image.cfm?id=106047" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Pennsylvania_1974_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Pennsylvania ;
    dcterms:date "1974"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://farm.fic.niu.edu/fic/laws/state/pa72.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Pennsylvania 1974) \"Forest reserve.\" Land, ten acres or more, stocked by forest trees of any size and capable of producing timber or other wood products. Source: \"PA FARMLAND & FOREST LAND ASSESSMENT ACT\" (CLEAN AND GREEN) Act of 1974, P.L. 973, No. 319 http://farm.fic.niu.edu/fic/laws/state/pa72.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Pennsylvania_Centre_County_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Pennsylvania_Centre_County ;
    :sourceRef "http://county.centreconnect.org/planning/compplan/draft/forest.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Pennsylvania-Centre County) Forests are a biological community dominated by trees and other woody plants covering a land area of one acre or more. This also includes forests that have been cut but not cleared. In other areas, Forests are a biological community dominated by trees and other woody plants covering a land area of 10,000 square feet or greater. http://county.centreconnect.org/planning/compplan/draft/forest.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Rhode_Island_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Rhode_Island ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dem.ri.gov/pubs/regs/regs/agric/ffosimp.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Rhode Island) - Any tract or contiguous tracts of land, ten (10) acres or larger, exclusive of house site, bearing a dense growth of trees, including underbrush and young regenerating forest and ancillary habitat areas having either the quality of self perpetuation, or being dependent upon its development by the planting and replanting of trees in stands of closely growing timber, actively managed under a stewardship plan approved by the director. http://www.dem.ri.gov/pubs/regs/regs/" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_South_Carolina_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_South_Carolina ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.state.sc.us/forest/lawpro.htm#20" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-South Carolina) From a fire management perspective - Lands shall be construed as \"forest land\" which have enough forest growth, standing or down, or have sufficient inflammable debris or, outside of corporate limits, to constitute, in the judgement of the State Commission of Forestry, a fire menace to itself or adjoining lands. http://www.state.sc.us/forest/lawpro.htm#20" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_South_Dakota_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_South_Dakota ;
    :sourceRef "Greg.Josten@state.sd.us" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-South Dakota) Forest: An ecosystem characterized by a more or less dense and extensive tree cover, often consisting of stands varying in characteristics such as species composition, structure, age class, and associated processes, and commonly including meadows, streams, fish, and wildlife. Forests include special kinds such as industrial forests, nonindustrial private forests, plantations, public forests, protection forests, and urban forests, as well as parks and wilderness. Source -" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Texas_1977_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Texas ;
    dcterms:date "1977"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://capitol.tlc.state.tx.us/cgi-bin/cqcgi?CQ_SESSION_KEY=XMYTLGTJBKOU&CQ_QUERY_HANDLE=123988&CQ_CUR_DOCUMENT=14&CQ_TLO_DOC_TEXT=YES" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Texas 1977) \"Forest\" means the standing trees on forest land. Source: CHAPTER 152. FOREST PEST CONTROL SUBCHAPTER A. GENERAL PROVISIONS http://capitol.tlc.state.tx.us/cgi-bin/cqcgi?CQ_SESSION_KEY=XMYTLGTJBKOU&CQ_QUERY_HANDLE=123988&CQ_CUR_DOCUMENT=14&CQ_TLO_DOC_TEXT=YES, http://www.capitol.state.tx.us/statutes/nr/nr0015200.html and http://www.statutes.legis.state.tx.us/Docs/NR/htm/NR.152.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Texas_1999_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Texas ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "60.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dir.state.tx.us/tgic/pubs/lulc-report.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Texas 1999) Forested – trees with crowns overlapping (generally 60-100% cover) http://www.dir.state.tx.us/tgic/pubs/lulc-report.pdf 1999" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Texas_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Texas ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.capitol.state.tx.us/tlo/74R/billtext/SB00977H.HTM" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Texas) \"Forest\" means a tract of land thick with trees and underbrush. http://www.capitol.state.tx.us/tlo/74R/billtext/SB00977H.HTM and . http://www.statutes.legis.state.tx.us/Docs/NR/htm/NR.152.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Texas_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Texas ;
    :sourceRef "http://capitol.tlc.state.tx.us/cgi-bin/cqcgi?CQ_SESSION_KEY=XMYTLGTJBKOU&CQ_QUERY_HANDLE=123988&CQ_CUR_DOCUMENT=14&CQ_TLO_DOC_TEXT=YES" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Texas) (3) \"Forest land\" means land on which the trees are potentially valuable for timber products, protection of watersheds, wildlife habitat, recreational uses, or for other purposes, but does not include land within the incorporated limits of a village, town, or city. http://capitol.tlc.state.tx.us/cgi-bin/cqcgi?CQ_SESSION_KEY=XMYTLGTJBKOU&CQ_QUERY_HANDLE=123988&CQ_CUR_DOCUMENT=14&CQ_TLO_DOC_TEXT=YES and http://www.statutes.legis.state.tx.us/Docs/NR/htm/NR.152.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Texas_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Texas ;
    :canopyThreshold "100.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.tpwd.state.tx.us/conserve/whap/appendices.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Texas) Deciduous or evergreen trees dominant; mostly greater than 30 feet tall with closed crowns or nearly so (71 to 100 percent canopy cover); midstory generally apparent except in managed monoculture. http://www.tpwd.state.tx.us/conserve/whap/appendices.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Texas_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Texas ;
    :canopyThreshold "60.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "4.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Texas) Trees with crowns overlapping (generally 60-100% cover) (woody veg > 4 m in height) www.tgic.state.tx.us/tgic/documents/plans/lulc-report.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Utah_Tremonton_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Utah_Tremonton ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ulct.org/resources/ordinance_codes/tremonton/tremzong.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Utah-Tremonton) Areas, groves, or stands of mature or largely mature (i.e., greater than six inches caliper) trees covering an area greater than one-quarter acre; or groves of mature trees (greater than 12 inches caliper) consisting of more than 10 individual trees. http://www.ulct.org/resources/ordinance_codes/tremonton/tremzong.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Virgin_Islands_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Virgin_Islands ;
    :canopyThreshold "50.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://rps.uvi.edu/CES/vivegzon.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Virgin Islands) Closed tree canopy (Trees >5 m, canopy cover > 50%) http://rps.uvi.edu/CES/vivegzon.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Virginia_2002_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Virginia ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "60.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.state.va.us/dcr/dnh/ncglossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Virginia 2002?) - Forest – vegetation dominated by trees (= 6m [20 ft] tall) producing a more or less closed canopy, typically with 60-100% cover; some forests may temporarily have < 60% canopy cover following disturbances such as windthrow, disease, etc. http://www.state.va.us/dcr/dnh/ncglossary.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Virginia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Virginia ;
    :sourceRef "James <starrj@dof.state.va.us>" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Virginia) - \"Forest land\" means land on which forest trees are found. Under Authority of Department of Forestry. § 10.1-1178. Definitions. \"Starr, James\" starrj@dof.state.va.us." .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Virginia_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Virginia ;
    :sourceRef "http://gypsymoth.ento.vt.edu/vagm/VDACS_CostShare02.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Virginia) – For Gypsy Moth Spraying - Any spray block proposed for treatment under this program must contain an area that meets the following definition of susceptible forest. A susceptible forest is a wooded area where the trees are 25 feet or more in height and 50% or more of the surface area, when viewed from above, is covered by the tree crowns of moderately or highly susceptible hardwood tree species. Any block that does not contain a forested area as defined will not be accepted" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Washington_1998_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Washington ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "30.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.efsec.wa.gov/oplarchive/DEIS/TOC/glossary.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Washington 1998) Forest (land use category) - Includes public or private forest lands and tree farms, and may be designated for recreational uses. Forested Wetland - Any area of vegetated wetland where woody vegetation over 20 feet tall and dominated by trees (e.g., alder, cedar, hemlock, cottonwood, some willow species) comprises at least 30 percent areal cover. http://www.efsec.wa.gov/oplarchive/DEIS/TOC/glossary.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_West_Virginia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_West_Virginia ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.legis.state.wv.us/scripts/as_web.exe?Command=search&file=total2&request=forest+definition&MaxHits=10&NumLines=1" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-West Virginia) (a) \"Timberland\" means any surface real property except farm woodlots of not less than ten contiguous acres which is primarily in forest and which, in consideration of their size, has sufficient numbers of commercially valuable species of trees to constitute at least forty percent normal stocking of forest trees which are well distributed over the growing site. http://www.legis.state.wv.us/scripts/as_web.exe?Command=search&file=total2&request=forest+definition&MaxHits=1" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Wisconsin_2017_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Wisconsin ;
    dcterms:date "2017"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://docs.legis.wisconsin.gov/statutes/statutes/77/VI/81" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Wisconsin 2017?) “Forestry\" means managing forest lands and their related resources, including trees and other plants, animals, soil, water and air. http://docs.legis.wisconsin.gov/statutes/statutes/77/VI/81" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Wyoming_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Wyoming ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "Howard Pickerd <HPICKE@state.wy.us>" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Wyoming) Forest -We informally use the FS definition of >10% crown cover to define forest vs nonforest. To the best of my knowledge there is no definition either in statute or in any written documents. \"Howard Pickerd\" HPICKE@state.wy.us" .

:def_Forest_Australia_Tasmania_nd_005
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Australia_Tasmania ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.forestrytas.com.au/forestrytas/pdf_files/sustainable_forest_management/sfm_2003/glossary.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia-Tasmania) An area incorporating all living and non-living components, dominated by trees having usually a single stem and a mature (or potentially mature) stand height exceeding 5m, with existing or potential projective foliage cover of overstorey strata, about equal to or greater than 30%. This definition includes native forests and plantations regardless of age, and areas of trees sometimes described as woodlands. http://www.forestrytas.com.au/forestrytas/pdf_files/sustainable_fores" .

:def_Forest_Australia_Victoria_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Australia_Victoria ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dse.vic.gov.au/dse/nrenfor.nsf/FID/-9A9762E4B40E608F4A256AB1000306D0?OpenDocument" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia-Victoria) An area, incorporating all living and non-living components, that is dominated by trees with an existing or potential stand height exceeding 5 metres, and with existing or potential projective foliage cover of overstorey strata at least 30 per cent. This definition includes Australia's diverse native forests and plantations, regardless of age. It is also sufficiently broad to encompass areas of trees that are sometimes described as woodlands. http://www.dse.vic.gov.au/dse/nr" .

:def_Forest_Australia_Victoria_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Australia_Victoria ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dse.vic.gov.au/dse/nrenfor.nsf/FID/-9A9762E4B40E608F4A256AB1000306D0?OpenDocument" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia-Victoria) Woody vegetation with a potential top height greater than five metres and with a crown cover projection greater than 10 percent. http://www.dse.vic.gov.au/dse/nrenfor.nsf/FID/-9A9762E4B40E608F4A256AB1000306D0?OpenDocument" .

:def_Forest_Belgium_Flemmish_Region_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Belgium_Flemmish_Region ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "20.2343"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Belgium-Flemmish Region 1997) - Wooded areas = 50 acres, width = 25 m, cover = 20 % (excepted for clear cutting or forest damages). (European Communities 1997a - p 112)." .

:def_Forest_Canada_BC_nd_006
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_BC ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.swp.bc.ca/myw/html/21_Glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada-BC) - Land having as its highest and best use the growing and harvesting of trees. BC Assessment Authority http://www.swp.bc.ca/myw/html/21_Glossary.htm" .

:def_Forest_Canada_BC_nd_007
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_BC ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.for.gov.bc.ca/tasb/legsregs/forest/foract/part2.htm#4" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada-BC) \"Forest land\" means land classified as forest land under section 4; = Forest land. The chief forester must classify land as forest land if he or she considers that it will provide the greatest contribution to the social and economic welfare of British Columbia if predominantly maintained in successive crops of trees or forage, or both, or maintained as wilderness. http://www.for.gov.bc.ca/tasb/legsregs/forest/foract/part2.htm#4" .

:def_Forest_Canada_BC_nd_008
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_BC ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.assessmentappeal.bc.ca/informationsheets/AACT1098board.asp#defn" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada-BC) \"Forest land\" means land, other than a farm, that (a) is forest reserve land, other than forest reserve land that is not used for the production and harvesting of timber, or (b) although not forest reserve land, has as its highest and best use the production and harvesting of timber; http://www.assessmentappeal.bc.ca/informationsheets/AACT1098board.asp#defn" .

:def_Forest_Canada_BC_nd_009
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_BC ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.for.gov.bc.ca/pab/publctns/glossary/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada-BC) Crown land or private land that is predominantly maintained in one or more successive stands of trees, successive crops of forage, or wilderness. [Source: Glossary of Forestry Terms, Province of British Columbia, Ministry of Forests, http://www.for.gov.bc.ca/pab/publctns/glossary/glossary.htm via Igor A. Yakovlev]" .

:def_Forest_Canada_Manitoba_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_Manitoba ;
    :sourceRef "http://web2.gov.mb.ca/laws/statutes/ccsm/f150e.php" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada-Manitoba) \"Forest land\" means any uncultivated land in the province on which trees or shrubs are growing or standing; any barren, dry marsh, or bog, whether the land is owned by the Crown or by private persons, or held under lease from the Crown; (« forêt ») http://web2.gov.mb.ca/laws/statutes/ccsm/f150e.php" .

:def_Forest_Canada_New_Brunswick_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_New_Brunswick ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.gnb.ca/public/fire-feu/prevent-e.asp" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada-New Brunswick) Forest land means any land outside the boundaries of a city or town and not cultivated for agricultural purposes on which trees, shrubs, plants or grass are growing. http://www.gnb.ca/public/fire-feu/prevent-e.asp" .

:def_Forest_Canada_Nova_Scotia_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_Nova_Scotia ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.gov.ns.ca/just/regulations/regs/for8297.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada-Nova Scotia 2009) \"Forest land\" means land bearing forest growth or land from which the forest has been removed but which shows surface evidence of past forest occupancy and is not now in other use; http://www.gov.ns.ca/just/regulations/regs/for8297.htm,. http://www.gov.ns.ca/just/regulations/regs/fofire.htm and https://nslegislature.ca/sites/default/files/legc/statutes/forests.htm" .

:def_Forest_Canada_Ontario_2003_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_Ontario ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.mnr.gov.on.ca/stdprodconsume/groups/lr/@mnr/@forests/documents/document/mnr_e000254.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada-Ontario 2003). (Silvicultural Management) An area managed for the production of timber and other forest products, or maintained under woody vegetation for such indirect benefits as protection of site or for recreation. http://www.mnr.gov.on.ca/stdprodconsume/groups/lr/@mnr/@forests/documents/document/mnr_e000254.pdf" .

:def_Forest_Canada_Prince_Edward_Island_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_Prince_Edward_Island ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.gov.pe.ca/law/statutes/pdf/f-14.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada-Prince Edward Island) “Forest land” means (i) any land, excluding the cleared land immediately adjacent to an occupied building, on which living or dead trees are the tallest type of vegetation, (ii) any land on which tree seedlings exist or have been planted and are retained for the purposes of producing forest products, or (iii) any land which is being manipulated by tree harvesting, site preparation, tree planting, and or other techniques that promote the establishment of tree seedlin" .

:def_Forest_Canada_Yukon_2017_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_Yukon ;
    dcterms:date "2017"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.emr.gov.yk.ca/forestry/pdf/yukon-forestry-handbook-2017.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada-Yukon 2017) An ecosystem characterized by a more or less dense and continuous tree cover, often consisting of stands varying in composition, structure, age class and associated processes, and commonly including meadows, streams, fish and wildlife. http://www.emr.gov.yk.ca/forestry/pdf/yukon-forestry-handbook-2017.pdf" .

:def_Forest_INDIA_Kerala_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :INDIA_Kerala ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.kerenvis.nic.in/legislation/Microsoft%20Word%20-%20Act2003.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(INDIA-Kerala 2003) “forest” means any land principally covered with naturally grown trees and under growth and includes any forest statutorily recognized and declared as reserved forest, protected forest or otherwise, but does not include any land which is used principally for the cultivation of crops of long duration such as tea, coffee, rubber, pepper, cardamom, coconut, arecanut or cashew or any other sites of residential buildings and surroundings essential for the convenient use of such bu" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_FS_INT_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_FS_INT ;
    :canopyThreshold "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.4047"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-FS-INT) Land that is at least 10 percent stocked by forest trees of any size (or 5 percent crown cover where stocking cannot be determined), or land formerly having such tree cover, and is not currently developed for a nonforest use. The minimum area for classification as forest land is one acre. Roadside, stream-side, and shelterbelt strips of timber must be at least 120 feet wide to qualify as forest land. Unimproved roads and trails or natural clearings in forested areas shall be " .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_FS_NC_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_FS_NC ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-FS-NC) Land not currently developed for nonforest use and having a stocking value of at least 10.0 of all live forest trees of any size or formerly having a stocking value of at least 10.0. Unimproved roads and trails, streams or other bodies of water or clearings in forest areas will be classed as forest if less than 120 feet wide. The minimum area for classification of forest land is one acre and 120 feet in width. Roadside, streamside, and shelterbelt strips of timber must be at l" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_FS_R8_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_FS_R8 ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.4047"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-FS-R8) Land at least 10.0 percent stocked by forest trees of any size, or land formerly having such tree cover, and is not currently developed for non-forest use. The minimum area for classification of forestland is 1 acre. Roadside, streamside, and shelterbelt strips of timber must have a width of at least 120 feet wide to qualify as forestland. Unimproved roads, and trails, streams and other bodies of water, or natural clearings in forested areas shall be classified as forest, if l" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_FS_2004_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_FS ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.cbd.int/doc/world/us/us-nr-vfe-en.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-FS 2004) Land with a specified minimum tree crown cover and generally more than the specified minimum area, including land that formerly had such tree cover and that will be naturally or artificially regenerated. The trees should generally be able to reach a minimum specified tree height at maturity in situ. It may consist either of closed forest formations in which trees of various stories and undergrowth cover a high proportion of the ground, or of open forest formations with a con" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_DA_R8_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_R8 ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.r8web.com/gwj/lrmp/plandocs/glossary.html#definitions" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA–R8) An area managed for the production of timber and other forest products, or maintained under woody vegetation for indirect benefits as protection of a watershed, recreation, or wildlife habitat. http://www.r8web.com/gwj/lrmp/plandocs/glossary.html#definitions" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_EPA_R3_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_EPA_R3 ;
    :heightMin "1.83"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.epa.gov/region3/mtntop/pdf/VIII.Glossary.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-EPA-R3) - Land bearing a stand of trees of any stature, including seedlings, and of species attaining a minimum of 6 feet average height at maturity or land from which such a stand has been removed but on which no other use has been substituted. The term is commonly limited to land not in farms; forests on farms are commonly called woodland or farm forest. http://www.epa.gov/region3/mtntop/pdf/VIII.Glossary.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_FED_EPA_R3_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_EPA_R3 ;
    :canopyThreshold "25.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.epa.gov/region3/mtntop/pdf/VIII.Glossary.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-EPA-R3) - Land with at least 25 percent tree canopy or that has been stocked with at least 10 percent forest trees of any size, including land that formerly had such tree cover and that will be naturally or artificially reforested. http://www.epa.gov/region3/mtntop/pdf/VIII.Glossary.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Alabama_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Alabama ;
    :sourceRef "http://farm.fic.niu.edu/fic/laws/state/al40.html#stat" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Alabama) forest (meaning real property used for the growing and sale of timber and forest products) Source: http://farm.fic.niu.edu/fic/laws/state/al40.html#stat" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Alaska_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Alaska ;
    :sourceRef "http://touchngo.com/lglcntr/akstats/Statutes/Title41/Chapter17/Section950.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Alaska) \"Forest land\" means land stocked or having been stocked with forest trees of any size and not currently developed for nonforest use, regardless of whether presently available or accessible for commercial purposes, and includes any such land under state, municipal, or private ownership; http://touchngo.com/lglcntr/akstats/Statutes/Title41/Chapter17/Section950.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Arkansas_1995_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Arkansas ;
    dcterms:date "1995"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.4047"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "Jim Grant <jim.grant@mail.state.ar.us>" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Arkansas 1995) Forestland - an area at least 1 acre in size that is at least 10 percent stocked with trees, or formerly having such tree cover and not currently developed for nonforest uses. Forest Inventory and Analysis definition - Forest Statistics for Arkansas Counties - 1995 Jim Grant jim.grant@mail.state.ar.us - no official definitions in Arkansas law" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Arkansas_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Arkansas ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.forestry.state.ar.us/bmp/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Arkansas) - Land bearing forest growth, or land from which the forest has been removed, and is in any stage of forest growth, or production, or maintains the potential for forest growth. http://www.forestry.state.ar.us/bmp/glossary.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_California_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_California ;
    :sourceRef "http://ceres.ca.gov/foreststeward/pdf/CFIPguide.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-California) \"Forestland\" means the land: (1) can support 10 percent or more tree cover with trees native to California, including native oaks, (generally but not always this is Site V (Dunning) and better timberland); and (2) is zoned to allow forest resource management. http://ceres.ca.gov/foreststeward/pdf/CFIPguide.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_California_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_California ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.energy.ca.gov/global_climate_change/documents/SB_812_20020909_chapter.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-California) ‘‘Forest’’ means lands that support, or can support,’’ at least 10 percent tree canopy cover and that allow for management of one or more forest resources including timber, fish and wildlife, biodiversity, water quality, recreation, aesthetics and other public benefits. http://www.energy.ca.gov/global_climate_change/documents/SB_812_20020909_chapter.pdf and http://www.arb.ca.gov/bluebook/bb03/HS/42801.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_California_Mendocino_County_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_California_Mendocino_County ;
    :sourceRef "http://mendolafco.org/lafcopp/lafcopandp2002.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-California-Mendocino County) “Forest Land” means lands, which are suited for and are appropriately retained for the growing, harvesting and production of timber and forest and timber-related products. The classification includes lands eligible to be zoned Timberland Production (TPZ), including lands which have the present or future potential for timber production, intermixed smaller parcels and other contiguous lands, the inclusion of which is necessary for the protection and efficien" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Colorado_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Colorado ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.palmerfoundation.org/Legal_CO.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Colorado) \"Forest land\" means land of which at least ten percent is stocked by forest trees of any size and includes land that formerly had such tree cover and that will be naturally or artificially regenerated. \"Forest land\" includes roadside, streamside, and shelterbelt strips of timber which have a crown width of at least one hundred twenty feet. \"Forest land\" includes unimproved roads and trails, streams, and clearings which are less than one hundred twenty feet wide. http://www.p" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Florida_1999_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Florida ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dot.state.fl.us/surveyingandmapping/Manuals/fluccmanual.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Florida 1999) Forests (Upland) - This category of land cover is reserved for those upland areas which support a tree canopy closure of ten (10) percent or more. The Upland Forests include both the xeric (drysite) and mesic (moderately moist site) forest communities. Wetland, or hydric, forest communities fall under the broad wetland category. Also included in the Upland Forest category are areas in which timber harvesting has occurred but which exhibit no evidence of being developed f" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Florida_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Florida ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.myflorida.com/dor/tips/tip98a115.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Florida) ``Forest\" means land stocked by trees of any size used in the production of forest products, or forest land that has been harvested and is not currently developed for nonforest use. http://www.myflorida.com/dor/tips/tip98a115.html and http://election.dos.state.fl.us/laws/98laws/ch_98-294.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Florida_Hernando_Co_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Florida_Hernando_Co ;
    :areaMin "8.0937"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.co.hernando.fl.us/pa/greenbelt.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Florida-Hernando Co.) Timberland - Must be a minimum of 20 acres in size and in planted pines or a predominantly natural stand of pines. A forestry management plan must be implemented and followed and a copy of the plan kept on file with the Property Appraiser's Office. Larger tracts will be reviewed and approved based on the merchantability of the timber and whether or not management has been sufficient. This guideline covers both hard wood and mixed tracts. Christmas tree production" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Hawaii_Kauai_Co_1988_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Hawaii_Kauai_Co ;
    dcterms:date "1988"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.4047"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fs.fed.us/pnw/pubs/rb156.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Hawaii-Kauai Co. 1988) Land at least 10 percent stocked with trees and not now developed for nonforest use; also includes land 50 percent or more covered by shrubs. The minimum area recognized as forest land is 1 acre. This land includes both timberland and other forest land (Buck et al. 1988). http://www.fs.fed.us/pnw/pubs/rb156.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Idaho_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Idaho ;
    :sourceRef "http://www2.state.id.us/tax/propertytax/PTpdfs/revisedforestlanddesign.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Idaho) Forestland means privately owned land being held and used primarily for the continuous purpose of growing and harvesting trees of a marketable species. http://www2.state.id.us/tax/propertytax/PTpdfs/revisedforestlanddesign.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Idaho_1974_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Idaho ;
    dcterms:date "1974"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "https://adminrules.idaho.gov/rules/current/20/0201.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Idaho-1974) Forest Land. Federal, state and private land growing forest tree species which are, or could be at maturity, capable of furnishing raw material used in the manufacture of lumber or other forest products. The term includes federal, state and private land from which forest tree species have been removed but have not yet been restocked. It does not include land affirmatively converted to uses other than the growing of forest tree species https://adminrules.idaho.gov/rules/cur" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Idaho_2005_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Idaho ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www3.state.id.us/oasis/2005/H0126.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Idaho-2005) \"Forest\" means forest land and the timber thereon. \"Forest land\" means privately owned land being held and used primarily for the continuous purpose of growing and harvesting trees of a marketable species. Having met the above criteria, forest land may be further identified by the consideration of any of the following criteria: (a) Forest land is land evidenced by present use and silvicultural treatment. (b) Forest land is land which has a dedicated use that is further evi" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Illinois_1996_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Illinois ;
    dcterms:date "1996"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.legis.state.il.us/ilcs/ch525/ch525act40.htm#Top" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Illinois 1996) State forests shall include only such lands as are decided by the Department of Natural Resources to be more valuable for the growing of forests than for other purposes, and shall have for their purpose the production of forest products, the protection of watersheds that are subject to serious erosion, the maintenance of purity of springs and streams and to afford recreation places for the people of the State. (Source: P.A. 89-445, eff. 2-7-96.) Source: http://www.legis" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Illinois_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Illinois ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.legis.state.il.us/commission/jcar/admincode/017/017015370000010R.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Illinois) \"Forest\" means an area whose principal crop is trees. http://www.legis.state.il.us/commission/jcar/admincode/017/017015370000010R.html and http://dnr.state.il.us/legal/1537.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Illinois_nd_005
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Illinois ;
    :sourceRef "http://dnr.state.il.us/legal/62-1701.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Illinois) \"Forestry\" means land used or managed for the long-term production of wood, wood fiber, or wood-derived products. Allowable support facilities include water impoundments, access and fire control lanes, erosion control structures such as grassed waterways, downdrains, terraces and sediment ponds, and other incidental facilities related to sound multiple use management of the forest resource. http://dnr.state.il.us/legal/62-1701.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Illinois_nd_006
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Illinois ;
    :sourceRef "http://dnr.state.il.us/mines/lrd/guides/citrec7.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Illinois) Land used or managed for the long-term production of wood, wood fiber or wood derived products. Land used for facilities in support of forest harvest and management operations that is adjacent to or an integral part of these operations is also included. http://dnr.state.il.us/mines/lrd/guides/citrec7.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Iowa_1999_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Iowa ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.legis.state.ia.us/IACODE/1999SUPPLEMENT/161A/42.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Iowa 1999) \"Forest\" means stands of native or introduced trees containing at least two hundred trees per acre and located on privately owned land. However, a stand of fruit trees is not a forest. 1999. http://www.legis.state.ia.us/IACODE/1999SUPPLEMENT/161A/42.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Kansas_1971_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Kansas ;
    dcterms:date "1971"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "Atchison <ratchiso@oznet.ksu.edu>" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Kansas 1971) An area managed for the production of timber and other forest produce, or maintained under woody vegetation for such indirect benefits as protection of catchment areas or recreation. \"Terminology of Forest Science, Technology, Practice & Products\" SAF, 1971. Robert L. Atchison ratchiso@oznet.ksu.edu" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Kansas_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Kansas ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.4047"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "Atchison <ratchiso@oznet.ksu.edu>" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Kansas) Forest land - Land at least 10% stocked by forest trees of any size, or formerly having such tree cover, and not currently developed for non-forest use. Stocking is measured by comparing specified standards with basal area and /or number of trees, age or size and spacing. The minimum area classification for forest land is 1 acre. Roadside, streamside, and shelterbelt strips of timber must have a crown width of at least 120 feet to qualify as forest land. \"An Analysis of the Fo" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Kentucky_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Kentucky ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.lrc.state.ky.us/kar/405/030/010.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) Forest land\" means land used or managed for the long-term production of wood, wood fiber, or wood derived products. Land used for facilities in support of forest harvest and management operations which is adjacent to or an integral part of these operations is also included. http://www.lrc.state.ky.us/kar/405/030/010.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Kentucky_nd_005
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Kentucky ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "Steve.Kull@mail.state.ky.us" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) Forestland - land at least 10 percent stocked by forest trees of any size, including land that formerly had such cover and that will be naturally or artificially regenerated. The State of Kentucky does not have the terms Forest, Forestland, or Tree officially defined in State Statute or Regulation. The Division of Forestry utilizes the Society of American Forester's definitions for these terms as listed in John A. Helms' The Dictionary of Forestry. Steve.Kull@mail.state.ky.u" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Maine_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Maine ;
    :sourceRef "http://janus.state.me.us/legis/statutes/17/title17sec3853-D.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Maine) \"Forest land\" means land used for the production of forest products. http://janus.state.me.us/legis/statutes/17/title17sec3853-D.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Maine_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Maine ;
    :sourceRef "http://janus.state.me.us/legis/statutes/36/title36sec573.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Maine) Forest land. \"Forest land\" means land used primarily for growth of trees to be harvested for commercial use, but does not include ledge, marsh, open swamp, bog, water and similar areas, which are unsuitable for growing a forest product or for harvesting for commercial use even though these areas may exist within forest lands. Source: http://janus.state.me.us/legis/statutes/36/title36sec573.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Maine_nd_005
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Maine ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.state.me.us/revenue/propertytax/Bulletins/Tax%20Bulletin%2019.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Maine) Forestland--means land used primarily for growth of trees to be harvested for commercial use; may be either seedling, pole timber, or saw log stands. Forestland does not include ledge, marsh, open swamp, bog, water and similar areas that are unsuitable for growing a forest product or for harvesting for commercial use even though these areas may exist within forestlands. http://www.state.me.us/revenue/propertytax/Bulletins/Tax%20Bulletin%2019.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Maine_nd_006
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Maine ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.google.com/search?q=cache:www.memun.org/municipal_resources/Public_files/TAXDATA/HTML/PropertyTaxBull/html/bulletin19.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Maine) Land used primarily for growth of trees to be harvested for commercial use; may be either seedling, poletimber, or sawlog stands. Land which would otherwise be included in this definition shall not be excluded because of: (1) Multiple use for public recreation; (2) Statutory or governmental restrictions which prevent commercial harvesting of trees or require a primary use of the land other than commercial harvesting; (3) Deed restrictions, restrictive covenants or organizationa" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Maine_Acton_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Maine_Acton ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.actonmaine.com/warrant/2003/warrant.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Maine-Acton 2003) Forest Land means land used primarily to grow trees to be harvested for commercial use, but does not include marsh, open swamp, bog, water and similar areas, which are unsuitable for growing a forest product or for harvesting for commercial use even though these areas may exist within forest lands. http://www.actonmaine.com/warrant/2003/warrant.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Maryland_1974_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Maryland ;
    dcterms:date "1974"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://ia700309.us.archive.org/35/items/landuseclassific209mary/landuseclassific209mary.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Maryland 1974)- These lands are at least 10% stocked with trees capable of producing timber or other wood products, and lands dedicated to forest production but temporarily cleared (i.e. logged). This lands include abandoned fields with woody brush that prevents classification as Agricultural land. http://ia700309.us.archive.org/35/items/landuseclassific209mary/landuseclassific209mary.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Maryland_2007_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Maryland ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "0.4047"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dnr.state.md.us/download/reforest.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA—STATE-Maryland 2007) (i) \"Forest\" means a biological community dominated by trees or other woody plants covering a land area of 1 acre or more.(ii) \"Forest\" includes an area that has been cut but not cleared of trees or other woody plants. Maryland 2007. http://www.dnr.state.md.us/download/reforest.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Maryland_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Maryland ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.mde.state.md.us/assets/document/sedimentStormwater/MDEFHOESManualDraft063005_glossary.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Maryland) - Land bearing forest growth or land from which the forest has been removed but which shows evidence of past forest occupancy and which is not now in other use. http://www.mde.state.md.us/assets/document/sedimentStormwater/MDEFHOESManualDraft063005_glossary.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Maryland_1974_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Maryland ;
    dcterms:date "1974"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://ia700309.us.archive.org/35/items/landuseclassific209mary/landuseclassific209mary.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Maryland-1974) - Forest land are lands that are at least 10 percent stocked with trees capable of producing timber or other wood products that exert an influence on climate or water regime. Lands from which trees have been removed to less than 10 percent stocking but which have not been developed for other use are also included. http://ia700309.us.archive.org/35/items/landuseclassific209mary/landuseclassific209mary.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Maryland_Easton_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Maryland_Easton ;
    :canopyThreshold "50.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.town-eastonmd.com/Planning/fco/fco_a002.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Maryland-Easton) \"Forest\" means a biological community dominated by trees and other woody plants covering a land area of 10,000 square feet or greater. B. \"Forest\" includes: (1) Areas that have at least 100 live trees per acre with at least 50 percent of those trees having a 2-inch or greater diameter at 4.5 feet above the ground and larger; and (2) Areas that have been cut but not cleared. C. \"Forest\" does not include orchards. http://www.town-eastonmd.com/Planning/fco/fco_a002.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Maryland_Rockville_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Maryland_Rockville ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.rockvillemd.gov/e-gov/rec-parks/ForestConservationManual.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Maryland-Rockville 2009) “forest\" means (1) a contiguous biological community dominated by trees and other woody plants covering a land area of five thousand (5,000) square feet or greater. (2) \"Forest\" includes:a. Areas that have at least one hundred (100) live trees per acre with at least fifty (50) percent of those trees having a two-inch or greater diameter at four and one-half (4.5) feet above the ground and larger; and b. Areas that have been cut but not cleared. (3) \"Forest\" do" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Maryland_Rockville_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Maryland_Rockville ;
    :canopyThreshold "50.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ci.rockville.md.us/cityprojects/envguide/eggloss.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Maryland-Rockville) A biological community dominated by trees and other woody plants covering a land area of 10,000 square feet or greater. Forest includes: (1) Areas that have at least 100 trees per acre with at least 50 percent of those trees having a 2-inch or greater dbh. (2) Forest areas that have been cut, but not cleared. Forest does not include orchards. http://www.ci.rockville.md.us/cityprojects/envguide/eggloss.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Massachusetts_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Massachusetts ;
    :canopyThreshold "15.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.state.ma.us/dem/regs/304011c.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Massachusetts) Forest Land means land with at least 15% of the area occupied by the crowns of forest trees of any size that contains at least 7.5 square feet of basal area per acre; or that is a plantation containing at least 500 trees per acre; or land recently harvested that is in the process of regeneration. http://www.state.ma.us/dem/regs/304011c.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Massachusetts_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Massachusetts ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.daviesand.com/Laws/Chapter_61/Ch61_Regs/" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Massachusetts) Forest Lands: (1) To be eligible for classification, land must meet the following criteria: (a) be a parcel of land containing ten or more adjacent or contiguous acres; (b) be at least 16 and 7/8% stocked with forest products and contain at least 7 and 5/10 square feet of basal area per acre by forest trees of any size; or formerly had such tree cover and is not currently developed for nonforest use, or is a plantation containing at least 500 trees per acre; and (c) has" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Massachusetts_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Massachusetts ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.forestmeister.com/laws/ch61.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Massachusetts) Land that is at least sixteen and seven-tenths per cent stocked, that contains at least seven and five-tenths square feet of basal area per acre by forest trees of any size; or that formerly had such tree cover and is not currently developed for non-forest use; or that is a plantation containing at least five hundred trees per acre. [Source Chapter 61 Massachusetts Taxation Law - http://www.forestmeister.com/laws/ch61.html]" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Michigan_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Michigan ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "16.1874"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dnr.state.mi.us/www/law/law_book/statutes/code/part501.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Michigan) \"Forest land\" means a tract of land or the timber rights in that land owned or occupied by a member, which land is at least 10% occupied by forest tree species with a growth potential of 50 cubic feet per acre per year and consists of 40 acres or more. Forest land includes land from which forest tree species have been removed and have not been restocked, but does not include land converted to uses other than the growing of forest tree species or land currently zoned for uses" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Michigan_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Michigan ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.michigan.gov/dnr/0" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Michigan) \"Forest land\" means timbered land, potential timber-producing land, cutover or burned timber land or grass lands not including lands devoted to agriculture. http://www.michigan.gov/dnr/0,1607,7-153-10367_11851-24039--,00.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Michigan_nd_005
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Michigan ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.michiganlegislature.org/law/getObject.asp?objName=324-51101&objType=section&highlight=forest" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Michigan) (d) \" Forest land\" means a tract of land that may include nonproductive land that is intermixed with productive land that is an integral part of a managed forest and that meets all the following: (i) Does not have material natural resources other than those resources suitable for forest growth or the potential for forest growth. (ii) Is not used for agricultural, mineral extraction except as provided in section 51113, grazing, industrial, developed recreational, residential," .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Michigan_2002_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Michigan ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "https://www.legislature.mi.gov/(S(tirvdsukrupau3mkfduqnn55" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Michigan 2002) - “Forest” means a tract of land that is at least 10% stocked by trees of any size, whether of commercial or noncommercial species, or formerly having tree cover and not currently developed for nonforest use, including woodlands, woodlots, windbreaks, and shelter belts https://www.legislature.mi.gov/(S(tirvdsukrupau3mkfduqnn55))/documents/mcl/pdf/mcl-chap320.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_State_Minnesota_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_State_Minnesota ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "https://www.revisor.mn.gov/statutes/?id=88.01" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-State-Minnesota 2009) -\"Forest land\" means land which is at least ten percent stocked by trees of any size and capable of producing timber, or of exerting an influence on the climate or on the water regime; land from which the trees described above have been removed to less than ten percent stocking and which has not been developed for other use; and afforested areas. - https://www.revisor.mn.gov/statutes/?id=88.01" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Minnesota_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Minnesota ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.revisor.leg.state.mn.us/stats/89/51.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Minnesota) Forest land or forest. Forest land or forest, means land on which occurs a stand or potential stand of trees valuable for timber products, watershed or wildlife protection, recreational uses or other purposes, and shall include lands owned or controlled by the state of Minnesota. http://www.revisor.leg.state.mn.us/stats/89/51.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Montana_1996_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Montana ;
    dcterms:date "1996"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :areaMin "6.0703"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://data.opi.mt.gov/bills/1997/Bills/Senate/SB0100_ENR.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Montana 1996) \"Forest\" means forest land and the timber on the land. (5) \"Forest land\" means contiguous land of 15 acres or more in one ownership that is capable of producing timber that can be harvested in commercial quantity and is producing timber unless the trees have been removed by man through harvest, including clearcuts, or by natural disaster, including but not limited to fire. Forest land includes land: (a) that has not been converted to another use. http://data.opi.mt.gov/b" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Montana_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Montana ;
    :areaMin "6.0703"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://data.opi.state.mt.us/bills/mca/15/44/15-44-102.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Montana) \"Forest land\" means contiguous land of 15 acres or more in one ownership that is capable of producing timber that can be harvested in commercial quantity and is producing timber unless the trees have been removed by man through harvest, including clearcuts, or by natural disaster, including but not limited to fire. Forest land includes land: a) that has not been converted to another use; and b) on which the annual net wood production equals or exceeds 25 cubic feet an acre at" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Nevada_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Nevada ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.leg.state.nv.us/NRS/NRS-527.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Nevada) “Forest” or “forest land” means land on which occurs a stand or potential stand of trees valuable for timber products, watershed or wildlife protection, recreational uses or for other purposes. http://www.leg.state.nv.us/NRS/NRS-527.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Nevada_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Nevada ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.state.nv.us/cnr/ndwp/dict-1/WORD_F.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Nevada) Land which is at least 10 percent occupied by forest trees of any size or formerly having had such tree cover and not currently developed for non-forest use. Lands developed for non-forest use include areas for crops, improved pasture, residential, or administrative areas, improved roads of any width, and adjoining road clearing and power line clearing of any width. http://www.state.nv.us/cnr/ndwp/dict-1/WORD_F.htm Water Words Dictionary, http://www.nalms.org/glossary/lkword_f" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_New_York_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_New_York ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dec.state.ny.us/website/regs/199.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-New York) Forest land means land primarily devoted to and suitable for forest crop production under accepted evenaged or unevenaged forest management systems through natural regeneration or through forestation and sufficiently stocked with forest trees to produce a merchantable forest crop within 30 years of time of original certification. Forest land shall consist of a stand or stands of commercial species of forest trees which contain at least either 500 stems per acre or 60 square " .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_North_Carolina_1990_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_North_Carolina ;
    dcterms:date "1990"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "16.7"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-North Carolina 1990) Forestland - Land at least 16.7 percent stocked by forest trees of any size, or formerly having had such tree cover, and not currently developed for nonforest use. Source: Forest Statistics for North Carolina, 1990. Resource Bulletin SE-120, by Tony G. Johnson. USDA-Forest Service, Southeastern Forest" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_North_Carolina_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_North_Carolina ;
    :areaMin "8.0937"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.cals.ncsu.edu/wq/LandPreservationNotebook/statutes/nc/presentusevalue.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-North Carolina) Individually owned forestland consisting of one or more tracts, one of which consists of at least 20 acres that are in actual production and are not included in a farm unit. http://www.cals.ncsu.edu/wq/LandPreservationNotebook/statutes/nc/presentusevalue.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_North_Carolina_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_North_Carolina ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.cals.ncsu.edu/wq/LandPreservationNotebook/statutes/nc/presentusevalue.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-North Carolina) Land that is a part of a forest unit that is actively engaged in the commercial growing of trees under a sound management program. Forestland includes wasteland that is a part of the forest unit, but the wasteland included in the unit shall be appraised under the use-value schedules as wasteland. A forest unit may consist of more than one tract of forestland, but at least one of the tracts must meet the requirements in G.S. 105-277.3(a)(3), and each tract must be under" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_North_Carolina_Counties_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_North_Carolina_Counties ;
    :areaMin "8.0937"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.lincolncounty.org/County/Departments/Tax/LandUseValueQualifications.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-North Carolina-Counties) Forestland means land that is a part of a forest unit that is actively engaged in the commercial growing of trees under a sound management program. Forestland includes wasteland that is a part of the forest unit, but the wasteland included in the unit shall be appraised under the use value schedules as wasteland. The requirements for a forestland deferment are as follows: May consist of more than one tract of forestland, but at least one of the tracts must mee" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Ohio_2001_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Ohio ;
    dcterms:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ohiodnr.com/forestry/rules/pdf/3-10-01.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Ohio 2001) \"Forest land\" means land for which the primary purpose is the growing, managing and harvesting of a merchantable forest product of commercial species under accepted silvicultural systems through natural or artificial reforestation methods and for which there is an approved forest management plan. The forest land shall consist of a stand or stands of commercial species of forest trees which contain at least fifty square feet of basal area or at least three hundred stems per " .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Oklahoma_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Oklahoma ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Oklahoma 2003) Forest means a tract of land that is at least ten percent (10%) stocked by trees of any size, whether of commercial or noncommercial species, or formerly having tree cover and not currently developed for nonforest use, including woodlands, woodlots, windbreaks, and shelterbelts; www.lsb.state.ok.us/2003-04SB/sb606_cs.rtf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Oklahoma_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Oklahoma ;
    :sourceRef "http://oklegal.onenet.net/oklegal-cgi/isearch" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Oklahoma) \"Forests\" means forest land that is at least ten percent (10%) stocked by forest trees of any size, whether of commercial or noncommercial species, or formerly having such tree cover and not currently developed for nonforest use, including woodlands, woodlots, windbreaks and shelterbelts; Source: &sect;2-1301-102. http://oklegal.onenet.net/oklegal-cgi/isearch" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Oregon_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Oregon ;
    :sourceRef "http://arcweb.sos.state.or.us/rules/OARS_600/OAR_629/629_022.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Oregon) \"Forestland\" means land zoned in a county comprehensive plan for forest or farm use that is capable of producing commercial hardwood or softwood timber, regardless of the vegetation currently on the land. http://arcweb.sos.state.or.us/rules/OARS_600/OAR_629/629_022.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Oregon_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Oregon ;
    :areaMin "4.0469"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.savinggraves-us.org/or/laws/308a.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Oregon) “Forestland\" means forestland that is a parcel of land of more than 10 acres that has been zoned in the comprehensive plan for exclusive farm use, forest use or farm and forest use and that is, as of the assessment date for which value for the forest homesite is being determined: (a) Land that has as its highest and best use the growing and harvesting of trees of a marketable species; (b) Land that has been designated as forestland under ORS 321.257 to 321.390 or 321.805 to 32" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Oregon_nd_005
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Oregon ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.leg.state.or.us/ors/321.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Oregon) Any land producing forest products. http://www.leg.state.or.us/ors/321.html and http://www.leg.state.or.us/99reg/measures/sb1100.dir/sb1151.en.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Oregon_nd_006
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Oregon ;
    :sourceRef "http://rredc.nrel.gov/biomass/states/bio_glossary/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Oregon) Any land that is capable of producing or has produced forest growth or, if lacking forest growth, has evidence of a former forest and is not now in other use. http://rredc.nrel.gov/biomass/states/bio_glossary/glossary.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Oregon_nd_007
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Oregon ;
    :sourceRef "http://159.121.125.11/forasst/Library/Pub/UrbanFP.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Oregon) Forestland” means land used for the growing and harvesting of forest tree species, regardless of how the land is zoned, taxed or how any state statutes or local ordinances, rules or regulations are applied. http://159.121.125.11/forasst/Library/Pub/UrbanFP.pdf, http://www.cof.orst.edu/cof/teach/for442/odfdefin.htm and http://arcweb.sos.state.or.us/rules/OARS_600/OAR_629/629_600.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Oregon_nd_008
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Oregon ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://159.121.125.11/rp/Far/crt5ind26.asp#SelectRef" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Oregon) Land at least 10% stocked by forest trees of any size, including land that formerly had such tree cover and that will be regenerated. Strips of forest must have a crown width of 36.58 meters to qualify as forestland. http://159.121.125.11/rp/Far/crt5ind26.asp#SelectRef" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Oregon_nd_009
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Oregon ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.law.utexas.edu/dawson/nuisance/or_nuis.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Oregon) Land that is used for the growing and harvesting of forest tree species. http://www.law.utexas.edu/dawson/nuisance/or_nuis.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Oregon_Klamath_County_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Oregon_Klamath_County ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.co.klamath.or.us/ComDevelopment/Planning/GOAL4.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Oregon-Klamath County) Forest lands are (1) lands composed of existing and potential forest lands suitable for commercial forest uses; (2) other forested lands needed for watershed protection, wildlife and fish habitat, and recreation; (3) lands where extreme conditions of climate, soil and topography require the maintenance of vegetative cover irrespective of use; and (4) other forested lands in urban and agricultural areas that provide urban buffers, wind breaks, wildlife and fish h" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Oregon_Multnomah_Co_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Oregon_Multnomah_Co ;
    :sourceRef "http://www2.co.multnomah.or.us/Community_Services/LUT-Planning/urban/CRGNSAPlan/PartII/NSAMP_PII_C2Forest.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Oregon-Multnomah Co.) - Those lands used or suitable for the production of forest products. http://www2.co.multnomah.or.us/Community_Services/LUT-Planning/urban/CRGNSAPlan/PartII/NSAMP_PII_C2Forest.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Pennsylvania_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Pennsylvania ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.pacode.com/secure/data/025/0088.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Pennsylvania) Land used for the long-term production of wood, wood fiber or wood-derived products; watershed protection or site stabilization and for the production, protection and management of species of fish and wildlife. Land used for facilities in support of forestry and watershed management operations which is adjacent to or an integral part of these operations is also included. http://www.pacode.com/secure/data/025/0088.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Rhode_Island_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Rhode_Island ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.state.ri.us/dem/pubs/regs/regs/forest/altgrant.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Rhode Island) -“Forestland” means any tract or contiguous tracts of land, five (5) acres or more bearing a dense growth of trees, young regenerating forest, and having either the quality of selfperpetuation, or being dependent upon its development by the planting and replanting. http://www.state.ri.us/dem/pubs/regs/regs/forest/altgrant.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Rhode_Island_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Rhode_Island ;
    :sourceRef "http://rredc.nrel.gov/biomass/doe/rbep/ri_wd_waste/one.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Rhode Island) I.2.c. Forestland - In this report, forestland is defined in the same way as \"commercial forestland,\" and is based on the standard definition developed by the USDA Forest Service. According to the Forest Service, \"Commercial forestland is land that is capable of producing more than 20 cubic feet of biomass per acre per year.\" http://rredc.nrel.gov/biomass/doe/rbep/ri_wd_waste/one.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Rhode_Island_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Rhode_Island ;
    :sourceRef "http://farm.fic.niu.edu/fic/laws/state/ri44271.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Rhode Island) The term \"forest land\" means any tract or contiguous tracts of land, ten (10) acres or larger bearing a dense growth of trees, including any underbrush thereon, and having either the quality of self perpetuation, or being dependent upon its development by the planting and replanting of trees in stands of closely growing timber, actively managed under a forest management plan approved by the director of environmental management. http://farm.fic.niu.edu/fic/laws/state/ri44" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_South_Carolina_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_South_Carolina ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t48c029.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-South Carolina 2009) Forest land\" or \"forest\" means land supporting a stand or potential stand of trees valuable for timber products, watershed or wildlife protection, recreational uses, or for other purposes. South Carolina South Carolina Code of Laws (Unannotated) Current through the end of the 2009 Session http://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t48c029.htm and http://www.lpitr.state.sc.us/code/t48c029.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_South_Dakota_1998_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_South_Dakota ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.4"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "Greg.Josten@state.sd.us" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-South Dakota 1998) Forest land: Land at least 10 percent stocked by forest trees of any size, including land that formerly had such tree cover and that will be naturally or artificially regenerated. Forest land includes (a) transition zones, such as areas between forested and nonforested lands that are at least 10 percent stocked with forest trees, and forest areas adjacent to urban and built-up lands, (b) pinion-juniper and chaparral areas. The minimum area for classification of fore" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Tennessee_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Tennessee ;
    :sourceRef "http://farm.fic.niu.edu/fic/laws/state/tn675100.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Tennessee) \"Forest land\" means land constituting a forest unit engaged in the growing of trees under a sound program of sustained yield management or any tract of fifteen (15) or more acres having tree growth in such quantity and quality and so managed as to constitute a forest; Source: http://farm.fic.niu.edu/fic/laws/state/tn675100.html and http://www.padctn.com/greenbelt_law.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Texas_nd_005
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Texas ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.capitol.state.tx.us/statutes/nr/nr0015200.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Texas) \"Forest land\" means land on which the trees are potentially valuable for timber products, protection of watersheds, wildlife habitat, recreational uses, or for other purposes, but does not include land within the incorporated limits of a village, town, or city. http://www.capitol.state.tx.us/statutes/nr/nr0015200.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Texas_nd_006
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Texas ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.tpwd.state.tx.us/texaswater/rivers/riddellcriminaltrespass.phtml" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Texas) Forest land” means land on which the trees are potentially valuable for timber products. http://www.tpwd.state.tx.us/texaswater/rivers/riddellcriminaltrespass.phtml" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Vermont_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Vermont ;
    :canopyThreshold "50.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "10.1172"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://farm.fic.niu.edu/fic/laws/state/vt323751.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Vermont) (9) \"Managed forest land\" means any land, exclusive of any housesite, which is at least 25 acres in size and which is under active forest management for the purpose of growing and harvesting repeated forest crops in accordance with accepted forest management practices. There shall be a presumption that land is under active forest management if at least 50 percent of the land: (A) is certified to be a \"tree farm\" under the American Tree Farm System; (B) has qualified for a fed" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Vermont_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Vermont ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Vermont) Forest land means any land, exclusive of any housesite, which is under active forest management for the purpose of growing and harvesting repeated forest crops. www.leg.state.vt.us/statutes/fullchapter.cfm?Title=24&Chapter=075." .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Virginia_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Virginia ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dof.virginia.gov/edu/glossary.htm#F" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Virginia 1997) Forest Land - Land at least 10 percent stocked by trees of any size or formerly having had such tree cover and not currently built-up or developed for agricultural use. Forestland may include Grassland, Shrubland, Treeland, Wetland, and/or Barren land. Examples of forest land use are grazing, recreation, and timber production. See Forest Land Class for further breakdowns. Virginia Fire Law defines forestland as 80 woody stems per acre http://www.dof.virginia.gov/edu/glo" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Virginia_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Virginia ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.4047"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dof.virginia.gov/gis/dwnld-vaforest2000-faq.shtml" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Virginia 2000) Forestland is defined as lands with at least a stocking of 10% cover of live forest trees of any size, or formerly having such tree cover, and not currently developed for non-forest use. The minimum area for classification of forestland is usually 1 acre with a minimum width of 120 feet stem-to-stem. Forested strips must be at least 120 feet wide for a continuous length of at least 363 feet in order to meet the acre threshold. Unimproved roads and trails, and clearings " .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Virginia_Ablemarle_County_2010_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Virginia_Ablemarle_County ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.albemarle.org/department.asp?department=finance&relpage=3309" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Virginia-Ablemarle County 2010) - Land used for forestal use must be a minimum of twenty acres and must include standing timber and trees devoted to tree growth in such quantity and so spaced and maintained as to constitute a forest area. Requires a minimum of 20 or more contiguous unimproved acres exclusively devoted to forestal use with no livestock access. Forestal acreage with livestock access must be qualified under the agricultural use category. Forestal participants are require" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Virginia_Loudoun_Coounty_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Virginia_Loudoun_Coounty ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.co.loudoun.va.us/finserv/landuse2.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Virginia-Loudoun Coounty) To qualify for this category, the property must be a minimum of twenty acres and must meet the standards for productive forestland or nonproductive forestland. http://www.co.loudoun.va.us/finserv/landuse2.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Washington_1996_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Washington ;
    dcterms:date "1996"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.gmaboards.wa.gov/eastern/ew_decisions/ew1996/96-1-0017" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Washington 1996) Land primarily devoted to growing trees for long-term commercial timber production on land that can be economically and practically managed for such production, including Christmas trees subject to the excise tax imposed under RCW 84.33.100 through 84.33.140, and that has long-term commercial significance. In determining whether forest land is primarily devoted to growing trees for long-term commercial timber production on land that can be economically and practically" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Washington_1996_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Washington ;
    dcterms:date "1996"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.gmaboards.wa.gov/eastern/ew_decisions/ew1996/96-1-0017" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Washington 1996) Land primarily useful for growing trees, including Christmas trees subject to the excise tax imposed under RCW 84.33.100 through 84.33.140, for commercial purposes, and that has long-term commercial significance for growing trees commercially. The Growth Management Act RCW 36.70A.30(8). http://www.gmaboards.wa.gov/eastern/ew_decisions/ew1996/96-1-0017,ellensburg,orderoncomplianceandinvalidity.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Washington_2001_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Washington ;
    dcterms:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.leg.wa.gov/sl/2001-02/5497-s_sl.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Washington 2001) “Forest land\" means all land which is capable of supporting a merchantable stand of timber and is not being actively used for a use which is incompatible with timber growing. Forest land does not include agricultural land that is or was enrolled in the conservation reserve enhancement program by contract if such agricultural land was historically used for agricultural purposes and the landowner intends to continue to use the land for agricultural purposes in the futur" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Washington_2010_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Washington ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://app.leg.wa.gov/rcw/default.aspx?cite=76.09.020" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Washington 2010)\"Forestland\" means all land which is capable of supporting a merchantable stand of timber and is not being actively used for a use which is incompatible with timber growing. Forestland does not include agricultural land that is or was enrolled in the conservation reserve enhancement program by contract if such agricultural land was historically used for agricultural purposes and the landowner intends to continue to use the land for agricultural purposes in the future. " .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Washington_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Washington ;
    :sourceRef "http://farm.fic.niu.edu/fic/laws/state/wa8434.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Washington) (3) \"Timber land\" means any parcel of land that is five or more acres or multiple parcels of land that are contiguous and total five or more acres which is or are devoted primarily to the growth and harvest of forest crops for commercial purposes. Wash. Rev. Code secs. 84.34.010 to - .922 http://farm.fic.niu.edu/fic/laws/state/wa8434.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Washington_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Washington ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.sanjuancounty.org/assessor/dfl.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Washington) State Tax Assessment- Any parcel of land twenty or more acres in size or multiple parcels of land that are contiguous and total twenty acres or more in size that is primarily used for the growth and harvesting of timber. http://www.sanjuancounty.org/assessor/dfl.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Washington_Bainbridge_Island_2004_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Washington_Bainbridge_Island ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ci.bainbridge-isl.wa.us/documents/CompPlan2004_Glossary.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Washington-Bainbridge Island 2004) Land used for growing trees, not including Christmas trees, for commercial purposes (as shown by record of income) that has long-term commercial significance; or unharvested forest land preserved in open space for the environmental benefits and maintenance of rural character. http://www.ci.bainbridge-isl.wa.us/documents/CompPlan2004_Glossary.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Washington_San_Juan_County_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Washington_San_Juan_County ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.co.san-juan.wa.us/assessor/current.aspx" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Washington-San Juan County) - Timber Land means any parcel of land that is five or more acres or multiple parcels of land that are contiguous and total five or more acres which is or are devoted primarily to the growth and harvest of forest crops for commercial purposes. http://www.co.san-juan.wa.us/assessor/current.aspx" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Washington_San_Juan_County_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Washington_San_Juan_County ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.co.san-juan.wa.us/assessor/default.asp?page=dfl" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Washington-San Juan County) Land designated as ‘forest land’ means any parcel of land twenty or more acres in size or multiple parcels of land that are contiguous and total twenty acres or more in size that is primarily used for the growth and harvesting of timber. Forest land refers only to the land. http://www.co.san-juan.wa.us/assessor/default.asp?page=dfl" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Washington_Stevens_County_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Washington_Stevens_County ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.co.stevens.wa.us/assessor/Current%20Land%20Use/PDF%20docs/continuance.PDF" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Washington-Stevens County) Forestland means all land in contiguous ownership of 20 or more acres; which is primarily devoted to and used for growing and harvesting timber. http://www.co.stevens.wa.us/assessor/Current%20Land%20Use/PDF%20docs/continuance.PDF" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Wisconsin_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Wisconsin ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.wra.org/pdf/government/landuse/Proposal_Shoreland_Changes2003.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Wisconsin 2003) \"Forest Land\" means any area on which trees exist, standing or fallen, alive or dead, that are primarily grown because they are valuable for forest products, watershed or wildlife protection or non-residential recreational uses in contrast to areas where shade or ornamental trees are grown primarily because they are valuable for landscape, aesthetic, agricultural or similar purposes. http://www.wra.org/pdf/government/landuse/Proposal_Shoreland_Changes2003.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Wyoming_2002_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Wyoming ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.osmre.gov/stateregs/wyregschap1.txt" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Wyoming 2002) Forestry means land used or managed for the long-term production of wood, wood fiber, or wood-derived products. http://www.osmre.gov/stateregs/wyregschap1.txt (2002)" .

:def_Forest_INDONESIA_Papua_2002_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :INDONESIA_Papua ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://74.125.93.132/search?q=cache:bwzUkrDvEFsJ:www.papuaweb.org/dlib/lap/sullivan/perdasi-perdasus/forestry.rtf+%22forest+means%22&cd=215&hl=en&ct=clnk&gl=us&client=safari" ;
    :definitionText "(INDONESIA-Papua-2002) Forest means a unit of ecosystem in the form of lands comprising biological resources, dominated by trees in their natural forms and environment, which can not be separated each other. http://74.125.93.132/search?q=cache:bwzUkrDvEFsJ:www.papuaweb.org/dlib/lap/sullivan/perdasi-perdasus/forestry.rtf+%22forest+means%22&cd=215&hl=en&ct=clnk&gl=us&client=safari" .

:def_Forest_Russia_Khabarovsk_Krai_1999_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :Russia_Khabarovsk_Krai ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://wenku.baidu.com/view/d74f09d349649b6648d747c8.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Russia Khabarovsk Krai 1999) Forest is defined as the totality of forest vegetation, land, wildlife, and other components’ of the environment having important ecological, economic and social significance. http://wenku.baidu.com/view/d74f09d349649b6648d747c8.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_California_2002_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_California ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.climatechange.ca.gov/publications/legislation/SB_812.PDF" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-California 2002) ‘‘Forest’’ means lands that support, or can support,’’ at least 10 percent tree canopy cover and that allow for management of one or more forest resources including timber, fish and wildlife, biodiversity, water quality, recreation, aesthetics and other public benefits. http://www.climatechange.ca.gov/publications/legislation/SB_812.PDF" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_California_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_California ;
    :sourceRef "http://caselaw.lp.findlaw.com/cacodes/prc/4789-4789.7.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-California) \"Forest land\" means timberland defined pursuant to subdivision (g), and other lands that have been withdrawn from timber production, such as units of the state park system, national parks, and wilderness areas. http://caselaw.lp.findlaw.com/cacodes/prc/4789-4789.7.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Georgia_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Georgia ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.legis.state.ga.us/legis/2003_04/fulltext/sb356.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Georgia 2003) - 'Forest' means lands that support, or can support, at least 10 percent tree canopy cover and that allow for management of one or more forest resources including but not limited to timber, fish and wildlife, biodiversity, water quality, air quality, soil conservation, recreation, aesthetics, or other benefits. http://www.legis.state.ga.us/legis/2003_04/fulltext/sb356.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Idaho_1974_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Idaho ;
    dcterms:date "1974"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "https://adminrules.idaho.gov/rules/current/20/0201.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Idaho 1974) Noncommercial Forest Land. Habitat types not capable of producing twenty (20) cubic feet per acre per year. https://adminrules.idaho.gov/rules/current/20/0201.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Indiana_1999_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Indiana ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.state.in.us/legislative/ic/1999/title6/ar1.1/ch6.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Indiana 1999) Sec. 1. For the purpose of property taxation, forest land may be classified and assessed under this chapter if the land satisfies the conditions prescribed in this chapter for classification as native forest land or a forest plantation. (Formerly: Acts 1975, P.L.47, SEC.1.) IC 6-1.1-6-2 Sec. 2. Land may be classified as a forest plantation if it is cleared land which has growing on it a good stand of timber producing trees as that concept is understood by competent fores" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Minnesota_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Minnesota ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.revisor.leg.state.mn.us:81/SEARCH/BASIS/mnstat/public/www/DDW?W%3DTEXT+PH+IS+%27forest+means%27+ORDER+BY+SORT_KEY/Ascend%26M%3D1%26K%3D88.01%26R%3DY%26U%3D20%26PCU%3D1" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Minnesota) \"Forest land\" means land which is at least ten percent stocked by trees of any size and capable of producing timber, or of exerting an influence on the climate or on the water regime; land from which the trees described above have been removed to less than ten percent stocking and which has not been developed for other use; and afforested areas. Source: Section: 88.01 continued... http://www.revisor.leg.state.mn.us:81/SEARCH/BASIS/mnstat/public/www/DDW?W%3DTEXT+PH+IS+%27for" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Mississippi_2008_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Mississippi ;
    dcterms:date "2008"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://msucares.com/pubs/publications/p1250.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Mississippi 2008) Forestland -- Land which is currently producing (or, in some cases, capable of producing) a forest. http://msucares.com/pubs/publications/p1250.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Montana_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Montana ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dnrc.state.mt.us/forestry/classifi.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Montana) \"Forest land\" means land that has enough timber, standing or down, slash, or brush to constitute in the judgment of the department a fire menace to life or property. Grassland and agricultural areas are included when those areas are intermingled with or contiguous to and no further than one-half mile from areas of forest land. http://www.dnrc.state.mt.us/forestry/classifi.htm and http://www.discoveringmontana.com/racicot/eo/21-22-23Background.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Nebraska_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Nebraska ;
    :sourceRef "ghergenr@unlnotes.unl.edu" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Nebraska) Nebraska accepts the definitions of forestland, forest, etc. as defined in the U.S. Forest Service's Forest Inventory and Analysis program. ghergenr@unlnotes.unl.edu." .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_New_Hampshire_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_New_Hampshire ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.gencourt.state.nh.us/rsa/html/XIX-A/227-G/227-G-2.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-New Hampshire) \"Forestland'' means all lands in this state, except those owned and managed by the United States of America, which by reason of their location and character of soil have the capacity to grow trees and the continuance of which under forest cover is of substantial importance to the public interest. http://www.gencourt.state.nh.us/rsa/html/XIX-A/227-G/227-G-2.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_New_Jersey_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_New_Jersey ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.judiciary.state.nj.us/criminal/charges/arson2.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-New Jersey) A \"forest\" means and includes any forest, brush land, grass land, salt marsh, wooded area and any combination thereof, including but not limited to, an open space area, public lands, wetlands, park lands, natural habitats, a State conservation area, a wildlife refuge area or any other designated undeveloped open space whether or not it is subject to specific protection under law. http://www.judiciary.state.nj.us/criminal/charges/arson2.htm" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_New_York_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_New_York ;
    :sourceRef "http://assembly.state.ny.us/cgi-bin/claws?law=37&art=12" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-New York) \"Forest land\" includes not only lands which may be covered with tree growth but also lands which are best adapted to forests. http://assembly.state.ny.us/cgi-bin/claws?law=37&art=12" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_North_Dakota_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_North_Dakota ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.legis.nd.gov/cencode/t57c57.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-North Dakota) \"Forest\" means an area of land normally supporting a growth of planted tree cover, woodlands, or windbreaks. http://www.legis.nd.gov/cencode/t57c57.pdf" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Oregon_nd_010
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Oregon ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.leg.state.or.us/ors/526.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Oregon) \"Forestland\" means any woodland, brushland, timberland, grazing land or clearing, which, during any time of the year, contains enough forest growth, slashing or vegetation to constitute, in the opinion of the forester, a fire hazard, regardless of how the land is zoned or taxed. Source: 526.005 Definitions http://www.leg.state.or.us/ors/526.html" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Oregon_Yamhill_County_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Oregon_Yamhill_County ;
    :canopyThreshold "100.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.co.yamhill.or.us/assessor/bin/forest.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Oregon-Yamhill County) Forest land is land which either is being held or used predominantly to grow and harvest trees of a; marketable species and has been designated as forest land or is land the highest and best use of which is to grow and harvest such trees. A. Land may qualify if the designated area is at least two contiguous acres of bare land or two contiguous acres plus one homesite of improved land in one ownership. B. The land must meet one of the following stocking requireme" .

:def_Forest_USA_STATE_Pennsylvania_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Forest ;
    :hasCategory :Ecological ;
    :hasJurisdictionLevel :Local ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Pennsylvania ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dcnr.state.pa.us/forestry/sfrmp/overview.htm#sustainability" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Pennsylvania) Forests are defined as ecosystems dominated by trees, but with other components such as shrubs, herbs, mammals, birds, insects, microscopic creatures, soil, air, water, and the interactive processes that bind them together. http://www.dcnr.state.pa.us/forestry/sfrmp/overview.htm#sustainability" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.bartleby.com/61/52/T0335200.html" ;
    :definitionText "Etymology: Middle English, from Old English treow. dreu-. To be firm, solid, steadfast; hence specialized senses “wood,” “tree,” and derivatives referring to objects made of wood. http://www.bartleby.com/61/52/T0335200.html and http://www.bartleby.com/61/roots/IE87.html\\" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://europa.eu.int/comm/dg08/forests/en/en4_6.htm" ;
    :definitionText "As indicated above, many definitions of \"forest\" included the term \"tree.\" Therefore, we also need to understand what is considered a \"tree.\" Many of the above forest definitions included definitions of \"tree.\" Several have built-in height thresholds varying from 2-15 m. (For reference, shrubs may be considered - a vegetation type where the dominant woody elements are shrubs which grow to a height of more than 50 cm and less than 5 metres on maturity. The height limits for trees and shrubs shoul" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :definitionText "As of 12 April 2018, there are nearly 250 definitons of trees listed below." .

:def_Tree_Antigua_and_Barbuda_1941_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Antigua_and_Barbuda ;
    dcterms:date "1941"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "Diann <laynec@candw.ag>" ;
    :definitionText "(Antigua and Barbuda 1941) - Timber - Any kind of growing tree except brushwood or trees growing on cultivated lands or on cleared lands or pasture lands on any estate. Forestry Act. 1941. Craig and Diann laynec@candw.ag ." .

:def_Tree_Argentina_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Argentina ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Argentina 2009) Tree, mature native. - An autochthonous weedy species, with a central stem, whcih ramifies from above ground level. Includes palm trees. Presidential Regulation Order (Presidencia de la Nación Argentina 2009)" .

:def_Tree_Argentina_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Argentina ;
    :sourceRef "Mirta Rosa Larrieu <milarr@sagyp.mecon.ar>" ;
    :definitionText "(Argentina) Woody plant with a defined stem and canopy clearly formed with secondary growth and lignificated tissues. \"Mirta Rosa Larrieu\"milarr@sagyp.mecon.ar" .

:def_Tree_Australia_Tasmania_1985_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Australia_Tasmania ;
    dcterms:date "1985"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fpa.tas.gov.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0019/58114/A_guide_to_planning_approvals_for_forestry_in_Tasmania_Nov_2011.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia Tasmania 1985) A tree is any living or dead woody plant and includes seedlings and regrowth. http://www.fpa.tas.gov.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0019/58114/A_guide_to_planning_approvals_for_forestry_in_Tasmania_Nov_2011.pdf" .

:def_Tree_Australia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Australia ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://155.187.10.12/glossary/fl-aust.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia) A woody plant at least 5 metres high, with a main axis the lower part of which is usually unbranched - http://155.187.10.12/glossary/fl-aust.html" .

:def_Tree_Australia_NSW_Penrith_City_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Australia_NSW_Penrith_City ;
    :heightMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Australia–NSW – Penrith City) A perennial plant with a self-supporting stem which: (a) has a girth of 30cm or more, measured at a distance of 40cm above ground; and (b) has a height in excess of 3m. www.penrithcity.nsw.gov.au/PCC/tree.htm" .

:def_Tree_Australia_NSW_1938_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Australia_NSW ;
    dcterms:date "1938"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.forest.nsw.gov.au/education/glossary/default.asp#Ltr_W" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia-NSW 1938) - A perennial plant having a self-supporting woody stem or trunk which usually develops woody branches (under the Soil Conservation Act, 1938 a tree includes sapling, shrub or scrub). http://www.forest.nsw.gov.au/education/glossary/default.asp#Ltr_W" .

:def_Tree_Australia_NSW_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Australia_NSW ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://155.187.10.12/glossary/fl-nsw.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia-NSW) - A woody plant usually with a single distinct trunk and generally more than 5 m high. http://155.187.10.12/glossary/fl-nsw.html" .

:def_Tree_Australia_Queensland_1959_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Australia_Queensland ;
    dcterms:date "1959"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "https://www.legislation.qld.gov.au/view/whole/html/inforce/2016-07-01/act-1959-058" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia–Queensland 1959) trees includes not only timber trees, but all other trees, and shrubs, bushes, seedlings, saplings, and re-shoots of every description and any parts thereof. https://www.legislation.qld.gov.au/view/whole/html/inforce/2016-07-01/act-1959-058" .

:def_Tree_Australia_Victoria_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Australia_Victoria ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dse.vic.gov.au/dse/nrenfor.nsf/FID/-9A9762E4B40E608F4A256AB1000306D0?OpenDocument" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia-Victoria) Includes trees, shrubs, bushes, seedlings, saplings and reshoots whether alive or dead of any genus, species or variety usually growing in a forest and includes every part of such tree. http://www.dse.vic.gov.au/dse/nrenfor.nsf/FID/-9A9762E4B40E608F4A256AB1000306D0?OpenDocument" .

:def_Tree_Australia_Victoria_1958_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Australia_Victoria ;
    dcterms:date "1958"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www8.austlii.edu.au/cgi-bin/viewdoc/au/legis/vic/consol_act/fa1958116/s3.html#state_forest" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia–Victoria 1958)  \"tree\" or trees includes trees shrubs bushes seedlings saplings and reshoots whether alive or dead; http://www8.austlii.edu.au/cgi-bin/viewdoc/au/legis/vic/consol_act/fa1958116/s3.html#state_forest" .

:def_Tree_Bahamas_2010_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Bahamas ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.bahamasforestry.com/docs/ForestryAct2010.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Bahamas 2010) Trees includes any perennial plant with a self supporting stem, shrubs, bushes, palms, stumps, seedlings, saplings and coppice shoots the species of which may reach a height of ten feet or more. Bahamas Forestry Act of 2010. http://www.bahamasforestry.com/docs/ForestryAct2010.pdf" .

:def_Tree_Bangladesh_1927_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Bangladesh ;
    dcterms:date "1927"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Bangladesh 1927) Tree includes palms, bamboos, stumps, brush-wood and canes. LEX-FAOC006895. BANGLADESH: Forest Act, 1927. Date of text: 1927." .

:def_Tree_Barbados_1981_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Barbados ;
    dcterms:date "1981"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Barbados 1981) Applies to any tree the circumference of which is one metre or more at a point half a metre or more from the ground but does not apply to a tree the killing of which if for the prevention of imminent danger or is in compliance with an obligation under any other enactment. LEX-FAOC002736. BARBADOS: Trees (Preservation) Act, 1981 (Act No. 49). Date of text: 07 December 1981." .

:def_Tree_Belize_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Belize ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.belizeaudubon.org/new_site/wp-content/uploads/2014/10/Forest_Act_213.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Belize 2000) “trees” includes shrubs, bushes, palms, bamboos, creepers, canes, stumps, seedlings, saplings and coppice shoots; http://www.belizeaudubon.org/new_site/wp-content/uploads/2014/10/Forest_Act_213.pdf" .

:def_Tree_Belgium_Wallonie_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Belgium_Wallonie ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://mrw.wallonie.be/cgi/dgrne/sibw/eunis.glo.pl?WORD=tree" ;
    :definitionText "(Belgium-Wallonie) A woody plant with a single main stem (the trunk), that is unbranched near the ground; some trees (e.g. oak, ([Quercus]) and ash ([Fraxinus])) have multi-trunked forms. At the end of each growing season there is no die-back of aerial parts, apart from the loss of foliage. Trees which are able to reach a height of 5m at maturity. http://mrw.wallonie.be/cgi/dgrne/sibw/eunis.glo.pl?WORD=tree" .

:def_Tree_Bhutan_1969_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Bhutan ;
    dcterms:date "1969"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://extwprlegs1.fao.org/docs/pdf/bhu2744.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Bhutan 1969) Tree include palms, bamboos, stumps, brushwood and canes. http://extwprlegs1.fao.org/docs/pdf/bhu2744.pdf" .

:def_Tree_Belize_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Belize ;
    :definitionText "(Belize) Includes shrubs, bushes, palms, bamboos, creepers, canes, stumps, seedlings, saplings and coppice shoots. [LEX-FAOC002737] BELIZE: Forests Ordinance (Chapter 176)." .

:def_Tree_Bolivia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Bolivia ;
    :sourceRef "Luis Castello <faopaf@caoba.entelnet.bo>" ;
    :definitionText "(Bolivia) ÁRBOL: Planta perenne de tronco leñoso y elevado que se ramifica a cierta altura del suelo; constituye un elemento de bosque, pero en forma individual tiene una existencia limitada. Source: Luis Castello faopaf@caoba.entelnet.bo Adjunto sírvase encontrar la versión no oficial y premilinar del Glosario Forestal elaborado por el Proyecto de Apoyo a la Coordinación e Implementación del Plan de Acción Forestal para Bolivia" .

:def_Tree_Botswana_1968_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Botswana ;
    dcterms:date "1968"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.mewt.gov.bw/uploads/files/forest_act.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Botswana 1968) Includes palms, shrubs, bushes, climbers, seedlings, saplings and regrowth of all ages and of all kinds, and any part thereof. [LEX-FAOC002748] BOTSWANA: Forest Act. Date of consolidation/reprint: 1976. Date of original text: 10 March 1968. http://www.mewt.gov.bw/uploads/files/forest_act.pdf" .

:def_Tree_Bulgaria_1988_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Bulgaria ;
    dcterms:date "1988"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "Forest Research Institute <forestin@bulnet.bg>" ;
    :definitionText "(Bulgaria 1988) Tree - species with long-living stems, from 3-5 m up to 150 m high (Delkov, N., 1988, Dendrology). Forest Research Institute <forestin@bulnet.bg>" .

:def_Tree_Canada_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Canada ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.pfc.cfs.nrcan.gc.ca/landscape/inventory/terms/haddon/glossary.html#T" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada) [arbre] A woody, perennial plant generally with a single, well-defined stem and a more or less definitely formed crown. Source: \"Forest Inventory Terms in Canada.\" From: \"Haddon, Brian\" <BHaddon@nrcan.gc.ca and http://www.pfc.cfs.nrcan.gc.ca/landscape/inventory/terms/haddon/glossary.html#T" .

:def_Tree_Canada_Alberta_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_Alberta ;
    :heightMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.agric.gov.ab.ca/agdex/100/3400600.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada-Alberta) - Woody, single-stemmed perennial plants which reach a mature height of at least 3 m. http://www.agric.gov.ab.ca/agdex/100/3400600.html" .

:def_Tree_Canada_British_Columbia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_British_Columbia ;
    :definitionText "(Canada-British Columbia) - Any living, erect, woody plant which is: 5 metres (16.3 feet) or more in height; or 10 centimetres (3.9 inches) or more in diameter measured 1.5 metres above the ground. www.civicinfo.bc.ca/Local_Content/legal-information/622.doc" .

:def_Tree_Canada_Calgary_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_Calgary ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.calgary.ca/docgallery/BU/cityclerks/23M2002.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada-Calgary) Any perennial woody plant that normally has one or few upright stems and is maintained as a tree and includes plants designated as trees by the General Manager, Parks; http://www.calgary.ca/docgallery/BU/cityclerks/23M2002.pdf" .

:def_Tree_Canada_Ontario_Guelph_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_Ontario_Guelph ;
    :heightMin "4.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.city.guelph.on.ca/uploaddocuments/d2169+Tree.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada-Ontario-Guelph) “Tree” means and includes any Deciduous or Coniferous growing tree that has a minimum height of 4.5 metres (15 feet) and a minimum diameter or 75 millimetres (3 inches) at a point one metre above ground level. http://www.city.guelph.on.ca/uploaddocuments/d2169+Tree.pdf" .

:def_Tree_Canada_Ontario_Halton_and_York_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_Ontario_Halton_and_York ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.region.halton.on.ca/PPW/archives/by-79-83.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada-Ontario-Halton and York) Any species of woody plant which has reached or can reach an average height of at least 5 metres (15 feet) at physiological maturity. http://www.region.halton.on.ca/PPW/archives/by-79-83.pdf and http://www.region.york.on.ca/Services/Forestry/Tree+By-Law/default+tree+by+law.htm" .

:def_Tree_Canada_Ontario_Simcoe_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_Ontario_Simcoe ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.county.simcoe.on.ca/services/forestry/bylaw.shtml" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada-Ontario-Simcoe) Any species of woody plant which has reached or can reach an average height of at least 5 metres (15 feet) at physiological maturity; http://www.county.simcoe.on.ca/services/forestry/bylaw.shtml" .

:def_Tree_Canada_Ontario_Stratford_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_Ontario_Stratford ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.city.stratford.on.ca/documents/bylaws/by_law_5_2003.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada-Ontario-Stratford 2003) Any shade or ornamental tree, all or part of which is located on, above or below a public highway. http://www.city.stratford.on.ca/documents/bylaws/by_law_5_2003.pdf" .

:def_Tree_Cape_Verde_1998_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Cape_Verde ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Cape Verde 1998) Árvore - As árvores, os arbustos e as formações herbáceas, com excepção das cultivadas ou destinadas a fins agrícolas; LEX-FAOC013213. CAPE VERDE: Forestry Act (No. 48/V/98)." .

:def_Tree_Chile_2008_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Chile ;
    dcterms:date "2008"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.conaf.cl/cms/editorweb/transparencia/potestades/Ley-20283_bn.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Chile 2008) Árbol: planta de fuste generalmente leñoso, que en su estado adulto y en condiciones normales de hábitat puede alcanzar, a lo menos, cinco metros de altura, o una menor en condiciones ambientales que limiten su desarrollo. Tree: usually woody stem plant, which in its adult stage and normal habitat can reach, at least, five meters high, or minor in environmental conditions that limit their development. http://www.conaf.cl/cms/editorweb/transparencia/potestades/Ley-20283_bn.pdf" .

:def_Tree_Costa_Rica_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Costa_Rica ;
    :definitionText "(Costa Rica) - Planta perenne de tronco leñoso y elevado que se ramifica a mayor o menor altura del suelo, que es fuente de materia prima que origina industrias como aserraderos, fabricas de tableros, de chapa, de fósforos, de celulosa, de aceites esenciales, de resinas y taninos\"(Reglamento a la Ley Forestal 7575)." .

:def_Tree_Cuba_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Cuba ;
    :sourceRef "Nelida Puentes Alvarez <npuentes@eco.upr.edu.cu>" ;
    :definitionText "(Cuba) Arbol: Planta de fuste generalmente leñoso, con la presencia de un solo tallo dominante en la base, que en su estado adulto y en condiciones normales de hábitat puede alcanzar, no menos de 5 metros de altura, o una menor en condiciones ambientales negativas que limiten su desarrollo. \"Nelida Puentes Alvarez\" npuentes@eco.upr.edu.cu" .

:def_Tree_Cyprus_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Cyprus ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "Publicity Sector <publicity@cytanet.com.cy>" ;
    :definitionText "(Cyprus)- A woody perennial plant, typically large and with a well-defined stem carrying a more or less definite crown and with a minimum height of 5 m. A.K. Christou \"Forestry Department - Research and Publicity Sector\" publicity@cytanet.com.cy" .

:def_Tree_Estonia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Estonia ;
    :sourceRef "Sulev Svilponis <Sulev@ekm.envir.ee>" ;
    :definitionText "(Estonia) [puud] - Long-lived higher plants with lignified stem. Estonian Encyclopedia From: \"Sulev Svilponis\" Sulev@ekm.envir.ee. Definitions are unofficial translations." .

:def_Tree_Ethiopia_1994_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Ethiopia ;
    dcterms:date "1994"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://cdm.unfccc.int/filestorage/L/4/Q/L4QB30W8C5RYZMT6UKOFX1PV9GNIHS/Annex%205%20Legal%20aspects.pdf?t=OXR8bHpqZnlvfDByMiF2MIecUaf9gjv8IjJT" ;
    :definitionText "(Ethiopia 1994) Trees. are defined as ..any woody plant regardless of its, species, age, size including bamboo, reeds and palms as well as other plants to be designated as .trees by the Ministry. (Art.2.4). The definition given to .forest. and .trees. in the SNNPRS Forestry Proclamation is similar to that given in the Federal Proclamation (Arts.2.3 and 2.8 of Proclamation No.77/2004). http://cdm.unfccc.int/filestorage/L/4/Q/L4QB30W8C5RYZMT6UKOFX1PV9GNIHS/Annex%205%20Legal%20aspects.pdf?t=OXR8bHp" .

:def_Tree_Ethiopia_2007_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Ethiopia ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.pfmp-farmsos.org/Docs/forest%20proclamation_english.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Ethiopia 2007) \"tree\" means any woody plant regardless of its species, age or size and includes bamboo, reeds and palms as well as other plants to be designated as such by the Ministry; http://www.pfmp-farmsos.org/Docs/forest%20proclamation_english.pdf" .

:def_Tree_Ethiopia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Ethiopia ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dse.de/zel/landinfo/pas/tk247_lup_eth/forest_inventory.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Ethiopia) A ligneous perennial species with a single (and occasionally double) stem. The distinction b/n woody shrub and small tree also need the knowledge of the species, as well as the ecology. http://www.dse.de/zel/landinfo/pas/tk247_lup_eth/forest_inventory.pdf." .

:def_Tree_European_Environment_Agency_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :European_Environment_Agency ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.epa.gov/trs" ;
    :definitionText "(European Environment Agency)- Any large woody perennial plant with a distinct trunk giving rise to branches or leaves at some distance from the ground.(Source: CED) European Environment Agency (EEA), European Topic Centre on Catalogue of Data Sources (ETC/CDS) : General Multilingual Environmental Thesaurus Term Detail. http://www.epa.gov/trs" .

:def_Tree_Fiji_1978_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Fiji ;
    dcterms:date "1978"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.paclii.org/fj/legis/consol_act_OK/fa98/" ;
    :definitionText "(Fiji 1978) Tree - \"trees\" include trees, shrubs and bushes of all kinds, seedlings, saplings and re-shoots of all ages, climbers and creepers and any part of the tree. http://www.paclii.org/fj/legis/consol_act_OK/fa98/" .

:def_Tree_Fiji_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Fiji ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Fiji 2000) Includes trees, shrubs and bushes of all kinds, seedlings, saplings and re-shoots of all ages, climbers and creepers and any part of the tree. Malakai Sevudredre, Conservator of Forests, F.9641/2. 01/06/2000." .

:def_Tree_Finland_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Finland ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "Seppo Ruotsalainen <Seppo.Ruotsalainen@metla.fi>" ;
    :definitionText "(Finland) trees (5 m tall, clear trunk): Guide book for woody plants in Finland. Seppo Ruotsalainen <Seppo.Ruotsalainen@metla.fi" .

:def_Tree_France_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :France ;
    :sourceRef "Michel Godron <michel.godron@libertysurf.fr>" ;
    :definitionText "(France) tree = arbre : plante ligneuse dotée d'une écorce, d'une assise subérophellodermique et d'une tige capable d'atteindre 8 mètres de hauteur (les Palmiers ne sont donc pas des arbres) \"Michel Godron\" <michel.godron@libertysurf.fr" .

:def_Tree_Gambia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Gambia ;
    :sourceRef "http://extwprlegs1.fao.org/docs/pdf/gam19052.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Gambia) - A woody perennial plant typically large that has the potential of growing to more than three meters and with a single well defined stem carrying a more or less defined crown, and includes palm. Source: Danso A. A. Forestry Department <forestry.dept@gamtel.gm and  http://extwprlegs1.fao.org/docs/pdf/gam19052.pdf and http://extwprlegs1.fao.org/docs/pdf/gam19052.pdf" .

:def_Tree_Gambia_1998_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Gambia ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://extwprlegs1.fao.org/docs/pdf/gam19052.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Gambia-1998) \"forest tree\" includes all trees growing within a forest, whether planted or not, and all naturally grown trees outside a forest; http://extwprlegs1.fao.org/docs/pdf/gam19052.pdf" .

:def_Tree_Ghana_1999_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Ghana ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Ghana 1999) A tall plant that can usually last for long period of time. A tree also has a thick central wooden stem or the trunk from which branches grow, which normally bears the leaves. (Osei Kofi, Forestry Dept.- Letter 7 May 99)" .

:def_Tree_Grenada_1949_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Grenada ;
    dcterms:date "1949"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Grenada 1949) Includes palms, bamboos, stumps, brushwood and canes. LEX-FAOC005062. GRENADA: Forest, Soil and Water Conservation Ordinance. An ordinance to make provision for the conservation of forest, soil, water and other natural resources of the Colony. Date of original text: 01 August 1949." .

:def_Tree_Guatemala_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Guatemala ;
    :definitionText "(Guatemala) - Planta leñosa con fuste y copa definida. (Decreto 106-96, capitulo II: definiciones; art. 4)" .

:def_Tree_ICRAF_2017_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :ICRAF ;
    dcterms:date "2017"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://dx.doi.org/10.5716/WP16079.PDF" ;
    :definitionText "(ICRAF - 2017) Woody, self-supporting perennial life forms, regardless of the plant family (thus including conifers, broadleaved trees and shrubs, palms and bamboos, but excluding, for example rattans (not self-supporting), sugarcane and tufted grasses (non-woody)) http://dx.doi.org/10.5716/WP16079.PDF" .

:def_Tree_India_1927_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    dcterms:date "1927"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://envfor.nic.in/legis/forest/forest4.html" ;
    :definitionText "(India 1927) \"tree\" includes palms, bamboos, stumps, brush-wood and canes. http://envfor.nic.in/legis/forest/forest4.html,  http://extwprlegs1.fao.org/docs/pdf/ind3171.pdf and http://nbaindia.org/uploaded/Biodiversityindia/Legal/3.%20Indian%20forest%20act.pdf" .

:def_Tree_India_Andhra_Pradesh_1967_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :India_Andhra_Pradesh ;
    dcterms:date "1967"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.forests.ap.gov.in/apforest_act_1967.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(India Andhra Pradesh 1967) ‘tree’ includes bamboos, stems, brushwood and canes. http://www.forests.ap.gov.in/apforest_act_1967.pdf" .

:def_Tree_India_Kerala_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :India_Kerala ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.kerala.gov.in/law_reforms/12_treegroth.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(India Kerala) Any woody plant whether fruit bearing or not and includes bamboos. http://www.kerala.gov.in/law_reforms/12_treegroth.pdf" .

:def_Tree_India_Madhya_Pradesh_1927_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :India_Madhya_Pradesh ;
    dcterms:date "1927"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://banajata.org/pdf/state-level/chattisgarh.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(India Madhya Pradesh 1927) The act goes on to define the trees that include palms, bamboos, stumps, brushwood and canes. http://banajata.org/pdf/state-level/chattisgarh.pdf" .

:def_Tree_India_Mizoram_2010_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :India_Mizoram ;
    dcterms:date "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.forest.mizoram.gov.in/index.php?option=com_content&task=view&id=127" ;
    :definitionText "(India Mizoram 2010) ‘Tree’ includes palms, bamboos, stumps, brushwood and canes; Mizoram (Forest) Act,19553. http://www.forest.mizoram.gov.in/index.php?option=com_content&task=view&id=127" .

:def_Tree_India_Tamil_Nadu_1882_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :India_Tamil_Nadu ;
    dcterms:date "1882"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "https://www.forests.tn.gov.in/tnforest/app/webroot/img/document/legislations/01_Tamilnadu%20Forest%20Act%201882.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(India Tamil Nadu 1882) Tree \"Tree\" includes stumps, bamboos and brushwood; https://www.forests.tn.gov.in/tnforest/app/webroot/img/document/legislations/01_Tamilnadu%20Forest%20Act%201882.pdf" .

:def_Tree_India_Tamil_Nadu_and_Pondicherry_2008_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :India_Tamil_Nadu_and_Pondicherry ;
    dcterms:date "2008"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.saiindia.gov.in/english/home/public_folder/Professional_Practices_Group/State_Local_Manual/PUDUCHERRY_MANUAL/Wad%20Manual/Forest.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(India Tamil Nadu and Pondicherry 2008?) Tree - Includes any tree seedling, sapling, transplant or coppice shoot of any age and any root, branch or other part. http://www.saiindia.gov.in/english/home/public_folder/Professional_Practices_Group/State_Local_Manual/PUDUCHERRY_MANUAL/Wad%20Manual/Forest.pdf" .

:def_Tree_India_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    :heightMin "1.37"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://moef.gov.in/nfc/s-git.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(India) - In this report, denotes all perennial woody vegetation (including bamboos, palms, coconut, neem, peepal, fruit trees, etc.). It excludes non-perennial non-woody species (e.g., banana) and tall shrubs or climbers (e.g., lantana or canes). For the purpose of assessing tree cover, only those trees having diameter of 10 cm or more at breast height (1.37 m) have been considered. In case of trees having multiple branches below breast height, the individual stems with diameter over 10 cm at b" .

:def_Tree_India_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    :sourceRef "http://moef.gov.in/nfc/s-git.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(India) - The term used in this report refers to the notional area covered by crown of trees that is too small to be delineated by digital interpretation of remote sensing data used for forest cover delineation. http://moef.gov.in/nfc/s-git.pdf" .

:def_Tree_Ireland_2014_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Ireland ;
    dcterms:date "2014"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "https://www.agriculture.gov.ie/media/migration/forestry/forestrythelaw/ForestryAct2014240517.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Ireland 2014) “tree” means a free standing woody perennial plant whose species has the potential to have a more or less definite crown and be capable of reaching a minimum height of 5 metres at maturity and includes a sapling and the species of birch and hazel. https://www.agriculture.gov.ie/media/migration/forestry/forestrythelaw/ForestryAct2014240517.pdf" .

:def_Tree_Kenya_2005_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Kenya ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://formin.finland.fi/public/download.aspx?ID=15959&GUID=%7B88EFD0B8-9F47-4528-A24F-66DDE0CFE370%7D" ;
    :definitionText "(Kenya 2005) Tree means any timber producing plant, or shrubs, bush of any kind and includes a seedling, sapling or reshoot of any age or any part thereof . http://formin.finland.fi/public/download.aspx?ID=15959&GUID=%7B88EFD0B8-9F47-4528-A24F-66DDE0CFE370%7D" .

:def_Tree_Isle_of_Man_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Isle_of_Man ;
    :sourceRef "daff@gov.im" ;
    :definitionText "(Isle of Man) The term \"tree\" is generally not defined. In certain Acts the term is given a special meaning, e.g. - In the Forestry Act \"trees\" is defined as including shrubs. \"IOM Gov DAFF\" <daff@gov.im" .

:def_Tree_Israel_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Israel ;
    :heightMin "4.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "GilS@kkl.org.il" ;
    :definitionText "(Israel) Tree: A plant with woody stem (s), with height at maturity of 4 meters or higher. From: GilS@kkl.org.il" .

:def_Tree_Japan_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Japan ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "Yukichi Konohira <Konohira@cc.tuat.ac.jp>" ;
    :definitionText "(Japan) A woody perennial plant whose cambium makes secondary growth (often includes tree ferns and bamboo). High tree : a tree with enough height ( usually more than 5m ) and with a stem readily distinguishable from branches. Low tree : a tree with a certain height limit and the general absence of a well-defined main stem. Yukichi Konohira <Konohira@cc.tuat.ac.jp" .

:def_Tree_Kyrgyzstan_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Kyrgyzstan ;
    :sourceRef "Irina Yunusova <irina@lesic.elcat.kg>" ;
    :definitionText "(Kyrgyzstan) - A perennial plant with clearly defined stem, carrying side branches and with a top shoot. The whole system of branches together with the corresponding part of the stem forms the crown. Tree is a widely spread life form of plants, playing the major role in the forest and landscape formation. Source: Irina Yunusova irina@lesic.elcat.kg" .

:def_Tree_Lesotho_1998_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Lesotho ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Lesotho 1998) Tree - Include any seedlings, saplings, transplant or coopice shoot of any age. Forestry Act 1998. Via David May ISTF CVP Lesotho." .

:def_Tree_Lithuania_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Lithuania ;
    :heightMin "11.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "Sekrtetore <sek@mp.is.lt>" ;
    :definitionText "(Lithuania) - A woody perennial plant, typically large and with a well defined stem or stem carrying a more or less definite crown, attaining a minimum diameter 14 cm and a minimum height 11 m at maturity. Source: A. Kuliesis, Director of Lithuanain Forest Inventory and Management Institute Email: Sekrtetore sek@mp.is.lt" .

:def_Tree_Luxembourg_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Luxembourg ;
    :definitionText "(Luxembourg) Eléments ligneux pérennes comportant un tronc principal unique ou , s'agissant de taillis, comprennant plusieurs tiges, un houppier plus ou moins caractérisé. Source: Definitions De La Foret Utilisees Dans Le Cadre De L'inventaire Forestier National Au Luxembourg (Marc Wagner)" .

:def_Tree_Malaysia_1984_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Malaysia ;
    dcterms:date "1984"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://extwprlegs1.fao.org/docs/pdf/mal3252.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Malaysia 1984) -A wood perennial with a well-defined stem or trunk which supports a crown of branches and leaves (except in coppice management systems) and of a species which is usually capable of reaching a height of 5 meter at maturity in most of its distribution area. However, the legal definition under the Malaysian National Forestry Act 1984, it is defined as to include roots, stumps, branches, stems, leaves, brush-wood, palms, bamboos, canes, and creepers. From: hcthang@forestry.gov.my (T" .

:def_Tree_Mauritius_1983_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Mauritius ;
    dcterms:date "1983"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.intnet.mu/iels/Forest_act_1983.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Mauritius 1983) - \"Tree\" includes live or dead timber, shrubs, underwood, brushwood, bamboo, palm, branches and twigs. (The Forests and Reserves Act 1983 - http://www.intnet.mu/iels/Forest_act_1983.htm)" .

:def_Tree_Mexico_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Mexico ;
    :sourceRef "Inventario <varelah@servidor.unam.mx>" ;
    :definitionText "(Mexico) (Arbol).- Planta leñosa, usualmente de más de tres metros de alto, cuyo tallo forma en su base un tronco manifiesto y que más arriba se ramifica formando una copa. Source: Glosario de Términos de la Memoria del Inventario Nacional Forestal Periódico y del Reglamento de la Ley Forestal from Unidad del Inventario <varelah@servidor.unam.mx" .

:def_Tree_Morocco_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Morocco ;
    :heightMin "7.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "m.ellatifi@ellatifi.8m.com" ;
    :definitionText "(Morocco) Tree ( Arabic : Shajarah, French : Arbre, Spanish : Arbol) - Woody perennial plant with one main stem, and a total height greater than 7 m. Mohammed Ellatifi, m.ellatifi@ellatifi.8m.com" .

:def_Tree_Myanmar_1992_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Myanmar ;
    dcterms:date "1992"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://sunsite.nus.edu.sg/apcel/dbase/myanmar/primary/myafor.html#ch1" ;
    :definitionText "(Myanmar 1992) Includes root, stump, stem, branch, bush, creeper, bamboo, cane, orchid and seedling. Source: FOREST LAW State Law and Order Restoration Council Law No. 8/92 (3 November 1992) http://sunsite.nus.edu.sg/apcel/dbase/myanmar/primary/myafor.html#ch1 and" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nalms.org/glossary/lkword_t.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Nalms) A woody plant which at maturity is usually 6 meters (20 feet) or more in height and generally has a single trunk, unbranched for 1 m or more above the ground, and a more or less definite crown; e.g., red maple (Acer rubrum), northern white cedar (Thuja occidentalis) http://www.nalms.org/glossary/lkword_t.htm" .

:def_Tree_New_Zealand_1949_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :New_Zealand ;
    dcterms:date "1949"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(New Zealand 1949) - Includes not only timber trees, but also all other kinds of trees, shrubs, and bushes, seedlings, saplings, cuttings, suckers, and shoots of every description. (from Forests Act 1949)" .

:def_Tree_New_Zealand_2011_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :New_Zealand ;
    dcterms:date "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.maf.govt.nz/portals/0/documents/forestry/forestry-ets/2011-ETS-look-up-tables-guide.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(New Zealand 2011) Forest species - A tree species capable of reaching at least five metres in height at maturity in the place that it is located, but does not include tree species grown or managed primarily for the production of fruit and nut crops. For the purposes of the Forestry ETS, any woody vegetation (and including tree ferns) capable of reaching 5 metres in the place it is growing is considered to be a “tree”. http://www.maf.govt.nz/portals/0/documents/forestry/forestry-ets/2011-ETS-loo" .

:def_Tree_Northern_Mariana_Islands_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Northern_Mariana_Islands ;
    :sourceRef "Estanislao Villagomez <stanvill@gtepacifica.net>" ;
    :definitionText "(Northern Mariana Islands) A physical, living plant structure that utilizes solar energy in combination with water moisture and minerals in the ground to produce and contribute life sustaining oxygen for all other living organisms on the planet. Source: Estanislao Villagomez stanvill@gtepacifica.net Division of Agriculture." .

:def_Tree_Pakistan_1927_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Pakistan ;
    dcterms:date "1927"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Pakistan 1927) Tree includes palms, bamboos, stumps, brush-wood and canes. Pakistan Forest Act of 1927. Source: Mumtaz Ahmad, Section Forest Officer, Pakistan Min. of Environment, Local Government, and Rural Development." .

:def_Tree_Papua_New_Guinea_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Papua_New_Guinea ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(Papua New Guinea) Any woody perennial plant that has a single stem (except coppices) and with a diameter greater than 10 cm dbh and height of more than 5 metres and having a somewhat distinct crown shape. Vitus Ambia, Papua New Guinea Forest Authority." .

:def_Tree_Romania_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Romania ;
    :heightMin "7.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "Sorin Sfirlogea <sorinsf@rosilva.ro>" ;
    :definitionText "(Romania) - Wooden perennate plant, with a minimum 7 m height, able to accumulate vegetal biomass and to reproduce itself. Source: Sorin Sfirlogea <sorinsf@rosilva.ro National Forests Administration." .

:def_Tree_SADC_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :SADC ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(SADC 1997) Self-supporting, single stemmed for with a few definitive trunks branching about ground level. Woody plants typically +/- 5 m in height. (Trevett 1997)" .

:def_Tree_SAF_1958_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :SAF ;
    dcterms:date "1958"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "2.44"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(SAF 1958) A woody plant having one well defined stem and a more or less definitely formed crown, usually attaining a height of at least 8 feet. (SAF 1958)" .

:def_Tree_SAF_1971_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :SAF ;
    dcterms:date "1971"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(SAF 1971) A woody perennial plant, typically large and with a single well defined stem carrying a more or less definite crown. (FORD-ROBERTSON 1971)" .

:def_Tree_SAF_1998_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :SAF ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "4.57"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(SAF 1998) A woody perennial plant, typically large and with a well-defined stem or stems carrying a more or less definite crown --note sometimes defined as attaining a minimum diameter of 5 in (12.7 cm) and a minimum height of 15 ft (4.6 m) at maturity, with no branches within 3 ft (1 m) of the ground\". SAF (1998)" .

:def_Tree_Science_botany_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Science_botany ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.biology-online.org/dictionary/Tree" ;
    :definitionText "(Science: botany) A woody plant at least 5 metres high, with a main stem the lower part of which is usually unbranched. http://www.biology-online.org/dictionary/Tree" .

:def_Tree_Seychelles_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Seychelles ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fstcu.org/national/seychell/vegtypes.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Seychelles) Bush vegetation: Mixture of cinnamon, prune de France and various tree species, generally lower than 10m. http://www.fstcu.org/national/seychell/vegtypes.htm . By default, a tree would be 10 m or greater." .

:def_Tree_Sierra_Leone_1988_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Sierra_Leone ;
    dcterms:date "1988"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Sierra Leone 1988) Any woody vegetation. LEX-FAOC005732. SIERRA LEONE: Forestry Act, 1988. Being an Act to make new provisions in the Law relating to Forestry in Sierra Leone and for connected purpose." .

:def_Tree_Solomon_Islands_1999_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Solomon_Islands ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Solomon Islands 1999) Includes any root, stump, stem, branch, brushwood, ung(?) tree or sapling. . [LEX-FAOC018884] SOLOMON ISLANDS: Forests Act (No. 3 of 1999). Date of text: 24 September 1999." .

:def_Tree_Solomon_Islands_2004_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Solomon_Islands ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.parliament.gov.sb/files/legislation/Bills/2004/The%20Forests%20Bill%202004.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Solomon Islands 2004) Trees include a seedling sapling and pole. http://www.parliament.gov.sb/files/legislation/Bills/2004/The%20Forests%20Bill%202004.pdf" .

:def_Tree_South_Africa_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :South_Africa ;
    :heightMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "Graeme Wild <GraemeW@za.sappi.com>" ;
    :definitionText "(South Africa) A woody single stemmed plant more than 3m in height or a woody multi-stemmed plant more than 5m in height. From: Graeme Wild <GraemeW@za.sappi.com" .

:def_Tree_South_Sudan_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :South_Sudan ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(South Sudan 2009) “Tree” means forest trees including bushes, palms, bamboos, shrubs, brushwood, creepers and climbers at all stages of their growth; (GOSS, 2009)" .

:def_Tree_St_Lucia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :St_Lucia ;
    :sourceRef "chiefforest@maffe.org" ;
    :definitionText "(St. Lucia) A large woody plant with a clearly defined bale or stem and a well developed crown. Includes palms, bamboos, stumps, brushwood and canes. (Source: Michael Andrew, chiefforest@maffe.org)" .

:def_Tree_Standard_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Standard ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.wildlifetrust.org.uk/herts/reserves/glossary.html#Acid" ;
    :definitionText "(Standard) - Trees within a coppiced woodland which are allowed to grow to maturity and traditionaly then felled or large timber http://www.wildlifetrust.org.uk/herts/reserves/glossary.html#Acid" .

:def_Tree_Swazi_Nation_1910_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Swazi_Nation ;
    dcterms:date "1910"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Swazi Nation 1910) \"brushwood\" means any bushes, underwood or similar growths on Government land or on Swazi nation land which are not included in the terms \"indi- genous timber\" or \"government timber\"; www.sntc.org.sz/documents/ForestPreservationAct.do" .

:def_Tree_Swaziland_1951_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Swaziland ;
    dcterms:date "1951"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Swaziland 1951) Tree means the whole or any part of any tree as ordinarily understood or of shrub, bush, seedling, transplant, sapling, reshoot, underbrush or regrowth. LEX-FAOC012388. SWAZILAND: Private forests Act 1951 (No. 3 of 1951). An Act to provide for the better regulation and protection of private forests in Swaziland." .

:def_Tree_Swaziland_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Swaziland ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.sntc.org.sz/legislat/sntcact1.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Swaziland) \"tree\" means a perennial plant having a self-supporting woody main stem or trunk and growing to a height of not less than five feet, but does not include bushes or shrubs http://www.sntc.org.sz/legislat/sntcact1.html" .

:def_Tree_Sweden_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Sweden ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Sweden 2000) - Tree - able to reach 5 meters when soil fertility and surrounding environment optimal. For FRA 2000 - Source: UN/ECE 2000 p 87" .

:def_Tree_Taiwan_ROC_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Taiwan_ROC ;
    :sourceRef "service@dns.forest.gov.tw" ;
    :definitionText "(Taiwan, ROC) A woody plant having one well-defined stem and a more or less definitely formed crown, usually attaining a DBH of at least 10cm, and all bamboo stands. Source: \"&ordf;L&deg;È&sect;&frac12;service\" service@dns.forest.gov.tw" .

:def_Tree_Tanzania_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Tanzania ;
    :sourceRef "Forestry <forestry@sua.ac.tz>" ;
    :definitionText "(Tanzania) - Includes palms, bamboos, canes, shrubs, bushes ,plants, poles, climbers, seedlings, saplings and regrowth thereof, all ages and all kinds and part. From: Tanzania Forest policy, Roger Malimbwi, Faculty of Forestry <forestry@sua.ac.tz" .

:def_Tree_Tanzania_2002_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Tanzania ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.parliament.go.tz/Polis/PAMS/Docs/14-2002.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Tanzania 2002) ''tree'' includes palms, bamboos, canes, shrubs, bushes, climbers, forest seedlings, transplants,  http://www.parliament.go.tz/Polis/PAMS/Docs/14-2002.pdf" .

:def_Tree_Thailand_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Thailand ;
    :sourceRef "Songkram Thammincha <fforskt@ku.ac.th>" ;
    :definitionText "(Thailand) - Plant with gbh15 cm divided into 3 classes: gbh 16-45 cm, gbh 46-100 cm; gbh 100 cm. Songkram Thammincha <fforskt@ku.ac.th" .

:def_Tree_Tonga_1961_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Tonga ;
    dcterms:date "1961"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "Via James Barton <jpbarton@xtra.co.nz>" ;
    :definitionText "(Tonga 1961) Includes palms, shrubs, bushes, climbers, seedlings, saplings, and re-shoots of all ages and of all kinds, and any part thereof. Forests Act 1961 (Chapter 126 of the 1988 Revised Edition of the Laws of Tonga). Via James Barton jpbarton@xtra.co.nz" .

:def_Tree_Trinidad_and_Tobago_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Trinidad_and_Tobago ;
    :definitionText "(Trinidad and Tobago) Tree - all species of trees listed in the second schedule and bamboo, palms and brushwood found growing on state lands – Forests Act: Chapter 66:01. Narine Lackhan, Director of Forestry." .

:def_Tree_Turkey_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Turkey ;
    :sourceRef "yilmazersin@hotmail.com" ;
    :definitionText "(Turkey) The trees are the plants of at least 8 m., or more height, have crowns and the wooden stems, at any age or diameter. Source: Turkey's Forest Law No.6831 - \"Ersin Yýlmaz\" yilmazersin@hotmail.com" .

:def_Tree_Uganda_1947_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Uganda ;
    dcterms:date "1947"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(Uganda 1947) - Includes trees palms, bamboo, canes shrubs bushes, climbers, seedlings, and re-growth of all ages and of all kinds, and any part thereof. THE FORESTS ACT, 1947. An Act To Consolidate the Law Relating to Forests and Forest Reserves." .

:def_Tree_UN_EPEAPAP_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :UN_EPEAPAP ;
    :heightMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.eapap.unep.org/lc/cd/html/training/module1.html" ;
    :definitionText "(UN EP/EAP.AP) - Trees are woody plants land cover with a single well defined stem and more than 3 meters in height. http://www.eapap.unep.org/lc/cd/html/training/module1.html" .

:def_Tree_UN_FAO_1998_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(UN FAO 1998) - A woody perennial plant with a single well defined stem or, in the case of coppice, with several stems, carrying a more or less defined crown. Includes: a) bamboos, palms meeting the above criteria, b) trees as described above being at least 3 m tall, c) woody plants without a tree-like appearance but being more than 5 m tall (Choudhury and Jansen 1998)." .

:def_Tree_UN_FAO_1998_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(UN FAO 1998) - A woody perennial plant with a single, well defined stem carrying a more-or-less-defined crown and being at least 3 m tall. Note: where a clear separation between trees and shrubs is too difficult to establish, a sub-condition of Height is applied: a woody plant higher than 5 m is classified as a Tree; a woody plant lower than 5 m is classified as a shrub. This general rule is subject to the following exception: a woody plant with the clear physiognomic aspect of tree can be clas" .

:def_Tree_UN_FAO_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/methods_and_science/lulucf/application/pdf/060830_killmann.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN FAO 2000 and 2005) A woody perennial with a single main stem or, in the case of coppice with several stems, having a more or less definite crown. Includes: Bamboos, palms another woody plants meeting the above criterion (UN-ECE/FAO 1997 and FAO 1998). and http://unfccc.int/files/methods_and_science/lulucf/application/pdf/060830_killmann.pdf" .

:def_Tree_United_Kingdom_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :United_Kingdom ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.forestry.cov.uk/website/foreststats./sources.html" ;
    :definitionText "(United Kingdom) – A tree is defined by its species, a list of tree species is given in Chapter 4 of (http://www.forestry.cov.uk/website/foreststats./sources.html. From Stefania Pizzirani, Research Gate. 4 Feb. 2014." .

:def_Tree_United_Kingdom_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :United_Kingdom ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.bailii.org/ew/cases/EWHC/Admin/2009/220.html" ;
    :definitionText "(United Kingdom) A tree is only a tree if its trunk had a diameter of at least seven inches. Lord Demning. http://www.bailii.org/ew/cases/EWHC/Admin/2009/220.html" .

:def_Tree_United_Kingdom_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :United_Kingdom ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.u-net.com/trees/p4.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(United Kingdom) Native Tree - Those trees that colonised the British Isles after the last ice age and before they were cut off from the rest of Europe by the rising sea levels. Includes the island of Ireland as well as Britain. http://www.u-net.com/trees/p4.htm." .

:def_Tree_United_Kingdom_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :United_Kingdom ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.woodlander.co.uk/cgi-bin/viewrecordsalpha.asp?page=2&letter=t" ;
    :definitionText "(United Kingdom) Not easy to define, a tree is a woody plant that often grows to 6m (20ft) or more on a single stem. Compare with shrub. http://www.woodlander.co.uk/cgi-bin/viewrecordsalpha.asp?page=2&letter=t" .

:def_Tree_USA_Congress_OTA_1984_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_Congress_OTA ;
    dcterms:date "1984"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://govinfo.library.unt.edu/ota/Ota_4/DATA/1984/8426.PDF" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-Congress-OTA 1984) A woody perennial plant having a single, usually elongate, main stem generally with few or no branches on its lower part. http://govinfo.library.unt.edu/ota/Ota_4/DATA/1984/8426.PDF" .

:def_Tree_USA_FED_5WAY_1985_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_5WAY ;
    dcterms:date "1985"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-5WAY 1985) Tree. (III) A woody plant usually having one erect perennial stem at least 7.5 cm in diameter at breast height at maturity: a more or less definitely formed crown of foliage, and a height of at least 5 m at maturity (Land Use and Land Cover Common Terminology Work Group 1985)." .

:def_Tree_USA_FED_Census_1870_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_Census ;
    dcterms:date "1870"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://memory.loc.gov/cgi-bin/query/r?ammem/gmd:@field(NUMBER+@band(g3701gm+gct00008" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-Census 1870) Trees grow to 30 feet or higher. http://memory.loc.gov/cgi-bin/query/r?ammem/gmd:@field(NUMBER+@band(g3701gm+gct00008))" .

:def_Tree_USA_FED_DA_FS_1979_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_FS ;
    dcterms:date "1979"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "3.96"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-FS 1979) A woody plant having one erect perennial stem or trunk at least 3 inches (7.5 centimeters) in diameter at ‘breast height (4 1/2 feet or 1.3 meters), a more or less definitely formed crown of foliage, and a height of at least 13 feet (4meters) (LITTLE 1979)" .

:def_Tree_USA_FED_DA_FS_1989_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_FS ;
    dcterms:date "1989"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "4.88"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-FS 1989) A woody plant usually having one or more perennial stem at least 3 inches d.b.h. at maturity, a more or less definitely formed crown of foliage, and a height of at least 16 feet at maturity (USDA Forest Service 1989)." .

:def_Tree_USA_FED_DA_FS_1999_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_FS ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "3.66"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.srsfia.usfs.msstate.edu/scripts/ew.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-FS 1999) A woody plant usually having one or more perennial stems, a more or less definitely formed crown of foliage, and a height of al least 12 feet at maturity. http://www.srsfia.usfs.msstate.edu/scripts/ew.htm and http://www.gcrio.org/OnLnDoc/senate_epw990603.html" .

:def_Tree_USA_FED_DA_FS_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_FS ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "4.57"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://fia.fs.fed.us/tools-data/docs/default.asp" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-FS 2006) A woody perennial plant, typically large, with a single well-defined stem carrying a more or less definite crown; sometimes defined as attaining a minimum diameter of 3 inches (7.6 cm) and a minimum height of 15 ft (4.6 m) at maturity. For FIA, any plant on the tree list in the current field manual is measured as a tree. http://fia.fs.fed.us/tools-data/docs/default.asp" .

:def_Tree_USA_FED_DA_NRCS_1992_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_NRCS ;
    dcterms:date "1992"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "4.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ftc.nrcs.usda.gov/doc/nri/72.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-NRCS 1992) (Cover) An Earth Cover (Level 1) category with vegetative cover recognized as woody plants which usually have one perennial stem, a definitely formed crown of foliage, and a mature height of at least 4 meters. This category contains all trees, even those planted for the purposes of producing food and ornamentals, including Christmas trees. The second level categories of tree cover include fruit and nut trees, conifers, hardwoods, inter-mixed, and tropical species. [NRI-92]" .

:def_Tree_USA_FED_DA_NRCS_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_NRCS ;
    :heightMin "4.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://nsscnt.nssc.nrcs.usda.gov/nfm/apxframe.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-NRCS) For the purpose of developing ecological site descriptions, a woody-stemmed perennial plant, usually single stemmed, that can grow to 4 meters in height at maturity. http://nsscnt.nssc.nrcs.usda.gov/nfm/apxframe.htm and National Soil Survey Handbook http://www.statlab.iastate.edu/soils/nssh/622.htm" .

:def_Tree_USA_FED_DA_SCS_FS_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_SCS_FS ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-SCS & FS 1997) (Forest tree) A woody perennial plant having a single well developed main stem and usually more than 12 feet in height at maturity. (FS 1977)" .

:def_Tree_USA_FED_DI_FWS_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DI_FWS ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nwi.fws.gov/contents.html#concept" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DI-FWS) A woody plant which at maturity is usually 6 m (20 feet) or more in height and generally has a single trunk, unbranched for 1 m or more above the ground, and a more or less definite crown; e.g., red maple (Acer rubrum), northern white cedar (Thuja occidentalis). http://www.nwi.fws.gov/contents.html#concept" .

:def_Tree_USA_FED_EPA_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_EPA ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.epa.gov/fedrgstr/EPA-IMPACT/2003/August/Day-11/i20345.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-EPA 2003) A tall woody plant having comparatively great height and a single trunk from which an annual fruit or vegetable crop is produced for commercial purposes, such as maple tree for syrup, papaya tree, or orchard tree. Plantain and banana plants are also included. Trees used for pulp or timber are not considered trees under this part. http://www.epa.gov/fedrgstr/EPA-IMPACT/2003/August/Day-11/i20345.htm" .

:def_Tree_USA_FED_FGDC_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_FGDC ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://biology.usgs.gov/fgdc.veg/standards/appendix3.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-FGDC 1997) Woody plants that generally have a single main stem and have more or less definite crowns. In instances where life form cannot be determined, woody plants equal to or greater than 5 m in height will be considered trees. [Source: http://biology.usgs.gov/fgdc.veg/standards/appendix3.htm]" .

:def_Tree_USA_FED_FGDC_2007_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_FGDC ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fgdc.gov/standards/projects/FGDC-standards-projects/vegetation/index_html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-FGDC 2007 Draft) A woody plant that generally has a single main stem and a more or less definite crown. In instances where growth form cannot be determined, woody plants equal to or greater than 5 m in height at maturity shall be considered trees (adapted from FGDC 1997). Includes dwarf trees (Tart et al. 2005b) or “treelets” (Box 1981). http://www.fgdc.gov/standards/projects/FGDC-standards-projects/vegetation/index_html" .

:def_Tree_USA_FED_NOAA_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_NOAA ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "6.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.csc.noaa.gov/crs/lca/tech_cls.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-NOAA 2003) Single-stemmed, woody vegetation unbranched 2 to 3 feet above the ground having a height greater than 6 meters (20 feet). http://www.csc.noaa.gov/crs/lca/tech_cls.html" .

:def_Tree_USA_STATE_Airports_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Airports ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.townofbourne.com/Town%20Offices/Bylaws/Chapter5.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Airports) \"Tree\" means a tree or other object of natural growth. http://www.townofbourne.com/Town%20Offices/Bylaws/Chapter5.htm" .

:def_Tree_USA_STATE_Arizona_Tempe_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Arizona_Tempe ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.tempe.gov/tdsi/Planning/CPTED/cpted3.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Arizona-Tempe) A woody plant which, at maturity, has one well-defined trunk at least two (2) inches in diameter, a height of at least ten (10) feet, and a formed crown of foliage. http://www.tempe.gov/tdsi/Planning/CPTED/cpted3.htm" .

:def_Tree_USA_STATE_Arkansas_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Arkansas ;
    :sourceRef "Jim Grant <jim.grant@mail.state.ar.us>" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Arkansas) Tree - a woody plant at least 8 feet tall with one well-defined stem and a more or less definitely formed crown. Other definitions say a woody plant from 12 - 15 feet tall with one well-defined stem and a more or less definitely formed crown. Several sources. The SAF definition is one stem and 15 feet. Other definitions ranged from 8 - 15 feet. Jim Grant jim.grant@mail.state.ar.us no official definitions in Arkansas law." .

:def_Tree_USA_STATE_California_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_California ;
    :heightMin "4.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://mississauga.ca/CORPSVCS/clerk/bylaws/tree_residentinfo.PDF" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-California) A self-supporting woody plant which will reach a height of at least 4.5 m (15 ft) at maturity; http://mississauga.ca/CORPSVCS/clerk/bylaws/tree_residentinfo.PDF" .

:def_Tree_USA_STATE_Florida_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Florida ;
    :heightMin "4.57"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Florida) Any self-supporting, woody plant that normally grows to a minimum height of 15 feet or greater with a mature crown spread of 15 feet or greater and having trunks that can be maintained with over five feet of clear wood. Mangroves shall be considered trees. 24.73.97.98/BDLG%5CTreePermApp.doc" .

:def_Tree_USA_STATE_Hawaii_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Hawaii ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fs.fed.us/psw/publications/documents/psw_gtr076/psw_gtr076.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Hawaii) Tree--A woody plant that usually has an erect perennial stem or trunk at least 7.5 cm d.b.h. and a total height of at least 5 m. http://www.fs.fed.us/psw/publications/documents/psw_gtr076/psw_gtr076.pdf" .

:def_Tree_USA_STATE_Illinois_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Illinois ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.legis.state.il.us/ilcs/ch225/ch225act740.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Illinois) \"Tree\" or \"trees\" means any tree, standing or felled, living or dead, and includes both those trees included within the definition of \"timber\" in Section 2 of the \"Timber Buyers Licensing Act\" and Christmas trees. The term does not apply to trees or parts of trees that have been cut into firewood http://www.legis.state.il.us/ilcs/ch225/ch225act740.htm" .

:def_Tree_USA_STATE_Indiana_Bloomington_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Indiana_Bloomington ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.city.bloomington.in.us/code/TITLE12/Chapter_12_24_TREES/12_24_010_Definitions_.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Indiana-Bloomington) A woody, perennial plant with one main stem or trunk which develops many branches. http://www.city.bloomington.in.us/code/TITLE12/Chapter_12_24_TREES/12_24_010_Definitions_.html" .

:def_Tree_USA_STATE_Iowa_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Iowa ;
    :sourceRef "http://www2.legis.state.ia.us/wais/bin/waisgate?WAISdocID=4782917490+0+0+0&WAISaction=retrieve" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Iowa) Forest trees. The ash, black cherry, black walnut, butternut, catalpa, coffee tree, the elms, hackberry, the hickories, honey locust, Norway and Carolina poplars, mulberry, the oaks, sugar maple, cottonwood, soft maple, osage orange, basswood, black locust, European larch and other coniferous trees, and all other forest trees introduced into the state for experimental purposes, shall be considered forest trees within the meaning of this chapter. In forest reservations which are " .

:def_Tree_USA_STATE_Kansas_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Kansas ;
    :heightMin "3.96"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "Atchison <ratchiso@oznet.ksu.edu>" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Kansas) A woody plant usually having one or more erect perennial stems, a stem diameter at breast height of at least 3 inches, a more or less definitely formed crown of foliage, and a height of at least 13 feet at maturity. Robert L. Atchison ratchiso@oznet.ksu.edu" .

:def_Tree_USA_STATE_Kentucky_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Kentucky ;
    :sourceRef "Steve.Kull@mail.state.ky.us" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) A woody perennial plant, typically large and with a well-defined stem or stems carrying a more or less definite crown (usually more that 12 feet in height at maturity). The State of Kentucky does not have the terms Forest, Forestland, or Tree officially defined in State Statute or Regulation. The Division of Forestry utilizes the Society of American Forester's definitions for these terms as listed in John A. Helms' The Dictionary of Forestry. Steve.Kull@mail.state.ky.us" .

:def_Tree_USA_STATE_Maryland_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Maryland ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "6.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Maryland 2000) Tree – trees are greater than 5.0 inches diameter at breast height (DBH) and greater than 20 feet tall dnrweb.dnr.state.md.us/download/education/wetlands.doc" .

:def_Tree_USA_STATE_Maryland_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Maryland ;
    :heightMin "6.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://pilot.wash.lib.md.us/washco/forestcn.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Maryland) A large, branched woody plant having one or several self-supporting stems or trunks that reach a height of at least 20 feet at maturity. http://pilot.wash.lib.md.us/washco/forestcn.html" .

:def_Tree_USA_STATE_Maryland_Easton_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Maryland_Easton ;
    :heightMin "6.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.town-eastonmd.com/Planning/fco/fco_a002.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Maryland-Easton) \"Tree\" means a large, branched woody plant having one or several self-supporting stems or trunks that reach a height of at least 20 feet at maturity. http://www.town-eastonmd.com/Planning/fco/fco_a002.pdf" .

:def_Tree_USA_STATE_Maryland_Laytonsville_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Maryland_Laytonsville ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.laytonsville.md.us/tree_ordinance.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Maryland-Laytonsville) A perennial plant that has a woody stem or trunk, and which customarily grows to a height of not less than ten feet when fully grown. http://www.laytonsville.md.us/tree_ordinance.htm" .

:def_Tree_USA_STATE_Maryland_Rockville_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Maryland_Rockville ;
    :heightMin "6.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ci.rockville.md.us/cityprojects/envguide/eggloss.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Maryland-Rockville) A large, woody plant having one or several self-supporting stems or trunks and numerous branches that reach a height of at least 20 feet at maturity. http://www.ci.rockville.md.us/cityprojects/envguide/eggloss.htm" .

:def_Tree_USA_STATE_Michigan_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Michigan ;
    :heightMin "4.57"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://mff.dsisd.net/PDF/0-IntroStuff/4-Glossary.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Michigan) TREE: It might seem silly, at first, to define a tree. Everyone knows what a tree is . . . don't they? The difference between and tree and shrub can be defined without difficulty. A tree is \"a woody perennial plant, typically large and with a well-defined stem or stems carrying a more or less definite crown --- note sometimes defined as attaining a minimum diameter of 5 inches and a minimum height of 15 feet at maturity, with no branches within 3 feet of the ground\" [Society" .

:def_Tree_USA_STATE_Missouri_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Missouri ;
    :sourceRef "Mike Hoffmann <hoffmm@mail.conservation.state.mo.us>" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Missouri) Although we do not have \"official\" definitions, we commonly use the accepted SAF definitions for these terms. See Dictionary of Forestry; John A. Helms, editor; published 1998 by the Society of American Foresters. \"Mike Hoffmann\" <hoffmm@mail.conservation.state.mo.us>" .

:def_Tree_USA_STATE_Nevada_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Nevada ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.state.nv.us/cnr/ndwp/dict-1/WORD_T.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Nevada) A woody plant which at maturity is usually 6 meters (20 feet) or more in height and generally has a single trunk, unbranched for 1 m or more above the ground, and a more or less definite crown; e.g., red maple (Acer rubrum), northern white cedar (Thuja occidentalis). Water Words Dictionary http://www.state.nv.us/cnr/ndwp/dict-1/WORD_T.htm and http://www.nalms.org/glossary/lkword_f.htm Lake and Water Words Glossary" .

:def_Tree_USA_STATE_New_Mexico_2007_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_New_Mexico ;
    dcterms:date "2007"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.conwaygreene.com/lpbin21/lpext.dll/Test/NMACRaw/1/51fd0/571dd/572c0/572d3?fn=document-frame.htm&f=templates&2.0" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-New Mexico-2007) “ “Tree” means a woody perennial plant usually having a single main stem generally with few or no branches on its lower part; however, species such Gambel oak (quercus gambelii) and one seed juniper (juniperus monosperma) may be multi-stemmed and species such as fir (abies), spruce (picea) and juniper (juniperus) may have many branches on the stem’s lower part. http://www.conwaygreene.com/lpbin21/lpext.dll/Test/NMACRaw/1/51fd0/571dd/572c0/572d3?fn=document-frame.htm&f" .

:def_Tree_USA_STATE_North_Carolina_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_North_Carolina ;
    :sourceRef "Brown <David.R.Brown@ncmail.net>" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-North Carolina) Tree - A woody perennial plant, typically large and with a single well defined stem carrying a more or less definite crown. Source: Terminology of Forest Science, Technology Practice and Products. Edited by F.C. Ford-Robertson. Society of American Foresters, Washington, D.C., 1971. David R. Brown <David.R.Brown@ncmail.net>" .

:def_Tree_USA_STATE_Oregon_Canby_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Oregon_Canby ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ci.canby.or.us/municipalcode/Title12%20StreetsSidewalks&PublicPlaced/12.32TreeRegulations.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Oregon-Canby) A woody perennial plant having a single elongated main stem generally with few or no branches on its lower part. http://www.ci.canby.or.us/municipalcode/Title12%20StreetsSidewalks&PublicPlaced/12.32TreeRegulations.htm" .

:def_Tree_USA_STATE_South_Dakota_1996_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_South_Dakota ;
    dcterms:date "1996"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "3.96"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "Greg.Josten@state.sd.us" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-South Dakota 1996) Tree: A woody plant usually having one or more erect perennial stems, a stem diameter at breast height of at least 3 inches, a more or less definitely formed crown of foliage, and a height of at least 13 feet at maturity. Source - Leatherberry, Earl C., Ronald J. Piva, and Gregory J. Josten. 2000. South Dakota's Forest Resources Outside the Black Hills National Forest, 1996. USDA Forest Service North Central Research Station, Res. Pap. NC-338. Greg.Josten@state.sd.u" .

:def_Tree_USA_STATE_Virginia_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Virginia ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "3.05"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dof.virginia.gov/edu/glossary.htm#F" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Virginia 1997) A woody plant having a well-defined stem, more or less definitely formed crown and usually attaining a height of at least 10 feet. http://www.dof.virginia.gov/edu/glossary.htm#F." .

:def_Tree_USA_STATE_Virginia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Virginia ;
    :sourceRef "James <starrj@dof.state.va.us>" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Virginia) - \"Forest trees\" means only those trees which are a part of and constitute a stand of potential, immature, or mature commercial timber trees. The term \"forest trees\" includes shade trees of any species around houses, along highways and within cities and towns if the trees constitute an insect or disease menace to nearby timber trees or timber stands. Under Authority of Department of Forestry. § 10.1-1178. Definitions. \"Starr, James\" starrj@dof.state.va.us" .

:def_Tree_USA_STATE_Virginia_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Virginia ;
    :sourceRef "James <starrj@dof.state.va.us>" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Virginia) Real Estate - TREE. A tree is single woody stem of a species presently or prospectively suitable for commercial industrial wood products. Standards for Classification of Real Estate As Devoted To Forest Use Under The Virginia Land Use Assessment Law Under the authority of 58.1-3229, et. seq. of the Code of Virginia \"Starr, James\" starrj@dof.state.va.us" .

:def_Tree_USA_STATE_Washington_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Washington ;
    :sourceRef "http://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=76.09.020" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Washington)\"Forest trees\" does not include hardwood trees cultivated by agricultural methods in growing cycles shorter than fifteen years if the trees were planted on land that was not in forest use immediately before the trees were planted and before the land was prepared for planting the trees. \"Forest trees\" includes Christmas trees, but does not include Christmas trees that are cultivated by agricultural methods, as that term is defined in RCW 84.33.035. http://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/" .

:def_Tree_USA_STATE_Wisconsin_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Wisconsin ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.legis.state.wi.us/rsb/code/nr/nr037.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Wisconsin) A woody plant which at maturity is 20 feet or more in height, with a single trunk, unbranched for at least several feet above the ground and having a more or less definite crown. http://www.legis.state.wi.us/rsb/code/nr/nr037.pdf" .

:def_Tree_Venezuela_1977_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Venezuela ;
    dcterms:date "1977"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "Via <Profauna@marnr.gov.ve>" ;
    :definitionText "(Venezuela 1977) ARBOL: planta perenne de tronco leñoso y elevado que se ramifica a cierta altura del suelo, con una altura superior a los 5 metros: constituye un elemento del bosque. Reglamento de la Ley Forestal de Suelos y Aguas (1977). Areas Naturales Protegidas de Venezuela. Series Aspectos Conceptuales y Metodológicos, DGSPOA/ACM/01, feb 1992. Via Profauna@marnr.gov.ve" .

:def_Tree_WCMC_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :WCMC ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.wcmc.org.uk/forest/data/cdrom2/text2.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(WCMC) Mainly phanerophytes (single-trunked individuals, as most trees) and not chamaephytes (multi-stemmed individuals, as most shrubs). http://www.wcmc.org.uk/forest/data/cdrom2/text2.htm" .

:def_Tree_Yemen_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Yemen ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "m.ellatifi@ellatifi.8m.com" ;
    :definitionText "(Yemen) - Woody perennial plant with one main stem, and a total height greater than 5 m. Mohammed Ellatifi, m.ellatifi@ellatifi.8m.com" .

:def_Tree_Zambia_1973_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Zambia ;
    dcterms:date "1973"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.parliament.gov.zm/sites/default/files/documents/acts/The%20Forest%20Act%202015.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Zambia 1973 and 2015) Includes bushes, climbers, coppice, palms, reshoots, saplings, seedlings and shrubs of all ages and of all kinds and nay part thereof. LEX-FAOC003914. ZAMBIA: Forests Act 1973 (Act No. 39). An Act to repeal and replace the Forest Act and to provide for the establishment and management of national forests and local forests, the conservation and protection of forests and trees, the licensing and sale of forest produce and other matters. “ http://www.parliament.gov.zm/sites/d" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_005
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree" ;
    :definitionText "A large perennial woody plant. Though there is no set definition of size, it is generally at least 6 m (20 ft) high at maturity, and with branches supported on a single main stem. Compared with most other forms of plants, trees are long-lived. http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_006
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://explanation-guide.info/meaning/Tree.html" ;
    :definitionText "A large perennial woody plant. Though there is no set definition of size, it is generally at least 6 m (20 ft) high at maturity, and with branches supported on a single main stem. Compared with most other forms of plants, trees are long-lived. A few species of trees grow to over 100 m (300 ft) tall and some live for several millennia. Trees are important components of the natural landscape and significant elements in landscaping. http://explanation-guide.info/meaning/Tree.html and http://en.wiki" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_007
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :heightMin "3.05"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://ag.arizona.edu/arec/pubs/rmg/2._Rangeland_Management_/4Terms.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "A large woody perennial plant, usually single stemmed, that has a definite crown shape and characteristically reaches a mature height of more than 10 feet. RANGELAND TERMINOLOGY http://ag.arizona.edu/arec/pubs/rmg/2._Rangeland_Management_/4Terms.pdf; http://www.agroselviter.unito.it/range/docs/4Terms.pdf; https://extension.usu.edu/rangelands/htm/intro-rangelands/range-terms" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_008
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.geog.ouc.bc.ca/conted/onlinecourses/enviroglos/t.html#anchor122359" ;
    :definitionText "A large woody plant that has a trunk which supports branches and leaves. http://www.geog.ouc.bc.ca/conted/onlinecourses/enviroglos/t.html#anchor122359 and http://www.physicalgeography.net/physgeoglos/anchor122359" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_009
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.naturedetectives.org.uk/NR/rdonlyres/D5E0AFFC-D1FD-447E-9E1B-2EE0F61EB1C8/0/2927Woodlandmaths.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "A large woody plant, usually with a main stem or trunk http://www.naturedetectives.org.uk/NR/rdonlyres/D5E0AFFC-D1FD-447E-9E1B-2EE0F61EB1C8/0/2927Woodlandmaths.pdf" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_010
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.privateforestry.org.au/glos_o-z.htm" ;
    :definitionText "A perennial plant having a self-supporting woody main stem or trunk which usually develops woody branches. A tree, under the Soil Conservation Act, 1938, includes sapling, shrub and scrub in this definition. http://www.privateforestry.org.au/glos_o-z.htm" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_011
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.botany.com/16.tr.html" ;
    :definitionText "A perennial plant that grows from the ground with a single, normally tall, woody, self-supporting trunk or stem and an elevated crown of branches and foliage (or only foliage as in the palms). http://www.botany.com/16.tr.html" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_012
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.wordsmyth.net/cgi-bin/simplesearch.cgi?matchent=trees&matchtype=exact&matchid=-1&retall=1&template=wordsmyth&senses=1" ;
    :definitionText "A perennial woody plant consisting of roots, a trunk, and branches, usu. growing to a substantial height. http://www.wordsmyth.net/cgi-bin/simplesearch.cgi?matchent=trees&matchtype=exact&matchid=-1&retall=1&template=wordsmyth&senses=1" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_013
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dictionary.com/cgi-bin/dict.pl?term=tree" ;
    :definitionText "A perennial woody plant having a main trunk and usually a distinct crown. http://www.dictionary.com/cgi-bin/dict.pl?term=tree" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_014
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :definitionText "A perennial woody plant with a single stem which from natural tendencies generally divides into two or more branches at some distance from the ground. (Moon and Brown 1914)." .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_015
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fix.net/~ggoven/trees.html" ;
    :definitionText "A plant is called a tree if it has a woody stem 8 feet or more in height. The stem often has no branches for several feet above the ground. At the top it has a crown of branches and leaves. Botanists do not separate shrubs and trees. Shrubs are smaller. They branch close to the ground and have many stems. http://www.fix.net/~ggoven/trees.html and http://www.optonline.com/comptons/ceo/04851_A.html" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_016
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dictionary.com/cgi-bin/dict.pl?term=tree" ;
    :definitionText "A plant or shrub resembling a tree in form or size. http://www.dictionary.com/cgi-bin/dict.pl?term=tree" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_017
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.landhelp.info/FramifyGlossary.php" ;
    :definitionText "A plant that is usually more than 12 feet tall and has a single main woody stem with a distinct crown of leaves. http://www.landhelp.info/FramifyGlossary.php" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_018
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.enchantedlearning.com/subjects/plants/glossary/indext.shtml" ;
    :definitionText "A plant that produces wood (made by xylem cells). These tall plants grow taller each year. http://www.enchantedlearning.com/subjects/plants/glossary/indext.shtml" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_019
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.LittleExplorers.com/Tisfor.shtml" ;
    :definitionText "A plant with a trunk, leaves, and roots. http://www.LittleExplorers.com/Tisfor.shtml" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_020
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.m-w.com/cgi-bin/dictionary?book=Dictionary&va=tree" ;
    :definitionText "A shrub or herb of arborescent form <rose trees <a banana tree http://www.m-w.com/cgi-bin/dictionary?book=Dictionary&va=tree" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_021
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.orgler.ws/huxley/Huxley%20Tree%20Ordinance%202001.htm" ;
    :definitionText "A single stemmed, woody plant with a mature height of a minimum of fifteen (15) feet; a small tree less than twenty-five feet (25’), a medium tree twenty-five to forty feet (25’-40’), and a large tree over forty feet (40’). http://www.orgler.ws/huxley/Huxley%20Tree%20Ordinance%202001.htm" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_022
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.notredame.ac.jp/cgi-bin/wn?tree#Overview" ;
    :definitionText "A tall perennial woody plant having a main trunk and branches forming a distinct elevated crown; includes both gymnosperms and angiosperms) http://www.notredame.ac.jp/cgi-bin/wn?tree#Overview of noun tree" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_023
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.cup.cam.ac.uk/elt/dictionary/default.asp?String=tree*1%2B0&ACT=SELECT" ;
    :definitionText "A tall plant which has a wooden trunk and branches that grow from its upper part. Other tall plants which do not have wooden trunks are also often referred to as trees - palm trees. http://www.cup.cam.ac.uk/elt/dictionary/default.asp?String=tree*1%2B0&ACT=SELECT" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_024
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.linguistics.ruhr-uni-bochum.de:8099/cgi-bin/search.sh?tmpl=tmpls&itmpl=tmpls&form=tree" ;
    :definitionText "A tall plant with a hard trunk, branches, and leaves. http://www.linguistics.ruhr-uni-bochum.de:8099/cgi-bin/search.sh?tmpl=tmpls&itmpl=tmpls&form=tree" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_025
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :definitionText "A tall, woody plant. (Scrabble words)" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_026
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.workinghumor.com/dictionary/index.php?s=tree&B1=Search%21" ;
    :definitionText "A thing that will stand in one place fifty years and then suddenly jump in front of a woman driver. Banana River Peelings, (The Left Handed Dictionary) http://www.workinghumor.com/dictionary/index.php?s=tree&B1=Search%21" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_027
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :definitionText "A very large bush, shrub. Babylon.com" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_028
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://woodmagic.forprod.vt.edu/Kids/glossary/" ;
    :definitionText "A very large plant that is at least 20 feet tall, it has only one main trunk (stem) that grows in circumference (around) every year. The stem is persistent (it does not die back), and the stem lives for many, many years. The stem also has a vascular system – it has cells that look and act like straws. http://woodmagic.forprod.vt.edu/Kids/glossary/" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_029
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.foreignword.com/Tools/dictsrch_aff.asp?menu=Y&query=forest&src=BP&srcbox=18&go=Translate&trg=AG" ;
    :definitionText "A very tall plant that has a wooden trunk, branches, and leaves. http://www.foreignword.com/Tools/dictsrch_aff.asp?menu=Y&query=forest&src=BP&srcbox=18&go=Translate&trg=AG" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_030
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://ehe.nmsu.edu/directory/esource/Powerpoint/HORT%20302-02a%20Definitions%20&%20Tools.ppt" ;
    :definitionText "A woody perennial at least 10 ft. tall, usually with one main stem. http://ehe.nmsu.edu/directory/esource/Powerpoint/HORT%20302-02a%20Definitions%20&%20Tools.ppt" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_031
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.m-w.com/cgi-bin/dictionary?book=Dictionary&va=tree" ;
    :definitionText "A woody perennial plant having a single usually elongate main stem generally with few or no branches on its lower part [Source: WWWebster] http://www.m-w.com/cgi-bin/dictionary?book=Dictionary&va=tree" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_032
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.tiburon.org/Government/images/Departments/planning%20dept/plng%20forms/TreeOrd.htm#Section%2015A-2.%20Definitions" ;
    :definitionText "A woody perennial plant that has a trunk circumference of twenty (20) inches measured at twenty-four (24) inches above the ground surface; or A woody perennial plant at least fifteen (15) feet in height that usually, but not necessarily, has a single trunk. In applying subsection (1) above, for trees with more than one trunk, the circumference measurement shall be ascertained from a single measurement around the outside perimeter of all trunks and shall not be calculated as the sum total of the " .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_033
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :definitionText "A woody perennial plant with a single, well defined stem carrying a more-or-less-defined crown (Ford-Robertson, 1971)." .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_034
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.anzlic.org.au/icsm/topo/tddsect3.htm" ;
    :definitionText "A woody perennial plant, having a self-supporting main stem or trunk http://www.anzlic.org.au/icsm/topo/tddsect3.htm" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_035
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :definitionText "A woody perennial, usually seed-bearing plant 20 feet tall or more at maturity (in temperate area of moderate rainfall), in which the main stem (q.v.) dominates the lateral branches in growth, either through life (as in most conifers) to produce a conical or pyramidal outline, or only during early growth after a few years forking one to several times to produce several ascending, almost equally important branches that collectively form a flat or rounded crown. Encyclopedia Britannia 1970." .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_036
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :heightMin "4.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.blm.gov/nstc/library/pdf/1734-6.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "A woody perennial, usually singlestemmed plant that has a definite crown shape and reaches a mature height of at least 4 meters. The distinction between woody plants known as trees and those called shrubs is gradual. Some plants, such as oaks (Quercus spp.), may grow as either trees or shrubs (SRM 1999). http://www.blm.gov/nstc/library/pdf/1734-6.pdf" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_037
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :heightMin "6.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.habitat-restoration.com/paeglos.htm" ;
    :definitionText "A woody plant 5 inches or greater in diameter at breast height and 20 feet or taller. http://www.habitat-restoration.com/paeglos.htm" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_038
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :heightMin "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.tropicalforages.info/key/Forages/Media/Html/Glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "A woody plant at least 3 metres high, usually with an evident trunk. http://www.tropicalforages.info/key/Forages/Media/Html/Glossary.htm" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_039
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://biotech.icmb.utexas.edu/search/dict-search.phtml?title=tree" ;
    :definitionText "A woody plant at least 5 meters (metres) high, with a main stem the lower part of which is usually unbranched. http://biotech.icmb.utexas.edu/search/dict-search.phtml?title=tree and http://www.graylab.ac.uk/cgi-bin/omd?tree" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_040
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :heightMin "3.05"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://fwie.fw.vt.edu/rhgiles/appendices/glosst.htm" ;
    :definitionText "A woody plant having a well-defined stem, more or less definitely formed crown and usually attaining a height of at least 10 feet. http://fwie.fw.vt.edu/rhgiles/appendices/glosst.htm; http://ext.msstate.edu/pubs/pub1250.htm; http://ruralsystemguide.com/Appendices/GlossF.html" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_041
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :heightMin "2.44"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://64.77.121.89/T-U-V-W-X.html" ;
    :definitionText "A woody plant having one well-defined stem and a more or less definitely formed crown, usually attaining a height of at least 8 ft. http://64.77.121.89/T-U-V-W-X.html" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_042
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :heightMin "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.worldagroforestrycentre.org/sea/AgroModels/DBases/af/" ;
    :definitionText "A woody plant having one well-defined stem and a more or less definitely formed crown and roots, usually attaining a height of at least 2 metres. http://www.worldagroforestrycentre.org/sea/AgroModels/DBases/af/" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_043
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :heightMin "2.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.bugwood.caes.uga.edu/glossary/http://www.bugwood.caes.uga.edu/glossary/" ;
    :definitionText "A woody plant having one well-defined stem and a more or less definitely formed crown and roots, usually attaining a height of at least 2.5 metres. http://www.bugwood.caes.uga.edu/glossary/http://www.bugwood.caes.uga.edu/glossary/ and http://www.worldagroforestrycentre.org/InformationResources/T-V.asp" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_044
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.reference.com/browse/wiki/Tree" ;
    :definitionText "A woody plant that has many secondary branches supported clear of the ground on a single main stem or trunk with clear apical dominance. http://www.reference.com/browse/wiki/Tree" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_045
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.bugwood.caes.uga.edu/glossary/" ;
    :definitionText "A woody plant that produces one main trunk or bole and a more or less distinct and elevated head. http://www.bugwood.caes.uga.edu/glossary/ and http://www.worldagroforestrycentre.org/InformationResources/T-V.asp" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_046
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.rook.org/earl/bwca/lists/glossary/" ;
    :definitionText "A woody plant that usually grows to at least 20' in height at maturity, typically having a single trunk with no branches within 3' of the ground. Mitigin the Ojibwe. Boundary Waters Compendium Glossary - http://www.rook.org/earl/bwca/lists/glossary/" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_047
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.aces.edu/waterquality/glossary/glossary_results.php3?rowid=5326" ;
    :definitionText "A woody plant which at maturity is usually 6 meters (20 feet) or more in height and generally has a single trunk, unbranched for 1 m or more above the ground, and a more or less definite crown; e.g., red maple (Acer rubrum), northern white cedar (Thuja occidentalis). http://www.aces.edu/waterquality/glossary/glossary_results.php3?rowid=5326" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_048
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.boldweb.com/greenweb/glossary.htm#T" ;
    :definitionText "A woody plant with a distinct central trunk. Compare shrub. (SHRUB -- A woody plant with a framework of branches and little or no central stem.) http://www.boldweb.com/greenweb/glossary.htm#T" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_049
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.tnw.org.uk/Note17.html" ;
    :definitionText "A woody plant with a single main stem in natural growth http://www.tnw.org.uk/Note17.html" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_050
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://endeavor.des.ucdavis.edu/cnps/intro.html#use" ;
    :definitionText "A woody plant with a tall final height; commonly with one stem [trunk] from the base. http://endeavor.des.ucdavis.edu/cnps/intro.html#use" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_051
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.hww.ca/glossary.asp#letterT" ;
    :definitionText "A woody plant, usually four or more metres tall, with a single main stem (trunk) and a more or less distinct crown of leaves. http://www.hww.ca/glossary.asp#letterT" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_052
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :heightMin "6.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.inwoodlands.org" ;
    :definitionText "A woody, perennial plant which attains the height of 20 feet or higher and a DBH of 4 inches or larger and tends to have a single, central bole. http://www.inwoodlands.org / and http://www.fnr.purdue.edu/inwood/glossary.html" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_053
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.gardenweb.com/glossary/tree" ;
    :definitionText "A woody, self-supporting perennial plant usually with a single main stem and generally growing more than 20 feet tall http://www.gardenweb.com/glossary/tree" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_054
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.graylab.ac.uk/cgi-bin/omd?trees" ;
    :definitionText "A woody, usually tall, perennial higher plants (angiosperms, gymnosperms, and some pterophyta) having usually a main stem and numerous branches. http://www.graylab.ac.uk/cgi-bin/omd?trees" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_055
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :heightMin "1.37"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://envfor.nic.in/nfc/s-git.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "All perennial woody vegetation (including bamboos, palms, coconut, neem, peepal, fruit trees, etc.). It excludes non-perennial non-woody species (e.g., banana) and tall shrubs or climbers (e.g., lantana or canes). For the purpose of assessing tree cover, only those trees having diameter of 10 cm or more at breast height (1.37 m) have been considered. In case of trees having multiple branches below breast height, the individual stems with diameter over 10 cm at breast height have been considered " .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_056
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :definitionText "All plants which grow with a permanent single woody stem or trunk of some height, branching out at some distance from the ground. Encyclopedia Britannia 1910." .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_057
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.botany.com/16.tr.html" ;
    :definitionText "An herb or shrub growing naturally in or trained into the form or a tree. http://www.botany.com/16.tr.html" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_058
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :heightMin "3.66"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.harcourt.com/dictionary/def/1/0/5/7/10579900.html" ;
    :definitionText "An imprecise term for a perennial woody plant that is larger than a bush or shrub, generally understood to describe a large growth having one main trunk with few or no branches projecting from its base, a well-developed crown of foliage, and a height at maturity of at least 12 feet. http://www.harcourt.com/dictionary/def/1/0/5/7/10579900.html" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_059
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "https://secure.finishlinestudios.com/users/www_cityofbaraboo_com/files/code/chapters/43/Chapter26.doc" ;
    :definitionText "Any object of natural growth, except farm crops which are cut at least once a year, and except shrubs, bushes or plants which do not grow to a height of more than five feet. https://secure.finishlinestudios.com/users/www_cityofbaraboo_com/files/code/chapters/43/Chapter26.doc" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_060
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.wordsmyth.net/cgi-bin/simplesearch.cgi?matchent=trees&matchtype=exact&matchid=-1&retall=1&template=wordsmyth&senses=1" ;
    :definitionText "Any of a variety of shrubs, bushes, or plants similar to a tree in shape or size http://www.wordsmyth.net/cgi-bin/simplesearch.cgi?matchent=trees&matchtype=exact&matchid=-1&retall=1&template=wordsmyth&senses=1" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_061
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://machaut.uchicago.edu/cgi-bin/WEBSTER.sh?WORD=tree" ;
    :definitionText "Any perennial woody plant of considerable size (usually over twenty feet high) and growing with a single trunk. http://machaut.uchicago.edu/cgi-bin/WEBSTER.sh?WORD=tree" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_062
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.eastgr.org/citycode/IIIPARKS/35.html" ;
    :definitionText "Any self-supporting woody plant of a species which normally grows to an overall height of fifteen (15) feet or more. (Ord., 2-28-92; Ord., 8-14-92) http://www.eastgr.org/citycode/IIIPARKS/35.html" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_063
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ucmp.berkeley.edu/glossary/gloss8botany.html" ;
    :definitionText "Any tall plant, including many conifers and flowering plants, as well as extinct lycophytes and sphenophytes. http://www.ucmp.berkeley.edu/glossary/gloss8botany.html" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_064
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :heightMin "6.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.railtrails.org/whatwedo/railtrailinfo/resources/glossary.html#F" ;
    :definitionText "Any woody plant that normally grows to a mature height greater than 20 feet and has a diameter of four inches or more at a point four feet above the ground. http://www.railtrails.org/whatwedo/railtrailinfo/resources/glossary.html#F" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_065
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.goaforest.com/regulation/body_preservoftrees2.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Any woody plant whose branches spring from and are supported upon a trunk or body and whose trunk or body is not less than five centimetre in diameter at a height of thirty centimetres from the ground level and is not less than one metre in height from the ground level; http://www.goaforest.com/regulation/body_preservoftrees2.htm" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_066
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "Via John Palmer <j.palmer@nrint.co.uk>" ;
    :definitionText "Anything that ordinarily one would call a tree. Source: Jon Robins \"Hedge of darkness\" in the Law - T2 section of The Times Newspaper, London, 05 August 2003, page 21. Via John Palmer j.palmer@nrint.co.uk" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_067
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :definitionText "Differ from herbs in having woody structure and perennial life and from shrubs in developing single stems that elevate the crowns above other forms of vegetation. (Fergusen 1916)" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_068
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :definitionText "Erect plant with a single woody stem capable of reaching a height of at least 6-8 m (20-25 ft.) at maturity. Academic American Encyclopedia" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_069
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :definitionText "Forest tree, a tree of the forest, especially a timber tree, as distinguished from a fruit tree. Webster's Revised Unabridged Dictionary, © 1996, 1998 MICRA, Inc" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_070
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://crossword911.com/tree.html" ;
    :definitionText "Large plant with trunk – http://crossword911.com/tree.html." .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_071
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.globalff.org/Feature_Articles/Previous_Articles/pre-defo.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Large, generally single-stemmed, woody plants. (http://www.globalff.org/Feature_Articles/Previous_Articles/pre-defo.htm and http://www.geocities.com/atlas/word/gff_deforest.html)" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_072
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.cof.orst.edu/cof/teach/for442/odfdefin.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Live tree - a tree that has 10 percent or greater live crown http://www.cof.orst.edu/cof/teach/for442/odfdefin.htm" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_073
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :heightMin "7.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://fiesta.bren.ucsb.edu/~idgec/publications/reports/forest.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Mature tree. Has a single well-defined stem and is taller than 7 meters, different from a mature shrub that is usually less than 7 meters. http://fiesta.bren.ucsb.edu/~idgec/publications/reports/forest.pdf" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_074
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :heightMin "6.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "Perennial plant with woody stem - usually a single stem or trunk made up of wood and protected by an outer layer of bark. It absorbs water through a root system. There is no clear dividing line between shrubs and trees, but sometimes minimum height of 6 m (20 ft.) is used to define a tree. Lindley and Moore 1998." .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_075
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :definitionText "Perennial woody plant that typically has a single up-right stem or trunk. Colliers Encyclopedia." .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_076
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.encyclopedia.com/articles/13034.html" ;
    :definitionText "Perennial woody plant with a single main stem (the trunk or bole) from which branches and twigs extend to form a characteristic crown http://www.encyclopedia.com/articles/13034.html" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_077
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :definitionText "Perennial, woody species life form with a single stem (trunk), normally greater than 4 to 5 meters or 13 to 16 feet in height; under certain environmental conditions, some tree species may develop a multi-stemmed or short growth form (less than 4 meters or 13 feet in height). (Anderson et al. 1998)" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_078
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://crossword911.com/tree.html" ;
    :definitionText "Plant with branches. http://crossword911.com/tree.html." .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_079
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :definitionText "Plants having a well-developed, woody stem and usually more than 12 feet in height at maturity. www.socrates.lv-hrc.nevada.edu/fia/dab/core1-7/appendix7_12_00.doc" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_080
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "lizell@thurston.com" ;
    :definitionText "Plants having true xylem and phloem; with true leaves present and usually having more than one vein (megaphylls); enations absent; stems branching in various ways or unbranched; reproducing by means of seeds developed from ovules. (lizell@thurston.com from Stern (1991))." .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_081
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.chesco.com/~treeman/words/words-t.html" ;
    :definitionText "Plants that are perennial (live for several to many years), woody (have tough cell walls of wood), shedding (use and shed woody and non-woody parts) and compartmented (made up of many compartments). Trees usually have a single stem over three yards tall. Shrubs usually have many stems less than three yards tall. http://www.chesco.com/~treeman/words/words-t.html" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_082
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "Self-supporting, woody plants with a single main stem and which commonly reach a height of over 5 meters (Hamilton 1991)." .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_083
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "Barry Wyatt <BKW@WPO.NERC.AC.UK>" ;
    :definitionText "Single-stemmed woody plants (From: Barry Wyatt BKW@WPO.NERC.AC.UK - Dansereau, P. (1957)." .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_084
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ucmp.berkeley.edu/glossary/gloss5ecol.html" ;
    :definitionText "Tall plant with a central trunk. The term does not imply anything about relationships, but is a growth pattern that has evolved several times in plants. http://www.ucmp.berkeley.edu/glossary/gloss5ecol.html" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_085
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.allwords.com/query.asp" ;
    :definitionText "Tall woody perennial plant that typically has one main stem or trunk and which, unlike a shrub, usually only begins to branch at some distance from the ground; http://www.allwords.com/query.asp" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_086
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.christiantech.com/cgi-bin/webster.exe?search_for_cgi-bin_texts_web1828=tree" ;
    :definitionText "The general name of the largest of the vegetable kind, consisting of a firm woody stem springing from woody roots, and spreading above into branches which terminate in leaves. A tree differs from a shrub principally in size, many species of trees growing to the highth of fifty or sixty feet, and some species to seventy or eighty, and a few, particularly the pine, to a much greater highth http://www.christiantech.com/cgi-bin/webster.exe?search_for_cgi-bin_texts_web1828=tree" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_087
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.guiaverde.com/arboles/glosario.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Tree (Árbol) - Vegetal leñoso al menos de 5 m. de altura con el tallo simple, denominado tronco, hasta la llamada cruz, en donde se ramifica y forma la copa. Tiene considerable crecimiento en grosor. Se diferencia del arbusto en que suele ser más alto y no se ramifica hasta cierta altura. http://www.guiaverde.com/arboles/glosario.htm" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_088
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.anzlic.org.au/icsm/topo/tddsect4.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Tree (cover) - The amount or density of tall woody plants occupying the surface of a specified area http://www.anzlic.org.au/icsm/topo/tddsect4.htm" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_089
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://birdcare.com/bin/showdict?tree+layer" ;
    :definitionText "Tree (layer) - The highest vegetation zone, lying above the shrub layer, from about eight metres upwards. The tree tops themselves form the canopy. Birdwatcher's Dictionary http://birdcare.com/bin/showdict?tree+layer" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_090
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://code.municipalworld.com/kitchener/690.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Tree means any tree, sapling or shrub, now or hereafter growing on property of the City, unless a contrary intention appears. http://code.municipalworld.com/kitchener/690.pdf" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_091
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.newrichmond.org/treeord.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Tree means any tree. http://www.newrichmond.org/treeord.pdf" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_092
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "https://www.thoughtco.com/worlds-smallest-tree-species-1343503?utm_campaign=wilat&utm_medium=email&utm_source=cn_nl&utm_content=9497194&utm_term" ;
    :definitionText "Tree -The definition of a tree that most tree scholars recognize is \"a woody plant with a single erect perennial trunk that reaches at least 3 inches in diameter at breast height (DBH} when mature https://www.thoughtco.com/worlds-smallest-tree-species-1343503?utm_campaign=wilat&utm_medium=email&utm_source=cn_nl&utm_content=9497194&utm_term" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_093
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/methods_and_science/lulucf/application/pdf/060830_killmann.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Trees outside forests - Trees outside forests include all trees found outside forests and outside other wooded lands: - stands smaller than 0.5 ha; - tree cover in agricultural land, e.g. agroforestry systems, home gardens, orchards; - trees in urban environments; - along roads and scattered in the landscape. (IPCC 2006 GL FRA 2005) http://unfccc.int/files/methods_and_science/lulucf/application/pdf/060830_killmann.pdf" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_094
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.blm.gov/nstc/library/pdf/samplveg.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "USA-FED-DI-BLM 1999, 2001) A woody perennial, usually single-stemmed plant that has a definite crown shape and characteristically reaches a mature height of at least 5 meters (16 feet). Some plants, such as oaks (Quercus spp.), may grow as either trees or shrubs http://www.blm.gov/nstc/library/pdf/samplveg.pdf , http://www.blm.gov/nstc/library/pdf/utilstudies.pdf, and http://www.blm.gov/nstc/library/pdf/1734-7.pdf" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_095
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.alienexplorer.com/ecology/e17.html" ;
    :definitionText "Usually trees are defined as having a large, single trunk rising above the ground. The trunk is composed of wood and is divided usually into a series of branches. http://www.alienexplorer.com/ecology/e17.html" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_096
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.eresourcesystems.com/Help/Glossary/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "Woody perennial having an elongated stem, usually standing over 15 feet tall at maturity. http://www.eresourcesystems.com/Help/Glossary/glossary.html" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_097
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://bpc.iserver.net/cgi-bin/hilite.pl/codes/scottsva/_DATA/TITLE17/Chapter_17_44__GENERAL_AND_SPECIAL/17_44_080_Tree_protection_regu.html" ;
    :definitionText "Woody perennial plant characterized by having a main stem or trunk or a multi-stemmed trunk system with more or less definitely formed crown, usually over ten feet high at maturity. This definition shall not include trees planted, grown and held for sale by licensed nurseries or the first removal or transplanting of such trees pursuant to and as part of the operation of a licensed nursery business. http://bpc.iserver.net/cgi-bin/hilite.pl/codes/scottsva/_DATA/TITLE17/Chapter_17_44__GENERAL_AND_S" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_098
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.gap.uidaho.edu/handbook/LandCoverMapping/UNESCO/default.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Woody perennial plants, usually single stemmed with definite crown shape and reaching a height of five meters in height when mature. http://www.gap.uidaho.edu/handbook/LandCoverMapping/UNESCO/default.htm" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_099
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://corssword911.com/tree.html" ;
    :definitionText "Woody plant – http://corssword911.com/tree.html." .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_100
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :definitionText "Woody plant that renews its growth every year (called a perennial). Most plants classified as trees have a single self-supporting trunk containing woody tissue and in most species the trunk produces secondary limbs, called branches. Encyclopedia Britannia 1995." .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_101
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.pfmt.org/glossary/t.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Woody plant that usually grows to at least 20 feet in height at maturity, typically having a single trunk with no branches within 3 feet of the ground http://www.pfmt.org/glossary/t.htm" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_102
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.google.com/search?q=cache:www.iversonsoftware.com/business/plant/Tree.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Woody plant with a distinct main stem, or trunk. At maturity, trees are usually the tallest of plants, and their height and single main stem differentiate them from shrubs, which are shorter and have many stems. Trees are perennials, plants that live for at least three years. Some species of tree only grow to 4 m (13 ft) in height, but the tallest species may reach heights of more than 112 m (more than 367 ft). http://www.google.com/search?q=cache:www.iversonsoftware.com/business/plant/Tree.htm" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_103
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :heightMin "7.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.aswm.org/lwp/nys/glossary.htm#T" ;
    :definitionText "Woody plants greater than 7 meters tall, and usually with one main trunk http://www.aswm.org/lwp/nys/glossary.htm#T" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_104
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :heightMin "3.7"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "Woody plants having a well-developed stem and which are usually more than 3.7 meters in height at maturity. (Lund 1984)" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_105
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :heightMin "3.96"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "Woody plants having one erect perennial stem or trunk at least 3 inches d.b.h., a more or less definitely formed crown of foliage, and a height of at least 13 feet (at maturity) (Little 1979)." .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_106
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :definitionText "Working trees - those intentionally established in rural and urban landscapes to achieve specific functions (Perry et al. 2005)." .

:def_Tree_FAO_2002_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :FAO ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/DOCREP/005/Y2328E/y2328e00.htm#toc" ;
    :definitionText "(FAO-2002) Trees growing outside the forest and not belonging to the category of forests, forest lands, or other wooded land. According to this definition, Trees outside forests are located on \"other land\", such as agricultural land, built-up areas such as settlements and infrastructure, and bare land (dunes, former mining areas, etc.). (Bellefontaine, Ronald et al. 2002. Trees outside forests - Towards a better awareness. FAO Conservation Giude 35. http://www.fao.org/DOCREP/005/Y2328E/y2328e00." .

:def_Tree_FAO_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :FAO ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :heightMin "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :areaMin "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/docrep/006/ac840e/AC840E00.htm#TOC" ;
    :definitionText "(FAO-2003) Trees on land not defined as forest and other wooded land. Includes: trees on land that fulfils the requirements of forest and other wooded land except that the area is less than 0.5 ha; trees able to reach a height of at least 5 m at maturity in situ where the stocking level is below 5 percent; trees not able to reach a height of 5 m at maturity in situ where the stocking level is below 20 percent; scattered trees in permanent meadows and pastures; permanent tree crops such as fruit-" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_107
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.saiindia.gov.in/english/home/public_folder/Professional_Practices_Group/State_Local_Manual/PUDUCHERRY_MANUAL/Wad%20Manual/Forest.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Tree lands: (India Tamil Nadu and Pondicherry 2008?) i.e., those areas which though outside the scope of the ordinary forest management are essential for the amelioration of physical conditions of the country. http://www.saiindia.gov.in/english/home/public_folder/Professional_Practices_Group/State_Local_Manual/PUDUCHERRY_MANUAL/Wad%20Manual/Forest.pdf" .

:def_Tree_Unknown_nd_108
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.lars.cl/biblioteca/Coura_Samuel.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Trees on land not defined as forest and other wooded land. This may include agricultural land, including meadows and pasture, built-on land and barren land. (da Costa Coura, Samuel Martins et al. 2006+ Evaluation of High Resolution Imagery to Identify Trees Outside Forest (TOF) In Brazilian Atlantic Rain Forest http://www.lars.cl/biblioteca/Coura_Samuel.pdf.)" .

:def_Tree_Australia_Victoria_1958_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Australia_Victoria ;
    dcterms:date "1958"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www8.austlii.edu.au/cgi-bin/viewdoc/au/legis/vic/consol_act/fa1958116/s3.html#state_forest" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia – Victoria 1958) \"timber\" includes fallen trees felled trees and all wood whether sawn split hewn or otherwise fashioned http://www8.austlii.edu.au/cgi-bin/viewdoc/au/legis/vic/consol_act/fa1958116/s3.html#state_forest" .

:def_Tree_Belize_2000_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Belize ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.belizeaudubon.org/new_site/wp-content/uploads/2014/10/Forest_Act_213.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Belize – 2000) “timber” or “lumber” includes trees when they have fallen or have been felled, and all wood, whether cut up or fashioned or hollowed out for any purpose or not; http://www.belizeaudubon.org/new_site/wp-content/uploads/2014/10/Forest_Act_213.pdf" .

:def_Tree_Canada_Alberta_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_Alberta ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.qp.alberta.ca/1266.cfm?page=F22.cfm&leg_type=Acts&isbncln=9780779784318" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada – Alberta 2000) “timber” means all trees living or dead, of any size or species and whether standing, fallen, cut or extracted; http://www.qp.alberta.ca/1266.cfm?page=F22.cfm&leg_type=Acts&isbncln=9780779784318" .

:def_Tree_Canada_BC_1996_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_BC ;
    dcterms:date "1996"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.bclaws.ca/EPLibraries/bclaws_new/document/ID/freeside/96157_01#section1" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada –BC 1996) -cx\"timber\" means trees, whether standing, fallen, living, dead, limbed, bucked or peeled; http://www.bclaws.ca/EPLibraries/bclaws_new/document/ID/freeside/96157_01#section1" .

:def_Tree_India_Tamil_Nadu_1882_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :India_Tamil_Nadu ;
    dcterms:date "1882"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "https://www.forests.tn.gov.in/tnforest/app/webroot/img/document/legislations/01_Tamilnadu%20Forest%20Act%201882.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(India – Tamil Nadu 1882) Timber\" - \"Timber\" includes trees when they have fallen or have been felled, and all wood, whether cut up or fashioned or hollowed out for any purpose or not; https://www.forests.tn.gov.in/tnforest/app/webroot/img/document/legislations/01_Tamilnadu%20Forest%20Act%201882.pdf" .

:def_Tree_Ireland_2014_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Ireland ;
    dcterms:date "2014"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "https://www.agriculture.gov.ie/media/migration/forestry/forestrythelaw/ForestryAct2014240517.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Ireland – 2014) “timber” means the wood produced by a tree, whether or not the tree is standing; https://www.agriculture.gov.ie/media/migration/forestry/forestrythelaw/ForestryAct2014240517.pdf" .

:def_Tree_Tanzania_200_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Tanzania_200 ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.parliament.go.tz/Polis/PAMS/Docs/14-2002.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Tanzania – 200)2 ''timber'' means any wood or tree which has falled or has been felled or cut off and all wood whether unsawn, hewn, sawn or machined, split, or otherwise cut up or fashioned and shall include lumber, flooring strips, shingles, and sleepers but does not include any article manufactured from such wood or firewood; http://www.parliament.go.tz/Polis/PAMS/Docs/14-2002.pdf" .

:def_Tree_Thailand_1964_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Tree ;
    :appliesIn :Thailand ;
    dcterms:date "1964"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www2.austlii.edu.au/~graham/AsianLII/Thai_Translation/National%20Reserve%20Forest%20Act.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Thailand 1964) “Timber” includes all species of plant; whether having trunk or growing in cluster or creeping, live or dead, as well as root, node, stump, sucker, branch, bud, tuber, corn, remains, extremity or any part of plant that is cut, stabbed, sawed, spitted, trimmed, chopped, dug, or done in any manner what so ever; http://www2.austlii.edu.au/~graham/AsianLII/Thai_Translation/National%20Reserve%20Forest%20Act.pdf" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :definitionText "3.1 AFFORESTATION - Afforestation may be a legal term or a process of stocking land. In the case of the latter, we group the definitions into those that imply a change in land cover only and those that imply a change in land cover and use. Four definitions specify \"crops\" implying that the trees will be later removed for commercial purposes. The time period for lands \"never having been forested\" vary from never to 30 to 100 years." .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :sourceRef "http://orb.rhodes.edu/Medieval_Terms.html" ;
    :definitionText "AFFOREST: To make into a forest by application of forest law. http://orb.rhodes.edu/Medieval_Terms.html" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :sourceRef "http://info.sjc.ox.ac.uk/forests/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Place an area under forest law and administration; the creation of a forest by stipulated procedures (M, 26 (v) – 30 (r)); (2) http://info.sjc.ox.ac.uk/forests/glossary.htm" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.hants.org.uk/newforest/bibliog.html" ;
    :definitionText "To bring land within Forest Law (historically) or in current parlance to bring within the control of the Verderers and their Bye-Laws. It is a legal act. http://www.hants.org.uk/newforest/bibliog.html" .

:def_Afforestation_Australia_and_New_Zealand_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Australia_and_New_Zealand ;
    :definitionText "(Australia and New Zealand) The establishment of a species of forest on an area where it does not occur naturally (British Commonwealth Terminology) (Ford-Robertson 1971)." .

:def_Afforestation_Bolivia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Bolivia ;
    :sourceRef "Luis Castello <faopaf@caoba.entelnet.bo>" ;
    :definitionText "(Bolivia) AFORESTACION: Siembra de árboles en tierras que nunca antes tuvieron bosques, por ejemplo, en sabanas, praderas y llanos naturales. Source: Luis Castello faopaf@caoba.entelnet.bo Adjunto sírvase encontrar la versión no oficial y premilinar del Glosario Forestal elaborado por el Proyecto de Apoyo a la Coordinación e Implementación del Plan de Acción Forestal para Bolivia" .

:def_Afforestation_Bulgaria_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Bulgaria ;
    :sourceRef "Forest Research Institute <forestin@bulnet.bg>" ;
    :definitionText "(Bulgaria) Afforestation - The creation of new forests includes the activities connected with the collection of seeds, production of seedlings and saplings, afforestation, selective cuttings, inventory of the young forests and preventing of the erosion. Areas for afforestation in the forest lands are: bare lands, non-regenerated cutting areas and burnt out lands. The afforestation in the forest lands aims: 1. Regeneration and helping the regeneration in mature high-stemmed or coppice forests; 2." .

:def_Afforestation_Cape_Verde_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Cape_Verde ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.indexmundi.com/cape_verde/environment_current_issues.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Cape Verde) Afforestation - converting a bare or agricultural space by planting trees and plants; reforestation involves replanting trees on areas that have been cut or destroyed by fire. http://www.indexmundi.com/cape_verde/environment_current_issues.html" .

:def_Afforestation_Canada_BC_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_BC ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.for.gov.bc.ca/pab/publctns/glossary/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada - BC) The establishment of trees on an area that has lacked forest cover for a very long time or has never been forested. [Source: Glossary of Forestry Terms, Province of British Columbia, Ministry of Forests, http://www.for.gov.bc.ca/pab/publctns/glossary/glossary.htm via Igor A. Yakovlev] and http://www.cinar.gr/delfi The DELFI Vocabulary of Forest Fire Terms" .

:def_Afforestation_Canada_BC_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_BC ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.for.gov.bc.ca/pab/publctns/westland/gloss.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada - BC) The process of converting open land into forest. http://www.for.gov.bc.ca/pab/publctns/westland/gloss.htm" .

:def_Afforestation_Canada_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Canada ;
    :sourceRef "http://carbon.cfs.nrcan.gc.ca/definitions_e.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada) Afforestation - The conversion of land that has not been forested for at least 50 years to forested land through human activities such as planting and seeding. http://carbon.cfs.nrcan.gc.ca/definitions_e.html" .

:def_Afforestation_Colombia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Colombia ;
    :sourceRef "Gerardo Lozano <glozano@impsat.net.co>" ;
    :definitionText "(Colombia) Areas de Aptitud Forestal: \"se definen como aquellas que originalmente tuvieron bosques o deberían tenerlo de acuerdo a criterios eco-biológicos y socio-económicos\" ( Ministerio del medio Ambiente. Doc. Compes 2834. Politica de Bosques\"). \"Gerardo Lozano\" <glozano@impsat.net.co." .

:def_Afforestation_Cote_dIvoire_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Cote_dIvoire ;
    :definitionText "(Cote d’Ivoire) Sont considérés comme reboisement, les terrains plantés de main d'homme en espèces ne donnant pas de produits agricoles, ainsi que les forêts naturelles enrichies artificiellement en essence de bois d'oeuvre par des travaux de plantation ou be silviculture. TITRE I DEFINITIONS, Article 1. - LOI NO 65/425 DU 20 DEC 1965. portant Code Forestier" .

:def_Afforestation_Cuba_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Cuba ;
    :sourceRef "Christoph Kleinn <ckleinn@catie.ac.cr>" ;
    :definitionText "(Cuba) Forestación: la acción de poblar con especies arbóreas terrenos donde nunca hubo bosques, naturales o artificiales, o donde hace mucho desaparecieron. Christoph Kleinn <ckleinn@catie.ac.cr" .

:def_Afforestation_Cyprus_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Cyprus ;
    :sourceRef "Publicity Sector <publicity@cytanet.com.cy>" ;
    :definitionText "(Cyprus) Afforestation: the establishment of a forest or stand in an area where the preceding vegetation or land use was not forest. A.K. Christou \"Forestry Department - Research and Publicity Sector\" publicity@cytanet.com.cy" .

:def_Afforestation_Czech_Republic1995_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Czech_Republic1995 ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.uhul.cz/images/ke_stazeni/legislativa_jazyky/Lesni_zakon_en.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Czech Republic1995) Afforestation shall mean the establishment of forest stand, http://www.uhul.cz/images/ke_stazeni/legislativa_jazyky/Lesni_zakon_en.pdf" .

:def_Afforestation_EC_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :EC ;
    :sourceRef "http://ec.europa.eu/agriculture/publi/enlarge/gloss_en.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(EC) Measures to encourage new woodland development, including financial incentives for farmers who convert agricultural land to woodland and forest. http://ec.europa.eu/agriculture/publi/enlarge/gloss_en.pdf" .

:def_Afforestation_EU_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :EU ;
    :sourceRef "http://europa.eu.int/comm/dg08/forests/en/en4_6.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(EU) The establishment of a more or less contiguous tree cover, normally by planting, in areas which have previously been without trees http://europa.eu.int/comm/dg08/forests/en/en4_6.htm." .

:def_Afforestation_Fiji_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Fiji ;
    :definitionText "(Fiji) Newly planted trees where no trees existed before. Malakai Sevudredre, Conservator of Forests, F.9641/2. 01/06/2000." .

:def_Afforestation_France_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :France ;
    :sourceRef "Michel Godron <michel.godron@libertysurf.fr>" ;
    :definitionText "(France) afforestation = reboisement ou repeuplement : plantation de jeunes arbres ou semis de graines d'arbres \"Michel Godron\" <michel.godron@libertysurf.fr" .

:def_Afforestation_Ghana_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Ghana ;
    :definitionText "(Ghana) An act to plant areas of land with trees to attain forest status. Example is woodlot establishment. (Osei Kofi, Forestry Dept.- Letter 7 May 99)" .

:def_Afforestation_GMUNCCD_2008_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :GMUNCCD ;
    dcterms:date "2008"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.global-mechanism.org/dynamic/documents/document_file/final2-viet-nam-climate-change-report---1july08.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(GM/UNCCD 2008) -The process of establishing and growing forests on bare or cultivated land, which has not been forested in recent history. http://www.global-mechanism.org/dynamic/documents/document_file/final2-viet-nam-climate-change-report---1july08.pdf" .

:def_Afforestation_Hungary_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Hungary ;
    :definitionText "(Hungary) The activity aimed at reproducing the felled or dead growing stock of the forest. The afforestation may be performed: a) by natural means aa) from the seed of the wood being felled dropping onto the soil (natural afforestation from seed origin), and ab) from the shoots sprouting from the root or stump of the felled wood (natural afforestation from shoot origin), ac) by select-cutting ensuring the creation and continuous maintenance of a mixed-age growing stock; b) artificially, in the " .

:def_Afforestation_India_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    :sourceRef "Varma <v.varma@landfood.unimelb.edu.au>" ;
    :definitionText "(India) Bringing any land under forest cover, which was not previously under forest cover. [Source: Glossary of Technical Terms, Forest Research Institute, India. From: \"Vivek K. Varma\" <v.varma@landfood.unimelb.edu.au Date: Fri, 17 Jul 1998 02:28:29 -0400 (EDT)]" .

:def_Afforestation_Indonesia_2002_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Indonesia ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.globalforestwatch.org/common/indonesia/sof.indonesia.english.low.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Indonesia - 2002) The establishment by human action of forest cover on land that was not previously forested or was not forested within living memory. http://www.globalforestwatch.org/common/indonesia/sof.indonesia.english.low.pdf" .

:def_Afforestation_IPCC_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :IPCC ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.junkscience.com/draft_AR4/GLOSSARY_SOD_TSU_FINAL.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(IPCC - 2003) Planting of new forests on lands that historically have not contained forests. For a discussion of the term →forest and related terms such as →afforestation, →reforestation, and →deforestation: see the IPCC Report on Land Use, Land-Use Change and Forestry (IPCC, 2000). See also the Report on Definitions and Methodological Options to Inventory Emissions from Direct Human-induced Degradation of Forests and Devegetation of Other Vegetation Types (IPCC, 2003) (Source: Second Order Draf" .

:def_Afforestation_IPCC_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :IPCC ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.grida.no/climate/ipcc/regional/327.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(IPCC -1997) Forest stands established artificially on lands that previously have not supported forests for more than 50 years http://www.grida.no/climate/ipcc/regional/327.htm" .

:def_Afforestation_Isle_of_Man_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Isle_of_Man ;
    :sourceRef "daff@gov.im" ;
    :definitionText "(Isle of Man) \"Afforestation\" is also not generally defined, but is normally taken as meaning new planting of previously bare land. \"IOM Gov DAFF\" <daff@gov.im" .

:def_Afforestation_Kyrgyzstan_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Kyrgyzstan ;
    :sourceRef "Irina Yunusova <irina@lesic.elcat.kg>" ;
    :definitionText "(Kyrgyzstan) - The creation and growing of artificial forest plantations on the territories formerly not covered with the forest. Source: Irina Yunusova irina@lesic.elcat.kg" .

:def_Afforestation_Latvia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Latvia ;
    :sourceRef "Maksym Polyakov <mpoliak@pcomp.nauu.kiev.ua>" ;
    :definitionText "(Latvia) A complex of measures to afforest such land (area) not covered by forest where forest has not grown before. Source: \"Maksym Polyakov\" mpoliak@pcomp.nauu.kiev.ua" .

:def_Afforestation_Lithuania_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Lithuania ;
    :sourceRef "Sekrtetore <sek@mp.is.lt>" ;
    :definitionText "(Lithuania) Establishment of trees on a non-forest land. Source: A. Kuliesis, Director of Lithuanain Forest Inventory and Management Institute Email: Sekrtetore sek@mp.is.lt" .

:def_Afforestation_Malaysia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Malaysia ;
    :sourceRef "hcthang@forestry.gov.my" ;
    :definitionText "(Malaysia) The artificial establishment of forests by direct seeding or planting seedlings or cuttings on lands which previously (within the living memory or within 50 years) and did not carry any forests. From: hcthang@forestry.gov.my (Thang Hooi Chiew), Forestry Department Peninsular Malaysia" .

:def_Afforestation_Morocco_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Morocco ;
    :sourceRef "m.ellatifi@ellatifi.8m.com" ;
    :definitionText "(Morocco) Afforestation / Forestation (Arabic : Tashjeer, French : Boisement/Reboisement) - Artificial creation (by man) of a forest on an land which has never been forested before, as far as man’s memory can remember, using seedlings, vegetative materials or seeds(sowing) Mohammed Ellatifi, m.ellatifi@ellatifi.8m.com" .

:def_Afforestation_Northern_Mariana_Islands_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Northern_Mariana_Islands ;
    :sourceRef "Estanislao Villagomez <stanvill@gtepacifica.net>" ;
    :definitionText "(Northern Mariana Islands) Afforestation - The science and art of diversifying existing forestland with other suitable species for any generalized purpose beneficial to mankind, wildlife and ecosystem. Source: Estanislao Villagomez stanvill@gtepacifica.net Division of Agriculture." .

:def_Afforestation_Pakistan_1_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Pakistan_1 ;
    :definitionText "(Pakistan 1) To establish a forest on an area from which forest vegetation has always or long been absent. Definition adopted from the British Commonwealth Forest Terminology Part-I, 1953. Source: Mumtaz Ahmad, Section Forest Officer, Pakistan Min. of Environment, Local Government, and Rural Development." .

:def_Afforestation_Pakistan_2_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Pakistan_2 ;
    :definitionText "(Pakistan 2) To establish a species or frees on an area in which it did not occur naturally. Definition adopted from the British Commonwealth Forest Terminology Part-I, 1953. Source: Mumtaz Ahmad, Section Forest Officer, Pakistan Min. of Environment, Local Government, and Rural Development." .

:def_Afforestation_Papua_New_Guinea_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Papua_New_Guinea ;
    :definitionText "(Papua New Guinea) The replanting of trees in areas that did not support trees previously in living memory. Such areas include grasslands and savanna that are common in the Highlands and in the western side of the main island of New Guinea. Vitus Ambia, Papua New Guinea Forest Authority." .

:def_Afforestation_Paraguay_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Paraguay ;
    :sourceRef "cdcdpnvs@venus.pla.net.py" ;
    :definitionText "(Paraguay) Forestación: La acción de establecer bosques, con especies nativas o exóticas en terrenos que carezcan de ellas o donde son insuficientes. Ley N&deg; 536 - DE FOMENTO A LA FORESTACION Y REFORESTACION. Capítulo I. Artículo 2do. cdcdpnvs@venus.pla.net.py (Nombre Apellido)" .

:def_Afforestation_Romania_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Romania ;
    :sourceRef "Sorin Sfirlogea <sorinsf@rosilva.ro>" ;
    :definitionText "(Romania) - The act of installation, through artificial methods, of the forest vegetation on lands where forest was never present or it was removed for a long time. Sorin Sfirlogea <sorinsf@rosilva.ro National Forests Administration." .

:def_Afforestation_Taiwan_ROC_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Taiwan_ROC ;
    :sourceRef "service@dns.forest.gov.tw" ;
    :definitionText "(Taiwan, ROC) To forest in Nonforested land (grass lands or bare soil). Source: \"&ordf;L&deg;È&sect;&frac12;service\" <service@dns.forest.gov.tw" .

:def_Afforestation_United_Kingdom_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :United_Kingdom ;
    :definitionText "(United Kingdom) The new planting of bare lands with trees, usually of a substantial area. (Forestry Commission 1998)" .

:def_Afforestation_Ukraine_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Ukraine ;
    :sourceRef "Maksym Polyakov <mpoliak@pcomp.usau.kiev.ua>" ;
    :definitionText "(Ukraine) Creation of forest plantation on the lands which previously were not covered by forest. Note that ``forest plantations'' defined as ``forest stands created by planting of seedlings, saplings of trees or shrubs or by sowing of their seeds'', i.e. it here this means only origination of stands, not intensity of management. . [Source: State Standard of Ukraine, DSTU 2980-95 ``Forest plantations. Terms and definitions'', being in force since 01.01.96. From: \"Maksym Polyakov\" mpoliak@pcomp.u" .

:def_Afforestation_UNDP_1999_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :UNDP ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.un.org.vn/undp/projects/profor/pdffiles/trexler.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UNDP 1999) - Generally refers to planting of trees on ground where trees have never existed or were last present hundreds of years ago. Afforestation carbon offset projects bear an additional burden of showing ecological compatibility. http://www.un.org.vn/undp/projects/profor/pdffiles/trexler.pdf." .

:def_Afforestation_UN_DP_1999_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :UN_DP ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.profor.info/pdf/InnovatForesFinanc.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-DP 1999) Generally refers to planting of trees on ground where trees have never existed or were last present hundreds of years ago. Afforestation carbon offset projects bear an additional burden of showing ecological compatibility. http://www.profor.info/pdf/InnovatForesFinanc.pdf" .

:def_Afforestation_UN_EP_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :UN_EP ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://digitalcommons.unl.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1030&context=usdafsfacpub" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-EP 2003) - Planting of new forests on lands that historically have not contained forests. http://digitalcommons.unl.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1030&context=usdafsfacpub" .

:def_Afforestation_UNFCCC_2001_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :UNFCCC ;
    dcterms:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.unfccc.int/resource/docs/cop6secpart/l11r01.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UNFCCC 2001) “Afforestation” is the direct human-induced conversion of land that has not been forested for a period of at least 50 years to forested land through planting, seeding and/or the human-induced promotion of natural seed sources; http://www.unfccc.int/resource/docs/cop6secpart/l11r01.pdf" .

:def_Afforestation_UN_FRA_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FRA ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FRA 2000) Artificial establishment of forest on lands which previously did not carry forest within living memory. (UN-ECE/FAO 1997 and FAO 1998)" .

:def_Afforestation_USA_STATE_Maryland_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Maryland ;
    :sourceRef "http://pilot.wash.lib.md.us/washco/forestcn.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA – STATE -Maryland) The establishment of a forest, according to the definitions and procedures contained herein, on an area which is not presently in forest cover. http://pilot.wash.lib.md.us/washco/forestcn.html" .

:def_Afforestation_USA_FED_CIA_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_CIA ;
    :sourceRef "https://www.cia.gov/library/publications/the-world-factbook/docs/notesanddefs.html#2032" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-CIA) converting a bare or agricultural space by planting trees and plants; reforestation involves replanting trees on areas that have been cut or destroyed by fire. https://www.cia.gov/library/publications/the-world-factbook/docs/notesanddefs.html#2032" .

:def_Afforestation_Venezuela_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Venezuela ;
    :sourceRef "Via <Profauna@marnr.gov.ve>" ;
    :definitionText "(Venezuela) AFORESTACION: plantación de árboles en tierras que antes no tuvieron bosques, por ejemplo, en sabanas, praderas y llanos naturales. Reglamento de la Ley Forestal de Suelos y Aguas (1977). Areas Naturales Protegidas de Venezuela. Series Aspectos Conceptuales y Metodológicos, DGSPOA/ACM/01, feb 1992. Via Profauna@marnr.gov.ve" .

:def_Afforestation_WAF_2004_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :WAF ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.worldagroforestry.org/sea/Publications/files/book/BK0073-04.PDF" ;
    :definitionText "(WAF 2004) The establishment of forest on land that has been without forest for a period of time and was previously under a different land-use. http://www.worldagroforestry.org/sea/Publications/files/book/BK0073-04.PDF" .

:def_Afforestation_World_Bank_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :World_Bank ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.holz.uni-goettingen.de/ek/woodsat/pdf/worldbankforestry.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(World Bank 2000) – (Also reafforestation) Establishment of a tree crop in an area from which it has always or long been absent. . http://www.holz.uni-goettingen.de/ek/woodsat/pdf/worldbankforestry.pdf." .

:def_Afforestation_Yemen_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Yemen ;
    :sourceRef "m.ellatifi@ellatifi.8m.com" ;
    :definitionText "(Yemen) - ( Local Arabic term : Tashjeer or Tahreej) Artificial creation (by man) of a forest on an land. Mohammed Ellatifi, m.ellatifi@ellatifi.8m.com" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_005
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.deltaenviro.org.za/resources/envirofacts/afforestation.html" ;
    :definitionText "Afforestation is the planting of trees for commercial purposes, usually on land supporting non-forest veld types, e.g. grassland or fynbos. http://www.deltaenviro.org.za/resources/envirofacts/afforestation.html" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_006
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "Lorenzo Ciccarese <ciccarese@anpa.it>" ;
    :definitionText "An establishment system that consists in seeding or planting (stocking) forest trees in order to create a new forest ecosystem. Lorenzo Ciccarese ciccarese@anpa.it" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_007
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.grida.no/climate/ipcc/tectran/362.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Artificial establishment of forest stands on lands that previously have not supported forests for more than 50 years. http://www.grida.no/climate/ipcc/tectran/362.htm" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_008
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.bugwood.caes.uga.edu/glossary/" ;
    :definitionText "Conversion of bare land into forest land by planting of forest trees. http://www.bugwood.caes.uga.edu/glossary/" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_009
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.lehigh.edu/~kaf3/books/reporting/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "Conversion of bare or cultivated land into forest http://www.lehigh.edu/~kaf3/books/reporting/glossary.html" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_010
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.gcrio.org/OnLnDoc/senate_epw990603.html" ;
    :definitionText "Conversion of non-forest to forest on lands that have, historically, not contained forests and did not in 1990. http://www.gcrio.org/OnLnDoc/senate_epw990603.html" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_011
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "Maksym Polyakov <mpoliak@pcomp.usau.kiev.ua>" ;
    :definitionText "Creation of forest plantation on the lands which previously were not covered by forest. The establishment of forest stand. [Source: Act on Forests and Amendments to Some Acts (the Forest Act) dated 3 November 1995. Ministry of Agriculture of the Czech Republic. Prague, 1996. 58 pp. From: \"Maksym Polyakov\" <mpoliak@pcomp.usau.kiev.ua Date: Mon, 15 Jun 1998 11:32:47 +0300 (MSD)]" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_012
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "Lorenzo Ciccarese <ciccarese@anpa.it>" ;
    :definitionText "Creation of new forest by planting\" (Hibberd 1991a). Lorenzo Ciccarese ciccarese@anpa.it" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_013
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.plant-a-tree-today.org/webcontrol/ShowPicture.asp?Status=ShowLibraryPDF&LiId=40" ;
    :definitionText "Direct human-induced conversion of non-forested land to forested land. In the context of the Kyoto Protocol to the UNFCCC, afforestation can take place on land not covered by forest for a period of at least 50 years. http://www.plant-a-tree-today.org/webcontrol/ShowPicture.asp?Status=ShowLibraryPDF&LiId=40" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_014
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://info.sjc.ox.ac.uk/forests/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Establish a tree crop on an area which has not carried wood for some time (L, 236) http://info.sjc.ox.ac.uk/forests/glossary.htm" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_015
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "Igor Yakovlev <yakovlev@mari-el.ru>" ;
    :definitionText "Establishing new forests on lands which have not contained forests before. [From: \"Igor Yakovlev\" yakovlev@mari-el.ru Date: Wed, 10 Jun 1998 02:51:19 -0400 (EDT)]" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_016
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :definitionText "Establishing new forests on lands which, historically, have not contained forests (Schlamadinger 1998)." .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_017
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :definitionText "Establishment of forest on unforested lands or areas that have been deforested for at least 30 years (WWF/IUCN 1996)." .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_018
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://epdweb.engr.wisc.edu/dmc/courses/hazards/BB02-apx1.html" ;
    :definitionText "Forestation -- the establishment of a forest, either natural or human-made, on an area that previously have had none. http://epdweb.engr.wisc.edu/dmc/courses/hazards/BB02-apx1.html" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_019
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.usask.ca/agriculture/caedac/dbases/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Generally refers to the planting of trees on ground where trees have never existed or were last present hundreds of years ago. Afforestation carbon offset projects bear an additional burden of showing ecological compatibility. http://www.usask.ca/agriculture/caedac/dbases/glossary.htm and http://www.undp.org/seed/forest/pdf/InnovatForesFinanc.pdf." .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_020
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.forestry.gov.uk/forestry/hcou-4ubj75" ;
    :definitionText "Growing or planting of new woods or forests http://www.forestry.gov.uk/forestry/hcou-4ubj75" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_021
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://greenplanet.eolss.net/EolssLogn/mss/C09/E4-27/E4-27-08/E4-27-08-04/E4-27-08-04-TXT.aspx#Glossary_" ;
    :definitionText "Human-induced conversion of land to forest, where the land has not been forested for a period of at least fifty years. http://greenplanet.eolss.net/EolssLogn/mss/C09/E4-27/E4-27-08/E4-27-08-04/E4-27-08-04-TXT.aspx#Glossary_" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_022
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.eia.doe.gov/oiaf/1605/vr95rpt/gloss.html" ;
    :definitionText "Planting of new forests on lands that have not been recently forested. http://www.eia.doe.gov/oiaf/1605/vr95rpt/gloss.html and http://www.epa.gov/globalwarming/publications/outreach/general/glossary.pdf and http://www.theadvisorygroup.com/PDF2/publications/Carbon%20Sequestration%20Paper.pdf" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_023
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :definitionText "Planting of new forests on lands which, historically, have not contained forests. These newly created forests are included in the category Changes in Forest and Other Woody Biomass Stocks in the Land Use Change and Forestry module of the emissions inventory calculations (IPCC 1996)." .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_024
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.sfrc.ufl.edu/Extension/ssfor11.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Planting or seeding trees in an area previously devoid of trees, for example, pastures and agricultural fields. http://www.sfrc.ufl.edu/Extension/ssfor11.htm" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_025
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.rona.unep.org/action/ap1.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Planting trees where there were none before. http://www.rona.unep.org/action/ap1.htm" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_026
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://fiesta.bren.ucsb.edu/~idgec/publications/reports/forest.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Process of establishing forests on previously non-forested lands. http://fiesta.bren.ucsb.edu/~idgec/publications/reports/forest.pdf" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_027
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.graylab.ac.uk/cgi-bin/omd?afforestation" ;
    :definitionText "The act of converting into forest or woodland. http://www.graylab.ac.uk/cgi-bin/omd?afforestation" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_028
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.christiantech.com/cgi-bin/webster.exe?search_for_cgi-bin/texts/web1828=afforestation" ;
    :definitionText "The act of turning ground into forest or wood land. http://www.christiantech.com/cgi-bin/webster.exe?search_for_cgi-bin/texts/web1828=afforestation" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_029
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://harp.gsfc.nasa.gov/v0ims/glossary.of.terms.html" ;
    :definitionText "The act or process of establishing a forest especially on land not previously forested. [Source: WWWebster Dictionary and EPO. http://harp.gsfc.nasa.gov/v0ims/glossary.of.terms.html and http://www.windows.umich.edu/glossary/glossary_afforestation.html" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_030
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.doc.mmu.ac.uk/aric/diction.html" ;
    :definitionText "The conversion of non-forested areas to forest by tree planting. http://www.doc.mmu.ac.uk/aric/diction.html" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_031
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :canopyThreshold "50.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ci.rockville.md.us/cityprojects/envguide/eggloss.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The creation on a tract that is not presently in forest cover, of a biological community dominated by trees and other woody plants, at a density of at least 100 trees per acre with at least 50 percent of the trees having the capability of growing to a diameter, at 4.5 feet above the ground (diameter at breast height), of 2 inches or more within seven years. http://www.ci.rockville.md.us/cityprojects/envguide/eggloss.htm" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_032
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://europa.eu.int/comm/development/forests/en/en4_6.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The establishment of a more or less contiguous tree cover, normally by planting, in areas which have previously been without trees http://europa.eu.int/comm/development/forests/en/en4_6.htm" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_033
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dnr.state.md.us/criticalarea/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "The establishment of a tree crop on an area from which it has always or very long been absent. http://www.dnr.state.md.us/criticalarea/glossary.html" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_034
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://biology.usgs.gov/s+t/SNT/noframe/zy198.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The establishment of forest by natural succession or by the planting of trees on land where they did not grow formerly. http://biology.usgs.gov/s+t/SNT/noframe/zy198.htm" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_035
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.globalchange.org/glossall/glossa-c.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The establishment of forest cover on land not previously forested. Afforestation may be necessary to increase the net capacity of Earth's forests to absorb CO2 and other greenhouse gases (Source: Mintzer, 1992) http://www.globalchange.org/glossall/glossa-c.htm" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_036
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :definitionText "The establishment of forest on a previously non-forested site (Prüller 1998)." .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_037
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.forestry.sa.gov.au/pdf/glossary.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "The planting of a crop or plantation of trees on land not currently covered with forest. http://www.forestry.sa.gov.au/pdf/glossary.pdf" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_038
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.bugwood.caes.uga.edu/glossary/" ;
    :definitionText "The planting of a forest crop on land that has not previously, or not recently, carried a forest crop. http://www.bugwood.caes.uga.edu/glossary/" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_039
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dnr.state.md.us/criticalarea/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "The planting of open areas which are not presently in forest cover http://www.dnr.state.md.us/criticalarea/glossary.html" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_040
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.deltaenviro.org.za/resources/envirofacts/afforestation.html" ;
    :definitionText "The planting of trees for commercial purposes, usually on land supporting non-forest veld types, e.g. grassland or fynbos. Source: http://www.deltaenviro.org.za/resources/envirofacts/afforestation.html" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_041
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.wrm.org.uy/actors/WB/1991policy3.html" ;
    :definitionText "The planting of trees in unforested areas. http://www.wrm.org.uy/actors/WB/1991policy3.html" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_042
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.climateservices.com/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The planting of trees on ground where trees have never existed or were last present hundreds of years ago. Afforestation carbon offset projects bear an additional burden of showing ecological compatibility. http://www.climateservices.com/glossary.htm" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_043
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.harcourt.com/dictionary/def/2/6/7/5/267500.html" ;
    :definitionText "The process of converting bare or cultivated land into forest, by planting seeds or transplanting seedlings or mature trees. http://www.harcourt.com/dictionary/def/2/6/7/5/267500.html" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_044
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.geocities.com/RainForest/Andes/7292/Terms.html" ;
    :definitionText "To convert (open land) into a forest by planting trees http://www.geocities.com/RainForest/Andes/7292/Terms.html" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_045
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.allwords.com/query.asp#AHD" ;
    :definitionText "To convert (open land) into a forest by planting trees or their seeds. http://www.allwords.com/query.asp#AHD" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_046
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :definitionText "Upland afforestation - A sudden and fundamental change of vegetation from moorland and bog to woodland\". (Hibberd 1991b)." .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_047
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "Lorenzo Ciccarese <ciccarese@anpa.it>" ;
    :definitionText "When revegetation is established outside the forest areas (Setiadi 1996). Lorenzo Ciccarese ciccarese@anpa.it" .

:def_Afforestation_Austria_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :Austria ;
    :sourceRef "Weiss Peter <weissp@ubavie.gv.at>" ;
    :definitionText "(Austria) (Neubewaldung) - A land use change from different uses to forests. Both natural regeneration and artificial planting count as afforestation. (Austrian Forestry Act (Federal Legal Gazette no. 440/1975, as amended Federal Legal Gazette 231/1977, 142/1978 and 576/1987) From: Weiss Peter weissp@ubavie.gv.at)" .

:def_Afforestation_Canada_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :Canada ;
    :sourceRef "http://nrcan.gc.ca/cfs/proj/ppiab/sof/sof.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada) The establishment of a tree crop on an area from which it has always or very long been absent. Where such establishment fails and is repeated, the latter may properly be termed \"reafforestation\". (http://nrcan.gc.ca/cfs/proj/ppiab/sof/sof.html)" .

:def_Afforestation_Denmark_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :Denmark ;
    :sourceRef "PMP@sns.dk" ;
    :definitionText "(Denmark) Planting of agriculture-land with a forest obligation written in the cadastre. (From: PMP@sns.dk Date: Tue, 29 Sep 1998 09:31:59 +0100)" .

:def_Afforestation_EU_2013_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :EU ;
    dcterms:date "2013"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32013D0529" ;
    :definitionText "(EU 2013) ‘afforestation’ means the direct human-induced conversion of land that has not been forest for a period of at least 50 years to forest through planting, seeding and/or the human-induced promotion of natural seed sources, where the conversion has taken place after 31 December 1989; http://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32013D0529" .

:def_Afforestation_Italy_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :Italy ;
    :sourceRef "Biometria <isafa.biofor@tqs.it>" ;
    :definitionText "(Italy) (rimboschimento) - Outplanting forest stock on areas previously managed for other uses (agricultural lands, barren lands, etc.) (ISTAT). 'Imboschimento'(afforestation) is used very seldom. From: Vittorio Tosi ISAFA Biometria <isafa.biofor@tqs.it and Lorenzo Ciccarese ciccarese@anpa.it ISTAT (1950-1997). Statistiche Forestali. Annuari 1-47. Istituto Nazionale di Statistica. Rome." .

:def_Afforestation_St_Lucia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :St_Lucia ;
    :sourceRef "chiefforest@maffe.org" ;
    :definitionText "(St. Lucia) The planting of forest tree species in an area which was not occupied by forest before. (Source: Michael Andrew, chiefforest@maffe.org)" .

:def_Afforestation_UN_FAO_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO) The establishment of a tree crop on an area from which it has always or very long been absent. Where such establishment fails and is repeated, the latter may properly be termed reafforestation (FAO 1997)." .

:def_Afforestation_UN_FAO_2001_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 2001) Afforestation is the conversion from other land uses into forest, or the increase of the canopy cover to above the 10% threshold. Explanatory note (extract): Afforestation is the reverse of deforestation and includes areas that are actively converted from other land uses into forest through silvicultural measures. Afforestation also includes natural transitions into forest, for example on abandoned agricultural land or in burnt-over areas that have not been classified as forest dur" .

:def_Afforestation_USA_FED_DA_FS_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_FS ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-FS) Establishment of forest crops by artificial methods, such as planting or sowing on land where trees have never grown. [Source: Timber Harvesting and Engineering Glossary, USFS]" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_048
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :definitionText "Artificial establishment by planting or seeding of forest on a non-forest area (e.g. agricultural or other land). [Source: UN/ECE 1990, via Brita Pajari]" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_049
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://epdweb.engr.wisc.edu/dmc/courses/hazards/BB02-apx1.html" ;
    :definitionText "Establishment of a tree crop in an area where trees have always or long been absent. http://epdweb.engr.wisc.edu/dmc/courses/hazards/BB02-apx1.html and http://dnr.state.il.us/legal/1537.htm" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_050
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://solstice.crest.org/social/SJ-glossary/A.html#" ;
    :definitionText "Forest crops established by purposeful planting on land previously not used for tree crops. http://solstice.crest.org/social/SJ-glossary/A.html#" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_051
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.state.nv.us/cnr/ndwp/dict-1/WORD_A.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The artificial establishment of forest crops by planting or sowing on land that has not previously, or recently, grown trees. http://www.state.nv.us/cnr/ndwp/dict-1/WORD_A.htm" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_052
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :definitionText "The establishment of a forest or stand in an area where the preceding vegetation or land use was not forest (Helms 1998)." .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_053
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :definitionText "The establishment of a forest or stand of trees by sowing, planting, or natural regeneration on an area not previously forested, or in areas where forests were cleared long ago and other land-use patterns have dominated the landscape for many generations (e.g., the moorlands of Great Britain) (Dunster and Dunster 1996)." .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_054
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.shsu.edu/~chemistry/Glossary/a.html#A" ;
    :definitionText "The process or act of changing land into forest by planting trees, seeding, etc. on land formerly used for something other than forestry. This can obviously be contrasted with deforestation. [American Forestry; v100; 23-25; 1994.] [New Scientist; v143; 30-35; 1994.] http://www.shsu.edu/~chemistry/Glossary/a.html#A" .

:def_Afforestation_Unknown_nd_055
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Afforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :definitionText "To produce a forest product \"crop\" on lands that previously have not supported forests for more than 50 years. IPPC Guidelines." .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.cgiar.org/cifor/publications/occpaper/occpaper9.html" ;
    :definitionText "Definitions are grouped depending on if they are changes in land cover, land use, or both. Additional discussions of the meaning of \"deforestation\" may be found in Sunderlin, William D.; Resosudarmo, Ida Aju Pradnja. Rate and Causes of Deforestation in Indonesia: Towards a Resolution of the Ambiguities. http://www.cgiar.org/cifor/publications/occpaper/occpaper9.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :sourceRef "http://info.sjc.ox.ac.uk/forests/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Disafforest - Free forest land from the operation of forest law (to be distinguished from ‘deforest’, q.v.) (P 205); remove an area of land from the constraints of forest law (R 166); release land from forest law (L 237) http://info.sjc.ox.ac.uk/forests/glossary.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :Administrative ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.hants.gov.uk/newforest/bibliog.html" ;
    :definitionText "Disafforestation – to remove land from the authority of the Verderers. http://www.hants.gov.uk/newforest/bibliog.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Australia_NSW_EPA_1995_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Australia_NSW_EPA ;
    dcterms:date "1995"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfcccbali.org/unfccc/component/option" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia – NSW-EPA 1995). The removal of forest and undergrowth (NSW-EPA, 1995) http://unfcccbali.org/unfccc/component/option,com_glossary/Itemid,100/func,display/letter,D/catid,31/page,1/" .

:def_Deforestation_Bolivia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Bolivia ;
    :sourceRef "Luis Castello <faopaf@caoba.entelnet.bo>" ;
    :definitionText "(Bolivia) DEFORESTADO: Desprovisto de bosque, por haber talado. Source: Luis Castello faopaf@caoba.entelnet.bo Adjunto sírvase encontrar la versión no oficial y premilinar del Glosario Forestal elaborado por el Proyecto de Apoyo a la Coordinación e Implementación del Plan de Acción Forestal para Bolivia." .

:def_Deforestation_Bulgaria_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Bulgaria ;
    :sourceRef "Forest Research Institute <forestin@bulnet.bg>" ;
    :definitionText "(Bulgaria) Deforestation - destruction of the forests on certain area under the influence of natural disasters, uncontrolled or planned (final cuttings) human activities. This term is not defined in the forestry law. Forest Research Institute forestin@bulnet.bg" .

:def_Deforestation_Canada_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Canada ;
    :sourceRef "http://carbon.cfs.nrcan.gc.ca/definitions_e.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada) Deforestation - The conversion of forested land to nonforested land as a direct result of human activities. http://carbon.cfs.nrcan.gc.ca/definitions_e.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Canada_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Canada ;
    :sourceRef "http://environment.nelson.com/glossary.html#D" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada) To clear an area of forests or trees, usually for commercial use of the lumber or agricultural use of the land. http://environment.nelson.com/glossary.html#D" .

:def_Deforestation_Cape_Verde_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Cape_Verde ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.indexmundi.com/cape_verde/environment_current_issues.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Cape Verde) Deforestation - the destruction of vast areas of forest (e.g., unsustainable forestry practices, agricultural and range land clearing, and the over exploitation of wood products for use as fuel) without planting new growth. http://www.indexmundi.com/cape_verde/environment_current_issues.html" .

:def_Deforestation_EC_2008_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :EC ;
    dcterms:date "2008"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://ec.europa.eu/environment/forests/deforestation.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(EC 2008) Deforestation is the permanent destruction of forests and woodlands. http://ec.europa.eu/environment/forests/deforestation.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_EC_DGVIII_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :EC_DGVIII ;
    :sourceRef "http://europa.eu.int/comm/dg08/forests/en/en4_6.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(EC-DGVIII) The depletion of tree crown cover to less than 10 per cent http://europa.eu.int/comm/dg08/forests/en/en4_6.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Fiji_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Fiji ;
    :definitionText "(Fiji) Removal of forested areas. Malakai Sevudredre, Conservator of Forests, F.9641/2. 01/06/2000." .

:def_Deforestation_France_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :France ;
    :sourceRef "Michel Godron <michel.godron@libertysurf.fr>" ;
    :definitionText "(France) deforestation = déforestation = déboisement = essartage (autrefois) = défrichement (mais ce terme est souvent plus vague) : destruction durable d'une forêt \"Michel Godron\" michel.godron@libertysurf.fr" .

:def_Deforestation_Ghana_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Ghana ;
    :definitionText "(Ghana) A process whereby trees are forests are removed or degraded through a variety of activities by man. A typical example is exploitation of timber. (Osei Kofi, Forestry Dept.- Letter 7 May 99)" .

:def_Deforestation_Global_Forest_Watch_2014_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Global_Forest_Watch ;
    dcterms:date "2014"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.globalforestwatch.org/howto#terminology" ;
    :definitionText "(Global Forest Watch 2014) - Deforestation - How one defines “deforestation” is dependent on how one defines “forest.” As noted above, various definitions of forest exist and GFW does not aim to provide a consensus view. Correspondingly, GFW does not provide a single definition for “deforestation.” In general writing, GFW uses “deforestation” to refer to the removal of a significant number of trees from a landscape, typically in the context of human actions rather than natural events such as fir" .

:def_Deforestation_ICRAF_2017_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :ICRAF ;
    dcterms:date "2017"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://dx.doi.org/10.5716/WP16079.PDF" ;
    :definitionText "(ICRAF- 2017) Change from a forested to a non-forested state, which depending on forest definition, relates to both institutional and tree cover dimensions http://dx.doi.org/10.5716/WP16079.PDF" .

:def_Deforestation_Indonesia_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Indonesia ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://redd.unfccc.int/files/national_frel_for_redd__in_indonesia_2015.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Indonesia 2009) Minister of Forestry No. 30/2009 that stated deforestation as the permanent alteration from forested area into a non-forested area as a result of human activities (MoFor, 2009). http://redd.unfccc.int/files/national_frel_for_redd__in_indonesia_2015.pdf and https://www.elaw.org/system/files/REDD_PERMENHUT_P-30-2009_BILINGUAL.pdf" .

:def_Deforestation_Indonesia_2015_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Indonesia ;
    dcterms:date "2015"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://redd.unfccc.int/files/national_frel_for_redd__in_indonesia_2015.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Indonesia 2015) In this submission, deforestation was defined as a conversion of natural forest cover into other land-cover categories that has only occurred one time in particular areas. The practical definition emphasises on land cover instead of land use. Consequently it is different from the definition of deforestation by FAO, which employed terminology of land use. http://redd.unfccc.int/files/national_frel_for_redd__in_indonesia_2015.pdf" .

:def_Deforestation_IPCC_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :IPCC ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.junkscience.com/draft_AR4/GLOSSARY_SOD_TSU_FINAL.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(IPCC - 2003) Deforestation - Conversion of forest to non-forest. For a discussion of the term →forest and related terms such as →afforestation, →reforestation, and deforestation: see the IPCC Report on Land Use, Land-Use Change and Forestry (IPCC, 2000). See also the Report on Definitions and Methodological Options to Inventory Emissions from Direct Human-induced Degradation of Forests and Devegetation of Other Vegetation Types (IPCC, 2003). (Source: Second Order Draft Glossary IPCC WGI Fourth " .

:def_Deforestation_Kenya_2005_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Kenya ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://formin.finland.fi/public/download.aspx?ID=15959&GUID=%7B88EFD0B8-9F47-4528-A24F-66DDE0CFE370%7D" ;
    :definitionText "(Kenya 2005) Deforestation means the negative reduction of forest cover from the original status. http://formin.finland.fi/public/download.aspx?ID=15959&GUID=%7B88EFD0B8-9F47-4528-A24F-66DDE0CFE370%7D" .

:def_Deforestation_Mexico_2014_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Mexico ;
    dcterms:date "2014"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://redd.unfccc.int/files/frel_mexico_modified.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Mexico 2014) The General Law for the Sustainable Development of Forests indicates that deforestation refers to \"the process of reducing the capacity of ecosystems to provide environmental services and to produce goods.\" In the context climate change mitigation in Mexico, forests are considered a regulator of the carbon cycle. http://redd.unfccc.int/files/frel_mexico_modified.pdf" .

:def_Deforestation_Morocco_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Morocco ;
    :sourceRef "m.ellatifi@ellatifi.8m.com" ;
    :definitionText "(Morocco) Deforestation (Arabic : Zawal Al Ghabah, French : Déforestation, Spanish : deforestacion) – Aggression (negative action) leading to the removal of trees and stands from the forest. This agreesion, if not stopped in time, could put in jeopardy the preservation of the forest. The cause could be anthropic (cutting), fire (burning), or livestock (overgrazing). Mohammed Ellatifi, m.ellatifi@ellatifi.8m.com" .

:def_Deforestation_Nepal_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Nepal ;
    :sourceRef "Gautam <khg13@student.canterbury.ac.nz>" ;
    :definitionText "(Nepal) deforestation = reduction of stocking due to overcutting for fuelwood, timber, and fodder (from Master plan for the forestry sector Nepal, main report, 1988). Krishna H Gautam <khg13@student.canterbury.ac.nz" .

:def_Deforestation_Northern_Mariana_Islands_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Northern_Mariana_Islands ;
    :sourceRef "Estanislao Villagomez <stanvill@gtepacifica.net>" ;
    :definitionText "(Northern Mariana Islands) Deforestation - A science and are of harvesting or act of destroying a forestland to meet a particular objective. Source: Estanislao Villagomez stanvill@gtepacifica.net Division of Agriculture." .

:def_Deforestation_Pakistan_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Pakistan ;
    :definitionText "(Pakistan) To remove, kill or destroy all or most of the trees of a forest so that reproduction is impossible except by artificial means. Definition adopted from the British Commonwealth Forest Terminology Part-I, 1953. Source: Mumtaz Ahmad, Section Forest Officer, Pakistan Min. of Environment, Local Government, and Rural Development." .

:def_Deforestation_Philippines_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Philippines ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nscb.gov.ph/ru12/DEFINE/DEF-ENV.HTM" ;
    :definitionText "(Philippines) - The destruction of forest trees in such a manner as to leave practically little or no chance at all of normal recovery for a forest. Some of the factors responsible for the destruction of forest products include: illegal loggers, illegal forestry product gatherers, timber smugglers, kaingeros, squatters, forest incendiaries, miners, atmospheric agents, biological agents. http://www.nscb.gov.ph/ru12/DEFINE/DEF-ENV.HTM" .

:def_Deforestation_Philippines_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Philippines ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nscb.gov.ph/ru12/DEFINE/DEF-ENV.HTM" ;
    :definitionText "(Philippines) Deforested Area - the area which has been denuded but has not been reforested as of the end of the reference year. http://www.nscb.gov.ph/ru12/DEFINE/DEF-ENV.HTM" .

:def_Deforestation_Romania_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Romania ;
    :sourceRef "Sorin Sfirlogea <sorinsf@rosilva.ro>" ;
    :definitionText "(Romania) - The act of removing the forest vegetation from forest lands, without changing the land destination (considering the administrative point of view). Sorin Sfirlogea <sorinsf@rosilva.ro National Forests Administration." .

:def_Deforestation_South_Sudan_2009_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :South_Sudan ;
    dcterms:date "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(South Sudan 2009) “Deforestation” means reduction of forest cover from the original status;" .

:def_Deforestation_St_Lucia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :St_Lucia ;
    :sourceRef "chiefforest@maffe.org" ;
    :definitionText "(St. Lucia) The cutting down of forest or destruction of forests. (Source: Michael Andrew, chiefforest@maffe.org)" .

:def_Deforestation_Taiwan_ROC_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Taiwan_ROC ;
    :sourceRef "service@dns.forest.gov.tw" ;
    :definitionText "(Taiwan, ROC) The behavior and activity of destroy forest, included forest fire, disease, insect pest, illegal cutting and illegal cultivation. Source: \"&ordf;L&deg;È&sect;&frac12;service\" service@dns.forest.gov.tw" .

:def_Deforestation_Uganda_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Uganda ;
    :sourceRef "Paolo Viskanic <viskanic@imul.com>" ;
    :definitionText "(Uganda) - When the biomass abstracted is higher than the natural growth. The Environmental Act (1995). Paolo Viskanic viskanic@imul.com." .

:def_Deforestation_UN_DP_1999_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :UN_DP ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.un.org.vn/undp/projects/profor/pdffiles/trexler.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-DP 1999) The conversion of forested to non-forested land. Deforestation can involve the cutting and burning of trees to provide land for agricultural purposes or clearing for residential and industrial uses. http://www.un.org.vn/undp/projects/profor/pdffiles/trexler.pdf .and http://www.profor.info/pdf/InnovatForesFinanc.pdf" .

:def_Deforestation_UN_EP_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :UN_EP ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nyo.unep.org/action/ap1.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-EP) The felling of trees, usually for commercial purposes. http://www.nyo.unep.org/action/ap1.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_UN_FAO_1998_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "1998"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfcccbali.org/unfccc/component/option" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 1998) Refers to change of land cover with depletion of tree crown cover to less than 10%. Changes within the forest class (e.g. from closed to open forest) which negatively affect the stand or site and, in particular, lower the production capacity, are termed forest degradation http://unfcccbali.org/unfccc/component/option,com_glossary/Itemid,100/func,display/letter,D/catid,31/page,1/." .

:def_Deforestation_UN_FAO_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://faov02.fao.org:70/0gopher_root%3a[fao.fra" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO) and (EU) The depletion of forest crown cover to less than 10%. [Source: from http://faov02.fao.org:70/0gopher_root%3a[fao.fra]def_uk.txt (concepts, definitions and methodology of the FAO Forest Resources Assessment 1990) via Bernhard Schlamadinger] http://europa.eu.int/comm/development/forests/en/en4_6.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_UN_FAO_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    :canopyThreshold "20.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO) Developed countries: Change of forest with depletion of tree crown cover to less than 20 percent (FAO 1997)." .

:def_Deforestation_UN_FAO_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO) Developing countries: Change of forest with depletion of tree crown cover to less than 10 percent (FAO 1997)." .

:def_Deforestation_UN_FCCC_2001_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FCCC ;
    dcterms:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.unfccc.int/resource/docs/cop6secpart/l11r01.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FCCC 2001) - the direct human-induced conversion of forested land to nonforested land. Decision 11/CP.7 ftp://ftp.fao.org/docrep/fao/009/j9345e/j9345e00.pdf and http://www.unfccc.int/resource/docs/cop6secpart/l11r01.pdf" .

:def_Deforestation_UN_FCCC_2006_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FCCC ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.iop.org/EJ/article/1748-9326/3/2/025011/erl8_2_025011.pdf?request-id=dc893ad1-7028-4e4a-a91d-c44bc540a975" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FCCC 2006) A ‘measurable sustained decrease in crown cover’ below a 10–30% threshold. http://www.iop.org/EJ/article/1748-9326/3/2/025011/erl8_2_025011.pdf?request-id=dc893ad1-7028-4e4a-a91d-c44bc540a975" .

:def_Deforestation_UN_FRA_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FRA ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FRA 2000) Refers to change of land cover with depletion of tree crown cover to less than 10 percent. Changes within the forest class (e.g. from closed to open forest) which negatively affect the stand or site and, in particular, lower the production capacity, are termed forest degradation. (UN-ECE/FAO 1997 and FAO 1998)" .

:def_Deforestation_UN_HCR_2005_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :UN_HCR ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://postconflict.unep.ch/liberia/displacement/documents/UNHCR_IUCN_Forest_Management_Refugee_Returnee_Situations.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-HCR 2005) The depletion of tree crown cover to less than 10 per cent. http://postconflict.unep.ch/liberia/displacement/documents/UNHCR_IUCN_Forest_Management_Refugee_Returnee_Situations.pdf UNHCR 2005." .

:def_Deforestation_USA_EIA_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :USA_EIA ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.eia.gov/tools/glossary/index.cfm?id=D" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-EIA) The net removal of trees from forested land. http://www.eia.gov/tools/glossary/index.cfm?id=D" .

:def_Deforestation_USA_FED_CIA_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_CIA ;
    :sourceRef "https://www.cia.gov/cia/publications/factbook/docs/notesanddefs.html#2032" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-CIA) Tthe destruction of vast areas of forest (e.g., unsustainable forestry practices, agricultural and range land clearing, and the over exploitation of wood products for use as fuel) without planting new growth. https://www.cia.gov/cia/publications/factbook/docs/notesanddefs.html#2032" .

:def_Deforestation_USA_FED_EPA_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_EPA ;
    :sourceRef "http://homeguides.sfgate.com/deforestation-effects-global-scale-78864.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-EPA) Deforestation is the \"permanent removal of standing forests. http://homeguides.sfgate.com/deforestation-effects-global-scale-78864.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Venezuela_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Venezuela ;
    :sourceRef "Via <Profauna@marnr.gov.ve>" ;
    :definitionText "(Venezuela) DEFORESTACION: eliminar por métodos mecánicos la vegetación alta y mediana para erradicarla totalmente (1); tala de un bosque con el propósito de habilitar la tiera,para uso agrícola o ganadero y/o aprovechar la madera para la construcción o propósitos industriales. Reglamento de la Ley Forestal de Suelos y Aguas (1977). Areas Naturales Protegidas de Venezuela. Series Aspectos Conceptuales y Metodológicos, DGSPOA/ACM/01, feb 1992. Via Profauna@marnr.gov.ve" .

:def_Deforestation_World_Bank_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :World_Bank ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.holz.uni-goettingen.de/ek/woodsat/pdf/worldbankforestry.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(World Bank 2000) Change of forest with depletion of tree crown cover to less than 10 percent. The clearing of forests and the conversion of land to non-forest uses. . http://www.holz.uni-goettingen.de/ek/woodsat/pdf/worldbankforestry.pdf." .

:def_Deforestation_Yemen_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Yemen ;
    :sourceRef "m.ellatifi@ellatifi.8m.com" ;
    :definitionText "(Yemen) Deforestation (Arabic : Zawal Al Ghabah, French : Déforestation, Spanish : deforestacion) – Aggression (negative action) leading to the removal of trees and stands from the forest. This agreesion, if not stopped in time, could put in jeopardy the preservation of the forest. The cause could be anthropic (cutting), fire (burning), or livestock (overgrazing). Mohammed Ellatifi, m.ellatifi@ellatifi.8m.com" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :definitionText "A change from forest cover into some other land cover formations, without the revival of forests by natural or artificial reforestation within a human planning horizon (Palo 1999)." .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_005
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.sprl.umich.edu/GCL/notes2/Deforestation.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "A complete and permanent removal of all forest cover. http://www.sprl.umich.edu/GCL/notes2/Deforestation.pdf" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_006
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://science.howstuffworks.com/environmental/conservation/issues/what-is-deforestation.htm" ;
    :definitionText "A fancy word that means exactly what you probably think it means: the destruction of forested lands. http://science.howstuffworks.com/environmental/conservation/issues/what-is-deforestation.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_007
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://cbmjournal.springeropen.com/articles/10.1186/s13021-016-0054-9" ;
    :definitionText "A long term loss of canopy cover and area, notably a conversion to another non-forest use, which been monitored effectively over time at multiple scales effectively for tropical forests using remote sensing technologies . http://cbmjournal.springeropen.com/articles/10.1186/s13021-016-0054-9" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_008
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :definitionText "A reduccion de areas arbolades (Bosques y Selvas) (Herrera 1999)." .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_009
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.spcforests.org/Library/usestatus/usestatus.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Changes of land use which lead to a depletion of tree crown to less than 10% (this definition relates to the definition of forests as ecosystems with a minimum 10% cover of trees). (FAO, 1990) http://www.spcforests.org/Library/usestatus/usestatus.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_010
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.oldhamagenda21.demon.co.uk/Plan/Glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Chopping down the natural forest of an area …. http://www.oldhamagenda21.demon.co.uk/Plan/Glossary.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_011
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.devon.gov.uk/agenda21/glossary.html#terminology" ;
    :definitionText "Clearing land and trees http://www.devon.gov.uk/agenda21/glossary.html#terminology" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_012
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ran.org/kids_action/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "Clearing land of trees by cutting or burning. http://www.ran.org/kids_action/glossary.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_013
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.schools.wafa.org.au/terms.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Clearing trees for timber, fuel, farmland or for new settlements from a piece of land without the intention of reforesting. http://www.schools.wafa.org.au/terms.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_014
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.gardenweb.com/glossary/deforestation" ;
    :definitionText "Clearing trees from a woodland, often done to promote food for wildlife as well as to provide timber. http://www.gardenweb.com/glossary/deforestation" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_015
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.isabelperez.com/select/forest.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Cutting down trees is called deforestation. http://www.isabelperez.com/select/forest.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_016
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.wisegeek.com/what-is-hard-deforestation.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Deforestation (Soft) happens when trees are cleared, but they later grow back. http://www.wisegeek.com/what-is-hard-deforestation.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_017
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.trfic.msu.edu/data_portal/Landsat7doc/defor_fact.html" ;
    :definitionText "Deforestation (Tropical) - The clearing of tropical forests across the Earth http://www.trfic.msu.edu/data_portal/Landsat7doc/defor_fact.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_018
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.globaled.org/issues/152/a.html" ;
    :definitionText "Deforestation includes the destruction of forests…as well as woodlands…. The term deforestation does not apply to the removal of trees from plantations or industrial forests. http://www.globaled.org/issues/152/a.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_019
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.globaled.org/issues/152/a.html" ;
    :definitionText "Deforestation involves the permanent destruction of indigenous forests and woodlands. . http://www.globaled.org/issues/152/a.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_020
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://curiosity.discovery.com/question/deforestation-biggest-threat-biodiversity" ;
    :definitionText "Deforestation is just what it sounds like: the destruction of large areas of forest lands or rainforests. http://curiosity.discovery.com/question/deforestation-biggest-threat-biodiversity" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_021
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://wiki.answers.com/Q/What_is_deforestation?altQ=What_is_deforrestation#slide=1" ;
    :definitionText "Deforestation is people cutting down whole forests of trees, and making it even less likely for humans to survive. http://wiki.answers.com/Q/What_is_deforestation?altQ=What_is_deforrestation#slide=1" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_022
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.s-cool.co.uk/a-level/biology/ecological-concepts/revise-it/human-effects-on-the-environment" ;
    :definitionText "Deforestation is the rapid destruction of woodland. Although it can occur due to natural catastrophe it is most commonly caused by human intervention. http://www.s-cool.co.uk/a-level/biology/ecological-concepts/revise-it/human-effects-on-the-environment" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_023
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://eschooltoday.com/forests/what-is-deforestation.html" ;
    :definitionText "Deforestation is when humans remove or clear large areas of forest lands for non-forest use. These include clearing for farming purposes, ranching and urban use. In these cases, trees are never re-planted. http://eschooltoday.com/forests/what-is-deforestation.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_024
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://answers.ask.com/Science/Other/what_is_deforestation" ;
    :definitionText "Deforestation is when trees are cut down or cleared out. Deforestation is becoming a large problem in rain forest areas, because the trees that are cut down for use aren't being replaced. http://answers.ask.com/Science/Other/what_is_deforestation" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_025
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.hq.nasa.gov/iwgsdi/ISS_SDI_Land_Use.html" ;
    :definitionText "Deforestation Rate (396 UN CSD) - Area of forest harvested per year for lumber http://www.hq.nasa.gov/iwgsdi/ISS_SDI_Land_Use.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_026
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.unredd.net/index.php?option=com_docman&task=doc_download&gid=7437&Itemid=53" ;
    :definitionText "Deforestation: this involves a decrease in the area covered by forest. However, it cannot be so defined without adding a reference to its use (or allocation). In point of fact, there exist certain forms of forest utilization - and priority objectives of forest management - that clear temporarily the forest cover while guaranteeing its maintenance. This is the case of clearcutting of areas where forest will regenerate itself or be regenerated, or of the final cut in an even-aged forest sylvicultu" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_027
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :definitionText "Destruction of forest for timber, fuel, charcoal burning, and clearing for agriculture and extractive industries such as mining without planting new trees to replace those lost (reafforestation) or working on a cycle that allows natural forest to regenerate (Lindley and Moore 1998)." .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_028
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.climnet.org/CAN_2008_sep_LCA_REDD.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Direct, human-induced conversion of natural forest to non-forest land or plantation. The canopy cover threshold, demarcating the transition from native forest to non-forest land, should be defined for specific forest ecosystems. http://www.climnet.org/CAN_2008_sep_LCA_REDD.pdf" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_029
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.notredame.ac.jp/cgi-bin/wn?deforestation" ;
    :definitionText "Disforestation -- the removal of trees. http://www.notredame.ac.jp/cgi-bin/wn?deforestation" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_030
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://p5uni.ii.pw.edu.pl/infterra/" ;
    :definitionText "Forest cover destruction Source: Infoterra Thesaurus http://p5uni.ii.pw.edu.pl/infterra/" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_031
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.oznet.ksu.edu/library/MISC2/SB661.PDF" ;
    :definitionText "Forest loss; typically defined as a forest losing 40 percent or more of the trees. http://www.oznet.ksu.edu/library/MISC2/SB661.PDF" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_032
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://wings.ucdavis.edu/Book/Atmosphere/beginner/deforestation-01.html" ;
    :definitionText "Happens when people cut down forests or when trees are burned. http://wings.ucdavis.edu/Book/Atmosphere/beginner/deforestation-01.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_033
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.wrm.org.uy/oldsite/deforestation/Africa/Gambia.html" ;
    :definitionText "In simple terms, can be the gradual reduction of the stocking of the vegetation cover resulting from human activities. http://www.wrm.org.uy/oldsite/deforestation/Africa/Gambia.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_034
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.undp.org.vn/undp/docs/2002/DevGlossary.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Loss of forest cover from 40% of the trees or more. http://www.undp.org.vn/undp/docs/2002/DevGlossary.pdf" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_035
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.hq.nasa.gov/iwgsdi/ISS_SDI_Land_Use.html" ;
    :definitionText "Loss of forest land due to logging, disease, or infestation http://www.hq.nasa.gov/iwgsdi/ISS_SDI_Land_Use.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_036
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.globalchange.org/glossall/glossa-c.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Loss of forest. (Source: Mintzer, 1992). http://www.globalchange.org/glossall/glossa-c.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_037
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.oup-usa.org/reference/globalchange/amazonia.html" ;
    :definitionText "Loss of primary (sometimes called mature, virgin, or old-growth) forest. http://www.oup-usa.org/reference/globalchange/amazonia.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_038
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.chevron.com//COMMUNITY/EDUCATION/GREENHOUSE/GLOSSARY.SHTML" ;
    :definitionText "Massive destruction of the world's forests through logging, burning and other human activities. http://www.chevron.com//COMMUNITY/EDUCATION/GREENHOUSE/GLOSSARY.SHTML" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_039
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.cifor.cgiar.org/publications/pdf_files/SPubs/SP-LStock-n.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "More or less permanent removal of most of the natural tree cover from an area. http://www.cifor.cgiar.org/publications/pdf_files/SPubs/SP-LStock-n.pdf" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_040
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.soton.ac.uk/~engenvir/glossary.html#def" ;
    :definitionText "Permanent clearance of trees and woodland. http://www.soton.ac.uk/~engenvir/glossary.html#def" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_041
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.cifor.org/publications/html/occpaper9/chapter6.html" ;
    :definitionText "Permanent forest cover removal - http://www.cifor.org/publications/html/occpaper9/chapter6.html." .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_042
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fs.fed.us/institute/cifor/cifor_260.html" ;
    :definitionText "Rate and total area of forest land converted to non-forest land cover, classed by major forest type http://www.fs.fed.us/institute/cifor/cifor_260.html." .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_043
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.gsu.edu/~mstnrhx/ecogloss.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Removal of trees from a forested area without adequate replanting. http://www.gsu.edu/~mstnrhx/ecogloss.htm and http://ecology.org/biod/library/glos_index.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_044
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.npwrc.usgs.gov/resource/literatr/avian/avian.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Removal of trees from a forested area without adequate replanting or natural regeneration (Miller 1991:A6). http://www.npwrc.usgs.gov/resource/literatr/avian/avian.htm Glossary of Avian Terms For Use in Avian Conservation Biology" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_045
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.gsu.edu/~mstnrhx/ecogloss.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Removal of trees from a forested area without adequate replanting. http://www.gsu.edu/~mstnrhx/ecogloss.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_046
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.geog.ouc.bc.ca/physgeog/physgeoglos/d.html" ;
    :definitionText "Removal of trees from a habitat dominated by forest. http://www.geog.ouc.bc.ca/physgeog/physgeoglos/d.html and http://www.physicalgeography.net/physgeoglos/d.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_047
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.geog.psu.edu/courses/geog103/SUSDEV1.html" ;
    :definitionText "Removal of trees from an area without adequate replanting http://www.geog.psu.edu/courses/geog103/SUSDEV1.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_048
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deforestation" ;
    :definitionText "Removal of trees, often as a result of human activities. http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deforestation" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_049
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://school.discovery.com/lessonplans/programs/geo_mexico/" ;
    :definitionText "The act of cutting down forests in large swathes http://school.discovery.com/lessonplans/programs/geo_mexico/" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_050
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://oald8.oxfordlearnersdictionaries.com/dictionary/deforestation" ;
    :definitionText "The act of cutting down or burning the trees in an area http://oald8.oxfordlearnersdictionaries.com/dictionary/deforestation" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_051
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.createqrcodes.org/deforestation-and-the-environment.html" ;
    :definitionText "The act of cutting down trees and clearing forests in order to benefit people. http://www.createqrcodes.org/deforestation-and-the-environment.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_052
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.epa.gov/ceisweb1/ceishome/atlas/ohiolandchange/ohiolandchangeglossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "The act of removing forests from an area in favor of another land cover type, often agriculture or urban. In many areas forests are cut down to obtain lumber. http://www.epa.gov/ceisweb1/ceishome/atlas/ohiolandchange/ohiolandchangeglossary.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_053
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/deforestation" ;
    :definitionText "The act or result of cutting down or burning all the trees in an area http://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/deforestation" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_054
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.m-w.com/cgi-bin/dictionary?book=Dictionary&va=deforestation" ;
    :definitionText "The action or process of clearing of forests. The state of having been cleared of forest. [Source: WWWebster Dictionary] http://www.m-w.com/cgi-bin/dictionary?book=Dictionary&va=deforestation" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_055
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.aloha.net/~ani/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "The burning and bulldozing of trees for the purpose of lumber, agriculture, or ranching. http://www.aloha.net/~ani/glossary.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_056
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ask.com/question/what-is-deforestation" ;
    :definitionText "The burning and logging of trees in the forest. It kills animals and destroys habitats. http://www.ask.com/question/what-is-deforestation" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_057
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :definitionText "The change from forest cover into some other land cover formation without the planned revival of forests by natural or artificial reforestation. (Wardle et al. 2003)." .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_058
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.wfmz.com/weather/What-is-deforestation/180118" ;
    :definitionText "The clearing Earth's forests on a massive scale, often resulting in damage to the quality of the land. http://www.wfmz.com/weather/What-is-deforestation/180118" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_059
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://epdweb.engr.wisc.edu/dmc/courses/hazards/BB02-apx1.html" ;
    :definitionText "The clearing of a previously forested area. Though humans are the primary deforesters, natural agents, such as volcanic eruptions, erosion, and landslides may also contribute. Clear cutting, if followed by reforestation, is not an act of deforestation. http://epdweb.engr.wisc.edu/dmc/courses/hazards/BB02-apx1.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_060
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.cobeconet.com/resources/worldbank/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "The clearing of forested land. http://www.cobeconet.com/resources/worldbank/glossary.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_061
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ask.com/question/what-is-deforestation" ;
    :definitionText "The clearing of forests mainly by human activity, which results in the damage to the quality of the land. Forests are cut down in the process ... http://www.ask.com/question/what-is-deforestation" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_062
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://lifestyle.iloveindia.com/lounge/what-is-deforestation-11731.html" ;
    :definitionText "The clearing of forests mainly due to human activity by the process of logging or burning - http://lifestyle.iloveindia.com/lounge/what-is-deforestation-11731.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_063
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.unisdr.org/unisdr/glossaire.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The clearing or destruction of a previously forested area. http://www.unisdr.org/unisdr/glossaire.htm and http://www.reliefweb.int/library/mcda/refman/glossary.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_064
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://info.live58.org/why-should-i-care-about-deforestation/" ;
    :definitionText "The clearing the earth’s forest on a massive scale, resulting in damage to the quality of the land. http://info.live58.org/why-should-i-care-about-deforestation/" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_065
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.pachamama.org/effects-of-deforestation" ;
    :definitionText "The clearing, destroying, or otherwise removal of trees through deliberate, natural or accidental means. http://www.pachamama.org/effects-of-deforestation" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_066
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.usask.ca/agriculture/caedac/dbases/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The conversion of forested to non-forested land. Deforestation can involve the cutting and burning of trees to provide land for agricultural purposes or clearing for residential and industrial uses. http://www.usask.ca/agriculture/caedac/dbases/glossary.htm and http://www.undp.org/seed/forest/pdf/InnovatForesFinanc.pdf" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_067
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.theblackvault.com/documents/ota/Ota_4/DATA/1984/8426.PDF" ;
    :definitionText "The conversion of forests to land uses that have a tree cover of less than 10 percent. http://www.theblackvault.com/documents/ota/Ota_4/DATA/1984/8426.PDF 1984 and http://www.nap.edu/openbook.php?record_id=1985&page=663" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_068
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://ellerbruch.nmu.edu/classes/cs255f03/cs255students/jedens/P12/deforestation.ppt" ;
    :definitionText "The cutting down and burning of the trees in our forests (especially in the rain forest). http://ellerbruch.nmu.edu/classes/cs255f03/cs255students/jedens/P12/deforestation.ppt" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_069
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://environment.nationalgeographic.com/environment/global-warming/deforestation-overview.html" ;
    :definitionText "The cutting down and clearing away forest on a very large scale. http://environment.nationalgeographic.com/environment/global-warming/deforestation-overview.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_070
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://gradestack.com/CBSE-Class-9/What-is-Deforestation-/14919-2955-3388-study-wtw" ;
    :definitionText "The cutting down and clearing of the forests. http://gradestack.com/CBSE-Class-9/What-is-Deforestation-/14919-2955-3388-study-wtw" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_071
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.britannica.com" ;
    :definitionText "The cutting down and clearing of trees from forests, usually causing ecological harm. Encyclopædia Britannica. (2003, Nov.) Encyclopædia Britannica Online. [Online]. Available: http://www.britannica.com and http://www.rss.chalmers.se/gem/Education/RSES-2003/final_report_group_1.pdf" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_072
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://dictionary.cambridge.org/define.asp?key=deforestation*1+0" ;
    :definitionText "The cutting down of trees in a large area - http://dictionary.cambridge.org/define.asp?key=deforestation*1+0" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_073
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.spcforests.org/Library/usestatus/usestatus.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The deliberate and accidental destruction or removal of forests through the use of fire, felling for timber and fuel, overgrazing, clearance or destruction for agricultural and urban-industrial expansion, and other human activities. http://www.spcforests.org/Library/usestatus/usestatus.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_074
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://europa.eu.int/comm/development/forests/en/en4_6.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The depletion of tree crown cover to less than 10 per cent http://europa.eu.int/comm/development/forests/en/en4_6.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_075
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ocdsb.edu.on.ca/WOODSweb/geomatics/English/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "The destruction of a forest by removal of trees and plants http://www.ocdsb.edu.on.ca/WOODSweb/geomatics/English/glossary.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_076
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.kgv.edu.hk/eden/glossary.php" ;
    :definitionText "The destruction of forest. This normally refers to deforestation of tropical rainforests in Indonesia, Brazil and in West Africa. http://www.kgv.edu.hk/eden/glossary.php" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_077
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://dictionary.cambridge.org/define.asp?key=deforestation*1+0" ;
    :definitionText "The destruction of forests by people http://dictionary.cambridge.org/define.asp?key=deforestation*1+0" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_078
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ficus.usf.edu/docs/guide_issues/glossary/D.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The destruction of forests, usually caused by clear-cutting (followed by soil oxidation and/or erosion), poor agricultural practices, agricultural overuse, overcutting of forests, or overgrazing. http://www.ficus.usf.edu/docs/guide_issues/glossary/D.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_079
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.icons.umd.edu/resource/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The destruction of the world's forests, mainly rain forests, through direct human activity such as logging or slash and burn clearing for agriculture and grazing, and the indirect effects of pollution and acid rain. http://www.icons.umd.edu/resource/glossary.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_080
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.cia.gov/cia/publications/factbook/docs/notes.html" ;
    :definitionText "The destruction of vast areas of forest (e.g., unsustainable forestry practices, agricultural and range land clearing, and the over exploitation of wood products for use as fuel) without planting new growth. http://www.cia.gov/cia/publications/factbook/docs/notes.html." .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_081
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.spcforests.org/Library/usestatus/usestatus.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The disruption of the forest ecosystem by changes in land use that deplete tree crown cover to less than 10 percent of the land area (FAO, 1995). By this definition, very productive agricultural land with less than 10 percent tree crown cover is considered deforested. On the other hand, logging or any form of removal of 90 percent of the trees leaving only 10 percent of the tree crown cover would not be considered deforestation but would be considered as degradation if it results in damage to th" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_082
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.uiowa.edu/~africart/teachers/glossary/GlD.html" ;
    :definitionText "The large scale cutting down or clearing away of trees. http://www.uiowa.edu/~africart/teachers/glossary/GlD.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_083
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nationalgeographic.com/wildworld/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "The large-scale removal of trees from a habitat dominated by forest. http://www.nationalgeographic.com/wildworld/glossary.html and http://www.internet.ve/wildlife/glosario.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_084
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.lfc.edu/academics/biology/westley/adam2.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The logging or general destruction of forest. http://www.lfc.edu/academics/biology/westley/adam2.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_085
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.globalchange.umich.edu/globalchange2/current/lectures/deforest/deforest.html" ;
    :definitionText "The long-term reduction of the tree canopy cover below a 10 percent threshold. http://www.globalchange.umich.edu/globalchange2/current/lectures/deforest/deforest.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_086
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.prb.org/pubs/lessons/5billion/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The loss of trees due to overcutting of forests. Source: http://www.prb.org/pubs/lessons/5billion/glossary.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_087
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.lehigh.edu/~kaf3/books/reporting/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "The loss of tropical forests due to collection of fuelwood, commercial logging, shifting cultivation, grazing, road construction, ranching, mining and fire. Leads to soil erosion and flooding and endangers wildlife through habitat destruction. http://www.lehigh.edu/~kaf3/books/reporting/glossary.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_088
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.theforestproject.co.uk/why-take-action/deforestation" ;
    :definitionText "The loss or destruction of natural forests and is an increasing global problem with far reaching environmental and economic consequences. http://www.theforestproject.co.uk/why-take-action/deforestation" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_089
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://environment.about.com/od/biodiversityconservation/f/deforestation-overview.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The loss or destruction of naturally occurring forests, primarily due to human activities such as logging, cutting trees for fuel, slash-and-burn agriculture, clearing land for livestock grazing, mining operations, oil extraction, dam building, and urban sprawl or other types of development and population expansion. http://environment.about.com/od/biodiversityconservation/f/deforestation-overview.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_090
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.abf90.dial.pipex.com/bco6.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The mass destruction, usually for the supply of timber, of large areas of forest. http://www.abf90.dial.pipex.com/bco6.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_091
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.eia.doe.gov/oiaf/1605/ggrpt/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "The net removal of trees from forested land. http://www.eia.doe.gov/oiaf/1605/ggrpt/glossary.html and http://www.theadvisorygroup.com/PDF2/publications/Carbon%20Sequestration%20Paper.pdf" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_092
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nafi.com.au/k12/ourforests/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "The permanent clearing of forest areas, preventing regrowth e.g. clearing land for agriculture http://www.nafi.com.au/k12/ourforests/glossary.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_093
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://ps.ucdavis.edu/classes/ire001/env/deforest.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The permanent destruction of forests and woodlands. http://ps.ucdavis.edu/classes/ire001/env/deforest.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_094
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.panda.org/resources/factsheets/forests/frame.htm?31defor.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The permanent destruction of indigenous forests and woodlands. http://www.panda.org/resources/factsheets/forests/frame.htm?31defor.htm and http://abe.msstate.edu/csd-tc/p3-g2/intro.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_095
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://anmf.web1000.com/BIBLIOGRAPHY%20ON%20AFRICA%20MOUNTAINS.html" ;
    :definitionText "The permanent loss of forests to other land uses such as agriculture, grazing, new settlements, infrastructure, and dam reservoirs. http://anmf.web1000.com/BIBLIOGRAPHY%20ON%20AFRICA%20MOUNTAINS.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_096
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.sovereignty.net/p/land/gba-gloss.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The permanent removal of a forest from its natural habitat by man's activities. http://www.sovereignty.net/p/land/gba-gloss.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_097
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://collections.ic.gc.ca/abnature/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The permanent removal of forest and undergrowth http://collections.ic.gc.ca/abnature/glossary.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_098
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.bsrsi.msu.edu/rfrc/deforestation.html" ;
    :definitionText "The process in which a forest is cut down, burned or damaged is called \"deforestation.\" http://www.bsrsi.msu.edu/rfrc/deforestation.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_099
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://ohia.com/ohia/roadshows/sky/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The process of clearing forests. http://ohia.com/ohia/roadshows/sky/glossary.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_100
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.europe.apnet.com/inscight/12031996/defores1.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The process of clearing land of trees or forest. http://www.europe.apnet.com/inscight/12031996/defores1.htm or http://www.harcourt.com/dictionary/def/2/8/3/7/2837200.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_101
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.worldbank.org/html/schools/glossary.htm#d" ;
    :definitionText "The process of clearing of forests. http://www.worldbank.org/html/schools/glossary.htm#d" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_102
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.sandiegozoo.org/wildideas/glossary_c-d.html" ;
    :definitionText "The process of destroying forest habitat(s). http://www.sandiegozoo.org/wildideas/glossary_c-d.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_103
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.greenhousefriendly.com/glossary.shtml#D" ;
    :definitionText "The process of removing forested areas. Examples include cutting or burning to provide land for agricultural purposes, residential or industrial building sites, roads etc., or harvesting the trees for building materials or fuel. http://www.greenhousefriendly.com/glossary.shtml#D" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_104
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://wwf.panda.org/about_our_earth/about_forests/deforestation/" ;
    :definitionText "The process whereby natural forests are cleared through logging and/or burning, either to use the timber or to replace the area for alternative uses. http://wwf.panda.org/about_our_earth/about_forests/deforestation/" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_105
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.faculty.rsu.edu/~felwell/glossary/body.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The removal of all trees from an area (see also DEPLETION, ENVIRONMENT and DESERTIFICATION). http://www.faculty.rsu.edu/~felwell/glossary/body.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_106
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.epa.nsw.gov.au/soe/95/28.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The removal of forest and undergrowth http://www.epa.nsw.gov.au/soe/95/28.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_107
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://environment.jbpub.com/mckinney/interactive_glossary_showterm.cfm?term=deforestation%20" ;
    :definitionText "The removal of forest cover from an area. http://environment.jbpub.com/mckinney/interactive_glossary_showterm.cfm?term=deforestation%20" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_108
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://library.thinkquest.org/26634/sitemapf.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The removal of forest growth http://library.thinkquest.org/26634/sitemapf.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_109
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://search.nap.edu/nap-cgi/morehits.cgi?file=840-846.htm&term=forest&isbn=0309043867&display=" ;
    :definitionText "The removal of forest stands by cutting and burning to provide land for agricultural purposes, residential or industrial building http://search.nap.edu/nap-cgi/morehits.cgi?file=840-846.htm&term=forest&isbn=0309043867&display=" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_110
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://harp.gsfc.nasa.gov/v0ims/glossary.of.terms.html" ;
    :definitionText "The removal of forest stands by cutting and burning to provide land for agricultural purposes, residential or industrial building sites, roads, etc. or by harvesting the trees for building materials or fuel. Oxidation of organic matter releases CO2 to the atmosphere, and regional and global impacts may result. Source: EPO. http://harp.gsfc.nasa.gov/v0ims/glossary.of.terms.html, http://cdiac.esd.ornl.gov/cdiac/glossary.html#D , and http://www.eia.doe.gov/oiaf/1605/95report/glossary.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_111
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://books.nap.edu/openbook.php?record_id=1605&page=843" ;
    :definitionText "The removal of forest stands by cutting and burning to provide land for agricultural purposes, residential or industrial building sites, roads, etc., or by harvesting the trees for building materials or fuel. Oxidation of organic matter releases CO2 to the atmosphere, and regional and global impacts may result. http://books.nap.edu/openbook.php?record_id=1605&page=843" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_112
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.cleantechindia.com/climatechange/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The removal of forest stands. http://www.cleantechindia.com/climatechange/glossary.htm , http://www.eia.doe.gov/oiaf/1605/vr95rpt/gloss.html and http://www.eia.doe.gov/oiaf/1605/gg98rpt/glossary.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_113
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.hwwa.de/Projekte/Forsch_Schwerpunkte/FS/Klimapolitik/PDFDokumente/Michaelowa" ;
    :definitionText "The removal of forests from the land. http://www.hwwa.de/Projekte/Forsch_Schwerpunkte/FS/Klimapolitik/PDFDokumente/Michaelowa,%20Koch%20(2001).pdf" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_114
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.sitesalive.com/admin/glossary/sectD.html" ;
    :definitionText "The removal of trees and forests from the land http://www.sitesalive.com/admin/glossary/sectD.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_115
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.lpb.org/programs/forest/glossary.html#d" ;
    :definitionText "The removal of trees and often the plants associated with them. http://www.lpb.org/programs/forest/glossary.html#d" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_116
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.harcourtcollege.com/geography/regionalatlas/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "The removal of trees by people or their livestock. http://www.harcourtcollege.com/geography/regionalatlas/glossary.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_117
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www-pub.naz.edu:9000/~jborsos9/deforestation.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The removal of trees from a forested area that can be the result of Mother Nature, e.g. forest fires, or of human nature. http://www-pub.naz.edu:9000/~jborsos9/deforestation.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_118
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "https://www.coris.noaa.gov/glossary/#/search/main" ;
    :definitionText "The removal of trees from a habitat dominated by forest. https://www.coris.noaa.gov/glossary/#/search/main" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_119
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.life123.com/home-garden/green-living/energy-consumption/what-is-deforestation.shtml?fcsource=dell" ;
    :definitionText "The removal of trees from forests by humans. http://www.life123.com/home-garden/green-living/energy-consumption/what-is-deforestation.shtml?fcsource=dell" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_120
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.notredame.ac.jp/cgi-bin/wn?cmd=wn&word=deforestation" ;
    :definitionText "The removal of trees http://www.notredame.ac.jp/cgi-bin/wn?cmd=wn&word=deforestation" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_121
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.minntrees.org/asp/default.asp?PageID=59" ;
    :definitionText "The removal of trees without replacing them with young trees. http://www.minntrees.org/asp/default.asp?PageID=59" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_122
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.notredame.ac.jp/cgi-bin/wn?deforestation" ;
    :definitionText "The state of being clear of trees. http://www.notredame.ac.jp/cgi-bin/wn?deforestation and http://info.live58.org/why-should-i-care-about-deforestation/" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_123
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.africanculturalcenter.org/10_0glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "The state of having been cleared of forests. http://www.africanculturalcenter.org/10_0glossary.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_124
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://answers.ask.com/Science/Other/what_is_deforestation" ;
    :definitionText "The term used for when people completely remove trees and vegetation from a large forested area. Think of it like shaving, except instead of hairs, it's trees. Once an area is deforested, there's nothing left except dirt. http://answers.ask.com/Science/Other/what_is_deforestation" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_125
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.geocities.com/RainForest/Andes/7292/Terms.html" ;
    :definitionText "To clear away the trees or forests from. http://www.geocities.com/RainForest/Andes/7292/Terms.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_126
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.mso.anu.edu.au/~ralph/OPTED/v003/wb1913_d.html" ;
    :definitionText "To clear of forests; to disforest. http://www.mso.anu.edu.au/~ralph/OPTED/v003/wb1913_d.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_127
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.dictionary.com/cgi-bin/dict.pl?term=deforestation" ;
    :definitionText "To cut down and clear away the trees or forests from. http://www.dictionary.com/cgi-bin/dict.pl?term=deforestation" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_128
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://nhd.heinle.com/nhd-bin/searchNHD.pl" ;
    :definitionText "To remove the trees from an area as by fire, flood, logging, etc. http://nhd.heinle.com/nhd-bin/searchNHD.pl" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_129
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.chias.org/www/edu/cse/owpglo.html" ;
    :definitionText "To strip or deprive of trees and forest; the loss of our forest. http://www.chias.org/www/edu/cse/owpglo.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_130
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://kids.ran.org/kidscorner/rainforests/wordup.html" ;
    :definitionText "When a living forest is destroyed due to things such as logging, cattle ranching, or oil drilling. http://kids.ran.org/kidscorner/rainforests/wordup.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Brazil_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :appliesIn :Brazil ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.gisdevelopment.net/application/gii/planning/giipl0015a.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Brazil) The conversion of areas of primary forest physiognomy by anthropogenic activities, for the development of agriculture and cattle raising, detected by orbital platforms. Gross deforestation indicates that areas in process of secondary succession or forest recovery are not subtracted in the calculation of the extent and the rate. The above definition does not include areas of forest affected by selective logging activities or wild fires, which are object of specific reports by INPE. http:" .

:def_Deforestation_EU_2013_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :appliesIn :EU ;
    dcterms:date "2013"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32013D0529" ;
    :definitionText "(EU 2013) ‘deforestation’ means the direct human-induced conversion of forest to land that is not forest, where the conversion has taken place after 31 December 1989; http://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32013D0529" .

:def_Deforestation_Italy_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :appliesIn :Italy ;
    :sourceRef "Lorenzo Ciccarese <ciccarese@anpa.it>" ;
    :definitionText "(Italy) A loss of forest area because of change of land use to agricultural lands, barren lands, buildings, roads, pipelines, etc. Burned forest areas are not considered deforested. ISTAT (1950-1997). Statistiche Forestali. Annuari 1-47. Istituto Nazionale di Statistica. Rome. Lorenzo Ciccarese ciccarese@anpa.it" .

:def_Deforestation_Malaysia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :appliesIn :Malaysia ;
    :sourceRef "hcthang@forestry.gov.my" ;
    :definitionText "(Malaysia) - The conversion of forest or forest land to permanent non-forestry uses such as for agricultural crops, infrastructural and industrial development, settlements etc. From: hcthang@forestry.gov.my (Thang Hooi Chiew), Forestry Department Peninsular Malaysia" .

:def_Deforestation_UN_FAO_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    :sourceRef "http://faov02.fao.org:70/0gopher_root%3a[fao.fra" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO) The change of land use from forest to other land-use. [Source: from http://faov02.fao.org:70/0gopher_root%3a[fao.fra]def_uk.txt (concepts, definitions and methodology of the FAO Forest Resources Assessment 1990) via Bernhard Schlamadinger]" .

:def_Deforestation_UN_FAO_2001_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 2001) Deforestation is the conversion of forest to another land use or the long-term reduction of tree canopy cover below the 10% threshold. Explanatory note (extract): Deforestation implies the long-term or permanent loss of forest cover. Such a loss can only be caused and maintained through a continued man-induced or natural perturbation. Deforestation includes, for example, areas of forest converted to agriculture (including agroforestry), pasture, water reservoirs and urban areas. Th" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_131
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://ches.ing.ula.ve/GAIA/gis/maps/CaseStudies/explain/caseT.exp" ;
    :definitionText "A complete change in land use from forest to agriculture - including shifting cultivation and pasture - or urban use.http://ches.ing.ula.ve/GAIA/gis/maps/CaseStudies/explain/caseT.exp" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_132
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://fiesta.bren.ucsb.edu/~idgec/publications/reports/forest.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "A complete transformation in land use from forest to agricultural and urban uses, such as those brought upon by shifting cultivation, agroforestry and pasture. Excluded in the process is the large scale clear-cutting of plantations adopted by commercial tree growers.http://fiesta.bren.ucsb.edu/~idgec/publications/reports/forest.pdf" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_133
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :sourceRef "Lorenzo Ciccarese <ciccarese@anpa.it>" ;
    :definitionText "A process of land-use change from forest to other uses, because of population pressure, shifting cultivation, agricultural development, transmigration, forest fires, or unsupervised and poor logging practices, climatic and human-induced disturbancies (Setiadi 1996, modified). Lorenzo Ciccarese ciccarese@anpa.it" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_134
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fs.fed.us/institute/cifor/cifor_260.html" ;
    :definitionText "Area of forest permanently converted to non-forest land use, e.g., urbanization and Semi-permanent or temporary loss or gain of forest ecosystems, e.g., grasslands and agriculture. http://www.fs.fed.us/institute/cifor/cifor_260.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_135
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :definitionText "Conversion of forest land to other land use (Schlamadinger 1998)." .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_136
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.greenhouse.gov.au/ncas/files/strategic/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "Conversion of forests to another land use, frequently accompanied by burning (IPCC 1996c). http://www.greenhouse.gov.au/ncas/files/strategic/glossary.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_137
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :definitionText "Converting forest land to other vegetation or uses (i.e., cropland, pasture, dams). www.wws.princeton.edu/cgi-bin/byteserv.prl/~ota/disk1/1992/9217/921713.PDF" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_138
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.auburn.edu/~hurlbkl/definition.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Forest conversion to other uses, leaving out logged areas to regenerate. http://www.auburn.edu/~hurlbkl/definition.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_139
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.peopleandplanet.net/section.php?section=1&topic=8&PHPSESSID=1a9faae006a4efebfebe57431f0ca5ac" ;
    :definitionText "The conversion of forest lands to alternative uses such as cropland or human settlement. http://www.peopleandplanet.net/section.php?section=1&topic=8&PHPSESSID=1a9faae006a4efebfebe57431f0ca5ac" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_140
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nafi.com.au/k12/ourforests/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "The permanent clearing of forest areas, preventing regrowth e.g. clearing land for agriculture. http://www.nafi.com.au/k12/ourforests/glossary.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_141
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fieldtripearth.org/qa_article.xml?id=28" ;
    :definitionText "The permanent conversion of forests to pasture, farmland, or urban landscape. http://www.fieldtripearth.org/qa_article.xml?id=28" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_142
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://edugreen.teri.res.in/explore/glossary.htm#d" ;
    :definitionText "The practice or process that result in the long-term change in land-use to non-forest uses. http://edugreen.teri.res.in/explore/glossary.htm#d" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_143
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.undp.org/gef/workshop/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The process of degradation or loss of forests by shifting use of the forest to agriculture—including shifting cultivation and pasture—urban use, and timber harvesting, thus reducing the forests contribution to preserving biodiversity, water retention, soil and climate preservation, and other environmental services. http://www.undp.org/gef/workshop/glossary.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_144
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.pfmt.org/glossary/d.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The unintentional or intentional conversion of land use from forest to nonforest. Associated with nonrenewable timber harvesting practises in ecologically sensitive areas, such a tropical reinforests. http://www.pfmt.org/glossary/d.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_145
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://earthobservatory.nasa.gov:81/Library/glossary.php3?mode=alpha&seg=d" ;
    :definitionText "Those practices or processes that result in the change of forested lands to non-forest uses. http://earthobservatory.nasa.gov:81/Library/glossary.php3?mode=alpha&seg=d" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_146
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.epa.gov/globalwarming/publications/outreach/general/glossary.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Those practices or processes that result in the conversion of forested lands for non-forest uses. http://www.epa.gov/globalwarming/publications/outreach/general/glossary.pdf and. http://www.doc.mmu.ac.uk/aric/diction.html." .

:def_Deforestation_Austria_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :Austria ;
    :sourceRef "Weiss Peter <weissp@ubavie.gv.at>" ;
    :definitionText "(Austria) (clearing) (Rodung) - A land use change of forest land to other uses. Deforestation (clearing) is forbidden in Austria (due to former laws deforestation (clearing) is countrywide forbidden in Austria since about 150 years). However, if public interest in the different land use is higher than public interest in the conservation of the forest, the authority may give its approval for the deforestation (clearing). Usually, as a compensation other adequate areas have to be afforested. (Aust" .

:def_Deforestation_Canada_BC_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_BC ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.for.gov.bc.ca/pab/publctns/glossary/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada - BC) Clearing an area of forest on a non-temporary basis for another use. Clearcutting (even with stump removal), if shortly followed by reforestation for forestry purposes, is not deforesting. [Source: Glossary of Forestry Terms, Province of British Columbia, Ministry of Forests, http://www.for.gov.bc.ca/pab/publctns/glossary/glossary.htm via Igor A. Yakovlev]" .

:def_Deforestation_Canada_Sask_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_Sask ;
    :sourceRef "http://nfdp.ccfm.org/silviterm/silvi_e/silvitermatode.htm#D" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada - Sask.) [deboisement (n.m.)] Permanent removal of forest cover and withdrawal of land from forest use, whether deliberately or circumstantially. [Source: Silvicultural Terms in Canada - Second Edition 1995 From: Mark Johnston <johnston@larix.derm.gov.sk.ca Date: Tue, 16 Jun 1998 17:44:48 -0600] http://nfdp.ccfm.org/silviterm/silvi_e/silvitermatode.htm#D" .

:def_Deforestation_Canada_NR_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_NR ;
    :sourceRef "https://www.nrcan.gc.ca/forests/inventory/13419" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada NR). Deforestation is the permanent removal of forest cover from an area, and the conversion of the previously forested land to other uses. https://www.nrcan.gc.ca/forests/inventory/13419" .

:def_Deforestation_Canada_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :Canada ;
    :sourceRef "http://nrcan.gc.ca/cfs/proj/ppiab/sof/sof.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada) Clearing an area of forest for another long-term use. (http://nrcan.gc.ca/cfs/proj/ppiab/sof/sof.html )" .

:def_Deforestation_Cyprus_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :Cyprus ;
    :sourceRef "Publicity Sector <publicity@cytanet.com.cy>" ;
    :definitionText "(Cyprus) Deforestation: the removal of a forest stand from an area where the land is put to a nonforest use. A.K. Christou \"Forestry Department - Research and Publicity Sector\" publicity@cytanet.com.cy" .

:def_Deforestation_India_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    :sourceRef "Varma <v.varma@landfood.unimelb.edu.au>" ;
    :definitionText "(India) Removal of forest cover from a forest land. It excludes clearfelling. [Source: Glossary of Technical Terms, Forest Research Institute, India. From: \"Vivek K. Varma\" <v.varma@landfood.unimelb.edu.au Date: Fri, 17 Jul 1998 02:28:29 -0400 (EDT)]" .

:def_Deforestation_Indonesia_2002_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :Indonesia ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.globalforestwatch.org/common/indonesia/sof.indonesia.english.low.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Indonesia - 2002) The permanent removal of forest cover and conversion of the land to other uses. According to the land use definition used by FAO and accepted by most governments, forest land that has been harvested, even clear-cut, is not regarded as deforested because, in principle, trees may regrow or be replanted. Deforestation is recorded only when the land is permanently converted to nonforest use. However, the remote sensing imagery used in this report to determine land cover (the prese" .

:def_Deforestation_Lithuania_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :Lithuania ;
    :sourceRef "Sekrtetore <sek@mp.is.lt>" ;
    :definitionText "(Lithuania) Clearing of an area with the purpose to change forest land to other land use category. Source: A. Kuliesis, Director of Lithuanain Forest Inventory and Management Institute Email: Sekrtetore sek@mp.is.lt" .

:def_Deforestation_Mexico_INEGI_y_SEMARNAP_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :Mexico_INEGI_y_SEMARNAP ;
    :definitionText "(Mexico -INEGI y SEMARNAP) Proceso de cambio de uso del suelo de forestal a otro uso (INEGI y SEMARNAP 1999)." .

:def_Deforestation_Pakistan_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :Pakistan ;
    :definitionText "(Pakistan) To remove the tree crop from a piece of land without the intention of reforesting. Definition adopted from the British Commonwealth Forest Terminology Part-I, 1953. Source: Mumtaz Ahmad, Section Forest Officer, Pakistan Min. of Environment, Local Government, and Rural Development." .

:def_Deforestation_Papua_New_Guinea_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :Papua_New_Guinea ;
    :definitionText "(Papua New Guinea) - The removal of trees from forestland and subsequent conversion of land-use from forestry to other such as agriculture. Vitus Ambia, Papua New Guinea Forest Authority." .

:def_Deforestation_Tanzania_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :Tanzania ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.unep-wcmc.org/forest/restoration/docs/TanzaniaFLR.PDF" ;
    :definitionText "(Tanzania) Normally refers to clearing of a forest or woodland cover and replacing it with other land uses i.e. converting forest land to agriculture farms or settlement areas. http://www.unep-wcmc.org/forest/restoration/docs/TanzaniaFLR.PDF" .

:def_Deforestation_UN_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :UN ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nscb.gov.ph/peenra/Publications/Compendium/glossary.PDF" ;
    :definitionText "(UN) - Clearing of tree formations and their replacement by non-forest land uses. (UN Glossary of Environment Statistics) http://www.nscb.gov.ph/peenra/Publications/Compendium/glossary.PDF" .

:def_Deforestation_UN_EP_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :UN_EP ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://digitalcommons.unl.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1030&context=usdafsfacpub" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-EP 2003) - Conversion of forest to non-forest. http://digitalcommons.unl.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1030&context=usdafsfacpub." .

:def_Deforestation_UN_FAO_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/DOCREP/X7273E/x7273e05.htm#P0_0" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 2000) - A permanent conversion to other uses. http://www.fao.org/DOCREP/X7273E/x7273e05.htm#P0_0." .

:def_Deforestation_UN_FAO_2000_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfcccbali.org/unfccc/component/option" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 2000) - The conversion of forest to another land use or the long-term reduction of tree canopy cover below the 10% threshold (FAO, 2000) http://unfcccbali.org/unfccc/component/option,com_glossary/Itemid,100/func,display/letter,D/catid,31/page,1/" .

:def_Deforestation_UN_FAO_2001_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/docrep/003/y0900e/y0900e11.htm#P1_7" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 2001) -The conversion of forest to another land use or the long-term reduction of the tree canopy cover below the minimum 10 percent threshold (see the UN-FAO 2001 definition of forest and the following explanatory note). Explanatory note: Deforestation implies the long-term or permanent loss of forest cover and implies transformation into another land use. Such a loss can only be caused and maintained by a continued human-induced or natural perturbation. Deforestation includes areas of " .

:def_Deforestation_UN_FAO_2004_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fao.org/forestry/foris/webview/forestry2/index.jsp?siteId=4261&sitetreeId=13629&langId=1&geoId=0" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 2004) - The conversion of forest to another land use or the long-term reduction of the tree canopy cover below the minimum 10 percent threshold. Explanatory notes: 1. Deforestation implies the long-term or permanent loss of forest cover and implies transformation into another land use. Such a loss can only be caused and maintained by a continued human-induced or natural perturbation. 2. Deforestation includes areas of forest converted to agriculture, pasture, water reservoirs and urban a" .

:def_Deforestation_UN_FAO_nd_005
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    :sourceRef "Graeme Wild <GraemeW@za.sappi.com>" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO) - To clear an area, other than purely temporarily, of forest. Clear cutting (even with stump removal), if shortly followed by reforestation, is not deforesting. From: Graeme Wild <GraemeW@za.sappi.com" .

:def_Deforestation_UN_FCCC_2001_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FCCC ;
    dcterms:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfcccbali.org/unfccc/component/option" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FCCC 2001) The direct human-induced conversion of forested land to non-forested land. (UNFCCC, 2001) http://unfcccbali.org/unfccc/component/option,com_glossary/Itemid,100/func,display/letter,D/catid,31/page,1/" .

:def_Deforestation_UN_FCCC_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FCCC ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfcccbali.org/unfccc/component/option" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FCCC) The removal of forest stands by cutting and burning to provide land for agricultural purposes, residential or industrial building sites, roads, etc., or by harvesting the trees for building materials or fuel. http://unfcccbali.org/unfccc/component/option,com_glossary/Itemid,100/func,display/letter,D/catid,31/page,1/" .

:def_Deforestation_USA_STATE_Maryland_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Maryland ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.wrm.org.uy/actors/WB/1994policy.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA –STATE- Maryland) -The clearing of forests and the conversion of land to nonforest uses. http://www.wrm.org.uy/actors/WB/1994policy.html" .

:def_Deforestation_USA_Congress_OTA_1984_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :USA_Congress_OTA ;
    dcterms:date "1984"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://govinfo.library.unt.edu/ota/Ota_4/DATA/1984/8426.PDF" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-Congress-OTA 1984) : The conversion of forests to land uses that have a tree cover of less than 10 percent. http://govinfo.library.unt.edu/ota/Ota_4/DATA/1984/8426.PDF" .

:def_Deforestation_WAF_2004_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :appliesIn :WAF ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.worldagroforestry.org/sea/Publications/files/book/BK0073-04.PDF" ;
    :definitionText "(WAF 2004) The conversion of forest land to non-forest land. http://www.worldagroforestry.org/sea/Publications/files/book/BK0073-04.PDF ." .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_147
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :definitionText "Cambio de uso del suelo que impica la desaparicion de las selva o el bosque (Herrera et al. n.d.)." .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_148
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :definitionText "Change in forest land use from forestry to other purposes, such that it no longer functions as a forest ecosystem (Repetto and Gillis 1998)." .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_149
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nrcan-rncan.gc.ca/cfs-scf/science/prodserv/glossary_e.html#22" ;
    :definitionText "Clearing an area of forest for another long-term use. http://www.nrcan-rncan.gc.ca/cfs-scf/science/prodserv/glossary_e.html#22 Déboisement http://www.fnfp.gc.ca/rep99/gloss-e.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_150
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.for.gov.bc.ca/pab/publctns/glossary/glossary.txt" ;
    :definitionText "Clearing an area of forest on a non-temporary basis for another use. http://www.for.gov.bc.ca/pab/publctns/glossary/glossary.txt" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_151
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://typhoon.sdsu.edu/nasa_lcluc/forest.html" ;
    :definitionText "Clearing an area of forest on a non-temporary basis for another use. Clearcutting (even with stump removal), if shortly followed by reforestation for forestry purposes, is not deforesting. http://typhoon.sdsu.edu/nasa_lcluc/forest.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_152
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :definitionText "Clearing an area permanently for another use, such as agriculture or road building (Ecoforestry 1997)." .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_153
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :definitionText "Clearing of forest from large tracts of land which consequently remains unforested either as barren land or as agricultural crop. (Bruening n.d.)." .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_154
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfcccbali.org/unfccc/component/option" ;
    :definitionText "Clearing of tree formations and their replacement by non forest land use (PEENRA website) http://unfcccbali.org/unfccc/component/option,com_glossary/Itemid,100/func,display/letter,D/catid,31/page,1/" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_155
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.schools.wafa.org.au/terms.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Clearing trees for timber, fuel, farmland or for new settlements from a piece of land without the intention of reforesting. http://www.schools.wafa.org.au/terms.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_156
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :definitionText "Conversion of any forest (natural forest, modified forest, or planted forest) to non-forest conditions (cropland, pasture, or urban land) (IUCN, UNEP, WWF 1991)." .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_157
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.wisegeek.com/what-is-hard-deforestation.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Deforestation (Hard) occurs when forested lands are clearcut and then compromised so that the trees cannot grow back. http://www.wisegeek.com/what-is-hard-deforestation.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_158
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.sprl.umich.edu/GCL/notes2/Deforestation.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Deforestation (Wasteful) – occurs when forests yielding high values of goods and services are clearcut and replaced with land uses that yield lower returns. http://www.sprl.umich.edu/GCL/notes2/Deforestation.pdf." .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_159
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://wiki.answers.com/Q/What_is_deforestation?altQ=What_is_deforrestation#slide=1" ;
    :definitionText "Deforestation happens when human beings turn forested land into non-forested land due to our activities. It is not a good thing for wildlife because it takes away much of their natural habitat. http://wiki.answers.com/Q/What_is_deforestation?altQ=What_is_deforrestation#slide=1" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_160
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.globalchange.umich.edu/globalchange2/current/lectures/deforest/deforest.html" ;
    :definitionText "Deforestation implies the long-term or permanent loss of forest cover and its transformation into another land use. http://www.globalchange.umich.edu/globalchange2/current/lectures/deforest/deforest.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_161
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://abushald.blogspot.com/2008/11/why-is-deforestation-important.html" ;
    :definitionText "Deforestation is when forests, rain forests or a group of trees in the same area are living with animals and many different types of plants, are being chopped of, or mostly burnt for the land use. http://abushald.blogspot.com/2008/11/why-is-deforestation-important.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_162
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://eschooltoday.com/forests/what-is-deforestation.html" ;
    :definitionText "Deforestation is when humans remove or clear large areas of forest lands and related ecosystems for non-forest use. These include clearing for farming purposes, ranching and urban use. In these cases, trees are never re-planted. http://eschooltoday.com/forests/what-is-deforestation.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_163
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.meritnation.com/ask-answer/question/what-is-deforestation/forest-society-and-colonialism/6273919" ;
    :definitionText "Deforestation is when humans remove or clear large areas of forest lands for non-forest use. These include clearing for farming purposes, ranching and urban use. Inthese cases, trees are never re-planted. http://www.meritnation.com/ask-answer/question/what-is-deforestation/forest-society-and-colonialism/6273919" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_164
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.mongabay.com/08define.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Deforestation refers to the loss of forest cover; land that is permanently converted from forest to agricultural land, golf courses, cattle pasture, homes, lakes, or desert. The FAO (Food and Agriculture Organization of the U.N.) defines tropical deforestation as \"change of forest with depletion of tree crown cover to less than 10%.\" Depletion of forest to tree crown cover greater than 10% (say from 100% to 12%) is considered forest degradation. Logging most often falls under the category of for" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_165
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deforestation" ;
    :definitionText "Deforestation, clearance or clearing is the removal of a forest or stand of trees where the land is thereafter converted to a non-forest use.[1] Examples of deforestation include conversion of forestland to farms, ranches, or urban use http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deforestation" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_166
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.northern.edu/natsource/BIRDS/Conser1.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Destruction of forested habitats for conversion to other uses. http://www.northern.edu/natsource/BIRDS/Conser1.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_167
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :definitionText "Eliminacion total de la vegetacion y su reemplazo por usos no forestales de la tierra (Varela 1998)." .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_168
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://loki.stockton.edu/~epsteinc/deforest.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Forests are removed and the land changed to another kind of land use. http://loki.stockton.edu/~epsteinc/deforest.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_169
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://hcd.ucdavis.edu/classes/iad10/enviro.html" ;
    :definitionText "Large scale cutting of forest; replacement with other plant cover (esp. pasture) http://hcd.ucdavis.edu/classes/iad10/enviro.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_170
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :definitionText "Loss of forest cover which is not replaced by either natural regeneration or replanting of trees (WWF/IUCN 1996)." .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_171
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :definitionText "Para la delimitacion y cuantificacion de la deforestacion, la ha definido como la remocion temporal o permanente de la cubierta vegetal natural para dedicar otro uso no forestal (Anon. 1995a)." .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_172
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://nfdp.ccfm.org/silviterm/silvi_e/silvitermatode.htm#D" ;
    :definitionText "Permanent removal of forest cover and withdrawal of land from forest use, whether deliberately or circumstantially http://nfdp.ccfm.org/silviterm/silvi_e/silvitermatode.htm#D" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_173
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :definitionText "Se considera el cambio de uso del suelo de foresta a no forestal en un periodo determinado. Tambien puede expresarse como la elimiacion completa de areas arbolada a usos del suelo no forestales (Herrera 1998)." .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_174
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.oxfam.org.uk/coolplanet/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The clearance of all the trees and undergrowth in a forest to make land usable for farming. http://www.oxfam.org.uk/coolplanet/glossary.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_175
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.sprl.umich.edu/GCL/wri/forest/deforest.html" ;
    :definitionText "The clearing of forest lands for all forms of agricultural uses (shifting cultivation, permanent agriculture and ranching) and for other land uses such as settlements, other infrastructure and mining. In tropical countries, this entails clearing that reduces tree crown cover to less than 10 percent. As defined here, deforestation does not include other alterations, such as selective logging (unless the forest cover is permanently reduced to less than 10 percent), that can substantially affect fo" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_176
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "https://www.uni-hohenheim.de/i490a/teaching/M4901-430/ws_03_04/reading_materials/New_Neef_Schwarzmeier_Studie.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "The clearing of forests and the conversion of land to non-forest uses such as cropland or human settlement. https://www.uni-hohenheim.de/i490a/teaching/M4901-430/ws_03_04/reading_materials/New_Neef_Schwarzmeier_Studie.pdf" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_177
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.wrm.org.uy/actors/WB/1991policy3.html" ;
    :definitionText "The clearing of forests and the conversion of land to nonforest uses. http://www.wrm.org.uy/actors/WB/1991policy3.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_178
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.businessdictionary.com/definition/deforestation.html" ;
    :definitionText "The clearing of virgin forests, or intentional destruction or removal of trees and other vegetation for agricultural, commercial, housing, or firewood use without replanting (reforesting) and without allowing time for the forest to regenerate itself. Deforestation is one of the major factors contributing to the greenhouse effect and desertification. http://www.businessdictionary.com/definition/deforestation.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_179
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.globalchange.umich.edu/globalchange2/current/lectures/deforest/deforest.html" ;
    :definitionText "The conversion of forest to another land use http://www.globalchange.umich.edu/globalchange2/current/lectures/deforest/deforest.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_180
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.globalchange.umich.edu/globalchange2/current/lectures/deforest/deforest.html" ;
    :definitionText "The conversion of forest to another land use or the long-term reduction of the tree canopy cover below a 10 percent threshold. Deforestation implies the long-term or permanent loss of forest cover and its transformation into another land use. http://www.globalchange.umich.edu/globalchange2/current/lectures/deforest/deforest.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_181
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.climateservices.com/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The conversion of forested to non-forested land. Deforestation can involve the cutting and burning of trees to provide land for agricultural purposes or clearing for residential and industrial uses. . http://www.climateservices.com/glossary.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_182
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://ukdb.web.aol.com/hutchinson/encyclopedia/50/M0020550.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The destruction of forest for timber, fuel, charcoal burning, and clearing for agriculture and extractive industries, such as mining, without planting new trees to replace those lost (reafforestation) or working on a cycle that allows the natural forest to regenerate. http://ukdb.web.aol.com/hutchinson/encyclopedia/50/M0020550.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_183
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.quiknet.com/~mathman/csus/Site_Map/Glossary/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The destruction of forests, typically to clear land for agriculture or ranching or to provide fuel and timber. http://www.quiknet.com/~mathman/csus/Site_Map/Glossary/glossary.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_184
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.greenpeace.org/raw/content/usa/turning-up-the-heat-global-w.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "The direct, human-induced conversion of forested land to non-forested land (2008). http://www.greenpeace.org/raw/content/usa/turning-up-the-heat-global-w.pdf" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_185
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.conserve-energy-future.com/causes-effects-solutions-of-deforestation.php" ;
    :definitionText "The felling and clearing of forest cover or tree plantations in order to accommodate agricultural, industrial or urban use. It involves permanent end of forest cover to make that land available for residential, commercial or industrial purpose. http://www.conserve-energy-future.com/causes-effects-solutions-of-deforestation.php" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_186
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://forestry.oxfordjournals.org/content/77/1/9.full.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "The felling of trees without subsequent replanting or regeneration, i.e. the conversion of previously forested land to agricultural, urban or other land uses, which do not have a substantial tree canopy cover (<10 per cent, according to the definition in FAO (2000)).. http://forestry.oxfordjournals.org/content/77/1/9.full.pdf" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_187
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.canadian-forests.com/fsc-glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "The long-term removal of trees from forested site to permit other site uses. http://www.canadian-forests.com/fsc-glossary.html and http://www.web.net/~fscca/standard.htm#anchor88641. Cutting of trees followed by regeneration is not deforestation. syn: forest clearing disturbance, conversion, or wasteful destruction of forest lands. (AGRO) (Dunster and Dunster 1996)." .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_188
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://greenliving.lovetoknow.com/What_is_Deforestation" ;
    :definitionText "The net loss of forests. A \"net loss\" of forests occurs when more forest cover is removed than is replaced, leaving the landscape substantially altered. http://greenliving.lovetoknow.com/What_is_Deforestation" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_189
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nafi.com.au/k12/ourforests/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "The permanent clearing of forest areas, preventing regrowth e.g. clearing land for agriculture http://www.nafi.com.au/k12/ourforests/glossary.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_190
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.socialwatch.org/indicators/Glossary.htm#Deforestation" ;
    :definitionText "The permanent clearing of forest lands for shifting cultivation, permanent agriculture or settlements; it does not include other alterations such as selective logging. http://www.socialwatch.org/indicators/Glossary.htm#Deforestation" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_191
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.auburn.edu/~hurlbkl/definition.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The permanent destruction of forests and woodlands; it occurs as the forests are converted for agricultural uses. http://www.auburn.edu/~hurlbkl/definition.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_192
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.livescience.com/27692-deforestation.html" ;
    :definitionText "The permanent destruction of forests in order to make the land available for other uses. http://www.livescience.com/27692-deforestation.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_193
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.scar.toronto.edu/~97fauche/termassignment.html#" ;
    :definitionText "The permanent destruction of indigenous forest and woodland. Deforestation thus refers to clearing of original forests, and it includes a range of processes, from a selective removal of valuable timber species to clear cutting followed by burning and creation of pasture and agricultural fields (Keller, 1994). http://www.scar.toronto.edu/~97fauche/termassignment.html# What is deforestation, the state of deforestation. Keller, M. (1994) Controls on Soil-Atmosphere fluxes of nitrous oxide and metha" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_194
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.globaled.org/issues/152/a.html" ;
    :definitionText "The permanent destruction of indigenous forests and woodlands. . http://www.globaled.org/issues/152/a.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_195
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.botany.uwc.ac.za/envfacts/facts/deforestation.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The permanent destruction of indigenous forests and woodlands. The term does not include the removal of industrial forests such as plantations of gums or pines. http://www.botany.uwc.ac.za/envfacts/facts/deforestation.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_196
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.gn.apc.org/LivingEarth/RainforestDB/glossary.a-e.html#climax_forest" ;
    :definitionText "The permanent removal of forest and undergrowth. http://www.gn.apc.org/LivingEarth/RainforestDB/glossary.a-e.html#climax_forest" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_197
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :definitionText "The process of land cover transformation from forest to non-forest (Achard et al. 1998)." .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_198
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "https://www.princeton.edu/~achaney/tmve/wiki100k/docs/Deforestation.html" ;
    :definitionText "The removal of a forest or stand of trees where the land is thereafter converted to a nonforest use.[1] Examples of deforestation include conversion of forestland to agriculture or urban use. The term deforestation is often misused to describe any activity where all trees in an area are removed. However in temperate mesic climates, the removal of all trees in an area—in conformance with sustainable forestry practices—is correctly described as regeneration harvest.[2] In temperate mesic climates," .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_199
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :definitionText "The removal of a forest stand where the land is put to a non-forest use (Helms 1998)." .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_200
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.buzzle.com/articles/causes-and-effects-of-deforestation.html" ;
    :definitionText "The removal of forest or trees from a land and converting it for nonforest use http://www.buzzle.com/articles/causes-and-effects-of-deforestation.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_201
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.minntrees.org/facts/ff17.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The removal of trees without replacing them with young trees. http://www.minntrees.org/facts/ff17.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_202
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :definitionText "The temporary or permanent clearance of forest for agriculture or other purposes (Grainger 1993)." .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_203
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.globalchange.umich.edu/globalchange2/current/lectures/deforest/deforest.html" ;
    :definitionText "The transformation of forested lands by human actions. http://www.globalchange.umich.edu/globalchange2/current/lectures/deforest/deforest.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_204
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :definitionText "The willful and permanent transition in vegetative cover from that which is clearly \"forest\" (regardless of the commercial or aesthetic value of the trees) to that which is clearly devoted to other uses - with trees seen as undesirable invaders. On this definition, the clear cutting of portions of a forest with the intention of allowing regeneration of trees does not qualify as deforestation - even though all the trees are removed at a certain time (Daniel W. Bromley, Deforestation: Institutiona" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_205
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :definitionText "To clear an area, other than purely temporarily, of forest. 1) While man is the main deforester, natural agencies (e.g. volcanic eruption, landslides) may also contribute. (2) Clear cutting (even with stump removal), if shortly followed by reforestation is not deforesting. (Ford-Robertson 1971)." .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_206
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://wiki.answers.com/Q/What_is_deforestation_and_deforestation#slide=2" ;
    :definitionText "Trees being cut down and not being replanted/ http://wiki.answers.com/Q/What_is_deforestation_and_deforestation#slide=2" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_207
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCoverUse ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.shsu.edu/~chemistry/Glossary/de.html#D" ;
    :definitionText "Type of \"forestry practice\" which involves the permanent removal of forests and their undergrowth so that the land can serve another purpose. http://www.shsu.edu/~chemistry/Glossary/de.html#D" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_208
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :Other ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.uncc.edu/~chamato/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Annual Deforestation - Annual loss of forest land; reflects land degradation http://www.uncc.edu/~chamato/glossary.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_209
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :Other ;
    :sourceRef "http://www-pub.naz.edu:9000/~jwitten2/about2.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Deforestation occurs in a number of ways, both natural and unnatural. http://www-pub.naz.edu:9000/~jwitten2/about2.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_210
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :Other ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.auburn.edu/~hurlbkl/definition.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Induced land degradation in developing countries that is a direct result of land tenure systems that facilitate property-right acquisition in idle lands. http://www.auburn.edu/~hurlbkl/definition.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_211
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :Other ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.globalchange.org/glossall/glossd-f.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Loss of forest. http://www.globalchange.org/glossall/glossd-f.htm" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_212
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :Other ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.britell.com/misc/lex.html" ;
    :definitionText "Simply means to \"divest of forests\". http://www.britell.com/misc/lex.html" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_213
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :Other ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.greenpeace.org/raw/content/usa/turning-up-the-heat-global-w.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "The direct, human-induced conversion of forested land to non-forested land (2008). http://www.greenpeace.org/raw/content/usa/turning-up-the-heat-global-w.pdf" .

:def_Deforestation_Unknown_nd_214
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Deforestation ;
    :hasCategory :Other ;
    :sourceRef "http://ellerbruch.nmu.edu/classes/cs255f03/cs255students/jedens/P12/deforestation.ppt" ;
    :definitionText "Deforestation is the inevitable result of the current social and economic policies being carried out in the name of development http://ellerbruch.nmu.edu/classes/cs255f03/cs255students/jedens/P12/deforestation.ppt" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :definitionText "3.5 REFORESTATION - Reforestation is sorted by restoration of land cover and land cover and use. Several specified the planting of \"crops.\"" .

:def_Reforestation_Australia_NSW_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Australia_NSW ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.forest.nsw.gov.au/education/glossary/default.asp#Ltr_W" ;
    :definitionText "(Australia-NSW) Replanting of a forest on cleared or destroyed forest areas. http://www.forest.nsw.gov.au/education/glossary/default.asp#Ltr_W" .

:def_Reforestation_Austria_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Austria ;
    :sourceRef "Weiss Peter <weissp@ubavie.gv.at>" ;
    :definitionText "(Austria) (Wiederbewaldung): Reforestation areas are temporarily unstocked areas caused by harvesting, wind breaks, natural disasters and so on. These areas have to be reforested artificially (usually within 3 years, under certain circumstances within maximal 8 years) or with methods of natural regeneration (usually within 8 years, under certain circumstances within maximal 11 years). In Austria reforestation has always been recognized as a part of forest management and has never been linked up " .

:def_Reforestation_Brazil_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Brazil ;
    :sourceRef "Erich Schaitza <erich@cnpf.embrapa.br>" ;
    :definitionText "(Brazil) REFLORESTAMENTO always, no matter the previous land use was not a forest and it is the first time this land bears a forest. Currently, reforestation (REFLORESTAMENTO) is the general name of planted forests. From: Erich Schaitza <erich@cnpf.embrapa.br." .

:def_Reforestation_Bulgaria_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Bulgaria ;
    :sourceRef "Forest Research Institute <forestin@bulnet.bg>" ;
    :definitionText "(Bulgaria) Reforestation - there is no special definition for \"reforestation\". It is part of the afforestation activities. Forest Research Institute forestin@bulnet.bg" .

:def_Reforestation_Canada_BC_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_BC ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.for.gov.bc.ca/pab/publctns/westland/gloss.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada - BC) Regeneration (reforestation): The renewal of a tree crop either by natural means (seeded on-site from adjacent stands or deposited by wind, birds, or animals) or by planted seedlings or direct seeding. http://www.for.gov.bc.ca/pab/publctns/westland/gloss.htm" .

:def_Reforestation_Canada_BC_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_BC ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.for.gov.bc.ca/pab/publctns/glossary/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada - BC) The natural or artificial restocking (i.e., planting, seeding) of an area with forest trees. Also called forest regeneration. [Source: Glossary of Forestry Terms, Province of British Columbia, Ministry of Forests, http://www.for.gov.bc.ca/pab/publctns/glossary/glossary.htm via Igor A. Yakovlev]" .

:def_Reforestation_Canada_Sask_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_Sask ;
    :sourceRef "Mark Johnston <johnston@larix.derm.gov.sk.ca>" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada - Sask.) [reboisement (n.m.)] syn. reafforestation - Successful renewal of a forest crop by planting or direct seeding. [Source: Silvicultural Terms in Canada - Second Edition 1995 From: Mark Johnston <johnston@larix.derm.gov.sk.ca Date: Tue, 16 Jun 1998 17:44:48 -0600]" .

:def_Reforestation_Canada_Sask_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Canada_Sask ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.studyweb.com/Agriculture/" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada - Sask.) The natural or artificial restocking of an area with trees. [Source: Chapter F-19.1: An Act Respecting the Management of Forest Resources... new provincial legislation on forest management From: Mark Johnston <johnston@larix.derm.gov.sk.ca Date: Tue, 16 Jun 1998 17:44:48 -0600] also http://www.studyweb.com/Agriculture/" .

:def_Reforestation_Canada_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Canada ;
    :sourceRef "http://carbon.cfs.nrcan.gc.ca/definitions_e.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada) - The conversion of non-forested land to forested land through human activities, on land that was forested but that had been converted to non-forested land. http://carbon.cfs.nrcan.gc.ca/definitions_e.html" .

:def_Reforestation_Canada_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Canada ;
    :sourceRef "http://nrcan.gc.ca/cfs/proj/ppiab/sof/sof.html" ;
    :definitionText "(Canada) The reestablishment of trees on denuded forest land by natural or artificial means, such as planting or seeding. State of Canada's Forests 1996-97. (http://nrcan.gc.ca/cfs/proj/ppiab/sof/sof.html)" .

:def_Reforestation_Chile_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Chile ;
    :definitionText "(Chile) La acción de poblar con especies arbóreas o arbustivas mediante plantación, regeneración manejada o siembra, un terreno que haya sido objeto de explotación extractiva (Cerda 1998)." .

:def_Reforestation_Colombia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Colombia ;
    :sourceRef "Gerardo Lozano <glozano@impsat.net.co>" ;
    :definitionText "(Colombia) Es el establecimiento de árboles para formar bosques, realizado por el hombre. (Decreto 1791 de 1996. Ministerio del medio Ambiente.) \"Gerardo Lozano\" glozano@impsat.net.co and María del Pilar Pardo mpp@LatinMail.com" .

:def_Reforestation_Cuba_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Cuba ;
    :sourceRef "Christoph Kleinn <ckleinn@catie.ac.cr>" ;
    :definitionText "(Cuba) Reforestación: la acción de poblar con especies arbóreas áreas que hayan sido objeto de aprovechamiento previos o arrasadas por incendios y otras causas. Christoph Kleinn <ckleinn@catie.ac.cr" .

:def_Reforestation_Cyprus_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Cyprus ;
    :sourceRef "Publicity Sector <publicity@cytanet.com.cy>" ;
    :definitionText "(Cyprus) Reforestation: the establishment of a forest cover in an area where there was a forest before but due to some reasons (fire, felling etc.) has been removed. A.K. Christou \"Forestry Department - Research and Publicity Sector\" publicity@cytanet.com.cy" .

:def_Reforestation_Denmark_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Denmark ;
    :sourceRef "PMP@sns.dk" ;
    :definitionText "(Denmark) Reforestation forests with a forest-obligation written in the cadastre must be reforested, if not deforestation takes place and that is forbidden without permission from the national forest-authorities. A forest obligation states that the area in principle shall be used for forests purposes forever (so-called 'good and sustainable forestry'). If the owner can give the forest authorities a very good reason - for instance the soil is not suited for forestry - he can have permission to ra" .

:def_Reforestation_EU_2013_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :EU ;
    dcterms:date "2013"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32013D0529" ;
    :definitionText "(EU 2013) ‘reforestation’ means any direct human-induced conversion of land that is not forest to forest through planting, seeding and/or the human-induced promotion of natural seed sources, which is confined to land that was forest but ceased to be forest before 1 January 1990, and which has been reconverted to forest in the period after 31 December 1989; http://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32013D0529" .

:def_Reforestation_EU_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :EU ;
    :sourceRef "http://europa.eu.int/comm/dg08/forests/en/en4_6.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(EU) The restoration of tree cover, to areas from which trees have recently been removed, by planting, encouragement of natural regeneration, or a combination of these methods http://europa.eu.int/comm/dg08/forests/en/en4_6.htm." .

:def_Reforestation_Fiji_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Fiji ;
    :definitionText "(Fiji) Areas where trees have been felled and replanted. Malakai Sevudredre, Conservator of Forests, F.9641/2. 01/06/2000." .

:def_Reforestation_Ghana_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Ghana ;
    :definitionText "(Ghana) When a degraded or removed forest land is restored to its original forest status. (Osei Kofi, Forestry Dept.- Letter 7 May 99)" .

:def_Reforestation_GMUNCCD_2008_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :GMUNCCD ;
    dcterms:date "2008"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.global-mechanism.org/dynamic/documents/document_file/final2-viet-nam-climate-change-report---1july08.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(GM/UNCCD 2008) This process increases the capacity of the land to sequester carbon by replanting forest biomass in areas where forests have been previously harvested. Registration: The formal acceptance by the CDM Executive Board of a validated project as a CDM project activity. http://www.global-mechanism.org/dynamic/documents/document_file/final2-viet-nam-climate-change-report---1july08.pdf." .

:def_Reforestation_Indonesia_2002_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Indonesia ;
    dcterms:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.globalforestwatch.org/common/indonesia/sof.indonesia.english.low.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(Indonesia - 2002) The establishment by humans of forest cover on land that was formerly forested. http://www.globalforestwatch.org/common/indonesia/sof.indonesia.english.low.pdf" .

:def_Reforestation_IPCC_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :IPCC ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.grida.no/climate/ipcc/regional/327.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(IPCC - 1997) Forest stands established artificially on lands that have supported forests within the last 50 years http://www.grida.no/climate/ipcc/regional/327.htm" .

:def_Reforestation_Italy_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Italy ;
    :sourceRef "Biometria <isafa.biofor@tqs.it>" ;
    :definitionText "(Italy) (ricostituzione boschiva) - A forest activity aimed to restore or improve the forest tree and shrub cover through seeding, planting and 'regeneration coppicing' (in Italian riceppatura, which is a coppicing method for regenerating stumps, for example, after fire). (ISTAT) 'Rimboschimento' (reforestation), also for ex-novo planting in bare lands.From: Vittorio Tosi ISAFA Biometria isafa.biofor@tqs.it and Lorenzo Ciccarese ciccarese@anpa.it" .

:def_Reforestation_Kyrgyzstan_New_Forest_Code_1999_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Kyrgyzstan_New_Forest_Code_1999 ;
    :sourceRef "Irina Yunusova <irina@lesic.elcat.kg>" ;
    :definitionText "(Kyrgyzstan - New Forest Code (1999)) - The installation of forest plantations on areas previously covered by forest. Source: Irina Yunusova irina@lesic.elcat.kg" .

:def_Reforestation_Kyrgyzstan_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Kyrgyzstan ;
    :sourceRef "Irina Yunusova <irina@lesic.elcat.kg>" ;
    :definitionText "(Kyrgyzstan) - An active (with human support) form of afforestation on the territories formerly covered with the forest (lands) Source: Irina Yunusova irina@lesic.elcat.kg" .

:def_Reforestation_Kyrgyzstan_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Kyrgyzstan ;
    :sourceRef "Irina Yunusova <irina@lesic.elcat.kg>" ;
    :definitionText "(Kyrgyzstan) (from Russian it is likely to be translated as \"forest regeneration\") - The process of the creation of the forest generation under the forest cover, at the fellings and forest fires sites, and other areas formerly covered with the forest. Forest regeneration can be natural, artificial and mixed. Source: Irina Yunusova irina@lesic.elcat.kg" .

:def_Reforestation_Lithuania_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Lithuania ;
    :sourceRef "Sekrtetore <sek@mp.is.lt>" ;
    :definitionText "(Lithuania) The reestablishment of forest cover on forest land either naturally or artificially. Source: A. Kuliesis, Director of Lithuanain Forest Inventory and Management Institute Email: Sekrtetore sek@mp.is.lt" .

:def_Reforestation_Malaysia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Malaysia ;
    :sourceRef "hcthang@forestry.gov.my" ;
    :definitionText "(Malaysia) - The artificial establishment of forests by direct seeding or planting seedlings or cuttings on lands which previously (within the living memory or within 50 years) carry forests. From: hcthang@forestry.gov.my (Thang Hooi Chiew), Forestry Department Peninsular Malaysia" .

:def_Reforestation_Morocco_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Morocco ;
    :sourceRef "m.ellatifi@ellatifi.8m.com" ;
    :definitionText "(Morocco) Reforestation (Arabic : I’adat tashjeer/tahreej, French : Reboisement) - Artificial creation (by man) of a forest on an land which has been forested before, but on which the forest has disappeared, using seedlings, vegetative materials or seeds (sowing) Mohammed Ellatifi, m.ellatifi@ellatifi.8m.com" .

:def_Reforestation_Nicaragua_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Nicaragua ;
    :sourceRef "Harrie <harnic@ibw.com.ni>" ;
    :definitionText "(Nicaragua) Reforestación - Draft.La acción de poblar con especies arbóreas o arbustivas mediante plantación, regeneración manejada o siembra, un terreno que haya sido objeto de aprovechamiento previo o afectado por incendios o fenómenos naturales. www.nicarao.org.ni/ja (see Borrador de la ley, CAPITULO II DEFINICIONES) Harrie <harnic@ibw.com.ni>" .

:def_Reforestation_Northern_Mariana_Islands_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Northern_Mariana_Islands ;
    :sourceRef "Estanislao Villagomez <stanvill@gtepacifica.net>" ;
    :definitionText "(Northern Mariana Islands) Reforestation - A science and art of establishing a multistorey species of trees beneficial to mankind, wildlife and ecosystem. Source: Estanislao Villagomez stanvill@gtepacifica.net Division of Agriculture." .

:def_Reforestation_Pakistan_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Pakistan ;
    :definitionText "(Pakistan) To restock felled or otherwise cleared woodland. Definition adopted from the British Commonwealth Forest Terminology Part-I, 1953. Source: Mumtaz Ahmad, Section Forest Officer, Pakistan Min. of Environment, Local Government, and Rural Development." .

:def_Reforestation_Paraguay_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Paraguay ;
    :sourceRef "cdcdpnvs@venus.pla.net.py" ;
    :definitionText "(Paraguay) Reforestación: La acción de poblar con especies arbóreas mediante plantación, regeneración manejada o siembra, un terreno anteriormente boscoso que haya sido objeto de explotación extractiva. Ley N&deg; 536 - DE FOMENTO A LA FORESTACION Y REFORESTACION. Capítulo I. Artículo 2do. cdcdpnvs@venus.pla.net.py (Nombre Apellido)" .

:def_Reforestation_Philippines_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Philippines ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nscb.gov.ph/ru12/DEFINE/DEF-ENV.HTM" ;
    :definitionText "(Philippines) Reforestation - the act of planting trees on bare or open land which is used to be covered with forest growth. http://www.nscb.gov.ph/ru12/DEFINE/DEF-ENV.HTM" .

:def_Reforestation_Romania_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Romania ;
    :sourceRef "Sorin Sfirlogea <sorinsf@rosilva.ro>" ;
    :definitionText "(Romania) - The act of installation, through artificial methods, of the forest vegetation on lands where forest was recently removed. Sorin Sfirlogea <sorinsf@rosilva.ro National Forests Administration." .

:def_Reforestation_Russian_Federation_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Russian_Federation ;
    :sourceRef "Igor Yakovlev <yakovlev@mari-el.ru>" ;
    :definitionText "(Russian Federation)Process of establishing of forest cultures on before forested areas. (Forest cultures (specific Russian term) - forest, which was created by seeding or planting). [From: \"Igor Yakovlev\" yakovlev@mari-el.ru Date: Wed, 10 Jun 1998 02:51:19 -0400 (EDT)]" .

:def_Reforestation_St_Lucia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :St_Lucia ;
    :sourceRef "chiefforest@maffe.org" ;
    :definitionText "(St. Lucia) The planting of forest trees in an area where forest existed before (Source: Michael Andrew, chiefforest@maffe.org)" .

:def_Reforestation_Taiwan_ROC_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Taiwan_ROC ;
    :sourceRef "service@dns.forest.gov.tw" ;
    :definitionText "(Taiwan, ROC) To reforest in cut-over areas. Source: \"&ordf;L&deg;È&sect;&frac12;service\" service@dns.forest.gov.tw" .

:def_Reforestation_UN_DP_1999_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :UN_DP ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.profor.info/pdf/InnovatForesFinanc.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-DP 1999) Generally refers to planting trees on land that has been cleared of forest within the relatively recent past. May or may not refer to planting trees on land that has just been harvested. http://www.profor.info/pdf/InnovatForesFinanc.pdf" .

:def_Reforestation_UN_FAO_1997_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 1997) - Establishment of a tree crop on forest land (FAO 1997)." .

:def_Reforestation_UN_FAO_2001_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 2001) - The re-establishment of forest formations after a temporary condition with less than 10% canopy cover due to human-induced or natural perturbations. Explanatory note (extract): The definition of forest clearly states that forests under regeneration are considered as forests even if the canopy cover is temporarily below 10 per cent. Many forest management regimes include clearcutting followed by regeneration, and several natural processes, notably forest fires and windfalls, may l" .

:def_Reforestation_UN_FAO_2005_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    dcterms:date "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://unfccc.int/files/methods_and_science/lulucf/application/pdf/060830_killmann.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO 2005) - Establishment of forest plantations on temporarily unstocked lands that are considered as forests http://unfccc.int/files/methods_and_science/lulucf/application/pdf/060830_killmann.pdf" .

:def_Reforestation_UN_FAO_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FAO ;
    :sourceRef "Graeme Wild <GraemeW@za.sappi.com>" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FAO) The establishment of forest, naturally or artificially, on an area previously in forest cover (FAO - IUFRO). From: Graeme Wild GraemeW@za.sappi.com" .

:def_Reforestation_UNFCCC_2001_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :UNFCCC ;
    dcterms:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.unfccc.int/resource/docs/cop6secpart/l11r01.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(UNFCCC 2001) “Reforestation” is the direct human-induced conversion of non-forested land to forested land through planting, seeding and/or the human-induced promotion of natural seed sources, on land that was forested but that has been converted to non-forested land. For the first commitment period, reforestation activities will be limited to reforestation occurring on those lands that did not contain forest on 31 December 1989; http://www.unfccc.int/resource/docs/cop6secpart/l11r01.pdf" .

:def_Reforestation_UN_FRA_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :UN_FRA ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :definitionText "(UN-FRA 2000) Artificial establishment of forest on lands which carried forest before. (UN-ECE/FAO 1997 and FAO 1998)" .

:def_Reforestation_United_Kingdom_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :United_Kingdom ;
    :definitionText "(United Kingdom) Re-establishment of a tree crop on forest land (British Commonwealth Terminology) (Ford-Robertson 1971)." .

:def_Reforestation_USA_STATE_Maryland_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Maryland ;
    :canopyThreshold "50.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://pilot.wash.lib.md.us/washco/forestcn.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA –STATE- Maryland) The creation of a biological community dominated by trees and other woody plants containing at least 100 live trees per acre with at least 50 percent of those trees having the potential of attaining a 2-inch or greater diameter measured at 4.5 feet above the ground, within 7 years, according to procedures set forth in the Washington County Forest Conservation Technical Manual. The term also includes landscaping of areas under an approved landscaping plan establishing a for" .

:def_Reforestation_USA_EIA_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :USA_EIA ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.eia.gov/tools/glossary/index.cfm?id=R" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-EIA) Replanting of forests on lands that have recently been harvested or otherwise cleared of trees. http://www.eia.gov/tools/glossary/index.cfm?id=R" .

:def_Reforestation_USA_FED_DA_FS_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :USA_FED_DA_FS ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.fs.fed.us/land/emterms.html" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-FED-DA-FS) The restocking of an area with forest trees, by either natural or artificial means, such as planting (http://www.fs.fed.us/land/emterms.html)." .

:def_Reforestation_USA_STATE_Oregon_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Oregon ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.cof.orst.edu/cof/teach/for442/odfdefin.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Oregon) \"Natural reforestation\" means restocking a site with self-grown trees resulting from self-seeding or vegetative means. http://www.cof.orst.edu/cof/teach/for442/odfdefin.htm" .

:def_Reforestation_Venezuela_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Venezuela ;
    :sourceRef "Via <Profauna@marnr.gov.ve>" ;
    :definitionText "(Venezuela) REFORESTACION: cultivo de árboles, con fines económicos o con fines de protección en áreas donde ya habían existido vegetacón en épocas pasadas. Reglamento de la Ley Forestal de Suelos y Aguas (1977). Areas Naturales Protegidas de Venezuela. Series Aspectos Conceptuales y Metodológicos, DGSPOA/ACM/01, feb 1992. Via Profauna@marnr.gov.ve" .

:def_Reforestation_WAF_2004_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :WAF ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.worldagroforestry.org/sea/Publications/files/book/BK0073-04.PDF" ;
    :definitionText "(WAF 2004) - The establishment of forest on land previously under a forest land-use. http://www.worldagroforestry.org/sea/Publications/files/book/BK0073-04.PDF" .

:def_Reforestation_WCMC_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :WCMC ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.panda.org/downloads/forests/wcmcflrmapping.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(WCMC) - The managed reestablishment of forests on lands that once contained forests. http://www.panda.org/downloads/forests/wcmcflrmapping.pdf" .

:def_Reforestation_World_Bank_1999_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :World_Bank ;
    dcterms:date "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www-wds.worldbank.org/servlet/WDSContentServer/WDSP/IB/1999/09/17/000178830_98101901520841/Rendered/INDEX/multi0page.txt" ;
    :definitionText "(World Bank 1999) The replacement of trees in cut-over forest areas. http://www-wds.worldbank.org/servlet/WDSContentServer/WDSP/IB/1999/09/17/000178830_98101901520841/Rendered/INDEX/multi0page.txt" .

:def_Reforestation_World_Bank_2000_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :World_Bank ;
    dcterms:date "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.holz.uni-goettingen.de/ek/woodsat/pdf/worldbankforestry.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(World Bank 2000) The replacement or establishment of a tree crop on forestland. . http://www.holz.uni-goettingen.de/ek/woodsat/pdf/worldbankforestry.pdf World Bank 2000." .

:def_Reforestation_Yemen_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Yemen ;
    :sourceRef "m.ellatifi@ellatifi.8m.com" ;
    :definitionText "(Yemen) Reforestation (Arabic : I’adat tashjeer/tahreej, French : Reboisement) - Artificial creation (by man) of a forest on an land which has been forested before, but on which the forest has disappeared, using seedlings, vegetative materials or seeds (sowing) Mohammed Ellatifi, m.ellatifi@ellatifi.8m.com" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://ifdn.com/teacher/glossary.htm#d" ;
    :definitionText "A process by which a forest regrown http://ifdn.com/teacher/glossary.htm#d" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_003
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "Lorenzo Ciccarese <ciccarese@anpa.it>" ;
    :definitionText "A sylvicultural system that consists in seeding or planting tree forest stock in a forest area after felling or when species are unreliable for natural regeneration. Lorenzo Ciccarese ciccarese@anpa.it" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_004
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :definitionText "Artificial (planting, seeding) or natural re-establishment of forest on previously forest or other wooded land. [Source: UN/ECE 1990, via Brita Pajari]" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_005
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.gcrio.org/OnLnDoc/senate_epw990603.html" ;
    :definitionText "Conversion of non-forest to forest on lands which had, historically, contained forests but which had been converted to some other use as of 1990. http://www.gcrio.org/OnLnDoc/senate_epw990603.html" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_006
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.abforestprod.org/ARglossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "Establishment of a replacement stand of trees after harvesting operations are complete, based on scientific silvicultural practices that may include natural seeding or suckering, mechanical seeding or planting of seedlings. http://www.abforestprod.org/ARglossary.html" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_007
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.grida.no/climate/ipcc/tectran/362.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Forest stands established artificially on lands that have supported forests within the last 50 years http://www.grida.no/climate/ipcc/tectran/362.htm" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_008
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.climateservices.com/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Generally refers to planting trees on land that has been cleared of forest within the relatively recent past. May or may not refer to planting trees on land that has just been harvested. . http://www.climateservices.com/glossary.htm and http://www.undp.org/seed/forest/pdf/InnovatForesFinanc.pdf" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_009
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.oxfam.org.uk/coolplanet/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Planting trees to replace forests which have been harvested or destroyed. http://www.oxfam.org.uk/coolplanet/glossary.htm" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_010
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://fiesta.bren.ucsb.edu/~idgec/publications/reports/forest.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "Process of re-establishing forests on previously forested lands. http://fiesta.bren.ucsb.edu/~idgec/publications/reports/forest.pdf" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_011
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.notredame.ac.jp/cgi-bin/wn?reforestation" ;
    :definitionText "Re-afforestation -- (the restoration (replanting) of a forest that had been reduced by fire or cutting) http://www.notredame.ac.jp/cgi-bin/wn?reforestation" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_012
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.deltaenviro.org.za/resources/envirofacts/afforestation.html" ;
    :definitionText "Reafforestation - is the restocking of existing forests and woodlands which have been depleted. http://www.deltaenviro.org.za/resources/envirofacts/afforestation.html" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_013
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://education.vsnl.com/deep/" ;
    :definitionText "Reafforestation - The planting of trees on land that was previously under the forest cover, but which has been depleted by habitat destruction or over-exploitation. http://education.vsnl.com/deep/" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_014
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ces.ncsu.edu/nreos/forest/woodland/won-26r.html" ;
    :definitionText "Reestablishing a forest by planting or seeding an area from which forest vegetation has been removed. http://www.ces.ncsu.edu/nreos/forest/woodland/won-26r.html and http://msucares.com/pubs/pub1250.htm" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_015
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.mrsc.org/environment/forest/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "Reestablishing a forest in an area where trees have been removed. http://www.mrsc.org/environment/forest/glossary.htm" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_016
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :canopyThreshold "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://greenplanet.eolss.net/EolssLogn/mss/C10/E5-03/E5-03-01/E5-03-01-05/E5-03-01-05-TXT.aspx#Glossary" ;
    :definitionText "Reestablishment of forest formation after a temporary (less than 10 years) period with less than 10% canopy cover due to human induced or natural perturbations. http://greenplanet.eolss.net/EolssLogn/mss/C10/E5-03/E5-03-01/E5-03-01-05/E5-03-01-05-TXT.aspx#Glossary" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_017
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.bugwood.caes.uga.edu/glossary/" ;
    :definitionText "Replacing forests after felling. http://www.bugwood.caes.uga.edu/glossary/" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_018
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.oznet.ksu.edu/library/MISC2/SB661.PDF" ;
    :definitionText "Replacing forests. http://www.oznet.ksu.edu/library/MISC2/SB661.PDF" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_019
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.eia.doe.gov/oiaf/1605/ggrpt/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "Replanting of forests on lands that have recently been harvested or otherwise cleared of trees. http://www.eia.doe.gov/oiaf/1605/ggrpt/glossary.html" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_020
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.eia.doe.gov/oiaf/1605/vr95rpt/gloss.html" ;
    :definitionText "Replanting of forests on lands that have recently been harvested. http://www.eia.doe.gov/oiaf/1605/vr95rpt/gloss.html, http://www.theadvisorygroup.com/PDF2/publications/Carbon%20Sequestration%20Paper.pdf and http://www.epa.gov/globalwarming/publications/outreach/general/glossary.pdf" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_021
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :definitionText "Restocking an area with forest trees. [Source: Timber Harvesting and Engineering Glossary, USFS]" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_022
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :definitionText "Restoration of recently cleared forest (WWF/IUCN 1996)." .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_023
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.plant-a-tree-today.org/webcontrol/ShowPicture.asp?Status=ShowLibraryPDF&LiId=40" ;
    :definitionText "Revegetation - Re-establishment of non-forest vegetation and restoration of degraded non-forested lands, such as overgrazed native grasslands or cultivated wetlands http://www.plant-a-tree-today.org/webcontrol/ShowPicture.asp?Status=ShowLibraryPDF&LiId=40" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_024
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.nscb.gov.ph/ru12/DEFINE/DEF-ENV.HTM" ;
    :definitionText "The act of planting trees on bare or open land which is used to be covered with forest growth. http://www.nscb.gov.ph/ru12/DEFINE/DEF-ENV.HTM" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_025
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :definitionText "The act of renewing forest cover by planting seeds or young trees. [Source: WWWebster Dictionary]" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_026
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.idahoforests.org/dict1.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The act of replanting or reseeding a forest area to replace trees removed by harvest or destroyed by fire, wind or disease. http://www.idahoforests.org/dict1.htm" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_027
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :canopyThreshold "50.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.ci.rockville.md.us/cityprojects/envguide/eggloss.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The creation of a biological community dominated by trees and other woody plants containing at least 100 trees per acre, with at least 50 percent of those trees having the potential of attaining a 2-inch or greater dbh within seven years. http://www.ci.rockville.md.us/cityprojects/envguide/eggloss.htm" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_028
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.plant-a-tree-today.org/webcontrol/ShowPicture.asp?Status=ShowLibraryPDF&LiId=40" ;
    :definitionText "The direct human-induced conversion of non-forested land back to forested land. In the context of the Kyoto Protocol to the UNFCCC, reforestation can take place on land that was historically forested but as of December 31, 1989 was subject to another land-use http://www.plant-a-tree-today.org/webcontrol/ShowPicture.asp?Status=ShowLibraryPDF&LiId=40" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_029
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://greenplanet.eolss.net/EolssLogn/mss/C09/E4-27/E4-27-08/E4-27-08-04/E4-27-08-04-TXT.aspx#Glossary_" ;
    :definitionText "The establishment of forest in an area where there was forest during the previous 50 years. http://greenplanet.eolss.net/EolssLogn/mss/C09/E4-27/E4-27-08/E4-27-08-04/E4-27-08-04-TXT.aspx#Glossary_" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_030
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :definitionText "The establishment of plantations] to produce a forest product \"crop\" on lands that have supported forests within the last 50 years and where the original crop has been replaced with a different one (Brown et al. 1986)." .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_031
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.sfrc.ufl.edu/Class/for3162c/silvterm.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "The natural or artificial restocking of an area with forest trees. http://www.sfrc.ufl.edu/Class/for3162c/silvterm.pdf. Typically, refers to planting (Dunster and Dunster 1996)." .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_032
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.lehigh.edu/~kaf3/books/reporting/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "The natural or artificial restocking of an area with forest trees, most commonly used in reference to the artificial. The Art and Science of Sustainable Use. 1997. http://www.lehigh.edu/~kaf3/books/reporting/glossary.html" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_033
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :definitionText "The natural or artificial restocking of an area with trees. www.superiornationalforest.org/july4thstorm1999/Appendix%20B.doc" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_034
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.woodrow.org/teachers/biology/institutes/1992/old_growth.html" ;
    :definitionText "The planting of trees for re-establishment of a former forest. http://www.woodrow.org/teachers/biology/institutes/1992/old_growth.html" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_035
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :definitionText "The planting of trees on land from which the forest has been removed. [Source: Water Words Dictionary]" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_036
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.minntrees.org/facts/ff17.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The planting of young trees in forests that have been affected by harvest, fire, disease, wind or other factors. . http://www.minntrees.org/facts/ff17.htm" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_037
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.rfa.gov.au/cra/vic/cenhigh/press/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "The re-establishment of a stand of trees by planting or sowing with species native to the locality on previously cleared or poorly forested land. http://www.rfa.gov.au/cra/vic/cenhigh/press/glossary.html" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_038
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :definitionText "The reestablishment of forest cover either naturally (by natural seeding, coppice, or root suckers) or artificially (by direct seeding or planting). Note - reforestation usually maintains the same forest type and is done promptly after the previous stand or forest was removed (Helms 1998)." .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_039
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://assets.panda.org/downloads/lowermekongregionaloverview.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "The re-establishment of trees and understorey plants at a site previously occupied by forest cover. http://assets.panda.org/downloads/lowermekongregionaloverview.pdf" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_040
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.vanaturally.com/glossary.html" ;
    :definitionText "The renewal of forest cover by natural regeneration or the planting of seeds or seedlings http://www.vanaturally.com/glossary.html" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_041
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://ohia.com/ohia/roadshows/sky/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The renewal of forest cover by seeding or planting. http://ohia.com/ohia/roadshows/sky/glossary.htm" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_042
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.wrm.org.uy/actors/WB/1991policy3.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The replacement of trees in cut-over forest areas. http://www.wrm.org.uy/actors/WB/1991policy3.htm, https://www.uni-hohenheim.de/i490a/teaching/M4901-430/ws_03_04/reading_materials/New_Neef_Schwarzmeier_Studie.pdf and http://www.nap.edu/openbook.php?record_id=1985&page=671" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_043
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://buttecreekwatershed.org/ecr/new/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "The replanting of trees in an area that was previously forested. http://buttecreekwatershed.org/ecr/new/glossary.htm" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_044
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.soton.ac.uk/~engenvir/glossary.html#D" ;
    :definitionText "The replanting of trees in areas which have been cleared of woodland. http://www.soton.ac.uk/~engenvir/glossary.html#D" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_045
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://solstice.crest.org/renewables/SJ/glossary/A.html#AFFORESTATION" ;
    :definitionText "The replanting of trees on previously forested lands. http://solstice.crest.org/renewables/SJ/glossary/A.html#AFFORESTATION" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_046
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :definitionText "The restocking of felled or otherwise cleared woodland. [Source: British Commonwealth Forest Terminology via Renate Prüller]" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_047
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://greenplanet.eolss.net/EolssLogn/mss/C09/E4-27/E4-27-08/E4-27-08-05/E4-27-08-05-TXT.aspx#Glossary_" ;
    :definitionText "To re-establish tree cover on a once-forested site. http://greenplanet.eolss.net/EolssLogn/mss/C09/E4-27/E4-27-08/E4-27-08-05/E4-27-08-05-TXT.aspx#Glossary_" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_048
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.timbertax.org/research/aghndbk/glossary.htm" ;
    :definitionText "To reestablish trees on a harvested area by planting trees, setting tree seeds, seeding-in from adjacent trees, or sprouts from the stumps or roots of harvested trees http://www.timbertax.org/research/aghndbk/glossary.htm" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_049
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "Lorenzo Ciccarese <ciccarese@anpa.it>" ;
    :definitionText "When revegetation is established within the forest areas (Setiadi 1996). Lorenzo Ciccarese ciccarese@anpa.it" .

:def_Reforestation_Bolivia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Bolivia ;
    :sourceRef "Luis Castello <faopaf@caoba.entelnet.bo>" ;
    :definitionText "(Bolivia) REFORESTACIÓN: Tala de un bosque con el propósito de crear tierra arable, para usos agrícolas o ganaderos y aprovechar la madera para la construcción o propósitos industriales. Este proceso elimina los árboles y el sotobosque, alterando todo el ecosistema, con la consecuente perdida de humus del suelo, con las consecuencias de escorrentia superficial por la baja infiltración, perdida de animales y plantas útiles al hombre, y la inestabilidad de las cuencas hidrográficas. A causa de la " .

:def_Reforestation_India_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :India ;
    :sourceRef "Varma <v.varma@landfood.unimelb.edu.au>" ;
    :definitionText "(India) Bringing any deforested land under forest cover. [Source: Glossary of Technical Terms, Forest Research Institute, India. From: \"Vivek K. Varma\" <v.varma@landfood.unimelb.edu.au Date: Fri, 17 Jul 1998 02:28:29 -0400 (EDT)]" .

:def_Reforestation_IPCC_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :IPCC ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.junkscience.com/draft_AR4/GLOSSARY_SOD_TSU_FINAL.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(IPCC - 2003) Deforestation - Conversion of forest to non-forest. For a discussion of the term →forest and related terms such as →afforestation, →reforestation, and deforestation: see the IPCC Report on Land Use, Land-Use Change and Forestry (IPCC, 2000). See also the Report on Definitions and Methodological Options to Inventory Emissions from Direct Human-induced Degradation of Forests and Devegetation of Other Vegetation Types (IPCC, 2003). (Source: Second Order Draft Glossary IPCC WGI Fourth " .

:def_Reforestation_Latvia_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Latvia ;
    :sourceRef "Maksym Polyakov <mpoliak@pcomp.nauu.kiev.ua>" ;
    :definitionText "(Latvia) A complex of measures to afforest land (area) not covered by forest. Source: \"Maksym Polyakov\" <mpoliak@pcomp.nauu.kiev.ua" .

:def_Reforestation_Thailand_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Thailand ;
    :sourceRef "Wilailak Pangtawaong <wpangtaw@deqp.go.th>" ;
    :definitionText "(Thailand) The planting of forests on lands which have historically contained forests but which have since been converted to some other use. The report of Thailand's National Greenhouse Gas Inventory, 1990. \"Wilailak Pangtawaong\" wpangtaw@deqp.go.th" .

:def_Reforestation_Ukraine_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :Ukraine ;
    :definitionText "(Ukraine) (Artificial) reforestation -- creation of forest plantations on the lands which were not previously under forest (covered by forest) with the aim of formation economically valuable, high productive and biologically sustainable forest stands. Note that ``forest plantations'' defined as ``forest stands created by planting of seedlings, saplings of trees or shrubs or by sowing of their seeds'', i.e. it here this means only origination of stands, not intensity of management (Polyakov 1998)" .

:def_Reforestation_UN_EP_2003_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :UN_EP ;
    dcterms:date "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
    :sourceRef "http://digitalcommons.unl.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1030&context=usdafsfacpub" ;
    :definitionText "(UN-EP 2003) - Planting of forests on lands that have previously contained forests but that have been converted to some other use. http://digitalcommons.unl.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1030&context=usdafsfacpub" .

:def_Reforestation_USA_STATE_Illinois_nd_001
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :USA_STATE_Illinois ;
    :sourceRef "http://dnr.state.il.us/legal/1537.htm" ;
    :definitionText "(USA-STATE-Illinois) \"Reforestation\" means the natural or artificial restocking with trees on forest land. http://dnr.state.il.us/legal/1537.htm" .

:def_Reforestation_WCMC_nd_002
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :appliesIn :WCMC ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.panda.org/downloads/forests/wcmcflrmapping.pdf" ;
    :definitionText "(WCMC) Forest restoration - the establishment of forests containing native species with a high ecological integrity. Restoration is defined as the deliberate alteration of ecological patterns and processes for the purpose of recreating some presumed set of natural, predisturbance ecosystem conditions. http://www.panda.org/downloads/forests/wcmcflrmapping.pdf" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_050
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :definitionText "Establishing forests on lands which have, historically, previously contained forests but which have been converted to some other use. This \"other use\" must have prevailed for at least 20 (or other number to be chosen) years, or, alternatively, the \"other use\" can be shorter if the land has been counted as \"deforested\" within a commitment period under the Kyoto Protocol (Schlamadinger 1998)." .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_051
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :definitionText "Planting of forests on lands which have, historically, previously contained forests but which have been converted to some other use. Replanted forests are included in the category, Changes in Forest and Other Woody Biomass Stocks, in the LUCF module of the emissions inventory calculations (IPCC 1996)." .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_052
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://epdweb.engr.wisc.edu/dmc/courses/hazards/BB02-apx1.html" ;
    :definitionText "The establishment of a tree crop on forest land following deforestation. http://epdweb.engr.wisc.edu/dmc/courses/hazards/BB02-apx1.html" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_053
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.harcourt.com/dictionary/def/8/5/7/2/8572900.html" ;
    :definitionText "The reestablishment and development of a timber crop on forest land. Also, REAFFORESTATION. http://www.harcourt.com/dictionary/def/8/5/7/2/8572900.html" .

:def_Reforestation_Unknown_nd_054
    rdf:type :Definition ;
    :defines :Reforestation ;
    :hasCategory :LandCover ;
    :sourceRef "http://www.deltaenviro.org.za/resources/envirofacts/afforestation.html" ;
    :definitionText "The restocking of existing forests and woodlands which have been depleted. Source: http://www.deltaenviro.org.za/resources/envirofacts/afforestation.html" .
